window.AKK_AN_INNOCENT_GIRL_SEEKING_A_HUSBAND_WAS_DECEIVED_AND_MARRIED_A_CHILDLESS_OFFICER_CRYING_WITH_EMOTION_CHAPTERS=(window.AKK_AN_INNOCENT_GIRL_SEEKING_A_HUSBAND_WAS_DECEIVED_AND_MARRIED_A_CHILDLESS_OFFICER_CRYING_WITH_EMOTION_CHAPTERS||[]).concat([{"number":1,"title":"Chapter 1: Warmth.","paragraphs":["Outside the window, the north wind howled. Inside, the heated brick bed was burning, filling the room with a sweltering heat.","\"Wife, does it hurt?\"","The man's hoarse voice sounded by her ear. He was tall and robust, his muscles rock-hard as his thick arms embraced her.","She could feel a scorching heat radiating from his arms.","In a haze, Qiao Lanshu looked at the man above her, her nose stinging with emotion. \"Brother Zheng...\"","Qiao Lanshu wrapped her arms around the man's broad shoulders. Feeling the warmth and rapid breathing coming from him, her tears fell once again.","The man picked her up and slowly carried her from the living room to the bedroom. He comforted her in a low voice:","\"Don't be afraid... I'll be gentle. Otherwise, your body won't be able to take it...\"","The man's voice was deep and laced with tenderness. Qiao Lanshu immersed herself in his gentle offensive.","She thought to herself, if only she could have a child with Brother Zheng, how wonderful that would be.","...","Clackety-clack! Clackety-clack!","The train pulled into the station.","Qiao Lanshu jolted awake, suddenly realizing she was already on the train heading north!","Her face was stained with tears, and the collar of her clothes was soaked damp.","Once again, she had dreamed of Qin Yuanzheng.","She wiped her tears and got off the train. Her head was throbbing, her mind still entirely consumed by the illusory dream of her intimacy with Qin Yuanzheng.","His touch felt so real. It was as if his large, calloused hands were still lingering on her skin, and his scalding breath was still brushing against her ear.","He was a native Northern man, tall and muscular, capable of lifting her up with just one arm.","Every time they were intimate, he always loved to pick her up, holding her as if she were a child.","She loved his gentle and considerate nature, but sometimes, she was also afraid of his sturdy, fierce, and unrestrained body.","She wondered, which military unit was her Brother Zheng stationed at right now?","Qiao Lanshu walked out of the train station. Remembering something, she opened her right palm. Written on it in fountain pen was a line of small text:","\"Sun Mingyong, Battalion Commander of the Independent Second Battalion, Longcheng Production and Construction Corps.\"","Oh, right. This was her former fiance.","The real reason she came to the North this time was to find her fiance.","Her father had financially supported Sun Mingyong for ten years, and the two of them had gotten engaged three years ago.","This year, Sun Mingyong mentioned in his letter that he had been promoted to battalion commander.","The family members of a battalion commander were allowed to accompany the army. It just so happened that Lanshu had graduated and was facing the prospect of being sent down to work in the countryside. Therefore, Qiao Lanshu departed from Yangcheng by train, traveling for three days and three nights to reach Longcheng, over two thousand kilometers away, to find her fiance.","However, having lived through a past life, Qiao Lanshu knew that Sun Mingyong was not in the military at all.","Relying on the money provided by the Qiao family, he had found a job at a food factory in the North, and had even married a wife and had children.","Meanwhile, Qiao Lanshu had waited for him alone at the train station for four whole hours.","In the end, cold and starving, she had walked out of the train station late at night, only to faint by the roadside. She was picked up by a street thug and locked away in a mountain cave dwelling.","By the time she finally managed to escape from the mountains, two years had passed. Her health was ruined, leaving her unable to bear children.","With the help of the Women's Federation, she entered a food factory and worked there for a few years.","Later on, she met Qin Yuanzheng.","At the time, Qin Yuanzheng, a brigade commander nearing forty, happened to suffer from infertility as well. He fell in love with Qiao Lanshu at first sight and actively pursued her.","He was eleven years older than her, mature, steady, gentle, and caring.","He cherished her like a precious treasure, soothing her wounds inch by inch.","Yet, in the fifth year of their marriage, an old injury of his flared up and became infected, ultimately taking his life.","Devastated by the blow, Qiao Lanshu fell severely ill and never recovered. In the final days of her life, she was rarely lucid and would constantly dream of Qin Yuanzheng.","She dreamed of the times they spent together.","At this thought, Qiao Lanshu's face instantly darkened.","Given the chance to start over, she had to go find Qin Yuanzheng sooner!","This time, she would marry him early. Even if he was infertile, she did not mind.","This time, she had a healthy body, and he had not yet gone to execute that mission.","They could share a much longer future together."]},{"number":2,"title":"Chapter 2: Finding a Girl","paragraphs":["It was already late autumn. While the south was still basking in bright sunshine, the north had unexpectedly grown this cold.","Especially when Qiao Lanshu arrived, it was nearly dark. Once the sun went down, the stark temperature difference between day and night made the weather even more freezing.","Having grown up in Yangcheng, Qiao Lanshu simply couldn't withstand this kind of cold.","However, her biological mother had passed away early, and her stepmother was eager to marry her off as soon as possible. Therefore, faced with the choice between being sent down to the countryside or going to the military base to find her fiancé, she chose to head north to find him.","It was just that it was truly too cold here.","She was only wearing a short-sleeved T-shirt, black trousers, and black cloth shoes.","Her stepmother did know that the north was cold, so she had purposely prepared a thin cotton-padded jacket for her.","But wearing this jacket felt no different from wearing nothing at all!","Standing inside the train station, Qiao Lanshu's small face was turning pale blue from the cold, and her teeth were chattering.","At the entrance of the station, carrying a bag in one hand and holding her letter of introduction in the other, she gazed at the familiar yet strange station.","This time, she wouldn't foolishly wait around for four hours.","She was going to find Qin Yuanzheng!","She just didn't know where Brother Zheng was at this moment.","Shivering all over from the cold, she retreated back into the station. She found a ticket clerk and went over to ask, Hello, comrade. Could you please tell me how to get to this place?","It was getting late, and the ticket clerk was preparing to get off work. Seeing Qiao Lanshu's pale, freezing face and hearing her non-local accent, the clerk quickly asked, Comrade, where are you heading? It's so late, why are you still here?","As she spoke, she leaned closer to look at what Qiao Lanshu held in her palm.","Qiao Lanshu asked with a trembling voice, I'm going to the military base to find my fiancé. His unit is the Independent Second Battalion of the Longcheng Production and Construction Corps. The address is the South Suburb Forestry Farm in Longcheng. Do you know how to get there?","The ticket clerk replied, Oh my, you've arrived too late. The number three bus to the South Suburb Forestry Farm stops running at six in the evening. If you can't make it, take your letter of introduction and go to the Production and Construction Corps Headquarters building across the street. They will help accommodate military family members.","While speaking, the extremely helpful ticket clerk led Qiao Lanshu out of the station and pointed at a building diagonally across the street. See that? That's the General Headquarters of our Production and Construction Corps. Go over there and explain your situation to them.","The moment Qiao Lanshu stepped out of the train station, the biting northwest wind hit her face, making her feel as if her very soul was freezing to death.","She nodded gratefully, thanked the clerk, and then walked stiffly across the street.","She had only eaten a single rice cake since morning. Now, it was already past nine at night, and she hadn't had anything else to eat or drink.","She felt dizzy, and the cold seemed to pierce right into her bones.","Otherwise, in her past life, she wouldn't have fainted.","This time, she had to hold on.","Just then, she saw several tall men in military uniforms lift the windproof curtain at the entrance of the headquarters building, striding out while talking amongst themselves.","Qiao Lanshu cast a casual glance and immediately froze.","The man walking at the front looked somewhat familiar.","Her heart skipped a beat, and she subconsciously chased after them. Comrade, PLA comrade...","Her voice was too soft, and the men were arguing so heatedly that they didn't hear her at all.","Seeing them walking further away, Qiao Lanshu grew anxious and quickly ran over. PLA comrades, please wait a moment.","In her panic, she sped up and rushed forward blindly.","Suddenly, she tripped over something, let out a cry of alarm, and fell to the ground.","The bag in her hand flew out and hit the leg of that exceptionally tall soldier.","The soldiers turned around abruptly and looked at the girl lying on the ground.","One of them exclaimed in shock, Is she alright? Why is she dressed so thinly? Don't tell me she fainted from the cold.","Another said, Quickly check on her, make sure she hasn't seriously injured herself from the fall.","The man at the front stared at Qiao Lanshu, a hint of surprise in his eyes.","Those deep eyes were something Qiao Lanshu would never forget, even in death.","She felt flustered and at a loss for what to do.","Qin Yuanzheng. This was her Brother Zheng.","So, in her panic, she closed her eyes and pretended to faint.","The soldiers grew a bit nervous. Regiment Commander Qin, she really fainted!","Regiment Commander Qin frowned, his deep voice ringing out. You all head back to the base first. I'll drop her off at the military hospital on my way."]},{"number":3,"title":"Chapter 3: I Came to Find My Husband","paragraphs":["Qin Yuanzheng personally wrapped the young girl who had fainted at the gate of the command headquarters in his military greatcoat, and then carried her over his shoulder into the headquarters building.","He called over two guards, had them bring a car around, and sent the little girl to the military region hospital.","He did not go with them, heading straight to the military base instead.","Qiao Lanshu was a bit disappointed. Fortunately, it was not cold in the hospital, and there was hot water to drink.","Most importantly, she had avoided the miserable fate of her past life. She did not have to freeze and faint on the street, get picked up by a ruffian, and then be locked away in a mountain cave dwelling.","Qiao Lanshu had caught a cold from the freezing weather, so she simply stayed in the hospital for a day. By the second day, she could not help but ask a nurse, \"Comrade, I would like to ask, which kind-hearted comrade saved me last night? I want to thank him in person.\"","The nurse smiled and said, \"The people who brought you here last night are from the 21st Regiment of our Production and Construction Corps. I heard you were saved by their regiment commander. If you want to say thank you, you can go look for Regiment Commander Qin.\"","So her Brother Zheng was now in the 21st Regiment of the Construction Corps, and he was even a regiment commander.","Her Brother Zheng was truly amazing.","Qiao Lanshu nodded, pondering in her heart: should she play pitiful and wear thin clothes to go thank Brother Zheng?","Or should she first go buy some clothes, find a guesthouse, track down Sun Mingyong to settle the marriage issue, and finally come back to find Brother Zheng?","Being in an unfamiliar place with no acquaintances, she had to get herself settled first, right?","...","Meanwhile, outside a construction site office in a certain mining area, Qin Yuanzheng was accompanying Commander Li out of the mine. Before getting into the car, Commander Li suddenly asked, \"Yuanzheng, how old are you this year?\"","Qin Yuanzheng: \"Twenty-nine.\"","Commander Li looked at him. \"Why haven't you settled the major event of your life yet? Why didn't you go to the mixer arranged by the base with the female workers from the textile factory?\"","Qin Yuanzheng lowered his head. \"Don't ask when you already know the answer. I'm still busy here.\"","Commander Li snorted coldly. \"You're always like this whenever this is brought up. I heard you rescued a little girl from the south a couple of days ago? Haven't you gone to check on her these past two days?\"","Qin Yuanzheng: \"...\"","Commander Li said meaningfully, \"Saving a life is a great grace... Since you brought the person back, you should go check on her more often. At the very least, you need to help her get settled, right?\"","Qin Yuanzheng nodded helplessly. \"Understood. I'll go this afternoon.\"","Right before getting into the car, Commander Li was still talking: \"If you can settle your marriage issue as soon as possible, your future path will be much smoother, understand?\"","What else could Qin Yuanzheng say? He could only nod. \"Understood.\"","After finally sending Commander Li off, Qin Yuanzheng stood by the road with his hands on his hips. He looked up at the gloomy gray sky and sighed.","He was tall, muscular, and had sharp, striking facial features. Over the years, there had been quite a few women who took a liking to him.","He used to think about starting a family too. After all, what man didn't dream of a wife, kids, and a warm bed?","But two years ago, when he returned from a mission and had a routine physical examination, the medical report showed that he had low sperm motility.","The doctor told him that this counted as infertility, and he would never have biological children of his own in this lifetime.","Because of this, the girls who had previously gone on blind dates with him all turned their attention to his other comrades.","He himself lost interest and decided to dedicate his whole life to serving his country, giving up on marriage.","However, his older cousin, who was the director of a food factory, was very invested in the major event of his life.","So, he simply asked his cousin to introduce him to divorced female comrades who already had children.","Thinking of this, it just so happened that he had to visit his cousin's house today to go on a blind date with a divorced female comrade.","With this in mind, Qin Yuanzheng left the mining area and drove back to the headquarters building.","He parked the car, went to the nearby supply and marketing cooperative to buy two jars of canned fruit and half a pound of biscuits, and carried them to the military region hospital.","Qiao Lanshu was resting in the hospital. It had been too cold these past two days, and she had caught a cold again, constantly having a runny nose and sneezing.","It seemed the freezing weather had truly made her sick.","Moreover, because the climate here was dry, completely incomparable to the humid south, her throat and nasal passages felt extremely uncomfortable. She would even wake up from the dryness while sleeping.","Her skin had become somewhat allergic due to the excessive dryness, breaking out in quite a few small red bumps that were both dry and painful. Her lips were also chapped and hurt a lot.","Qiao Lanshu had grown up in a well-off family. Although her stepmother had never really liked her and secretly planned to kick her out once she graduated.","But as a teacher, she didn't dare to mistreat Qiao Lanshu when it came to basic necessities like food, clothing, housing, and transportation.","Setting aside her past life, Qiao Lanshu had indeed never suffered such hardships.","Now, she decided to rest well for a few days and focus on recovering from her illness first.","At this moment, a knock came from the door. Holding her water cup, she sat up and looked toward the doorway.","She had thought it would be a nurse coming in, but instead, a man wearing a military greatcoat entered.","The man was very tall with broad shoulders and wheat-colored skin. He sported a buzz cut, and his sharp eyes lowered slightly as he stared at her for a moment.","The moment she met the man's gaze, Qiao Lanshu's heart instantly started pounding.","Qiao Lanshu was currently wearing a white Dacron shirt and black trousers. Her waist-length hair was draped over her shoulders, and straight bangs covered her forehead, revealing a small face that still carried a bit of baby fat.","With her fair skin, almond-shaped eyes, cherry-like lips, and an oval face, she looked exactly like a good, obedient girl.","As soon as the good girl saw him, her little face turned red, and her small hands rubbed the hem of her shirt as if she were somewhat nervous.","However, the way she looked at him was extremely focused, carrying a hint of the joy of a long-awaited reunion or the pleasant surprise of regaining something lost, which left Qin Yuanzheng completely baffled.","Consequently, Qin Yuanzheng even lowered his voice, afraid of frightening her. \"I heard you caught a cold. Are you feeling any better?\"","Qiao Lanshu nodded, her bright black eyes staring fixedly at him. Her nasal voice was heavy, and her tone was soft. \"Much better. It's just a bit too cold, and I brought too few clothes.\"","Listening to her speak and looking at her pitiful appearance, Qin Yuanzheng asked in a low voice, \"You're not a local? Where are you from?\"","Qiao Lanshu replied, \"From Yangcheng.\"","Qin Yuanzheng was a bit surprised. \"Then you've crossed more than half the country. That's quite far. What are you doing here? Going down to the countryside?\"","However, going down to the countryside meant having special buses to drop them off and dedicated personnel to receive them.","Within their Construction Corps, there were people specifically assigned to settle the educated youth who came down to the countryside for construction. Over the years, they had already received tens of thousands of educated youth.","As a result, to Qin Yuanzheng's absolute astonishment, the little girl in front of him actually said, \"I came to the military base to find my husband.\"","Qin Yuanzheng: \"...\"","The expression on Qin Yuanzheng's face was somewhat stunned as he looked at Qiao Lanshu.","The little girl looked delicate and soft, and her voice was gentle and sweet. She seemed so tiny that he thought she was still a child.","After a long while, he finally asked, \"Find your husband... How old are you?\"","Qiao Lanshu blushed and said, \"I'll be eighteen in a few days. Here is my household register, and my letter of introduction.\"","As she spoke, she took out a pile of documents.","Qin Yuanzheng: \"...\"","Looking at this silly girl who had absolutely no guard up against him, Qin Yuanzheng suddenly felt a sense of responsibility in his heart.","After all, she was the girl he had rescued. She was completely alone here, a stranger in a strange land, so he had to help her out, right?","He set the two jars of canned yellow peaches and the biscuits he was holding on the table.","Then, he took off his military overcoat, revealing the uniform underneath.","He pulled up a chair and sat by the bed.","Even though they were both seated, Qiao Lanshu was still significantly shorter than him. Looking at Qin Yuanzheng sitting so close, she could even catch the crisp, cool scent of pine and cypress mixed with coal dust radiating from him, and she quietly blushed again.","Qin Yuanzheng, a dozen years younger, looked even taller and more handsome.","Qin Yuanzheng looked at her, finding it somewhat amusing.","This little girl was truly prone to shyness, blushing at the drop of a hat.","So, he pulled his chair back a bit, putting some distance between them.","Qiao Lanshu: ...","Wait, why did he move away?","Qin Yuanzheng looked at her and asked, \"Which regiment, battalion, and company does your fiancé belong to? What is his name? Tell me, and I will help you find him.\""]},{"number":4,"title":"Chapter 4: It doesn't look like anything good at first glance.","paragraphs":["In her previous life, when Qiao Lanshu was picked up by a loafer,","The man, seeing her sweet and pretty appearance, fair skin, and hearing her soft-spoken voice, liked her immensely and took her straight home.","Later, when the man learned she had come to find her husband-to-be and that her fiancé was a battalion commander, he was nearly scared to death.","So, he secretly went out to inquire about Sun Mingyong. If Sun Mingyong really was a battalion commander, he planned to send Qiao Lanshu back, hoping to gain the battalion commander's favor.","However, it turned out Sun Mingyong was no battalion commander at all; he wasn't even a soldier.","He was just an ordinary worker at a food factory.","Therefore, that loafer told Qiao Lanshu the news and threatened her to bear him a son.","Fearing she might run away, he took her back to his old home in the mountains and locked her directly in a cave dwelling.","Qiao Lanshu lived in that cave dwelling for over a year, completely cut off from the outside world.","Even now, reborn, all she knows is that Sun Mingyong works at a food factory and has married and had children.","As for which food factory Sun Mingyong is at or where he lives, she doesn't know.","Moreover, having been reborn, even if she knew, she would have to pretend not to.","Otherwise, being arrested as a spy would be a real problem.","Now, Qin Yuanzheng offered to help her find the person. Without hesitation, she handed him the introduction letter and the address Sun Mingyong had written in the letter.","Qin Yuanzheng took it, glanced at it, and asked her, \"Since you've come all this way to find your husband and join him with the army, didn't he come to the station to pick you up?\"","Normally, in their unit, if family members come to visit, the unit grants leave.","Welcoming family is a very important matter, to be taken seriously.","Qiao Lanshu lowered her head, thinking of the cold wind she endured at the station in her past life. Feeling both angry and resentful, she said with a grim expression, \"My father wrote to him and sent a telegram, but he didn't come.\"","Qiao Lanshu looked far too innocent. Even when she was angry, her words came out soft and girlish, not sounding angry but more like she was being coquettish, and her little expression looked somewhat aggrieved.","Qin Yuanzheng's heart softened a bit too. He said softly,","\"Perhaps he didn't receive the letter, or maybe he had some urgent task. Don't worry, I'll go ask around for you. Since you're sick, rest well. It's cold outside, and you're not used to it, so don't go out. Drink plenty of water; it's very dry here.\"","Listening to his instructions, Qiao Lanshu felt immensely grateful. She nodded, looking at Qin Yuanzheng with eager eyes, \"Regiment Commander Qin, are you leaving?\"","Looking at her little face, Qin Yuanzheng suddenly felt reluctant to go.","This young girl seemed like an innocent child who knew nothing of the world, with no relatives or friends here, and no teacher accompanying her. How would she manage alone?","Qin Yuanzheng thought, since he was the one who saved her, he really should take more care of her;","After all, he himself had no family or home to worry about.","So he nodded and said, \"Yes, I'll go inquire about this Sun Mingyong for you. You rest properly here. When I have time, I'll come see you.\"","Qiao Lanshu was somewhat reluctant to see him go, but she also knew they had only met twice by chance and were practically still strangers.","Qin Yuanzheng might be taking extra care of her because he was a soldier, but she couldn't trouble him too much.","So, she could only say, \"Alright, then I'll trouble you, Regiment Commander Qin.\"","Her voice was soft, and she looked pitiful. Qin Yuanzheng stood up and said to her, \"Then you rest well.\"","When Qin Yuanzheng came out of the ward, the doctors and nurses in the hallway looked at him as if they'd seen a ghost.","They had all just heard Qin Yuanzheng speak.","Too gentle, gentle enough to be spine-chilling.","Qin Yuanzheng had visited the hospital many times before because his soldiers had been injured; he came frequently. But each time, he wore a stern expression and spoke coldly and harshly.","Why was he so gentle today? It was unsettling.","After Qin Yuanzheng left, several nurses came to the ward door to look and immediately understood: \"Oh, it's this young girl. How pitiful.\"","\"No wonder even Regiment Commander Qin turned gentle. Who could see this girl and not be gentle?\"","\"Ah, this girl came from so far away, with no relatives or friends here. I wonder what she came for?\"","I heard it's something like looking for her husband? Anyway, it's not about being resettled in the countryside; otherwise she would have been sent to the village for resettlement long ago.","...","After leaving the ward, Qin Yuanzheng walked while pulling out Sun Mingyong's letter to read.","This letter was written by Sun Mingyong to Qiao Lanshu's father. It said he had earned a second-class merit, been promoted to battalion commander, and that everything was going smoothly here, thanking Uncle Qiao for his support and nurturing, etc.","Qin Yuanzheng read for a while and suddenly stopped in his tracks.","He looked at the words on the page, his brows furrowing tightly: \"Battalion Commander Sun Mingyong, Independent Second Battalion, Longcheng Production and Construction Corps?\"","Qin Yuanzheng initially thought he had misread it. He stopped, staring at the words on the letter over and over, and finally confirmed he was not mistaken.","What was written was indeed Independent Second Battalion Commander.","The Production and Construction Corps' Independent Second Battalion was a unit directly under the Corps Headquarters, under its direct jurisdiction, located at the South Suburb Forest Farm in Longcheng.","The battalion commander of this Independent Second Battalion, Qin Yuanzheng knew him. Not only did he know him, they were close comrades-in-arms.","If Sun Mingyong really was this battalion commander, he could find him immediately.","But the problem was, the battalion commander of the South Suburb Forest Farm Independent Second Battalion was not named Sun Mingyong; he was named Zhao Jiannong, already married with two daughters.","Moreover, Zhao Jiannong was also from the north, not a southerner.","Qin Yuanzheng instinctively wanted to turn back and tell the young girl from the south that the information she provided was incorrect.","However, he paused, thought about it, and still walked away with the letter.","Forget it, he'd better go to the Independent Second Battalion first and ask if there was anyone named Sun Mingyong.","...","Seeing that it was getting late, Qin Yuanzheng had promised his cousin to go to his house for dinner.","So, he first returned to the mining area, went to his office, and found the regiment's chief of staff, Lin Yucheng. He told Lin Yucheng the address and name, as well as Sun Mingyong's age and place of origin, saying to him:","\"This afternoon, go to the South Suburb Forest Farm. Ask Battalion Commander Zhao if there is, or ever was, a person named Sun Mingyong in their battalion. Investigate carefully and report back to me.\"","Lin Yucheng: \"Received!\"","After a moment, Staff Officer Lin couldn't help but ask, \"Regiment Commander, who is this Sun Mingyong? How come I've never heard of him? Is he a spy? What should we do if we find him?\"","Qin Yuanzheng shook his head: \"No need to take any action. Just find out the situation regarding this person and then tell me.\"","This Sun Mingyong, fabricating the identity of a battalion commander to deceive a young woman, is clearly no good from the get-go.","Once they find him, he'll go and confront the man first. That way, the young woman won't have to go over there and risk being foolishly tricked again."]},{"number":5,"title":"Chapter 5: Blind Date","paragraphs":["After Qin Yuanzheng delegated the task of finding the person, he packed his things, grabbed two tins of canned mandarin oranges and a bottle of sorghum liquor, and left the office.","Leaving the mining area, he got into his car and drove all the way to the food factory's family residential compound in the northern part of the city.","His cousin, Yang Wenyan, was the director of the food factory in the city's north.","Ever since he was transferred to work at the mining area here, his cousin Yang Wenyan had been very welcoming, always inviting him over for dinner during holidays and festivals.","After all, Qin Yuanzheng's hometown wasn't around Longcheng. His family lived over by the Changbai Mountains, which was quite a distance away.","Working far from home, having a relative look out for him was a real blessing.","Therefore, Qin Yuanzheng visited his cousin quite frequently.","He arrived at the food factory's dormitory area, parked the car, took out his gifts, found the building where Yang Wenyan lived, and went straight up to the second floor.","Yang Wenyan's home was a two-bedroom apartment with a living room. Though it wasn't exactly spacious, being assigned such an apartment in the city was no easy feat.","After all, the Production and Construction Corps had to settle tens of thousands of educated youths sent down to the countryside every year, making housing extremely tight.","When Qin Yuanzheng stepped into Yang Wenyan's home, his cousin's wife, Deng Xiaozhen, had already finished cooking dinner.","His cousin and his wife didn't have any children yet, but at this moment, Qin Yuanzheng immediately spotted a seven- or eight-year-old boy sitting in the room.","The boy, wearing a somewhat worn-out padded jacket, stared at Qin Yuanzheng with a reserved and cautious expression.","Qin Yuanzheng stood at the door, paused his steps, and looked at Yang Wenyan.","Yang Wenyan walked over to him: \"It's freezing. Come in, let's shut the door first.\"","As he spoke, he closed the door, then leaned in close to Qin Yuanzheng's ear and lowered his voice, \"Didn't you say last time that you wanted to find a female comrade who already has a child? Take a look at this one today.\"","Qin Yuanzheng: ...","Qin Yuanzheng had indeed said something like that.","He was nearing thirty. Not only his superiors but also his family members were constantly asking him about settling down and starting a family.","He suffered from infertility. Although his sexual function was perfectly fine and he was very robust, his sperm was too weak and had low motility. The doctor had told him that he might never have children in his lifetime.","If he had to get married, he would either have to find a woman who didn't want to have children, or simply find a divorcée who already had a child.","He had only mentioned this last week, and this week, his cousin and cousin-in-law had already found someone for him.","For a moment, Qin Yuanzheng didn't know what to say.","His cousin Yang Wenyan took his military overcoat to hang it up while saying, \"Yuanzheng, you look incredibly handsome in this uniform! There must be plenty of girls who fancy you, right?\"","Qin Yuanzheng stood at 1.88 meters, and with his military boots on, he was over 1.9 meters tall. He had a firm, muscular build that made him look tall, mighty, and imposing.","Many women loved exactly his type.","If it weren't for his infertility, his superiors would definitely be fighting to marry their daughters off to him.","Yang Wenyan shook his head, sighed, and pulled him inside to sit down, whispering again, \"The female comrade here today is a worker at the textile factory, just like your cousin-in-law. She got divorced two years ago and is raising her son on her own. Look, her son is quite well-behaved too.\"","Qin Yuanzheng asked, \"Why hasn't she found someone else after being divorced for two years?\"","Yang Wenyan shook his head: \"I'm not sure. You can ask her yourself in a bit.\"","With that, Yang Wenyan turned to the boy sitting on the sofa and said, \"Xiaoyuan, come here and say hello to Uncle Qin.\"","The boy gave Qin Yuanzheng a timid glance and called out, \"Uncle.\"","Qin Yuanzheng nodded. He patted his pockets, only to find them completely empty.","He then reached directly into his trouser pocket, pulled out a five-yuan bill, and handed it to the boy, saying, \"Uncle didn't bring a greeting gift. Take this and buy yourself some candy.\"","The boy silently accepted it and tucked the money into his pocket.","Before long, his cousin-in-law Deng Xiaozhen came out carrying dishes of food, accompanied by a female comrade with short hair.","When the two women saw the tall and broad Qin Yuanzheng, they both froze for a moment.","Deng Xiaozhen quickly recovered and said cheerfully, \"Oh my, our Regiment Commander Qin is here! Huiping, come, let me introduce you. This is Regiment Commander Qin Yuanzheng, the one I told you about. Yuanzheng, this is a female comrade from our textile factory. Her name is Wang Huiping.\"","Wang Huiping looked to be around thirty years old. She had short hair, a slightly plump figure, and a round face when she smiled, giving her a very amiable and kind appearance.","When she looked at Qin Yuanzheng, she seemed a bit shy. She nodded at him and said, \"Hello, Regiment Commander Qin. I am Wang Huiping.\"","Qin Yuanzheng glanced at her, nodding: \"Hello, I am Qin Yuanzheng. You can just call me by my name.\"","With that, the two were officially acquainted. Since the food was ready, the group sat down and had dinner together.","During the meal, Yang Wenyan and Deng Xiaozhen did most of the talking, while Wang Huiping would chime in occasionally.","The boy named Xiaoyuan, however, was exceptionally quiet, just focusing on his food without making a sound.","Qin Yuanzheng wasn't much of a talker either, so he just ate slowly. Once he finished, seeing that it was getting late, he prepared to take his leave.","Yang Wenyan held him back and asked in a low voice, \"So, what do you think?\"","Qin Yuanzheng didn't really have any particular thoughts. He remained silent for a few seconds before replying, \"I don't really have any thoughts on it.\"","Yang Wenyan: ...","Yang Wenyan clicked his tongue and said:","\"Comrade Wang Huiping has a good personality and a steady job. Plus, she already has a son, so it wouldn't matter if you two don't have kids after getting married. You're close in age, too. Isn't it a perfect match? So many people fall in love over time just by spending time together. You should interact with her more, just treat it as giving each other a chance, you know?\"","Over the past two years, Qin Yuanzheng had grown thoroughly annoyed by the constant nagging from his superiors and family regarding his marriage.","He fell silent again, pondering for a moment before saying, \"It's getting late. I'll walk Comrade Wang Huiping home.\"","By saying this, he was agreeing with Yang Wenyan's suggestion to spend some time together and see how things go.","Delighted, Yang Wenyan patted him on the shoulder and said, \"Now that's more like it. Make sure you talk to her a bit more on the way back. Don't be so quiet, understand?\"","Qin Yuanzheng nodded, put on his military overcoat, and stood by the door to wait.","A short while later, Wang Huiping also put on her coat and came out, holding her son's hand.","The two exchanged a glance, and Wang Huiping spoke up with a smile: \"Comrade Qin, our textile factory dormitory isn't far. I can walk back by myself. There's no need to trouble you to see me off.\"","Qin Yuanzheng: \"It's dark out and unsafe. I'd better take you back. Besides, the child shouldn't be exposed to the freezing cold, or he'll easily get sick.\"","As he said this, his mind drifted back to Qiao Lanshu, who was currently staying in the hospital.","That young girl caught a cold the moment she was exposed to a chilly breeze. Her constitution was incredibly fragile.","He walked to the entrance of the residential compound and opened the car door. It was Wang Huiping's first time riding in a car, so she became a bit tense, though the awe and envy in her eyes were unmistakable.","After all, it was a motor car. In this day and age, how many people could afford to drive a car?"]},{"number":6,"title":"Chapter 6: Find Her a Mature and Steady Partner","paragraphs":["Wang Huiping lived in the textile factory's dormitory, in a small one-bedroom apartment assigned to her by her workplace.","Qin Yuanzheng drove her to the entrance of her dormitory. Wang Huiping opened the car door herself and stepped out with her child.","She looked at the car, then at Qin Yuanzheng's military uniform, and smiled gently. \"Comrade Qin, I'll be heading back now.\"","Qin Yuanzheng nodded. He hesitated for a moment before saying, \"See you another day.\"","Hearing this, Wang Huiping immediately felt there was a chance. She smiled and nodded. \"Alright, I live right here and work at the textile factory. You can come find me at the factory.\"","Qin Yuanzheng agreed. He then glanced at Xiao Yuan, didn't say much else, and drove away.","In truth, Qin Yuanzheng actually liked children quite a bit.","In this day and age, there probably weren't many people who disliked children.","At the very least, he had once thought about taking a wife, having a few kids, and living a harmonious and beautiful life.","But now...","He decided to listen to his cousin's advice and try getting to know this female comrade, Wang Huiping. If their personalities meshed well, starting a family with her wouldn't be a bad idea.","As he drove and pondered, a thought suddenly struck him. He wondered if Staff Officer Lin had managed to dig up any information on that guy, Sun Mingyong.","With this in mind, he turned the steering wheel and headed toward the barracks in the mining district.","Half an hour later, Staff Officer Lin was standing in Qin Yuanzheng's dorm room.","Staff Officer Lin said, \"Regimental Commander, I've already gone over there to ask. The Independent Second Battalion doesn't have anyone named Sun Mingyong at all. Battalion Commander Zhao even specifically had each company bring out their roll call rosters to check, and we are certain there is no such person.\"","Staff Officer Lin was always meticulous in his work. He added,","\"I had them check the records for past discharges and transfers, but nothing came up. There were two people with the exact same name, but their ages and hometowns didn't match. One is in his forties, discharged due to injury a few years ago, and is a local. The other is a new recruit who just enlisted last year, only eighteen years old, and also from this province, not an outsider.\"","The information Qiao Lanshu had provided indicated that Sun Mingyong was a native of Yangcheng in the south and was twenty-six years old this year.","None of it matched up.","Qin Yuanzheng had actually already reached a conclusion.","That Sun Mingyong was likely just deliberately deceiving the young lady.","This kind of situation was actually quite common.","After all, in this era, with people separated by vast distances, someone could spout a bunch of nonsense in a letter and there was no way for the other party to verify it.","Qin Yuanzheng then said, \"Then go ask around the First and Third Battalions. Ask around our regiment too. I simply don't believe we can't find this guy.\"","Staff Officer Lin replied,","\"Regimental Commander, actually, I did go and ask the First and Third Battalions. The Third Battalion said there are no southerners named Sun Mingyong in the army. However, at the Chengbei Food Factory, which partners with our military cafeteria, there is an employee named Sun Mingyong. This Sun Mingyong works in the factory's business department and handles business liaison work. But whether it's exactly the man we're looking for, I'll have to go over and verify it tomorrow.\"","But regardless, Sun Mingyong was definitely not a military man. The young lady had certainly been scammed.","Qin Yuanzheng pondered for a few seconds and asked, \"Is this Sun Mingyong married?\"","Staff Officer Lin answered, \"Yes, he's married. His wife is the daughter of the food factory's director, and they have two children, a son and a daughter.\"","Qin Yuanzheng: \"...\"","With a dark expression, Qin Yuanzheng told Staff Officer Lin, \"Investigate this Sun Mingyong thoroughly.\"","If Sun Mingyong had really deceived the young lady while already having a family here, then he was guilty of marriage fraud. For a person like that, let alone joining the Party, even his job should be stripped from him.","...","Qin Yuanzheng went to the hospital that very night to visit Qiao Lanshu.","He looked inside from the doorway of the ward and saw the young woman sitting on the bed with her hair draped loosely over her shoulders. She was holding a piece of paper and writing a letter, presumably to send back home.","The girl looked very well-behaved and quiet. She indeed looked like someone who would be easy to deceive.","How could such a pretty and docile young woman survive without someone to protect her?","Qin Yuanzheng knocked and entered. When Qiao Lanshu saw him, her expression lit up with pleasant surprise. \"Regimental Commander Qin, are you here to see me?\"","She had thought that Qin Yuanzheng would have gone home by this hour.","To her surprise, he had just visited at noon and was here again now. She felt a flutter of excitement in her heart. \"Please, have a seat.\"","As she spoke, she busily pulled up a chair for him, grabbed a thermos to pour him some hot water, and then fetched a canned treat from the table to offer him.","The jar was a bit hard to open. She twisted it a couple of times but couldn't get the lid off.","Suddenly, Qin Yuanzheng walked over. The two of them were standing very close. She looked up and saw his strong, chiseled jawline.","Qin Yuanzheng hadn't taken off his overcoat yet. He was radiating body heat. He carried a faint scent of alcohol, mixed with the slightly pungent smell of coal and the chilly, crisp scent of cedar. The mingled scents felt warm and enveloping.","It was a scent that uniquely belonged to Qin Yuanzheng.","Qiao Lanshu's small face instantly flushed crimson.","Qin Yuanzheng took the jar from her hands. His hands were large and broad, rough on both the palms and the backs, with thick knuckles and long, slender fingers.","With a casual twist, he popped the lid open. He then handed the jar back to Qiao Lanshu and said, \"There you go.\"","Qiao Lanshu: \"...\"","Blushing, Qiao Lanshu took the jar back. She gave him a slightly shy glance and said, \"Thank you. You are so strong.\"","Qin Yuanzheng nodded with a wooden expression.","What did she mean by strong? He hadn't even used any force just now.","He sat down, looked at Qiao Lanshu's slightly flushed face, and sighed inwardly once again.","Seeing his hesitant expression, Qiao Lanshu guessed that he had probably found Sun Mingyong.","After all, it must be very easy for the military to track someone down.","She already knew the outcome, so she wasn't surprised at this moment.","She sat down, placed the open jar in front of Qin Yuanzheng, and asked softly, \"Regimental Commander Qin, coming over so late... do you have something to tell me?\"","Qin Yuanzheng nodded. Indecision was not in his nature, but at this very moment, he still felt a bit hesitant.","He was worried that the young lady wouldn't be able to handle the blow.","However, short-term pain was better than long-term suffering. Rather than letting her continue to be deceived, it was better to let her know the truth sooner rather than later.","So, Qin Yuanzheng explained Sun Mingyong's situation.","As he spoke, he kept a close eye on Qiao Lanshu's expression.","Then, just as he had expected, Qiao Lanshu began to cry.","She blinked her large, dark eyes twice, and two streams of tears rolled down her cheeks.","Qin Yuanzheng: \"...\"","Qiao Lanshu had fair skin, so when she cried, her nose turned red. Looking at him with teary eyes, she asked, \"Is it true? Then what should I do now?\"","Qin Yuanzheng: \"...\"","Qin Yuanzheng was nearly thirty years old and had even been to the battlefield. He considered his heart and body to be as hard as steel.","Yet, at this moment, his heart still softened.","He remained silent for a long while before finally saying, \"Don't cry. There are plenty of unmarried men in the military. Didn't you say you liked battalion commanders? I'll introduce one to you.\"","Qiao Lanshu: \"...\"","When did she ever say she liked battalion commanders?","After Qin Yuanzheng said this, he suddenly felt that it was a pretty good idea.","There were exactly two unmarried battalion commanders in their regiment.","They were his own soldiers; he knew better than anyone what kind of men they were.","He could definitely do a good job of vetting any potential suitors for the young lady.","For such a sweet girl, he absolutely had to find her someone mature, reliable, and caring. Otherwise, he just wouldn't be able to rest easy."]},{"number":7,"title":"Chapter 7: She Was Not Interested in Me","paragraphs":["Looking at Qin Yuanzheng's expression, Qiao Lanshu could tell he wasn't joking.","Suddenly, she was at a loss for what to do.","She had come all this way specifically for him, but the Qin Yuanzheng standing before her now was far too serious. Furthermore, he was older, heavily built, and had a somewhat fierce, intimidating look about him.","Coupled with his years of experience in the military, he exuded a deeply commanding presence.","As a young girl of seventeen or eighteen, even with the memories of her past life echoing in her mind, Qiao Lanshu didn't dare act too rashly at this moment.","She just sat there, nervously twisting the hem of her shirt with both hands, completely unsure of what to say.","She couldn't quite figure out what was going through his mind. He had been so passionate toward her in her past life, but that was the Qin Yuanzheng who was nearing forty.","It wasn't this younger version of him. She figured it might be best to spend a few more days together to deepen their understanding of one another.","Qin Yuanzheng, on the other hand, thought his own idea was brilliant.","After he finished speaking, he looked at the young girl sitting with her head bowed, twisting her shirt hem, and naturally assumed she was just being shy.","He stood up and said to her, Don't worry, little miss. Since your parents are thousands of miles away and you don't have any relatives or friends here, I'll take charge of your affairs for the time being. After all, I was the one who rescued you, and my old superior specifically asked me to check in on you.","In truth, his old superior's real intention had been for him to spend more time getting to know this sweet Southern girl, not just to act as her caretaker.","However, Qin Yuanzheng felt that Qiao Lanshu was far too innocent and young, so it never even crossed his mind to consider her in a romantic light.","Qiao Lanshu was lost for words. Meeting his gaze, which looked at her as if she were a mere child, she could only nod in agreement.","Qin Yuanzheng was a man of action. As soon as he returned to his quarters, he began working on the matter. He pulled up a list of all the unmarried officers, from the rank of platoon leader up to battalion commander, stationed within the three independent battalions surrounding Longcheng.","Naturally, there were also a few unmarried platoon and company commanders within his own regiment, so he added their names to the list as well.","His top picks were, of course, the battalion commanders, since officers of that rank were permitted to have their families live on base with them.","However, company and platoon commanders were acceptable alternatives. After all, Qiao Lanshu could simply find a job locally and settle down in the area.","He stayed up late in his dorm drawing up the list. He didn't even need to look up their personnel files; he was intimately familiar with every single one of them.","He started by filtering the candidates based on their character and family backgrounds. After crossing off a few names, he moved on to screening them by height and physical appearance.","After all, the girl was so sweet and gentle; he couldn't possibly pair her up with some fierce, rough-looking brute.","Given how pretty and adorable she was, he had to find someone decently handsome. Otherwise, wouldn't it be like planting a beautiful flower in a pile of cow dung?","Her family background was also quite impressive. Her father was the manager of a state-owned department store, and her stepmother was an elementary school teacher. Both parents were college-educated, and the girl herself had graduated from high school. Not only was she fair, affluent, and beautiful, but she was also a proper intellectual.","Therefore, the prospective groom's family conditions couldn't be too shabby either. It was true that there were plenty of uneducated men in the military, and those with a middle school diploma were few and far between.","However, the officers had almost all attended military academies, so their educational backgrounds weren't an issue. The real challenge was matching her family's social standing.","After a whole night of nitpicking, Qin Yuanzheng found himself utterly speechless. Staring at the list, he muttered, These guys really deserve to be single!","The handsome ones lacked a good physique; the ones with both good looks and a good build had terrible family backgrounds.","Out of the dozen or so names on the initial list, only two or three survived his rigorous screening.","Early the next morning, when he arrived at the mining district office, he glanced at Lin Yucheng, who was sweeping the floor. Suddenly, he asked, Staff Officer Lin, how old are you?","Commander, I'm two years younger than you. I turned twenty-seven this year, Lin Yucheng replied.","Lin Yucheng was twenty-seven, unmarried, and a local. Both his parents were employed workers, and he had three siblings, all of whom seemingly had stable jobs.","Qin Yuanzheng cast a critical eye over Lin Yucheng's height and facial features. Honestly, he was just average. Pairing him with that sweet girl was stretching it a bit.","Lin Yucheng felt a chill creep up his spine under the intense scrutiny. Fidgeting uncomfortably, he stammered, C-Commander, why are you staring at me like that?","It was giving him the creeps.","Qin Yuanzheng remained silent for a few seconds before saying, You know about the girl I rescued a few days ago, right?","Lin Yucheng nodded, looking back at him. Yeah, what about her? Do you need me to drop her off at the train station?","Qin Yuanzheng was speechless.","Feigning nonchalance, Qin Yuanzheng said, Her fiance, Sun Mingyong, turned out to be a con artist, as you know. It's truly pitiful, she traveled thousands of miles looking for her man, completely unaware she was being deceived. You're not married yet, are you? Perfect. Go over there and see if you two hit it off.","Lin Yucheng was completely bewildered.","He instantly flushed with embarrassment. Scratching the back of his head, he stammered, I-isn't that a bit inappropriate? Commander, do you really think I'm good enough?","Qin Yuanzheng narrowed his eyes at him. What's inappropriate about it? Just go over and let her have a look at you. Sure, you're a bit of a downgrade for her, but if you clean yourself up nicely, you won't be an absolute eyesore.","Lin Yucheng was speechless.","...","And so, Lin Yucheng put genuine effort into grooming himself. He wore a crisp, perfectly pressed military uniform and his military cap. He had shaved his face clean, gotten a fresh haircut, and even trimmed his fingernails.","Carrying two jars of canned oranges and a pound of brown sugar, he arrived at the hospital on a bitterly cold afternoon with the north wind howling.","Qiao Lanshu was sitting on her hospital bed, her back ramrod straight and her hands resting politely on her knees, with her long hair cascading freely down her shoulders.","She looked at Lin Yucheng with mild curiosity, thinking to herself that the suitor Commander Qin had introduced was indeed a fine-looking young man.","It was just a pity he was a bit too fair-skinned and polished. She preferred dark-skinned, rugged, and tough men like Commander Qin.","Sitting across from Qiao Lanshu and being stared at so intently, Lin Yucheng's face flushed bright red. He was so nervous he didn't even know what to do with his hands.","Hello, Comrade Qiao Lanshu, he said stiffly. I am the Chief of Staff of the 21st Regiment of the Longcheng Construction Corps. My name is Lin Yucheng. I'm twenty-seven years old and a Longcheng local.","Qiao Lanshu nodded politely and replied, Hello.","Lin Yucheng waited for her to introduce herself, but after saying that single word of greeting, Qiao Lanshu simply fell silent.","He glanced over and saw the adorable, well-behaved girl looking down, absentmindedly poking at her quilt out of sheer boredom.","Lin Yucheng was speechless once again.","Well, the message couldn't be any clearer. The girl simply wasn't interested in him.","A wave of disappointment washed over Lin Yucheng. He wanted to strike up a conversation, but Qiao Lanshu gave him absolutely nothing to work with. Sitting there in silence was too awkward to bear.","As a result, he quickly excused himself and left the room.","From the moment he walked through the door to the moment he left, less than ten minutes had passed.","The moment Lin Yucheng stepped out of the ward and reached the bottom of the stairs, he was nearly startled out of his skin by Qin Yuanzheng, who was lurking right by the staircase!","C-Commander! Lin Yucheng gasped in shock. What are you doing standing here?","Didn't he know that sneaking up on people like that could give someone a heart attack?","Clad in a heavy military overcoat with his hands shoved deep into his pockets, Qin Yuanzheng stared at Lin Yucheng. Well? How did it go? Why did you come out so fast?","Before Lin Yucheng could answer, Qin Yuanzheng's tone suddenly turned fierce. Don't tell me you didn't like her?","Frightened by his stern tone, Lin Yucheng ducked his head slightly and hurriedly explained, \"No, Commander, it was the girl who didn't like me. She couldn't even be bothered to say a word to me.\"","Qin Yuanzheng: \"...\"","The fierce glare in Qin Yuanzheng's eyes instantly faded.","He rubbed his nose. \"So she was the one who didn't fancy you. Well, that makes perfect sense. You're pretty average anyway.\"","Lin Yucheng: \"...\"","Lin Yucheng was utterly speechless. He had already suffered enough blows to his ego today, yet his commander still had to mock him like this.","Qin Yuanzheng turned around and walked away. \"Guess you just don't have the luck for it. Come on, let's get back to work.\"","Lin Yucheng: \"...\""]},{"number":8,"title":"Chapter 8: She Cried","paragraphs":["After Staff Officer Lin left, Qiao Lanshu went to bed to rest.","She had been in the hospital for two days. Her cold from the freezing weather had improved a lot, and she could not stay in the hospital forever.","So, the next day, she took out ten yuan and asked a hospital nurse to help her buy a padded cotton jacket.","Although the supply and marketing cooperative sold cotton and fabric, ready-to-wear clothes were scarce. It was especially difficult to find clothes that fit someone with her petite frame.","Therefore, the nurse told her directly, \"How about this: I will charge you five yuan, and you do not need to give me any cotton ration coupons. I will give you a set of cotton-padded clothes and trousers I just made for myself. They might be a bit big, but can you make do with them?\"","This was because the military officers in the unit took great care of Qiao Lanshu.","And since Qiao Lanshu was a Southerner, young, and spoke with a gentle and soft voice, even the doctors and nurses took good care of her.","So, hearing the nurse's offer, Qiao Lanshu was extremely grateful. \"Okay, thank you so much, Sister.\"","Her sweet way of calling her Sister delighted the nurse, who replied, \"I will give you two pairs of socks as well. It is cold here, and you will not survive without thick socks.\"","Qiao Lanshu thanked her profusely again.","The weather was not considered too cold yet. When winter truly arrived, just a cotton jacket and thick socks would not be enough.","However, by that time, Qiao Lanshu might not even be here anymore.","A wave of disappointment washed over her.","She liked Qin Yuanzheng, but from what she could tell, he seemed to only see her as a child.","Wearing the cotton jacket, trousers, and thick socks the nurse had brought her, Qiao Lanshu packed her belongings and went through the discharge procedures.","Her cold was much better, though she still had a runny nose and a rather heavy nasal voice.","The padded jacket and trousers were a bit large, so she rolled up the pant legs and sleeves twice. Then, she braided her long hair into two thick, shiny black braids before carrying her bundle out of the hospital.","Before leaving, she specifically instructed the nurse, \"Sister, if Regiment Commander Qin comes looking for me, please tell him I have gone to stay at the guesthouse.\"","The nurse smiled and agreed.","Terrified that Qin Yuanzheng would not be able to find her when he came, Qiao Lanshu repeated the message to the guard at the main gate as she walked out of the hospital.","She first took all her things to the guesthouse and used her letter of introduction to book a room.","Then, taking advantage of the fine weather and bright sun, she hurried off to the supply and marketing cooperative to do some shopping.","She still had to stay here for a few days, so she needed to buy daily necessities like a towel and a washbasin, as well as some food.","Actually, her hands, face, and even her lips felt a bit dry and itchy, but she did not have any ration coupons for skincare products. She wondered what the locals used to moisturize their faces.","With these thoughts in mind, she walked all the way to the nearby supply and marketing cooperative.","Fortunately, the guesthouse, the cooperative, and the hospital were not far from each other. She could get there with just a half-hour walk.","As she neared the entrance of the cooperative, her footsteps suddenly halted, and her gaze locked fiercely onto a specific direction.","Sun Mingyong was wearing the uniform of a food factory worker, accompanied by a young woman in the same uniform.","The woman was also holding the hand of a five- or six-year-old boy.","The two emerged from the supply and marketing cooperative, both carrying things in their hands.","Sun Mingyong was from Yangcheng. He had traveled north at the age of fifteen, penniless and without anyone to rely on at the time.","Relying on the relationship between his late father and the Qiao family, he received financial support from Father Qiao. Over the years, the money and grain the Qiao family had sent him probably amounted to over a thousand yuan.","That was no small sum.","After not seeing him for many years, Sun Mingyong had grown taller, but his facial features had not changed much.","With a dark and gloomy expression, Qiao Lanshu stared fixedly at Sun Mingyong. Waiting until they left the cooperative, she immediately followed behind him, tailing them all the way to the food factory's dormitory area.","Sensing someone behind him, Sun Mingyong glanced back. His heart instantly skipped a beat, and he blurted out subconsciously, \"Lanshu...\"","Sun Mingyong's wife turned to look at him. \"Huh? What did you say?\"","Sun Mingyong forced a smile. \"Ah, I was just saying that I left some reference books at the factory and need to go back and get them. You two go on home first; I will be right back.\"","His wife suspected nothing and nodded. \"Hurry up then, I will go back and start cooking.\"","Sun Mingyong nodded, then turned and strode briskly over.","Qiao Lanshu stood outside the main gate of the food factory's dormitory area. It was exactly the time when everyone was having lunch.","Both Sun Mingyong and his wife worked at the food factory and had taken advantage of their lunch break to go shopping and bring their child home to eat.","He walked up to Qiao Lanshu, looked around, and seeing that no one was nearby, asked in a low, caring voice, \"Shushu, what are you doing here?\"","Qiao Lanshu sneered. \"Why do you think I am here?\"","Sun Mingyong played dumb, saying, \"If you were coming, why did you not write me a letter in advance? Or send a telegram so I could pick you up. It is different here from Yangcheng. The climate is dry and cold. A girl like you will not be able to adapt to it.\"","As he spoke, he took a ten-yuan note out of his pocket and handed it to Qiao Lanshu. \"Lanshu, take this and buy yourself something. You have never suffered any hardships since you were little, so do not let yourself suffer here either.\"","Initially, Qiao Lanshu did not want the money, but on second thought, this was all her father's money anyway, so why should she not take it?","She accepted the money and then said, \"How could ten yuan possibly be enough? It is so cold here, I need to buy some good things. Did you not just say I should not suffer any hardships?\"","Sun Mingyong's face darkened, but he did not say anything else. Instead, he took out the remaining five ten-yuan notes from his pocket and handed them all to Qiao Lanshu. \"Sixty yuan, is that enough?\"","Qiao Lanshu took all sixty yuan before looking at Sun Mingyong with a faint, mocking smile.","\"Well, well, Sun Mingyong. I remember when you first left home, you did not even have a single penny in your pocket. My dad bought your train ticket, and he found someone to exchange grain coupons for you. Even the clothes and shoes you wore were made from fabric provided by our family... Now, you are handing out ten-yuan notes without batting an eye. It seems you have become quite wealthy.\"","Hearing Qiao Lanshu's words, Sun Mingyong knew she was being sarcastic.","But he did not want to blow things out of proportion right now.","After all, the woman he married was the daughter of the food factory's director.","If it had not been for that, he would not have landed a job at the food factory, let alone in the leisurely sales department where he spent his days rubbing elbows with cadres from various departments.","Sun Mingyong looked around, and after ensuring no one was watching, he grabbed Qiao Lanshu's arm and whispered, \"Lanshu, this is not the place to talk. You haven't eaten yet, right? The state-run restaurant here has local dishes; let me take you out to eat.\"","Qiao Lanshu wrenched her arm free from his grasp. She was not tall and did not have much strength.","So, she furiously jumped up and slapped him hard across the face.","Although it did not hurt much, the slap still left Sun Mingyong utterly bewildered.","Qiao Lanshu's expression was icy. \"Sun Mingyong, it has already come to this, and you still are not going to give me an explanation?\"","What she hated was not that Sun Mingyong had married someone else; after all, there was no emotional foundation between the two of them.","What she hated was the fact that Sun Mingyong had already started a family and had a child, yet he still dragged her along and deceived her family. He had pocketed every single cent and food coupon her father had sent.","Before, she had even wondered: were military officers really that poor?","Now she knew the truth—he had been using her family's money to support his own wife and child!","Sun Mingyong covered his face, but he didn't lash out.","He merely frowned and said with a defeated look,","\"Lanshu, you grew up surrounded by wealth and comfort. Both your parents are capable people. As a pampered young lady, what could you possibly understand? You have no idea how hard it was for me. When I first came here, I didn't even have a place to live; I had to sleep in a cave dwelling! The army wouldn't take me, and I couldn't find a job. Do you know how difficult that was? I almost froze to death in the heavy snow, do you know that?\"","Qiao Lanshu found it laughable. She was someone who had to survive under the thumb of a stepmother; how easy could her life have been?","Sun Mingyong only nearly froze to death, he didn't actually die!","She looked at him with a cold expression. \"So what? So you took the money my dad gave you, disguised yourself as a wealthy young master from the South, and came here to commit marriage fraud, is that it?\"","She pointed a finger at him. \"You just wait. I'm going straight to your workplace to report you! I'll make sure you lose your job and get sent to a labor farm to clear wastelands!\"","Hearing this, Sun Mingyong was genuinely terrified.","He grabbed Qiao Lanshu's hand in a death grip, a flash of ruthlessness crossing his eyes. \"Qiao Lanshu! What exactly do you want? Are you trying to ruin me?\"","Of course, Qiao Lanshu didn't mean it—even if she was going to report him, it wouldn't be right now.","She was no match for him physically.","In her past life, if she hadn't escaped and received help from the Women's Federation, Sun Mingyong wouldn't have even admitted to the marriage fraud!","This time, Qiao Lanshu thought, she would still send him to a labor camp!","For a gentleman, ten years is never too late to take revenge.","Being yanked by Sun Mingyong, her arm hurt so much that tears welled up in her eyes.","Taking advantage of the situation, she pretended to look utterly heartbroken and said, \"I traveled thousands of miles to find you, thinking I could join you as a military spouse, only to find out you've been lying to me. Do you know how devastated I am?\"","Seeing her cry, Sun Mingyong loosened his grip slightly.","After all, he had truly liked Qiao Lanshu in the past. She was well-behaved, quiet, and beautiful.","When he was young and followed his father to the Qiao household for the first time, he had secretly fallen in love with her.","He had also once fantasized about marrying her as a proud military officer.","But the army rejected him, so he had to find another way out.","Otherwise, as a poor boy with no family backing and not even a job, the Qiao family would definitely look down on him.","He didn't want to live his whole life in the shadow of the Qiao family, subject to their whims and moods.","He took out a handkerchief to wipe away her tears.","\"Don't cry, Lanshu. I really had my difficulties. This time, I've let you down, and I am truly sorry. Whatever you want, just ask. But I beg you, please don't report me. I worked so hard to get this job; please don't ruin my future, okay?\"","Qiao Lanshu glanced at his handkerchief in disgust and didn't take it. She said, \"Since we are ending things, let's make a clean break. Over the years, the money and food coupons my dad sent you must amount to at least eight hundred, if not a thousand. Just give me a thousand yuan and another five hundred in national food coupons, and we'll call it even.\"","Sun Mingyong was speechless.","His face darkened as he muttered, \"A thousand yuan, and five hundred in food coupons...\"","Qiao Lanshu glared at him. \"Don't tell me you're refusing to pay it back!\"","Her eyes were dark and bright. Even when she glared, she didn't look angry; in fact, she looked incredibly cute.","Sun Mingyong stared blankly at her face, swallowed hard, and then said, \"No, I mean, I can scrape together a thousand yuan, but five hundred in national food coupons is a bit difficult. I can give you at most two hundred in national coupons and three hundred in local coupons. Will that work?\"","Money was just a worldly possession. As long as he could keep his job and his marriage remained intact, he could quickly earn the money back.","Right now, all he needed to do was placate Qiao Lanshu and put her on a train back to the South, and everything would be perfectly fine.","Sun Mingyong immediately added, \"Give me two days. Two days from now, at this exact time, come to the back door of the food factory in the north of the city. I'll give you the money and the coupons, okay?\"","Qiao Lanshu nodded. \"Fine.\"","Then, she turned around and walked away.","Sun Mingyong wanted to say something more to her but didn't dare to chase after her.","With a dark expression, Qiao Lanshu walked out of the food factory's dormitory area and headed to the cooperative store to buy some things.","She pondered in her heart: as soon as she got her hands on the money and coupons, she would immediately write a letter to report Sun Mingyong!","That bastard shouldn't even dream of having a good life for the rest of his days!","...","Using the sixty yuan she had taken from Sun Mingyong earlier, Qiao Lanshu bought some daily necessities at the cooperative store, such as a washbasin, a towel, soap, and a toothbrush.","Then, she wanted to buy some fresh fruits and vegetables. After all, she hadn't had any of those during her two days in the hospital.","But when she went over to look, there were hardly any fresh fruits or vegetables available.","Instead, the shelves were filled with all sorts of canned goods.","With a frown, she bought a radish, a few potatoes, some biscuits, and noodles, then walked out of the store carrying her purchases.","On her way back to the guesthouse, she passed by the county textile factory building. Suddenly, she saw Qin Yuanzheng accompanying a female worker from the factory. The woman was leading a young boy by the hand. They were walking along the street, heading to who knows where.","This scene felt inexplicably familiar, didn't it?","Qiao Lanshu thought of when she had just run into Sun Mingyong—it had been the exact same harmonious picture of a family of three.","Qiao Lanshu was speechless.","When she saw Sun Mingyong's family of three, she had felt nothing but anger.","But now, seeing Qin Yuanzheng's family of three, she felt an inexplicable tightness in her chest.","Before she could even process it, tears were already streaming down her face.","Qiao Lanshu wiped the corners of her eyes and walked dejectedly toward the guesthouse with her bags.","So it turned out that Qin Yuanzheng was not only married at this time, but he also had a child?","But the Qin Yuanzheng in her past life had told her that he was single and had never been married.","Let alone having a child.","What on earth was going on?","...","In truth, Qin Yuanzheng hadn't planned on meeting Wang Huiping so soon, but he passed by the textile factory every day on his way to the military headquarters.","Today had just been a coincidence. He happened to run into Wang Huiping and her son at the factory gates. Since they bumped into each other, they walked together for a bit and chatted for a while.","His feelings about interacting with Wang Huiping were actually quite bland. He couldn't say he liked it, but he didn't dislike it either.","When they talked, Wang Huiping would accommodate him, and the child was quiet, so everything felt just fine.","But just fine was all it was.","Qin Yuanzheng escorted Wang Huiping and her son back to the textile factory, then went to the mining area to handle some business.","When he returned in the afternoon, he habitually made a turn toward the hospital and drove right up to the entrance.","As it turned out, the nurses told him that the young lady had recovered, been discharged, and had gone to the guesthouse.","Could a young girl like her manage living in a guesthouse all by herself?","Was it even safe?","With a frown, he drove off toward the guesthouse.","Upon arriving at the front desk of the guest house, he made a quick inquiry. The receptionist immediately replied, \"Comrade, are you looking for Comrade Qiao Lanshu? She is in Room 203 on the second floor. Here is a visitor's pass, take it.\"","Qin Yuanzheng accepted the pass and was just about to head upstairs when the clerk suddenly spoke up again.","\"By the way, that young girl came back crying this afternoon. Her eyes were completely swollen from it. I asked her if she had run into some trouble, but she wouldn't say a word. You're her friend, right? You should go up and check on her. The poor thing, all alone out here, it breaks your heart...\"","Qin Yuanzheng stopped in his tracks, his expression instantly darkening. \"She was crying?\""]},{"number":9,"title":"Chapter 9: Don't Make a Decision So Quickly","paragraphs":["Qiao Lanshu returned to the guesthouse, rubbing her hands together from the cold.","As soon as she got back to her room, she hurriedly poured half a basin of hot water to soak her feet. It took quite a while for her to warm up.","The guesthouse had heating connected to the mining area. Once winter arrived, boiler workers in the mining area were responsible for heating water, so the guesthouse was relatively warm, given its close proximity.","Qiao Lanshu was truly having a hard time adapting to the climate here; it was just too terribly cold.","She was now genuinely afraid of the cold.","So, skipping her meal, she climbed straight into bed after soaking her feet and burrowed under the covers.","The room was extremely dry. Her lips were cracked and bleeding, and a few red rashes had broken out on her fair, tender skin. They felt dry and itchy to the touch, and she had no idea what was causing them, which made her feel quite distressed.","Maybe she should just give up on getting revenge. She could take the thousand yuan and the food coupons, hand in the report letter, buy a train ticket, and just go back to Yangcheng.","To suffer here for a scumbag like Sun Mingyong felt somewhat unworthy to her.","Besides, the reason she had wanted to stay—Qin Yuanzheng—already had a wife and children. If she stayed any longer, it would be somewhat ridiculous.","However, she was also worried at the same time. If she did not want to marry, she would have to go down to the countryside to work after returning home.","She had heard that working in the countryside was very bitter and exhausting, requiring one to do farm work under the scorching sun and biting wind.","She didn't know if she would be able to handle it.","Deep in thought, Qiao Lanshu began to seriously consider her future.","Lying in bed, she wrapped herself tightly in the blankets, holding a cup of hot water and taking small sips.","Because the room was so dry, she really wanted to drink water, but she didn't dare to drink too much for fear of having to go to the bathroom frequently. It was so cold that she didn't even want to take her pants off.","Just as she was thinking this, a knock came from outside the door.","Qiao Lanshu asked warily, \"Who is it?\"","Qin Yuanzheng's voice rang out from outside the door, \"Comrade Qiao Lanshu, it's me, Qin Yuanzheng.\"","Qiao Lanshu's eyes lit up. Throwing off the covers, she immediately jumped out of bed.","However, after taking just two steps, she suddenly paused, and the look of pleasant surprise instantly faded into disappointment.","She walked to the door, opened it, and looked at Qin Yuanzheng reservedly. \"Commander Qin, it's so late. Why did you come over?\"","Qin Yuanzheng glanced at his watch. Wasn't it only six o'clock in the evening? It wasn't that late, was it?","Seeing Qiao Lanshu standing at the door with no intention of inviting him in, his eyes flickered, but he didn't say much.","Instead, he took a step back and handed over the items he was carrying. Looking at Qiao Lanshu's somewhat cracked lips, he said, \"Comrade Xiao Qiao, I saw that you are having a bit of trouble adapting to the climate here, so I bought this for you. See if you can use it.\"","Qiao Lanshu took it and took a look, finding that the paper bag contained two jars of vanishing cream and a small jar of sheep oil ointment.","She had seen vanishing cream before, but this sheep oil ointment was new to her. She picked it up curiously to examine it, and Qin Yuanzheng explained to her, \"I heard from the female comrades at the supply and marketing cooperative that this sheep oil can be applied to the lips, and it's harmless even if accidentally ingested. It can also be used on the hands and feet.\"","Qiao Lanshu had a small, cherry-like mouth. Her lips were naturally moist and supple, but now they were dry, cracked, and peeling.","Looking at these items, Qiao Lanshu cast a strange look at Qin Yuanzheng.","Qin Yuanzheng was taking care of Qiao Lanshu as if she were a child, and he didn't think there was anything inappropriate about buying these things for her.","But for Qiao Lanshu, wasn't it a bit strange for a male comrade to buy such things for a female comrade?","Qin Yuanzheng asked her, \"What's wrong? You don't like it?\"","He had specially found someone to exchange for daily necessity coupons and then went to the supply and marketing cooperative to buy them.","He said, \"The cooperative only has this kind of vanishing cream. They don't carry the brands from Yangcheng. Otherwise, how about I write a letter to my comrade-in-arms and ask him to buy some from Shanghai and mail them over?\"","How could Qiao Lanshu trouble Qin Yuanzheng like that?","She quickly said, \"No need, this is already very good. I was just needing this. Thank you so much, Commander Qin. Let me give you the money for it.\"","As she spoke, she hurriedly reached into her pocket, pulled out a ten-yuan bill, and tried to press it into Qin Yuanzheng's hand.","As soon as Qin Yuanzheng saw her taking out money, his face immediately darkened. He said, \"Comrade Xiao Qiao, you don't need to give me money. I am also following orders from my superiors to come and take care of you. These things didn't cost much, so don't take it to heart.\"","Qiao Lanshu: \"...\"","Qiao Lanshu's mood instantly worsened. She looked up at Qin Yuanzheng and murmured, \"So it was because of orders from your superiors?\"","She knew it. How could a cold and tough man like Qin Yuanzheng be so good to her?","Buying things for her and even introducing potential marriage partners to her.","Qin Yuanzheng watched as Qiao Lanshu's sparkling eyes instantly dimmed, her eyelids drooping.","He didn't know what he had said wrong, nor could he figure out why the young lady was suddenly unhappy again.","Looking at Qiao Lanshu's slightly reddened eyes, he guessed that she had been crying over her fiancé.","So, he comforted Qiao Lanshu, saying, \"Don't be sad. You didn't like the one I introduced last time, right? I'll introduce you to another one tomorrow. I guarantee his character is impeccable.\"","Qiao Lanshu: \"...\"","Qiao Lanshu hastily said, \"There's no need, Commander Qin, really no need. You don't have to introduce anyone to me anymore.\"","Qin Yuanzheng: \"...\"","Qin Yuanzheng looked at her face and asked, \"Why? Are you going back to Yangcheng?\"","Qiao Lanshu scratched her head. \"If I can't stay, then I have no choice but to go back.\"","Qin Yuanzheng: \"...\"","Yangcheng was over two thousand kilometers away from here. Taking the train required two transfers, and the journey would take several days.","If she returned to Yangcheng from here, she would definitely never come back.","Qin Yuanzheng didn't know what he was thinking, but subconsciously, he didn't really want Qiao Lanshu to leave. He said:","\"You're just a young girl; you don't know how harsh the countryside can be. Settling down here and finding a job is always better than going down to the countryside. Besides, even if you want to go back, you should find a man to accompany you. The journey is too far and unsafe.\"","He thought for a moment and added, \"It just so happens that there are many unmarried military officers here. I can introduce one to you, which is better than going back and going on blind dates by yourself. What do you say?\"","After all, she had already been deceived once. This young lady was a bit naive. If she was tricked again, she wouldn't have a man like him to help her.","Qin Yuanzheng continued, \"You should meet a few more people. Don't make a decision so quickly.\"","Qiao Lanshu looked at him, feeling a sudden impulse. She asked, \"Commander Qin, what about you? Are you married?\"","Qin Yuanzheng: \"???\"","Taken aback by her question, Qin Yuanzheng was momentarily stunned. A strange feeling welled up inside him as he wondered why the young lady would ask such a thing.","He kept a straight face and said, \"My situation is rather special, so it's not convenient to tell you.\"","He couldn't very well tell a teenage girl that he suffered from infertility. So, after saying that, Qin Yuanzheng left, as it was hard to explain anyway.","...","Qin Yuanzheng was a man of his word. The very next day, he arranged for a battalion commander to come over and deliver sweet potatoes to Qiao Lanshu.","The young battalion commander was tall and handsome. Dressed in a crisp military uniform, he walked over holding a bag of sweet potatoes. The moment he laid eyes on Qiao Lanshu, his entire face flushed red.","Stuttering slightly, the young battalion commander said, \"Comrade Xiao... Xiao Qiao, hello. These are sweet potatoes grown by our unit. They are very sweet. Our commander asked me to bring some over for you to try.\"","With that, he shoved the sweet potatoes into Qiao Lanshu's arms.","Qiao Lanshu: \"...\"","Holding the sweet potatoes, Qiao Lanshu looked up at the soldier standing before her. Her voice was gentle, but her words were completely ruthless.","She said, \"I am sorry, Comrade, but I do not think you are my type. We are not a good match. Could you go back and tell your commander that we should just forget about it this time, okay?\"","The young soldier was taken aback. His face still completely red, he stuttered and nodded instinctively, saying, \"O-okay.\"","Qiao Lanshu then asked, \"So, can I still eat these sweet potatoes?\"","Blushing, the young soldier nodded. \"Y-yes, you can.\"","\"Then please thank your commander for me,\" Qiao Lanshu replied.","With that, she took the sweet potatoes back inside and closed the door.","The young soldier stared at the closed door and let out a silent sigh.","It was such a pity that such a wonderful girl was not interested in him."]},{"number":10,"title":"Chapter 10: Repaying the Money","paragraphs":["Over the past two days, Qiao Lanshu had met with two more company commanders on blind dates. She honestly had to admire Qin Yuanzheng.","He seemed incredibly persistent about setting her up with military officers.","But the truth was, she wasn't dead set on marrying an officer.","Originally, Qiao Lanshu had wanted to marry Qin Yuanzheng. However, once she realized that was impossible, she dropped the idea entirely.","Now, her only focus was to settle the matter with Sun Mingyong so she could pack up and return to Yangcheng.","Once she got back, she would have her father buy her a job. She really had no desire to be sent down to the countryside.","Meanwhile, Sun Mingyong had been running himself ragged over the past few days trying to scrape together a thousand yuan and five hundred yuan's worth of food stamps.","He didn't dare breathe a word of this to his wife, so he had to figure it out all by himself.","In just two days, he had borrowed money from almost every colleague and friend at the factory.","But while he could hide this from others, he couldn't keep it from his father-in-law.","After all, his father-in-law was Wei Zhengye, a director at the food factory.","One day, Wei Zhengye tracked him down and asked with a dark expression, Mingyong, I hear you've been going around asking to borrow money the last couple of days?","Stared down by his father-in-law, Sun Mingyong broke into a cold sweat. He hurried to explain, Dad, it's like this. My mother has fallen ill. They sent me a telegram from home saying her condition isn't very optimistic. I can't go back right now, so I thought I'd send them some money and food stamps.","Wei Zhengye had only one daughter and no sons, and he doted on her as the apple of his eye. Although he hadn't explicitly demanded that Sun Mingyong marry into their family as a live-in son-in-law, the current situation wasn't much different from it.","Hearing this, Wei Zhengye looked somewhat surprised. Your mother? Didn't you say she was a primary school teacher in Yangcheng? She was perfectly fine last month, how did she suddenly become severely ill this month?","Sun Mingyong put on a bitter smile. Alas, who could have predicted it? Life is full of uncertainties. Even though I really want to go back, work at the factory has been so busy lately, and the children need to go to school. They can't do without me...","He phrased it this way specifically to curry favor with his father-in-law.","By showing that he wouldn't abandon his duties even when his mother was gravely ill, he knew Wei Zhengye would think more highly of him.","Sure enough, when Wei Zhengye heard this and realized his son-in-law had no intention of leaving, he felt quite satisfied.","Since that's the case, you should have come to me, Wei Zhengye said. When you run into trouble, you should turn to your family to solve it. There's no need to borrow money from outsiders.","He paused, then asked, How much are you still short?","Dad, there's no need, Sun Mingyong replied immediately. I can manage it myself. Besides, I've already scraped together enough money. I'm going to take the afternoon off to go wire the funds.","Hearing this, Wei Zhengye didn't press the matter further.","He hadn't really intended to give Sun Mingyong much money anyway. After all, he was just a son-in-law, not a son. Why give him so much money? What if the guy took the money and ran?","After leaving the factory, Sun Mingyong took out the cash he had scraped together and counted it. It was exactly a thousand yuan.","He had enough food stamps now, too.","But the mountain of debt he had just taken on would likely take him two or three years to pay off completely.","Fortunately, he had managed to fob off his father-in-law, so he wouldn't have to worry about his wife asking any questions later on.","Clutching the money, Sun Mingyong went to the back gate of the food factory and waited for Qiao Lanshu to arrive.","Truth be told, handing over so much money all at once made him physically sick.","He only earned forty yuan a month. Though he occasionally made a little under-the-table income through his connections in the sales department, it wasn't much.","A thousand yuan was the equivalent of two full years' salary.","And that wasn't even counting the five hundred yuan's worth of food stamps.","This Qiao Lanshu really had the nerve to ask for so much!","Qiao Lanshu showed up shortly after. The mere sight of Sun Mingyong filled her with a visceral disgust. Too repulsed to even waste words on him, she simply held out her hand. Where's the money?","Sun Mingyong looked at Qiao Lanshu, who was bundled up tightly in a gray padded cotton jacket and a large scarf, leaving only her small face exposed. With immense reluctance, he pulled out the cash and the stamps, and said,","Lanshu, since you're taking the money, consider our business settled. Don't mention a word of this to my wife. Also, when you get home, please explain things to your father. Tell him I had my own difficulties and didn't mean to treat you this way...","Qiao Lanshu snatched the cash and stamps from his hand and shot him a withering glare. You talk too much.","With that, she spun on her heel and walked away, not bothering to say another word to him.","Sun Mingyong: ...","As he watched Qiao Lanshu's retreating back, a dark, vicious look flashed through Sun Mingyong's eyes."]},{"number":11,"title":"Chapter 11: Followed and Kidnapped","paragraphs":["Although giving the money to Qiao Lanshu was meant to put an end to their past, Sun Mingyong still couldn't put his mind at ease.","That was why he spent the entire day keeping a close eye on the food factory's security office, terrified that Qiao Lanshu might drop off a whistleblowing letter.","Fortunately, right up until the end of his shift, there was no sign of her.","Sun Mingyong was usually the first to leave work, but today, he dragged his feet.","He waited until everyone else had gone and the sky was growing dark before finally dawdling out of his office.","Wrapping his heavy coat tightly around himself, he walked toward the main gate, just as a man in his thirties stepped out of the security office.","This man was a temporary worker at the security office. He was from the countryside, in his early thirties, unmarried, and didn't even have a girlfriend.","He was tall and scrawny with a pockmarked face. As soon as he spotted Sun Mingyong, he hurried over. \"Supervisor Sun, working late today?\"","Sun Mingyong was merely a salesman, nowhere near a supervisor level.","But that was just how Niu Li was; he flattered everyone by calling them \"supervisor.\"","Seeing him, Sun Mingyong felt a surge of irritation. \"Niu Li, did you need something from me?\"","Niu Li strolled over, threw an arm around Sun Mingyong's shoulders, and lowered his voice. \"I saw everything at noon. Come on, tell me, who was that young girl? She's quite a looker.\"","Sun Mingyong's face instantly darkened.","Niu Li was a temp at the security office. Earlier that morning, he must have been manning the back gate.","Who knew where he had been hiding? Sun Mingyong certainly hadn't noticed him.","Niu Li continued, \"Supervisor Sun, that's not very fair of you. If it weren't for my help back then, you wouldn't have even made it through the factory gates. What, now that you know a pretty girl, you're not going to introduce us?\"","Truth be told, when Sun Mingyong was down on his luck and looking for a job at the factory, Niu Li had merely opened the gate for him. Yet, even now, Niu Li never missed a chance to bring it up.","Sun Mingyong scoffed. \"The girl is only eighteen. How old are you?\"","Niu Li's eyes lit up. \"Eighteen? Eighteen is perfect! I saw you give her quite a bit of money, didn't I? If you set us up, I'll pay you back every last cent. How about it?\"","Sun Mingyong: \"...\"","Truth be told, Sun Mingyong was actually tempted.","He had given Qiao Lanshu so much money, yet he still had to live in constant fear that she might write a letter to report him.","Rather than dealing with that, it would be much better to find a man for her—someone who could keep her in line.","As for her parents, all he had to do was send them a letter or a telegram to stall for time, and he could easily string them along for ages.","It really was a brilliant idea.","Why hadn't he thought of this earlier?","The only downside was that Qiao Lanshu was so pretty; it felt like a waste to hand her over to Pockmarked Niu.","With this in mind, Sun Mingyong didn't agree right away. Instead, he said,","\"Well, I'll have to ask the girl what she thinks. She came all the way here from Yangcheng. She has no family or friends in this city and has been staying at a guesthouse. If I don't look out for her, no one else will. Give me a few days, and I'll find some time to ask her about it.\"","A gleam flashed in Niu Li's eyes as he repeated, \"She's from Yangcheng? What's a young girl like her doing all the way out here with no family or friends?\"","\"To find a husband, of course,\" Sun Mingyong replied. \"Never mind, you wouldn't understand. Let me talk to her first, and we'll see.\"","With that, Sun Mingyong hurried away.","Niu Li stood at the factory gates, chewing over Sun Mingyong's words.","A young girl like that, with no family or friends around to protect her... wouldn't she be as easy to handle as a helpless little rabbit?","The next day, Sun Mingyong kept an eye on the security office again, but there were still no whistleblowing letters to be seen.","As for that temp, Niu Li, he hadn't shown up for work today.","Sun Mingyong cast a discreet glance at the security office before heading to his own desk.","Meanwhile, Qiao Lanshu had also left her room. Clutching three whistleblowing letters, she spent a few cents on a bus fare. She dropped off one letter at the Municipal Industrial Bureau, another at the Municipal Commercial Bureau, and delivered the final one to the Municipal Revolutionary Committee.","She wasn't sure if the Chengbei Food Factory fell under the jurisdiction of the Industrial Bureau or the Commercial Bureau. Since she couldn't figure it out, she decided to cover all her bases.","If neither of those bureaus took action, the Revolutionary Committee certainly would.","Worried that Sun Mingyong might have connections inside the factory, she hadn't even considered submitting the letters there.","Her task complete, Qiao Lanshu hopped on a bus heading back to the guesthouse.","The weather outside had turned bitterly cold, and she had no desire to be outdoors.","She figured she would buy her train ticket back to Yangcheng tomorrow. Trains didn't run every day; she had asked around and learned there was only one train every three days heading to Hankou, which meant she would have to transfer twice to get home.","After getting off the bus, she still had a bit of a walk to reach the guesthouse. She trotted along the path, but after a short distance, she suddenly got the eerie feeling that someone was following her.","Glancing over her shoulder, she spotted a man bundled up tightly in thick clothes, walking with his head down.","Qiao Lanshu's heart began to race. After all, there were hardly any pedestrians on the street at this hour. Most people were at work, and those who weren't were huddled up warmly at home. Who would wander around in the freezing wind for no reason?","At this thought, Qiao Lanshu instantly quickened her pace.","However, she wasn't fast enough. Realizing she was trying to flee, the man broke into a run, closing the distance in long strides. He grabbed her violently from behind, clamped a hand over her mouth, and began dragging her into a deserted alleyway nearby.","Qiao Lanshu was so terrified her heart nearly stopped. She struggled and tried to scream with all her might. In her panic, she kicked backward, landing a harsh blow right between the man's legs. He let out a miserable yelp, and his grip loosened.","Qiao Lanshu snatched up a rock from the ground and began smashing it blindly against Niu Li's body.","However, she didn't have much strength, and Niu Li was wearing thick winter layers. The rock barely did any damage.","Seizing the moment, Qiao Lanshu wrenched herself free and sprinted toward the mouth of the alley.","\"Help!\" she screamed at the top of her lungs as she ran.","During the struggle, her scarf had fallen to the ground, leaving her hair wildly disheveled and her appearance completely frantic.","She burst out of the alleyway into the howling, bone-chilling wind, shrieking, \"Help! Somebody, help me!\"","The memory of her past life—being abducted and locked away in a cave dwelling—had long been a haunting nightmare.","She never imagined that she would encounter something like this in broad daylight. Just how lawless was this city? It was absolutely terrifying.","At this moment, Qiao Lanshu hadn't yet connected her attempted kidnapping to Sun Mingyong.","But no matter who the attacker was, she blamed Sun Mingyong anyway!","As she ran, she cursed inwardly, Sun Mingyong, you bastard, just you wait!","Tears streaming down her face, Qiao Lanshu screamed for help as her short legs carried her as fast as they could. She ran until she was gasping for air, a sharp ache building in her chest!","The kick had left Niu Li in agonizing pain, but after a few seconds of recovery, he snapped back to his senses. He had already gone this far; he absolutely couldn't let his prize escape now. Gritting his teeth, he scrambled up and chased after her.","Niu Li cursed through gritted teeth, \"Damn it, such a wildcat. Once I drag you back, I'm going to have to discipline you properly.\"","Besides, she had come from so far away; no one would even know if he dragged her home.","Thinking this, he caught up to Qiao Lanshu in a few strides and violently pinned her to the ground. \"Where do you think you're running to, huh?\"","Pinned to the ground, Qiao Lanshu instinctively shielded her head with her hands. \"Don't hit me, please don't hit me!\"","She was terrified he would strike her head and beat her senseless; if that happened, she would be completely doomed.","However, before Niu Li even had the chance to strike her, he was sent flying by a tremendous force.","His world spun as he was launched three or four meters away. It wasn't until a loud thud echoed that he finally felt the agonizing pain radiating from his chest!","He had actually just been sent flying by a single kick.","Behind Qin Yuanzheng followed a young, neatly dressed company commander.","Standing behind Qin Yuanzheng and witnessing his explosive rage, the company commander was completely stunned.","In his utter fury just now, Qin Yuanzheng had used seventy or eighty percent of his strength to kick Niu Li flying.","He still retained a shred of rationality, knowing that at the very least, he couldn't beat a man to death in the middle of the street.","But even so, Niu Li had lost consciousness.","Qin Yuanzheng strode over and carefully helped up Qiao Lanshu, who was still covering her head on the ground in a pitiful state. Suppressing the anger in his heart, he looked at her with a grave expression. \"Comrade Xiao Qiao, are you alright?\""]},{"number":12,"title":"Chapter 12: Interrogation","paragraphs":["Qiao Lanshu was almost scared to death just now.","She was trembling all over with fear, thinking that this was her fate. Even with a second chance at life, she thought she couldn't escape the destiny of being locked in a cave dwelling by a hooligan.","But Qin Yuanzheng came.","Qin Yuanzheng saved her once again.","Qiao Lanshu's clothes were covered in dirt. Her hair was disheveled, and she was shaking all over.","Qin Yuanzheng felt terrible. He really hadn't expected that in Longcheng City, where troops were stationed, there would still be such hooligans.","He was absolutely furious.","Qiao Lanshu's nose tingled, and she suddenly threw her arms around Qin Yuanzheng and burst into tears.","Qin Yuanzheng felt a bit awkward. He had always been single, had never been in a relationship, and hadn't even held a girl's hand.","Being in such close contact with a young woman all of a sudden, and being hugged by her to boot, his whole body instantly tensed up, and he became somewhat at a loss for what to do.","Oddly enough, he hadn't felt this way the first time he took the young woman to the hospital.","Qiao Lanshu didn't cry loudly. She just leaned against his chest, sobbing softly, her tears flowing endlessly, which made Qin Yuanzheng's heart ache for her.","He patted Qiao Lanshu's back soothingly and said in a low voice, \"It's okay, everything is fine now. Don't cry.\"","As he spoke, he picked Qiao Lanshu up in his arms and strode towards the guest house.","The young company commander following behind him tied up the unconscious Niu Li with a rope and hauled him straight to the nearby police station.","Qin Yuanzheng brought Qiao Lanshu back to the guest house. Then, he prepared to get up, intending to fetch some hot water so she could wash her face and hands.","However, Qiao Lanshu sat on the bed, reached out, and tightly gripped his sleeve, looking at him with tearful eyes.","Qin Yuanzheng: \"...\"","Qin Yuanzheng's heart softened at the sight. It seemed the young woman was truly terrified this time, so he naturally sat down on the chair next to her.","He let Qiao Lanshu hold onto his sleeve.","Qiao Lanshu continued to shed silent tears. She didn't speak, just stared at him.","Qin Yuanzheng felt both heartache and a bit of embarrassment.","He despised himself inwardly. The young woman in front of him was about ten years younger than him. She was just an innocent girl, and her reliance on him was simply because he had been taking care of her recently.","For him to actually feel uncomfortable about this meant there was definitely something wrong with his mind.","Sitting there, he asked Qiao Lanshu, \"Were you frightened just now?\"","Qiao Lanshu nodded silently.","It was more than just being frightened. For a split second, she thought she had returned to her previous life.","She looked at her hand and quietly pulled it back, too embarrassed to keep clutching Qin Yuanzheng's sleeve.","Qin Yuanzheng actually felt a bit disappointed by this.","He asked in a low voice, \"Do you know what's going on with that man?\"","Qiao Lanshu shook her head silently. \"I don't know. I don't know him.\"","Moreover, this hooligan who tailed her was not the same person as the one who locked her in the cave dwelling in her previous life.","Qin Yuanzheng comforted her gently, \"It's alright, don't be afraid. Today, I'll arrange for people to take turns keeping you company at the guest house. If you need to go out for errands, I'll have someone accompany you.\"","Qiao Lanshu thought about how such a good man like Qin Yuanzheng was already married, which meant there was no point in her staying here.","After all, she had already reported Sun Mingyong. Even if the report was unsuccessful, she could just go back and tell her father, letting him deal with Sun Mingyong.","She was afraid that if she stayed any longer, what if she got kidnapped again?","Qiao Lanshu shook her head and said, \"No need. I want to go home.\"","Qin Yuanzheng: \"...\"","This time, Qin Yuanzheng didn't dare to suggest she stay and find a military officer to marry or anything like that.","He remained silent for a long while before saying to her, \"Alright, I'll have someone accompany you to buy a ticket tomorrow.\"","In his mind, he pondered over which company commander or battalion commander he should arrange to accompany the young woman to buy the ticket.","Who knows, maybe they would hit it off on the way?","This time, Qin Yuanzheng stayed in the room with Qiao Lanshu for quite a while. When the young company commander returned from the police station, he stood up and said to Qiao Lanshu, \"I'll have Xiao Yang stay with you. I'm going to the police station to interrogate that bastard.\"","Qiao Lanshu nodded and watched Qin Yuanzheng walk out the door.","Outside the door, the young company commander instinctively tried to follow Qin Yuanzheng.","Qin Yuanzheng looked back at him and said, \"You stay.\"","The company commander: \"...\"","The company commander asked in bewilderment, \"Commander, didn't you say you wanted me to come on a blind date with a girl? If I stay here to guard sister-in-law, what about the girl over there?\"","Qin Yuanzheng: \"...\"","Qin Yuanzheng was left speechless. He looked at the company commander and said, \"What sister-in-law? What girl?\"","He pointed to the closed door of room 203 and said, \"This is the girl you're supposed to have a blind date with. You better guard her well.\"","With that, Qin Yuanzheng strode away.","He was still mulling over the term \"sister-in-law,\" thinking that these subordinates of his really had no tact. Not to mention the fact that he wasn't planning on getting married, even if he were to marry, he wouldn't find a girl this young. She was over ten years younger than him; how could he possibly bring himself to do that?","The young company commander: \"...\"","He stood there bewildered for a long time, scratching his head and thinking: just now, he saw Commander Qin almost lose control and kick the man to death. The young woman had been trying hard to hold back her tears, but as soon as she saw Commander Qin, she hugged him and started crying.","How could they not be a couple?","Why did he find that so hard to believe?","...","Qin Yuanzheng arrived at the police station. There were only three police officers in total at the station. The deputy chief of the police station, Li Jianlin, had been idly warming himself by the fire and drinking tea.","But suddenly, there was work to do.","And the suspect was dragged in and delivered by military officers.","He stood at the door of the interrogation room, looking at the unconscious Niu Li, and frowned. \"Why does this kid look a bit familiar?\"","Longcheng City wasn't big, with only a few factories, so many people knew each other.","Before Li Jianlin could recognize the man, Qin Yuanzheng walked in.","As soon as Li Jianlin saw him, he was startled. He quickly went to greet him and asked, \"Isn't this Chief Qin? How do you have the time to come here today?\"","Could it be that the person in the interrogation room had committed some major crime?","The people in the police station were basically all transferred from the military.","Li Jianlin himself had transferred from a battalion-level position in the army. He knew Qin Yuanzheng, but the two were not very close.","As soon as Qin Yuanzheng entered, he took off his military overcoat, and then he also took off the military uniform underneath.","He might have to beat someone up later, and wearing a military uniform would make it inconvenient. After all, he had to maintain the image of a soldier.","Li Jianlin watched with trepidation and asked, \"Chief, what exactly is going on?\"","Qin Yuanzheng glanced at him and said, \"Don't get involved in this. I will interrogate him personally. Is that bastard awake yet?\"","Li Jianlin shook his head. \"No, he's passed out cold.\"","He had just been wondering whether to send the man to the hospital for a check-up, because following the footprints on his clothes and pulling them open, he saw that the injuries underneath were not light. There was a large dark bruise on his chest.","Qin Yuanzheng sneered coldly, his voice dark and chilling, \"Use cold water to splash him awake. I have questions to ask him.\"","Li Jianlin assumed this involved military secrets, wondering to himself: could that unconscious pockmarked guy be a spy?","That damned spy! Just what kind of heinous acts had he committed to actually warrant a personal interrogation by a full regimental commander from the military district?"]},{"number":13,"title":"Chapter 13: Sun Mingyong Arrested","paragraphs":["It was perfectly reasonable for Qin Yuanzheng to conduct the interrogation personally.","After all, his 21st Regiment was stationed in the mining area and in charge of the coal. This entire region fell under his jurisdiction.","Although the Public Security Bureau was understaffed and largely hands-off, the presence of the military kept the management of this area quite stable.","Even if there were usually some hooligans loitering around, they didn't dare to do anything too outrageous.","After all, once caught, the punishment would range from a light sentence of labor reform to execution by firing squad.","Niu Li, who had been kicked unconscious, was jolted awake by a basin of cold water. His clothes were soaking wet, and he shivered violently from the cold. Upon waking, he clutched his chest, groaning and continuously crying out in pain.","Deputy Chief Li Jianlin sat beside Qin Yuanzheng, casting a highly pitying glance at Niu Li.","He had no idea what crime this guy had committed, but he was certainly out of luck to have fallen into Regiment Commander Qin's hands.","Commander Qin was a living Yama, the King of Hell. Having risen all the way from a conscript to a full regiment commander, who in the military didn't know his fearsome reputation?","Qin Yuanzheng didn't speak, so Li Jianlin began to follow standard procedure. \"Quiet, what are you yelling for?\"","Niu Li looked up and first saw Li Jianlin. Li Jianlin was the Deputy Chief of the Public Security Bureau, someone Niu Li recognized.","Then, he glanced at Qin Yuanzheng and was instantly terrified by his dark, fierce expression.","He swallowed nervously, no longer daring to cry out in pain, and pleaded to Li Jianlin, \"Comrade Police, I... I'm innocent!\"","Qin Yuanzheng sneered. \"Innocent? Kidnapping a woman on the street—do you know what the consequences are?\"","Qin Yuanzheng pulled the pistol from his waist, slammed it onto the table, and stared darkly at Niu Li. \"Still not going to confess?\"","Niu Li was speechless.","Niu Li was a coward at heart. When bullying the young girl from the south, he had been exceedingly vicious.","But now, looking at the gun slammed on the table, he nearly wet himself in terror.","Trembling all over, he babbled incoherently, \"I'll confess, I'll confess, I'll tell you everything...\"","Ten minutes later, Qin Yuanzheng and Li Jianlin emerged from the interrogation room.","Li Jianlin said with a dark face, \"This Niu Li is incredibly audacious, actually trying to snatch a woman in broad daylight! According to the law, behavior like his warrants the firing squad!\"","Li Jianlin wasn't exaggerating. In this day and age, even having illicit relationships could lead to execution, let alone someone like Niu Li, who attempted to kidnap a female comrade on the street.","Niu Li was naturally terrified as well. Therefore, he claimed he was wrongly accused and was merely acting on someone else's orders.","He had said, \"It was Sun Mingyong, a salesman from our factory, who told me to do it. For some unknown reason, he gave that girl a lot of money. After she left, he regretted it and told me to snatch the money back from her... That's really all there is to it, Comrade Police. I absolutely, positively had no intention of kidnapping a female comrade. Even if you gave me ten times the courage, I wouldn't dare do such a thing.\"","Anyway, his kidnapping attempt had failed, and nothing had actually happened. By claiming he was only after the money, his story seemed plausible, and the police couldn't definitively judge that he intended to kidnap her.","That charge meant taking a bullet, and he couldn't afford to bear it.","At the same time, Niu Li began to harbor deep resentment toward Sun Mingyong.","He had claimed the young girl came from thousands of miles away, with no family or anyone to rely on. Yet here was a full regiment commander from the military district coming after him! Did that look like having no one to rely on?","Sun Mingyong must have set him up on purpose. Once he found the chance, he absolutely had to get his revenge.","Previously, Qin Yuanzheng had been thinking about going to the food factory to verify Sun Mingyong's identity and thoroughly investigate whether he was truly suspected of deceiving the young girl, tricking her into marriage and having children.","Now, after interrogating Niu Li, what else was there to misunderstand?","Sun Mingyong was afraid his marriage fraud would be exposed, so he hired someone to control Qiao Lanshu.","He even sought out a thug like Niu Li.","Qin Yuanzheng said to Li Jianlin, \"Take your men to the food factory and bring Sun Mingyong in for questioning.\"","With such a case occurring in his jurisdiction, Li Jianlin didn't dare delay. He immediately headed out with two junior police officers, making a beeline for the North City Food Factory.","Meanwhile, inside the business department office of the North City Food Factory, Sun Mingyong kept walking over to the window every now and then to glance down at the guardhouse. At the same time, he pondered inwardly: Why hasn't that bastard Niu Li come back to work yet? Could it be that he hasn't succeeded?","He really was an unreliable piece of trash.","However, it had already been two days, and he hadn't seen anyone dropping off a report letter at the guardhouse. It seemed Qiao Lanshu didn't have the guts to report him.","Previously, he had thought that simply putting Qiao Lanshu on a train would be the end of it.","But now, he felt he still couldn't let Qiao Lanshu go back. If she went back, she would complain to Father Qiao. When Father Qiao took action, he would truly have no room to maneuver.","With this in mind, Sun Mingyong couldn't even focus on his work. He quickly packed up his things and headed out.","He needed to make a trip to the post office to see if Qiao Lanshu had already mailed a letter home.","He had to find a way to intercept the letter.","However, just as Sun Mingyong stepped out of the office, he saw several men in police uniforms walking toward him. Beside the police officers was Director Wei Zhengye.","Looking at Wei Zhengye's gloomy face, Sun Mingyong's heart instantly skipped a beat. A strong sense of foreboding washed over him. He stood frozen at the office door, his throat suddenly feeling dry.","Watching Wei Zhengye approach, he called out in a hoarse voice, \"Dad...\"","With a sharp slap, Wei Zhengye walked right up and struck him across the face without a word.","This slap was delivered with full force, and half of Sun Mingyong's face swelled up instantly.","Although Wei Zhengye was already a grandfather, he wasn't even fifty yet, and he still had plenty of strength.","Sun Mingyong saw stars from the blow. Dizzy, he slumped to the ground, but still gritted his teeth and said, \"Dad, Dad, this is all a misunderstanding. I can explain...\"","Slap!","Wei Zhengye struck him again.","Sun Mingyong dropped straight to his knees before him, crying, \"Dad, I truly love Hongmei! You've seen it these past few years, I've been genuinely good to her. And the children, we have two children! Dad, the kids can't have a father in a labor camp!\"","Wei Zhengye's eyes turned red with anger at his words.","Of course he didn't want his grandson and granddaughter to have a father sent off to a labor camp.","That would be a lifelong stain; wherever they went, people would point fingers behind their backs and look down on them.","And precisely because of that, Wei Zhengye was so furious!","He kicked Sun Mingyong and scolded, \"Don't say these things to me. Get lost and explain yourself properly to the police comrades!\"","Deputy Chief Li Jianlin, leading the two police officers, watched this good show unfold and couldn't help but mutter inwardly. This Sun Mingyong looked quite ordinary, not particularly handsome at all.","Yet he managed to date someone in Yangcheng while marrying someone else here. If the woman from Yangcheng hadn't taken a train all the way here to find her husband, everyone would probably have been kept in the dark forever.","Furthermore, because of their engagement, the young woman back in Yangcheng was having a hard time finding a husband.","Worse yet, she might be assigned to go down to the countryside as an educated youth. Dragging this out year after year would only waste the girl's youth.","That bastard Sun Mingyong had truly committed a grave sin.","Deputy Chief Li Jianlin tied Sun Mingyong up and took him straight back to the Public Security Bureau.","Wei Zhengye stood at the factory gates. Although he was still furious, he had to figure out a way to bail Sun Mingyong out.","No matter how much of a scumbag Sun Mingyong was, Wei Zhengye still had to think about his two grandchildren.","As Sun Mingyong was forced into the police car, his face red and swollen, he continued to beg Wei Zhengye for mercy. Dad, please think of a way to help me, Dad! I just loved Hongmei too much, I had no other choice. From now on, I will be like your own flesh and blood. I will take care of you in your old age. Dad, I can even have the kids take your surname...","Standing there and listening to these words, Wei Zhengye felt both angry and exasperated.","He hated himself for not having vetted Sun Mingyong more thoroughly back then.","Initially, he had only considered the fact that Sun Mingyong was a southerner. Knowing it was not easy for him to return to his hometown, he figured that once Sun secured a job here, it would be even more impossible for him to go back.","In this way, it was almost like having a live-in son-in-law. He would be able to keep a close eye on Sun Mingyong and ensure his daughter was never mistreated.","But he never in a million years expected that while he was calculating how to control Sun Mingyong, Sun Mingyong was busy scheming against his daughter!","Back at the Public Security Bureau, Li Jianlin scolded him. Have some shame! Deceiving women, committing marriage fraud, and even instigating Niu Li to stalk and kidnap a female comrade. Every single one of these charges is enough to get you shot.","Sun Mingyong: ???","Sun Mingyong was shocked. Comrade Police, do not talk nonsense! I never instigated Niu Li to stalk or kidnap any female comrade. I barely even know Niu Li. Whatever he did has absolutely nothing to do with me!","One look at his expression, and Li Jianlin knew he was feeling guilty and scared, just spouting nonsense to make excuses.","Li Jianlin sneered and said, Nothing to do with you? Then why do you look so guilty? Get inside and confess everything. Maybe you can fight for a lenient sentence!","With that, he led Sun Mingyong into an interrogation room at the bureau.","The Public Security Bureau was not large, consisting of only four rooms, two of which were interrogation rooms.","Niu Li was locked in the room next door. After his confession, he had been confined there. The severe aches and pains all over his body were unbearable, and he was still lying there groaning, looking half-dead.","Just as Sun Mingyong was brought in, before the interrogation could even begin, personnel from the City Industrial Bureau arrived. A team of two went to the food factory in the north of the city, stating they had received a tip-off letter about Sun Mingyong and needed to verify the situation on-site.","Upon learning that Sun Mingyong had been taken away by the police, they took their leave and headed straight to the Public Security Bureau as well.","Less than half an hour after the people from the Industrial Bureau left, members of the Municipal Revolutionary Committee showed up. A group of five or six people stormed aggressively into the factory director's office.","Seeing this group from the Revolutionary Committee, the atmosphere in the entire factory grew tense and heavy.","Factory Director Yang Wenyan and Factory Supervisor Wei Zhengye busied themselves serving tea and water, placating them with a polite and accommodating tone. After the Revolutionary Committee members finally left, Director Yang Wenyan wiped the cold sweat from his forehead and spoke sternly to Wei Zhengye.","You were the one who recommended Sun Mingyong, and he is your son-in-law. Now that this has happened, he must be expelled from the Party and stripped of his position! We will need to hold a general assembly at the factory to publicly criticize him. As his father-in-law, you need to step back to avoid any suspicion. Do not come into work for the next couple of days.","Previously, Wei Zhengye had claimed his son-in-law came from a good background, had attended middle school, and had impeccable political roots. Since there was an open position at the factory, Director Yang Wenyan had signed off on his employment.","Now, with Sun Mingyong involved in such a scandal, their food factory had practically become infamous throughout Longcheng City.","Yang Wenyan figured that the next time he went to the Industrial Bureau for a meeting, they would be singled out and criticized as a negative example.","Forget about this year; their factory had zero chance of winning any excellence awards for the next three years.","Yang Wenyan was absolutely furious. The more he thought about it, the more frustrated he became, leading him to harshly reprimand Wei Zhengye all over again.","Looking utterly gloomy, Wei Zhengye left the food factory. He had no choice but to go home and rest, waiting ten days to half a month before returning to work."]},{"number":14,"title":"Chapter 14: Your regimental commander is quite fierce.","paragraphs":["Sun Mingyong had been hauled into the Public Security Bureau, but he stubbornly refused to admit to any marriage fraud.","He said to the Deputy Bureau Chief, Li Jianlin, \"Officer, I really didn't commit marriage fraud. Wei Hongmei and I were introduced by our parents, and we liked each other, so we proudly registered our marriage. I absolutely did not deceive her!\"","Li Jianlin’s face darkened. \"Then what about Qiao Lanshu from Guangzhou? She has your letters. In those letters, you lied and said you were the commander of the Independent Second Battalion. You even promised her that if she married you, she could join the military as your dependent!\"","Sun Mingyong argued further:","\"Yes, I admit, I once harbored a slight romantic interest in Comrade Qiao Lanshu. I thought about pursuing her and marrying her. But ever since I started a family with Hongmei, I never went back. Comrade Qiao Lanshu and I haven't seen each other in years. As for the contents of those letters, I only wrote them to keep Mother Qiao happy. Mother Qiao is in poor health, and I was worried she wouldn't be able to handle the truth.\"","Despite Sun Mingyong’s endless explanations and excuses, the evidence in the letters was indisputable. He was simply trying his best to downplay the severity of his actions.","At that moment, Qin Yuanzheng, who was sitting next to Li Jianlin, suddenly spoke up. He asked Sun Mingyong, \"Qiao Lanshu’s father sent you a telegram and wrote to you, telling you that Comrade Qiao Lanshu was coming to Longcheng City to find you. Why didn't you go to the station to meet her?\"","Sun Mingyong was momentarily speechless. He hesitated before saying, \"She had a letter of introduction, and she’s a grown woman. Even if I didn't pick her up, she could have stayed at a guest house. That shouldn't be a problem, right?\"","Hearing this, Qin Yuanzheng’s anger flared even more.","It was clear from Sun Mingyong’s words that he had no regard whatsoever for Qiao Lanshu’s safety.","He hadn't considered how helpless and lost a seventeen or eighteen-year-old girl would feel stepping off a train onto completely unfamiliar soil.","Qin Yuanzheng was in civilian clothes, having long since taken off his military uniform, so Sun Mingyong had assumed he was just a temporary worker at the bureau.","That was until Qin Yuanzheng suddenly stood up, his face grim, walked toward him, and kicked him squarely in the chest.","Sun Mingyong was sent flying against the wall. Clutching his chest, his vision went dark from the pain, and for a long time, he couldn't utter a single word.","His head was buzzing, and he curled up on the floor, looking half-dead.","Li Jianlin was startled by the sudden outburst.","He had no idea why Qin Yuanzheng had suddenly flown into such a rage.","He quickly ran over, grabbed Qin Yuanzheng’s arm, and whispered, \"Stay calm, stay calm! Don't kick him to death.\"","Qin Yuanzheng said coldly, \"The mere fact that he dared to impersonate a military officer and commit fraud in the name of a battalion commander is enough to have him sent to a labor camp, not to mention the marriage fraud involved.\"","Deputy Bureau Chief Li Jianlin nodded. \"True, impersonating a military officer is a serious crime.\"","Qin Yuanzheng felt that even a firing squad would be too merciful for someone like Sun Mingyong. Such a person deserved to be sent to the harshest and most exhausting labor at the Haixi Prison Farm to clear wasteland, never to be allowed back.","Since Qin Yuanzheng had spoken, the approval process became simple. Such cases required the military's seal and signature anyway, and since Qin Yuanzheng was right there, Li Jianlin handed the verdict directly to him to sign.","Sun Mingyong was sentenced to twelve years of hard labor at the Haixi Prison Farm, the most grueling facility available.","Furthermore, even after his twelve-year sentence was served, it would be impossible for him to return.","Because his household registration would be transferred there, he would be rooted there for the rest of his life.","Before being sent off for labor reform, officials from the Municipal Revolutionary Committee also arrived.","They subjected Sun Mingyong to a long period of ideological education and harsh criticism.","Finally, as a cautionary example, Sun Mingyong was paraded through various units and factories. He was also publicly denounced at a mass meeting to serve as a warning to everyone else.","Sun Mingyong paid a heavy price for the mistakes he had committed.","Even though Wei Zhengye wanted to help, once the military intervened, he was completely powerless.","After all, no one was willing to help him.","His daughter, Wei Hongmei, brought her two children back to her parents' home and cried to Wei Zhengye, \"Dad, you have to think of something! The children can't grow up without a father.\"","Wei Zhengye was already frustrated. He looked at his disappointing daughter and said, \"There is no room for maneuver in this matter. If it were just the Revolutionary Committee or the Public Security Bureau, I could still use my connections and find a way. But the military has stepped in. Tell me, what can I do?\"","Wei Hongmei sobbed, \"Why does the military have the time to meddle in such trivial matters? Just because he impersonated an officer in a letter to his family?\"","Hearing his daughter say this, Wei Zhengye’s temper instantly flared. He slammed the table and asked:","\"Is that not enough? He was deceiving people on both ends, impersonating someone on both sides! He deserves it! You will divorce him immediately. Take the divorce certificate and find another father for the children. Once the children's household registration is moved to a new father, the problem will be solved. From now on, act as if Sun Mingyong never existed, do you understand?\"","Wei Hongmei shook her head and cried, \"Mingyong was very good to me and the kids. Dad, I can't live without Mingyong.\"","Wei Zhengye was utterly frustrated by his daughter’s lack of sense.","This daughter had been spoiled by him since she was a child. She had never suffered and knew nothing of the complexity of people.","Just because Sun Mingyong was slightly nice to her, she became completely devoted, never once wondering why Sun Mingyong would be so good to her when she was plain-looking and a bit plump.","When Sun Mingyong said it was love at first sight, she believed him.","When Sun Mingyong praised her for being beautiful and virtuous, saying he would only love her for the rest of his life, she believed every word.","Wei Zhengye couldn't talk sense into her, nor could he teach her.","He stood up in a rage and scolded her:","\"Your father almost lost his job because of this! The factory manager told me to go home to avoid suspicion. It’s been several days, and no one has notified me to go back to work. Think about it—if I lose my job, how are you going to support yourself and the children on your meager salary? Hongmei, you’re almost thirty years old. Be realistic and think about these issues instead of talking about love and affection all day. It’s embarrassing.\"","After being scolded by her father, Wei Hongmei went back home crying with her children.","However, she soon moved back to her parents' house again.","The dormitory she had been living in was assigned to Sun Mingyong by the food factory, and it had now been reclaimed by the factory.","Wei Hongmei had previously refused to work because she thought the food factory was too tiring, so she naturally had no housing of her own.","She was currently unemployed, and Wei Zhengye could no longer use his connections to get her a job. He could only arrange for her to help out at a relative's unlicensed clinic to earn a few yuan for the time being.","...","The Sun Mingyong incident caused a huge stir in Longcheng City.","Everyone knew that Qin Yuanzheng had personally handled Sun Mingyong’s case.","However, everyone assumed Qin Yuanzheng had intervened because Sun Mingyong had committed fraud by impersonating a military officer.","No one knew that Qin Yuanzheng was actually doing it mostly to get revenge on behalf of Qiao Lanshu.","Qiao Lanshu wasn't sure if it was from the scare or something else, but she had come down with another cold, accompanied by a bit of a fever.","There was no helping it; her plans to return home had to be put on hold for a few more days.","She spent the entire day lying in the guesthouse, not even daring to step out the door.","All she wanted was to recover quickly and go home. If she had to go to the countryside, then so be it; it was better than staying here.","At the door, Young Company Commander Yang was holding two thermoses in one hand as he knocked. \"Comrade Xiao Qiao, I've brought some hot water for you. May I come in?\"","Qiao Lanshu nodded. Her voice was thick with congestion and a bit raspy as she said, \"Please, come in.\"","Young Company Commander Yang pushed open the door to Room 203. He glanced at Qiao Lanshu, who was sitting on the kang bed wrapped up like a zongzi in a thick quilt, and found her quite adorable.","With a slight flush on his face, he placed the thermoses on the windowsill across from her and asked, \"Comrade Xiao Qiao, have you finished your medicine? Do you need me to get you some more?\"","For the past few days, Qin Yuanzheng had assigned Young Company Commander Yang to stay at the guesthouse, ostensibly to protect and look after Qiao Lanshu.","However, Qiao Lanshu knew that Qin Yuanzheng was trying to set her up with him.","On one hand, he truly wasn't comfortable leaving her alone; on the other, he was indeed trying to play matchmaker, creating more opportunities for them to spend time together.","But in truth, it wasn't just Qiao Lanshu who lacked interest.","Ever since Young Company Commander Yang had seen Qin Yuanzheng carry Qiao Lanshu back to the guesthouse, he had already begun looking at her as his \"Sister-in-law.\"","He assumed that Colonel Qin liked Qiao Lanshu, but she was put off by the Colonel's infertility, so the two of them were currently having a lover's spat.","As Qin Yuanzheng's subordinate, he didn't dare breathe a word about his superior's private affairs.","Regardless, he kept himself busy running errands, carrying out his duties with diligence and efficiency.","Qiao Lanshu could tell that Young Company Commander Yang was maintaining a respectful distance, which made their interactions feel quite relaxed.","Qiao Lanshu tried to hold back, but eventually, curiosity got the better of her. She asked, \"Young Company Commander Yang, why hasn't your Colonel Qin shown his face these past few days? Is the unit that busy?\"","Sweeping the floor with great industry, Young Company Commander Yang replied, \"Oh, the Colonel? He's been busy interrogating a prisoner for the last couple of days.\"","Qiao Lanshu was surprised. \"Your unit has prisoners to interrogate?\"","Young Company Commander Yang quickly clarified, \"No, no, it was at the police station. Something about impersonating a military officer and marriage fraud. The person has already been sent for reform through labor.\"","Young Company Commander Yang paused for a moment before adding, \"I heard the Colonel was furious. He kicked the guy once, nearly killing him on the spot.\"","Qiao Lanshu: \"...\"","Qiao Lanshu muttered quietly, \"Your Colonel is quite terrifying.\""]},{"number":15,"title":"Chapter 15: You Should Let Off Some Steam Too","paragraphs":["The fierce-looking Qin Yuanzheng, having finished dealing with Sun Mingyong's matter, directly signed off and sentenced Sun Mingyong's case.","That Niu Li, of course, was also criticized along with him and sent off for reform through labor.","Both men were sent to the farthest and most arduous Meixi Prison Farm to reclaim wasteland.","These two also served as an example for the people of Longcheng City. From now on, let's see who would dare to bully female comrades again.","After being busy for two days, when Qin Yuanzheng returned to his office, Staff Officer Lin's look at him seemed a bit off.","Qin Yuanzheng had been wearing a cold expression for several days because of Sun Mingyong's affair.","He was clearly quite furious.","Seeing his reaction, anyone who didn't know better might think it was his sister or daughter who had been deceived.","Qin Yuanzheng personally watched Sun Mingyong and Niu Li being escorted onto the train to Meixi Prison and even arranged for personnel to escort them himself before returning to the mining district office.","He glanced at Staff Officer Lin and said in a deep voice, \"Are you that idle?\"","Staff Officer Lin: \"...\"","Staff Officer Lin quickly brewed him a cup of tea, carried it with both hands, and placed it on his desk: \"Regiment Commander, here, have a cup of tea to cool down your anger. Don't be mad, don't be mad.\"","Qin Yuanzheng picked up the cup, took a sip of tea, and said somewhat perplexedly, \"What anger? I'm not angry.\"","Staff Officer Lin hurriedly said, \"Right, right, right, you're not angry. I was mistaken.\"","Qin Yuanzheng: \"...\"","Qin Yuanzheng pointed at Staff Officer Lin, who quickly retreated more than ten steps away.","Joking aside, even he couldn't withstand a kick from Regiment Commander Qin.","However, he still dared to say a couple of words: \"Regiment Commander, your temper is just too fiery these days. To be honest, you should hurry up and find a partner, settle down, and... vent some of that fire...\"","Before he could finish, Qin Yuanzheng suddenly stood up. Staff Officer Lin jumped in fright and instantly bolted out the door.","Qin Yuanzheng: \"...\"","Qin Yuanzheng's face darkened. He wasn't really angry before, but now, after what Staff Officer Lin said, he felt even more irritated.","Vent fire... vent what fire?","In this freezing cold weather, people are about to freeze to death, and he's talking about venting fire.","Qin Yuanzheng, nearly thirty, actually understood everything.","Having spent over a decade in the army, what kind of crude jokes hadn't his comrades-in-arms told?","It's all about guns, war, women...","Qin Yuanzheng indeed had abundant energy and needs in that regard.","But ever since he decided not to marry, he had increased his daily training load. After all, he didn't have to go to the battlefield now, so he could only channel his energy into the training ground.","By doubling his training and work every day, over time, he stopped thinking about unnecessary things.","Sometimes, seeing his married comrades-in-arms, with their silly, eager anticipation to see their families, he even found it rather baffling.","It's just having a family, right? Just being able to sleep on the same kang with them?","Is that worth being so happy about?","Better to spend that time running a few more laps on the training ground to improve physical fitness.","Thinking about this, Qin Yuanzheng couldn't help but think of Qiao Lanshu again.","He wondered how that young woman was doing now. She was frightened by Niu Li a couple of days ago; he didn't know if she had recovered.","Qin Yuanzheng originally wanted to go see her.","But then he thought, it's better to leave the opportunity for Xiao Yang. Xiao Yang's parents both had jobs, he himself was a company commander, good-looking, not too old, and a good match for Qiao Lanshu.","Qin Yuanzheng thought and thought, then sighed. He didn't even know why he was sighing, but he just felt restless all over and found nothing interesting to do.","After finishing a cup of tea in the office, he stood up and went to work in the mining district.","Their 21st Regiment was specifically responsible for the coal mining in Longcheng City, and the work was not easy.","As the regiment commander, Qin Yuanzheng bore a heavy burden.","To facilitate coal transportation, three roads were planned to be built in the surrounding area. Personnel from the Railway Bureau and Engineering Bureau would come to cooperate later, and one or two battalion-level engineering corps would be assigned to work with the 21st Regiment to build the roads.","This project was just in the planning stages, but the preliminary work was also very busy, requiring coordination with engineers from the provincial level.","Although these tasks could be delegated to others, Qin Yuanzheng had nothing better to do, so he took care of everything personally.","In the afternoon, when he returned to the mining district office, he unexpectedly saw Wang Huiping and her son standing inside.","Staff Officer Lin stood to the side, making meaningful eye contact at Qin Yuanzheng.","Qin Yuanzheng was somewhat surprised and asked Wang Huiping, \"What brings you here?\"","Since their blind date, Qin Yuanzheng and Wang Huiping had only met twice.","The first time was at the home of Qin Yuanzheng's cousin, Yang Wenyan, where they had a meal together.","The second time was a chance encounter on the road. Of course, this \"chance\" was actually Wang Huiping knowing Qin Yuanzheng would pass by there, so she deliberately waited for him.","Wang Huiping was very satisfied with Qin Yuanzheng. Not to mention his excellent physique and appearance, just his position and rank were already beyond what she could normally aspire to.","If it weren't for Qin Yuanzheng's infertility issue and the fact that she happened to have a son, she probably wouldn't even have had the chance to meet him.","Qin Yuanzheng was busy with work, treating her with lukewarm indifference and never taking the initiative to seek her out.","So, she swallowed her pride and came herself.","She smiled and said, \"I recently managed to buy a pig's trotter, stewed it with soybeans, and brought some for you to try.\"","Her son, Xiao Yuan, stood timidly beside her. Qin Yuanzheng reached out and ruffled his hair, asking him, \"Have you eaten, Xiao Yuan?\"","Xiao Yuan looked at him and suddenly said, \"Dad, I've already eaten.\"","Qin Yuanzheng: \"???\"","Staff Officer Lin beside them slowly opened his mouth wide, looking at Qin Yuanzheng in shock, then at Wang Huiping and Xiao Yuan.","His face was full of astonishment.","Actually, looking at them now, they really did resemble a family of three.","Wang Huiping quickly tugged at Xiao Yuan, whispering to him, \"Xiao Yuan, don't call him that randomly. You should call him Uncle Qin.\"","Then, she looked somewhat embarrassed at Qin Yuanzheng: \"Sorry about that, the child doesn't understand. Please don't take it to heart.\"","Qin Yuanzheng certainly wouldn't hold it against a child.","After all, he and Wang Huiping were indeed dating, and they were still in the process of getting to know each other. It was normal for the child to misunderstand their relationship during this time.","He said, \"It's not a big deal. Don't blame the child.\"","However, he didn't take the food container from Wang Huiping. He said, \"Pig's trotters are hard to come by, and the child is still young. Keep it to nourish his health. Please take it back.\"","Wang Huiping insisted on placing the stewed pig's trotter on the desk, smiling at Qin Yuanzheng: \"Regiment Commander Qin, I've saved some for the child at home. This portion, Xiao Yuan said he wanted to give it to you. He wanted you to try it.\"","Qin Yuanzheng wasn't the type to be overly hesitant. Since Wang Huiping put it that way, it would be unseemly to keep refusing back and forth.","He nodded: \"Then thank you, Comrade Wang, and thank you, Xiao Yuan.\"","As he spoke, he raised his hand and glanced at his watch. It was already getting late. The weather was cold, and outside, darkness fell early, with the north wind howling.","Winter hasn't even arrived yet, but it's already bitterly cold. In a little while, it will probably snow.","I wonder if that young woman from the south has ever seen snow, and if she can stand the winters here.","Qin Yuanzheng picked up the food container with one hand and said to Wang Huiping, \"It's getting dark, let me see you off.\"","Wang Huiping did not refuse. She had been wanting to spend more time with Qin Yuanzheng, so she took Xiao Yuan's hand and followed him out.","The three of them left together. Qin Yuanzheng drove, taking Wang Huiping and Xiao Yuan back to the textile factory's dormitory area.","The sky darkened quickly. Watching Xiao Yuan get out of the car, Qin Yuanzheng noticed the child's nose was red from the cold.","He said to Wang Huiping, \"The weather is cold. From now on, go straight home after work. There's no need to come all that way to find me.\"","Hearing this, Wang Huiping was taken aback for a moment.","However, she quickly nodded and said to him from the roadside, \"Alright, Regiment Commander Qin. Xiao Yuan and I will wait for you to visit.\"","Qin Yuanzheng was silent for a while, then said, \"The workload is heavy lately, I'm very busy. I may not have any free time,\"","He paused, glancing at Xiao Yuan, who was still looking at him with hopeful eyes.","Qin Yuanzheng's expression faltered slightly, and he added, \"We'll see in a few days.\"","With that, he drove away.","He needed to go back and think things over carefully.","Wang Huiping led Xiao Yuan upstairs to their dormitory room. She said in a low voice, \"Xiao Yuan, you did very well today. Next time you see Uncle Qin, remember to call him 'Dad,' okay?\"","Xiao Yuan nodded silently. \"I know, Mom.\"","Wang Huiping returned to her one-bedroom apartment. There was indeed some stewed pork trotters left at home. She ladled them out into a bowl and brought it to Xiao Yuan to eat.","She herself, however, couldn't stand the smell. So, the moment she set the bowl down, she turned and ran to the bathroom, where she retched dryly for a long time.","It frightened Xiao Yuan, whose face turned pale.","He asked anxiously, \"Mom, are you okay?\"","Wang Huiping's complexion was poor. After a long silence, she finally shook her head and said, \"Mom's fine. Once Mom marries Uncle Qin, we can live in a big house and have a good life. Remember to call him 'Dad' next time you see him, understand?\"","Xiao Yuan: \"...\"","Xiao Yuan said softly, \"Mom, will this uncle hit people?\"","He was still terrified from the last one.","Wang Huiping thought of the reputation Qin Yuanzheng had in the army and stated with certainty, \"No, he's different from other men.\"","So, no matter what, she had to hold onto Qin Yuanzheng this time.","Only...","She reached out and touched her own stomach. This child absolutely could not be kept.","..."]},{"number":16,"title":"Chapter 16: Aren't you going in to say hello","paragraphs":["Qin Yuanzheng took some time off today and came to the guesthouse. At the entrance, he ran into Young Company Commander Yang, who was carrying a lunchbox to deliver food to Qiao Lanshu.","When Xiao Yang saw Qin Yuanzheng approaching, he immediately ran over and said, \"Regiment Commander, why haven't you come over these past two or three days? Comrade Xiao Qiao often asks about you.\"","Qin Yuanzheng asked him, \"How is Comrade Xiao Qiao's illness? Is she better?\"","Xiao Yang nodded. \"Much better. She had a low-grade fever before. The doctor said it was caused by shock and freezing. He told her to stay indoors and not go out these few days when the temperature drops, and to drink more rice soup and such. I go to the hospital canteen every day to get it for her.\"","As he spoke, Xiao Yang lifted the lunchbox in his hand to show Qin Yuanzheng.","Qin Yuanzheng listened, nodded, and asked again, \"Is Comrade Xiao Qiao going to buy a train ticket? Did she say when she's leaving?\"","Xiao Yang was a bit puzzled. Since Regiment Commander Qin cared so much about Qiao Lanshu, why didn't he ask her himself?","He had no idea that Qin Yuanzheng had realized his attitude towards Qiao Lanshu was slightly different from normal. Thus, he quickly reined himself in, trying to nip his feelings in the bud.","He was infertile and almost thirty years old.","The young girl was only eighteen, still in the prime of her youth. She would definitely want to have children in the future. It would be best for her to find a partner of a similar age and matching social status.","Thinking about it this way, just as his cousin had said, it seemed Wang Huiping was more suitable for him.","With these thoughts, he felt somewhat disheartened.","He said, \"It might snow in the next couple of days, and the trains might not depart on time. Persuade her not to rush back. It won't be too late to leave after the snow stops.\"","Xiao Yang nodded. \"Regiment Commander, I'll go tell Comrade Xiao Qiao in a moment.\"","Qin Yuanzheng nodded. He looked at Xiao Yang and asked again, \"How have you and Comrade Xiao Qiao been getting along these past few days?\"","Young Company Commander Yang smiled foolishly, revealing a mouthful of white teeth. Once he opened his mouth, he couldn't stop talking. He said:","\"We've been getting along quite well. Comrade Xiao Qiao loves reading, so I went to the library and found her several issues of the 'Red Flag' magazine. Oh, right, she also likes reading the newspaper. I brought her many copies of the 'People's Daily' and the 'Longcheng Daily'. She says the magazines are more interesting because they have some literary works in them, and she asked me to find more for her.","Oh, and Comrade Xiao Qiao also said the dough drop soup here is delicious. She had never had it in the South. I've been getting her a bowl every day recently. But the melon-substitute vegetable doesn't taste very good. She frowns after just one bite and seems to have a hard time eating it. I told her next time I'd exchange some food stamps to buy her some white flour steamed buns. The weather here is too cold. She said she appreciated my help and tries to stuff money into my hands every day. I wouldn't dare take it, so I refused...\"","Xiao Yang rambled on and on, but surprisingly, Qin Yuanzheng didn't find it annoying and listened very attentively.","He suddenly felt like smoking, even though he rarely smoked at all.","So, he took out a pack of Da Qian Men from his overcoat pocket and pulled out a cigarette, preparing to light it.","Young Company Commander Yang saw this and immediately said, \"By the way, Comrade Xiao Qiao hates it when people smoke. Yesterday, someone was smoking outside the window just as Comrade Xiao Qiao opened it for ventilation. She choked on the smoke and coughed for a long time, coughing so hard that tears came to her eyes. It scared me to death; I almost took her to see a doctor.\"","Qin Yuanzheng: \"...\"","Qin Yuanzheng silently put the cigarette back.","He looked at Xiao Yang, reached out and patted his shoulder, and said, \"Alright then, get along well with Comrade Xiao Qiao. Hurry up and deliver the food to her, don't let it get cold.\"","With that, he turned around and prepared to leave.","Xiao Yang quickly asked, \"Eh? Regiment Commander, aren't you going to see Comrade Xiao Qiao?\"","Regiment Commander Qin clearly cared a lot about Comrade Xiao Qiao, and Comrade Xiao Qiao also cared about Regiment Commander Qin, asking about him from time to time.","Since Regiment Commander Qin was already here, why wouldn't he go in and see her?","Qin Yuanzheng shook his head. \"It's enough that you're here. I still have things to do, I'll take my leave first.\"","Saying that, he quickly left, afraid that he wouldn't be able to resist going in to see Qiao Lanshu. If the young girl cried then, he wouldn't bear to leave.","Xiao Yang: \"...\"","Qiao Lanshu also knew that it was about to snow here. Although she had been staying in the guesthouse every day for the past two days, she had read many local magazines and newspapers and had a rough understanding of the climate here.","It was expected to snow in a few days, and once it snowed, the trains would stop running.","However, it wasn't the Winter Solstice yet. The snow would probably only last for a day. After it stopped snowing, she could just buy a ticket and leave.","After the Winter Solstice, it would get even colder. If a heavy snowstorm sealed off the mountains then, the trains would definitely have to suspend operations.","When Xiao Yang came in, Qiao Lanshu was reading the Longcheng Daily. She asked Xiao Yang, \"Company Commander Yang, why are you back late this time?\"","People in the army were very punctual. Young Company Commander Yang always went to get food at a fixed time and returned at a fixed time every day. Today, however, he was ten minutes late.","Xiao Yang explained to her, \"Oh, our Regiment Commander just came over and called me over to ask some questions, so it took up a little time.\"","Qiao Lanshu: \"???\"","Qiao Lanshu froze for a few seconds, immediately put down the newspaper, walked over, and asked, \"Your Regiment Commander came over? Where is he? Is he outside?\"","Qiao Lanshu's accent was completely different from the local one. Xiao Yang thought her voice and accent were both very pleasant to hear.","Therefore, he also really liked talking to Qiao Lanshu. If it weren't for Regiment Commander Qin, he would really have wanted to try pursuing her.","He looked at Qiao Lanshu and said, \"He came, but left again. He just asked me if you were feeling better, and also said it's going to snow soon, so he wanted you to postpone your return to Yangcheng. Then, he said he had something else to do and left first without coming up.\"","Qiao Lanshu: \"...\"","Qiao Lanshu's bright eyes dimmed a little.","She nodded. \"Alright...\"","However, she quickly cheered up again and said, \"By the way, I want to go to the supply and marketing cooperative today to buy some food. Can you accompany me?\"","Eating potatoes, coarse grain steamed breads, sometimes melon-substitute vegetables, and even stiff wire-like noodles every day here was simply hard to swallow.","But food was precious, and Qiao Lanshu didn't want to waste it, so she swallowed it with great difficulty every time.","She couldn't take it anymore. She wanted to go to the supply and marketing cooperative to buy some biscuits or something, or anything else would do, as long as it was a bit more delicious. She had money!","Xiao Yang immediately nodded. \"Sure, when? I'll escort you there.\"","He didn't dare let Qiao Lanshu go out alone. If Regiment Commander Qin found out, he would definitely beat him to death.","After finishing her meal, Qiao Lanshu put on a thick padded jacket and padded trousers, wrapped her head in a scarf, and went out with Xiao Yang.","The supply and marketing cooperative wasn't far. It took them only about ten minutes of walking to get there.","The roadsides around them were bare, covered entirely in yellow earth.","In the northern winters, one truly couldn't see a single trace of green.","When the two of them stepped out, Qin Yuanzheng was standing right there at the street corner opposite the guesthouse.","He had originally just wanted to stand across the street and look up at the second-floor window.","He knew this behavior of his was wrong, but he just couldn't help himself.","He just wanted to see how the young girl was doing, as he could never quite put his mind at ease about her.","Yet he did not dare to actually go meet her, afraid that he might make a mistake.","Therefore, he stood at the street corner opposite her place for quite a while. Then, he saw Qiao Lanshu walking out of the door with Xiao Yang.","The young girl was not tall. Wrapped up in a thick padded winter coat that made her look round and bundled up, she appeared surprisingly adorable.","For some inexplicable reason, a smile escaped Qin Yuanzheng's lips.","The young girl walked beside Young Company Commander Yang, keeping an arm's length between them. He had no idea what Xiao Yang said to her, but the young girl burst into laughter. On her fair little face, her eyes curved into sweet crescents, revealing two small dimples.","With her bright white teeth and a charmingly red tip of her nose, she truly was a beautiful girl.","He had introduced several military officers to her before, but she had not taken a liking to a single one of them.","This time, however, she and Xiao Yang seemed to be getting along quite well, chatting and laughing together.","Moreover, several days had already passed, and Comrade Xiao Yang had not been returned yet.","It seemed that the young girl liked Xiao Yang's type.","Qin Yuanzheng watched the two of them walk away, feeling as though he were watching his own daughter being married off.","This is good, he thought to himself.","He had personally rescued this girl, and now he was personally marrying her off to an officer under his command. He felt completely at peace with it.","With this thought in mind, Qin Yuanzheng turned around and walked away.","He figured he probably would not come back here ever again."]},{"number":17,"title":"Chapter 17: Refusal","paragraphs":["Qiao Lanshu went to the supply and marketing cooperative to look around. Using the grain coupons and money she got from Sun Mingyong, she bought two packs of dried noodles and also two canned meat products.","She then bought half a jin of biscuits, planning to take them back for a late-night snack. After all, since she'd been here, she never seemed to eat enough and felt hungry every night.","Fresh fruits and vegetables were scarce and hard to come by in the northern winter.","She had heard that the military unit had vegetables grown in greenhouses, but those were specifically supplied to the troops.","Ordinary people could hardly buy them.","Thinking that she and Qin Yuanzheng had no fate together, but since he had saved her and helped her a great deal, she asked Xiao Yang, \"Company Commander Yang, I'd like to buy something for Regiment Commander Qin to thank him for his help. What do you think I should buy?\"","Company Commander Xiao Yang thought for a moment and said, \"I don't know what the Regiment Commander likes either, Comrade Xiao Qiao. You don't need to buy anything; he wouldn't accept it. There are rules in our unit against accepting gifts.\"","Hearing this, Qiao Lanshu thought again and said, \"Then how about I send a letter of thanks to your unit? Would that be okay?\"","Company Commander Xiao Yang nodded, \"That's a good idea. The Regiment Commander would definitely be very pleased.\"","Qiao Lanshu was someone who acted on her decisions. As soon as she returned to the guesthouse, she started writing the thank-you letter.","...","Meanwhile, Qin Yuanzheng had specifically gone to the food factory at noon today to meet with his cousin, Yang Wenyan.","Yang Wenyan initially thought he had come because of the Sun Mingyong matter and kept saying, \"Yuanzheng, I'm really sorry. I truly had no idea that scoundrel Sun Mingyong dared to impersonate an officer and was swindling his way around here. If I had known, I would never have let him into the factory.\"","In those days, all new employees had to undergo family background checks.","Sun Mingyong had money orders and grain coupons sent from a department store in Yangcheng, along with a letter of introduction from Qiao's father obtained from the neighborhood committee, so his identity appeared legitimate.","Coupled with Wei Zhengye's guarantee, he smoothly entered the factory.","Yangcheng was too far away, and no one thought to verify things there.","Qin Yuanzheng sat in Yang Wenyan's office. He was tall, sturdy, with ruggedly handsome features, and wore a crisp military uniform. The female workers in the factory were all stealing glances at him.","As soon as Yang Wenyan saw his tall and handsome cousin, he shook his head inwardly with regret.","What a pity, a real shame.","Such a strong, healthy body... how could he be infertile? It just didn't make sense.","After sitting down, Qin Yuanzheng said, \"Cousin, I came today to talk to you about Comrade Wang Huiping and me.\"","Yang Wenyan's eyes lit up and he immediately asked, \"How did it go? Getting along alright this time? Are you planning to marry her?\"","Qin Yuanzheng was silent for a moment before shaking his head. \"Cousin, she and I aren't suitable, so I've decided to let it go. Since you were the matchmaker, I came specifically to tell you. Also, you don't need to introduce anyone to me in the future. I really don't want to get married.\"","Yang Wenyan: \"...\"","Yang Wenyan frowned and said to him, \"Yuanzheng, Comrade Wang Huiping has a job, a son, and a gentle personality. What more are you looking for? What kind of woman do you actually like? Tell me, and I'll have people introduce you to someone?\"","The image of Qiao Lanshu instantly appeared in Qin Yuanzheng's mind.","However, he immediately stopped himself from dwelling on it. He said, \"No need. The one I like... isn't here.\"","Yang Wenyan was speechless. \"There are so many factories, so many outstanding female comrades. How could there not be one?\"","Qin Yuanzheng was a man of his word. Once he made a decision, he wouldn't dwell on it. He stood up and said, \"Cousin, really, it's not necessary. I'm very busy at the mining area, so I'll take my leave now.\"","With that, he turned and left the office.","Yang Wenyan sighed.","Previously, Qin Yuanzheng's parents had written to him, asking him to look after his cousin and to pick from the female workers at the factory to introduce a match to Qin Yuanzheng.","He had agreed quite readily at the time.","Yet years had passed, and Qin Yuanzheng was still single.","After returning home, Yang Wenyan told his wife, Deng Xiaozhen, about this.","Deng Xiaozhen worked at the textile factory and was a colleague of Wang Huiping's. Busy in the kitchen, she was somewhat surprised to hear Yang Wenyan's words: \"What? Such a good comrade, and Yuanzheng still didn't take a liking to her?\"","Yang Wenyan took off his coat and hung it on the hook by the door. \"He's decided not to get married. He even said something about the girl he likes not being around here.\"","Deng Xiaozhen, holding a spatula, also felt speechless upon hearing this: \"There are so many female workers in the factories here. If none of them catch his eye, then probably in the whole country there isn't one he'd fancy. He wouldn't be wanting to marry a fairy goddess, would he?\"","Deng Xiaozhen muttered to herself that she hadn't realized before that Qin Yuanzheng's standards were so high.","Yang Wenyan had been utterly exhausted lately due to matters at the factory.","He said, \"Forget it. Since he doesn't want to get married, I won't meddle anymore from now on. You go and tell Wang Huiping, ask her not to come around anymore. Her conditions are good too; she should look for someone else.\"","Deng Xiaozhen, stir-frying vegetables, said:","\"Her conditions are good, but she is divorced after all, and with a son. What average man is willing to marry a woman with a boy? If it were a girl, it would be easier to find a match... Ah, I think Huiping really likes Yuanzheng. She might still try to fight for a chance.\"","Yang Wenyan snorted coldly. \"A regimental-level cadre, never married, tall, handsome, and strong. Who wouldn't like him? If it weren't for his infertility, it wouldn't have been Wang Huiping's turn.\"","Deng Xiaozhen shook her head while stir-frying. She had thought this pair might work out.","Early the next morning, when Deng Xiaozhen arrived at the textile factory, she found Wang Huiping and told her about it.","The smile instantly vanished from Wang Huiping's face.","She was silent for a moment before saying, \"Last time I brought him stewed pig's trotters, and he personally escorted Xiao Yuan and me home. When we parted, he even said he would come see me next time. I thought...\"","Deng Xiaozhen patted her arm. \"A melon forced off the vine isn't sweet. Besides, this melon isn't one you can force anyway. Just keep looking. With your good conditions, are you afraid of not finding a man?\"","That's what they said, but they both knew Wang Huiping was unlikely to find another man as outstanding as Qin Yuanzheng.","So, after returning home, Wang Huiping grew more and more unwilling to accept it the more she thought about it.","Therefore, she went to the supply and marketing cooperative to buy some canned goods and liquor. After her shift, she found Deng Xiaozhen, saying she wanted to have another meal with Qin Yuanzheng, to ask him face-to-face if there was still a chance.","Deng Xiaozhen felt somewhat awkward but agreed to go back and have Yang Wenyan contact Qin Yuanzheng.","On the afternoon of the third day, snow had begun to fall. Qin Yuanzheng hadn't taken the car; he rode his bicycle to the entrance of Yang Wenyan's residential compound.","By then, the snow was already heavy, accumulating in a thick layer on the ground.","He found himself wondering: I wonder if Comrade Xiao Qiao is cold in the guesthouse? She's from the south and has never seen snow. She's probably delighted, right?","Yang Wenyan, Deng Xiaozhen, and Wang Huiping were already inside the room.","It was much like the first time they had met, the difference being that Xiao Yuan wasn't present this time.","Qin Yuanzheng found it a bit strange. Why hadn't Xiao Yuan come this time?","But he didn't ask, nor was there any need to.","Wang Huiping walked over with a smile and said, \"Regiment Commander Qin, you're here. Everyone was waiting for you.\"","As she spoke, she reached out to take the overcoat he was taking off.","However, Qin Yuanzheng avoided her hand and hung the coat on the wall himself.","Seeing this, how could Wang Huiping not understand?","Was Qin Yuanzheng truly not intending to pursue a relationship with her?","Clearly, the feelings during their first two meetings had been quite positive.","Looking at Qin Yuanzheng's tall, broad back, she pressed her lips together and brought out the wine glasses she had prepared earlier.","Deng Xiaozhen had already set out the dishes. Wang Huiping went over with the glasses and wine, saying with a smile, \"It's snowing heavily today. Let's have a drink together to warm ourselves up.\""]},{"number":18,"title":"Chapter 18: His Needs","paragraphs":["Qin Yuanzheng and Yang Wenyan usually drank a bit of alcohol.","Qin Yuanzheng's alcohol tolerance was quite good, honed during his time in the military.","Seeing the liquor Wang Huiping brought out, Yang Wenyan immediately said, \"Oh, this is Fenjiu? Not bad, quite hard to get, isn't it?\"","Wang Huiping smiled and said, \"It's alright. I had some saved-up liquor ration tickets, so I could buy a jin at the supply and marketing cooperative. It just so happens there's heavy snow today, let's have some drinks to warm ourselves up.\"","As she spoke, she placed four cups on the table and began pouring. \"I've already warmed the wine. Let me pour for you.\"","Deng Xiaozhen and Yang Wenyan looked at Wang Huiping, genuinely thinking she was a good person.","Although her looks were somewhat plain, she was virtuous and capable. The key point was she already had a son; raising him to adulthood, the boy would eventually call Qin Yuanzheng 'Dad' too. That seemed pretty good, didn't it?","Wang Huiping handed them the wine, one cup each. The wine was warm and mellow.","It was indeed good liquor, usually hard to come by, and Yang Wenyan was particularly fond of it.","He said to Qin Yuanzheng, \"Come on, Yuanzheng, it's been a long time since we brothers drank together. Let's take advantage of today and have a few more cups.\"","Qin Yuanzheng nodded and downed the wine in one gulp.","He turned to look out the window. Outside, heavy snow was swirling down. The windowsill and the distant scenery were instantly blanketed in a vast whiteness.","The view outside was beautiful, but it was bitterly cold. He wondered what that young girl was doing now?","Was she leaning by the bed watching the snow?","Wanting to go out and play in it, yet afraid of the cold, then sitting by the window with a conflicted expression?","Thinking of this, Qin Yuanzheng smiled again.","He felt he must be drunk, his mind always wandering to Qiao Lanshu.","That young girl was only eighteen. He mustn't make a mistake.","With this thought, Qin Yuanzheng took another sip of wine.","The more they ate, the warmer it got. Qin Yuanzheng took off his jacket, wearing only a dacron shirt.","He rolled up his sleeves, revealing his muscular, veined forearms.","Yang Wenyan, while drinking, told them about Sun Mingyong.","He said, \"That scoundrel Sun Mingyong, he sure can spin a tale! An orphan, yet he claimed his father was a department store manager and his mother a primary school teacher! If he had just properly married his fiancée, it might not have counted as such a big lie. The key is, he actually dumped his fiancée and then married Wei Zhengye's daughter. What a bastard.\"","Deng Xiaozhen sighed with feeling. \"So you see, when finding a partner, it's best to know their background. For those coming from other places, how would we know their family situation? It's so far away, we can't exactly verify it, can we?\"","As she spoke, she glanced at Qin Yuanzheng.","Wang Huiping also asked curiously, \"How did I hear that Sun Mingyong's fiancée came all the way from Guangzhou to look for him? Otherwise, he might not have been exposed.\"","Yang Wenyan snorted coldly. \"Exactly. I heard the young girl waited at the station with no one to pick her up, then went to the headquarters. An officer from our unit even took her to the hospital.\"","Deng Xiaozhen asked curiously, \"What does that southern girl actually look like? Was she not pretty? Otherwise, why would Sun Mingyong abandon her?\"","Hearing this, Qin Yuanzheng said in a low voice, \"The young girl is quite pretty. Sun Mingyong is the ugly one.\"","Everyone: \"...\"","Deng Xiaozhen asked curiously, \"Yuanzheng, you've seen that girl? I heard she's only eighteen, is that true?\"","Wang Huiping also stared at him.","Qin Yuanzheng didn't want to say more on the subject and simply said, \"This wine tastes good, very mellow.\"","Wang Huiping smiled, stood up, and poured another cup for Yang Wenyan and Qin Yuanzheng, saying, \"Regiment Commander Qin, Director Yang, please drink more. There's plenty of wine.\"","Seeing Qin Yuanzheng's reluctance to talk, Yang Wenyan changed the subject. He asked Wang Huiping, \"Comrade Wang, it's been over two years since your divorce, right? Hadn't you thought about finding someone again before?\"","Wang Huiping's smile turned somewhat bitter. \"I was a bit afraid before. Afraid of finding someone who would hit me. I could endure it, but Xiao Yuan is still young, he couldn't take it.\"","Hearing this, Qin Yuanzheng looked up at her, thinking this woman had it tough too.","He despised men who bullied women, let alone those who hit their own wives and children. Were they even human?","Deng Xiaozhen sighed. \"The child is the real pity. Xiao Yuan is still so little.\"","The two women chatted for a while longer. Deng Xiaozhen thought that since Wang Huiping's situation was so pitiful, Qin Yuanzheng might soften.","However, Qin Yuanzheng kept staring at the heavy snow outside, lost in thought.","Of course, Qin Yuanzheng's attitude was already quite clear. Wang Huiping had initially wanted to ask something, but now she didn't dare.","The meal lasted over an hour. Outside, the north wind howled, rattling the windows.","The snow was falling heavier too.","Yang Wenyan, his face flushed from drinking, hooked his arm around Qin Yuanzheng's shoulder and said, \"It's snowing heavily outside. Stay and sleep here tonight, don't leave. The bed in the room you used before is still there.\"","When Qin Yuanzheng first arrived in Longcheng, he had stayed at Yang Wenyan's place for a while.","Back then, he wasn't a regimental-level officer yet, and Yang Wenyan wasn't married either.","In the blink of an eye, several years had passed.","He nodded and said, \"You all take your time eating. I'll go back to the room and lie down for a bit.\"","He hadn't drunk for a long time. Having accidentally had a few extra cups today, he felt hot all over and a bit dizzy.","His body temperature was naturally high, and he usually didn't wear much even in cold weather.","Now, after drinking, he felt unbearably hot and restless.","He returned to the small room he had stayed in before and first opened the window for ventilation.","The howling north wind, carrying cotton-like snowflakes, blew in through the window.","The cool breeze cleared his head a little.","He then closed the window again, leaving only a narrow crack.","He was too hot, unbearably restless all over, feeling as if he were lying on a steamer, heat emanating from his entire body.","He took off his shirt, wearing only a camouflage-colored tank top.","Closing his eyes, his mind grew hazy. Comrade Xiao Qiao's smiling face lingered persistently in his thoughts.","Qin Yuanzheng tugged at his trousers, feeling some discomfort.","He pressed his hand against the black leather belt, thinking about unfastening it and taking off his pants to sleep, which would be more comfortable.","But then he remembered this wasn't his own dormitory.","Better not.","Enduring it, he tugged at his trousers again, feeling very uncomfortable.","It was strange. He usually had good self-control and hadn't felt this kind of desire for a long time.","But this time, the urge was particularly strong.","And at a time like this, the image of Comrade Xiao Qiao's smiling face he had seen outside the guesthouse two days ago grew clearer and clearer in his mind."]},{"number":19,"title":"Chapter 19: He Made a Mistake","paragraphs":["Qin Yuanzheng's self-control had always been excellent, but this time, he almost lost it.","If Comrade Xiao Qiao knew that he was thinking of her face at a time like this, she would probably cry from anger.","Sigh, at his age, almost thirty, was he really going to make this kind of mistake?","If only he didn't suffer from infertility, he thought vaguely, maybe he would fight for it.","And just like that, Qin Yuanzheng drifted into a hazy sleep.","But in the middle of the night, his acute senses as a soldier caused his eyes to snap open.","He turned to look at the door and saw the door to his room open, followed by a woman walking in.","There was no light in the room, and the north wind howled outside amidst a heavy snowstorm, allowing no light to filter in.","In the darkness, he vaguely recognized the woman as Wang Huiping.","The snow was probably too heavy, and since he and Yang Wenyan had drunk too much, no one could escort Wang Huiping back.","So, Deng Xiaozhen let Wang Huiping stay the night here as well.","However, in the dead of night, why did Wang Huiping suddenly walk into his room?","When he came in earlier, he was so dizzy that he seemed to have forgotten to lock the door.","Frowning slightly, he remained silent for two seconds, only to see Wang Huiping yawn and walk straight toward him.","Did she drink too much and walk into the wrong room? Or was it something else...","Regardless of whether she did it intentionally or otherwise, Qin Yuanzheng couldn't be bothered to figure it out.","When Wang Huiping got close, Qin Yuanzheng suddenly flipped up. Wang Huiping, as if not expecting him to suddenly rise, let out a low cry of fright. Then, Qin Yuanzheng struck her on the neck with the palm of his hand, knocking her out cold.","Qin Yuanzheng's head was still a bit dizzy. He looked down at his lower abdomen...","Something was wrong.","This wasn't a normal reaction to just drinking alcohol. Besides, how many hours had it been?","He raised his hand to check his watch; it was already past midnight.","He remembered eating dinner at seven, which took an hour, so it was eight.","When he came in to lie down, it definitely wasn't even nine o'clock.","It was now past twelve. Over three hours had passed, yet his head was still dizzy, and his whole body felt weak and sore, but certain parts of him were extremely energetic.","It had ached all night.","Even in his sleep, he had dreamed of Comrade Xiao Qiao...","Qin Yuanzheng's face darkened. He grabbed his shirt, draped it over himself, walked out of the room, and turned on the living room lights.","Then, he went to knock on Yang Wenyan's door.","Yang Wenyan had been drinking and was sleeping soundly. Hearing the knock, he was still a bit groggy and mumbled, Xiaozhen, did we not close the window tightly? Why is it banging?","Deng Xiaozhen sat up from the bed, listened for a moment, and asked, Who is it?","Qin Yuanzheng's cold and deep voice carried over. Cousin-in-law, it's me. I have to leave, so I came to let you know.","Deng Xiaozhen: ...","Whenever Qin Yuanzheng stayed over in the past, he would always leave on his own before dawn. When had he ever knocked on their door?","Deng Xiaozhen pushed Yang Wenyan and said, Yuanzheng is knocking on the door. Get up quickly.","Yang Wenyan got up groggily, put on his padded jacket, and opened the door with Deng Xiaozhen. Rubbing his eyes, he asked, Yuanzheng? Do you have an emergency mission? Why are you leaving in the middle of the night?","Qin Yuanzheng had already put on his jacket and overcoat.","The overcoat was long, reaching all the way to his knees, which finally made his expression look a bit more natural.","Otherwise, given his physical fitness, it would be too obvious in this state, and it wouldn't be good if his cousin and cousin-in-law saw it.","He said with a serious expression, There's no mission, it's just time for me to go. Cousin, Cousin-in-law, Comrade Wang Huiping somehow wandered into my room just now. I thought a thief had broken in and was startled, so I conveniently knocked her out. You guys should go in and take a look. I won't stay here any longer. I'm leaving first. Let's have a meal next time I'm free.","With that, Qin Yuanzheng strode to the door, opened it, and walked out.","Yang Wenyan: ???","Yang Wenyan hurriedly chased after him, saying, Oh my, it's the middle of the night and snowing outside. What's the rush?","Qin Yuanzheng's voice came from the stairwell. The snow has stopped. Don't see me out, Cousin, go back quickly.","Before he finished speaking, he had already walked down from the third floor and out of the building.","Deng Xiaozhen stood frozen for a few seconds before she reacted. She quickly pushed open the door to the room where Qin Yuanzheng had been sleeping, turned on the light, and looked.","Wang Huiping was lying face down on the floor wearing only thin, unlined garments.","Deng Xiaozhen: ...","Yang Wenyan was no longer sleepy at all.","He walked over briskly.","Deng Xiaozhen was still saying, No, Huiping didn't even drink that much tonight. How did she get so drunk? She even walked into the wrong room when getting up in the night. Look at this mess. Thankfully, Yuanzheng held back. Otherwise, who could withstand a punch from him?","Yang Wenyan glared at her and said angrily, How can you be so dense? Do you think Wang Huiping just walked into the wrong room? She clearly had ulterior motives! I was wondering why she didn't bring Xiao Yuan over tonight and even specifically bought good wine. So this was her plan all along!","He sneered, She's quite smart, knowing to pick a heavy snowy day. What a pity, Yuanzheng is a soldier. Are soldiers that easy to scheme against?","Deng Xiaozhen was dumbfounded. Looking at Yang Wenyan, she said, What do you mean by that? What scheme? Comrade Wang Huiping is a very simple and pragmatic woman. She wouldn't do something like this, would she?","Yang Wenyan said angrily:","You can know a person's face but not their heart! If Sun Mingyong could pretend to be a military officer to trick someone into marriage, what is impossible? You're not the roundworm in her stomach; how well can you really know this Wang Huiping? Yuanzheng insisted on leaving in the middle of the night and didn't want to stay here for another second. It seems he is angry with us. He might even mistakenly believe that we had a hand in tonight's affairs. If so, I won't even be able to explain it to him in the future.","Hearing this, Deng Xiaozhen remembered that Qin Yuanzheng was a regiment commander, and they really valued this relative.","Deng Xiaozhen said angrily, This Wang Huiping really doesn't know her place!","Yang Wenyan: Don't associate with her anymore. What a mess!","Deng Xiaozhen was also angry inside. She went into the room and finally managed to wake Wang Huiping up.","The side of Wang Huiping's neck ached terribly. She reached up to rub her neck and saw Deng Xiaozhen standing in front of her with an unhappy expression, as well as Yang Wenyan standing at the door with a darkened face.","Her heart skipped a beat, knowing that her scheme had been for nothing.","Sure enough, not only had she drawn water with a bamboo basket—achieving nothing—but she had also ended up offending everyone.","But at this moment, she couldn't admit to it. Feigning surprise, she asked Deng Xiaozhen, Xiaozhen, what's wrong? Did you need something from me in the middle of the night?","Deng Xiaozhen looked at her, unsure if she had really drunk too much and walked into the wrong room or what. She simply said, In the middle of the night, you walked into the wrong room. You walked into Yuanzheng's room.","Wang Huiping's expression instantly turned into a panic. What? That... that's really a misunderstanding. I... I didn't do it on purpose...","Deng Xiaozhen couldn't be bothered to watch her act anymore. She sighed and simply said, Yuanzheng looked awful just now. He said he thought there was a thief and knocked you out on reflex. Yuanzheng is strong; is your neck alright?","She hoped nothing was seriously wrong so Wang Huiping wouldn't use it as an excuse to leech off their family. She didn't have the money to compensate her.","Wang Huiping rubbed her neck. It did hurt quite a bit, but she was more concerned about Qin Yuanzheng. So, she said, My neck is fine, Xiaozhen. What about Commander Qin...","Yang Wenyan let out a cold snort and said sarcastically, He left in the middle of the night, braving the heavy snow. He was probably afraid of being robbed again.","Wang Huiping was speechless.","She immediately stood up and said, I... I really went into the wrong room. No, I have to go apologize to him.","Yang Wenyan rolled his eyes in anger, turned around, and went back into his room.","Deng Xiaozhen also said, There's no need, Huiping. Let's just drop this matter here. Don't go looking for Yuanzheng anymore. The two of you really aren't suitable for each other.","Wang Huiping remained silent.","Since Deng Xiaozhen had made it so clear, Wang Huiping could no longer stay there.","She put on her padded cotton coat and prepared to leave.","Right before she walked out the door, Deng Xiaozhen asked her one last time, Huiping, did you really go into the wrong room tonight?","Standing in the dark stairwell, Wang Huiping nodded. Of course it's true, Xiaozhen. Do even you not believe me?","Deng Xiaozhen just smiled. Take it easy on your way back. Careful, the ground is slippery.","With that, Deng Xiaozhen shut the door.","Wang Huiping walked out of the residential compound. It was pitch black outside, the road covered in a vast expanse of white.","She had said she was leaving, and neither Deng Xiaozhen nor Yang Wenyan had asked her to stay, even though she was a woman and it was the middle of the night.","It seemed Deng Xiaozhen was truly going to cut ties with her over this incident.","Wang Huiping felt a wave of bitterness in her heart.","What had she done wrong? She just wanted to find someone to rely on so she could live a carefree life for the rest of her days.","...","Qin Yuanzheng left Yang Wenyan's house late in the night.","He rode his bicycle back to his dormitory in the mining area military base.","As a commander, his dorm was a small one-bedroom apartment with a living room, which was more than enough for one person.","Originally, the base had wanted to allocate him a two-bedroom apartment in the main compound.","But he didn't have a family and didn't plan on getting married in the future, so he declined it.","Over the years, he continued to live in this small dorm.","As soon as he returned to his room, he locked the door from the inside, stripped off his clothes, and lay down on the bed.","He unbuckled his belt and took off his pants.","He finally felt a bit of relief.","This entire evening had nearly suffocated him with pent-up frustration.","Not having a wife was fine; he would just have to take matters into his own hands to satisfy his needs.","It had been a long time since he had found any release, and he figured he must have drunk spiked wine tonight. Relying on self-control alone wasn't going to get him through this.","He didn't turn on the light. He just closed his eyes, enveloping himself in the darkness. Through the faint light coming from the window, his rugged facial features and the glistening beads of sweat on his forehead could be vaguely seen.","However, his physical fitness and endurance were exceptional, so for a long time, he couldn't quite reach the edge...","After a good while, his mind suddenly flashed back to the day Qiao Lanshu was kidnapped, when he had escorted her back to the guesthouse.","The scene of the young girl tightly gripping the hem of his shirt, looking up at him with tearful eyes.","With a boom, it felt as though something exploded in his mind.","Feeling the aftermath on his hand... he was stunned.","Did he... did he just commit a grave mistake?"]},{"number":20,"title":"Chapter 20: Does Commander Qin have any family members or children","paragraphs":["The next day, Qin Yuanzheng went to work in the mining area early in the morning.","As for Wang Huiping, he didn't ask about her again.","Wang Huiping had drugged his wine and deliberately walked into the wrong room in the middle of the night. This kind of thing was something he absolutely could not tolerate.","However, he had no intention of taking revenge.","After all, Wang Huiping was a single woman raising a young son. If he retaliated, she would inevitably lose her job.","At that point, it would be hard enough for her as an adult woman, let alone for a seven or eight-year-old boy.","The dormitories currently assigned by the work unit had heating, making it a better living environment for the child.","Therefore, Qin Yuanzheng chose not to make a fuss with Wang Huiping entirely for the sake of the child.","But this was a one-time exception. If Wang Huiping ever caused trouble again and fell into his hands, he would not show any mercy.","When Qin Yuanzheng arrived at the office, he saw Staff Officer Lin grinning at him.","Qin Yuanzheng had been sexually frustrated the night before and had to take matters into his own hands several times. He had vented his physical urges, but he still felt uncomfortable inside, as if something was missing.","Pent-up frustration lingered in his heart, leaving him feeling incredibly restless.","Now, seeing Staff Officer Lin smiling so weirdly, he felt a bit speechless. What are you laughing at? Do you have too much free time?","Staff Officer Lin: ...","Staff Officer Lin genuinely felt that Commander Qin needed to blow off some steam. Just looking at his recent mood, he was clearly too on edge.","He quickly handed over a letter and said, Reporting to the Commander, here is a letter of commendation addressed to you.","Qin Yuanzheng: ???","Qin Yuanzheng asked in bewilderment, What letter? For whom?","As he spoke, he picked up the letter to take a look.","The handwriting on it was very clean and elegant, looking exactly like something written by a well-behaved and gentle girl.","Every stroke was neat and tidy, and the characters were slightly rounded, looking quite cute.","People in the army usually had handwriting that was either scribbled or wildly unconstrained. Some soldiers' handwriting was even harder to read than a doctor's prescription.","Qin Yuanzheng had rarely seen such clean and lovely handwriting. Finding it quite novel, he admired the envelope for two minutes before saying, This handwriting is actually quite interesting.","Then, he looked at the words on the cover again. It indeed said it was addressed to the 21st Regiment of the Construction Corps, Commander Qin Yuanzheng.","Qin Yuanzheng opened the letter and asked, Who delivered this letter?","Staff Officer Lin smiled and said, Comrade Xiao Qiao delivered it in person. She said she wanted to thank you for saving her life. After much thought, she wrote you a letter of commendation. I initially thought this letter should be sent to Commander Li, but when I looked at the envelope, it had your name on it.","Staff Officer Lin found Comrade Xiao Qiao to be quite amusing. He said, Comrade Xiao Qiao wanted the army to commend you, but she didn't know she was supposed to send the commendation letter to your superior, so she just sent it directly to you. I wanted to explain it to her at the time, but I held back. I was afraid she would feel embarrassed.","Hearing this, Qin Yuanzheng also found it a bit funny.","A letter praising him was delivered right into his own hands. The little girl would probably feel embarrassed once she went back and realized what she had done.","Qin Yuanzheng fully opened the letter, took out the paper, and read it.","The letter spanned a full two pages.","In that clean and cute handwriting, it described how Commander Qin was passionate, kind, and majestically imposing, saving her twice. Once was at the entrance of the command headquarters when she had just arrived here.","The other time was at the entrance of the guesthouse when she was almost kidnapped.","She wrote that Commander Qin was like a deity descending from the heavens, saving her from a life-threatening crisis, and that he was the most amazing commander in her heart.","Reading up to this point, Qin Yuanzheng suddenly felt a rush of heat to his face.","His ears turned slightly red, and he coughed twice in discomfort before continuing to read.","Staff Officer Lin looked at his expression and instantly became incredibly curious. He leaned over and said, Commander, what's written in the letter? Let me have a look too, won't you?","However, Qin Yuanzheng immediately pressed down on the letter, glanced up at him, and said, What are you looking at? Do you have too much free time?","Staff Officer Lin: ...","Staff Officer Lin stared at Qin Yuanzheng's bright red ears and uncomfortable expression as if he had seen a ghost.","He whispered, Commander, something's not right with you. You're being flirtatious.","Qin Yuanzheng: ...","Qin Yuanzheng coughed, folded the letter, and carefully tucked it into his jacket pocket before saying, What do you mean something's not right? What flirtatious? What kind of nonsense are you spouting all day?","Staff Officer Lin, however, stroked his chin and suddenly seemed to realize something. Oh my, I was wondering why that Miss Xiao Qiao didn't take a fancy to me. Commander, do you think she might have taken a fancy to you?","Qin Yuanzheng: ...","Qin Yuanzheng's movements paused. He was silent for a moment before saying, She didn't take a fancy to you because you don't have the blessing. Didn't you see that Young Company Commander Yang gets along quite well with her?","Staff Officer Lin: ...","Staff Officer Lin thought for a moment and added, Commander, if you are interested in Comrade Xiao Qiao, you should give it a try. Maybe Comrade Xiao Qiao wouldn't mind your...","As he spoke, he quickly shut his mouth, not daring to say another word.","Qin Yuanzheng gave him a look and walked out the door with a dark expression.","Staff Officer Lin looked at Qin Yuanzheng's back and sighed inwardly.","Look at him, Commander Qin was clearly interested in Miss Xiao Qiao, yet he refused to make a move himself, insisting on introducing this person and that person to her instead.","Even though his infertility couldn't be cured, perhaps Miss Xiao Qiao wouldn't mind?","Qin Yuanzheng walked outside. The snow had stopped, and with the sun coming out, the snow on the ground was slowly beginning to melt.","He thought to himself, since it hadn't snowed these past few days, the little girl was probably going to buy her train ticket, right?","He reached up and pressed his chest pocket, which still held the letter the little girl had written to him.","He should go over and check on her.","With this thought in mind, he went to the supply and marketing cooperative and bought some snacks for the little girl, like candies, biscuits, sunflower seeds, and peanuts. Seeing some Pechoin skin cream, he also bought two tins.","On his way out, he spotted a red scarf and immediately stopped in his tracks.","The little girl had fair skin and glossy black hair; she would surely look beautiful wearing this scarf.","On an impulse, he bought the scarf as well.","Then, carrying his purchases, he drove his car toward the guesthouse.","...","Qiao Lanshu was not at the guesthouse at this moment.","Accompanied by Young Company Commander Yang, she had first gone to the railway station to buy a train ticket.","The ticket was for three days later. After buying it, she put it in her pocket.","Then, she went to the supply and marketing cooperative with Young Company Commander Yang. They arrived almost immediately after Qin Yuanzheng had left.","Young Company Commander Yang said, Comrade Xiao Qiao, are you looking to buy some local specialties to take back to your hometown? Let's go check the second floor, or we can go to a nearby department store. I can take you there; we just need to catch a bus.","Qiao Lanshu shook her head and said, No, I'm not buying local specialties.","She walked over to the counter selling fabric and cotton. Looking at the fabrics, she said softly, I want to buy some fabric to give to Commander Qin's family and child. Commander Qin has helped me so much, but I don't know how to repay him.","Young Company Commander Yang first nodded. \"Mhm, this fabric is quite nice...\"","Then, his expression suddenly blanked, and he blurted out, \"Huh? Commander Qin's family and child? Commander Qin has a family and a child?\"","He had been following Qin Yuanzheng for several years now, so how could he not know about this?"]},{"number":21,"title":"Chapter 21: What do you think of me","paragraphs":["Qiao Lanshu looked at the fabrics, thinking about her impending departure. The North and the South were so far apart; once she left, it might be a permanent farewell.","The thought of never seeing Qin Yuanzheng again left an ache in her heart.","Xiao Yang scratched his head. Watching Qiao Lanshu earnestly pick out fabrics, he whispered, \"Comrade Xiao Qiao, did you get something wrong? Our commander isn't married yet. He doesn't have a family, let alone children.\"","Qiao Lanshu: \"???\"","Shocked, Qiao Lanshu turned her head to look at him, her eyes wide and round. \"Huh?\"","Xiao Yang: \"...\"","Xiao Yang said hesitantly, \"Did I misunderstand? By family, did you mean the commander's parents and brothers? His home is over by the Changbai Mountains. He isn't a local, and his family isn't here. I think you shouldn't buy this; it can't be mailed back anytime soon anyway.\"","Qiao Lanshu: \"...\"","Qiao Lanshu stared at Xiao Yang, her eyes suddenly lighting up.","They were like two little light bulbs, shining brightly as she stared at him, making Xiao Yang's hair stand on end.","Suppressing her excitement, Qiao Lanshu asked cautiously, \"Then, does your commander have a girlfriend? Or someone he's currently seeing? Does he?\"","She leaned in close to Xiao Yang and asked urgently, \"Hurry up and tell me, does he or not?\"","Xiao Yang immediately shook his head and said, \"As far as I know, he probably doesn't. The commander said before that he won't get married.\"","Qiao Lanshu was taken aback. \"Not getting married? Why?\"","Xiao Yang became a little hesitant. He scratched his head and said, \"Well, about that...\"","Qiao Lanshu looked at him eagerly. \"Tell me! Is there a rule saying you can't?\"","Qiao Lanshu paid close attention to Commander Qin, and it seemed she was interested in Commander Qin too.","After spending these past few days together, Young Company Commander Yang already knew that the object of Qiao Lanshu's affection was Commander Qin, which was why she hadn't taken a fancy to anyone else among them.","He thought this was a good thing. The whole regiment was waiting to attend the commander's wedding banquet.","He hesitated for a moment, thinking it shouldn't be a big deal to tell Qiao Lanshu. After all, it wasn't a military secret.","So he said, \"Comrade Xiao Qiao, it's not convenient to talk here. Let's go outside.\"","With that, the two walked out the door of the supply and marketing cooperative, strolling along the small path toward the guesthouse.","Qiao Lanshu was incredibly anxious.","As soon as they were outside, she started urging him, \"There's no one here, hurry up and tell me.\"","Xiao Yang lowered his voice and said, \"It was probably two or three years ago. Our commander went to the province for a full physical examination. The results showed that he suffers from infertility. That is, he can't have children.\"","Qiao Lanshu: \"...\"","Xiao Yang sighed. \"Because of this, a female comrade who had been getting along pretty well with the commander turned around and ran off to marry another officer. After that incident, our commander went on a few blind dates organized by the military, but none of them worked out. Later, our commander said he wouldn't marry and that he would grow old alone.\"","Speaking of this, Xiao Yang started sighing again. He said, \"Our commander's character is absolutely flawless. It's such a pity...\"","As he spoke, he looked at Qiao Lanshu again and whispered, \"Comrade Xiao Qiao, I only told you this in secret. Please don't tell anyone else. It's not glorious for this kind of thing to spread.\"","Even though it had spread a long time ago.","Which female comrade in the nearby factories didn't know that Commander Qin of the 21st Regiment was infertile?","Everyone was even discussing how Qin Yuanzheng looked so robust and energetic, wondering how he could possibly be infertile.","Some people spread rumors, eventually claiming outright that he was impotent in that regard.","Because of this, even some female workers who didn't mind his infertility didn't dare go on a blind date with him, fearing that he was truly incapable in bed, which would mean living like a widow, wouldn't it?","What would be the point of getting married then?","Qiao Lanshu, however, didn't overthink it. Her heart and mind were entirely consumed by one thought: \"Commander Qin isn't married, and he doesn't have a girlfriend. Then, then I...\"","Full of anticipation, she looked at Xiao Yang and asked, \"Xiao Yang, what type does your commander like? I mean, well, you know...\"","As she spoke, she felt a bit too embarrassed to continue.","After all, she was thin-skinned and shy about asking.","Xiao Yang wanted to say something else, but then he noticed a car parked across from the guesthouse.","And the very subject of their conversation happened to be standing next to the car, holding something in his hand, looking up at the second floor of the guesthouse with a deep, dark gaze.","Xiao Yang froze for a moment, then hurried over. \"Commander, are you here to see Comrade Xiao Qiao?\"","Qiao Lanshu hadn't seen Qin Yuanzheng for a few days either. She had been holding herself back before, mistakenly believing that Qin Yuanzheng had a family and children, thus not daring to harbor any thoughts about him.","But now, how could she hold back?","The brave get to enjoy the world first!","Qin Yuanzheng first saw Xiao Yang, and then he saw Comrade Xiao Qiao, bundled up so tightly she looked perfectly round.","He stared at Comrade Xiao Qiao for a moment, completely ignoring Xiao Yang.","He walked over and asked, \"The snow is melting today, and the weather is cold. Why did you come out?\"","As he spoke, he took out the red scarf he had just bought, slipped it directly around Qiao Lanshu's neck, and wrapped it around twice in a very natural manner.","Qiao Lanshu: \"...\"","Standing nearby, Young Company Commander Yang was dumbfounded.","He looked at Commander Qin, and then looked at Comrade Xiao Qiao, whose eyes were full of the commander.","He knew it—he was just a third wheel!","After wrapping the scarf around Qiao Lanshu, Qin Yuanzheng suddenly realized that his behavior might have crossed a line.","He looked uncomfortable for a second, and then he heard Qiao Lanshu say, \"Young Company Commander Yang said it won't snow for the next few days and that the trains have resumed operation. So, I went and bought a train ticket. Look.\"","As she spoke, she pulled the train ticket out of her coat pocket and handed it to Qin Yuanzheng to see.","Qin Yuanzheng's expression froze, and he felt a pang of discomfort in his heart. He wanted to smile, but found he couldn't muster one at all.","He took the ticket and glanced at it. The train wouldn't depart for another three days, so Comrade Xiao Qiao would still have to stay here for three more days.","In three days, she would be leaving.","Qin Yuanzheng suddenly turned his head and gave Xiao Yang a look of deep frustration, as if disappointed he hadn't met expectations.","He had thought that since Xiao Yang had spent so many days with Comrade Xiao Qiao, and seeing how well the two of them got along...","...he had thought there might be a spark between them.","Yet in the end, no one in their unit was able to make such a wonderful girl stay!","Clearly, they deserved to be single.","Xiao Yang was baffled by his stare, having absolutely no idea what Commander Qin meant by it.","Qiao Lanshu looked eagerly at Qin Yuanzheng. Blushing slightly, with the tip of her nose red from the cold, she said, \"Commander Qin, could I have a word with you in private? I have something I want to tell you.\""]},{"number":22,"title":"Chapter 22: I Like Someone Like You","paragraphs":["Qin Yuanzheng lowered his head, looking at Qiao Lanshu who was gazing up at him eagerly. He couldn't help but think of the dream he had last night.","In his dream, Qiao Lanshu was also looking up at him like this. The difference was that the little girl in his dream had teary eyes and a soft voice, looking incredibly pitiful in front of him.","Feeling a bit guilty, he touched his nose and nodded. \"Alright, it's cold outside. Let's go back inside to talk.\"","With that, he picked up the items and led Qiao Lanshu back to the guesthouse.","Young Company Commander Yang followed behind them but didn't enter the room. He tactfully stood at the door, keeping watch for them.","The room was nice and warm, and Qiao Lanshu instantly breathed a sigh of relief.","She took off the red scarf around her neck, reaching out to stroke it affectionately. Then, she looked at Qin Yuanzheng and asked, \"Regiment Commander Qin, did you buy this specifically for me?\"","She emphasized the word \"specifically.\"","Qin Yuanzheng nodded, looking a bit uncomfortable. \"Yes. It's been too cold these past two days. I happened to see it when I went to the supply and marketing cooperative, so I bought one for you.\"","Qiao Lanshu instantly smiled, her eyes curving into crescents. She said, \"Thank you, I really like red.\"","Qin Yuanzheng scratched his head and touched his nose again, looking a bit flustered.","Keeping a straight face, he nodded. \"As long as you like it.\"","After that, he didn't know what else to say.","Pondering, he started searching for a topic. \"These past few days, I saw that you and Young Company Commander Yang were getting along pretty well. Why do you still want to go back to Yangcheng?\"","He had assumed that Qiao Lanshu and Young Company Commander Yang had already started dating, so why would she still want to return to Yangcheng?","Wouldn't it be great to just stay here, work, and follow the army as a military spouse?","He would certainly take extra care of her husband.","He could create more opportunities for Young Company Commander Yang, and it wasn't impossible for him to be promoted to deputy battalion commander within three years.","The families of battalion-level officers could follow the army and live in the military compound.","However, Qiao Lanshu replied, \"Young Company Commander Yang? He is quite nice, but he and I aren't suitable for each other, right?\"","Moreover, looking at Young Company Commander Yang's attitude, he didn't seem to have any intention of dating her either. Otherwise, she wouldn't have been able to get along with him so easily.","Hearing her say this, what else could Qin Yuanzheng not understand?","He frowned and asked somewhat helplessly, \"How come you haven't taken a liking to anyone? You...\"","He hesitated for a moment but still asked, \"What kind of person do you actually like? I'll help you look for one.\"","He thought Qiao Lanshu would reject him. After all, she was a southerner and couldn't adapt to this place, so it was normal for her to want to go back.","When the time came, he would arrange for two people to specially escort her to Hankou. Taking the train from here, it would take a day and a night to reach Hankou.","Then they would see her off onto the train heading to Yangcheng. That way, it would be much safer.","Qin Yuanzheng was already mulling this over in his mind, but Qiao Lanshu was looking at him with an eager gaze.","Meeting Qiao Lanshu's gaze, Qin Yuanzheng's expression blanked for a moment. Then, he felt the tips of his ears start to burn again.","He was almost thirty years old, and after all these years on the battlefield, what kind of severe storms and heavy waves hadn't he seen?","Yet, facing Comrade Xiao Qiao's gaze, he found himself somewhat at a loss for what to do.","Comrade Xiao Qiao mustered up her courage and boldly looked up at Qin Yuanzheng. She said, \"Regiment Commander Qin, I... I just like someone like you. Aren't you unmarried?\"","In her past life, it was said that he fell in love with her at first sight. Why did it seem like he wasn't interested in her this time?","Qin Yuanzheng: \"...\"","Qiao Lanshu's face was flushed red, and she was so nervous that she even stuttered a bit.","In this day and age, how many women dared to speak so bluntly to a man?","She had mustered a great deal of courage. After all, she had already bought her train ticket. Whether she left or stayed would all depend on this single move.","Blushing, she said, \"I asked Young Company Commander Yang, and he said you aren't married and don't have a partner. I, I just thought...\"","Qin Yuanzheng: \"Nonsense!\"","Qin Yuanzheng's expression turned serious. He stared at Qiao Lanshu's somewhat stunned eyes, held back for a moment, but still hardened his heart to reprimand her strictly. \"You only think this way because I saved you. How can marriage be treated as a child's play? You should know that at my age, I could even...\"","He almost blurted out, \"I could even be your dad.\"","But on second thought, there was only an 11-year difference between them. Being her dad seemed a bit of a stretch.","He paused and said, \"Don't bring this up again in the future. I'll just pretend I didn't hear it. You get some good rest first. I have things to do, so I'll be leaving now.\"","Saying this, he didn't even dare to look at Comrade Xiao Qiao's reddened eyes. He turned around and fled in panic.","Qiao Lanshu stood in the room, tears streaming down her face, crying miserably.","Young Company Commander Yang still didn't know what had happened. Seeing Qiao Lanshu crying so pitifully, he was stunned. He quickly walked in and said, \"Comrade Xiao Qiao, why are you crying? Did our regiment commander bully you?\"","That shouldn't be. Their regiment commander wasn't that kind of person.","It was Qiao Lanshu's first time confessing to a man, and it ended in such a disastrous way.","She felt awkward, ashamed, and extremely sad.","So, she just sat there, silently shedding tears without saying a word.","Young Company Commander Yang scratched his head, not knowing what to do. He stepped out of the room to go find Qin Yuanzheng.","Their regiment commander was such a grown man, yet he made a little girl cry. What kind of situation was this?","Little did he know, when Qin Yuanzheng came out of the guesthouse, he was also feeling terrible.","Sitting in the car, his heart was pounding loudly, thumping out of his chest.","His first reaction was that Comrade Xiao Qiao actually liked him, which simply made him feel pleasantly surprised.","But soon, he sobered up. He and Comrade Xiao Qiao were not suitable for each other.","Setting aside the age issue, just the fact that he was infertile made it impossible between them.","Young Company Commander Yang ran out and, seeing that his car hadn't left yet, hurried over and said, \"Commander, what happened between you two? Comrade Xiao Qiao has been crying nonstop. Do you want to go back and check on her?\"","Qin Yuanzheng fell silent for a moment before saying, \"No need. You go check on her.\"","With that, he left in a very cold and ruthless manner.","Yang: \"...\"","Yang was speechless. What in the world was going on?"]},{"number":23,"title":"Chapter 23: I Want to Get a Vasectomy","paragraphs":["Qin Yuanzheng turned Qiao Lanshu down, but he felt miserable inside.","Although he didn't show it, he suffered from insomnia the night he went back.","For so many years, his daily routine had always been extremely regular. Almost as soon as it was time, he could fall asleep the moment he lay down.","But tonight, he tossed and turned without the slightest bit of sleepiness.","Right now, not only was his body unbearably hot, but his heart was also restless.","If he hadn't known that the little girl liked him, he could have just endured it and suppressed his feelings in his heart, and that would be the end of it.","He had made it through all these years alone; there was no reason he couldn't keep living alone in the future.","But after learning the little girl's true feelings, his state of mind was completely different.","He could no longer righteously tell himself that loneliness was a necessity of life.","There would always be a trace of regret in his heart;","Perhaps when he grew old and looked back on his life, he would regret it and wonder why he had not been brave just once.","The next day, Qin Yuanzheng went to the mining area office with two dark circles under his eyes.","The little girl was taking the train the day after tomorrow. He kept thinking about this matter but didn't dare to go see her off.","He just hid in the mining area office and didn't return to his dormitory for two days.","On the morning of the third day, Young Company Commander Yang came back and asked Staff Officer Lin, Staff Officer Lin, where is our regiment commander? He hasn't been back to the dormitory for three days. Did he go on a mission?","Over the past few days, Staff Officer Lin had been tormented by Yama Qin until he barely looked human.","He sat in the office looking haggard and said weakly, What mission? It would be great if there really was a mission! The Devil went to patrol his territory. Go find him at the construction site.","The mining area was building roads recently, and The Devil went out with the engineers.","Young Company Commander Yang scratched his head and said, Oh no, there's no time. I have to take Comrade Xiao Qiao to the train station. Her train is at ten in the morning. Please tell the regiment commander and ask if he wants to go see her off.","As soon as Staff Officer Lin heard it was Comrade Xiao Qiao, he immediately perked up.","After all, he was the first person to go on a blind date with Comrade Xiao Qiao, and also the first to be rejected.","He looked at Yang with a surprised expression and said, Wait, how come I heard that Comrade Xiao Qiao took a fancy to you? What's going on? So you two aren't dating?","Young Company Commander Yang felt extremely helpless. Why did everyone think that way?","He actually wanted to date Comrade Xiao Qiao, but Comrade Xiao Qiao wasn't interested in him.","So he said, Comrade Xiao Qiao fell for our regiment commander, but our regiment commander rejected her. Comrade Xiao Qiao cried for two days, and our regiment commander didn't go see her even once. Now Comrade Xiao Qiao is leaving, and the regiment commander hasn't even mentioned seeing her off. Sigh, the regiment commander's heart is as hard as his fists.","Staff Officer Lin was speechless.","They all really hoped that Qin Yuanzheng could get married.","However, many female comrades were afraid that Qin Yuanzheng was incapable in that aspect, so they all stopped going on blind dates with him.","But apart from not being able to have children, their regiment commander was actually quite capable in that aspect!","Staff Officer Lin felt that since a silly girl had finally fallen for their regiment commander, he had to hurry up and help push things along.","He glanced at the time and said, It's only nine o'clock now. There's still time. I'll go talk to the regiment commander.","As he spoke, he hastily put on his coat and ran outside.","Young Company Commander Yang then went back to the guesthouse.","Qiao Lanshu had already packed her things and was ready to head out.","She didn't have many belongings, just two sets of clothes and some food to eat on the road.","Besides that, she was still wearing the red scarf that Qin Yuanzheng had given her around her neck.","Qiao Lanshu had been heartbroken for two days and was still feeling very sad.","Being rejected on her very first confession was actually quite embarrassing.","Fortunately, she was about to take the train home. As long as she ran far enough, the awkwardness wouldn't be able to catch up with her!","Standing in the guesthouse where she had stayed for many days, Qiao Lanshu looked at the scenery outside the window. The snow that fell a few days ago had long melted. The whole world looked gray and gloomy, the wind was blowing, and there was no one on the road.","Qiao Lanshu sighed. She sat on the chair, stroking the red scarf.","She always felt that Qin Yuanzheng should have feelings for her; otherwise, why would he treat her so well?","But why did Qin Yuanzheng reject her? Could it be just because she was ten years younger than him?","Qiao Lanshu was somewhat unwilling to give up. Young Company Commander Yang drove the military vehicle over to take Qiao Lanshu to the train station. On the way, Qiao Lanshu still couldn't help but ask, Company Commander Yang, what kind of person does your regiment commander actually like?","She sighed and said, Does he dislike me for being too young?","What could she do about that? She couldn't change her age.","Besides, she didn't even mind that he was old, yet he actually minded that she was young?","As he drove toward the train station, Young Company Commander Yang said, Comrade Xiao Qiao, I think our regiment commander actually cares about you quite a bit.","Qiao Lanshu's eyes lit up. Really?","Then why was Qin Yuanzheng so fierce that day? It really scared her to death.","As a military officer, his aura was already intimidating, and he had kept a straight face and acted fiercely toward her. She was genuinely frightened at the time and even regretted confessing to him.","If she had known, she would have let the feelings rot in her heart and never said a word.","Sigh, she had to sigh every time she thought about it.","Young Company Commander Yang had followed Qin Yuanzheng for so many years, so he had some understanding of Qin Yuanzheng's personality.","The way Qin Yuanzheng looked at Comrade Xiao Qiao was different. The day Comrade Xiao Qiao was almost kidnapped, their regiment commander's gaze was terrifying enough to kill.","Young Company Commander Yang then said, I think our regiment commander probably rejected you because he feels inadequate due to his infertility.","Qiao Lanshu was speechless.","Qiao Lanshu said in surprise, Really? Just because of that?","Young Company Commander Yang nodded. It must be because of that. Comrade Xiao Qiao, I hope you won't blame our regiment commander. He is actually a very good person. He probably didn't mean to be fierce to you on purpose.","Qiao Lanshu thought to herself, infertility wasn't a terminal illness. Even if they couldn't have children, they could just adopt one in the future.","Did Qin Yuanzheng reject her just for this?","Qiao Lanshu became even more unwilling to give up.","At this moment, they happened to pass by the military district hospital. Qiao Lanshu suddenly shouted, Stop the car!","Young Company Commander Yang immediately pulled over to the side of the road and asked her, Comrade Xiao Qiao, did you forget something and need to go back?","Qiao Lanshu had already opened the car door and stepped out. She said, No, I'm going to the hospital.","Her expression was firm, as if she had made some kind of resolution. She said to Young Company Commander Yang, I'm going to get my tubes tied!","Young Company Commander Yang: ????","Young Company Commander Yang quickly chased after her out of the car. Wait! Comrade Xiao Qiao, don't be impulsive!"]},{"number":24,"title":"Chapter 24: Strive for it once more","paragraphs":["Staff Officer Lin found Qin Yuanzheng, who was currently in a meeting with the engineers at the construction site.","Qin Yuanzheng was actually a bit distracted, glancing toward the train station every now and then.","Even though they were at the construction site right now and could not see anything from there.","Several engineers and designers beside him were comparing blueprints and discussing something heatedly. Qin Yuanzheng stood to the side, took out a cigarette, lit it, and smoked in silence.","Seeing this living King of Hell from afar, Staff Officer Lin felt a surge of inexplicable frustration.","Their regiment commander really needed to find a partner and settle down soon, then take a marriage leave and go home for a couple of weeks so that his subordinates could finally catch a break.","He was as energetic as a bull every day, constantly coming over to torment his soldiers!","Qin Yuanzheng was feeling incredibly irritable. As soon as he saw Staff Officer Lin, he frowned. Why are you here?","Staff Officer Lin walked over and lowered his voice. Commander, it is like this. Xiao Yang just came back and said he is taking Comrade Xiao Qiao to the train station. Her train is at ten o'clock. He asked if you want to go and see her off.","Qin Yuanzheng's heart stirred. He put out his cigarette, shoved it into his pocket, looked up at the sky, and remained silent for a long time.","Looking at his expression, Staff Officer Lin knew he was conflicted again.","He sighed and said, Ah, actually, it is fine if you do not see her off. Even though Comrade Xiao Qiao is only eighteen, pretty, and innocent, and was almost kidnapped right after she arrived... but it is fine. I am sure heaven will protect a good person like her during that three-day and four-night train journey.","Qin Yuanzheng was speechless.","Staff Officer Lin continued, Still, I do not know what her family is thinking, daring to put such a young girl on a train to the north all by herself. It is such a long distance; normal parents would never be at ease, right? Since she failed to get married this time, once she goes back, she will probably be married off to just anyone. Sigh, what a pitiful little girl. How will she survive without anyone to protect her?","Qin Yuanzheng remained speechless.","Qin Yuanzheng knitted his brows tightly and said, What era is this? Can parents still force their children into marriage?","However, Qin Yuanzheng suddenly thought of Wang Huiping drugging his wine and intentionally walking into the wrong room in the middle of the night, and he fell silent again.","Come to think of it, this era was actually the easiest time for someone to be forced into things.","Because once a physical relationship occurred, there was no turning back.","Qin Yuanzheng stayed silent, his heart growing increasingly agitated.","Staff Officer Lin immediately followed up, Of course, Comrade Xiao Qiao's parents might not be that unreasonable. However, given Comrade Xiao Qiao's situation, she will probably have to be sent down to the countryside. Sigh, with her petite and fragile figure, and her soft-spoken voice, I really do not know what kind of farm work she could possibly do in the countryside.","Watching Qin Yuanzheng's expression, he pushed further:","I heard that some pretty female educated youths get harassed by local young men after they go to the countryside. These youths either live in dilapidated houses or lodge with villagers. It is entirely possible for someone to climb the wall and sneak into their rooms in the middle of the night. Comrade Xiao Qiao is so beautiful, it is highly likely... Hey, Commander, where are you going? Wait for me!","Before Staff Officer Lin could even finish his sentence, he saw Qin Yuanzheng striding away without looking back.","Staff Officer Lin was about to chase after him when Qin Yuanzheng turned back and glared at him. You stay here and work.","Staff Officer Lin was full of question marks.","Before Staff Officer Lin could say a word, Qin Yuanzheng was already far away.","Unable to run away in time, Staff Officer Lin was grabbed by the chief engineer. Hey, hey, hey, Staff Officer Lin, you came at the perfect time. Let us go over these blueprints. Let us finish checking the work before Commander Qin gets back, and then you can just report to him. We are very busy.","Staff Officer Lin was speechless.","These cunning guys clearly did not want to deal with Commander Qin, which was why they were holding him back!","Qin Yuanzheng rushed back to his office in the mining area, but after being hit by the warm air from the heater, he calmed down again.","Wait, what was he getting so worked up about?","If he went over there and stopped Comrade Xiao Qiao, what would that even mean?","He had no justifiable reason to do so.","Moreover, he had been so fierce to Comrade Xiao Qiao before. After acting like that, how could he face her now?","Qin Yuanzheng stood with his hands on his hips, pacing back and forth in the office.","At that moment, the door to the guard room next door opened, and a guard ran over. Report!","Qin Yuanzheng said, Come in.","The guard opened the door, came in, and said loudly, Commander, there is a phone call for you.","Qin Yuanzheng immediately turned and walked toward the guard room next door. Who is it?","Usually, calls for him came from the headquarters building, so he assumed it was some kind of emergency.","As it turned out, the matter was indeed quite urgent, but the call was not from headquarters.","Young Company Commander Yang spoke urgently over the phone, Commander, you need to come to the First Military Region Hospital right away. Comrade Xiao Qiao has gone crazy. She says she wants to get her tubes tied.","Qin Yuanzheng was speechless.","Qin Yuanzheng thought he had misheard. Get her tubes tied? What the hell was that? It sounded like such an unfamiliar term.","What was more, associating it with Comrade Xiao Qiao made it sound incredibly scary.","Sweat broke out on Qin Yuanzheng's forehead. He said, seemingly calm, Calm down and repeat that.","Young Company Commander Yang paused for a moment and repeated in a very calm tone, Reporting to the Commander, Comrade Xiao Qiao suddenly got out of the car just now and refused to go to the train station. She says she wants to get her tubes tied. Do you think you should come over? I cannot stop her.","Qin Yuanzheng wiped the sweat from his forehead, his voice tightening. Did you not say she was going to the train station? Everything was fine, why does she suddenly want to get her tubes tied?","Young Company Commander Yang felt a bit guilty and stammered, Well, Commander, it is all my fault. On the way, Comrade Xiao Qiao asked me why you rejected her and whether it was because you thought she was too young. I said no... I said it might be because of your infertility issue... Anyway, after hearing that, Comrade Xiao Qiao started making a fuss about getting her tubes tied.","Hearing this, the veins on Qin Yuanzheng's forehead bulged. He gritted his teeth and said, I will deal with you when I get back! Keep a close eye on her. I am heading over right now.","Xiao Yang quickly agreed. After hanging up the phone, he walked out of the director's office, wiped the cold sweat from his forehead, and hurriedly ran down to the first floor, where he found Qiao Lanshu sitting on a hospital chair.","Qiao Lanshu had originally wanted to go straight to a doctor to consult about the tubal ligation, but seeing how nervous Young Company Commander Yang was, she found a chair to sit down and let Xiao Yang call Qin Yuanzheng first.","She actually did not intend to go through with the procedure; she just wanted to test the waters and see if Qin Yuanzheng cared about her.","If she was about to get her tubes tied and Qin Yuanzheng still did not show up, she would completely give up on him.","After returning to Yangcheng, she would go to the countryside if she had to, or marry someone if she had to. She would not think about Qin Yuanzheng anymore.","But if she did not fight for it this one last time, they would be worlds apart in the future, and it would be too late for regrets."]},{"number":25,"title":"Chapter 25: Let's Go Get Our Marriage License","paragraphs":["Young Company Commander Yang stood at the hospital entrance, looking out from time to time. Then, he suddenly ran back quickly, looking pleasantly surprised, and said to Qiao Lanshu, \"Comrade Xiao Qiao, my commander is here!\"","Qiao Lanshu's eyes lit up. She stuffed the train ticket in her hand into her pocket and immediately stood up. \"Really? Where is he?\"","Xiao Yang: \"He's outside the hospital. I guess he'll be right here.\"","Cars could be parked anywhere outside the hospital. After all, in this day and age, not many people could drive, so there was plenty of empty space outside.","Qin Yuanzheng parked the car at the hospital gate, opened the door, and got out.","Qiao Lanshu saw Qin Yuanzheng's figure. She turned around and ran towards the doctor's office. Xiao Yang was stunned and hurried to catch up with her. \"Comrade Xiao Qiao, you don't still want to go get a tubal ligation, do you?\"","No, this wasn't what they agreed upon!","Didn't they agree that if he called the commander over, she wouldn't get the ligation?","This little southern girl was really reckless, actually thinking of coming to get a ligation.","What normal unmarried young girl would think of getting a ligation?","Before Xiao Yang could catch up, he felt a gust of wind beside him. A tall figure rushed past him and then scooped up Comrade Xiao Qiao, who was bundled up like a dumpling, throwing her over his shoulder.","Xiao Yang: \"...\"","Xiao Yang was dumbfounded. As expected of their commander, he really had guts!","Qiao Lanshu was also startled. Did Qin Yuanzheng just hoist her over his shoulder?","What, what was going on? Had Commander Qin been angered by her to the point of losing his mind?","Although Qiao Lanshu looked well-behaved, she was very bold when doing things. However, when facing Qin Yuanzheng, she became a bit cowardly.","There was no helping it; Commander Qin was indeed a bit scary.","Qin Yuanzheng hadn't even had time to put on his overcoat. He was only wearing his military jacket, the buttons at his collar unfastened, and his forehead was covered in sweat.","He carried Qiao Lanshu directly, dumped her into the back seat of his car, and slammed the door shut.","Immediately after, he opened the door on the other side and sat down next to Qiao Lanshu.","Inside the narrow cabin, as soon as he entered, it instantly felt much more cramped.","He was tall with long legs and a sturdy build. Even sitting in the car, his head almost touched the roof.","It made Comrade Xiao Qiao look like a little dwarf in comparison.","Qiao Lanshu was getting a little nervous now. She didn't know where she got the courage to provoke such a fierce god.","She smiled at him ingratiatingly and said, \"Commander Qin, you, you're here?\"","As she spoke, she shifted to the side with a guilty conscience, reaching up to tug at the red scarf wrapped around her neck.","Qin Yuanzheng had a dark face, staring at her with a serious expression. Even though seeing Comrade Xiao Qiao's big dark eyes and her fair, cute little face would soften even the coldest and hardest of hearts.","But on his face, he still maintained a cold and stern look. He looked at Qiao Lanshu and asked in a low voice, \"Now you know to be scared?\"","Qiao Lanshu: \"...\"","Qin Yuanzheng: \"Why weren't you scared just now when you were making a fuss about getting a ligation?\"","Qiao Lanshu shrank her neck, hiding half of her small face in the red scarf, only using those big dark eyes to look at Qin Yuanzheng.","She looked at Qin Yuanzheng eagerly, not daring to speak at this moment. Her cowardly appearance was truly both infuriating and amusing.","Qin Yuanzheng looked at her and said, \"Don't shrink back. Speak.\"","Qiao Lanshu twisted the corner of her clothes, making eye contact with Qin Yuanzheng. Looking at his handsome, rugged features, her face flushed red, and she whispered, \"Say, say what?\"","The little girl's voice was soft and sweet, and she was even acting shy.","Qin Yuanzheng: \"...\"","Qin Yuanzheng's voice couldn't stay cold and hard anymore. He softened his tone and said, \"You're an unmarried young girl, why do you want to get a ligation?\"","Qiao Lanshu looked at him with a blushing face: \"You're asking when you already know the answer.\"","Qin Yuanzheng: \"...\"","Qiao Lanshu said recklessly, \"Of course it's because I want to date you. I heard you have infertility and don't want to get married because of it. So I decided to get a ligation too, so I won't be able to marry anyone else in the future either. We'll both be infertile, wouldn't we be a perfect match?\"","Anyway, in her previous life, Qin Yuanzheng probably only pursued her because he heard her body was ruined and she couldn't have children.","What love at first sight, he must have been lying to her!","Qin Yuanzheng: \"...\"","Qin Yuanzheng said with a dark face, \"Nonsense! You're an eighteen-year-old girl, what are you doing messing around with a ligation? This is a lifelong matter. If you regret it later, you won't even have a place to cry!\"","How could Qiao Lanshu regret it?","Being able to marry Qin Yuanzheng was her blessing in both her past and present lives. Even if she had to do it all over again ten times, she would still want to marry him.","She lowered her head and said in a muffled voice, \"Not having children isn't a big deal. I don't like kids anyway. I just want to date you, it's not a crime. Why are you being so fierce?\"","Qin Yuanzheng: \"...\"","Hearing her say this, Qin Yuanzheng immediately felt a bit angry again. He sat there, sulking for a good while, before apologizing in a low voice, \"I'm sorry, I didn't mean to be fierce with you.\"","He didn't want to be fierce with her either, but seeing her act so impulsively, he couldn't help himself!","The little girl was still inexperienced in the ways of the world and didn't know better. How could she be without someone looking after her?","Qin Yuanzheng was having an internal struggle, his face looking solemn.","Qiao Lanshu looked at his expression, not knowing why Qin Yuanzheng disdained her so much.","Clearly, in her previous life, he loved her to death, demanding her day and night, and would hug her and stick to her the moment they met.","Why was the Qin Yuanzheng who was a dozen years younger so cold to her and not easy to approach at all?","Her nose tingled, and with red eyes, she said, \"I don't mean to force you. This kind of thing is supposed to be mutual. If you don't like me, I won't pester you. The fact that you could come today already makes me very happy.\"","As she spoke, she took the train ticket out of her pocket again, smoothed out the wrinkles on it, and tentatively asked in a low voice, \"The train is leaving soon. Could I trouble you to take me to the train station?\"","Anyway, once she returned to Yangcheng, the two of them would never have to see each other again for the rest of their lives.","That was fine. No one would ever know she had such an embarrassing past.","Qin Yuanzheng turned his head, looked at the train ticket in her hand, and suddenly said, \"After all this, you still want to go back? Go back for what? To just find some random man to marry?\"","He said viciously, \"Don't even think about it!\"","As he spoke, he suddenly reached over, snatched the train ticket from Qiao Lanshu's hand, tore it into pieces, and tossed them out the window. A gust of wind blew, and they were gone.","Qiao Lanshu: \"...\"","Qiao Lanshu was completely stunned. She looked at Qin Yuanzheng in astonishment. As expected of her Brother Zheng, he truly had guts!","His movements just now when tearing up the train ticket were so handsome.","Qin Yuanzheng stared at her and said, \"You brought this upon yourself. Don't regret it later.\"","With that, Qin Yuanzheng opened the car door and walked around to the driver's seat.","Qiao Lanshu asked blankly, \"Commander Qin, where are we going now?\"","Qin Yuanzheng started the car and said, \"To get our marriage certificate!\"","Qiao Lanshu: \"...\""]},{"number":26,"title":"Chapter 26: Just a hug, what's there to be nervous about","paragraphs":["Qiao Lanshu was completely stunned by Qin Yuanzheng's efficiency.","Just a moment ago, she had been feeling sad about Qin Yuanzheng rejecting her.","Now, Qin Yuanzheng had suddenly torn up her train ticket and declared that they were going to get their marriage certificate.","Things were developing so fast, completely exceeding her expectations.","Sitting in the back seat, Qiao Lanshu didn't dare to move or make a sound.","On the surface, she looked quite nervous, as if she had been frightened, but in reality, she was absolutely thrilled inside.","She just knew it. Qin Yuanzheng had been so good to her, arranging for people to take care of her, buying her a scarf, and so on. It was impossible for him not to have any feelings for her.","She couldn't help but steal glances at Qin Yuanzheng from time to time, and the more she looked, the more handsome she found him.","She really had a great eye for men.","Since Qin Yuanzheng had made up his mind to get a marriage certificate with her, his efficiency in getting things done was incredibly fast.","He drove the car straight to the building of his dormitory.","Opening the car door, he looked at Qiao Lanshu. \"I have to go write the marriage application. It will take at least two days for it to be approved. For these two days, you can stay at my place.\"","He could just sleep in his office.","Qiao Lanshu's heart was pounding. She stepped out of the car in a daze and followed Qin Yuanzheng, still in a trance, to his one-bedroom dormitory.","Standing in the room, she still hadn't quite processed everything. Her eyes followed Qin Yuanzheng around, watching him eagerly.","Upon entering the room, Qin Yuanzheng first closed the window to prevent the cold wind from blowing on Qiao Lanshu.","Then, he quickly took his own ceramic water cup, washed it clean, and poured a cup of hot water.","He placed the hot water on the table and turned around, only to see Qiao Lanshu still standing at the door in a daze, too restrained and embarrassed to come inside.","He found it somewhat amusing. Just a moment ago in the car, listening to the things she said, she had been incredibly bold.","But now, she was acting like a turtle hiding in its shell?","As soon as Qin Yuanzheng had entered the room, he had taken off his coat, leaving only his inner shirt. When washing the cup, he had rolled up his sleeves, revealing his thick, sturdy arms.","The muscles on his arms were robust, with prominent veins and smooth muscle lines. He looked incredibly strong, as if a single punch from him could kill a man.","At this moment, he walked toward Qiao Lanshu. Qiao Lanshu looked at his arms, then at his solid chest muscles, and then at his ruggedly handsome face. Her entire face turned bright red.","She lowered her head shyly, her heart racing.","Qin Yuanzheng walked over, looked down at her flushed little face, and said, \"I thought you were so brave. What, now you know how to be scared?\"","Qiao Lanshu raised her head, revealing her fair and clean little face. She said, \"I'm not scared.\"","She was just a little shy, that was all.","Besides, in her previous life, Qin Yuanzheng had saved her three times.","What was there to be afraid of with a soldier like him?","She couldn't even love him enough.","Looking at her soft little face, Qin Yuanzheng tried to hold back, but he couldn't resist. He reached out and gently pinched her cheek.","The little girl's skin was smooth and soft, just like pinching a ball of dough.","He said in a low voice, \"Marriage is a lifelong matter. Have you thought it through clearly? You won't regret it later?\"","He paused for a moment and added, \"I previously thought you were young and naive, and I was afraid you would regret it, which is why I rejected you. Now, I'm asking you one more time. Are you sure you won't regret it?\"","Qiao Lanshu nodded. \"I won't regret it. Why would I regret it? Do you hit women?\"","Qin Yuanzheng was speechless.","Qin Yuanzheng's face darkened slightly, and he asked her in return, \"Has someone hit you? Did that Sun Mingyong hit you?\"","It seemed his sentence was still too light!","Qiao Lanshu quickly said, \"No, I was just asking casually.\"","Qin Yuanzheng gently rubbed her hair. \"I don't hit women, and it's even more impossible for me to hit my...\"","He paused, speaking somewhat awkwardly, \"My wife.\"","The word \"wife\" coming out of his mouth felt truly magical.","A wife. He was actually going to marry a wife?","Why did it feel like a dream?","Just then, a faint fragrance wafted over, and someone came and hugged him.","He looked down and saw Qiao Lanshu leaning into his embrace, blushing as she said, \"I don't regret it. I just like you...\"","Qin Yuanzheng froze.","His entire body stiffened for a moment before he quickly reached out, pushed Qiao Lanshu away, and said with a stern face, \"Nonsense.\"","Qiao Lanshu was speechless.","Qin Yuanzheng looked at her with a serious face and said, \"We haven't gotten our marriage certificate yet. Right now, we are just in a normal comrade relationship. What does it look like to be hugging each other?\"","Qiao Lanshu was full of question marks.","Qiao Lanshu watched as Qin Yuanzheng, whose ears were completely red and who didn't even dare to make eye contact with her, said, \"I'm going to write the marriage application right now. You stay at home and try not to go out.\"","He hastily threw on his coat and emphasized one more thing, \"You are not allowed to run to the hospital again!\"","Watching his flustered retreating figure, Qiao Lanshu pursed her lips and giggled secretly.","Commander Qin was really cute. She truly had great taste!","However, she couldn't even hug him. Why was Commander Qin so serious?","...","After leaving the dormitory, Qin Yuanzheng was still worried.","Now that he considered Qiao Lanshu as his wife, he kept an even closer eye on her.","Young Company Commander Yang hadn't followed them, so he found two guards in the dormitory building and had them stand watch outside his door. Whatever requests Qiao Lanshu had, he told them to try their best to fulfill them.","If she wanted to go out, they had to follow her. In short, they had to prevent her from going to the hospital.","After arranging this matter, he hurried to the mining area office. Staff Officer Lin had already returned and happened to run into Qin Yuanzheng.","Staff Officer Lin looked left and right, but didn't see Comrade Xiao Qiao. His heart skipped a beat, and he looked at Qin Yuanzheng with exasperation, asking, \"Commander, you're back from the train station? Did you really send Comrade Xiao Qiao away?\"","Staff Officer Lin was so angry. He pointed at Qin Yuanzheng and said, \"Commander, you're going to regret this later!\"","Qin Yuanzheng was in a good mood now, so he wasn't angry at Staff Officer Lin pointing at him.","He walked over with a radiant face, looked at Staff Officer Lin, who was covered in dust, and actually said, \"Good job working hard this morning. Keep up the good work this afternoon.\"","Staff Officer Lin was speechless.","Staff Officer Lin looked at the smile on Qin Yuanzheng's face as if he had seen a ghost.","He looked up at the sky. Had the sun risen from the west today?","Their commander had been wearing a dark, gloomy face for the past few days, acting like a living Yama.","Why was he suddenly smiling?","He followed behind Qin Yuanzheng, and the two returned to the mining area management office. Qin Yuanzheng rummaged through his desk and asked Staff Officer Lin, \"Staff Officer Lin, how do you write that marriage application?\"","Staff Officer Lin stumbled, a look of shock on his face. \"M-Marriage application? Commander, who's getting married? Is it Young Yang?\"","Qin Yuanzheng had a smile on his face and said joyfully, \"Unfortunately, Young Yang won't be able to get married this time.\"","He said, \"I'm the one getting married. How do you write a marriage application again? Tell me.\"","Staff Officer Lin was speechless.","Staff Officer Lin suspected that Qin Yuanzheng was deliberately messing with him.","He said with an indignant expression, \"Reporting to the Commander, I've never been married, so I don't know how to write it either!\"","He asked again, \"Commander, so who are you going to marry? Are you really getting married? Does she really not mind your condition?\"","As he spoke, he shot a pointed glance at a certain area of Qin Yuanzheng's body.","Qin Yuanzheng wasn't angry at all; instead, he looked even more delighted. \"I am going to marry Comrade Xiao Qiao. She said she doesn't mind.\"","He fell silent for a moment before adding, \"She is still young, practically a child herself. I will take good care of her.\"","From now on, Comrade Xiao Qiao would be his wife, and he would cherish her like a child. He truly had to look after her well."]},{"number":27,"title":"Chapter 27: Marriage Application","paragraphs":["Qin Yuanzheng was getting married. This news quickly spread throughout the military district.","After all, Qin Yuanzheng had always been a prominent figure in the army.","Originally, he was the most favored son-in-law candidate among the leaders of various departments.","Later, he caused another stir in the military district when he was diagnosed with infertility.","Now, let alone in the army, even in the various factories of Longcheng City, whenever Regiment Commander Qin was mentioned, people would secretly ask, \"Is that the Regiment Commander Qin who is impotent?\"","Now, that impotent Regiment Commander Qin was getting married.","He wrote a marriage application in wild handwriting. Because he was somewhat anxious, he didn't even bother to wait and drove directly to the Construction Engineering Corps Headquarters building to find his superior, Commander Li.","Commander Li had just asked about his marriage a few days ago.","What did Qin Yuanzheng say at that time?","He said he had no plans to get married.","Well, now Qin Yuanzheng, who had no plans to get married, came in person with his marriage application for Commander Li to sign.","Commander Li was naturally happy that Qin Yuanzheng could get married. He said, \"I heard you carried the little girl directly out of the hospital?\"","Qin Yuanzheng: \"...\"","Qin Yuanzheng was completely bewildered: \"How did you know?\"","Commander Li snorted and said, \"You brat, you need to pay attention to your influence. So many people saw it. It wouldn't sound good if rumors spread that the army is forcibly taking civilian women.\"","Qin Yuanzheng: \"...\"","The marriage application wouldn't be approved until tomorrow.","Therefore, the earliest they could get their marriage certificate was tomorrow afternoon.","It wasn't that Qin Yuanzheng was in a rush; it was just that since he had decided to marry the young lady, he wanted to be efficient.","Company Commander Xiao Yang brought Qiao Lanshu's luggage from the hospital back to the guest house, but he couldn't find Qiao Lanshu.","He then took the luggage back to the mining area office.","Staff Officer Lin looked at Xiao Yang and asked, \"Xiao Yang, Comrade Xiao Qiao is going to get a marriage certificate with our regiment commander. Did you know about this?\"","Xiao Yang looked completely bewildered: \"Ah? Is it that sudden? I didn't know.\"","Staff Officer Lin shook his head and sighed: \"What a good girl Comrade Xiao Qiao is. Our regiment commander really got a bargain.\"","Xiao Yang deeply agreed. Who could say otherwise?","Their regiment commander was so fierce, who knew if Xiao Qiao could handle it?","...","By the time Qin Yuanzheng came out of the headquarters building, it was already getting late.","Today, he not only submitted his marriage application but also handed in a housing application.","He was getting married, so he couldn't let Comrade Xiao Qiao suffer any grievances.","He applied for a two-bedroom apartment with a living room in the military compound, and then found people to exchange for some industrial coupons and a bicycle coupon.","He had to get all the essentials ready, like a bicycle, a sewing machine, a watch, and a radio.","He also needed to have a new cotton quilt made, as well as a new padded cotton jacket for the young lady.","He listed everything he could think of first, running around all afternoon, exchanging for the coupons he lacked.","When he was about done, he prepared to get off work.","The thought of having Comrade Xiao Qiao waiting for him at home instantly warmed his heart.","He drove to the supply and marketing cooperative and bought half a catty of pork, a catty of flour, along with potatoes, sweet potatoes, and Chinese cabbage.","When he lived alone, he had nothing at home. He ate all three meals at the canteen and never cooked for himself.","Because of this, he had saved a lot of money. When the time came, he would hand all his money over to Comrade Xiao Qiao and let her manage the household.","Qin Yuanzheng took out his accumulated food and grocery coupons, bought a catty of fruit candies, two catties of biscuits, and some melon seeds and peanuts.","The young lady was still quite young; she probably liked eating these things, so he bought them as snacks for her.","Carrying these items, he returned to his dormitory.","Qiao Lanshu spent the entire day in Qin Yuanzheng's dormitory.","His dormitory was a small one-bedroom apartment with a living room. It wasn't spacious, but because there were few things, it looked quite empty.","In the small living room, there was only a wooden bench with a backrest, a round table, and two stools.","In the bedroom, there was a standard military double-tier iron bunk bed. The top bunk neatly held Qin Yuanzheng's daily necessities.","The quilt on the bottom bunk was also neatly folded, looking like a square block.","Qiao Lanshu walked around the room twice. The place was clean and deserted, with fewer things than she had during her few days at the guest house.","But this was Qin Yuanzheng's place. Since he brought her back here, it meant he truly wanted to marry her.","Qiao Lanshu felt happy in her heart. She sat on the bench in the living room, held Qin Yuanzheng's cup, drank half a cup of water, and then leaned back to rest.","At noon, a guard came over to deliver food to her, using Qin Yuanzheng's lunchbox.","The lunchbox contained stewed potatoes with vermicelli and a coarse grain steamed bun.","She ate it all, washed the lunchbox clean, and leaned back on the chair to take a nap.","She wasn't going to go out. What if she went out and Qin Yuanzheng regretted it and went back on his word?","She was going to stay right here; it would be best if everyone knew about it.","Just as the sky was getting dark, Qin Yuanzheng returned.","Carrying many things in his hands, the moment he returned, he asked the guard stationed outside, \"Did Comrade Xiao Qiao go out today?\"","The guard replied, \"Reporting to the Regiment Commander, no. I delivered lunch to her at noon and asked if she needed anything; she said no. I asked if she wanted to go out, and she said she wouldn't.\"","Qin Yuanzheng thought to himself, Comrade Xiao Qiao was so obedient. He told her not to go out, and she really didn't?","Such an obedient young lady—indeed, he wouldn't feel at ease leaving her with anyone else.","It was best to tie her to his side and look after her himself.","Qin Yuanzheng took out his key, opened the door, and went in.","The room was dark. He turned on the light and immediately saw Qiao Lanshu lying on her side on the bench, sleeping with her eyes closed.","Because she had been fiercely rejected by Qin Yuanzheng a few days ago, Qiao Lanshu hadn't slept well for three consecutive days.","Today, her emotions had calmed down, and she slept on the chair all day.","Woken up by the noise, she groggily opened her eyes.","Afraid that the light would make her uncomfortable, Qin Yuanzheng turned it back off.","He placed his things on the table, walked over to Qiao Lanshu, crouched down to look at her, and asked in a low voice, \"Why are you sleeping here? Isn't there a bed in the room?\"","Comrade Xiao Qiao had just woken up. She yawned with sleepy eyes, sat up, and looked at Qin Yuanzheng crouching in front of her in the dim light. Belatedly, she began to blush.","Qiao Lanshu said a bit shyly, \"That's your bed. Can I sleep on it?\"","Thinking about Comrade Xiao Qiao sleeping on his bed, wrapped in a quilt filled with his scent, Qin Yuanzheng's heart surged with heat.","He looked at Qiao Lanshu with dark eyes and said, \"We are about to get our marriage certificate. Of course you can sleep in my bed.\"","He paused for a moment, then added, \"Comrade Xiao Qiao, you know what marriage means, right?\"","Qiao Lanshu looked at him: \"I know.\"","\"You know?\" Qin Yuanzheng demanded. \"You know, and yet you still ask such a question? Once we get married, we will be lawful husband and wife. Not only are you allowed to sleep in my bed, but you will be sleeping in it for the rest of your life, understand?\"","He looked down at Qiao Lanshu's delicate face, his voice low, yet carrying a cold, unyielding dominance. \"I have already submitted the marriage application with your identification details on it. Comrade Qiao Lanshu, you no longer have any room to back out now.\""]},{"number":28,"title":"Chapter 28: Commander Qin, you are truly amazing","paragraphs":["Hearing Qin Yuanzheng say this, Qiao Lanshu felt a bit shy, but she was still happy in her heart.","How should she put it? Their current state was that both sides were afraid the other would run away.","So they had to quickly grab hold of each other and get their marriage certificate as soon as possible; that was better than anything else.","Qin Yuanzheng turned on the light and asked her, \"What do you want to eat? Noodles or steamed buns?\"","Qiao Lanshu followed behind him like a newlywed bride, saying shyly, \"Is there no rice? I want to eat rice.\"","When she was in Yangcheng before, although her stepmother disliked her and hoped to kick her out of the house every day, her stepmother didn't dare to mistreat her when it came to food, clothing, housing, and transportation.","After all, she was a people's teacher, and she was afraid of a stain on her reputation.","Therefore, Qiao Lanshu had rice to eat every day, and she rarely went hungry.","But after coming here, she hadn't eaten rice for several days.","Although noodles were delicious, she still wanted to eat rice!","Qin Yuanzheng carried the flour and vegetables into the kitchen. Hearing her say this, he paused for a moment, considered it for a few seconds, and then said, \"It's too late today. Let's eat steamed buns tonight. I'll go to the supply and marketing cooperative tomorrow to take a look; they should have Northeast rice.\"","Workers nowadays had a monthly grain quota.","For an ordinary female worker, if calculated in white flour, it was about three catties of white flour a month.","Of course, this was definitely not enough to eat, so many people were reluctant to exchange for white flour. After all, exchanging it for coarse grains or red flour meant they could get a few more catties.","As for pure white rice, it was even scarcer. It wasn't that the people here didn't eat it.","Rather, because of the local climate and geographical conditions, this area mainly grew drought-resistant and high-yield grain crops.","Such as wheat, corn, sorghum, millet, and so on.","Therefore, the food in the factory canteen here was mostly made of these: millet and sweet potato porridge, cornmeal steamed bread, and in difficult times, there were even hard-to-swallow wire noodles made from sorghum dregs.","Rice was only planted in local areas rich in spring water.","However, the area and yield were very limited, making it impossible to supply in large quantities, so it couldn't be bought at the supply and marketing cooperative.","However, Qin Yuanzheng was a commander. He could use his status to buy some, and he could also go to the supply and marketing cooperative to ask when Northeast rice would be available for sale.","If that didn't work, he would find a comrade-in-arms in Shanghai and ask them to help mail some.","Since he married Qiao Lanshu, he was going to treat her like a treasure. It was just rice; he definitely had to let her eat her fill.","As he kneaded the dough, he said to Qiao Lanshu, \"Don't worry, I'll go buy rice for you tomorrow.\"","Qiao Lanshu blushed and nodded, \"Thank you.\"","Qin Yuanzheng rolled his sleeves up high. While kneading the dough, he stared at her flushed little face and said, \"We will be husband and wife from now on, you don't need to be so polite.\"","Qiao Lanshu blushed and nodded. She just looked at Qin Yuanzheng, who was wearing a tank top and standing there kneading dough, and felt that he was very attractive.","Qin Yuanzheng's muscles were strong and beautiful. He was tall with broad shoulders. As he forcefully kneaded the dough while staring at her with those deep eyes and talking to her, she really couldn't handle it.","Qiao Lanshu stood there and asked him, \"What dishes are we making tonight? Let me help.\"","Qin Yuanzheng didn't actually need her help, but he wanted to spend a little more time with Qiao Lanshu and chat with her.","After all, the two were about to get their marriage certificate and get married, but they still didn't know each other very well.","So, Qin Yuanzheng said, \"You can peel the potatoes, just peeling two will be fine.\"","Qiao Lanshu took the potatoes, washed them clean in the sink, and then seriously began to peel them.","Qiao Lanshu also did chores at home and often had to help with cooking, so she worked nimbly.","Qin Yuanzheng quickly finished kneading the dough.","Because the dough still needed to rest, he was afraid Qiao Lanshu couldn't wait and would get hungry, so he prepared a small piece of dough separately to make noodles for her. \"Are you hungry? Have some noodles first?\"","Qiao Lanshu nodded, \"Okay... You even know how to make noodles? You're really amazing.\"","With starry eyes, Qiao Lanshu watched him casually swing his hands, and long, thin noodles appeared.","It was truly magical.","The look in her eyes as she gazed at Qin Yuanzheng was full of absolute admiration.","Qin Yuanzheng: \"...\"","It was just making noodles, yet the little girl looked at him with such eyes. How could he withstand this?","Qin Yuanzheng asked Qiao Lanshu to sit outside. He put the melon seeds, biscuits, and peanuts he had just bought into a plate, placed it on the coffee table, and said to her, \"Go sit down and eat something, I'll cook the noodles for you.\"","Qiao Lanshu looked at the overflowing plate and knew that Qin Yuanzheng had bought these specifically for her. After all, the house had been completely empty before with nothing in it.","She took a biscuit and took a bite, but couldn't resist walking to the kitchen door to watch him cook.","Qin Yuanzheng boiled the meat and potatoes together to make a minced meat and potato soup. Then he scooped up the cooked noodles, put them on a plate, and poured the minced meat and potatoes over them.","The noodles were chewy, and the minced meat and potatoes were hot and fragrant. Smelling this aroma, Qiao Lanshu's stomach began to rumble.","Qin Yuanzheng smiled, glanced at her, and said, \"I'll also stir-fry some vinegar-glazed cabbage, you will definitely love it.\"","Saying this, he went back, chopped the cabbage, stir-fried it with vinegar and garlic, and brought it out. A simple but delicious dinner was ready.","Qin Yuanzheng's cooking skills were quite good. The vinegar-glazed cabbage was stir-fried to be fresh, tender, and crisp, carrying a vinegar fragrance that was very refreshing to eat.","Every single noodle was coated in the minced meat and potato sauce, leaving a lingering savory taste in the mouth. Most importantly, Qin Yuanzheng knew she preferred mild flavors, so he made the dishes light, with just the right amount of saltiness.","Qiao Lanshu took just one bite and was amazed.","This was much more delicious than what she ate in the canteen.","She hadn't had a full meal in days, and now she was finally full. She looked at Qin Yuanzheng and sincerely praised, \"Commander Qin, the food you cook is really delicious, even better than the canteen's.\"","The people here all ate salty food. The climate was already dry, and with the salty food, Qiao Lanshu had done nothing but drink water all day.","Qin Yuanzheng hadn't done much, just cooked a meal, but this little girl praised him from beginning to end.","After eating, he went to wash the bowls, and the little girl started praising him again. \"Commander Qin, you wash the bowls so cleanly. You work so efficiently. From kneading the dough to finishing the meal and washing the bowls, it's only been an hour. You're really amazing.\"","Qin Yuanzheng washed the bowls clean and conveniently mopped the floor, and the little girl said again, \"Commander Qin, you even know how to mop the floor. The floor is mopped so cleanly. You are too amazing.\"","Qin Yuanzheng: \"...\"","Qin Yuanzheng went to boil water and carried the hot water to the washroom for the little girl to freshen up. Sure enough, the little girl dropped another line, \"Commander Qin, you can carry two buckets of water with one hand. How are you so amazing!\"","Qin Yuanzheng couldn't take it anymore. Anyone being followed around and praised for being amazing all night by a little girl wouldn't be able to take it.","He reached out and gently patted Comrade Xiao Qiao on the head. \"Hurry up and wash up while the water is hot,\" he said. \"Once you are done, get to bed and go to sleep.\"","Then, he turned and walked out of the bathroom, heading into the room to make the bed for the girl.","What Qiao Lanshu failed to see was that Commander Qin's ears and neck had turned completely red."]},{"number":29,"title":"Chapter 29: Overnight","paragraphs":["Qin Yuanzheng originally wanted to change all the bedsheets on his bed to a fresh set.","Although these sheets were not dirty, as he basically washed them once a month.","But the young girl might be shy; wouldn't she sleep more comfortably if he changed to fresh sheets?","However, as he was about to change them, he suddenly paused, harboring a secret thought in his heart.","That was, he wanted to see the young girl covered from head to toe in his scent, tainted with his aura... that kind of feeling...","Qin Yuanzheng wiped his face, feeling there was nothing to shy away from. After all, they were about to get their marriage certificate soon.","Thinking of this, Qin Yuanzheng decided not to change them. Instead, he simply laid an extra mattress pad on the bed to make it softer. Comrade Xiao Qiao looked delicate; a softer bed would let her sleep more comfortably.","The heating in the military dormitory was quite decent, keeping the room quite warm. He was only wearing a tank top, yet he still felt incredibly hot.","Nevertheless, he shut the windows tightly and stuffed some cloth strips into the gaps to prevent cold drafts from seeping in.","When Qiao Lanshu was at the guesthouse earlier, there was nowhere to take a shower.","The toilets were communal and required going outside, so she had not bathed for several days.","Although the climate here was very dry and cold, meaning going a few days without a bath was not too uncomfortable, she was not used to it and felt dirty all over.","Therefore, she simply took a hot shower here and washed her hair while she was at it.","Her hair was very long and thick. After washing, her thick hair draped loosely down her back, and she was not in a hurry to dry it.","Given how dry the room was, she figured it would dry quickly anyway.","She came out of the bathroom, her cheeks flushed pink from the steam.","Wearing a thin knit shirt and long pants she had brought from home, she walked into the room and looked around.","She saw Qin Yuanzheng hanging curtains.","She walked over, looked up at him, and asked, Commander Qin, what are you doing?","Qin Yuanzheng had not had curtains before; he just pasted newspapers on the windows to block the light casually.","Now, he felt the room without curtains was a bit cold, so he found a piece of cloth and nailed it above the window.","Standing on a stool, he looked up to nail the cloth in place, then replied, I am hanging up a cloth to block the wind.","As he spoke, he looked down at Qiao Lanshu. He saw her in thin clothes, her waist-length black hair cascading down. Her neat bangs covered her forehead, revealing only her smiling, crescent-shaped eyes and her flushed little face.","So well-behaved, he thought. He stared at Qiao Lanshu for a few seconds, and then the hammer in his hand lost its aim, smashing right onto his own finger.","Qin Yuanzheng: ...","Qin Yuanzheng closed his eyes, enduring the pain without showing it.","He quickly finished nailing the cloth, jumped down from the chair, neatly packed away his tools, and put them in the drawer.","He checked again and found the room had indeed warmed up a bit. He rubbed his nose, too embarrassed to look at Qiao Lanshu again, and said, That should do it. I will go boil some water so you can drink if you get thirsty in the middle of the night. You should get into bed and rest first.","Saying that, he strode out the door.","Qiao Lanshu still wanted to talk to him for a bit, but he ran off so fast.","Qiao Lanshu: ...","Qiao Lanshu thought about it and felt a bit shy. After all, a lone man and a lone woman sharing a room was still a bit nerve-wracking to think about.","It was better to just sleep first and talk about it tomorrow when she woke up.","With this thought, Qiao Lanshu sat on the bed.","The 1.2-meter single bed was made soft and cozy, and the quilt was neatly folded. This was Qin Yuanzheng's bed, and she was actually going to sleep in it.","It felt somewhat unbelievable just thinking about it.","She lowered her head, stroked the quilt, and chuckled softly for a moment.","The more time they spent together, the more she felt that Qin Yuanzheng was truly a good person.","Not only did he have good character and know how to take care of people, but he could also cook, and his cooking was delicious and perfectly suited her taste!","This man was so wonderful; how could God bear to let his line end?","Qiao Lanshu thought with some regret. She was actually very willing to bear him a child.","At this moment, Qin Yuanzheng, who had already left, suddenly returned.","He knocked on the door, then came in holding a new towel. He said, Dry your hair, and wait until it is dry before you sleep.","Qiao Lanshu took the towel with a blushing face, then looked at Qin Yuanzheng and asked, Commander Qin, where, where are you sleeping tonight?","Qin Yuanzheng: ...","Qin Yuanzheng was also a bit embarrassed. He barely even dared to look at Qiao Lanshu.","He said, I will sleep in the living room.","Saying that, he quickly turned and went out again.","Qiao Lanshu: ...","Qiao Lanshu could not understand it. Why was this man always in such a rush?","Every time she wanted to exchange a few more words with him, he would just run off in a hurry, completely denying her the chance.","After Qin Yuanzheng went out, he brought over a boiled kettle of water and placed it on the bedside cabinet. He also brought a glass, poured a cup of hot water to let it cool, and without saying much, he truly left the room this time.","He closed the door and then went to the bathroom to take a cold shower.","He had been feeling quite hot these past few days anyway, and now that he was spending time with Comrade Xiao Qiao, his body felt even hotter.","He suspected that the effects of the drug Wang Huiping had given him earlier had not worn off yet.","Otherwise, how could he be feeling more and more uncomfortable as the day went on?","Qin Yuanzheng took a cold shower, washing his overheated body until it emanated a chill. Then he came out of the bathroom, wearing an army green tank top and black cargo pants. With wet water droplets still clinging to his hair, he lay down directly on the wooden bench in the living room just like that.","He would make Comrade Xiao Qiao dry her hair before sleeping, but he was not very particular about himself. Anyway, he had a buzz cut, and a casual rub with his hands was enough to dry it.","As he lay on the bench, thinking of the young girl lying in his room, on his bed, his heart felt incredibly fiery.","This young girl was his wife, and he was finally going to have a wife.","What was it like to have a wife?","He had to prepare a house first. The house in the military compound should be approved, as it had already been prepared for him; he just had not gone to pick up the keys yet.","The house had basic furniture, including a heated brick bed, tables, chairs, and benches. He just needed to buy pots, pans, and bowls.","The young girl was from the south, so he needed to buy and stock up on some rice.","And he needed to buy the Three Turns and One Sound like a bicycle, sewing machine, watch, and radio, but what else did he need to buy?","He thought carefully in his heart. In the middle of the night, unable to sleep, he quietly got up, opened the bedroom door, and went in to take a look.","Comrade Xiao Qiao had already fallen asleep wrapped in the quilt.","Once asleep, Qiao Lanshu looked even more well-behaved.","Qin Yuanzheng tucked the corners of the quilt around her, his heart softening.","Oh right, he had to make her a soft, new cotton quilt.","...","When she woke up the next morning, Qiao Lanshu found that the sun was already out.","She sat on the bed in a daze for a few seconds before realizing where she was.","She suddenly snapped fully awake. How could she have slept until this hour? She wondered if Qin Yuanzheng would despise her for being lazy.","She hurried out of bed, tied her hair back casually, and ran out to take a look.","The house was completely empty; Qin Yuanzheng was nowhere to be found.","Puzzled, she walked into the kitchen and glanced around, only to spot a note resting on the counter. It read: \"There is millet porridge in the pot, remember to eat. I will be back at ten to take you shopping.\"","Qiao Lanshu: \"...\"","Qiao Lanshu stared at the bold, sprawling handwriting on the note for a long time. Then, she carefully tucked it into her pocket and went off to brush her teeth, beaming with joy."]},{"number":30,"title":"Chapter 30: Viewing the Wedding House","paragraphs":["Qin Yuanzheng went back that morning to retrieve the approval forms for his marriage application and housing allocation.","Because he was pushing for it so urgently, and since it was no easy feat for him to finally get married, everyone paid close attention to the matter.","His related procedures went through incredibly fast because everyone in the entire military base, from Commander Li down to the guards, was terrified that his wife might run away.","If Regiment Commander Qin's wife ran away just because the application process was too slow, who could bear that responsibility?","It wasn't like they could compensate him with another wife, right?","Who could afford to pay that kind of compensation?","After getting the approved application forms and the keys to their allocated house, Qin Yuanzheng hurriedly rushed back home.","When he arrived, he saw Qiao Lanshu still lying in bed. Thinking she had not yet gotten up, he asked her, Have you not gotten up to eat yet?","Qiao Lanshu looked at Qin Yuanzheng, who was standing tall and straight in his military greatcoat and cap, and her eyes immediately lit up. She sat up right away. I already ate.","She had just been idle with nothing to do. Originally, she wanted to tidy up the house, but the place was already neat and tidy, and the floor had been mopped spotlessly clean, leaving absolutely nothing for her to do.","So, she had simply gone back to bed to catch up on some sleep.","Looking at her, Qin Yuanzheng's voice softened significantly. Put your clothes on and bring your household register. Let's go get our marriage certificate.","Blushing, Qiao Lanshu put on her only thick cotton-padded jacket, wrapped her red scarf around her neck, and followed Qin Yuanzheng out the door.","Qin Yuanzheng glanced at her and said, Since we are going to get our marriage certificate today, we can drop by the supply and marketing cooperative to buy some fabric and have some new clothes made for you.","Over the years, Qin Yuanzheng had only worn military uniforms and had basically never had any new clothes made for himself.","However, at the end of every year, cotton ration tickets were still issued to him. He had saved all those tickets, accumulating quite a substantial amount over time.","Combined with a few more he had exchanged with his comrades, he had just enough to get Qiao Lanshu a brand-new cotton-padded jacket.","The climate here was too cold, and he figured the young girl probably wouldn't be able to withstand it. He needed to make sure her clothes were made thicker.","Qin Yuanzheng drove the car, taking Qiao Lanshu to the registration office at the sub-district administration.","Right at the entrance of the registration office, Wang Huiping happened to be walking by.","Her face was deathly pale, she looked terrible, and she was clutching her stomach with one hand.","She had just undergone a procedure at an illegal back-alley clinic, secretly aborting the child in her womb.","Previously, she had thought about finding a man to marry so she could logically give birth to the child.","Later, believing things might work out with Qin Yuanzheng, she decided to abort the baby, considering that Qin Yuanzheng suffered from infertility.","However, things did not work out with Qin Yuanzheng after all.","Seeing that it would be difficult to get an abortion if she delayed any longer, she went to the underground clinic to take the medicine.","As she came out this time, she happened to see Qin Yuanzheng walking toward the registration office with a tightly bundled-up young girl.","She wondered to herself: Qin Yuanzheng's attitude toward her had been quite decent at first. Why did he end up rejecting her later?","It turned out he had found someone better.","She stared at Qiao Lanshu for quite a while.","Just then, a woman carrying a basket who knew her came out and spotted her. She greeted her warmly, Oh, isn't this Huiping? Why does your face look so awful?","Wang Huiping quickly dropped the hand clutching her stomach, smiled gently, and said, It's my time of the month, so my stomach hurts a bit.","Being a woman herself, the other lady understood and told her, The weather is cold lately, so you still need to make sure you stay warm. Drink some brown sugar water.","As she spoke, she turned her head and noticed Qin Yuanzheng. With his tall, broad, and upright figure dressed in a military uniform, Qin Yuanzheng was incredibly eye-catching no matter where he went.","The woman lowered her voice and whispered to Wang Huiping, Oh my, I heard that the famous Regiment Commander Qin is getting married too. His partner is from the south, over ten years younger than him...","Wang Huiping was speechless.","Wang Huiping was genuinely somewhat surprised. Over ten years younger? How old is that girl?","The woman smiled and said, She seems to be only seventeen or eighteen, a young girl fresh out of school. Oh, this little girl is just naive and doesn't know what's good for a man. That Regiment Commander Qin is all looks and no use. After they get married, they'll just be lying under the covers purely chatting every night... Don't you think?","Wang Huiping was speechless again.","Wang Huiping really didn't know about this. She said in shock, Really? Didn't they say it was just infertility? That aspect... should be quite normal, right?","Otherwise, when Deng Xiaozhen introduced Qin Yuanzheng to her, she would have mentioned it.","Were they lying to her?","So, that night, she had even drugged Qin Yuanzheng, yet he still knocked her out and fled overnight.","Could it be because of this reason?","Because he was impotent?","The depressed mood Wang Huiping had been agonizing over for the past few days suddenly lifted a little.","She knew it. How could any man who took that kind of drug possibly hold back?","It turned out he just couldn't do it.","The two stood there chatting for a good while. The woman even added, That little girl looks quite pretty, just a bit on the shorter side, like a child. As for Regiment Commander Qin, it seems like an old house catching fire.","After a moment, she added another sentence, No, wait, he's a dud. He can't catch fire.","Saying this, she laughed and bid farewell to Wang Huiping. I still have things to do, so I'll be going now. You should go back and rest early too, look at how terrible your complexion is.","Wang Huiping nodded and looked toward the main entrance of the registration office again.","Qin Yuanzheng had long since taken the young girl inside, and now there was nothing to see at the door.","Wang Huiping thought to herself, if Qin Yuanzheng was impotent in that regard, then why was he taking a wife?","Could it be for future promotions?","Or to appease his family?","Did that little girl know he couldn't perform?","If she knew, she probably wouldn't marry him, right?","Wasn't his doing this considered marriage fraud?","...","The process of getting the marriage certificate was very simple, taking not even five minutes.","The clerk registered them, then heavily stamped two seals, and the certificate, looking much like a certificate of merit, was handed over.","Qiao Lanshu held the certificate and looked at it. Her name was right next to Qin Yuanzheng's, and their birth dates were written above.","She gazed at it preciously for a long time; she had finally received this certificate.","She whispered, Is this the marriage certificate? We are officially married now?","Just this thin piece of paper had tied their entire lives together?","How wonderful.","Qin Yuanzheng also took it and glanced at it. Seeing the eleven years and two months age gap between their birthdays, he still felt a stir of emotion.","He was a full eleven years older than his wife.","He put the certificate away safely and said to Qiao Lanshu, Let's go. I bought you a sewing machine, a watch, and a bicycle. I had someone put them in our home in the residential compound. Let's go back and take a look now.","On the way back to the compound, Qin Yuanzheng stopped to buy two pounds of walnut pastries. Walnut pastries were very expensive, but they were rich in oil and sugar, tasting fragrant and sweet. The young girl would definitely love them.","He handed the walnut pastries to Qiao Lanshu and said, Are you hungry? Eat some on the way.","Qiao Lanshu nodded but didn't eat. Instead, she continued to joyfully admire their marriage certificate.","Qin Yuanzheng drove Qiao Lanshu and arrived at the main gate of the military residential compound.","After getting out of the car, Qiao Lanshu held the walnut pastries in her arms while Qin Yuanzheng held the keys. After registering their information at the gate of the compound, the guard opened the main gate, and he led Qiao Lanshu inside.","The compound was very spacious. There were many children running around in the yard, making it look quite lively.","There were ten residential buildings in the compound, each with five floors, and two households on each floor.","This residential area was newly built a few years ago. When the Engineering Construction Corps first arrived, they enclosed this piece of land and then planned and built this neighborhood.","The apartments here were specially built for the military cadres of the Construction Corps.","The military regulations stated that the families of battalion-level cadres could accompany the army, so the resettlement of these officers' families and children had to be taken into account.","Qin Yuanzheng led Qiao Lanshu inside and said, \"The apartments in this neighborhood are connected to heating and running water. I heard it's very warm inside, not cold even in the dead of winter. I specifically asked someone to pick a lower-floor unit with good heating for me. It's in Building 5, Unit 1, on the second floor.\"","Comrade Xiao Qiao had short legs, so climbing stairs would be too tiring for her.","Seeing this neighborhood, Qiao Lanshu felt that she really liked it.","In her past life, she had also lived in this neighborhood. Although it wasn't this exact building, it didn't matter to her because the layout of the apartments here was all the same; living in any unit would be fine.","She had also been frightened by the previous kidnapping incident.","This compound had guards on duty, and strangers couldn't get in. Everyone living inside was a military officer, making it simply the safest place in the city.","She followed Qin Yuanzheng to the second floor of Unit 1 in Building 5. There were only two households on this floor, with their front doors right next to each other.","The neighboring unit was already occupied, and its door was currently closed.","Qin Yuanzheng took out the key, handed it to Qiao Lanshu, and said, \"Here, you open the door.\"","Qiao Lanshu took the key and opened the door.","The apartment wasn't large; it was a small layout with two bedrooms and two living areas.","The kitchen was on the balcony, facing south, with excellent sunlight.","The conditions here were incredibly good. In her old house in Yangcheng City, they still had to use well water.","However, these newly built apartments were already equipped with running water.","She walked back and forth around the house. Since the house had heating, there was no traditional heated brick bed; instead, both rooms had wooden beds.","There were tables, chairs, and stools for dining, but no sofa. The living room only had a 1.2-meter wooden cabinet and nothing else.","However, the sewing machine and bicycle that Qin Yuanzheng had mentioned were placed right there in the living room, and a Shanghai-brand women's mechanical watch was resting on the cabinet.","This was something Qin Yuanzheng had specially asked someone to buy, costing him one hundred and fifty yuan.","He picked up the watch and said to Qiao Lanshu, \"Come here, put the watch on and see how it looks.\"","Qiao Lanshu looked at the bicycle. It was a women's bicycle, which was tens of yuan more expensive than the standard heavy-duty 28-inch men's bicycles.","After all, their production volume was relatively low.","But the 28-inch men's bikes were too tall. She wasn't very tall herself and wouldn't be able to ride one.","This women's model, however, was just right and suited her perfectly.","She stroked it affectionately for a while. Her stepmother had a similar one, and she used to be so envious, but her stepmother never let her ride it. When she was going to school in the past, she had to walk for over forty minutes each way, making the round trip at least an hour and a half.","She had wanted a bicycle too, but her stepmother said young people needed the exercise and refused to buy her one.","So she hadn't dared to bring it up again.","Now that Qin Yuanzheng had bought her one, she still couldn't quite believe it. \"Is this bicycle really for me?\"","As Qin Yuanzheng watched her looking at the bicycle, her eyes sparkling as if gazing at some precious treasure, a smile involuntarily crept into his own eyes.","He nodded. \"Of course. From now on, whatever you want, just tell me, and I'll buy it for you.\"","Saying this, he suddenly walked over and reached out to hold Qiao Lanshu's hand. This was the first time he had ever held his wife's hand.","Qiao Lanshu looked up at him in surprise. He lowered his head, holding her delicate, slender hand. His broad, rough fingers gently rubbed against it, making Qiao Lanshu's face blush bright red.","He took out the watch, gently placed it on Qiao Lanshu's wrist, and said, \"See if the watch fits.\"","Blushing, Qiao Lanshu said, \"You've spent way too much. Why did you buy so many things?\"","She hadn't expected any of this at all. Moreover, if she had known earlier that Qin Yuanzheng was going to buy a sewing machine, she would have stopped him.","Because she didn't know how to make clothes at all...","She had no idea how to use a sewing machine, but since they had one at home now, she figured she would just have to learn.","Although she hadn't managed to learn it in her past life either.","Qin Yuanzheng said in a low voice, \"These are the essential purchases for a marriage: the 'three turning things and one sound', and the '108 legs'. Didn't you know?\"","Qiao Lanshu had roughly heard of this, but she wasn't entirely clear on the details. After all, no one had ever explained these things to her.","When she came here seeking her husband, she hadn't originally thought about all this.","Qin Yuanzheng finished putting the watch on her wrist, then reached out to rub Qiao Lanshu's hair, whispering, \"You really are a silly girl.\"","So easy to fool.","It was a good thing she met him. He would have to keep a close eye on her from now on."]},{"number":31,"title":"Chapter 31: You might find it hard to handle...","paragraphs":["Qin Yuanzheng led Qiao Lanshu out of the house. There is a department store nearby. Let's go check it out tomorrow and buy some daily necessities.","After all, they were getting married, so they definitely needed to properly purchase some things.","Qin Yuanzheng had been a soldier for over ten years. Aside from a portion he sent back home, he had saved most of the money he earned.","He used to think money wasn't of much use, since the military provided room and board.","But now that he had a wife, he felt that their home was lacking in every way and they needed to buy everything.","He wanted to buy everything he saw for Qiao Lanshu, always feeling like he could never dote on her enough.","Coming out of the house, Qiao Lanshu asked, Do you still have to go to work at the base?","Qin Yuanzheng nodded. I applied for a week of marriage leave, but it hasn't been approved yet, so I still have to head over today. Why don't you go back to the military dormitory for now?","There was nothing in this house, and his belongings hadn't been moved over yet either.","However, Young Company Commander Yang had already delivered Qiao Lanshu's belongings here.","Qiao Lanshu replied, There's no need. This place needs cleaning anyway, so I'll just stay here and tidy up a bit. When you get off work tonight, you can bring your things over, and we can stay here tonight, okay?","Looking at Qiao Lanshu's flushed little face, Qin Yuanzheng's heart stirred.","They had already gotten their marriage certificate and were legally husband and wife, so tonight...","He reached out and rubbed Qiao Lanshu's head, saying in a low voice, Alright. Just do some light tidying. Leave the rest for me to do when I get back. I'll come back early.","Standing at the door, Qiao Lanshu nodded shyly.","Looking back at her with every few steps he took, Qin Yuanzheng said, Wait for my return.","Qiao Lanshu waved her hand. Okay.","After Qin Yuanzheng left, Qiao Lanshu went back inside to clean. The house was relatively clean; after all, it was newly built and no one had lived there before.","The house was very new, but it was quite dusty.","She rummaged through her luggage and pulled out a towel she had brought from her hometown, using it directly as a rag.","She wiped down the tables, chairs, stools, windowsills, and everything else inside and out.","The water was so cold that it froze her small hands red.","After finishing the inside, she went to wipe down the front door.","At that moment, the next-door neighbor, who had returned at some unknown time, heard the noise and opened her door. It was a young woman with two braids.","The woman was slightly plump and wore a bright red padded jacket. Seeing Qiao Lanshu, she smiled and asked, Oh my, you must be Regiment Commander Qin's family member, right?","Holding the rag, Qiao Lanshu nodded. Hello, my name is Qiao Lanshu. I am Regiment Commander Qin's...","She paused for a moment before saying, ...family member.","The neighbor smiled and said, Oh, it's Comrade Little Qiao. My name is Huang Erling, the family member of Zhao Jiannong, the Battalion Commander of the Independent Second Battalion at the South Suburb Forestry Farm. Speaking of which, my Jiannong once fought in battles under Regiment Commander Qin. Just yesterday, Jiannong mentioned that we would be neighbors with Regiment Commander Qin from now on. He even asked me to take good care of you, saying you came from the south?","Battalion Commander of the Independent Second Battalion at the South Suburb Forestry Farm—wasn't that the title Sun Mingyong used to deceive her?","She never expected that she would actually become neighbors with Battalion Commander Zhao now. It was such a coincidence.","Qiao Lanshu nodded. My hometown is Yangcheng.","Huang Erling exclaimed, Oh wow, little girl, you've traveled quite far. It's true that fate brings people together from thousands of miles away. This is all destiny!","Qiao Lanshu also felt that perhaps she and Qin Yuanzheng truly shared this destiny.","A blessing spanning two lifetimes, past and present!","Huang Erling stepped out and said, Are you tidying up the house? Do you need any help? I have a mop and broom at my place. Let me come over and help you mop the floor.","Qiao Lanshu happened to not have a mop, so she quickly said, Just lend me the mop, and I can mop the floor myself.","Huang Erling brought over a mop and bucket, directly coming over to help her mop. She said, Oh, looking at you, I can tell you're not very used to doing chores. Let me help you mop. The kids have all gone to school, and I don't have a job, so I'm just idling around anyway.","Hearing this, Qiao Lanshu couldn't help but ask, Do they arrange jobs for military family members?","The house wasn't big, and Huang Erling worked fast, quickly finishing mopping the living room. When Qiao Lanshu tried to take the mop, she wouldn't even let her.","While mopping, Huang Erling said, Well, it's not that they can't arrange it, but you have to wait for an opportunity. Plus, my two girls are in school, so I have to take care of them and cook for them, so I didn't try to fight for one.","As she spoke, she glanced at Qiao Lanshu. Qiao Lanshu looked sweet and pretty, with a gentle and refined temperament, so she asked, How old are you?","Wiping the table, Qiao Lanshu replied, Eighteen.","Huang Erling smiled and said, I also got married at eighteen. My eldest daughter is already ten. Have you been to school?","Qiao Lanshu answered, I have. I just graduated from high school and came to the military base to find my husband.","Huang Erling then told her, I heard that the propaganda department is running literacy classes for the soldiers at the base, and they need to recruit some literacy teachers. Why don't you go and give it a try? Though I'm not sure if there are any open positions left. Oh, right, I also heard the food factory is recruiting temporary workers at the end of the year, so you could ask about that too.","Literacy classes were becoming popular nowadays. Not just in the military, but various factories, departments, and units were all starting literacy classes.","Ordinary people could also attend literacy classes to learn if they wanted to.","However, the literacy teachers in the military were partly dispatched from various schools, and partly recruited from military family members.","Military family members could join the propaganda department as teachers, but they didn't receive a regular salary, only a meager subsidy, and certainly didn't have a formal staff position.","If they wanted to become regular staff members, they would probably have to wait for an opportunity.","Moreover, the requirements were high; one had to have a high school diploma.","As for the temporary workers at the food factory, they received a fixed salary and could eat at the cafeteria.","Qiao Lanshu could well ask about both options.","Listening to Huang Erling, Qiao Lanshu pondered in her heart. After getting married, she still needed to find a job; otherwise, staying at home every day would be quite boring.","In her past life, she worked at the Chengbei Food Factory. In this life, she could also go and ask about it.","After all, Qin Yuanzheng couldn't have children, so she wouldn't have to raise any kids.","After Huang Erling helped her mop the floor, she took the mop and bucket back next door.","Feeling very embarrassed, Qiao Lanshu wrapped five or six walnut pastries that Qin Yuanzheng had bought for her in oil paper and brought them next door. Sister Ling, thank you for your help. These walnut pastries are very fragrant, have a taste.","Huang Erling quickly pushed her hand away, saying, You don't need to be so polite. Your Regiment Commander Qin took care of my Jiannong quite a bit in the past. I'm just returning the favor. We'll be neighbors from now on, so we should get along well and help each other out.","Qiao Lanshu insisted on placing the walnut pastries on their table, telling her, Give them to the children. The kids are still young and growing.","Hearing her say this, Huang Erling accepted the walnut pastries.","She looked at Qiao Lanshu. The girl was truly beautiful and looked very young—only eighteen. Her family wasn't around either, which really made one feel a sense of tender affection for her.","Huang Erling asked her, \"Do you want to go to the department store to pick up a few things? It isn't far from here. It has six floors and sells absolutely everything. You haven't been there yet, have you?\"","As Huang Erling spoke, she added with a suggestive hint, \"That Regiment Commander Qin is so tall and burly, with such a strong physique. With your frail little frame, I'm afraid you won't be able to handle him...\"","Lowering her voice, she continued, \"It is the perfect time to buy some nutritious food so you can nourish your body when you get back. From now on, you really have to build up your strength.\"","Otherwise, with Qiao Lanshu's thin and delicate little body, she would never be able to withstand Yama Qin's vigorous tossing."]},{"number":32,"title":"Chapter 32: Procurement","paragraphs":["Since they were idle anyway, Qiao Lanshu followed Huang Erling to stroll around the department store near the military compound.","Longcheng City wasn't large, but it still had three department stores.","The one Huang Erling brought her to was the closest to the military compound and was a full three stories high.","It sold absolutely everything, from towels and soap to watches and bicycles. You could buy anything, provided you had the ration coupons. Without coupons, having money alone was useless.","When Qiao Lanshu left home, her father had given her not only five hundred yuan and two hundred yuan worth of national grain coupons, but also some non-staple food coupons, cloth coupons, and so on.","After all, when he saw her off at the train station, the original intention was for her to join her husband at the military base.","So these things essentially served as her dowry.","Now, carrying these coupons, she could cut some new cloth to take back and make herself a new outfit.","Since she was getting married, she ought to wear red for good luck and festivity.","Huang Erling led Qiao Lanshu for about ten minutes before they arrived at the department store.","Passing by the fabric counter, Huang Erling asked Qiao Lanshu, Do you want to make new clothes? The plain weave fabric here is forty-five cents, while the corduroy is a bit more expensive at one dollar and fifty cents, but corduroy is warmer. Take a look.","The saleswoman at the fabric counter recognized Huang Erling. Looking at Qiao Lanshu, she asked, Sister Ling, who is this? Your younger sister from your hometown?","Huang Erling laughed, How could my family have such a pretty sister? This is Commander Qin's family member, Comrade Xiao Qiao. She is getting married, so I brought her to buy some cloth.","The saleswoman's eyes instantly widened, and she stared at Qiao Lanshu non-stop.","Qiao Lanshu was speechless.","It was truly bizarre. Why did everyone who heard she was Qin Yuanzheng's family member look at her with that kind of expression?","It made her feel very strange.","The saleswoman asked Huang Erling in astonishment, Sister Ling, how old is this little girl? Does she know that Commander Qin...","Saying this, she quickly shut her mouth and cast a somewhat embarrassed glance at Qiao Lanshu.","She wanted to say, isn't Commander Qin incapable? Does the little girl not know?","But under Huang Erling's glare, she didn't dare to finish. She hurriedly pulled out several bolts of cloth and said, How about you take a look at this? This twill fabric is quite thick and only costs sixty cents, which isn't expensive. Look at this army green one; it can be used to make a military-style uniform. You cannot imagine how sharp it looks when worn.","People nowadays, regardless of gender, all liked to wear military uniforms, so fabric in this color was extremely popular.","Twill was thick, warm, and durable. It could be worn for years without tearing, and with some patching and mending, it could last another three years. One piece of clothing could easily last for ten years.","Qiao Lanshu touched the fabric and also thought it was nice. She said, I will take this one. Sister Ling, if I want to make a set of clothes, how many feet of cloth should I buy?","Qiao Lanshu didn't know how to make clothes and wasn't very clear on this.","Huang Erling looked at her height and said, Seven feet will be more than enough.","When Qiao Lanshu came here, she only brought four sets of clothes she wore in Yangcheng. They were all very thin and couldn't be worn until summer.","Right now, she only had a newly bought padded jacket on her back. She needed to make at least two more sets to have enough to wear.","Coincidentally, her father had given her twenty feet of cloth coupons, so she bought fourteen feet worth. After the saleswoman cut the fabric, Qiao Lanshu went to buy a pair of fleece-lined warm shoes.","Originally, she wanted to buy leather shoes, but even if she bought them, she wouldn't be able to wear them in this weather.","Wearing something warm was much more practical.","She already had vanishing cream for her face, but she still needed some daily necessities.","She had Huang Erling lead her to the daily necessities section, where she bought soap, towels, two washbasins, as well as toothpaste and toothbrushes.","Qiao Lanshu wandered around the department store and, seeing water buckets, bought two of those as well, along with a water dipper and a washbasin stand.","Finally, she went to buy five bowls, five pairs of chopsticks, two stainless steel basins, and five dining plates.","She was very happy while buying these things because she was about to build her own little family. This feeling was very novel.","It also made her look forward to it.","She had bought quite a lot of things, but fortunately, she had Huang Erling to help carry them. Huang Erling then asked, Have you bought a mattress yet?","Their rooms all had beds, so they didn't need to heat a traditional kang.","But the bed was just a simple wooden frame; a mattress still needed to be laid on top of it.","Qiao Lanshu asked, Where can I buy a mattress?","Huang Erling replied, We can look around, but they are not easy to find. After all, these days, everyone heats a kang. You would be better off having two thick sleeping pads made; they are warm too.","Qiao Lanshu nodded, That works too.","Making sleeping pads also required fabric, so they had to go check out the cotton sellers, since pads needed cotton too.","Seeing Qiao Lanshu getting married at such a young age without any family to help her, having to figure out and buy everything herself, Huang Erling felt quite sorry for her.","Qin Yuanzheng's family wasn't around either, so they couldn't help out here.","Fortunately, although Comrade Xiao Qiao was young, she was quick and efficient in her actions and willing to listen to advice. As for Qin Yuanzheng, being older, he knew how to care for people and was very thoughtful. With the two of them as a couple, their future days would definitely get better and better.","Qiao Lanshu and Huang Erling simply couldn't carry any more, so the two of them first carried the things they just bought back to the military compound.","The two guards at the compound gate saw them, and one of them hurried over and said, Which floor do you live on, Sister-in-law? Let me help you carry these over.","Qiao Lanshu felt a bit embarrassed, but Huang Erling seemed used to it. She said, Building Five, Unit One, Second Floor. Thank you, young comrade.","The young guard picked up all the items and walked away briskly, as if flying.","Qiao Lanshu was speechless.","She hadn't even managed to say a single word of thanks.","Huang Erling said with a smile, Truly a strong and robust young man, so full of energy.","Qiao Lanshu smiled, not knowing how to respond to that.","Seeing her shy demeanor, Huang Erling told her, This is the benefit of being a military family member. You get to live in such a safe compound and have guards to help out. When my children were still small, I let them play in the yard by themselves without even needing to watch them. The guards at the gate would keep the doors shut tight to prevent them from going out.","Sometimes, if there were special circumstances at home and no way to take the children to the nursery, they would also ask the guards to help drop them off.","They were very happy to help run errands. After all, they were all comrades-in-arms with revolutionary bonds, and they watched over these children as if they were their own.","By the time the two of them returned to the second floor, they saw the guard had placed the things at the door and was standing there keeping watch.","That guard knew Qiao Lanshu's identity, she was Commander Qin's family member!","Huang Erling said, Young comrade, thank you for your hard work. Come in and have a cup of tea.","The young comrade quickly shook his head, No need, Sister-in-law. I will head back to my post now.","Their guardhouse had two people on duty, and usually, the requirements weren't that strict, so one of them could step out to help run errands and such.","Qiao Lanshu hurried to open the door, went inside, and brought out all the remaining walnut pastries. She shoved them into the guard's hands and said, You work hard standing guard. Take these to fill your stomach.","The guard absolutely refused to accept them, No need, Sister-in-law. We have rules; we cannot accept your things.","In fact, apart from what the military provided, they were not allowed to accept anything from anyone else.","So, the guard turned around and quickly ran away.","Qiao Lanshu: \"...\"","Huang Erling helped her carry the things into the house, looked around, and said, \"The house we live in is very new. Look, the walls are all white, so there is no need to paste newspapers over them. By the way, did you forget to buy a pot today?\"","Qiao Lanshu smiled and said, \"There is no need to buy a pot. Commander Qin has one in his dorm, and he will bring it over.\"","Huang Erling smiled and said, \"That works. I have to go now; the kids are about to finish school. I need to pick them up and buy some groceries on the way. Next time you want to buy groceries and don't know the way, just come find me, and I will take you.\"","Qiao Lanshu gratefully walked her to the door and said, \"Sister Ling, thank you so much for your trouble today.\"","Huang Erling waved her hand. \"No need to be so polite. We are neighbors now. As the saying goes, a distant relative is not as good as a near neighbor. Let's get along well and help each other out.\"","Qiao Lanshu nodded and watched Huang Erling return to the house next door.","She then began to organize the things she had just bought today.","However, she realized that everything she bought today was for daily use; she had forgotten to buy any food.","She figured she would just ask Qin Yuanzheng to buy some when he came back later.","Moreover, she felt troubled looking at the fabric and cotton she had brought back. She didn't know how to make clothes, so she would need to find someone to help her with these materials. She had forgotten to ask Huang Erling just now.","She went next door again and caught Huang Erling right before she left. When she asked her, Huang Erling immediately said, \"Sister, if you trust me, just give the materials to me and I will make them for you. Look at the clothes I am wearing—what do you think? I made them all myself.\"","Huang Erling happened to be unemployed and had a lot of free time. She often took on odd jobs, making clothes and quilts for others to earn some pocket money.","Of course, Qiao Lanshu trusted her. She immediately replied, \"Of course I trust you.\"","As she spoke, she took out a ten-yuan note and pressed it into Huang Erling's hand. \"Sister Ling, I need a padded cotton jacket, a set of everyday clothes, and two thick mattresses. I am not sure if there is enough cotton, so could you take a look for me? If it is not enough, I will go buy more.\"","She had run out of cotton ration coupons, but she could ask Qin Yuanzheng if he had any.","Neither of them had anyone to help prepare their bedding. They needed two mattresses for the bed and two quilts, all of which had to be newly made. After all, Qin Yuanzheng's quilts were single-sized ones issued by the military, which they couldn't use now that they were married.","Huang Erling handed the money back to her and said, \"I don't need this much. Five yuan is enough. Let's move the things to my house first, and I will rush to get the clothes done for you tonight.\"","Huang Erling was a woman of action. She immediately carried the newly bought fabric and cotton to her house next door, accepted five yuan from Qiao Lanshu, and then went out to pick up her children.","...","Meanwhile, Qin Yuanzheng thought that since they were moving today, he probably wouldn't have time to cook for his wife. So, he took two aluminum lunchboxes, got some food from the cafeteria, and then walked out of his office carrying them.","He first returned to his dormitory to gather his clothes and daily necessities, along with a steamer, a wok, a spatula, and other kitchen utensils. He put them all into the car, ready to take them to their new home.","His dormitory was quite empty, as he didn't have many belongings to begin with.","The furniture belonged to the military, so he couldn't take it with him.","He looked around, saw nothing else worth taking, stepped out of the dorm, and locked the door.","As he came out, he saw his cousin Yang Wenyan approaching.","Yang Wenyan was pushing a bicycle and said, \"Yuanzheng, I finally found you. Your sister-in-law made a pork and vegetable stew tonight. Hurry up and come back with me to eat.\"","Qin Yuanzheng used to go to Yang Wenyan's house for dinner from time to time.","But now, he shook his head and said, \"No thanks, Cousin. I have things to do.\"","Yang Wenyan thought he was just unwilling to go. He sighed and said, \"I am really sorry about what happened with Wang Huiping last time. Your sister-in-law and I truly didn't know anything about it. Please don't take it to heart.\"","Qin Yuanzheng nodded. \"I know, Cousin. I got married. I will be busy moving these next two days, and I am hosting a wedding banquet in three days. You should bring my sister-in-law over for dinner then.\"","Yang Wenyan: \"...\"","Yang Wenyan thought he had misheard.","He stared blankly at Qin Yuanzheng. \"Yuanzheng, what did you just say?\"","Got a marriage certificate?","What certificate? With whom?","It couldn't possibly be Wang Huiping, could it?"]},{"number":33,"title":"Chapter 33: Can I Sleep with You","paragraphs":["Qin Yuanzheng had no intention of hiding it from Yang Wenyan either.","After all, getting married was a joyous occasion.","Besides, telling his cousin early on would save him the trouble of trying to set him up on blind dates again.","Yang Wenyan asked him about the marriage in detail, and Qin Yuanzheng carefully recounted everything to him.","Hearing that the young lady was only eighteen this year and from Yangcheng, Yang Wenyan hesitated for a moment before saying, Well, Yuanzheng, you know that people around here rarely marry wives from out of town, right?","Qin Yuanzheng nodded. I know.","In this day and age, marrying a wife from out of town was quite risky.","After all, who wouldn't be homesick? A girl who had lived in the south from birth for over a decade was suddenly marrying into the north, thousands of miles away.","Let alone the dietary habits here, she might not even be able to stand the climate.","Perhaps in three to five years, she wouldn't be able to take it anymore and would run away with the family's money.","By then, the girl would only be in her early twenties and could easily find another family, but wouldn't Qin Yuanzheng be delayed in his own life?","Qin Yuanzheng, however, wasn't afraid of the little lady running away. If she dared to run, let alone a thousand miles, even if they were ten thousand miles apart, he would catch her and bring her back.","She had chosen this marriage herself; she had no room for regret.","Yang Wenyan looked at Qin Yuanzheng's expression and asked, Have you already gotten the marriage certificate?","Qin Yuanzheng nodded. We just got it this morning.","Yang Wenyan was actually quite surprised in his heart.","In the past, when he introduced potential dates to Qin Yuanzheng, they usually couldn't settle on anything even after meeting several times.","But now, he suddenly announced that he was officially married.","It seemed he really liked this young lady.","Yang Wenyan then said, You're finally married, I'm truly happy for you. As your older brother, let me buy you a sewing machine and a bicycle.","Qin Yuanzheng replied, Cousin, you don't need to spend your money. I've already bought all of those.","Yang Wenyan: ...","Yang Wenyan asked, You bought a watch too?","Qin Yuanzheng nodded.","Yang Wenyan fell silent for a moment, wondering just how much Qin Yuanzheng liked the girl to have bought absolutely everything.","So he asked again, What about furniture? Your place doesn't have a sofa, right? Let me buy you a small sofa.","Qin Yuanzheng hesitated for a second and didn't refuse again. He nodded, Alright, thank you, Cousin.","Yang Wenyan asked further, The residential compound you're in must be connected to the mining area's heating system, right? You don't need to build a heated brick bed?","Qin Yuanzheng shook his head. No need, we sleep on a regular bed in the apartment building.","Yang Wenyan also had a bed at home. He said, Mattresses made in the south are better. Over here, we all use thick cotton pads. You probably don't have enough cotton ration coupons, right? I'll go back and get some for you. The young lady is from the south, so she's probably afraid of the cold. Make the cotton pad thicker so it'll be comfortable to sleep on.","Yang Wenyan was like a mother hen, thinking of even this for him.","Qin Yuanzheng had originally planned to make a cotton pad anyway, so hearing Yang Wenyan say this, he didn't refuse.","The two took a detour directly to Yang Wenyan's house. Yang Wenyan went inside and brought out all the cotton ration coupons he had saved up, giving them to Qin Yuanzheng.","He said to Qin Yuanzheng, I saw some really nice fabric sofas selling in the department store before. I'll buy you a two-seater sofa; it'll look great in the living room. Do you like the kind I have at home? How about I buy the same one I use?","The sofa in Yang Wenyan's house was a two-seater, soft and squishy, and indeed very comfortable to sit on.","Qin Yuanzheng hadn't actually thought about buying a sofa, but when Yang Wenyan mentioned it, he figured Comrade Xiao Qiao would probably like it very much.","After all, a delicate girl like her surely wouldn't like those wooden benches.","He nodded and said, Cousin, the one like yours will be perfect.","Yang Wenyan nodded. Alright, I'll have it delivered to you tomorrow.","As he spoke, he reached out and patted Qin Yuanzheng on the shoulder, saying, Since you're married, live your life well. As long as the two of you get along, you can make your days prosperous and happy.","Qin Yuanzheng nodded in agreement. Anxious to get home to see Qiao Lanshu, he didn't stay long.","He stuffed the cotton coupons into his pocket and drove his car back to the gate of the military residential compound.","After parking the car, he carried two lunchboxes in a thermal bag, along with the things he had moved from the military dormitory, and arrived at his front door.","He had given the key to Qiao Lanshu that afternoon and hadn't kept one for himself, so he knocked on the door. It wasn't long before he heard Qiao Lanshu's voice from inside.","Qiao Lanshu, not knowing what she was busy with, called out, Coming!","As soon as he heard her voice, Qin Yuanzheng couldn't help but let the corners of his mouth turn up.","He said, It's me.","Qiao Lanshu hurried to open the door, her eyes sparkling as she looked at him. You're finally back?","She had seen that the sky outside was already dark and had been wondering why he wasn't back yet.","Qin Yuanzheng brought his things inside and looked at her sparkling eyes, asking gently, Was it boring being home alone?","Qiao Lanshu shook her head. No, I went shopping at the department store today. I bought towels, a washbasin, and some other things...","She chattered away, telling him all about going shopping with Huang Erling today, and even showed Qin Yuanzheng the things she had bought.","Qin Yuanzheng took off his coat, hung it on the wall, and praised her, My wife is so capable.","Qiao Lanshu: ...","Hearing him say this, Qiao Lanshu instantly blushed.","He called her his wife.","Qin Yuanzheng looked at her flushed face and thought to himself, We've barely even started.","Blushing from just this?","Qin Yuanzheng said, I brought some food back from the cafeteria. Let's wash our hands and eat.","The two sat at the already wiped-clean dining table and began to eat. Today's meal was noodles paired with hot and sour shredded cabbage. Qiao Lanshu was probably hungry, as she found the food quite tasty.","After dinner, Qin Yuanzheng unrolled the bedding he had brought back from the dorm and made the bed for Qiao Lanshu, letting her sleep by herself while he went to sleep in the next room.","Qiao Lanshu: ...","Lying in bed, Qiao Lanshu tossed and turned. They had already gotten their marriage certificate; why wasn't Commander Qin sleeping with her yet?","Could it be that Qin Yuanzheng wasn't with her because he liked her?","Was it just because he was afraid she would get her tubes tied?","But Brother Zheng in her past life had a massive desire for her. He would pester her several times a day, always seemingly insatiable.","Wearing only a thin long-sleeved top, Qiao Lanshu wrapped herself in the blanket. Her waist-length hair fell loosely around her. She reached out, pinched her hair, gave it a toss, and suddenly mustered the courage to sit up.","She got out of bed, walked to the next room, and knocked politely on the door.","Soon, Qin Yuanzheng opened the door. When he saw Qiao Lanshu, his breath hitched for a second, and he asked in a low voice, Why aren't you sleeping?","Qiao Lanshu looked at him with a blushing face and whispered, It's too cold. I... I can't sleep.","Qin Yuanzheng: ...","Qin Yuanzheng was only wearing a tank top and didn't feel cold at all. The heating in the room was quite adequate.","He stayed silent for a moment before saying, Go back and lie down first. I'll bring my blanket over to you.","Qiao Lanshu stood there without moving and said, Can I... can I sleep with you?"]},{"number":34,"title":"Chapter 34: The Bed Collapsed","paragraphs":["Hearing Qiao Lanshu say this, Qin Yuanzheng swallowed hard.","He actually didn't dare to sleep with Qiao Lanshu because he was afraid he wouldn't be able to control himself.","After all, he was a normal, energetic man. With such a delicate little girl lying next to him, who could hold back?","But he was also worried that Comrade Xiao Qiao's body wouldn't be able to handle it.","Therefore, he was quite conflicted when he lay in the next room.","He wasn't sleepy at all.","Seeing him stay silent, Qiao Lanshu asked a bit sadly, Regiment Commander Qin, haven't we already gotten our marriage certificate? Don't people sleep together after getting their certificate?","Qin Yuanzheng: ...","Qin Yuanzheng stayed silent for a moment before saying, Alright, you go back first. I'll bring the quilt over.","He thought to himself that it was just sleeping together; it didn't mean anything had to happen. The mattresses at home hadn't been made yet, so it was normal for the little girl to feel cold.","He brought two single quilts from the dormitory and spread them out, perfectly covering the double bed.","He pressed down on the bedding and said to Qiao Lanshu, My cousin gave me a few catties of cotton tickets, and I saved some myself. I'll go buy some cotton tomorrow to make mattresses and quilts, and then it will be warm.","When Yang Wenyan and Deng Xiaozhen got married, they had already made bedding, so he had been saving his cotton over the years, reluctant to use it.","Now, he gave all five catties of cotton tickets to Qin Yuanzheng at once.","Qin Yuanzheng had also saved a few catties of cotton tickets, and since he was getting married, he could apply for a material subsidy, which would probably give him an extra catty or two.","After all, this was the north, where the weather was cold, so the supply of cotton tickets was greater than in the south.","He did the math himself; if he exchanged some with his comrades, he estimated they could make one thick mattress, one thin mattress, and two quilts.","Hearing him say this, Qiao Lanshu immediately said, I brought my own cotton tickets. I bought some today to make a padded jacket, and I asked Sister Ling next door to help me make it.","Qin Yuanzheng nodded. I'll give you some more cloth tickets so you can make two more sets of clothes. It's cold here, so don't be reluctant to use the tickets.","Nowadays, tickets were needed for everything. Sometimes, tickets were even more useful than money.","It was only because Qin Yuanzheng was older and had delayed getting married that he had saved up so many tickets. Otherwise, if it were someone else, like Officer Xiao Yang, they might not have had this many cloth tickets.","After Qin Yuanzheng finished making the bed, he said, It's done. Go to sleep early.","With that, he picked up a small oil lamp, lit it, placed it in the room, and then turned off the electric light.","Qiao Lanshu sat on the bed and looked at Qin Yuanzheng in the dim light. Regiment Commander Qin, are you sleeping here too?","Looking at the little girl's eager eyes, Qin Yuanzheng's throat bobbed. He nodded. Yeah, didn't you say you were cold?","Hearing this, Qiao Lanshu felt happy in her heart.","It seemed Qin Yuanzheng didn't dislike her.","She immediately lay down on the bed, pulled up the quilt, and slept perfectly straight.","Qin Yuanzheng paused, glanced at Qiao Lanshu lying on the bed, stayed silent for a moment, and had no choice but to lie down himself.","For a moment, the two of them lay on their respective sides of the bed, the space between them wide enough to plant two acres of land.","Qiao Lanshu turned her head and sneaked a peek at Qin Yuanzheng.","She saw Qin Yuanzheng lying there, his posture as straight as a little poplar tree.","Qiao Lanshu found it really strange. He was lying in bed with his own wife, so how could Qin Yuanzheng be so indifferent?","Could it be that when people said he couldn't have children, they meant he was impotent?","But in her past life, Brother Zheng in his thirties and forties had been very fierce.","As Qiao Lanshu let her thoughts run wild, her face turned red.","She felt she should find a topic of conversation first, so she asked, Regiment Commander Qin, can I find a job in the future?","She had no relatives here, and the competition for jobs was so fierce, so she could only rely on Qin Yuanzheng to find work.","In her past life, she had worked at a food factory. The factory manager was Qin Yuanzheng's cousin, and they had met through Yang Wenyan's introduction.","Hearing her ask this, Qin Yuanzheng turned his head and looked at her in the dim candlelight, asking, You want to work?","Qiao Lanshu nodded. Yes, I have to find something to do.","She didn't want to rely too much on a man. Marrying far away from home, a woman still needed her own job and income.","Qin Yuanzheng fell silent for a while, seeming to think. He said, Finding a job isn't hard, but becoming a regular employee isn't easy. We have a lot of factories here. My cousin is the manager of the North City Food Factory...","As he spoke, he suddenly remembered that Sun Mingyong used to work at the food factory, and Sun Mingyong's father-in-law, Wei Zhengye, was a director at the factory.","He immediately said, Never mind, the food factory won't work. I'll go ask around tomorrow and see if there are any jobs suitable for you.","He felt that Comrade Xiao Qiao was young, soft-spoken, and pure-hearted, so he had to find her a simpler job.","He just didn't know where there were openings.","Qiao Lanshu turned on her side, stared at Qin Yuanzheng in the darkness, and said, If the food factory isn't hiring, I also heard that the propaganda department is looking for teachers for the literacy class. Can I go there?","Qin Yuanzheng raised an eyebrow. You want to do that?","Saying that, he thought about it for a moment. He knew the minister of the propaganda department, so he could ask him to look out for Qiao Lanshu.","However, the people in the literacy classes were all uneducated soldiers. They were military ruffians who spoke and acted rather roughly. Comrade Xiao Qiao was thin-skinned and young; what if someone flirted with her?","Qin Yuanzheng shook his head again and said, No, that won't work. Let me think about it some more.","Qiao Lanshu just looked at him and didn't speak.","Noticing her gaze, Qin Yuanzheng's ears turned red as he said, Go to sleep. It's late.","As if mustering her courage, Qiao Lanshu threw off her quilt and shifted toward Qin Yuanzheng's quilt.","Then, under Qin Yuanzheng's shocked gaze, she slipped into his quilt.","Qin Yuanzheng had a lot of internal heat and felt hot all over. The quilt was just draped casually over him, making it nice and warm inside.","Qiao Lanshu slipped into his quilt, leaned her body against his arm, and looked up at him with a blushing face.","Instantly, all the muscles in Qin Yuanzheng's body tensed up. His muscles became as hard as rock, and he didn't dare move an inch.","His right arm touched a patch of softness. This sensation made his forehead break out in a sweat. He didn't even dare to move his arm, afraid that if he used any force, he might hurt the little girl.","His voice was tight and a bit hoarse as he asked, What are you doing?","Qiao Lanshu looked at him and whispered, Regiment Commander Qin, I'm cold.","Qin Yuanzheng: ...","Qin Yuanzheng said stiffly, Then I'll give you my quilt?","Hearing him say this, Qiao Lanshu suddenly felt a bit aggrieved. She asked, Why did you marry me? Was it because you were afraid I would threaten you with getting a tubal ligation?","Qin Yuanzheng: ...","Qin Yuanzheng frowned, his voice low and gentle. Of course not. No one can threaten me.","As a soldier, how could he be casually threatened by anyone?","If he didn't want to, no one could force him to get married.","Looking at Qiao Lanshu's disappointed expression, his heart softened completely, and he quickly said, \"I... I got the marriage certificate with you because I like you.\"","Qiao Lanshu immediately looked up, her eyes sparkling as she looked at him. \"Really?\"","Immediately after, she added, \"Then, Regiment Commander Qin, can you give me a hug?\"","Qin Yuanzheng: \"...\"","It was just a hug, not like they were going to do anything else, so why was he so nervous?","His heart was pounding, and his palms were sweating.","He didn't refuse Qiao Lanshu. Sliding his right hand through the gap between her waist and the bed, he gave a gentle pull and pressed the petite Qiao Lanshu into his arms.","Although Qiao Lanshu had taken the initiative, at this very moment, with her face pressed against his rock-hard muscles, she didn't dare to make a sound.","She just lay against his chest, her heart thumping, too afraid to speak.","Qin Yuanzheng's whole body was tense. Holding Qiao Lanshu with one arm, he used his other hand to tidy up her messy hair and said in a somewhat hoarse voice, \"Alright, can we sleep now?\"","Qiao Lanshu didn't dare to speak and silently nodded.","Actually, she felt that since they had already gotten their marriage certificate, shouldn't they also do that kind of thing between a husband and wife?","But since Qin Yuanzheng wasn't taking the initiative, she was too embarrassed to bring it up.","How could Qin Yuanzheng endure this so well?","Could it be that he treated her like a child and thus had no desire for her?","Thinking this, Qiao Lanshu reached out and hugged Qin Yuanzheng as well.","As her hand brushed across his body, he instantly shuddered and suddenly grabbed her hand, asking in a hoarse voice, \"What are you doing?\"","With her hand held down by him, Qiao Lanshu blinked and said, \"I want to hug you too.\"","She had made it so obvious; if Qin Yuanzheng still didn't catch on, it would be really awkward!","Qin Yuanzheng looked down at her and said in a low voice, \"Stop messing around!\"","With her hand pinned down but still touching his hard abdominal muscles, she said, \"I'm not messing around. We're husband and wife now, aren't we supposed to be intimate?\"","She was determined to make this man take responsibility.","Her hand stroked the man's abs. Qin Yuanzheng, who was already holding back painfully, let out a muffled groan. He suddenly rolled over and pinned Qiao Lanshu to the bed, but right at that moment, there was a loud \"crack.\"","Qiao Lanshu felt the support beneath her back vanish. She let out a scream and was instantly caught by the quick-witted Qin Yuanzheng.","Then, the two of them crashed onto the floor.","Qin Yuanzheng held her tightly, one hand protecting her head and the other protecting her back. The two lay under the bed frame, staring dumbfounded at the collapsed wooden bed.","Qin Yuanzheng: \"...\"","Qiao Lanshu: \"...\"","Qiao Lanshu looked at Qin Yuanzheng, who said helplessly, \"I didn't use that much force just now, did I?\"","He had only pressed Qiao Lanshu onto the bed. Who knew this bed was so fragile?","When he got into bed earlier, he had heard the wooden bed creaking, as if it wasn't very sturdy. However, his attention had been completely absorbed by Qiao Lanshu at the time, so he hadn't thought much of it.","At this moment, the door next door opened. Huang Erling, still wearing an apron with cotton fuzz clinging to her clothes, had been staying up late making clothes. She suddenly heard a loud \"bang\" from next door, followed by Qiao Lanshu's scream.","She wondered to herself if Qin Yuanzheng had returned yet. After all, her own husband, Zhao Jiannong, hadn't come back.","Worried that something had happened to Qiao Lanshu, she came over and knocked on the door. \"Xiao Qiao, Xiao Qiao? Are you alright? What was that noise just now?\"","Blushing, Qiao Lanshu came out of the room. She grabbed a coat to wrap around herself, opened the door, and said with a bright red face, \"Sister Ling, it's so late, why haven't you slept yet?\"","Huang Erling looked at her flushed face and asked, \"What happened just now? Are you okay?\"","Qiao Lanshu shook her head, her face still red. \"I'm fine... It's just, just that the bed collapsed.\"","Huang Erling: \"...\"","Huang Erling looked a bit surprised. \"The bed collapsed?\"","Just then, she saw Qin Yuanzheng walking out of the room. He was wearing long pants and an olive green tank top. He was tall, heavily muscled, and had a gloomy expression on his face, making him look rather intimidating.","Startled, Huang Erling took two steps back and lowered her voice, \"So your Regiment Commander Qin came back?\"","Qiao Lanshu nodded. \"Yeah.\"","Huang Erling quickly said, \"I'm so sorry, so sorry. I really didn't know you two were busy with things. Oh my, what a fuss. I'll head back now, you guys continue, go ahead and continue.\"","Saying that, she awkwardly hurried back to her own room.","Good heavens, as expected of Regiment Commander Qin who had been abstinent for thirty years, he really is fierce.","Collapsing the bed on the very first night of their marriage, that's really something. Who knows how intense tonight must be!","It's just that with Comrade Xiao Qiao's petite frame, Regiment Commander Qin is twice her size. Who knows if she can handle it?","Huang Erling awkwardly ran back next door, while Qiao Lanshu turned around with a blushing face to look at Qin Yuanzheng.","Qin Yuanzheng walked over and closed the door. Then, he reached out to pull Qiao Lanshu into his arms, rubbed her head, and asked softly, \"Did it scare you?\"","Pausing for a moment, he added, \"Tomorrow I'll find someone to build a new bed.\"","It needs to be sturdy enough!"]},{"number":35,"title":"Chapter 35: Commander Qin is truly full of energy.","paragraphs":["That night, Qiao Lanshu and Qin Yuanzheng went to sleep in the second bedroom.","Fortunately, there was also a bed in the second bedroom. However, before sleeping, Qin Yuanzheng still checked the bed frame. In the middle of the night, he took a hammer and nails and repaired the bed with a clatter of clinking and banging.","Next door, Battalion Commander Zhao Jiannong returned in the middle of the night. Hearing the noise from next door, he went into his house, took off his coat, and hung it on the wall. He saw that his wife was not asleep yet and was in the corner of the living room, making clothes with a click-clack sound from the sewing machine.","He asked in a low voice, Has Regiment Commander Qin moved in next door? What is he doing making all that racket in the middle of the night?","Huang Erling looked up at him from her busy work and asked, Why are you so late today? Have you eaten?","Zhao Jiannong worked at the southern suburbs forestry center. Their troops were stationed there, responsible for managing the labor reform farm and building roads.","Originally, there was only one dirt road from the city to the southern suburbs forestry center. The bus only ran twice a day and stopped operating at six in the evening.","Now, because they needed to transport coal out, a new road was planned from the forestry center, and the construction of that road was also the responsibility of Zhao Jiannong's independent second battalion.","Therefore, Zhao Jiannong was usually quite busy, often leaving early and returning late.","He said to Huang Erling, I ate at the military canteen. We had a big meeting today, so I am a bit late.","It was all because of that Sun Mingyong, who not only impersonated a military officer but specifically impersonated him.","It resulted in him being called in for questioning by Commander Li, and after returning, he had to hold a general meeting for the entire unit.","In short, it was an unprovoked disaster.","He changed his clothes, took a quick shower, and came out. The clattering next door was still going on.","He remarked, Regiment Commander Qin sure has a lot of energy. What time is it, and he is still hammering away.","In the middle of the night, this was too disruptive to people's sleep.","Regiment Commander Qin was not usually this kind of person.","He put down the towel he was using to dry his hair and said to Huang Erling, I will go over and see if he needs any help.","Huang Erling paused her sewing, glared at him, and lowered her voice, What are you going to help with? Come back here.","Zhao Jiannong stopped in his tracks, walked over to look at her, and asked in a low voice, What is going on?","Huang Erling whispered, Regiment Commander Qin moved in with his wife. Tonight, it was probably quite intense... the bed collapsed. I went over to take a look, and the little girl's face was so red... Regiment Commander Qin is probably busy fixing the bed.","Zhao Jiannong: ...","Zhao Jiannong could not help but chuckle and said softly, Our Regiment Commander Qin is no ordinary man. Back when we were in the same squad, he was always first in military exercises. He is well-built and incredibly strong; no one ever wanted to spar with him. With a body like a wild bull, it is no wonder the bed collapsed.","Still, for Regiment Commander Qin to break the bed on his first day of marriage was just too funny.","Zhao Jiannong was about to die laughing.","...","Next door, Qin Yuanzheng finished fixing the bed. He put the tools away, pressed down on the bedboards, and seeing that the bed was now completely sturdy, finally began to make the bed.","After making the bed, it was getting late. Qiao Lanshu was indeed so sleepy she could not keep her eyes open. She finally stopped fussing, lay down obediently, pulled up the covers, closed her eyes, and fell asleep.","Qin Yuanzheng lay beside her, originally wanting to wait for her to take the initiative to snuggle up again.","As a result, not long after the little girl lay down, her breathing became even.","Qin Yuanzheng: ...","Qin Yuanzheng turned on his side and stared at Qiao Lanshu's sleeping face. As he watched, he pulled his wife into his arms.","She was his wife now, he could hug her whenever he wanted!","Holding his fragrant and soft wife, Qin Yuanzheng closed his eyes in satisfaction.","Sure enough, having a wife and not having a wife were vastly different!","Even if holding back was a little uncomfortable.","...","The next day, Qin Yuanzheng took Qiao Lanshu to the department store and bought some more food and daily necessities.","In the afternoon, Yang Wenyan brought some people over to deliver the two-seater sofa.","The sofa was velvet, beige, and about 1.5 meters long, fitting perfectly in the living room.","Yang Wenyan patted the sofa and said to Qiao Lanshu, Come, sister-in-law, see if you like this? If not, we can exchange it. I have already spoken with the department store manager.","Qiao Lanshu walked over, sat on the sofa, and then said, This is very nice, thank you, cousin.","Yang Wenyan looked at Qiao Lanshu, thinking that the little girl looked well-behaved and polite, and spoke with natural grace. No wonder Qin Yuanzheng liked her.","Yang Wenyan then asked Qin Yuanzheng, Are you hosting your wedding banquet tomorrow at the military base or a restaurant?","Qin Yuanzheng: At a restaurant. We will just invite a few close friends for a meal.","As for the military base, he had already paid to have extra dishes added to the canteen's meals.","The military personnel had to work and could not drink, so he also bought candy and distributed two pieces of wedding candy to everyone in his regiment.","Yang Wenyan then asked, Did you tell your parents? Are they coming?","Qin Yuanzheng shook his head, They are not coming. It is too far and unnecessary. When there is a chance in the future, I will take Xiao Qiao back to visit.","Yang Wenyan did not say anything else.","The banquet this time only consisted of two tables. Qin Yuanzheng invited his close comrades, as well as his cousin and cousin-in-law.","However, Deng Xiaozhen's younger brother, Deng Weijun, also came this time. Deng Weijun worked at the food factory and usually lived in the dormitories, so he was fairly well-acquainted with Qin Yuanzheng.","Therefore, when he heard that Qin Yuanzheng had gotten married, he insisted on coming to drink to his happiness no matter what.","The neighbor, Battalion Commander Zhao, also brought Huang Erling.","Both tables were full. Staff Officer Lin and Xiao Yang, as the ones who had been returned, looked at Comrade Xiao Qiao, who was wearing a fitted military uniform with two braids, standing next to Qin Yuanzheng, and felt a twinge of sour jealousy.","Staff Officer Lin said to Xiao Yang, We used to worry about our regiment commander, but looking at it now, he is the luckiest of us all.","Company Commander Xiao Yang nodded, Is that not right? Our regiment commander just has high standards; otherwise, he would not have delayed it until now.","Everyone drank and ate together. Yang Wenyan drank a lot; he was very happy and asked Qin Yuanzheng, who was sitting next to him, Yuanzheng, is my sister-in-law going to work after getting married? Our food factory happens to be hiring temporary workers. She can come and give it a try.","Jobs were hard to find nowadays. Even for temporary positions, everyone fought for them.","Over the past two days, Qiao Lanshu had inquired at the propaganda department, but they already had enough teachers for the literacy classes and had no vacancies.","So now, hearing Yang Wenyan say this, she immediately nodded, Cousin, can I really go? I want to work.","Qin Yuanzheng: ...","Deng Xiaozhen's younger brother, Deng Weijun, quickly said, Sister-in-law, of course you can go. Our food factory needs to hire five or six people this batch. You can definitely go, just let my brother-in-law arrange a light task for you.","Deng Weijun was a talkative guy. He said, Does the route from the mining area back to the military dormitories not pass right by the food factory? You can just have Regiment Commander Qin pick you up from work every day so you will not even have to walk yourself.","Qiao Lanshu's eyes lit up. She turned and looked at Qin Yuanzheng expectantly, Really? Then I will go to the food factory, okay?","Qin Yuanzheng: \"...\"","They had only just gotten married, and their marriage leave wasn't even over yet.","To think that Comrade Xiao Qiao was actually already thinking about going to work?"]},{"number":36,"title":"Chapter 36: Calling him husband is also fine.","paragraphs":["Qiao Lanshu wanted to work at the food factory, and naturally, Qin Yuanzheng couldn't refuse.","The young lady wanted to find a job and go to work every day; this was a good thing.","Otherwise, having no relatives or friends here, staying at home every day wouldn't be good for her.","So, he nodded and said, \"Alright then, Cousin, Weijun, I'll have to trouble you to take good care of my Xiao Qiao.\"","Yang Wenyan waved his hand and said, \"No trouble at all, we're all family, why are you being so polite?\"","However, Deng Xiaozhen's younger brother, Deng Weijun, was startled by Qin Yuanzheng's words.","He was just an ordinary worker. Usually, if he wanted to say even a couple of extra words to Commander Qin, he would be extremely cautious.","Now, for the sake of Comrade Xiao Qiao, Qin Yuanzheng actually used the word \"trouble\" with him. Frightened, he quickly stood up and said somewhat bashfully, \"Commander Qin, don't worry! You can safely leave Comrade Xiao Qiao in my hands. With me around, I definitely won't let anyone bully her.\"","Deng Xiaozhen looked at her somewhat foolish younger brother, simply not knowing what to say.","Qin Yuanzheng, however, held up his wine glass, stood up, toasted Deng Weijun, and said, \"Then thank you very much.\"","Everyone was a bit surprised seeing Qin Yuanzheng act like this. Even Staff Officer Lin and Young Company Commander Yang looked at each other in dismay.","It seemed that this Comrade Xiao Qiao held an unusual place in Commander Qin's heart.","Commander Qin was like an old house catching fire—he was truly smitten.","By the time the meal was over, it was already one o'clock in the afternoon.","Yang Wenyan told Qiao Lanshu to report to the food factory in a couple of days, saying he would help fill out the application form on his end.","Then everyone dispersed and went their separate ways to work.","Seeing that it was still early, Qin Yuanzheng took Qiao Lanshu to buy a bed.","Nowadays, many beds had to be custom-made. Of course, there were also ready-made ones, but there wouldn't be much choice in terms of style.","Qin Yuanzheng and Qiao Lanshu took a look around the furniture section on the first floor of the department store. There weren't many ready-made beds; most were wooden beds that required assembly.","Moreover, the beds weren't large, all being 1.5 meters wide.","Qin Yuanzheng reached out and pressed down on the bed board, his brows furrowing slightly.","Qiao Lanshu felt that the beds here weren't as nice-looking as the ones back in Yangcheng.","The wooden furniture in Yangcheng often featured beautiful, intricate wood carvings, whereas the ones here were much simpler and less complex.","However, the wood quality was still quite good. She looked at two of them and thought they were alright.","Watching Qin Yuanzheng pressing on the bed board with a frown, she asked softly, \"What's wrong? Is this one no good?\"","Qin Yuanzheng asked in a low voice, \"Do you like it?\"","Qiao Lanshu shook her head. \"I wouldn't say I like it, I just think it's okay?\"","Because there wasn't much to choose from here anyway.","Qin Yuanzheng, however, was dissatisfied. He whispered to Qiao Lanshu, \"This bed won't do. It's not sturdy enough.\"","He was strong and physically robust; he was afraid this bed wouldn't be able to withstand rough use.","Qiao Lanshu naturally had no idea about the little thoughts running through his mind.","Anyway, Qin Yuanzheng was very reliable when handling things, so she decided to just listen to him completely.","She said, \"Then let's look around some more.\"","Qin Yuanzheng simply took her hand and led her out of the department store.","He said, \"Forget it, let's just go back and build a kang.\"","There was no bed sturdier than a kang. No matter what they did, they wouldn't have to worry about it making noise, much less collapsing.","However, he certainly couldn't say that to Qiao Lanshu. He coughed, hiding his secret thoughts, and told her, \"The wooden beds here are only 1.5 meters wide, which is too narrow. I'm a big guy, and I'm afraid I'd crowd you. Besides, that bed isn't sturdy; the wooden boards creak and are prone to termites. It's not worth buying.\"","But speaking of building a kang, the rooms in the apartment building didn't have flues, so the kang would just be a place to sleep and couldn't be heated with fire. It wasn't like no one in the courtyard had built a kang; when the time came, he could just build one exactly like the others.","Qiao Lanshu didn't know all this; she just needed to listen to him.","She nodded. \"Okay, I'll listen to you.\"","Wrapped in a red scarf, Qiao Lanshu's exposed nose tip was red from the wind, and she looked at him with bright, dark eyes.","Qin Yuanzheng's heart softened. He couldn't help but reach over and pull Qiao Lanshu's scarf up a bit to cover her nose.","He said softly, \"It's getting dark, let's hurry back.\"","Having married a wife, Qin Yuanzheng finally applied for leave for the first time.","And it was marriage leave, at that.","However, because the recent construction in the mining area and the building of the highway both required Qin Yuanzheng to follow up, his superiors only approved seven days of leave.","They hadn't even done anything yet, and a whole day had already passed.","Qin Yuanzheng drove the car, bringing Qiao Lanshu to the entrance of the Construction Corps Headquarters building.","Qiao Lanshu recognized this place; opposite the headquarters building was the train station.","Looking at the train station across the street, Qiao Lanshu felt a bit emotional.","Qin Yuanzheng told her, \"Wait for me in the car, I'll be down within ten minutes.\"","Qiao Lanshu nodded and didn't ask what he was going up for.","Qin Yuanzheng was here to get grain.","He had bought ten catties of sweet potatoes and ten catties of rice.","These ten catties of rice were produced locally. Due to the climate, the rice yield was extremely scarce.","In the entire Longcheng City, there was only a small area where it was planted. Because that place had a natural spring, spring water was used to cultivate the rice.","Qin Yuanzheng wanted to buy his wife the rice she loved to eat. Not only did he search everywhere for Northeast rice, but he also sent a letter to a comrade in Shanghai, asking him to mail some rice back.","Then, he went straight to his superior, Commander Li, to ask him for rice.","Commander Li was rendered speechless. He pointed at Qin Yuanzheng and said, \"My own monthly rice ration is barely a few catties, I'm not giving it to you.\"","Qin Yuanzheng, with incredibly thick skin, said, \"Didn't you say before that as long as I get married, you'd give me a big gift? Now I've come to ask you for it. I just want rice, nothing else.\"","Commander Li: \"...\"","Commander Li had to concede to his thick skin. He said, \"You can have the rice, but let your little wife come up and let me have a look. I haven't even met her yet.\"","He really wanted to see what kind of heavenly beauty could move a man as hard as stone like Qin Yuanzheng.","Qin Yuanzheng hesitated for two seconds before saying, \"Let's wait a bit longer. Comrade Xiao Qiao is timid, and you might scare her.\"","Commander Li: \"...\"","Commander Li pointed at the door and said, \"Get out!\"","Qin Yuanzheng smoothly got out, then went to the logistics department next door. He collected Commander Li's ten catties of rice and ten catties of sweet potatoes, carrying one bag in each hand, and came out of the headquarters building.","Qiao Lanshu saw him come out, so she raised her arm and checked the new watch on her wrist.","Hmm, it really had taken exactly ten minutes.","Qin Yuanzheng placed the rice and sweet potatoes in the back seat, then opened the car door and got in. Looking at Qiao Lanshu, he asked, \"Did you wait long?\"","Qiao Lanshu shook her head and asked him, \"What did you go get?\"","Qin Yuanzheng started the car and left the headquarters building. He smiled and said, \"I went to get some rice for you.\"","Qiao Lanshu's eyes lit up, and she turned her head to look in the back.","Qin Yuanzheng had actually gone out of his way to buy rice for her. How wonderful.","She wanted to hug him, but since he was driving, she just kept staring at him with bright, sparkling eyes.","Qin Yuanzheng couldn't withstand her gaze, and the tips of his ears slowly turned red.","When the car drove into the military residential compound and he parked downstairs, he finally turned his head, looked at Qiao Lanshu, and asked in a low voice, \"Why do you keep staring at me?\"","Qiao Lanshu smiled shyly and said, \"Commander Qin, you are so good to me.\"","After a brief pause, she asked, \"Can I call you Brother Zheng?\"","Calling him Commander Qin felt rather distant.","Qin Yuanzheng stared at her cherry-red lips for a few seconds before nodding. \"You can,\" he replied in a hoarse voice.","Never mind calling him brother, calling him husband would do just fine."]},{"number":37,"title":"Chapter 37: Even a bed made of wood isn't sturdy enough for your antics.","paragraphs":["It was too cold in the car. Even if Qin Yuanzheng had some romantic thoughts in his heart, he didn't dare to act on them at this moment.","He was afraid the little girl would freeze.","So, the two of them quickly grabbed their things and returned home.","Warmed by the heating in the house, Qiao Lanshu immediately felt her numb legs and feet come back to life.","Qiao Lanshu took off her coat and scarf herself, stood on her tiptoes, and hung her clothes on the wall.","Then, when Qin Yuanzheng put the rice and sweet potatoes in the kitchen and walked to the door to take off his clothes, Qiao Lanshu took the initiative to take his coat and said, Brother Zheng, let me help you.","Qin Yuanzheng: ...","The little girl's Brother Zheng was so sweet and lingering. He didn't know if it was because of his own impure thoughts, but why did he feel his whole body burning up just from her calling him brother?","He took off his overcoat, then his jacket, and immediately after, he took off his shirt, leaving only an undershirt on.","The muscles under the undershirt were bulging, and his two arms were thick and powerful.","He just stood there, watching his petite little wife standing on her tiptoes, trying hard to hang his clothes for him.","His eyes were fixed on Qiao Lanshu, the corners of his mouth slightly turned up. He didn't help, just watched his little wife struggle to hang his clothes properly.","He thought to himself, Comrade Xiao Qiao is really cute. How could her personality be so good? After spending the day together, she had almost no temper at all.","Qiao Lanshu finished hanging the clothes, and when she turned around, she saw Qin Yuanzheng's thick arm reach over and press against the wall behind her.","Qin Yuanzheng leaned in, trapping her there with both arms. His whole body radiated heat, incredibly hot and restless.","Right in front of Qiao Lanshu's eyes was Qin Yuanzheng's chest, and behind her was the wall. She realized, was she being pinned against the wall by Qin Yuanzheng?","Qin Yuanzheng lowered his head, looking at her flushed little face. He didn't speak, just slowly leaned closer to her.","As he approached, he also watched Qiao Lanshu's reaction.","If Qiao Lanshu showed a panicked or disgusted expression, he would stop immediately.","But Qiao Lanshu didn't. She just blushed, looking at Qin Yuanzheng with a bit of surprise and shyness.","It wasn't until Qin Yuanzheng was right in front of her that she shyly closed her eyes.","Qin Yuanzheng looked down at her, reached out to rub her hair, and then suddenly leaned in and kissed her.","Everything was because he couldn't help himself.","He found that when facing Qiao Lanshu, he couldn't control his desires at all.","He had originally thought that the little girl was still young and didn't understand these matters between men and women.","He could take it slow, cultivate their feelings first, and then proceed step by step.","In short, he couldn't be impatient.","But now, he couldn't wait at all.","He just wanted to stick with her every day, kiss her, bite her, or, like some kind of mortise and tenon joint, forcefully bully her.","Qiao Lanshu was a little out of breath. Her face was flushed red, and her body was too soft to stand.","Qin Yuanzheng suddenly picked her up, like carrying a child. Qiao Lanshu was stunned.","She lay on his shoulder with a red face and whispered, Brother Zheng, you, put me down, I can walk by myself.","Qin Yuanzheng didn't want to let go; he just wanted to hold her.","He buried his head in Qiao Lanshu's neck, took a deep breath, and asked in a hoarse voice, Comrade Xiao Qiao, marrying me, you really won't regret it, right?","Qiao Lanshu nodded. Of course I don't regret it.","Qin Yuanzheng felt very bitter in his heart because of his infertility.","He couldn't give Qiao Lanshu a child.","Qiao Lanshu was 11 years younger than him. If he passed away before her in the future, what would she, a weak woman, do?","Without a child to accompany her, even if he left, he wouldn't be at peace.","Qin Yuanzheng carried Qiao Lanshu to the second bedroom. As soon as he sat down, the bed creaked.","Qin Yuanzheng: ...","The fierce desire in Qin Yuanzheng's heart that was about to be unleashed suddenly cooled down a bit.","Holding Qiao Lanshu, he whispered, This bed still won't do. First thing tomorrow morning, I'll go hire someone to build a heated brick bed.","What else could Qiao Lanshu say? She could only blush and nod.","Her lips were a bit swollen, looking red and a little pitiful.","As Qin Yuanzheng looked at her, his eyes grew even deeper.","He pressed Qiao Lanshu onto the bed and kissed her endlessly.","The difference in their body size and height was too great; Qiao Lanshu had no room to resist at all.","She could only let him do whatever he wanted.","Even though the two of them didn't do anything but kiss, the bed kept creaking, as if they were engaging in some intense exercise.","About half an hour later, Qin Yuanzheng released Qiao Lanshu and whispered, Rest for a while. I'll go cook some rice for you.","At this moment, Qiao Lanshu was already having trouble breathing. She looked at Qin Yuanzheng with red-rimmed eyes and nodded.","Qin Yuanzheng reached out, rubbed her hair, and whispered, Good girl.","Then, burning with heat, he took off his undershirt and headed to the kitchen to cook, looking back at her with every step.","At the same time, he was still thinking, no, tomorrow he must quickly get the heated brick bed built.","He suspected that the effects of the drug Wang Huiping had given him still hadn't worn off.","Spending these past two days with Comrade Xiao Qiao, he had held back until he could hardly take it anymore.","After eating, the two slept in the same bed again. This time, Qin Yuanzheng didn't pretend to be a gentleman anymore.","As soon as he got into bed, he pulled Qiao Lanshu into his arms and kissed her.","An older man nearing thirty was like an old house catching fire; once it started, it was out of control.","He bullied his delicate and soft little wife in his arms until her eyes were filled with tears, her body was completely weak, and she was crying and begging for mercy.","Qiao Lanshu was completely dazed. Last night, when she took the initiative, she was scolded for messing around.","Why did Comrade Qin Yuanzheng suddenly get the idea tonight?","In the middle of the night, the exhausted Qiao Lanshu had long since fallen asleep.","Only her lips were still a bit red and swollen, and the corners of her eyes were red, looking as if she had been crying.","Qin Yuanzheng, however, didn't feel sleepy at all.","Holding Qiao Lanshu and staring at her sleeping face, the emotions in his heart swelled.","He really liked Comrade Xiao Qiao too much.","Fortunately, Comrade Xiao Qiao didn't marry anyone else; otherwise, he, who was slow to realize his feelings, would have regretted it to death.","...","Early the next morning, after making breakfast, he was the first to get up and go out to find a master to build the heated brick bed.","In the military compound, families with children would hire someone to build a heated brick bed, because sometimes the heating wasn't very good and the house was cold. Plus, the heating was turned off early in the season, so without a heated bed, children could easily catch a cold.","The master was also easy to find. Their neighbor Huang Erling's uncle was a bricklayer who was very skilled at building them. More than half of the heated brick beds in this military compound were built by him.","Early in the morning, Qin Yuanzheng found Battalion Commander Zhao Jiannong next door and asked him to go find Uncle Huang together.","Zhao Jiannong and Qin Yuanzheng came out of the building together. He occasionally looked at him with teasing eyes and smiled, saying, You're really something. A wooden bed isn't enough for you to toss around on, so you have to build a brick bed, huh?"]},{"number":38,"title":"Chapter 38: Married a Good Wife","paragraphs":["Qin Yuanzheng was teased by Zhao Jiannong, but he wasn't angry.","Having just gotten married and taken a wife, Qin Yuanzheng was in an excellent mood.","He nodded and said, \"We really do need to build a kang. Those wooden bed boards are too flimsy; they creak whenever you press on them.\"","With that, he asked Zhao Jiannong, \"By the way, have you built a kang at your place yet?\"","Zhao Jiannong nodded. \"As soon as my wife and kids arrived, I had kangs built in both rooms. With two kids in the house, that small, creaky wooden bed just wouldn't do. The four of us couldn't squeeze into it.\"","Qin Yuanzheng was surprised. He asked, \"The four of you sleep together?\"","Zhao Jiannong: \"Of course. The kids want to sleep right next to their mom.\"","Qin Yuanzheng: \"...\"","Qin Yuanzheng suddenly felt that not having children was quite nice. At least no one would fight him for his wife.","The two men walked out of the residential compound. Zhao Jiannong pointed to an area of low-rise civilian houses across the street and said to Qin Yuanzheng, \"Uncle Huang lives around here. I'll take you over.\"","Both men were tall and sturdy. Wearing military caps, leather boots, and draped in military overcoats, they stood tall and looked exceptionally handsome.","Of course, there were many officers like them in their military compound, but Qin Yuanzheng was the only one with such an outstanding physique and appearance.","Zhao Jiannong had always thought that Qin Yuanzheng would marry the daughter of some commander, political commissar, or provincial committee member.","That would make him a highly prized son-in-law with a boundless future.","However, he never expected things to turn out the way they did.","Zhao Jiannong actually felt a bit regretful for him.","He asked, \"Does your little wife know about your medical condition?\"","Qin Yuanzheng nodded. \"She knows.\"","How could she not know? She had even made a fuss about getting her tubes tied, which had nearly scared him to death.","Zhao Jiannong added, \"She is quite young, isn't she? Does she not understand? She knows what infertility means, right?\"","Qin Yuanzheng: \"...\"","Qin Yuanzheng glanced at Zhao Jiannong, too lazy to even respond.","Holding back a smile, Zhao Jiannong patted him on the shoulder and said, \"Treat her well. She married you from thousands of miles away, and considering your infertility, it isn't easy for her.\"","Qin Yuanzheng fell silent. Of course, he knew it wasn't easy.","But he didn't want to miss out on Qiao Lanshu either.","He would cherish and love Qiao Lanshu like a precious treasure.","As they talked, they arrived at Uncle Huang's place.","Qin Yuanzheng said, \"I'll go to the supply and marketing cooperative to buy a bottle of liquor.\"","Zhao Jiannong nodded. \"It's best to buy some cigarettes too.\"","When Uncle Huang built kangs for others, he usually charged a fee. But if he did it for them, he probably wouldn't accept any money.","So, they could only buy him some gifts instead.","...","When Qiao Lanshu woke up, she heard voices and some noise coming from outside.","She picked up the watch on her bedside table and saw that it was already nine in the morning.","Heavens, she had actually slept in this late!","Qiao Lanshu, who had never slept in so late, panicked a little. She quickly got up, put on her clothes, and went out. She saw a gray-haired man in the next room working alongside Qin Yuanzheng, carrying the collapsed wooden boards out of the house.","Qin Yuanzheng had taken off his overcoat and jacket. Wearing only a dress shirt with the sleeves rolled up, he was using a handcart to haul the wood outside.","Seeing that Qiao Lanshu was up, the expression on his face softened. He said, \"You're awake? This is Uncle Huang. He's here to help us build the kang.\"","Qiao Lanshu quickly said, \"Thank you for your hard work, Uncle Huang. Have you eaten? There's white rice porridge in the pot. Let me serve you a bowl.\"","The porridge in the pot had been cooked for her by Qin Yuanzheng and was still warming on the stove.","Uncle Huang waved his hand and smiled. \"No need, I ate before I came. Listening to your accent, you don't sound like a local. Where are you from?\"","Qiao Lanshu replied, \"I'm from Yangcheng. Uncle Huang, please have a cup of tea first.\"","As she spoke, she briskly grabbed a cup, put in some tea leaves, and poured in hot water. She smiled and said, \"I brought this from Yangcheng. It's home-roasted tea. Try it, it's very fragrant.\"","Uncle Huang stopped working, took the teacup from her, sniffed it, and said, \"Not bad, this is good tea! Tea around here isn't cheap. It's all transported from the south and costs more than cigarettes.\"","Qiao Lanshu smiled and said, \"It just so happens I brought some when I came. You can take half a pound back with you later. Next time I get more, I'll bring you some again.\"","Uncle Huang didn't stand on ceremony. He said, \"Alright, then I won't be polite with you.\"","Saying that, he put the teacup down and went back into the room. He gestured to Qin Yuanzheng and said, \"This apartment building doesn't have a reserved flue, so a traditional kang won't really work. Nowadays, everyone in the compound is building wooden kangs. Have you seen the ones next door?\"","Qin Yuanzheng shook his head. \"No, but just do what you think is best. Let me know how many wooden boards and bricks you need, and I'll go find someone to bring them over now.\"","Their mining construction site had plenty of mud, bricks, and wood. He could just submit an application and have them brought straight over to fix up the kang.","Uncle Huang planned it out for a moment and said, \"We'll need to haul at least five carts of wooden boards. Two bags of yellow mud should be enough.\"","To build a traditional kang, like the ones in the countryside, you first had to use bricks to build a flue on the ground, then lay flat stones over the flue, and finally seal it with yellow mud.","After it dried, you would lay out kraft paper, put down a thick mattress, and then you could sleep on it.","The kangs here were much simpler. After all, the apartment buildings had central heating. Everyone built kangs just to sleep more comfortably, as sleeping on those small wooden beds just wasn't satisfying.","Especially for families with children, a standard bed simply couldn't fit everyone.","Qin Yuanzheng's kang was very large, taking up half the room. Looking at it, Qiao Lanshu thought it resembled a large communal bed that could easily fit four Qin Yuanzhengs lying side by side.","What a huge bed.","Because the kang was so large, it required a lot of wooden boards and mud.","Uncle Huang was a veteran at this and worked quickly, but even so, it kept him busy from morning until afternoon.","Finally, the kang was finished.","He first used yellow mud as a base to make a frame, then covered it with wooden boards. The boards could be lifted up, allowing the space underneath to be used for storage.","The boards were laid perfectly flat. Once a soft straw mat and a thick mattress were placed on top, it was ready for sleeping. It was incredibly sturdy; even if four or five children jumped around on it, it would hold up fine.","Uncle Huang sat on a chair to rest. He lit a Daqianmen cigarette and asked the two of them, \"Do you want to build a kang in the other room too?\"","Most people here built kangs in both rooms at the same time, and some even built one in the living room.","However, since Qin Yuanzheng couldn't have children and there were no elderly family members living with them, leaving the wooden bed in the next room was fine. No one usually slept there anyway.","So he said, \"No need, just this one is fine. Thank you for your hard work, Uncle Huang.\"","Uncle Huang had been working hard all day, so they had to invite him to stay for a meal.","Qiao Lanshu had already started steaming the sweet potato rice.","She didn't know how to cook Northern-style dishes; she only knew how to steam rice and stir-fry a few dishes.","She washed and peeled two potatoes, then stir-fried a plate of sour and spicy shredded potatoes.","She also took out five eggs and stir-fried a large plate of scrambled eggs with garlic chives.","She had brought Chinese sausage and cured meat from Yangcheng, which were originally meant for Sun Mingyong.","She steamed the cured meat, sliced it up, and stir-fried it with napa cabbage.","Qin Yuanzheng stood watching from the side, completely stunned. \"You know how to cook?\" he asked.","Truth be told, these weren't the kinds of dishes they usually ate, but they smelled incredibly fragrant, glistened appetizingly, and looked absolutely delicious.","Uncle Huang took a sip of his liquor, followed by a bite of the cured meat, and smiled. \"This cured meat is fantastic. Commander Qin is a lucky man to have married such a good wife.\"","The young woman didn't look very old, but she was excellent at handling social graces, very polite, and a fantastic cook.","She truly was a wonderful wife.","Qin Yuanzheng was quite surprised himself. He had always assumed that because his wife was so young, she would be the one needing his care.","Yet, as it turned out, she was highly organized and incredibly thoughtful when handling things on her own."]},{"number":39,"title":"Chapter 39: The Hatred of Wife-snatching","paragraphs":["After dinner, Uncle Huang happily left with the half-pound of tea leaves and a piece of cured meat that Qiao Lanshu had packed for him.","Qin Yuanzheng took a broom and a mop, spending quite a while tidying up the house.","Finally, he got the place completely clean.","The newly built kang looked solid. Having slept on a heated brick bed since he was a child, he felt a fond familiarity looking at it.","He reached out and touched it; the mud at the bottom wasn't dry yet and needed to air out. Tonight, the two of them would still have to sleep on the wooden bed in the next room.","Qiao Lanshu washed all the dishes and chopsticks before walking in and asking him, \"Brother Zheng, is there anything you need me to do?\"","Qin Yuanzheng had already cleaned everything inside and out.","He wiped his sweat with a towel, glanced at Qiao Lanshu, and said, \"Xiao Qiao, come here.\"","Qiao Lanshu walked toward him.","Then, Qin Yuanzheng pulled her into his arms and kissed her forcefully.","Qiao Lanshu: \"...\"","Qiao Lanshu blushed, her heart beating fast. She liked Qin Yuanzheng and enjoyed being intimate with him, but a rough and rugged man like him sometimes didn't know his own strength when he got excited.","Qiao Lanshu could barely handle his kisses. Still kissing her, Qin Yuanzheng suddenly lifted her up. Startled, Qiao Lanshu quickly wrapped her arms around his neck to keep from falling.","Supporting her with his thick, strong arms, Qin Yuanzheng murmured, \"Why are you so light? You need to put on some weight.\"","With that, not waiting for Qiao Lanshu to reply, he pinned her against the wall and continued kissing her.","After a while, he asked gruffly in her ear, \"What do you think of this kang?\"","Her lips numb, Qiao Lanshu blushed and nodded.","Qin Yuanzheng asked again, \"Have you ever slept on one?\"","Qiao Lanshu shook her head.","Holding her, Qin Yuanzheng gave her neck a light bite and said in a hoarse voice, \"From now on, you sleep with me.\"","Qiao Lanshu: \"...\"","The current Qin Yuanzheng was like a completely different person from when they first met.","He had become so clingy now that Qiao Lanshu was having a hard time handling it.","Just then, someone knocked on the door outside.","The two exchanged a glance, and Qin Yuanzheng said softly, \"I'll go get it.\"","He released Qiao Lanshu, turned, and went out to open the door. Standing outside was a tall man around thirty years old, wearing a black trench coat and with slicked-back hair.","The man was tall and thin, with fair skin and a handsome, somewhat roguish look. He smiled and said, \"Regiment Commander Qin, I heard you finally got married? This is a great occasion! Why didn't you tell me in advance so I could rush back early for your wedding banquet?\"","As soon as Qin Yuanzheng saw him, his face darkened. \"Director Guan, why are you here?\"","Guan Wenjun was the director of the provincial revolutionary committee. However, before coming to the committee, he had also been in the military and was once in the same regiment as Qin Yuanzheng.","The two had never really gotten along.","Guan Wenjun once liked a woman, but that woman liked Qin Yuanzheng. From then on, Guan Wenjun always claimed that Qin Yuanzheng stole his wife, and he swore that if Qin Yuanzheng ever got a girlfriend, he would steal her away.","In the end, Qin Yuanzheng was diagnosed with infertility and simply decided not to marry at all.","When Guan Wenjun heard about Qin Yuanzheng's marriage this time, he was truly shocked. He drove back overnight just to see what kind of deity had managed to tame Qin Yuanzheng.","Thick-skinned, Guan Wenjun squeezed his way in through the door that Qin Yuanzheng was blocking. With one hand in his pocket, he smoothed his hair, walked a circle around the room, and said, \"Regiment Commander Qin, this won't do. This is too shabby. Apart from this sofa, you don't even have any decent furniture in here.\"","Saying so, he wandered around a couple more times and continued, \"How come I heard that your cousin introduced you to a divorced female worker with a kid, and you married her? Tsk, tsk, tsk, Qin Yuanzheng, oh, Qin Yuanzheng. You have fallen! You have become vulgar! My former prospect was so beautiful, and she desperately wanted to be with you, yet you didn't even look at her. How is it that now you've settled for a divorcee with a child? Is there something wrong with your taste?\"","Guan Wenjun was so bothered.","He originally thought about stealing Qin Yuanzheng's wife to avenge his past grievance.","But as it turned out, Qin Yuanzheng was ruthless enough to just find a divorcee with a child.","Even if Qin Yuanzheng fancied her, Guan Wenjun certainly wouldn't.","How was he supposed to steal her then?","How could he get his revenge?","Therefore, Guan Wenjun came knocking directly to denounce Qin Yuanzheng.","Qin Yuanzheng's expression was somewhat ugly. He had never stolen Guan Wenjun's prospect at all. It was that woman who kept pestering him back then. To avoid her, he had taken on many missions and left for several months.","Who would have thought that Guan Wenjun would still hold a grudge to this day?","If it were in the past, Qin Yuanzheng wouldn't have cared.","But now, the thought of Xiao Qiao being stolen by Guan Wenjun would probably drive him mad.","With a dark expression, Qin Yuanzheng looked at Guan Wenjun and said, \"Director Guan, are you done talking? If you're done, please get out.\"","Guan Wenjun acted as if he didn't hear him and continued talking on his own, \"Hey, I heard you picked up a son for free. Where is he? Let me take a look. No matter what, he should call me godfather, right?\"","Qin Yuanzheng's face sank. \"Guan Wenjun, are you done or not?\"","Seeing Guan Wenjun walking toward his bedroom, Qin Yuanzheng frowned, rolled up his sleeves, and strode over.","However, Guan Wenjun suddenly stopped in his tracks.","He stared dumbfounded at Qiao Lanshu, who was walking out of the bedroom, his expression shocked and his movements stiff.","He stood there, looking Qiao Lanshu up and down several times, looking utterly stunned by her beauty.","Qiao Lanshu was wearing a thin, long-sleeved loungewear set. Her black hair cascaded down, and her neat bangs covered her brows, framing her small, palm-sized face.","She had heard them talking from inside the room. Based on her understanding of Qin Yuanzheng, seeing him roll up his sleeves meant a fight was about to break out.","That was why she hurried out.","She walked up beside Qin Yuanzheng, looking at Guan Wenjun with an awkward expression. \"H-hello.\"","Saying so, Qiao Lanshu tugged at Qin Yuanzheng.","Qin Yuanzheng, with a gloomy face, suppressed his frustration. He then walked over, casually poured a cup of cold tea, placed it on the table, and said, \"Drink. Drink it and leave.\"","Guan Wenjun: \"...\"","Guan Wenjun's throat bobbed. He glanced at Qiao Lanshu again before asking Qin Yuanzheng, \"Didn't they say she brought a son? It seems the rumors were wrong. She brought a daughter over?\"","Qin Yuanzheng: \"...\"","Qiao Lanshu: \"...\"","Guan Wenjun took a sip of the cold, bitter tea and said without changing his expression, \"Regiment Commander Qin, actually, I could also be your son-in-law and call you Dad...\"","With a loud bang, Guan Wenjun was kicked squarely by Qin Yuanzheng, and then Qin Yuanzheng threw him out.","Guan Wenjun: \"...\"","Guan Wenjun stood up from the ground. He patted his black trench coat, his expression still somewhat dazed.","Then, it belatedly dawned on him.","That beautiful little girl from just now wasn't Qin Yuanzheng's daughter; she was his fucking wife!","Fuck!","How could Qin Yuanzheng have such a charmed life? His luck was always better than his!","Inside the room, Qiao Lanshu asked in a low voice, \"Brother Zheng, who was that person?\"","He seemed a bit unhinged.","With a dark expression, Qin Yuanzheng said, \"He is the director of the Provincial Revolutionary Committee. If you ever see him in the future, stay far away from him.\"","Qiao Lanshu nodded.","It seemed that the man from just now did not have a very good relationship with Qin Yuanzheng. However, Qiao Lanshu figured she probably wouldn't have any reason to cross paths with him anyway."]},{"number":40,"title":"Chapter 40: It's Almost Turning People into Beasts","paragraphs":["After Guan Wenjun came out of the military compound, he felt completely out of sorts.","How should he put it? He once had a girlfriend he really liked, and at the time, he had already planned to marry her.","But after that girlfriend met Qin Yuanzheng, she had a change of heart and fell for Qin Yuanzheng instead.","She subsequently rejected his marriage proposal.","From then on, Guan Wenjun began to hate Qin Yuanzheng.","For all these years, he had been competing with Qin Yuanzheng.","After Qin Yuanzheng was promoted to regiment commander, Guan Wenjun left the military and joined the provincial revolutionary committee, where he was now a director.","He was still competing with Qin Yuanzheng; since Qin Yuanzheng wasn't getting married, he wouldn't look for a partner either.","Whenever Qin Yuanzheng went on a blind date, he paid close attention.","He was determined to snatch Qin Yuanzheng's dates away from him.","But this time, he had gone out of town on business. How many days had he even been gone?","Qin Yuanzheng had already gotten his marriage certificate.","Guan Wenjun kicked the wall angrily and cursed, \"Qin Yuanzheng, that bastard.\"","He was too scheming!","He suspected that Qin Yuanzheng had deliberately waited for him to go out of town on business so he could quickly get married.","He probably feared he would come and make trouble.","And he married such a delicate and beautiful little wife. Who was he trying to anger to death?","Even Qin Yuanzheng, who suffered from infertility, got married, while he, Guan Wenjun, was still single!","The more Guan Wenjun thought about it, the more uncomfortable he felt. After returning to his office at the provincial revolutionary committee, he asked his subordinate to investigate Qin Yuanzheng's little wife.","His subordinate said, \"Director, why are you also investigating Qin Yuanzheng's wife?\"","Guan Wenjun sat in his office chair, propped his legs up on the desk, pulled out a Daqianmen cigarette and lit it. Then he tossed the cigarette pack onto the desk and asked in surprise, \"Who else is investigating her?\"","The subordinate replied, \"Oh, a lot of people. I heard many in the military are looking into it. Weren't there quite a few daughters of the commanders who had their eyes on Qin Yuanzheng before? Later, because of his infertility, none of them dared to marry him. Now that they hear he's married, they're all feeling indignant again and are investigating the girl's background.\"","Guan Wenjun: \"...\"","Guan Wenjun said speechlessly, \"They all have way too much free time.\"","He took a drag of his cigarette, feeling that he had too much free time too, and asked, \"So? What's the deal with that little wife?\"","Saying that, he sneered again and added, \"Could it be that her family background isn't very good? What normal person would fall for Qin Yuanzheng? Don't you agree?\"","Subordinate: \"...\"","The subordinate had actually inquired about Qiao Lanshu as well. After all, Qin Yuanzheng getting married was a major event. Probably anyone who had heard of Qin Yuanzheng had asked about his wife.","The subordinate said, \"Director, Qin Yuanzheng's wife is named Qiao Lanshu. She came from Yangcheng a while ago, saying she came to the military base to find her husband. But guess what? She was tricked into a fake engagement! Her fiancé was already married, had found a job, and even had a child.\"","Guan Wenjun: \"...\"","The subordinate shared whatever information he had gathered: \"Anyway, this female comrade's background is spotless. She was probably willing to marry Qin Yuanzheng to repay him for saving her life. After all, Commander Qin rescued her and took care of her, so it's understandable.\"","Guan Wenjun scoffed coldly. \"She's young, so she's easy to deceive! What kind of good guy is Qin Yuanzheng? If you cut his heart open, it's a bastardly thing blacker than a black sesame riceball! He definitely saw that the little girl was gullible, so he deliberately approached her!\"","Guan Wenjun got angrier as he spoke. \"I'm telling you, he has a track record! After all these years, his methods for seducing young girls haven't changed! Isn't he disgusting?!\"","Listening to him curse, the subordinate didn't dare utter a word.","Qin Yuanzheng was the commander of the Construction Corps, which was not a low rank. No matter what, it wasn't someone people like them could curse at.","Only Guan Wenjun, whose rank was roughly equal to his, dared to curse like this.","After Guan Wenjun finished cursing, he stood up and said, \"No, this little girl must have been deceived. I have to be a good person and go save her.\"","Subordinate: \"...\"","With that, Guan Wenjun left, and who knew what he went off to do.","The subordinate pondered inwardly: Director Guan hasn't done many good deeds in his life; is he really going to save someone this time?","...","Qin Yuanzheng was actually on guard against Guan Wenjun too.","Guan Wenjun had a bit of a crazy streak. Over the years, both of them had been single, and since they were in different systems, they naturally coexisted peacefully.","But now that Qin Yuanzheng had taken a wife, he had to guard against Guan Wenjun.","Who knew if a guy like Guan Wenjun would try to snatch his wife?","It was entirely possible. After all, based on his understanding of Guan Wenjun, that guy was capable of anything.","Taking advantage of his marriage leave, Qin Yuanzheng stayed with Qiao Lanshu all day long, basically never letting her go out alone.","Although the newly built heated kang bed looked quite nice, it still needed to dry for a couple of days and couldn't be slept on yet. Qin Yuanzheng bought some kraft paper and pasted a layer over it.","The new thick mattress he had commissioned Huang Erling next door to make wasn't finished yet either.","They could only wait a bit longer.","The two of them still had to sleep on the small bed in the second bedroom.","When Qin Yuanzheng lay in bed, he was waiting for his little wife to snuggle into his arms.","However, Qiao Lanshu didn't. Qin Yuanzheng had been a bit scary the past two days; he had kissed her so much that she was afraid.","Her lips still hurt even now.","After getting into bed, she slept right on the edge. Qin Yuanzheng waited a while, but the little girl didn't burrow into his embrace.","Qin Yuanzheng turned his head to look at her. Qiao Lanshu blinked her eyes and asked, \"Brother Zheng, what's wrong?\"","Qin Yuanzheng looked at her. \"Going to sleep just like this?\"","Qiao Lanshu nodded, her voice soft. \"Brother Zheng, do you need something?\"","Qin Yuanzheng: \"...\"","Qin Yuanzheng's body moved slightly, and the bed let out a \"creak.\" Qin Yuanzheng: \"...\"","Qin Yuanzheng coughed and asked her, \"You aren't cold tonight?\"","Qiao Lanshu shook her head. \"I'm not cold.\"","Qin Yuanzheng nodded. \"Alright, let's sleep then.\"","Saying that, he pulled the light cord and turned off the light.","Qiao Lanshu closed her eyes and slept quietly.","However, how could Qin Yuanzheng hold back?","They had already hugged and kissed; how could he possibly fall asleep now?","So, not long after they lay down, Qiao Lanshu heard the bed creaking, and immediately after, that strong, broad chest appeared right in front of her.","Qin Yuanzheng reached out and pulled her into his arms. As soon as his fragrant and soft little wife was in his embrace, he buried his face in her neck, took a deep breath, and whispered, \"Alright, go to sleep.\"","Qiao Lanshu silently reached up to cover her mouth and whispered, \"Brother Zheng, my lips still hurt.\"","Qin Yuanzheng had been restraining himself, but hearing her say that made his heart burn hot again.","However, this bed was old. Just turning over made the bedboards scream in protest. Qin Yuanzheng gave Qiao Lanshu a tight squeeze and said in a deep voice, \"Just wait a couple of days...\"","He didn't continue speaking, afraid of scaring the little girl.","He wondered, could the medicine Wang Huiping used have been animal medicine?","It felt like it was going to turn a man into a wild beast.","It was so potent."]},{"number":41,"title":"Chapter 41: Got a Job","paragraphs":["Early this morning, Deng Xiaozhen's brother, Deng Weijun, came to the military residential compound looking for Qiao Lanshu.","Qin Yuanzheng was still on his marriage leave. He wanted to stick by his wife's side every single day and initially had no intention of going out.","After all, seeing that the heated brick bed was almost dry, they might even be able to sleep on it tonight.","With his well-behaved and beautiful little wife wandering around in front of him every day, he simply couldn't hold back.","Seeing Deng Weijun arrive, he felt a bit dissatisfied. Standing at the door, he asked, \"Weijun, why did you come over?\"","It was also Deng Weijun's first time here. Seeing Qin Yuanzheng's stern face, he immediately stood up straight and said, \"Regiment Commander Qin, our factory manager asked me to come over. Didn't Comrade Xiao Qiao mention wanting to find a job? The temporary workers our food factory hired this year need to come to the factory for a unified onboarding today, so I came to ask, is Comrade Xiao Qiao still going?\"","Qin Yuanzheng: \"...\"","As a military officer, Qin Yuanzheng actually had ways to find a job for Qiao Lanshu, but he had to wait for the right opportunity because there were many military dependents and a high demand for job openings.","For instance, the teacher position in the propaganda department that Qiao Lanshu had mentioned before was mostly held by military spouses.","Qin Yuanzheng didn't really want Comrade Xiao Qiao to go to work; after all, he was fully capable of supporting her.","He was destined to never have children, so he figured he would just raise his little wife like a child.","She could stay by his side, living a carefree life forever. His money was more than enough to provide for her.","But Comrade Xiao Qiao didn't seem to think that way.","Qiao Lanshu came out of the room and asked him, \"Brother Zheng, who is it?\"","She seemed to have heard something about a food factory.","Qin Yuanzheng stepped aside from the door and said to Deng Weijun, \"Come in and sit for a while.\"","Deng Weijun didn't dare to go inside at all.","Looking at Qin Yuanzheng, he seemed like some kind of large, fierce beast strictly guarding its territory. With such a strong sense of territoriality, Deng Weijun dared not act rashly.","He said, \"No need, Regiment Commander Qin. I've delivered the message and I still have to go back to the factory for work, so I'll be leaving first.\"","Qin Yuanzheng remained silent for two seconds before saying, \"Wait a moment, we will go over together.\"","Deng Weijun quickly nodded, \"Okay, okay, I will wait for you at the main gate of the compound.\"","Saying that, Deng Weijun quickly slipped away.","Qin Yuanzheng returned to the room and said to Qiao Lanshu, \"The comrade from the food factory is asking the newly hired workers to go handle their onboarding. Do you want to go?\"","Qiao Lanshu's eyes lit up and she nodded, \"Of course, are we going right now?\"","Qin Yuanzheng nodded, \"We'll leave now. Put on some extra layers, it's very cold outside.\"","The weather had been getting colder and colder lately.","Fortunately, the food factory had dedicated boiler workers running the heating, so it wasn't cold at all inside during the winter.","Qin Yuanzheng followed behind Qiao Lanshu back into the bedroom. He watched as she put on a base shirt and then slipped a woolen sweater over it.","He took a look and suddenly said, \"Do you not have any thick sweaters? Let's go to the supply and marketing cooperative later to buy some yarn, and we'll hire someone to knit a couple for you.\"","Qiao Lanshu didn't know how to knit sweaters, but Qin Yuanzheng was right; her clothes were still too thin.","Previously, she had only focused on buying cotton to make padded jackets and hadn't even thought about making sweaters.","She nodded, \"Okay, I'll listen to you.\"","Qin Yuanzheng looked at her with a smile in his eyes. Once Qiao Lanshu put on her thick padded jacket and thick padded trousers, he brought over the red scarf and personally wrapped it around her, saying, \"Cover your mouth and nose too, the wind is too biting.\"","Qiao Lanshu was bundled up like a zongzi, looking round and surprisingly adorable.","Qin Yuanzheng also put on his military uniform and overcoat, then led Qiao Lanshu outside.","The two met up with Deng Weijun at the main gate of the compound, and then they rode in Qin Yuanzheng's car to the food factory together.","In Longcheng City, there were a total of two food factories: one in the north of the city and one in the south.","Yang Wenyan was the factory manager at the food factory in the north, responsible for supplying the towns and villages in that northern district.","In her previous life, after escaping from the cave dwelling, Qiao Lanshu had been rescued by the public security comrades. With the assistance of the Women's Federation, she was arranged a job at this very food factory.","She was actually quite familiar with the place.","Looking at the familiar stretches of factory buildings, she felt a bit emotional.","After getting out of the car, Deng Weijun began introducing the food factory to her: \"Over there is the pickled vegetable workshop, responsible for making preserves. Our pickled vegetables here are very popular. We pickle hundreds of thousands of catties every year, and the surrounding villagers love eating them.\"","Hundreds of thousands of catties was a bit of an exaggeration, but there were probably over a hundred thousand.","The pickled vegetable workshop was only busy during the vegetable season. Once winter came and everything withered, there wouldn't be any vegetables to pickle even if they wanted to work.","Deng Weijun continued, \"We also have a brewing plant, making things like soy sauce, white liquor, vinegar... Our soy sauce and vinegar here are highly sought after, especially the vinegar, which is always in short supply.\"","As Deng Weijun spoke of these things, his expression was full of pride.","Having worked at the food factory for so long in her previous life, Qiao Lanshu had never heard of anyone named Deng Weijun.","She asked curiously, \"What is your job? Which workshop are you in?\"","Deng Weijun replied, \"I'm a boiler worker in the brewing workshop.\"","The brewing workshop had specific temperature requirements; it couldn't be too high or too low, so it required manual temperature control.","Therefore, they needed dedicated boiler workers to manually manage the heat.","Qiao Lanshu looked a bit bewildered.","She knew the person who fired the boiler in the brewing workshop in her past life, and it wasn't Deng Weijun.","Could it be that Deng Weijun resigned later on?","Seeing how proudly he spoke of the food factory, he didn't seem like someone who would quit.","Deng Weijun added, \"Oh right, we also have a pastry workshop where they steam bread, cakes, steamed buns, and such. There are boiler workers there too, responsible for adding coal and stoking the fire to steam things. You will probably be assigned to the pastry workshop; they happen to be short-staffed there, and the work is relatively light. However, it's best not to be placed in the deep-frying team. They fry dough twists and make pancakes there every day—it's hot and dangerous...\"","The people around here still loved eating fried dough twists. Deep-fried in oil, they were fragrant, crispy, and stored well.","During the New Year and other holidays, buying half a catty or a catty to give as gifts was considered quite respectable.","Hearing this, Qin Yuanzheng chimed in, \"Cousin probably won't put you in the deep-frying team.\"","Yang Wenyan would look out for Qiao Lanshu. Although he wouldn't be too blatant about it, he only needed to casually mention a word when assigning work to get things done.","There were twelve temporary workers hired this time. When Qiao Lanshu went in to handle her onboarding, Qin Yuanzheng waited for her at the factory gates.","Deng Weijun also changed into his work uniform and headed off to his shift.","The personnel section staff had already organized the onboarding paperwork, and the temporary workers were lining up to receive their forms.","When Qiao Lanshu walked in, she still drew sidelong glances from several people.","It was because she was exceptionally pretty. Although she wasn't very tall, she had an oval face, fair skin, and large, bright eyes. When she smiled slightly, two small dimples appeared, along with a row of white, shell-like teeth.","Beautiful people always attract attention, no matter where they go.","The personnel clerk looked at her and asked, \"What is your name?\"","Qiao Lanshu replied, \"My name is Qiao Lanshu.\"","Qiao Lanshu's onboarding application form had been personally delivered to the personnel section by the factory manager, Yang Wenyan.","The personnel department naturally knew. Realizing what was going on, the clerk handed her an employment confirmation form and said, \"Take this form and report to the supervisor at the pastry workshop next Monday.\"","Qiao Lanshu took the employment form with both hands, smiling happily. \"Okay, thank you.\"","As she walked out with the sign-in sheet, someone behind her asked, \"Who is she? A family member of one of the workers?\"","\"Oh, I haven't heard of her. Which worker is lucky enough to marry such a beautiful wife?\"","\"She probably got in through connections. Look at how petite she is; she should be selling goods at a department store. Here, it's all manual labor. Being pretty is useless.\"","...","Qiao Lanshu ignored their gossip. She carefully put away the employment form. Today was Friday. The factory often required overtime on Saturdays and Sundays, but during the slow winter season, they would give days off.","Right now, it was winter, their off-peak season.","Therefore, the personnel department arranged for all the temporary workers to report together next Monday.","Qiao Lanshu walked out of the factory in high spirits. Seeing her from afar, Qin Yuanzheng immediately strode over to meet her. Looking at her expression, he asked, \"Are you really that happy?\"","Qiao Lanshu smiled and nodded. \"Yes, I am! I have a job now.\"","Although it was only a temporary position, she knew that if she worked hard, she could definitely become a regular employee.","After all, becoming a regular employee wasn't too difficult. As long as she performed well and earned a \"Five Good\" commendation, she could be promoted to a permanent worker.","Qin Yuanzheng looked at the sky and said in a low voice, \"It's getting late. Let's hurry home.\"","The heated brick bed at home had already aired out;","He was going back to sleep on it tonight!","At the thought of this, his heart burned with passion. He wrapped his arm around Qiao Lanshu's waist, opened the car door, and said, \"Get in, let's go home.\""]},{"number":42,"title":"Chapter 42: For the First Time, Without Hurting You","paragraphs":["Now that Qiao Lanshu had a job, she was in high spirits. On their way back, she and Qin Yuanzheng went to the supply and marketing cooperative to buy groceries.","They still had plenty of the rice Qin Yuanzheng had brought back, as well as flour and sweet potatoes.","There was also still some of the cured meat and sausage she had brought, but they were out of vegetables.","The cooperative was quite crowded. Qin Yuanzheng instinctively reached out, resting his hand on Qiao Lanshu's shoulder to protectively pull her into his embrace.","Feeling the gazes of passersby, Qiao Lanshu blushed, pushed Qin Yuanzheng's hand away, and stepped to the side.","Qin Yuanzheng: \"???\"","He looked at her and asked, \"What's wrong?\"","Qiao Lanshu whispered, \"We are outside.\"","Qin Yuanzheng was puzzled. \"What does being outside have to do with anything?\"","Was he really that embarrassing to be seen with?","Blushing, Qiao Lanshu looked at him and murmured, \"We need to mind our public behavior.\"","Qin Yuanzheng: \"...\"","Before they got married, Qin Yuanzheng had been prudish enough. If Qiao Lanshu so much as touched him, he would scold her for fooling around.","Now that they were married and he actually wanted to be close to her, she was the one refusing.","Qin Yuanzheng felt like he had dropped a rock on his own foot.","Keeping a straight face, he followed behind the young woman. Whenever she took a fancy to something, he would hand over the money and ration coupons, then take charge of carrying the items.","In the northern winters, fresh fruits and vegetables were extremely scarce. If you wanted fruit, you could only buy apples, pears, or persimmons, and they were quite expensive.","Otherwise, there were only canned tangerines, yellow peaches, and hawthorns.","Vegetables were also limited, mostly consisting of locally grown napa cabbage, large radishes, green onions, and potatoes.","For Qiao Lanshu, who loved eating leafy greens, this was indeed a bit of a challenge.","However, she was highly adaptable and could get used to eating these foods.","In the north, winter storage cabbage was sold. People could use their ration coupons to buy a hundred catties of napa cabbage to store in the residential compound's basement.","At just two cents a catty, it was a staple vegetable that every household hoarded.","When Qin Yuanzheng was in the army, he never had the habit of storing winter vegetables.","Now that he had a wife, he brought Qiao Lanshu to the cooperative, went straight to the vegetable section, took out his money and coupons, and bought fifty catties of napa cabbage.","At two cents a catty, fifty catties only cost him one yuan.","Qin Yuanzheng loaded the cabbage into the car and asked Qiao Lanshu, \"What else do you want to buy?\"","The weather was cold, and they might not be able to come out for groceries later on. Besides, winter storage vegetables were only available for a short period; by deep winter, they would be gone.","Thinking they should stock up, Qiao Lanshu said, \"Let's buy some more things that store well, like potatoes and pickled vegetables.\"","At this time, potatoes were three cents a catty, and fresh green onions were five cents a catty. Everyone bought them by the dozens of catties.","Qin Yuanzheng nodded. \"Potatoes are fine. Let's get fifty catties.\"","Potatoes, green onions, napa cabbage, and large radishes were all must-have winter staples for the locals.","Qiao Lanshu then went and bought five catties of soybeans, planning to sprout them at home.","After buying the easily storable winter vegetables, Qiao Lanshu spotted a fruit vendor and immediately could not tear herself away.","She whispered to Qin Yuanzheng, \"Brother Zheng, how much are those apples per catty?\"","Walking around like this had given her some understanding of the local prices.","Winter vegetables here were relatively cheap, but fresh fruit was very rare. Canned fruit was virtually a hard currency; ordinary people simply could not bear to spend money on it.","How could Qin Yuanzheng bear to let Qiao Lanshu suffer? He immediately said, \"If you want to eat them, we will buy them. Apples store well, too. Let's buy twenty catties to keep at home, and you can eat one a day.\"","Qiao Lanshu quickly asked, \"How much are they per catty? Do you have fruit coupons?\"","Qin Yuanzheng nodded. \"Yes, I have saved up a lot of coupons.\"","In the past, he had nowhere to spend his coupons. Now, it was great; he could buy things for his little wife, and he was happy to spend them.","The price of apples and pears was ten times that of potatoes. After all, in this era, the state encouraged agricultural production to increase grain yields and solve the problem of feeding and clothing the people.","Most of the land was used to grow grain.","Fruit trees were only planted in a few areas, so their yield was nowhere near as high as napa cabbage.","The price was forty cents a catty, so twenty catties would cost eight yuan.","Eight yuan was almost half a month's salary for a temporary worker.","After all, Qiao Lanshu's job only paid eighteen yuan a month.","Qin Yuanzheng did not feel a pinch spending the money. He bought ten catties of apples and ten catties of pears. He also saw some locally grown persimmons at ten cents a catty; they were still rock-hard and needed to be left for a while before they could be eaten.","He bought ten catties of those, too.","Carrying thirty catties of goods, he did not feel heavy at all and even freed up a hand to hold Qiao Lanshu's. \"There is canned fruit over there. Want to buy a few jars?\"","Qiao Lanshu was too shy to hold hands with him, so she avoided his grasp.","Qin Yuanzheng: \"???\"","Qiao Lanshu did not like canned fruit anyway, so she said, \"We have enough food and fruit at home. Let's go make dinner.\"","With that, she walked out of the cooperative first, her face flushed.","Qin Yuanzheng's expression was not great. His little wife would not let him hold her hand, and it made him feel disgruntled.","After getting into the car, Qin Yuanzheng drove. Qiao Lanshu did not notice his sour mood and muttered to herself, \"We have rice, flour, sweet potatoes, potatoes, napa cabbage... Oh right, did we buy radishes?\"","Qin Yuanzheng nodded. \"We did.\"","Qiao Lanshu then said, \"I heard the pickled vegetables made by our food factory are delicious. After I start work, I will go to the brewing workshop to take a look and buy some pickled radish strips for us.\"","Qin Yuanzheng nodded somewhat absentmindedly. \"Okay, whatever you say.\"","When they arrived back at the apartment building, Qin Yuanzheng opened the car door, unloaded the groceries, and put them in their family's designated basement storage area beneath the building.","The once-empty basement was now packed to the brim.","Looking at it, Qin Yuanzheng felt a sense of joy.","After storing the vegetables, they carried the fruit, along with one napa cabbage, four potatoes, and two green onions, back upstairs to their apartment.","Just that one cabbage was enough for several meals.","Upon returning home, Qin Yuanzheng took off his coat and began to prepare dinner. He washed a piece of fruit for Qiao Lanshu and said, \"I will go cook. You rest for a bit.\"","Qiao Lanshu refused to just rest; she went into the kitchen to help wash and chop the vegetables.","The couple cooked together.","They made steamed rice again, and Qin Yuanzheng also steamed a few steamed buns. He always felt that rice was not filling enough; he preferred steamed buns.","Qin Yuanzheng made a potato and cured meat stew, stir-fried sour and spicy cabbage, and steamed some eggs.","The steamed eggs were specifically for Qiao Lanshu. He always felt his little wife was too skinny, looking so small and frail as if she were malnourished. She needed to eat more.","After dinner, Qin Yuanzheng boiled some hot water for Qiao Lanshu to bathe with. Then, he quietly went back to the bedroom.","The heated brick kang bed he had built a couple of days ago was already dry. He laid down two layers of kraft paper on top, followed by a straw mat.","Then, he went to the next room, brought over the two mattresses, and spread them out.","He pressed down with his hands. Yes, the kang was solid and sturdy. With the mattresses on top, it was not hard at all. He lay down on it for a moment to test it out and thought it was fine; the young woman should be able to get used to sleeping on it.","After Qiao Lanshu finished her shower and came out of the bathroom, she saw that Qin Yuanzheng had already made the kang.","Seeing her come out, Qin Yuanzheng stared at her with slightly darkened eyes. He said, \"You get on the kang first, I'm going to wash up.\"","With that, he strode to the bathroom.","Blushing, Qiao Lanshu walked to the edge of the bed—oh, wait, it should be the edge of the kang. This northern kang was truly large; it was big enough for her to roll around on it several times.","She took off her shoes, climbed onto the kang, and carefully smoothed out the mattress Qin Yuanzheng had laid out, making it perfectly neat.","Qin Yuanzheng showered very quickly. He had been holding back for several days. That desire had been increasing every day, gradually approaching its threshold, yet the feeling of having no outlet left him somewhat restless and agitated lately.","Fortunately, three days after their wedding, he could finally consummate their marriage today.","After his shower, Qin Yuanzheng put on his shorts and picked up his undershirt. However, he took one look at it, hesitated for only half a second, and tossed it aside.","It was fine to wear it normally for his wife to see.","But tonight, there was no need to wear it.","Qin Yuanzheng turned off the living room light and returned to the bedroom. At a glance, he saw his little wife lying on her stomach on the kang, reading a newspaper, her feet kicked up in the air, revealing her fair skin.","Qin Yuanzheng watched her for a few seconds. Sensing his gaze, Qiao Lanshu looked up. Their eyes met, and she sat up with a blush, saying rather nervously, \"Brother Zheng, are you done washing?\"","Although she had experiences from her past life, the pressure Qin Yuanzheng gave her at this moment was still very obvious.","She always felt like she was being targeted by a fierce beast, leaving her at a loss for what to do.","She only took one look at Qin Yuanzheng before abruptly withdrawing her gaze. Blushing all the way to the base of her neck, she stammered slightly, \"Brother Zheng, why... why aren't you wearing any clothes?\"","Qin Yuanzheng's skin was a wheat color, and his muscles were robust. Just looking at him made one blush.","Qiao Lanshu was too embarrassed to look closer. Qin Yuanzheng walked over and also got onto the kang. He embraced her and said softly, \"We are already husband and wife, why are you still so easily shy?\"","Held in his arms, Qiao Lanshu felt his strong heartbeat. She didn't want to be like this either, but she just couldn't control her habit of blushing easily.","It was also Qin Yuanzheng's first time. Looking at his little wife who was about ten years younger than him, his heart was filled with tender affection.","He whispered, \"Don't be nervous. I will be careful and won't hurt you.\"","A man like Qin Yuanzheng, who had rolled through the battlefield, usually lived quite roughly when he was alone.","But now, with Qiao Lanshu, he became cautious and gentle in every aspect.","He held Qiao Lanshu and kissed her, kissing her until she was... all over...","Then, he slowly took off Qiao Lanshu's clothes.","Never mind Qiao Lanshu, Qin Yuanzheng himself was nervous to death.","He felt as if he couldn't control his own strength. In a moment of excitement, there was a rip, and Qiao Lanshu's clothes were torn.","Qiao Lanshu: \"...\"","Qiao Lanshu's heart ached; she had brought these clothes all the way from Yangcheng.","Blushing, she pressed down on his hand and licked her numb lips. She felt as if her entire body was wrapped in a large furnace, making her flush and burn. With reddened eyes, she said, \"Oh my, Brother Zheng, this fabric is very expensive.\"","Qin Yuanzheng: \"...\"","Qin Yuanzheng's eyes were also turning red from excitement. He said gruffly, \"Be a good girl, I'll buy you a new one next time.\"","Qiao Lanshu: \"...\"","Qin Yuanzheng had been single for so many years, and this was his first time seeing a woman's body, let alone such a beautiful woman's.","Qiao Lanshu had a well-proportioned figure, plump where she should be and slender where she should be. Her fair skin flushed with a deep pink, and her long, seaweed-like black hair was scattered across the bedding. Her bangs were soaked with sweat, sticking to her forehead and face.","Qin Yuanzheng reached over and gently brushed the wet hair away from her neck.","At the touch of his rough fingers, she sensitively shrank her neck, looking a bit afraid of him.","Qin Yuanzheng asked in a hoarse voice, \"We've barely done anything yet. We haven't even started, and you already can't take it?\"","Qin Yuanzheng had immense strength, making it almost unbearable for Qiao Lanshu. She kept saying, \"Brother Zheng, you...\"","Every muscle in Qin Yuanzheng's body was taut. He was so hot that he was covered in sweat, soaking the bedding.","Qiao Lanshu felt herself sweating from the heat. She wiped the corner of her eye and whispered, \"Brother Zheng, you...\"","At this very moment, how could Qin Yuanzheng possibly put on the brakes?","He whispered comfortingly, \"******\"","...","Qiao Lanshu: \"...\"","Qin Yuanzheng possessed a healthy and robust body, and his vigor was terrifyingly abundant.","Qiao Lanshu reached out and pressed against his chest, trying to push him away. Qin Yuanzheng looked at her fingers—slender and long, like fresh scallions. He held her fingers and played with them for a while, and then, **********.","In her daze, Qiao Lanshu suddenly felt a sharp pain in her hand.","This cleared her head a bit. With belated realization, she found several ** on her fingers.","Qiao Lanshu pulled her hand back and glanced at it in confusion. Her mind was a complete mush, unable to process anything.","Before her eyes was only Qin Yuanzheng's face, moving closer and further away, along with his bulging chest muscles and a pair of beautifully sculpted arms.","His breathing was right by her ear, his voice laced with hoarseness.","Qiao Lanshu heard what he said, but it was as if the information couldn't reach her brain, because she remembered none of it.","She only knew to follow his voice and speak, but as for what she actually said, she had no idea.","Looking at Qiao Lanshu, who was on the verge of passing out, Qin Yuanzheng paused. He murmured, \"Be good, call out to me once more?\"","Qiao Lanshu asked blankly, \"Call what?\"","Qin Yuanzheng stared at her with bloodshot eyes, a heavy fire of desire burning within them. He whispered, \"Hubby.\"","Qiao Lanshu followed his lead and said, \"Hubby.\"","Hearing this soft, sweet \"hubby\" that sounded almost like she was acting spoiled,","Qin Yuanzheng instantly felt as if an electric current had shot through his entire body.","Then, he suddenly scooped Qiao Lanshu up and got off the kang.","Qiao Lanshu had a petite and slender figure. He held her in his arms like a child, his broad back completely shielding her from view.","From a distance, if it weren't for her slender legs being visible, no one would be able to tell that Qin Yuanzheng was carrying a person in his arms.","He carried Qiao Lanshu, pressing her against the wall and letting her lean on his broad shoulders. He coaxed her in a low voice, \"Good wife, call me hubby one more time?\"","Qiao Lanshu thought that if she just followed his demand, he would soften and let her go.","Therefore, she softly called out again, \"Hubby...\"","This time, it was like pouring gasoline onto a burning old house.","The fire raged even more fiercely.","Every part of Qin Yuanzheng was **","*********","At this very moment, he finally understood why his married comrades with families were always so homesick.","Right now, he had absolutely no desire to go to work.","All he wanted was to hold his sweet, soft little wife day and night, every single moment, and never go anywhere else."]},{"number":43,"title":"Chapter 43: Formal Onboarding","paragraphs":["Although it was Qin Yuanzheng's first time, he truly and profoundly experienced the joy of such matters.","He had originally intended to restrain himself a bit. After all, Qiao Lanshu was still young, and he needed to take good care of her.","Furthermore, these things couldn't be rushed; the first time definitely shouldn't last too long.","In the end, he was simply too excited and lost control...","By the time he came back to his senses, he didn't even know how many times it had been. He thought back and guessed it must have been three or four times, though he couldn't remember clearly.","He didn't know when, but Comrade Xiao Qiao had already fallen asleep.","Halfway through, he had called out to his little wife a few times, but she had only looked at him with aggrieved eyes, not saying a word, looking as if she had been loved silly.","Once Qin Yuanzheng sobered up, his heart ached for his little wife.","He quickly went to boil some hot water, then brought over a hot towel to wipe Qiao Lanshu's body.","Qiao Lanshu's skin was fair, making the marks on her body look incredibly prominent.","Qin Yuanzheng's heart ached terribly. He felt deeply remorseful that he had been so heavy-handed and vowed to be more careful in the future.","Moreover, he realized that he hadn't used any protection the entire night. Fortunately, he was infertile; otherwise, he really didn't want Comrade Xiao Qiao to get pregnant so quickly.","Thinking of this, he placed the hot towel on Qiao Lanshu's stomach to apply a warm compress.","Qiao Lanshu groggily opened her eyes, only to see Qin Yuanzheng sitting beside her, his head lowered as he gazed at her with affectionate eyes.","She asked in a low voice, Brother Zheng, what are you doing?","Looking at her sleepy, dazed appearance, Qin Yuanzheng simply didn't know how to dote on her enough. He whispered, Applying a warm compress to your stomach. Didn't you say it hurt?","Qiao Lanshu was speechless.","She really didn't know what to say.","Didn't Qin Yuanzheng know perfectly well why her stomach hurt?","That wasn't something a hot compress could relieve.","She moved the hot towel away, pulled the quilt over herself, and said, Brother Zheng, let's sleep. It's getting very late.","She guessed it was already the middle of the night. After all, Qin Yuanzheng had tossed her about endlessly; she even felt like it was almost dawn.","Qin Yuanzheng said softly, Alright, I'll go empty the water and come right back.","Saying that, he got up, emptied the water from the basin, hung up the towel, and quickly returned. He climbed onto the heated brick bed, slipped under the quilt, and reached out to pull Qiao Lanshu into his arms.","He used one hand to rub her stomach and asked softly, Does it still hurt? Do you want to drink some hot water?","Leaning against his broad chest, Qiao Lanshu blushed and said, It doesn't hurt anymore.","In truth, she still felt uncomfortable, but she was too embarrassed to say so.","Of course, it was also because she was too exhausted and really didn't want to talk anymore.","Outside the window, the north wind howled. Looking at the weather, it seemed like it was going to snow again.","Qin Yuanzheng's embrace was like a furnace, warm and toasty. Qiao Lanshu found it very comfortable, so she closed her eyes, feeling drowsy.","Qin Yuanzheng, however, had no sleepiness at all. He whispered in Qiao Lanshu's ear, Was it a bit too much? Is that why your stomach hurts?","Saying that, he sighed again, speaking as if he were both relieved and regretful, Good thing I have infertility, otherwise...","He didn't continue.","However, these words touched Qiao Lanshu's heart.","In her past life, when she was with Qin Yuanzheng, he was infertile, and her body was too damaged to bear children.","Therefore, they had been together for five years in their past life without having any children.","This time, Qiao Lanshu had avoided the tragic experiences of her past life and possessed a healthy body. But Qin Yuanzheng's infertility was innate, they called it something like asthenozoospermia, which seemingly couldn't be cured.","Feeling a bit melancholic, Qiao Lanshu took the initiative to kiss Qin Yuanzheng on the cheek and whispered, Brother Zheng, if you want a child, we can go to the orphanage and adopt one. I heard there are quite a few children there. We can pick one who is destined to be with us.","Holding Qiao Lanshu, Qin Yuanzheng said softly, No need. Raising you is enough. I don't want to raise a child.","It had taken him so much effort to finally get married and take a little wife. He wanted to spend a few more years living a beautiful, harmonious life with her.","His little wife was still young and pure-hearted; he needed to look after her more.","Right now, he truly didn't have any thoughts about having children.","Hearing him say this, Qiao Lanshu didn't bring it up again.","She was simply too tired, so she just closed her eyes and fell asleep nestled in his arms.","She slept very deeply. By the time they woke up, the sun was already high in the sky.","Qin Yuanzheng had been awake for a long time. According to his routine, he usually got up between five-thirty and six o'clock.","Then he would attend morning training, eat breakfast afterward, and head to the mining area and various construction sites.","But today, after waking up, he didn't get out of bed.","He continued to hold his soundly sleeping little wife in his arms, reluctant to let go.","Looking at the fragrant and soft little wife in his embrace, he thought to himself, no wonder people say women are made of water.","She really was like water, smooth, soft, and smelling faintly of soap. He absolutely loved it.","Unwilling to let go, he just lay there on the heated brick bed, using his arm as a pillow, and held Qiao Lanshu as they slept until past ten in the morning.","Since the beginning of his memory, Qin Yuanzheng had never slept in this late.","But after all, it was the joyful occasion of their wedding; indulging for a day was fine.","When Qiao Lanshu woke up, she rolled over, then frowned, let out a low hiss, and reached out to press her lower back.","Qin Yuanzheng immediately leaned over nervously, reached out to rub her lower back, and asked softly, Wife, what's wrong? Does your back hurt?","Qin Yuanzheng's palms were broad, warm, and rough, but he held back his strength, gently rubbing and pressing for her, which actually made her feel a bit more comfortable.","Lying on her stomach on the bedding, revealing her fair and lustrous back, Qiao Lanshu said to Qin Yuanzheng with grievance, My lower back is so sore, and it's all your fault.","Qin Yuanzheng was speechless.","Qin Yuanzheng swallowed hard, tugged at his pants somewhat guiltily, and then said, I'm sorry. I'll be careful next time. Don't be mad at me, okay?","How could Qiao Lanshu be mad at Qin Yuanzheng? She laughed softly and said, I'm not mad.","Qin Yuanzheng's heart softened, and he asked, Do you want porridge for breakfast? Millet porridge.","Qiao Lanshu nodded. Okay.","Qin Yuanzheng quickly got off the heated brick bed and went to cook porridge for Qiao Lanshu.","Qiao Lanshu was going to report to the food factory next Monday, so they only had these two days to be affectionate at home. Qin Yuanzheng cherished this time in his heart.","He decided that for these two days, he wouldn't go anywhere; he would just spend them right here on the bed!","...","Soon, it was time to officially start work.","In the personnel department's office, Wei Zhengye had also brought his daughter, Wei Hongmei, over.","Wei Hongmei was previously supported by Sun Mingyong; she didn't have a job herself.","Sun Mingyong would occasionally receive remittances from his parents in Yangcheng, and with Wei Zhengye's subsidies, the family of four never had to worry about food and drink.","But now that Sun Mingyong had been sent to a labor camp, leaving behind a debt of over a thousand yuan, how could Wei Hongmei possibly pay it off?","Although Wei Zhengye's heart ached for his daughter, for the sake of her long-term future, he swallowed his pride and applied for a temporary position for her.","When Wei Hongmei came to handle the onboarding procedures, she was still very reluctant. She said, \"Dad, aren't you a director at the food factory? How could you just arrange a temp job for me? Temp workers get low pay and no subsidies. They're treated as inferior in everything they do. I don't want to do it.\"","Wei Zhengye's face darkened. Angry yet helpless, he said, \"You still have two children to raise. How can you survive without working?\"","Wei Hongmei replied self-righteously, \"Don't I still have you? Dad, are you saying you don't want to take care of us anymore?\"","Wei Zhengye was speechless.","He sighed and said earnestly, \"It's not that Dad doesn't want to take care of you, but you have to stand on your own two feet. You don't have a husband to rely on anymore. If you don't work, what will you do when I'm no longer around?\"","At the mention of this, Wei Hongmei started crying again. She said, \"I wonder how Mingyong is doing over there. Is the labor camp hard? Does he have money to bribe people to make things easier?\"","Through her tears, she continued, \"It's all that woman's fault. Couldn't she just stay in Yangcheng? Why did she have to come all this way? Just how ugly is she? Does no man want her?\"","Wei Zhengye kept a dark expression and pulled Wei Hongmei into the personnel department office. \"Just keep your mouth shut and let's get your job sorted out first.\"","Because of Sun Mingyong's incident, Wei Zhengye had been scolded by the factory director and told to rest at home for a week. Over the past two days, for the sake of his daughter's job, he had shamelessly gone to the director again. After much pleading, the director also felt that Wei Zhengye and his daughter had been deceived by Sun Mingyong.","In a way, they were victims too. Seeing that his daughter was still struggling to raise two children, the director agreed to hire Wei Hongmei.","After all, it was just a temporary position. If she did well, she could strive to become a regular employee; if she did poorly, she would be fired. It wasn't a big deal.","Of course, to prevent any awkward encounters between Wei Hongmei and Qiao Lanshu, Factory Director Yang Wenyan told Wei Zhengye to assign his daughter to the brewing workshop to make pickled vegetables.","Therefore, upon coming in, Wei Hongmei was handed the onboarding form for the brewing workshop.","Walking out of the factory, Wei Hongmei was still asking, \"Dad, did that woman go back to Yangcheng?\"","Wei Zhengye said impatiently, \"Why do you keep asking about this? Why do you care where she went? It has nothing to do with you.\"","Wei Hongmei was speechless.","Wei Hongmei simply couldn't swallow her anger. She always felt that her beautiful life had been ruined by that woman.","Her heart was filled with hatred.","Qiao Lanshu, on the other hand, held no grudges against Wei Hongmei.","Her mind had only been set on finding Qin Yuanzheng and getting revenge on Sun Mingyong.","Now that Sun Mingyong had gotten his retribution, she had also married Qin Yuanzheng.","She didn't pay much attention to anyone else.","She and Qin Yuanzheng had been affectionate at home for a few days. Last night, she told Qin Yuanzheng that they could only do it one more time and couldn't fool around anymore.","It was her first day of work, and she wanted to leave a good impression on her colleagues.","So, bright and early on Monday morning, Qin Yuanzheng drove a high-spirited Qiao Lanshu to work.","Qiao Lanshu wore a newly made army-green cotton-padded jacket, a red scarf wrapped around her neck, and a woolen hat on her head. Her small face was snow-white, and her nose was red from the cold.","Breathing out puffs of white air, she arrived at the factory and casually asked someone, \"Hello, comrade. Could you tell me how to get to the pastry workshop?\"","Wei Zhengye, the person she had asked, froze for a moment. He looked Qiao Lanshu up and down before replying, \"Over there. It's the second workshop on the right.\""]},{"number":44,"title":"Chapter 44: Backdoor","paragraphs":["Qiao Lanshu did not recognize Wei Zhengye. After all, in her previous life, the time she worked at the food factory was two years later.","At that time, the director of this food factory was not Wei Zhengye.","Coupled with the fact that Wei Zhengye was not wearing his work uniform today.","Qiao Lanshu thanked Wei Zhengye for pointing the way, and then she ran towards the pastry workshop.","Wei Zhengye watched Qiao Lanshu's retreating figure for a moment before heading to the pickle workshop to find his daughter, Wei Hongmei.","Today was Wei Hongmei's first day at work. He was truly worried about his daughter, so he went over to check on her.","As a result, as soon as he entered the main gate of the pickle workshop, he saw Wei Hongmei standing at the entrance. She was wearing protective clothing but no gloves, and her eyes were red as she wiped away tears.","Wei Zhengye thought something terrible had happened to his daughter. He hurried over and asked, \"Hongmei, what is wrong with you? Is someone picking on you?\"","It did not make sense. He had already spoken with the supervisor of the pickle workshop and asked them to look after his Wei Hongmei.","Their food factory was very large, and each workshop had a workshop supervisor. Below the workshop, there were several shifts or teams, and each team had a team leader.","For example, the pickle workshop was divided into the pickling team, the soy sauce team, and so on.","Some jobs were easy, while others required manual labor, but the working hours and wages were about the same.","Wei Zhengye had thought of having the workshop supervisor assign his daughter, Wei Hongmei, to the pickling team. After all, winter was approaching, and there were no vegetables to pickle in the winter, so the workers were generally quite idle.","Seeing Wei Zhengye approach, Wei Hongmei immediately walked over with red eyes and said, \"Dad, didn't you say you had already put in a good word for me? Why did they still assign me to the pickling team?\"","Wei Zhengye thought the workshop supervisor had not helped him. Hearing this, his face instantly darkened, and he said, \"What is wrong? Is the pickling workshop not good? For the whole winter, there will be hardly any work for three or four months, and you can get off work early every day. Is that not good? Others are fighting to get in. You got assigned here, and you are still not satisfied?\"","Wei Hongmei stomped her feet in anxiety and angrily complained to Wei Zhengye,","\"Dad, you do not even know where they assigned me! They arranged for me to pickle radishes. Those radishes are huge and heavy, and we have to manually carry them basket by basket to wash them. The water in the pool is not heated; it is all cold water pumped straight from the lake!","\"We have to wear these kinds of gloves to wash them! After washing, we still have to cut them. The team leader said that every strip must be cut evenly, not big and small. My hands are frozen stiff, how can I even cut them? I do not dare to cut, I almost chopped my own fingers off!\"","Hearing his daughter say this, what else could Wei Zhengye not understand?","Wei Hongmei had been assigned to the washing and cutting team.","But at least she was assigned to the pickle workshop, which was better than the other workshops.","So he said, \"Wait here for a moment. I will go ask and see if the packaging team needs anyone.\"","Saying that, he walked towards the office of the pickle workshop.","The supervisor of the pickle workshop was a female comrade named Tang Wenxia. She was in her thirties, tall, and had a loud voice. She had worked in the pickle workshop for many years and was quite familiar with Wei Zhengye.","When Wei Zhengye came to the office to find her, she happened to be in the office sorting out the patrol forms of each team. Seeing Wei Zhengye come over, she thought Director Wei was there to inspect the work. She immediately stood up and said, \"Director Wei, why are you here at this hour? Are you here for a routine inspection?\"","Wei Zhengye shook his head. With his hands behind his back, he walked up to Tang Wenxia, stood still, and asked, \"Supervisor Tang, it is like this. Did my daughter not come to work today?\"","Tang Wenxia nodded. \"Oh right, now that you mention it, I remember. It is Comrade Wei Hongmei, right? I have already assigned her to the pickle day shift.\"","Wei Zhengye did not blush or skip a beat, asking directly, \"It is like this, Supervisor Tang. My daughter is currently raising two children on her own, and she usually has a lot of things to take care of at home. See if you can transfer her to the packaging workshop? The work there is easier, so she can save some energy to go home and take care of the children.\"","Nowadays, most female workers had children.","Although it was said that women hold up half the sky, the factory still had to give special care to those with children at home.","Manual labor still had to be left to the male comrades.","Wei Zhengye's son-in-law, Sun Mingyong, used to work in the office of the business department of the food factory. He dealt with clients every day, and more than half of the people in the factory knew him. Therefore, when the news of his marriage fraud came to light and he was brought to the general assembly to be criticized, everyone naturally knew about it.","Tang Wenxia knew that Wei Hongmei had lost her husband and had to raise two children alone, which was indeed difficult.","She looked a bit troubled and said, \"Director Wei, it is truly not that I do not want to take care of Comrade Wei Hongmei, but the positions in our pickle workshop are limited. Currently, only the cutting and washing workshop is short of hands, and the other workshops are not. If we force her in, someone must be willing to transfer to the cutting and washing workshop...\"","Of course, the cutting and washing workshop had vacancies precisely because it was too exhausting. If every workshop was as relaxing as the packaging workshop, why would anyone leave for no reason?","Tang Wenxia added, \"However, winter is setting in now, and the winter vegetables have all been harvested. The busy period will only last for this half a month. By next month, it will be relaxed. The next time we make pickles will be in the spring of next year, and the weather will not be cold then.\"","Wei Zhengye certainly knew this, but Wei Hongmei did not want to do it. Let alone half a month, Wei Hongmei could not endure this hardship for even a single day.","So Wei Zhengye asked again, \"How about you go and ask for me, and see if anyone in the packaging workshop is willing to transfer to the cutting and washing workshop? I can offer one hundred yuan to buy the spot.\"","Wei Zhengye's willingness to pay showed his sincerity.","However, if Tang Wenxia went to ask, would it not let everyone know that she was pulling strings for Wei Zhengye?","Moreover, if no one agreed to the transfer, would she not have stuck her neck out for nothing?","But if she did not go and ask, she would offend Wei Zhengye.","Therefore, Tang Wenxia fell silent for a moment, and suddenly said to Wei Zhengye:","\"Director Wei, why do you not go to the pastry workshop and ask? Does the pastry workshop not have a fermentation room? Perhaps they are short of people there. You could have Comrade Wei Hongmei go to the fermentation room to be responsible for monitoring the temperature. This job is light and has no pressure.","\"If the fermentation room is not short of people, she can also go to the pastry workshop to make biscuits. Biscuit making is all mechanized. The workers only need to pack the baked biscuits on the conveyor belt and put them into boxes, which is also very relaxing.","\"Oh, right, our bread workshop is also very relaxing. Except for pinching the dough, which is manual labor, baking bread is also mechanized. The workers only need to put the fermented dough on the conveyor belt. Which of these is not easier than our pickle workshop?\"","Wei Zhengye knew that Tang Wenxia found Wei Hongmei to be a hot potato, so she just wanted to send Wei Hongmei away quickly.","But Tang Wenxia had a point. Even though the pastry workshop didn't have a slow season in the winter like the pickle workshop did, the work there was physically much lighter. Aside from a few days of required overtime—making mooncakes for the Mid-Autumn Festival, jujube rice cakes at the end of the year, and dough lanterns for the first lunar month—the day-to-day work was actually quite relaxed.","At the very least, working in the pastry workshop meant no washing in freezing cold water, which meant Wei Hongmei wouldn't be constantly complaining about her hands going numb or her joints getting ruined by the cold.","Wei Zhengye thought it over and finally said, Alright then, I will go to the pastry workshop and ask.","However, the pastry workers had likely reported in today as well, meaning the workshop was probably already fully staffed. He would have to speak with the supervisor there to see if they could somehow open up a spot to squeeze Wei Hongmei in."]},{"number":45,"title":"Chapter 45: Fried Dough Twists","paragraphs":["When Qiao Lanshu arrived at the pastry workshop, she saw the personnel department staff leading two new employees toward the workshop.","She hurried to catch up and greeted the personnel staff.","The personnel clerk glanced at her and asked, Are you for the pastry workshop?","Qiao Lanshu nodded, Yes.","The clerk said, Alright, follow me.","The clerk took the three newcomers to the pastry workshop supervisor's office. Supervisor Liu Weihong warmly welcomed them: Oh my, Clerk Zhou, you've finally brought me some help. The pastry workshop has been increasing production lately, and we are severely short-handed. Everyone is complaining about the overtime.","Clerk Zhou immediately said, Then hurry up and assign them work. You've been allocated three people this time, which should definitely be enough.","Liu Weihong smiled and nodded, Alright, alright. By the way, are they all family workers?","As she spoke, she looked at the three new employees.","Two women and one man, all young.","Her gaze lingered on Qiao Lanshu's face for a long time. Looking at Qiao Lanshu's delicate and beautiful face, she frowned slightly and said, We do rough manual labor here, how did a pampered young lady end up here? Whose family member are you?","She asked Qiao Lanshu, Are you a family worker?","Qiao Lanshu: ...","For some reason, Qiao Lanshu saw disgust in the other party's eyes.","She said with a straight face, Supervisor Liu, I am not a family worker.","Liu Weihong kept a straight face and said, If you're not a family worker, then how did you get in?","Clerk Zhou from the personnel department quickly interjected, Oh, Supervisor Liu, this is a military family member. Her husband is an officer in the mining area.","These details were all written in her personal file; it was public information and not a secret. Anyway, the people in the personnel department and the logistics office all knew about it.","Therefore, Clerk Zhou lowered his voice and told Liu Weihong directly, Supervisor Liu, she is the family member of Commander Qin.","Liu Weihong: ...","Liu Weihong was shocked for a moment: Ah? You mean Qin Yuanzheng?","Qin Yuanzheng was truly famous.","After all, Yang Wenyan was the director of the food factory, so through Yang Wenyan's matchmaking, there were quite a few female comrades from the food factory who went on blind dates with Qin Yuanzheng.","Some were rejected by Qin Yuanzheng without even meeting him.","Some, like Wang Huiping, had eaten with Qin Yuanzheng at Yang Wenyan's house, and then there was no follow-up.","This Liu Weihong was one of those who had eaten with Qin Yuanzheng and had no follow-up.","Liu Weihong and Qin Yuanzheng simply didn't fancy each other.","Qin Yuanzheng had no intention of getting married, and Liu Weihong despised him for his inability to have children.","However, as the saying goes, once you've seen the vast ocean, other waters pale in comparison. Having had a blind date with someone as excellent as Qin Yuanzheng, how could Liu Weihong look up to other men?","So for the past two years, she had delayed getting married. She was already 27 this year and was still single.","She was on the verge of becoming an old maid.","She couldn't help but think of Qin Yuanzheng again. The more she thought about it, the more she felt that Qin Yuanzheng, a man who couldn't have children, was still so picky, which was truly shameless. She, an unmarried single female supervisor, hadn't even said anything.","So, seeing Qiao Lanshu at this moment, she suddenly sneered: Didn't he say he wouldn't get married? He couldn't have kids, so he wasn't going to marry, but hasn't he still gotten married now? Sure enough, a man's mouth is a deceitful ghost.","She looked Qiao Lanshu up and down critically and added:","What kind of work can a petite person like you do? Don't drag down the efficiency of our workshop. Under normal circumstances, someone like you wouldn't even be able to enter the gates of our factory;","You've pulled strings so blatantly, haven't you? If you have that kind of money, you should have used it at the department store or the supply and marketing cooperative, or even becoming a receptionist at a state-run restaurant or a registration clerk at a guesthouse wouldn't be bad. At least those are places where looks matter, right? Coming here, a pretty face won't put food on the table.","Liu Weihong rambled on, constantly criticizing Qiao Lanshu.","Qiao Lanshu listened to her without changing her expression and didn't say a word. She just followed behind Liu Weihong with the other two newcomers, listening to her assign tasks.","Liu Weihong assigned the other two to the bread team and the pastry team, and then said to the remaining Qiao Lanshu, You can go to the deep-frying team. It's the end of the year, and we need to fry dough twists. You can go over and help out.","The deep-frying team mainly fried dough sticks, fried pancakes, and dough twists.","Dough twists were easy to store, divided into large and small ones, and came in sweet and savory flavors.","Dough twists were heavy in oil, fragrant and crispy to eat, and were a New Year's gift that every household would buy during the holidays.","It was winter now, and the Spring Festival was just two months away, so of course, the dough twists had to be prepared.","Hearing that she was assigned to the deep-frying team, Qiao Lanshu felt a little uncomfortable. She was clearly being targeted.","After all, the deep-frying team was a high-temperature environment. It was very hot inside and also very dangerous. If she got splashed by hot oil, it would be disastrous.","Plus, being a southerner, she didn't know how to make dough twists at all.","However, it was her first day at work. If she showed dissatisfaction with the supervisor's arrangement on the very first day, she could forget about keeping this job.","It was better to just finish the first day properly and see what this Liu Weihong's deal was.","Qiao Lanshu nodded and said, Okay, Supervisor Liu, I will definitely work hard.","Liu Weihong gave her a critical look and said, Alright, go on. Brother Hu, you are responsible for guiding her.","Qiao Lanshu put on protective clothing, a mask, gloves, and a hat at the door, and walked into the deep-frying team.","As soon as she entered, a wave of heat hit her face.","It was really hot inside.","The oil in several large woks was bubbling and sizzling. Three people were responsible for one large wok.","Moreover, most of the workers here were men. At a glance, apart from two older women responsible for scooping out the dough twists, the rest were male workers.","Qiao Lanshu walked over calmly and said, Brother Hu, what do I need to do?","Brother Hu looked at this petite young woman and frowned slightly. He said, You...","He paused. He was going to ask her to scoop out the dough twists, but could she even lift that large slotted spoon?","He then asked, Do you know how to make dough twists?","As he spoke, he pinched a piece of dough with both hands, pulled it, folded it, and the stretched dough was quickly twisted into a strand, then thrown into the wok to fry. It instantly became a fragrant and crispy dough twist.","Qiao Lanshu: ...","Qiao Lanshu said modestly, Brother Hu, I will learn earnestly.","Which meant she didn't know how.","Brother Hu was speechless. He said, Forget it, you just scoop out the dough twists. Pay attention, don't let them over-fry. See this? A golden yellow color is fine. Any darker and it will be bitter.","Qiao Lanshu picked up the large slotted spoon and scooped the dough twists out of the wok little by little.","Her arm strength wasn't enough, so she scooped them out bit by bit without rushing. Her movements were quite steady, unlike some people who came in all flustered and ended up covered in oil splatters.","Brother Hu watched her for a while and then went back to making dough twists.","Meanwhile, on the other side, Wei Zhengye also came over. He found Liu Weihong and said, Supervisor Liu, do you have a moment? I need to ask you something."]},{"number":46,"title":"Chapter 46: Job Transfer","paragraphs":["When Liu Weihong saw Wei Zhengye approaching, she immediately went up to greet him enthusiastically, \"Director Wei, what brings you to me?\"","Wei Zhengye explained his daughter's situation and then asked Liu Weihong, \"The work over at the pickle workshop isn't quite suitable for my daughter. Do you have more vacancies over here?\"","Upon hearing this, Liu Weihong fell silent for a moment. It was completely obvious to her—Wei Zhengye wanted to find a cushy job for his daughter.","Did everyone treat their pastry workshop like a recycling bin for trash? Taking in just anyone?","However, Wei Zhengye was the factory director after all, with authority second only to the factory manager. Supervisors like her didn't dare offend him.","Wei Zhengye added, \"It's winter, and the end of the year is approaching. The pastry workshop must have a pretty heavy workload, right?\"","Liu Weihong smiled and nodded. \"Yes, lately we've been mainly busy frying dough twists. Our factory's small dough twists sell very well every year. Last year we didn't even have enough to sell, so this year's quota has increased by five thousand catties of flour.\"","This workload was indeed much heavier compared to last year, which was exactly why the pastry workshop needed to add more hands.","They had to guarantee production so everyone could have a good New Year.","Wei Zhengye then said, \"That's perfect. Today is Hongmei's first day on the job. She is very good at making pastries. Whether it's bread or cookies, she's great at it. She makes them a lot at home. How about I let her come over and give it a try?\"","Liu Weihong was speechless.","It was one thing to send his daughter over.","But he even specified that she should make bread and cookies.","Liu Weihong felt stifled, but she immediately thought of Qiao Lanshu, who was also a relative of the factory manager that had gotten in through the back door.","She might as well let the two back-door entries swap places. Since they both got in through connections, neither could blame the other.","Anyway, Liu Weihong felt annoyed just looking at Qiao Lanshu right now, so she immediately said, \"Director Wei, your timing is perfect. I have a new temp worker here. She looks thin, small, and delicate, just like a spoiled young lady. At first glance, you can tell she's not cut out for hard work. I happened to not want her either, so let's just send her to the pickle workshop.\"","Hearing her say this, Wei Zhengye's brow instantly relaxed. He said with a smile, \"Supervisor Liu, you really handle things thoughtfully. I'll consider myself indebted to you this time. I'll go call Hongmei over to report to you.\"","Saying that, Wei Zhengye walked away happily.","Liu Weihong turned around and went back to the frying team.","At this moment, Qiao Lanshu was standing next to Brother Hu, helping fry the dough twists.","She didn't know how to make dough twists, so she could only be responsible for frying them. Aside from it being a bit hot and her arms getting a bit sore, everything was going fairly smoothly.","She was very worried about over-frying the dough twists, so she watched them closely.","Seeing her working so earnestly, Brother Hu, who was originally somewhat dissatisfied with her, also began to approve of her in his heart.","New apprentices all needed at least a week of learning time.","Brother Hu actually didn't mind if she learned a bit slowly, but at the very least, she needed to have a serious attitude and be meticulous in her work.","Brother Hu watched the young girl waving the large slotted spoon, struggling to scoop up the dough twists. He walked over, reached out to take the spoon, and said to Qiao Lanshu, \"Alright, take a break. Go get a drink of water.\"","Actually, Qiao Lanshu had been working for less than an hour, but it was indeed hot here, and she needed to stay hydrated.","Plus, her arms had been continuously waving the iron spoon and were already very sore.","This large slotted spoon was actually quite heavy, which was why this workshop consisted mostly of men. Most young girls were in the bread workshop.","Wearing a mask and a hat, Qiao Lanshu only revealed a pair of bright black eyes. Her eyes curved into a smile as she said, \"Thank you, Brother Hu. I'll go get a drink of water then.\"","As she spoke and was just about to go drink some water, she saw Liu Weihong come in again.","As soon as Liu Weihong saw her, her brows furrowed. \"Are you here to act like a young lady or to work? How long have you been on duty? Has it even been an hour? And you're already slacking off?\"","Before Qiao Lanshu could even open her mouth, she heard Brother Hu say impatiently, \"I was the one who told her to rest. The girl hasn't had a single sip of water since she started her shift. I told her to take a break and get a drink. What's the problem?\"","Liu Weihong was speechless.","Liu Weihong really hadn't expected this. Brother Hu, who usually didn't talk much to people and never gave face to anyone, was actually speaking up for Qiao Lanshu.","She originally thought that given Brother Hu's level of pickiness, he would have scolded Qiao Lanshu to tears.","She said, \"Brother Hu, you aren't speaking up for her just because she's young and pretty, are you?\"","Brother Hu got angry. He heavily banged the spoon in his hand and stared at Liu Weihong, saying, \"What nonsense are you spouting? Work is work. Comrade Xiao Qiao is serious about her work, so of course I'm willing to speak up for her.\"","Brother Hu found Liu Weihong to be the most annoying person. She was simply a troublemaker, always stirring up unnecessary drama all day long, yet he never saw her do much actual work.","Being spoken to like this by Brother Hu, Liu Weihong felt she was losing face. She stopped arguing with Brother Hu, turned to Qiao Lanshu, and said, \"The director just came and said that the pickle workshop is short-handed and wants you to go over there. Let's go.\"","Brother Hu frowned and said suspiciously, \"The pickle workshop is only busy for these ten days or half a month. After that, they'll be the most idle ones. How could they still be short-handed? I'm the one who's short-handed, can't you see that?\"","Liu Weihong clicked her tongue and said to Brother Hu, \"Brother Hu, just relax. I'll find a male comrade to come over for you in a bit.\"","Saying that, Liu Weihong glared at Qiao Lanshu and said, \"Hurry up and come with me.\"","Brother Hu still felt displeased in his heart. He said, somewhat annoyed, \"If there's a male comrade, why didn't you bring him to me this morning? You really have a screw loose.\"","Liu Weihong was speechless.","Being choked back by Brother Hu like this, Liu Weihong was truly furious.","But she couldn't argue with Brother Hu either. Brother Hu was an old employee in the factory who had worked in several workshops, and his working ability was unquestionable.","He had been awarded \"Five-Good Worker\" several times. Originally, he should have been the one promoted to supervisor, but Liu Weihong had used her connections to snatch the spot and replace Brother Hu.","Brother Hu understood this in his heart, but he didn't say much about it.","Work was just like that. No matter when or where, it was always about favors, networks, and connections.","Qiao Lanshu followed Liu Weihong out of the frying team.","She seemed to have no temper at all. Whatever Liu Weihong said, she didn't refute, just obediently doing as she was told like a fool.","On the surface, she looked quite aggrieved, but in reality, her heart was singing with joy.","To think there was such a good thing!","The frying team was so hot, and the air inside was stuffy. Staying there for too long made one dry and irritated.","The key point was that after swinging the spoon for forty minutes, both her arms were incredibly sore and swollen.","Not to mention, there was also Supervisor Liu who was targeting her.","She took a deep breath of the cool and fresh air, following Liu Weihong toward the pickle workshop.","She was familiar with the pickle workshop. In her past life, she had worked in the pickle workshop and had done several jobs there. Comparatively speaking, she would get the hang of it much faster.","More importantly!","Winter was coming up next!","Starting from December on the new calendar, the pickle workshop would have almost no work at all. They could be idle until after the New Year!","Qiao Lanshu wondered to herself: would Liu Weihong really give her such a great job?","Could she be tricking her?"]},{"number":47,"title":"Chapter 47: He is like a worried old father.","paragraphs":["Liu Weihong brought Qiao Lanshu to the entrance of the pickles workshop, looked at her with disdain, and said, \"Go report to Supervisor Tang in the pickles workshop.\"","With that, Liu Weihong turned and walked away. If she hadn't been afraid of things going wrong with the job transfer and being seen by the factory director, she wouldn't have even bothered to escort Qiao Lanshu over.","After Qiao Lanshu went in, she asked around for Supervisor Tang. It just so happened that Tang Wenxia had just seen Wei Hongmei off and was standing at the door.","Seeing Qiao Lanshu approach, she knew this was the unlucky girl whose position had been taken by Wei Hongmei.","She felt a bit of sympathy for her in her heart.","She walked over and said, \"You must be Comrade Qiao Lanshu, right?\"","Qiao Lanshu nodded. \"I am.\"","Tang Wenxia looked at her petite figure and said, \"Let's go, to the cutting and washing workshop.\"","In the cutting and washing workshop, they were currently mainly processing pickled radishes and napa cabbage.","The large radishes, pulled straight from the muddy fields, had actually already gone through the first cleaning process via washing machines.","Water resources were scarce in the north, and clean water was very precious.","The machines would recycle the water, giving all the dirt-covered radishes a simple preliminary rinse.","Then, the rinsed radishes were sent over on a conveyor belt, where the workers would carefully wash them again. Once clean, they were sent to be cut into strips and then pickled.","Actually, Wei Hongmei was telling the truth when she said the work involved heavy lifting and the water was cold.","However, there weren't many occasions where female workers needed to do heavy lifting, and when they did, two women would carry the load together. They just needed to dump the radishes into the pool and let the machines stir them. Most of the time, male workers were responsible for the heavy lifting, while female workers handled the washing.","As soon as Qiao Lanshu arrived at the cutting and washing team, she immediately took out her knitted gloves from her padded coat pocket.","She put the knitted gloves on first, and then layered a pair of waterproof gloves over them. This way, her hands wouldn't hurt when washing the radishes.","Tang Wenxia was a bit surprised to see this. She said, \"You're quite smart, knowing how to keep warm.\"","Qiao Lanshu smiled and said, \"Because the waterproof gloves here are all too big, wearing knitted gloves inside makes them fit a bit better.\"","Tang Wenxia nodded and didn't say anything more. She found a female worker in her thirties and asked her to take charge of training Qiao Lanshu.","Then Tang Wenxia left.","The female worker assigned to guide Qiao Lanshu was named Wang Xue.","Wang Xue wasn't a talkative person, but since Wei Hongmei had just left and Qiao Lanshu had arrived, it was obvious that Wei Hongmei found the work here too tiring and had taken Qiao Lanshu's better position.","Wang Xue looked at Qiao Lanshu and comforted her, \"Since you're here, just work hard. Don't think our cutting and washing work is too exhausting. No matter how tiring it is, it's only for this half a month. After half a month, we'll have plenty of free time.\"","Qiao Lanshu knew Wang Xue was trying to console her. In reality, she was feeling quite pleased internally and wasn't sad at all.","She smiled and nodded. \"Thank you, Sister Wang.\"","Seeing how thin and small she was, Wang Xue asked, \"How old are you?\"","Qiao Lanshu: \"Sister Wang, I'm 18.\"","Wang Xue asked in surprise, \"Listening to your accent, you're not a local.\"","It was truly a rarity. Working in the factory, Wang Xue had basically never interacted with educated youth from out of town, and she had never heard such an accent before.","Qiao Lanshu explained, \"I'm from Yangcheng, in the southernmost part of the motherland.\"","Wang Xue led her to the large water pool, where everyone was washing radishes. They scooped up the washed radishes, placed them on the conveyor belt, and sent them to the vegetable cutting workshop.","Wang Xue said admiringly, \"With your little short legs, you sure can run far.\"","Qiao Lanshu: \"...\"","Wang Xue smiled and said, \"The water is cold, I don't know if you can handle it. Tomorrow, go to the supply and marketing cooperative and buy a pair of thermal waterproof gloves, then it won't be so cold.\"","Saying that, she even showed Qiao Lanshu her own gloves. The outside had a waterproof layer, and the inside was lined with a thin layer of cotton. Even though it was thin, it was very effective at keeping warm.","Qiao Lanshu didn't mention her knitted gloves and just nodded. \"Okay, thank you, Sister Wang.\"","Wang Xue waved her hand. \"Since I'll be guiding you from now on, I'm your master. Don't be so polite anymore.\"","Qiao Lanshu called out with a smile, \"Alright, Master.\"","Wang Xue really liked this little girl. She took her along to wash the radishes. After the washing was done, they went to another workshop to cut the radishes into strips.","A portion of the radishes needed to be diced to make sour and spicy diced radishes.","Another portion was to be cut into strips, making the very appetizing salty and spicy radish strips.","The radishes had to be cut into uniform long strips, which was hard to do while wearing gloves, so everyone took their gloves off.","Wang Xue taught Qiao Lanshu for a little while and then let her cut on her own.","She had thought Qiao Lanshu would need a few days to get used to it before she could cut the radishes evenly. To her surprise, right after starting, she was already cutting the radishes into perfectly uniform strips. At a glance, it looked like every single strip was almost identical.","Wang Xue was stunned. She said, \"Comrade Xiao Qiao, you are really something else! You cut these way too well!\"","Qiao Lanshu said modestly, \"It's all because you taught me well, Master.\"","Wang Xue: \"...\"","Wang Xue couldn't even cut them that beautifully herself; she felt she had no right to be called a master.","They worked for the whole morning. At noon, Wang Xue personally took Qiao Lanshu to the cafeteria to eat. After returning from lunch, they hurried to finish cutting the remaining radishes and sent them to be dried, after which they could get off work.","Qin Yuanzheng was very worried about Qiao Lanshu. So, even before it was time to get off work, he drove over early and waited at the entrance of the food factory.","He didn't know if his little wife had been bullied on her first day of work.","She was an outsider, couldn't understand the local dialect, and he wondered if she had any trouble communicating.","Most importantly, could she handle the work at the factory?","Qin Yuanzheng was acting like a worried old father. He sat in the car, constantly looking out the window, wondering why his little wife hadn't come out yet.","At this time, Liu Weihong, who got off work right on time, came out arm in arm with a colleague from the factory.","Both of them saw Qin Yuanzheng's car. A military vehicle was, of course, very conspicuous. Especially since Liu Weihong had been on a blind date with Qin Yuanzheng, she was even more familiar with his car.","The colleague beside her said, \"Oh my, it's a military car. This must belong to an officer at the battalion level or above, right? Since when do we have military family members in our factory?\"","Liu Weihong: \"...\"","Liu Weihong snorted coldly and said, \"That's the car of Commander Qin from the 21st Regiment, didn't you know? He's impotent in that aspect, and he definitely can't have children. Whoever becomes his wife is going to have a miserable life ahead.\""]},{"number":48,"title":"Chapter 48: My Husband Can Do It Several Times a Night","paragraphs":["Liu Weihong and her female colleague were badmouthing Qin Yuanzheng here.","They directly twisted Qin Yuanzheng's infertility into him being impotent.","Of course, Qin Yuanzheng didn't care about other people's opinions at all.","In the past, when he went on blind dates with those female comrades, the first thing he did was confess his infertility. After all, it was necessary to make such things clear in advance.","Therefore, Qin Yuanzheng's infertility was not a secret in the entire mining area, or even in the nearby factories.","From time to time, Liu Weihong would glance in Qin Yuanzheng's direction.","The female colleague was still talking, \"Oh, Weihong, didn't you go on a blind date with him back then? Why did you reject him? Otherwise, you could be sitting in a car right now, being a chief's wife. Traveling by car, how grand is that?\"","Liu Weihong scoffed coldly and said, \"What's so great about a car? Isn't it just as cold sitting inside?\"","The female colleague said, \"That's still better than us walking through the wind and snow, right?\"","At the same time, the female colleague muttered in her heart: Liu Weihong couldn't even afford a bicycle now, yet she was complaining about people being cold in a car. It was truly hilarious.","Liu Weihong actually felt resentful in her heart. Back then, she had merely hesitated and hadn't refused immediately; it was Qin Yuanzheng who had rejected her.","He was an infertile man, and she hadn't even said anything about it.","The more Liu Weihong thought about it, the angrier she got. She said, \"What's the use of being grand? If a man is impotent, he's impotent. Marrying him is just living like a widow.\"","\"Who said Regiment Commander Qin is impotent?\"","A soft voice rang out. The two of them looked back at the same time and saw Qiao Lanshu wearing a black woolen hat, her face tightly wrapped in a red scarf, revealing only a pair of dark eyes that were staring straight at Liu Weihong.","Today was her first day at work, and Liu Weihong hadn't bullied Qiao Lanshu any less. She made her fry dough twists when told to, and transferred her post when told to, although Wei Hongmei, who had been transferred over, was also a hot potato.","But tormenting Qiao Lanshu made Liu Weihong feel comfortable in her heart.","She thought Qiao Lanshu was really a pushover, so she said, \"I said it, so what? Am I wrong?\"","Qiao Lanshu said without blushing or skipping a heartbeat, \"Of course you're wrong. Regiment Commander Qin is my husband. Could I not know if my husband is potent or not? Let me tell you, my husband can go seven times a night. He's very fierce. You can't even find a man, so just go ahead and be jealous.\"","Liu Weihong: \"...\"","Liu Weihong and the female colleague beside her were stunned.","Qiao Lanshu looked so small and well-behaved, how could she speak so shamelessly?","Calling him husband left and right, and even saying he was fierce. Who around here directly called their spouse 'husband' like that?","Truly shameless!","No wonder Qin Yuanzheng took a liking to such a woman. No man could resist being chased by such a pretty little woman calling him husband!","Liu Weihong was dumbfounded. Pointing at Qiao Lanshu in shock, she screamed, \"What nonsense are you spouting?\"","That wasn't all. Qiao Lanshu was still talking. She looked well-behaved and her voice was soft, but the words she spoke could anger a person to death.","She said, \"I'm not spouting nonsense, Supervisor Liu. I heard you're already in your thirties and still haven't found a partner, so are you sexually frustrated? I heard that the more a person lacks something, the more they like to stare at it. Are you too lacking in men, so you keep staring at other people's husbands, saying this one is impotent and that one is impotent?","Whether other people's husbands are potent or not, what does it have to do with you? Anyway, potent or not, he's not your husband. If you have the energy to ponder over other people's husbands, you might as well spend some effort finding a few more matchmakers. Maybe you can even find a husband before you turn forty. By then, you can experience for yourself whether your husband is potent or not. Do you think my proposal is feasible or not?\"","Liu Weihong was so angry she almost fell backward. The female colleague beside her was also stunned by Qiao Lanshu's words.","She stared at Liu Weihong with a strange expression, making Liu Weihong feel uncomfortable all over.","She was almost driven to tears by anger. With red eyes, she shouted, \"Qiao Lanshu! What are you babbling about? I'm only 27! 27! How am I in my thirties? If you spout nonsense again, I'll tear your mouth apart!\"","Qiao Lanshu smiled and said, \"Oh, Supervisor Liu, I really hit the nail on the head, didn't I? So you're flying into a rage from humiliation? Don't be in a hurry, fate is predestined by heaven. Your true love...\"","She deliberately paused. Others thought she would say that Liu Weihong's true love hadn't arrived yet.","As a result, Qiao Lanshu slowly added a sentence: \"Maybe it died prematurely a long time ago?\"","Liu Weihong: \"...\"","Liu Weihong felt that Qiao Lanshu was cursing her to never get married.","She just wanted to find someone with a slightly higher status, a bit more handsome, a slightly higher salary, plus a bit of help from his family. Her requirements weren't that high.","But she just couldn't find one, which was why she had dragged it out until now. Seeing that it was the end of the year, and she would be 28 after the New Year, she was indeed getting a bit anxious.","So at this time, being told this by Qiao Lanshu made her break down a little.","Her anger surged. Staring at Qiao Lanshu, she was about to pounce over and hit her. The female colleague beside her quickly held her back and whispered, \"Don't be impulsive, her husband is here!\"","The two turned their heads to look. Sure enough, Qin Yuanzheng had gotten out of the car at some point. Wearing a crisp military overcoat and a military cap, with his broad shoulders and long legs, he walked over in just a few steps.","Liu Weihong's gaze couldn't help but be fixed on Qin Yuanzheng's body.","She thought Qin Yuanzheng would remember her, however, Qin Yuanzheng didn't even glance at her.","In his eyes, there was only the little wife he had just married and brought home.","Qin Yuanzheng walked over, lowered his head to look at Comrade Xiao Qiao, whose height only reached his chest, and affectionately gathered her scarf for her. He asked in a low voice, \"You came out but didn't hurry to find me. What are you talking about here?\"","Qiao Lanshu also didn't know when Qin Yuanzheng had come over, nor how much he had heard.","She felt so panicked in her heart. Could Qin Yuanzheng have seen her acting so mean just now?","She didn't want to have a bad image in front of Qin Yuanzheng.","She gave Qin Yuanzheng a sweet smile, then grabbed his arm and pulled him away: \"It's nothing, it's nothing, Brother Zheng, let's hurry home, it's too cold!\"","Qin Yuanzheng was dragged by her toward the car.","Qin Yuanzheng looked at Qiao Lanshu dotingly. Saying nothing, he took a big step forward, wrapped his arm around Qiao Lanshu, and opened the car door for her.","Leaving Liu Weihong and the other woman behind, watching their receding figures, the female colleague beside her said with a face full of envy, \"Regiment Commander Qin is really too handsome. His figure and appearance are simply beyond words.\"","Not to mention his aura of having been on the battlefield and commanding an army.","At this time, she could also somewhat understand Liu Weihong. Having been on a blind date with such an excellent man, when looking at others, how many could catch her eye?","The psychological gap would be too huge.","Qin Yuanzheng closed the car door for Qiao Lanshu, and then got into the car himself.","However, he didn't start the car immediately. Instead, he turned his head and looked at Qiao Lanshu with a profound gaze.","Qiao Lanshu felt a bit guilty: \"Brother Zheng, what's wrong?\"","Qin Yuanzheng gave a light chuckle. Leaning in close, he lowered his voice and said, \"Why aren't you calling me hubby anymore? You were saying it so smoothly just a moment ago.\"","Qiao Lanshu: \"...\"","Oh no, Brother Zheng heard everything!"]},{"number":49,"title":"Chapter 49: As expected of Qin Tuan, truly fierce.","paragraphs":["Qin Yuanzheng pulled Qiao Lanshu's scarf down, revealing her fair little face.","She gave a flattering smile and immediately started praising him blindly, \"Brother Zheng, you're off work right on time, and you even drove over specifically to pick me up. You are really too good. The car is parked so perfectly straight, too, unlike other people's cars that are all crooked.\"","Qin Yuanzheng looked out the window. His was the only car here.","Was his little wife feeling awkward and just making small talk?","Qin Yuanzheng just looked at Qiao Lanshu without saying a word. His gaze was deep, carrying a certain emotion that reminded Qiao Lanshu of her first time with Qin Yuanzheng. Back then, the way Qin Yuanzheng looked at her was exactly like this.","Qiao Lanshu instantly blushed red to her ears. She reached out to pinch Qin Yuanzheng's overcoat and whispered, \"You wear your clothes perfectly straight, too, much better looking than others...\"","Qin Yuanzheng couldn't hold back. He reached out to rub her head, then cupped the back of her head and kissed her on the lips.","Very forcefully.","Qiao Lanshu quickly begged for mercy, \"Brother Zheng, I still have to work tomorrow.\"","Qin Yuanzheng started the car and told her, \"Don't worry, since you've already put the words out there, I definitely can't let them fall flat. Seven times a night isn't impossible either. I'm mainly just afraid you won't be able to handle it and will pass out again, making me worry for ages.\"","Qiao Lanshu: \"...\"","Qin Yuanzheng turned his head, glanced at her with a smile in his eyes, and said, \"So, you need to eat a bit more tonight, and then we'll extend the battle line, conquering one stronghold after another to ensure the final mission is accomplished.\"","Qiao Lanshu: \"...\"","This was a husband and wife making love, not going to the battlefield to fight a war, Regiment Commander Qin!","Last night, Qiao Lanshu, perhaps afraid of Qin Yuanzheng, used having to work as an excuse to keep him from messing around.","Qin Yuanzheng had just tasted the forbidden fruit, so how could he hold back?","He spent the whole day thinking about his fragrant and soft little wife.","No matter what, he wouldn't be able to hold back tonight.","On the way, he drove and asked, \"How is your work in the pastry workshop? Which shift were you assigned to, and are you adapting well?\"","Qin Yuanzheng felt that since his cousin Yang Wenyan was the factory director, Qiao Lanshu should have been given a relatively easy job after going to the pastry workshop.","Instead, he heard Qiao Lanshu say, \"The pastry workshop isn't good. The workshop supervisor targeted me and assigned me to the deep-frying team to fry dough twists.\"","Qin Yuanzheng immediately stopped the car, turned to look at her with furrowed brows and a dark expression: \"Is that so? I'll go back and find my cousin.\"","How dangerous was the deep-frying team?","What if the oil splashed and burned Comrade Xiao Qiao?","His little wife's skin was fair and lustrous, her face and hands impeccably clean; she absolutely could not be left with scars.","Besides, his cousin was the factory director. What was wrong with pulling some strings for his wife and arranging a leisurely job?","So many people pulled strings; he didn't think there was anything wrong with doing it for his own little wife.","He was starting to get upset over how his cousin handled things.","Qiao Lanshu quickly held him down and said, \"No need! I was in the deep-frying team for less than an hour before they transferred me to the pickled vegetables team. Now I'm responsible for chopping radishes, which is super easy. My colleagues are also very easy to get along with. After these dozen or so days pass and the pickled vegetables are done, I'll be completely free.\"","Qin Yuanzheng: \"...\"","Qin Yuanzheng knew Qiao Lanshu could cook and did it very well.","Chopping radishes was definitely not a problem for her.","Moreover, chopping radishes did sound relatively easy—at least much better than the deep-frying team.","He pulled Qiao Lanshu's hands over, took off her knitted gloves, and inspected her hands over and over again.","Qiao Lanshu was beautiful, and her hands were exceptionally pretty too. Her palms were small, her fingers slender, and her nails a rosy pink. They felt soft and squishy to the touch, as if they had no bones.","Qin Yuanzheng really liked her hands. He gathered both of her hands, wrapped them in his own palms, gently rubbed them, and asked in a low voice, \"Is chopping radishes okay? Will your hands get hurt?\"","Qiao Lanshu shook her head and said, \"Of course not. They don't wear gloves, but I do, so you can rest assured.\"","Qin Yuanzheng was still uneasy. He said, \"I'll go find my cousin tomorrow and ask if there are any other positions available...\"","Qiao Lanshu hurriedly said, \"No need, the way things are now is just fine. You don't need to say any more.\"","Qiao Lanshu remembered that when spring came next year, the machinery factory would deliver a batch of new machines to their factory. By then, the pickled vegetables would be chopped by machines instead of by hand!","The machines would wash and chop. The female workers would only be responsible for tossing the radishes onto the conveyor belt one by one and putting the chopped radish strips into baskets. It would be incredibly easy.","Qiao Lanshu liked this job. It was leisurely, close to home, had good pay and benefits, and she could eat at the cafeteria at noon.","As long as she worked steadily at the food factory for two years, when the college entrance examination resumed in 1977, she could go take it.","Both her parents had gone to university, and she herself had graduated from high school. She was determined to take the college entrance exam.","Qiao Lanshu had her own plans in mind.","Therefore, she said to Qin Yuanzheng, \"Brother Zheng, thank you for considering so much for me. That's why I have such a stable job and life now. You're so good to me.\"","She held Qin Yuanzheng's hand, brought it to her lips for a kiss, and said with a beaming smile, \"I'm so lucky to be able to marry you.\"","Qin Yuanzheng: \"...\"","Qin Yuanzheng swallowed hard, his eyes growing dark and deep.","He suddenly leaned over, held Qiao Lanshu down, and kissed her.","Fiercely.","Qiao Lanshu found it a bit hard to breathe. The corners of her eyes turned red as she begged for mercy, \"Brother Zheng, there are people on the road...\"","Qin Yuanzheng's breathing was somewhat heavy. After a long time, he finally let her go, pressed his fingers against her lips, and whispered, \"Alright, let's go home.\"","Qiao Lanshu felt that Qin Yuanzheng was way too easy to tease.","She didn't feel like she had done anything, so why was he acting so fierce?","Thinking about their first night together, her heart suddenly started pounding a little. She felt she might not be able to handle it.","Qin Yuanzheng also felt he was being a bit impatient.","It was really strange. He wasn't some reckless eighteen or nineteen-year-old kid anymore; he was almost thirty. Why was he still so impulsive and completely unable to hold back?","Whenever he was with Qiao Lanshu, he felt hot inside and his whole body would go numb.","It was as if there was a fire inside his body, rampaging around, looking for a breakthrough point to vent itself out.","As soon as they returned to the residential compound and got out of the car, Qin Yuanzheng grabbed Qiao Lanshu's hand. Without saying a word, he just pulled her along and walked quickly upstairs.","Next door, Huang Erling heard the commotion and guessed that Qiao Lanshu from next door had returned.","The thick mattress, large quilt, and thick winter cotton jacket that Qiao Lanshu had asked her to make were already finished.","She thought she should have Qiao Lanshu come over to quickly take these things back.","However, just as she opened her door, the door next door slammed shut with a bang.","Huang Erling: \"...\"","Huang Erling walked over to the room next door. Just as she raised her hand to knock, she heard the faint, soft sound of Comrade Xiao Qiao begging for mercy from inside. \"Ah, Brother Zheng... Hubby, wait a moment...\"","Huang Erling: \"...\"","Even though Huang Erling was already a mother of two, she still couldn't help but blush.","Covering her mouth to hide a snicker, she thought to herself: As expected of Regiment Commander Qin, he really is fierce.","Comrade Xiao Qiao is definitely in for a rough time."]},{"number":50,"title":"Chapter 50: Taking a Bath Together","paragraphs":["Huang Erling quietly returned to her own room and quietly closed her door.","She was terrified of interrupting the intimate moments of the newlywed couple next door.","She thought to herself, no wonder Commander Qin likes Comrade Xiao Qiao so much.","You have to admit, this little girl from the south really is different. Her voice is soft, her smile is sweet, and most importantly, she is quite good at acting coquettishly.","She either calls him 'brother' or 'hubby'—what man could resist that?","Anyway, Huang Erling thought about it herself. If she were to call Zhao Jiannong 'hubby'...","Huang Erling broke out in goosebumps all over.","Just thinking about it was unbearable, let alone actually saying it out loud!","She might as well call him a blockhead.","Just then, Zhao Jiannong came out of the room and asked her, \"What were you doing outside just now?\"","They hadn't turned on the lights in their house yet; only a single kerosene lamp was lit in the living room.","Huang Erling took off her apron and said, \"Nothing much, I went to cook.\"","Originally, she had planned to take the mattress and other things over once the neighbors returned, but now it seemed better to wait until tomorrow.","Zhao Jiannong muttered, \"Is Commander Qin not back yet? Isn't it way past his off-work time?\"","Huang Erling: \"...\"","Huang Erling rolled her eyes at him. \"You're a grown man, why are you such a gossip!\"","Zhao Jiannong: \"...\"","Wait, he didn't even say anything much, how was that gossiping?","...","Next door, Qin Yuanzheng had been holding back the entire car ride. As soon as they got home, he pinned Qiao Lanshu against the wall and started undressing her himself.","The house had heating, so the moment they opened the door, a wave of warm air rushed over them.","Qin Yuanzheng took off Qiao Lanshu's scarf and then removed her hat.","Then he took off her thick padded winter coat.","Qiao Lanshu's thick, jet-black hair was tied into two thick braids, which were still neat and tidy.","As Qin Yuanzheng pulled her padded coat off, she quickly grabbed his reaching hand and said, \"Brother Zheng, I can take it off myself.\"","Saying this, she hurriedly took off her thick padded pants as well.","This was the inconvenient part about the North. It was too cold outside, so they had to wear a lot of layers.","Going out took over ten minutes just to put on clothes, and coming home meant taking them off piece by piece, which was quite a hassle.","Qiao Lanshu took off her padded clothes and pants, and placed her padded shoes neatly by the door. Crouching there and arranging the shoes, she said to Qin Yuanzheng, \"Brother Zheng, let's get a shoe rack made. We can measure the dimensions and make a six-tier one to hold lots of shoes.\"","Qin Yuanzheng, undressing at the same time, stared at her with deep eyes and nodded. \"Sure, I'll get it done tomorrow.\"","Qiao Lanshu arranged Qin Yuanzheng's shoes together with hers. Qin Yuanzheng wore a size 44, so his military boots were huge, making Qiao Lanshu's size 36 shoes look very petite in comparison.","She placed the two pairs of shoes neatly by the door and stared at them for a few seconds.","She loved seeing her things placed next to Qin Yuanzheng's. It gave her the feeling that everything was in pairs.","Being with the person you love was truly wonderful.","Qin Yuanzheng called out to her, \"Wife, what are you looking at?\"","Qiao Lanshu stood up and said, \"Looking at our shoes. Once we have a shoe rack...\"","She paused. Seeing Qin Yuanzheng stripped down to nothing but a pair of black shorts, her words caught in her throat, and she looked at him with intense shyness.","Qin Yuanzheng had even taken off his undershirt. He walked over and said to Qiao Lanshu, \"We're husband and wife now, what are you still shy about? Didn't we agree on seven times a night? Since it's still early, let's do two rounds first.\"","Two rounds?","Qiao Lanshu was stunned. She said, \"Brother Zheng, we haven't taken a bath yet.\"","Qin Yuanzheng had already slipped off her lightly padded jacket and started lifting her knit sweater, pulling it off in one swift motion to reveal her innermost thermal underwear.","Qin Yuanzheng didn't speak; he just held her and kissed her. Qiao Lanshu went weak all over from his kisses. Blushing, she said, \"Brother Zheng, wait a minute...\"","Qin Yuanzheng's hands slid in under the hem of her clothes.","His technique was like kneading dough.","He whispered in her ear, \"Do you have to take a bath every single day?\"","Qiao Lanshu felt her legs go a bit weak. She nodded and said softly, \"Yes, I have to wash.\"","Qin Yuanzheng ignored her, holding her close while using both his hands and mouth.","He teased his little wife until she was almost in tears before scooping her up in his arms and saying, \"Then let's wash together.\"","Qiao Lanshu: \"...\"","Qin Yuanzheng carried Qiao Lanshu into the kitchen. He was like sticky candy, insisting on staying glued to his little wife.","His voice was a bit hoarse as he set Qiao Lanshu down on a chair and said, \"Wait here, I'll heat some water for you.\"","He filled a pot with water and set it to boil, then opened the window and brought in six cornmeal buns that had been left outside to freeze.","Then, he put millet and water into another small pot, washed and chopped a sweet potato, and tossed it in to cook a pot of sweet potato millet porridge.","The six cornmeal buns were frozen rock hard.","He placed the buns into the millet pot so that by the time the porridge was done, the buns would be ready to eat too.","Qin Yuanzheng worked very quickly. Qiao Lanshu just sat there watching him work. She wanted to help, but Qin Yuanzheng wouldn't let her.","She wanted to leave the room, but he wouldn't let her do that either, insisting she sit there and keep him company.","Qiao Lanshu was wearing only thin pants, and her upper body was stripped down to just a camisole.","Even at home, she rarely dressed this scantily, so she felt a little embarrassed.","As for Qin Yuanzheng, he would turn back to look at her from time to time. His fiery gaze made her feel very shy.","Qin Yuanzheng really wanted to pin her down and have a go right then and there. Such a fragrant, soft little wife, with a great figure and fair skin, wearing nothing but a white camisole—she was simply too tempting.","He really could hardly control himself.","But his wife had said they had to bathe beforehand, otherwise she would feel uncomfortable all over.","What else could he do?","He could only carry his spirited, aroused state around while first cooking the millet porridge, heating up the buns, and boiling the bathwater.","After that, he went to the bathroom and scrubbed clean a large water vat inside.","This large water vat had been sitting in the bathroom ever since they first moved in.","Because tap water wasn't very reliable during these times, every household had the habit of storing water.","This vat was meant for storing water, but now Qin Yuanzheng was using it for their bath.","In this kind of weather, even with indoor heating, taking a bath every day made it easy to catch a cold.","Normally, Qiao Lanshu didn't take a full bath and would just soak her feet, but if they were going to do the deed, a bath was absolutely necessary.","After cleaning the large water vat, Qin Yuanzheng poured the boiling water into it, mixed in cold water, and tested the temperature with his hand. Deeming it just about right, he said to Qiao Lanshu, \"Alright, come take your bath.\"","Qiao Lanshu walked into the bathroom and took a look. The large vat was filled with hot water, and a towel and soap were laid out beside it."]},{"number":51,"title":"Chapter 51: Bathing and Fighting","paragraphs":["Qin Yuanzheng was truly considerate in everything he did, and he really knew how to take care of people.","He wouldn't let Qiao Lanshu lift a finger to do any household chores.","Qiao Lanshu stood at the bathroom door, her eyes sparkling. \"Brother Zheng, you're so smart to think of using this for bathing.\"","Why hadn't she thought of that before?","Both she and Brother Zheng had to work during the day and only came back to eat one meal at night. They actually didn't use much water. Using just one wooden barrel to store water would be more than enough.","The water left over from bathing could be used to flush the toilet, mop the floor, and so on.","Qin Yuanzheng looked at Qiao Lanshu. The young woman was wearing only a camisole. She had curves in all the right places, and her figure was beautifully voluptuous.","This kind of subtle reveal was the most alluring.","He was originally going to head back to the kitchen, but upon seeing Qiao Lanshu standing at the door, he couldn't help but pin her down and kiss her for a long time.","His hands weren't behaving, either.","His dough-kneading technique was becoming increasingly masterful.","More than ten minutes later, he finally let go of Qiao Lanshu and said, \"You go in and soak first. I'll be right there.\"","He pinched her earlobe and added, \"Wait for me inside.\"","Blushing, Qiao Lanshu went in to take her bath.","Qin Yuanzheng hurried back to the kitchen and checked on the millet porridge. It had been boiling for about twenty minutes and was just about done. He turned off the heat and let the porridge simmer in the pot.","Then, he turned and went to the bathroom, closing the door behind him.","Inside the cramped bathroom, Qiao Lanshu had just taken off her clothes and was carefully stepping on a stool to climb into the water vat.","As soon as the large-framed Qin Yuanzheng entered, the bathroom instantly felt a bit crowded.","The moment he saw Qiao Lanshu, his eyes darkened. He strode over and suddenly scooped up the petite Qiao Lanshu in his arms.","Qiao Lanshu let out a soft gasp and cried, \"Brother Zheng, put me down quickly.\"","Qin Yuanzheng said in a low voice, \"Why aren't you calling me Hubby anymore?\"","For some unknown reason, Qin Yuanzheng was extremely fixated on this term of endearment.","He would demand she say it from time to time.","Qiao Lanshu was willing to humor him. She wanted to captivate Qin Yuanzheng so much that he would be entirely infatuated with her, preferably head over heels, unable to live without her in the future.","Qiao Lanshu wrapped her arms around his neck and whispered, \"Hubby, put me down quickly.\"","Qin Yuanzheng held her, and the two of them entered the large water vat together.","This vat was actually more suitable for one person to bathe in; it was still too cramped for two.","But Qin Yuanzheng insisted on squeezing in with her.","Blushing, Qiao Lanshu said, \"Brother Zheng, isn't it too crowded?\"","Qin Yuanzheng said without batting an eye, \"It's not crowded. I think it's just right.\"","With that, he got into the vat first, sat down, and then had Qiao Lanshu sit on his lap with her back to him.","Qin Yuanzheng wrapped his arms around her and whispered in her ear, \"See? Isn't this just right?\"","Qiao Lanshu: \"...\"","Qin Yuanzheng held a washcloth in one hand to scrub Qiao Lanshu, while his other hand was submerged in the water, doing who-knows-what.","Qiao Lanshu's face flushed so red it looked like it might bleed. Calling him brother or hubby was of no use.","Qin Yuanzheng even said with a straight face, \"Didn't you say we have to bathe before we can be intimate? I'm helping you wash a bit cleaner. Be a good girl and don't squirm.\"","Qiao Lanshu: \"...\"","***********","Their bath took nearly an hour.","If it weren't for the water temperature dropping and Qin Yuanzheng worrying that Comrade Xiao Qiao might catch a cold, he wouldn't have wanted to get up at all.","Not to mention, this large water vat was quite useful. He felt it was great and was already pondering buying an even larger one next time.","During this bath, Qiao Lanshu was washed thoroughly clean from the inside out.","Qin Yuanzheng had personally bathed her. Except for her hair, every part of her had been meticulously scrubbed.","Ensuring that Qiao Lanshu wouldn't dare utter the words \"not clean\" ever again.","After the bath, Qin Yuanzheng wrapped Qiao Lanshu in a large towel, placed her on the small sofa, and said, \"Have some sweet potato and millet porridge. Do you want to eat a cornmeal steamed bun?\"","Exhausted, Qiao Lanshu lay paralyzed on the sofa. Wrapped in the towel blanket, her entire body was flushed with a pink hue. She whispered, \"Yes, I'm so hungry.\"","Qin Yuanzheng looked at her with a smile and deliberately teased, \"With so much just now, are you still not full?\"","Qiao Lanshu: \"...\"","Qiao Lanshu rolled over and ignored him.","With a smile on his face, Qin Yuanzheng reached out and rubbed Qiao Lanshu's head. His affectionate eyes were full of tender love for his little wife.","He casually pulled on a pair of shorts, then went to ladle out the sweet potato and millet porridge. He placed six cornmeal steamed buns on a plate, carried them out, and set them on the low table in front of the sofa.","Then, he tied on an apron and began cooking in quite a good mood.","First, he shredded a potato and stir-fried it with scallions and vinegar. Then, he sliced two of the sausages Qiao Lanshu had brought over and used them to scramble some eggs.","The two dishes were very simple, and it only took him half an hour to finish cooking them.","Then he brought them out and said, \"Comrade Xiao Qiao, get up and eat.\"","He took off his apron, came over, and picked up Qiao Lanshu, making her sit next to him as they ate together.","Qiao Lanshu didn't have a big appetite. She only had a bowl of porridge, half a steamed bun, and a little bit of the scrambled eggs.","The rest all went into Qin Yuanzheng's stomach.","He polished off the food completely and went to wash the pots and dishes.","Qiao Lanshu lay on the sofa, feeling drowsy.","Looking at Qiao Lanshu, Qin Yuanzheng wondered if he should find some books for his wife so she could read when she had nothing to do.","Oh, right. Since they got married, he hadn't bought a radio yet.","He could buy one for Comrade Xiao Qiao to listen to for fun.","Qiao Lanshu was almost asleep when Qin Yuanzheng picked her up, carried her back to the bedroom, and put her on the kang bed. He said to her with a serious face, \"Wife, the revolution has not yet succeeded, and comrades still need to work hard. We've only just occupied two strongholds, and there are still seven left unoccupied. It won't do for you to tap out now.\"","Qiao Lanshu: \"...\"","Over the course of the night, Qiao Lanshu truly paid the price for her big talk.","Commander Qin dragged her into fighting battles all night long. After every battle, he would report the combat results to her.","It wasn't until they had occupied seven strongholds and perfectly completed the mission that Commander Qin finally announced in her ear, \"The war has been won. Comrade Xiao Qiao performed well tonight. I'm going to reward you with a first-class merit.\"","Dazed and confused, Qiao Lanshu wondered what the reward could be.","Then, she felt Qin Yuanzheng's broad, warm hand press against her stomach, saying that she had been injured in battle and her stomach had gotten chubby, so he was going to give her a slimming and restorative massage.","Qiao Lanshu: \"???\"","If Qiao Lanshu hadn't been completely drained of energy, she would have kicked him right then and there, sending him straight to the floor."]},{"number":52,"title":"Chapter 52: The Newlyweds Who Are Sticky Sweet","paragraphs":["Qin Yuanzheng had been fighting battles with his little wife all night. He wasn't tired at all; instead, his whole body felt incredibly relaxed.","Perhaps it was because he had restrained himself for too long before, so now that he had finally released it, his entire state of being was completely different.","Qiao Lanshu, on the other hand, really suffered. Married to a husband as vigorous as a wild bull, she truly had no way out.","Qin Yuanzheng got onto the kang, slipped under the covers, turned on his side, and pulled his sleeping little wife into his arms.","In the dim light, he looked at Qiao Lanshu with deep affection. He reached out to smooth her hair and couldn't resist pressing a finger against her slightly swollen lips.","It seemed Qiao Lanshu was truly exhausted. No matter what he did, she didn't react at all.","Qiao Lanshu had fair skin, and even the slightest pressure would leave pink marks on it.","Needless to say, there were marks all over her now.","Qin Yuanzheng gently massaged her stomach while kissing her cheek.","Early the next morning, Qin Yuanzheng was the first to wake up. He got dressed and went downstairs to run over a dozen laps around the neighborhood.","Afterward, he went to a nearby state-run restaurant and bought two bowls of jellied tofu and three fried dough cakes. On his way back, he passed by some older women chatting. He caught a snippet of their conversation, hearing that since winter had arrived, the supply and marketing cooperative had a supply of mutton these past few days. Everyone was rushing to buy it, and it was apparently rationed.","Qin Yuanzheng immediately turned around and hurried to the meat counter inside the supply and marketing cooperative, where he indeed saw fresh mutton.","Here in the north, people mainly ate mutton. It was fresh and relatively cheap, costing about 80 cents a catty, while pork was around 85 cents a catty.","Qin Yuanzheng had some meat ration coupons on hand. He figured Qiao Lanshu might prefer pork fat, considering mutton could have a strong gamy smell.","So, he bought one catty of pork fat and two catties of mutton.","Meat was currently rationed and in short supply. Many people would only bear to buy and eat meat during the New Year.","Mutton hadn't been available for quite a while either. The recent supply was because winter had set in and it had snowed, prompting the pastoral areas to slaughter a batch of sheep.","Having bought the mutton and pork fat, Qin Yuanzheng hurried back home with the items in hand.","It was already seven in the morning. He needed to quickly bring the breakfast back, and after eating, drop his little wife off at the food factory for work.","He also planned to ask his cousin, Yang Wenyan, if there were any other jobs available at the factory.","He still didn't feel at ease letting Qiao Lanshu do the vegetable cutting job.","Carrying the meat, jellied tofu, and other items, Qin Yuanzheng ran into Battalion Commander Zhao Jiannong in the stairwell just as he was heading out.","Zhao Jiannong was fully dressed and ready to head to work at the southern suburbs forestry farm under his jurisdiction.","The military canteen provided breakfast, so Zhao Jiannong never ate at home, saving the food for his wife and children.","Seeing Qin Yuanzheng returning, he asked in surprise, Regiment Commander Qin, where did you go so early in the morning?","As he spoke, he caught sight of the breakfast in Qin Yuanzheng's hand and looked even more shocked.","He said, Hey, hey, hold on, Regiment Commander Qin, did you go out to buy breakfast?","He deliberately teased Qin Yuanzheng, And you bought two portions? Is one of them for me? I just so happen to not have eaten yet.","Qin Yuanzheng: ...","Without missing a beat or slowing his steps, Qin Yuanzheng replied, Get lost and go eat at your base.","With that, he took the stairs three at a time and disappeared in the blink of an eye.","Zhao Jiannong looked at his retreating back, smiling and shaking his head. Strange, how truly strange.","No wonder many elders said that when a man was unsettled, he just needed to marry a wife and he would settle down.","Look at Regiment Commander Qin, he was already completely wrapped around his little wife's finger.","Returning home, Qin Yuanzheng found the house quiet. It seemed Qiao Lanshu wasn't up yet.","Qiao Lanshu had to be at the food factory by eight o'clock. Although the factory wasn't far from their neighborhood, and it would take Qin Yuanzheng less than ten minutes to drive her there.","Still, she needed to get up early to eat breakfast. She couldn't go to work on an empty stomach, could she?","Qin Yuanzheng poured the two portions of jellied tofu into bowls and then walked into the master bedroom, finding Qiao Lanshu already sitting up and yawning.","With her hair draped over her shoulders, she sat on the kang. The marks on her fair arms looked even more conspicuous. It was only upon waking up that she realized she wasn't wearing anything at all.","She really didn't know what to say. She clearly remembered going to sleep wearing a little tank top last night.","How did she wake up without it?","She put the tank top back on and pulled a warm base layer over her head. Just then, she saw the bedroom door open as Qin Yuanzheng walked in.","Seeing her getting dressed, Qin Yuanzheng immediately walked over, gently pulled out the hair caught under her collar, and asked in a low voice, How are you feeling? Are you still sleepy?","Qiao Lanshu yawned and said, Mostly just too tired, and my lower back is so sore.","Actually, her stomach was also a bit uncomfortable, feeling bloated and achy.","After fixing her hair, Qin Yuanzheng didn't pull his hand back. Instead, his rough, warm hand gently squeezed the back of her neck.","This spot was Qiao Lanshu's most ticklish area. She immediately shrank her neck, trying to dodge Qin Yuanzheng's hand. Brother Zheng, stop it.","The more she protested, the more reluctant Qin Yuanzheng was to let go.","He didn't know why, but Qin Yuanzheng always felt like Qiao Lanshu's words sounded like she was acting coy.","Her voice was soft and sweet as she told him to stop.","How could he possibly resist?","Besides, he was only squeezing her neck, not anywhere else...","Seeing the look in Qin Yuanzheng's eyes, Qiao Lanshu truly conceded defeat.","She quickly begged for mercy, Alright, Brother Zheng, you really have to stop. I still have to go to work.","Qin Yuanzheng: ...","Looking somewhat disappointed, Qin Yuanzheng withdrew his hand and said, Alright.","No wonder his comrades would immediately ask for leave and refuse to go to work whenever their families came to visit.","He hadn't understood it before, but now, he understood it far too profoundly.","Right now, all he wanted was to stick with his little wife day and night, without going anywhere.","He brought over Qiao Lanshu's clothes and said, Let me help you put them on.","Qiao Lanshu: ...","Once again, Qiao Lanshu felt that her decision to go to work was incredibly wise.","If she stayed at home every day, wouldn't Brother Zheng put all his energy into tormenting her?","She truly wouldn't be able to handle it.","After breakfast, Qin Yuanzheng drove Qiao Lanshu to the food factory.","Qiao Lanshu's job today was still cutting radishes.","She actually quite enjoyed cutting radishes; it was a very stress-relieving task.","A few people would sit there, using knives to cut the radishes into strips, then place them on a conveyor belt to be dried before handing them over to the pickling team workers for preservation.","Qiao Lanshu had fought seven battles last night, and her lower back was still a bit sore. Fortunately, her current body was very young. How should she put it? It was resilient.","She recovered fairly quickly.","After sitting and cutting radishes for a while, she didn't feel as uncomfortable anymore.","After dropping her off at the food factory, Qin Yuanzheng didn't leave right away. He headed straight to the factory director's office to find his cousin."]},{"number":53,"title":"Chapter 53: Arrange a Leisurely Job for My Wife","paragraphs":["Yang Wenyan was still busy dealing with the aftermath of Sun Mingyong's mess.","Sun Mingyong was truly a cancer to the food factory. Just because of him, the entire factory had to spend days writing self-criticisms and reflecting on their mistakes.","As the factory manager, Yang Wenyan bore the brunt of it. Over the past few days, he had to run to the Industrial Bureau several times just to attend meetings and cooperate with inspections.","Now that the worst had finally passed, he could focus on his work at the factory in peace, so he called Wei Zhengye back to resume working.","Wei Zhengye was a director at the factory. Simply put, he acted as the manager's assistant, helping Yang Wenyan manage the food factory.","Without his help, it really would be impossible to manage everything.","When Qin Yuanzheng arrived, Wei Zhengye and Yang Wenyan were in the middle of a meeting, having gathered all the workshop supervisors.","The main purpose was for Yang Wenyan to convey the higher-ups' directives, urging everyone to be more careful in their daily work and to manage the people in their respective workshops well. If anyone wanted to introduce a new hire, they had to thoroughly investigate the person's background, or else he wouldn't sign off on it.","During the meeting, Liu Weihong spoke up: \"Manager, the reason Sun Mingyong was able to deceive Director Wei was because his hometown was too far away for us to investigate properly, right? This is a cautionary tale. Why did our factory hire someone from the south again? When you signed the paperwork, did you ask about her background? Let's hope she isn't another fraud.\"","Liu Weihong was still holding a grudge after being mocked by Qiao Lanshu after work yesterday.","Did Qiao Lanshu really think that just because she transferred to the pickles workshop, she, Liu Weihong, couldn't control her anymore?","Hmph, just wait and see.","Hearing this, Yang Wenyan scoffed coldly. He first gave Wei Zhengye a strange look before speaking: \"I know exactly what her background is. I'm the one who recommended her. Do I need you to remind me?\"","Liu Weihong: \"...\"","Yang Wenyan continued, \"Your pastry workshop has increased production recently, and the workload is heavy. As the supervisor, you need to stay alert and manage things strictly! It's almost the end of the year, and we absolutely cannot afford any mistakes! Pay more attention during work hours. If the workers haven't all left, the supervisor shouldn't leave first. You have to wait until everyone is gone, patrol the workshop once more, and check all the food and equipment before you can get off work. Understood?\"","Liu Weihong: \"...\"","Liu Weihong, who was always the first to leave the moment her shift ended, blushed bright red from the manager's criticism.","She lowered her head and said, \"I understand, Manager.\"","Although Liu Weihong said she understood, she was still unconvinced in her heart.","She thought to herself: So that Little Troll from the south is Manager Yang Wenyan's person. No wonder she dared to scold her after work.","During this meeting, the manager didn't scold anyone else, only her. It must be because that Little Troll secretly complained behind her back, right?","Liu Weihong's face darkened as she silently cursed Qiao Lanshu in her heart.","After the meeting ended, the group came out of the office and saw the tall and imposing Qin Yuanzheng standing by the window in the corridor.","The group curiously cast several glances at Qin Yuanzheng.","There were several military units stationed nearby, so soldiers were actually quite common.","However, such a tall, handsome, and young military officer was not a common sight.","Several female supervisors secretly stared at Qin Yuanzheng, whispering among themselves.","Wei Zhengye also looked at Qin Yuanzheng a few times and asked Liu Weihong, \"Supervisor Liu, do you know that officer?\"","Liu Weihong sneered, \"Who doesn't know him? He is the famous Commander Qin.\"","Wei Zhengye: \"...\"","Liu Weihong added, \"You probably don't know yet, but Commander Qin recently got married. He married a Southern Shorty, and that shorty even came to work at our factory. Oh, right, I heard that shorty was originally your son-in-law's fiancée. She came here looking for her husband, found out she was deceived, and turned around to marry the officer instead.\"","Wei Zhengye: \"...\"","Wei Zhengye looked absolutely shocked. Lately, he had been busy settling his daughter and grandson, dealing with his own work, and handling the fact that before Sun Mingyong was sent to a labor camp, he had borrowed money left and right, leaving behind over a thousand in debt. Recently, the debt collectors had even found their way to Wei Zhengye.","Wei Zhengye had been so overwhelmed that he really hadn't heard anything about this matter.","He stood there with a hesitant expression and looked back at Qin Yuanzheng again.","He saw that Qin Yuanzheng had already entered the factory manager's office and closed the door.","Wei Zhengye thought to himself: That southern girl actually didn't leave and even married a military officer.","She probably had some schemes and boldness; it seemed she couldn't be underestimated.","Wei Zhengye thought this, but soon pushed it out of his mind.","Sun Mingyong owed over one thousand three hundred in debt, borrowed from colleagues, friends, and people from partner units.","Now that he had gone to the labor camp, all these debts were piled onto Wei Zhengye.","Wei Zhengye was afraid those people would come to the factory to make a scene. If they ended up making him lose his job, then he, his daughter, and his grandson would have to survive on eating snow.","Therefore, Wei Zhengye pondered in his heart that he had to find a way to get some money.","But in times like these, everyone's wages and ration coupons were fixed. Where could he possibly go to get money?","...","Qin Yuanzheng came to Yang Wenyan's office. Seeing him, Yang Wenyan said in surprise, \"Yuanzheng? What brings you here?\"","Qin Yuanzheng rarely came to the factory to look for him. His sudden arrival must mean there was something important.","Yang Wenyan immediately stood up and asked worriedly, \"Did something happen?\"","Qin Yuanzheng also had a serious expression. He sat opposite Yang Wenyan and said very solemnly, \"Cousin, I came to ask you if you could transfer my wife to a lighter position?\"","Yang Wenyan was stunned: \"Isn't she making bread in the pastry workshop?\"","That was already quite a light job, wasn't it?","Yang Wenyan had been too busy lately. He had only said a quick word to the clerk in the personnel department without being too explicit. He just personally handed over Qiao Lanshu's documents and said, \"This girl is from my family, see to it that she's assigned a position.\"","Since he had put it like that, if the personnel department still didn't know what to do, it would be quite senseless.","Hearing him say this, Qin Yuanzheng was also a bit surprised. He said, \"Comrade Xiao Qiao is not in the pastry workshop. She was first transferred to the frying team to fry dough twists, and then she was transferred to the pickles team to chop radishes. I'm worried she'll cut her hands, and my heart would ache if that happens.\"","Yang Wenyan: \"...\"","Yang Wenyan's face darkened, and he said, \"Isn't this just messing around? The people in the frying team are either old workers skilled at making pastries or strong male workers. How could they assign a little girl like her over there?\"","There were no machines to make fried dough twists yet; they still had to be made manually.","A southerner, a girl who had never even kneaded flour, and they made her make fried dough twists?","It would make more sense to let her just eat them.","Yang Wenyan had a gloomy face, his head throbbing with anger. \"This Liu Weihong is really acting out of line. Recently, the pastry workshop has increased production. To avoid overtime and complete the tasks before the end of the year, everyone is working their lives away. By assigning workers like this, isn't she just holding back the experienced workers and lowering production?\"","Qin Yuanzheng dismissed the thought and simply said, \"Cousin, could you check if there are any lighter jobs available in the factory? If it is convenient, please keep an eye out for her. If it is too much trouble, do not force it. Comrade Xiao Qiao told me she actually enjoys cutting radishes.\"","Although Qin Yuanzheng himself could not fathom what was so appealing about slicing radishes.","Yang Wenyan thought for a moment before replying:","\"At the moment, all the positions in the factory are indeed full. Only the workshops that are scaling up production need extra hands. But there will definitely be opportunities, though we will have to wait until after the New Year, once the annual personnel changes are announced, to know for sure.","\"Do not worry, I will keep a lookout for you. The pickled vegetable workshop is fairly laid-back anyway. In about ten days, the workload will pretty much dry up. It might be best to let her stay there for now; it is actually much better than being in the other workshops.\"","Yang Wenyan felt that Liu Weihong was completely clueless and out of line. He needed to go have a talk with Liu Weihong and get to the bottom of what was really going on.","If another mess occurred, how could he possibly maintain his position as the factory director?"]},{"number":54,"title":"Chapter 54: Commander Qin, Is He Really Competent","paragraphs":["After Qin Yuanzheng left, Yang Wenyan immediately had someone call Liu Weihong over.","Liu Weihong had just been criticized during the meeting, so being called over again made her a bit unhappy.","Liu Weihong entered the factory manager's office and said, \"Manager, what do you need me for this time? I'm still busy.\"","Yang Wenyan looked at Liu Weihong, feeling quite a headache.","Previously, when the pastry workshop needed to promote a supervisor, he had wanted to promote the experienced master of the workshop, Lao Hu.","Instead, Liu Weihong used her connections to take the spot.","Liu Weihong did have some backing. Her father was the director of the personnel department in a subordinate county. Although it was just at the county level, the personnel department held significant power, and her father had some connections in the city.","Anyway, Liu Weihong had worked in the pastry workshop for quite a few years. Her performance wasn't outstanding, but it was acceptable enough, so he let the promotion slide.","As long as she did her job properly, Yang Wenyan couldn't be bothered to micromanage her.","But now, he had to ask her, \"Yesterday, the personnel department assigned three temporary workers to the pastry workshop. How did you arrange their work?\"","Liu Weihong: \"...\"","So it was about this. She knew that shorty must have complained.","However, she felt perfectly justified and said:","\"Manager, our frying team is short on people. I originally wanted to put her in the frying team, but later, seeing what a frail little girl she was, I thought it would be too hard for her. So I sent her to the pickled vegetables workshop. The people in the pickled vegetables workshop have it so easy. I treated her well enough, didn't I? That was all for your sake; I wouldn't bother with anyone else.\"","Yang Wenyan: \"...\"","Yang Wenyan's face darkened. He said coldly, \"The personnel department specifically assigned a male comrade to you. Why didn't you let the male comrade go? Liu Weihong, you know very well how you became a supervisor. Work is work. Stop playing these little games with me, understand?\"","Being reprimanded by Yang Wenyan like this, Liu Weihong felt a bit intimidated.","But she still tried to defend herself, saying:","\"Manager, yes, I did use connections back then, but Brother Hu didn't get promoted for his own reasons too, right? His temper is so awful that he scolds and drives away three or four apprentices a month. Who would want to work under him?","If we weren't really short of people, would I have assigned a girl to him? I just thought that if a little girl went over, he probably wouldn't scold her as harshly. Look, the male comrade who was transferred there yesterday got scolded by him all day again. It's hard to say if he'll even be able to keep working today.\"","Yang Wenyan: \"...\"","Although Liu Weihong was making excuses, what she said was indeed the truth.","Brother Hu simply had a bad temper and spoke bluntly. Whenever he saw someone clumsy, he would yell at them.","Yang Wenyan looked at Liu Weihong and said, \"This matter ends here. Do your job well. It's the end of the year, so don't cause any more trouble for me, do you hear me?\"","Liu Weihong: \"I know, I know.\"","She hurriedly left the factory manager's office and let out a long sigh of relief.","She thought to herself that it was fortunate Director Wei had asked her for a quota, which led her to transfer Qiao Lanshu away. Otherwise, her original intention was to just let Qiao Lanshu stay in the frying team frying dough twists forever.","Right, speaking of Director Wei, his daughter Wei Hongmei also came to the pastry workshop yesterday. Liu Weihong had arranged for her to go to the leisurely bread workshop, and she wondered how she was doing.","Liu Weihong didn't dare make any mistakes at work, especially since Manager Yang had repeatedly warned her.","Muttering to herself, she hurried to the bread workshop to take a look.","Wei Hongmei had been assigned to the bread workshop, originally in the packaging team, which involved packing the bread. It was such an easy job; others would fight tooth and nail to get such a good position.","But even with such a simple job, she managed to mess it up.","Yesterday afternoon, she packed perhaps not even ten loaves of bread, yet she somehow managed to crush four of them. The team leader of the bread team was furious with her but didn't dare to lash out because she was Director Wei's daughter.","So they reassigned her to the fermentation room to monitor the temperature.","Liu Weihong came over, took a walk around the workshop, asked a few questions, and then went to check the fermentation room. The fermentation of the dough required two people to monitor, so even if Wei Hongmei slacked off, there was someone else to keep an eye on things. This job was easy and the least likely to go wrong.","Liu Weihong immediately felt relieved and didn't bother with Wei Hongmei any further.","...","Meanwhile, over in the pickled vegetables workshop, Qiao Lanshu was truly getting addicted to chopping radishes. Every day when she went to work, she would change into her protective suit, put on her hat, mask, and gloves, pull up a stool to sit down, and start chopping radishes.","Qiao Lanshu and Wang Xue were in the same group. The two sat facing each other, chopping together, and could chop hundreds of pounds of radishes in a single morning.","Wang Xue had a cheerful personality and loved to talk. The two of them chatted while they chopped, and the morning passed quickly.","While chopping radishes, Wang Xue whispered to Qiao Lanshu, \"Xiao Qiao, weren't you in the pastry workshop before? Being suddenly transferred here, were you pushed out by someone?\"","Wang Xue had a knowing look on her face and said, \"I heard all about it. As soon as you came over here, that Wei Hongmei went over there.\"","Originally, Wang Xue's partner was Wei Hongmei, but Wei Hongmei refused to do the work and ran off. That morning, Wang Xue had to do all the work by herself, and she remembered it well.","Qiao Lanshu smiled and nodded. \"Yes, I was frying dough twists over there before.\"","Wang Xue scoffed coldly and said, \"Is Director Liu out of her mind, making a little girl like you fry dough twists... Oh, right, I heard something.\"","She leaned in mysteriously and smiled, \"As soon as Wei Hongmei went to the packaging team, she ruined several loaves of bread. The matter was hushed up; they just made her pay for them and then transferred her to an even easier job, watching the fermentation room.\"","Currently, in the food factories around Longcheng City, due to limitations in processing technology, people still preferred eating steamed buns, momo, flatbreads, and the like.","The prices for those were also relatively cheaper.","But bread was also supplied, specifically the pillow bread currently made by the food factory. The ingredients were simple: wheat flour, eggs, yeast, and sugar.","Once baked, the pillow bread was wrapped in greaseproof paper, placed in baskets, and delivered to major state-owned restaurants, supply and marketing cooperatives, as well as the cafeterias of certain work units.","Pillow bread was very expensive. A four-tael loaf of bread sold for twenty-five cents. You have to understand, at this time, a pound of potatoes was only four cents.","Precisely because it was expensive and produced in scarce quantities, pillow bread was considered a luxury item for ordinary people to improve their lives during holidays and the New Year, holding a status on par with canned goods.","As a result, as soon as Wei Hongmei started working, she ruined four of them.","She had to pay a whole dollar in compensation right away.","Even though Liu Weihong and the others tried to suppress the matter and keep it from spreading out of fear of being held accountable.","But the factory was only so big, and everyone were veteran employees who had worked there for years. They were all familiar with each other, so who could they really hide it from?","Wang Xue gloated, \"I'm just waiting to see her make a mistake. It'll be hilarious when it happens.\"","Qiao Lanshu knew that Wei Hongmei was Sun Mingyong's wife, and the two even had a child together.","However, Qiao Lanshu felt that Sun Mingyong was a fraud who had tricked people into marriage, and Wei Hongmei had likely been deceived by him as well. Because of this, she didn't hold any prejudice against Wei Hongmei.","She merely gossiped in a hushed voice, \"Isn't Wei Hongmei's father the director of our factory? I bet he will cover for him, right?\"","Wang Xue scoffed, \"Let him try! We'll see if he has enough money to cover this mess! Before Sun Mingyong left, he saddled them with over a thousand in unpaid debt. Oh, this family is going to put on quite a show for everyone.\"","Qiao Lanshu: \"...\"","As Wang Xue continued chatting, the topic eventually drifted back to Qin Yuanzheng. She winked at Qiao Lanshu and whispered, \"Hey, Comrade Xiao Qiao, tell me the truth. That Commander Qin... is he actually capable?\""]},{"number":55,"title":"Chapter 55: Lost My Mind, My Body Has a Mind of Its Own","paragraphs":["Wang Xue had become familiar with Qiao Lanshu. Plus, she was a straightforward person who said whatever was on her mind and couldn't hold back her words, which was why she dared to ask.","Had it been anyone else, they might not have had the nerve to ask.","After Liu Weihong returned from her blind date with Qin Yuanzheng, she had accidentally misspoken several times while chatting with others, saying things like Commander Qin was tall and strong, but actually impotent in that regard, and that Commander Qin was infertile, so marrying him would be like living as a widow.","In short, these words spread throughout the food factory, and everyone actually believed that Qin Yuanzheng was impotent.","After all, if the man was really capable, how could he resist finding a wife?","Just look at those unmarried young men; they couldn't even walk straight when they saw a young wife, and they would eagerly rush over at the mere mention of a blind date. Which of them could do without a woman?","Qiao Lanshu's face turned bright red at Wang Xue's question. She lowered her head, carefully dicing the radish, and nodded as she cut, saying, He is alright.","Looking at her expression, what else was there for Wang Xue not to understand?","She was an experienced woman herself, with children already in school. As soon as she saw Qiao Lanshu's little expression, she was amused. Oh my, that Liu Weihong really is a case of sour grapes! A lot of people actually believed her nonsense before.","Blushing, Qiao Lanshu thought of the scenes when she was with Qin Yuanzheng.","Setting everything else aside, just talking about those seven times last night, she had passed out twice.","Even now, her waist and stomach still felt a bit uncomfortable. How was he impotent?","He was far too capable.","When work ended at noon, Deng Xiaozhen's younger brother, Deng Weijun, also came over to see Qiao Lanshu.","Deng Weijun worked firing the boiler in the brewing workshop, which happened to be right next to the pickle workshop.","When he got off work to eat at the cafeteria, he came over to see Qiao Lanshu and asked, Sister-in-law, are you getting used to it here? No one is bullying you, right?","Wang Xue rolled her eyes at him and said, Comrade Xiao Qiao is in my group. Do you not know my character? Would I bully her?","Deng Weijun was a smooth talker. He immediately pulled out a few bright red hawthorns from his pants pocket and said enthusiastically, Oh, I was wondering who it was! So it is our Master Wang. With you looking out for my sister-in-law, I can rest completely easy. Come on, here, this is a little token of my respect for you. Please continue to take good care of my sister-in-law in the future.","Wang Xue spat playfully and said, She is a military officer's family member and a relative of the factory director. Looking out for their sake is enough; why would I need to do it for you? Hurry up and cool off somewhere else. With such a glib tongue, be careful you do not end up unable to find a wife.","Deng Weijun greeted Qiao Lanshu with a grin, placed a pear down next to her, and whispered, Sister-in-law, my sister gave this to me. I am giving you one, it is really sweet.","Pointing at him, Wang Xue said to Qiao Lanshu, Oh, just look at this scoundrel! He gives me hawthorns, but gives you a pear. If he dares to come around next time, I will definitely give him a beating.","Qiao Lanshu: ...","Smiling, Qiao Lanshu handed the pear to Wang Xue and said, Master Wang, you eat it. I have some at home too.","Wang Xue was only joking; how could she actually take Qiao Lanshu's pear? She waved her hand and said, No, no, you keep it and eat it. Gain a little weight so you can give our Commander Qin a big, chubby boy next year.","Qiao Lanshu: ...","Wang Xue suddenly realized she had misspoken. She reached out, lightly slapped her own mouth, and said somewhat embarrassedly, Um, Xiao Qiao? Did you guys go for a premarital checkup before you got married?","She was not sure if Qiao Lanshu knew about Qin Yuanzheng's infertility, and she did not dare to say it outright.","Qiao Lanshu shook her head. No. We like each other, so we did not consider anything else.","Her words were already very clear, so Wang Xue dropped the subject.","She just felt it was a pity in her heart. Looking at Comrade Xiao Qiao and Commander Qin, they were truly a handsome man and a beautiful woman, a perfect match.","If they could have children, who knows how good-looking they would be.","...","When it was time to get off work, Qin Yuanzheng came to pick up Qiao Lanshu again.","He arrived early every day just so he could pick up his little wife the moment she finished.","However, he had to go to work tomorrow as well, so he might not be able to come so punctually then.","Thinking about how his wife would have to ride her bicycle in such cold weather, braving the freezing wind to get home, Qin Yuanzheng's heart ached for her.","Fortunately, the food factory was not too far. He would pay closer attention to the time in the future and try to pick her up as early as possible.","When Qiao Lanshu's figure emerged from the food factory, Qin Yuanzheng's heart burned with passion.","He felt he was truly sick.","It was as if the effects of that medicine had remained in his body, making his desires skyrocket.","It was fine when he did not see his little wife.","But the moment he saw her now, the fire inside him went whoosh and started burning fiercely again.","Sitting in the car, watching Qiao Lanshu walk toward him, he tugged at his pants somewhat unnaturally.","Why did he feel like his pants had gotten smaller? Why were they so tight? It was strangely constricting.","He could not help but let his mind wander again. With a big build like his, big hands and big feet, that thing was also...","This size was a very poor match for Comrade Xiao Qiao.","Yet every time they exercised, he still liked to...","Comrade Xiao Qiao had said last night that she would not do it like that with him anymore.","If not like that, then how were they going to do it tonight?","Eating half and leaving half, how could he bear that.","Qin Yuanzheng tugged at his pants again, feeling somewhat uncomfortable.","He got out of the car. Blown by the freezing wind, his mind did not clear up; instead, it grew even more muddled.","Qiao Lanshu had already run up to him with a smile. She tilted her head up to look at him, her eyes sparkling. Brother Zheng, you came to pick me up again? You are so good to me.","Qin Yuanzheng: ...","Qin Yuanzheng held himself back from hugging and kissing her on the spot.","He rubbed her head and said, Are you cold? Get in the car first.","Although there was no heating in the car, it was at least an enclosed space where she would not have to face the cold wind, and the temperature was not as low.","Qiao Lanshu nodded, quickly opening the car door and slipping inside.","Qin Yuanzheng also hurried into the car. Looking at Comrade Xiao Qiao's pure and innocent smiling face, he felt like an absolute beast.","He clearly never had these kinds of thoughts before; he used to be very indifferent.","Why was he acting like he was possessed lately? Logically, he told himself he needed to exercise restraint. Comrade Xiao Qiao was young, and given the massive difference in their physical sizes, her body would not be able to handle it.","But the moment he held Comrade Xiao Qiao in his arms and gave her a couple of kisses, he lost all reason, and his body started to have a mind of its own.","By the time he came back to his senses, it had already been one, two, three, four, five, six, seven times.","Sitting in the car, Qin Yuanzheng sighed silently.","Qiao Lanshu adjusted her scarf. Seeing him sigh, she asked in confusion, Brother Zheng, what is wrong?","Qin Yuanzheng coughed and adjusted his sitting posture, saying, Nothing. It is just that my pants have gotten a bit small, and they feel a bit tight.","Qiao Lanshu did not think much of it and replied, Then how about we take them to Sister Ling next door and ask her to alter them for you?","Qin Yuanzheng: \"...\"","Qin Yuanzheng shook his head. \"No need, forget it. Let's just go home first.\"","With that, he started the car, ready to leave.","However, a security guard from the food factory suddenly came over and knocked on the car door.","Qin Yuanzheng opened the door and asked, \"What is it?\"","Thinking the guard was looking for her, Qiao Lanshu leaned over, resting her head against Qin Yuanzheng's arm to look out the window.","The guard saluted Qin Yuanzheng before speaking. \"Commander Qin, here is the situation. The police station just called the factory to say that a few of our workers have been arrested on suspicion of harassing women. One of them, named Deng Weijun, is your relative, right? Could you please notify his family to hurry over and bail him out?\"","In this day and age, harassing women could lead to a sentence in a labor camp.","However, since the guard specifically said \"suspicion of harassment,\" there had to be more to the story.","Qin Yuanzheng had been in a rush to take his little wife home and get her into bed.","What a nuisance. He frowned and said, \"Alright, I understand.\"","Why bother notifying other relatives? He might as well just swing by on the way and bail the man out himself.","That would save him from wasting any more of his time."]},{"number":56,"title":"Chapter 56: Haven't I been feeding you enough these days","paragraphs":["The reason the guard came looking for Qin Yuanzheng was that Deng Weijun had given Qiao Lanshu's name, claiming they were relatives.","But Deng Weijun didn't dare give the names of his older sister, Deng Xiaozhen, and his brother-in-law, Yang Wenyan.","He was afraid Deng Xiaozhen would break his legs.","Moreover, Yang Wenyan was the factory director and usually very strict. What if he got angry and fired Deng Weijun on the spot?","Deng Weijun was actually quite afraid of this brother-in-law.","He felt that Qiao Lanshu had a soft personality and was easy to talk to. If he got her to help bail him out of the police station, he could quietly sweep the matter under the rug without his sister and brother-in-law knowing. Wouldn't that solve everything?","However, he never expected that someone even more terrifying than his brother-in-law would show up.","Qin Yuanzheng, wearing a crisp military uniform, stood in front of the holding cell with a cold and stern expression, staring at him through the iron bars.","Looking at his dark expression, it seemed he was harboring some anger.","Deng Weijun: \"...\"","Deng Weijun's legs instantly went weak from fright. He stammered, \"Regiment... Regiment Commander Qin...\"","Qin Yuanzheng said, \"Come out.\"","The police comrade nearby had already opened the door. Deng Weijun stepped out of the holding cell, looking incredibly nervous.","Qiao Lanshu was sitting on a chair in the lobby. Seeing them come out, she immediately stood up. When she saw Deng Weijun, she asked with concern, \"Comrade Deng Weijun, are you alright?\"","Deng Weijun smiled awkwardly and said, \"Thank you for your concern, sister-in-law. I'm fine.\"","Li Jianlin, the deputy chief of the police station, was also there. He and Qin Yuanzheng were old acquaintances, so he added a few more words: \"Deng Weijun, you should hang out less with that crowd in the future. Who knows what trouble you might get into next time. Treat this as a lesson learned, understand?\"","Deng Weijun nodded with a long face. \"I know.\"","Qin Yuanzheng asked Li Jianlin, \"Is there bail to pay?\"","Li Jianlin replied, \"Of course. Ten yuan. Sign and leave your fingerprint here, and then you can go.\"","Qin Yuanzheng walked over, took out a stack of ten-yuan bills from his pocket, pulled one out, and placed it on the table. Then he signed, left his fingerprint, and led Deng Weijun out of the police station.","When Deng Weijun heard that the bail was ten yuan, his heart ached.","Ten yuan! That was almost a third of his salary. He only made 35 yuan a month!","He didn't dare speak to Qin Yuanzheng. He only dared to lean close to Qiao Lanshu and whisper to her, \"Sister-in-law, thank you both for coming to bail me out this time. I'll pay you back the ten yuan tomorrow. But I beg you, please don't tell my sister about this. She'll break my legs, really! She really will break my legs!\"","Deng Weijun lived in the staff dormitory and didn't work in the same factory as Deng Xiaozhen, so they didn't have to see each other often.","But he had been afraid of his sister since he was a child. Growing up, she had beaten him quite a lot.","When he left their hometown this time to come to Longcheng City to join his sister, his parents had told Deng Xiaozhen to keep a strict eye on him. If he dared to cause trouble, would his sister let him off?","Looking at Deng Weijun's pitiful appearance, Qiao Lanshu asked him, \"What exactly happened today? The police comrades said your group went to some girl's courtyard and peeked at her taking a bath? Is that true?\"","Of course, this matter might not be entirely true, which was why the police station had released them without alerting the Revolutionary Committee.","If it were true, and the other party reported it to the Revolutionary Committee, they wouldn't even need to notify the factory. By now, Deng Weijun might already be on a truck heading to a labor camp.","Qiao Lanshu felt that Deng Weijun probably wasn't that kind of person.","Speaking of this, Deng Weijun felt incredibly unlucky.","He whispered, \"Sister-in-law, of course it's not true! I went out for a stroll with Zheng Daliu and the others. They said they were going to a friend's house for some drinks and asked me to keep watch at the door to see if anyone was around. Before I even saw anyone, I heard them getting chased out. They said there was a girl taking a bath inside, and they were peeking! This time was really like a mouse drinking cat's milk—too thrilling!\"","Qiao Lanshu: \"...\"","Deng Weijun continued, \"Whether they peeked or not, I don't know. Anyway, I didn't look. Am I that kind of person? Besides, that woman didn't even look that great. She's already in her forties or fifties and still calls herself a girl. It's the middle of the day, there's no heating, and she's taking a bath in her room. Who knows what was really going on?\"","Seeing Deng Weijun getting closer and closer to Qiao Lanshu, Qin Yuanzheng reached out, placed his hand on Qiao Lanshu's shoulder, and pulled her into his embrace. He turned his head, glaring chillingly at Deng Weijun, and said, \"Hang out less with those people in the future. Don't you know they have criminal records?\"","Stared at by his chilling gaze, Deng Weijun subconsciously shrank his neck. He said, \"I, I didn't know. They are all workers in our factory. We are all colleagues. We usually just chat and play cards together.\"","Qin Yuanzheng said, \"They aren't innocent in getting arrested this time either. Look out for yourself in the future. If something like today happens again, have your sister bail you out.\"","He only helped bail Deng Weijun out today for the sake of his cousin Yang Wenyan; otherwise, he couldn't be bothered to care about these things.","Scolded by him, Deng Weijun didn't dare to breathe a word.","In front of Qiao Lanshu, he was incredibly noisy, but now, he was as timid as a quail. He quickly nodded and said, \"I know. I'll never dare do it again.\"","This lesson was enough. How would he dare go out and fool around with those people again?","Qin Yuanzheng took Qiao Lanshu to the car. It got dark early in winter, and it was already pitch black outside.","The wind was also strong at night. It was better to go home early and lie on the heated kang bed.","Qiao Lanshu whispered, \"So Weijun was instructed to keep watch at the door this time?\"","Qin Yuanzheng turned his head to look at her, his expression dark. He said, \"Weijun? Are you that close to him?\"","Qiao Lanshu: \"...\"","Qiao Lanshu had just said it casually. She said somewhat embarrassedly, \"No, it's just that he's quite a nice person.\"","Qin Yuanzheng felt a bit uncomfortable in his heart.","But at his age, he couldn't possibly bicker with his eighteen-year-old little wife over such a trivial matter.","That would make him seem very petty.","He fell silent for a moment before saying, \"Deputy Chief Li from the police station just told me that the guy named Zheng Daliu is no good. He has robbed people and beaten them up before. Later on, he caught a lucky break and managed to get a job in the factory. But after all these years, his true nature hasn't changed. I heard he's also fond of gambling.\"","Qiao Lanshu didn't know this Zheng Daliu. In her previous life, she had only entered the factory two years later. By then, let alone Zheng Daliu, even Deng Weijun wasn't at the factory anymore.","She had also been working for a short time this time around and hadn't met that Zheng Daliu.","She said, \"Hearing you say that, it seems that guy really isn't a good person. Who knows, maybe he really did go peek at women taking baths and made Deng Weijun keep watch for him. These people are truly awful.\"","Qin Yuanzheng drove in silence for a while. A few minutes later, unable to hold back any longer, he asked Qiao Lanshu, \"You seem to care quite a bit about Deng Weijun?\"","Qiao Lanshu let out a soft \"Ah\" and smiled. \"Not exactly, but I guess you could say we're friends? He's a really nice guy. Oh, right, he even gave me a pear at noon. He said it was shipped in from some county, and it was incredibly sweet.\"","Hearing this, Qin Yuanzheng abruptly pulled the car over to the side of the road. He leaned over, his face hovering just inches from hers. Qiao Lanshu pressed herself tightly against the passenger seat, her cheeks flushing as she looked up at him. \"Zheng Ge, wh-what's wrong?\"","Why did Qin Yuanzheng look so displeased? Had she said something wrong again?","Qin Yuanzheng stared at her and asked in a low, husky voice, \"Why are you eating things given to you by other men? Haven't I fed you well enough these past few days?\"","Qiao Lanshu: \"...\""]},{"number":57,"title":"Chapter 57: Don't you quite like this water tank","paragraphs":["Qiao Lanshu belatedly realized that her Brother Zheng seemed to be jealous.","In her previous life, she and Qin Yuanzheng had been together for five years. At that time, Qin Yuanzheng was promoted from brigade commander to division commander, and they moved into a bigger house.","Their living conditions had improved, but Qin Yuanzheng's health deteriorated day by day.","Back then, Qin Yuanzheng wouldn't get jealous when she interacted with other men.","On the contrary, he would from time to time invite his unmarried or divorced, childless comrades and subordinates to their home, deliberately introducing them to her.","Qin Yuanzheng was worried that after he passed away, since they had no children and Qiao Lanshu would be all alone in her early thirties and still very young, she would need someone to rely on.","So he thought about setting her up. He even introduced his rival, Guan Wenjuan, to Qiao Lanshu.","But what he didn't know was that after he left, Qiao Lanshu fell severely ill.","Her body was weak, and she often fell into illusions of her intimate moments with Qin Yuanzheng.","Now, looking at the jealous Qin Yuanzheng, she actually found it quite novel.","She looked at Qin Yuanzheng with a smile. Qin Yuanzheng looked displeased, his brows slightly furrowed as if he was truly a bit unhappy. However, he also knew he was being unreasonable, so he didn't dare say anything harsh. He just looked at Qiao Lanshu.","And Qiao Lanshu was actually still smiling.","Qin Yuanzheng reached out and pinched her cheek, saying while holding in his frustration, \"What are you smiling at?\"","Did she think his childish behavior was funny?","He just cared about Qiao Lanshu too much, which was why he was always so suspicious and paranoid.","Qiao Lanshu hugged him and took the initiative to kiss him on the cheek, whispering, \"I just think this version of Brother Zheng is so cute.\"","Qin Yuanzheng: ...","Cute?","That was not a word used to describe a man.","However, since his little wife had taken the initiative to kiss him, he naturally could not let her go.","So, right there in the car, he pinned his wife down and kissed her for a long time.","He didn't let her go until he had kissed Comrade Xiao Qiao into begging for mercy, and then he drove home, thoroughly satisfied.","...","After returning home, Qin Yuanzheng first boiled the bathwater.","Who asked his wife to refuse his touch if they did not take a bath?","She would say things like it was unhygienic.","The weather here was so cold and dry that many people only bathed once every few days.","But Qin Yuanzheng was willing to spoil his wife. After all, taking a bath together was quite interesting.","After changing her clothes, Qiao Lanshu came to the kitchen to cook with him.","Qin Yuanzheng said, \"Go out and rest. Aren't there biscuits and sunflower seeds on the table? Go have some. Do you want an apple? I'll cut one for you.\"","The two of them only came home for dinner at night, so the food stored in the basement had barely been touched.","The few apples sitting in the kitchen had not been eaten yet.","Qiao Lanshu said, \"I'll cut it.\"","As she spoke, she had already washed the apple clean and was cutting it with a knife.","Her knife skills were pretty good; after all, she had been cutting radishes for a long time, so she could cut the apple into evenly sized pieces.","Then she placed them on a plate.","Meanwhile, Qin Yuanzheng was kneading dough. He had bought lard and mutton in the morning, planning to render the lard later and make mutton soup noodles.","Qiao Lanshu picked up a piece of apple, walked over, and stood on her tiptoes to feed it to him. \"Brother Zheng, have some apple.\"","Qin Yuanzheng turned his head and took a bite, catching both the apple and her fingers in his mouth.","Qiao Lanshu's face immediately turned red. She quickly pulled her hand back, picked up the plate of apples, and walked away. \"Brother Zheng, I'm going out.\"","Qin Yuanzheng looked at her retreating figure and chuckled for a moment.","His wife was still quite shy.","They had been married for so many days, they had done everything, and he had seen everywhere, yet she was still this embarrassed?","This always made his heart itch, making him want to tease her.","After the couple finished eating, just like yesterday, they went to take a bath together.","Actually, Qiao Lanshu did not really want to take a bath anymore; she felt that just soaking her feet would be enough.","But after trying out the large water vat yesterday, Qin Yuanzheng felt it was great. He had gotten a taste of the sweetness, so today, right after dinner, he filled the large vat with water again.","How could Qiao Lanshu know the man's little schemes? She said, \"Brother Zheng, from now on, let's just take a bath once every few days. We don't need to do this every day. It's too much of a waste of water.\"","Qin Yuanzheng nodded without changing his expression and said, \"Alright. I was just worried you would catch a cold. Didn't you want to take a bath?\"","Saying that, he came over, closed the bathroom door, and then pulled Qiao Lanshu to take a bath.","Thinking of her experience from last night, Qiao Lanshu's face instantly turned bright red.","Taking a bath was actually quite comfortable, it was just a bit too much to handle.","Qin Yuanzheng even asked in her ear, \"What are you shy about? Didn't you like this vat a lot yesterday?\"","Qiao Lanshu whispered, \"I didn't say I didn't like it, but you can't bully me later.\"","As usual, Qin Yuanzheng got in first, and then let Qiao Lanshu sit on his lap. He asked in her ear, \"When have I ever bullied you? I can't even get enough of loving you.\"","Qiao Lanshu pushed away his roaming hands and said, \"Look, you're bullying me again.\"","Qin Yuanzheng did not withdraw his hands. He coaxed her in a low voice, \"Alright, then I'll take it slow, okay?\"","Qiao Lanshu was no match for him anyway. She couldn't push him away, nor could she run away. What else could she do?","She could only let him bully her.","Today, they once again bathed together for over an hour.","Finally, Qin Yuanzheng carried Qiao Lanshu out from inside, laughing as he teased her, \"How are you so weak? You can't take it anymore already?\"","Qiao Lanshu: ...","Qiao Lanshu leaned against Qin Yuanzheng's broad shoulders, her hand resting on her stomach.","She thought to herself, it was a pity that Brother Zheng had infertility. Otherwise, given the situation over the past few days, she figured she would have already gotten pregnant.","At this moment, Qin Yuanzheng was not thinking about children at all.","He felt that having Qiao Lanshu was enough. Qiao Lanshu was still young, and he had to raise her like a child.","At night, when the two were lying on the kang bed, Qiao Lanshu leaned into Qin Yuanzheng's embrace and whispered, \"Brother Zheng, I heard that there are two orphanages in our city with many homeless children. I want to...\"","Qin Yuanzheng immediately interrupted her. He said, \"I don't want to adopt a child right now.\"","In fact, he was never really obsessed with having children. It was just that the people around him minded his infertility too much and overreacted.","He whispered, \"Xiao Qiao, having you is enough for me. Let's talk about children later. If you still want a child ten years from now, it won't be too late for us to adopt then.\"","Qiao Lanshu smiled and said, \"No, what I mean is, I want to sponsor the children in the orphanage and send them some stationery, clothes, or food. Doesn't the orphanage have a sponsorship channel?\"","Qiao Lanshu wanted to do more good deeds and sponsor more children. Maybe Heaven, seeing how kind-hearted she was, would bless her and Brother Zheng with a child?","Hearing her say this, Qin Yuanzheng nodded without a second thought. He said, \"Sure, do whatever you want to do. I'll give you the money.\"","...","Qiao Lanshu was a woman of her word. The next day was a public holiday, so she did not go to work. However, Qin Yuanzheng had to report back to the military base because his seven-day marriage leave had come to an end.","After Qin Yuanzheng finished his lunch, he drove back to pick her up. Together, they bought a hundred pounds of potatoes and a hundred pounds of napa cabbage before heading to the orphanage in the eastern part of the city.","Qiao Lanshu had actually wanted to buy some flour, eggs, and similar groceries, but she realized they did not have enough ration coupons. They had no choice but to settle for winter vegetables.","Meanwhile, Guan Wenjun, the director of the Revolutionary Committee, caught wind of this and immediately hurried out of his office.","Rushing outside, he said, These past few days, Qin Yuanzheng has been watching his little wife like a hawk, not even letting her step out the front door. She has finally come out?","He pulled out a pair of sunglasses and slipped them on, running a hand through his hair. He turned to his subordinate and ordered, Get the car, we are going to the orphanage in the east end. Oh, right, go buy some food for the kids... What exactly did Qin Yuanzheng buy? Whatever it is, we have to buy something better than him!"]},{"number":58,"title":"Chapter 58: How come you're at the orphanage too","paragraphs":["Qiao Lanshu's decision to sponsor the orphanage wasn't a sudden whim.","However, at this time, the orphanage was officially called the Children's Upbringing Institute, where children without relatives to take them in were gathered and raised.","In her past life, when Qiao Lanshu was with Qin Yuanzheng, both of them had poor health. Plus, they didn't have any children of their own, so they sponsored many kids.","Qin Yuanzheng even funded and established many Hope Primary Schools in mountain villages under Qiao Lanshu's name.","But that was a matter for a few years later. The reform and opening-up had not yet begun, making many things difficult to accomplish.","Even for this visit to sponsor the institute, they had to submit an application and go through an approval process just to buy these supplies to bring over.","With limited food ration coupons and food shortages, they couldn't buy much.","Nevertheless, the director of the institute still received them warmly. The director said, \"Thank you for your sponsorship. It's been quite a while since anyone visited us.\"","The director was a thin, middle-aged woman. The entire institute housed over thirty children, yet there were only three female workers in total.","They were short-staffed, but it couldn't be helped. Hiring one more worker meant an extra expense. With so many children in the institute during this planned economy era, they could only rely on the older children to help with the chores.","The institute was located in a large compound consisting of single-story houses. A tall persimmon tree grew in the courtyard, and the ground was divided into cultivated vegetable patches. Since it was winter, there were no vegetables left in the fields, but normally, they grew their own food to eat.","The children here all slept on heated earthen beds, with seven or eight kids sharing one bed. Although the conditions were somewhat primitive, Qiao Lanshu noticed that the place was kept very clean, and the children were all wearing padded cotton jackets.","Coming out of the room, Qiao Lanshu asked, \"Director Shen, are all the children here?\"","The oldest children were thirteen or fourteen, while the youngest were only a few months old.","Once the children got a bit older, they would have to go out, find work, and support themselves.","Director Shen replied, \"There are a few more children in that small room over there.\"","She continued, \"They are all special needs children...\"","Qiao Lanshu nodded. She understood that not all the children in the institute were healthy.","She took out two bags of malt sugar and called out to the somewhat timid children standing in the courtyard, \"Children, come here! I have some candy for you.\"","Qiao Lanshu had originally wanted to buy the animal-shaped crackers produced by her food factory, but since she had just started working there, she had to wait until next month to get the internal subsidy coupons, so she didn't buy them.","She planned to buy some for the children when she visited again next month.","Because of the material shortages, everyone received very few sugar coupons—only a few taels per person per month. Unable to buy anything else, Qiao Lanshu could only buy the cheapest option: malt sugar, which didn't require coupons.","She bought the malt sugar at the department store. It was slightly more expensive than at the supply and marketing cooperative, but since it didn't require coupons, it cost one yuan per catty.","Qiao Lanshu bought two catties, which amounted to over a hundred pieces.","Holding the candy, she walked over one by one and gave two pieces to each of the children hiding in the rooms, behind the trees, and in the corners of the courtyard.","Director Shen and the female workers stood watching. Director Shen sighed emotionally, \"The children haven't had candy in half a year. Comrade Qiao, Commander Qin, I thank you on behalf of the children.\"","Watching Qiao Lanshu distribute the candy, Qin Yuanzheng thought she needed two pieces for herself as well; she looked like someone who really loved sweets.","With a faint smile on his lips, Qin Yuanzheng said to Director Shen, \"If you face any difficulties in the future, you can write to me. I will try my best to help however I can.\"","Hearing Qin Yuanzheng's words, Director Shen immediately became excited. \"Commander Qin, having your word is truly wonderful.\"","Saying this, she suddenly thought of something and probed tentatively, \"Commander Qin, bringing Comrade Qiao here this time... did you want to see the children for yourselves?\"","She spoke tactfully, but Qin Yuanzheng understood her meaning. She was asking if he had come to pick out a child and if he intended to adopt.","Qin Yuanzheng immediately shook his head and said, \"It was Comrade Little Qiao who wanted to come this time. She heard there was a children's institute here and was worried the kids weren't getting enough to eat.\"","Director Shen's expression showed a hint of disappointment.","She had been hoping that perhaps one or two lucky children might be adopted by Commander Qin.","After all, his was a military officer's family. If a child were adopted by them, they would never have to worry about their future again.","What a pity.","Director Shen smiled and nodded. \"So that's how it is. Comrade Little Qiao truly has a kind heart.\"","Qin Yuanzheng fell silent for a moment before asking, \"Do all the children here go to school?\"","Director Shen nodded. \"Of course. In the past, the children in our institute were educated internally by our caregivers using the same textbooks as the schools. However, in the last two years, our city built a few new primary schools, so now the children are all sent out to study at school.\"","If these children could successfully graduate from junior high school, the government would arrange jobs for them. Whether at a farm, a forestry center, or a factory, they would generally be provided with employment to help them become independent.","However, this was only in their city. Orphans in the villages were raised by the production brigades, which provided them with food, making their situation different from that in the city.","Hearing this, Qin Yuanzheng nodded and said no more.","After handing out the candy, Qiao Lanshu asked an older girl, \"Where are the rest of the children? Can you take me to them?\"","The girl, holding her candy, smiled and nodded. \"Okay, sister, follow me.\"","Qiao Lanshu followed the girl to a small room. On the heated earthen bed inside, there were five children. Some were sitting, some were lying down. The oldest was seven or eight, while the youngest was two or three.","The room was dim, with only a small window letting in some natural light.","When Qiao Lanshu walked in, she saw the children turn their heads to look at her.","Among these five children, two were born mentally disabled, and the others either had leg impairments or were so frail and sickly that they could only lie in bed, unable to withstand the wind.","These children relied entirely on the older kids for care. They couldn't go out to run and play like normal children.","They would probably be staying here for a very long time.","Feeling a pang of sympathy, Qiao Lanshu walked over and gave two pieces of candy to each of them. She reached out to gently rub the head of a little girl who looked about three years old and whispered, \"Eat the candy. It's very sweet.\"","This little girl had a problem with her legs; she had no strength and couldn't really stand up.","She timidly shrank back, staring at Qiao Lanshu with big, wide eyes.","Qiao Lanshu pressed the candy into her hands and left the room.","Her heart ached slightly, thinking that perhaps in another ten years, medical technology might be able to cure this girl's legs.","But right now, it seemed unlikely.","Qiao Lanshu stepped out of the room with a heavy heart. Just then, she heard a commotion coming from the courtyard.","Wearing sunglasses and a black overcoat, Guan Wenjun paraded in like a flaunting peacock, leading a group of people carrying several boxes of goods. Smiling brightly, he said, \"Oh my, Commander Qin, what a coincidence today! How come you're also visiting the orphanage?\"","As he spoke, he glanced again at the napa cabbages, potatoes, and other food piled up in the courtyard. With a look of utter disdain, he said, \"Commander Qin, are these the things you brought over?\""]},{"number":59,"title":"Chapter 59: The expression on the old man in her family was very unpleasant.","paragraphs":["This was Qiao Lanshu's second time meeting Guan Wenjun.","Actually, she had known Guan Wenjun in her past life.","However, the Guan Wenjun of that time was nowhere near as smug and successful as he was now.","As the director of the Provincial Revolutionary Committee, Guan Wenjun had offended far too many people. As soon as the policies opened up, he was ambushed with a sack over his head and beaten so badly he was nearly killed.","Ever since then, Guan Wenjun was left with a limp. Later on, he fled to the south to do business.","His escape had been a pathetic and miserable affair.","Qin Yuanzheng had helped him a few times, so the relationship between the two men had eased up quite a bit, and they kept in touch from time to time.","During the time when Qin Yuanzheng was bedridden with a severe illness, he had even planned to introduce Guan Wenjun to Qiao Lanshu.","Because Guan Wenjun had never married.","Thinking of this, Qiao Lanshu took a few more glances at Guan Wenjun, who was standing in the courtyard.","She wondered if the Guan Wenjun of this lifetime would still end up getting sacked and beaten.","Qin Yuanzheng was also a bit surprised to see Guan Wenjun arrive. Why are you here too?","Guan Wenjun took off his sunglasses and slipped them into his pocket. He had bought them over in Shanghai, and they were incredibly expensive.","He smoothed his hair back and said, Sponsoring the children at the orphanage is a good deed. What, only you, Qin Yuanzheng, are allowed to bring cabbages and small potatoes, but I am not allowed to bring milk powder and fine white flour?","Qin Yuanzheng was speechless.","Guan Wenjun certainly had deep pockets to actually buy milk powder and fine white flour. Truth be told, there were quite a few toddlers in the orphanage who really did need milk powder.","Director Shen had initially been a little nervous when she saw Guan Wenjun approaching.","After all, he was the director of the Provincial Revolutionary Committee. Who would not be afraid when seeing someone from the Revolutionary Committee?","However, her eyes widened when she heard him say he had brought milk powder and fine white flour.","What was there to be nervous about? This man was practically a living Bodhisattva!","Director Shen hurried forward to greet him, saying excitedly, Director Guan, on behalf of the children in the orphanage, I thank you for your generous sponsorship!","At the same time, she pondered in her heart that this Guan Wenjun must have done too many guilty deeds in his daily life, which was why he suddenly thought of doing good deeds.","Guan Wenjun walked over to Qiao Lanshu with a smile. Seemingly inadvertently, he stretched out his arm, revealing the Shanghai-brand mechanical watch on his wrist, and said smilingly:","Comrade Xiao Qiao, you just came to our north, with no relatives to rely on. You must be very unaccustomed to it, right? You did not even pick carefully when looking for a partner. Comrade Qin Yuanzheng has met with quite a few female comrades in the past. Has no one ever told you about this?","Qin Yuanzheng's face darkened instantly. He immediately walked over and glared at Guan Wenjun. Before he could even speak, Qiao Lanshu smiled and spoke up, giving an irrelevant answer, I did not expect such a coincidence today, that Director Guan would also come to sponsor the children of the orphanage. I have heard that Director Guan is generous, righteous, kind, and always ready to help others.","As she spoke, Qin Yuanzheng stared at her from the side, his gaze growing darker and darker, a jar of jealousy completely overturning in his heart.","Qiao Lanshu did not look at him, but continued to flatter Guan Wenjun, Just like today, Director Guan actually bought milk powder and fine white flour for the children. Director Guan, you really are a good person.","Guan Wenjun felt wonderful inwardly. With his hands in his pockets, he cast a smug glance at Qin Yuanzheng and said to Qiao Lanshu with a smile, Oh, it is alright, it is alright. It did not cost that much money. The main thing is that food stamps are hard to exchange, and it took me a while to find someone to trade with.","In reality, he had not looked for anyone to exchange stamps at all, because people had offered him plenty as tributes, and he accepted them all without the slightest fear of being reported.","Qiao Lanshu smiled and complimented him again, To go out of your way to find someone to exchange stamps just for the children in the orphanage, and to buy such good food to bring over, Director Guan is truly thoughtful. I have never met anyone more generous than you.","Meeting Qiao Lanshu's pretty little face and looking into her large, dark eyes, Guan Wenjun felt completely light and airy. Qin Yuanzheng could practically see an invisible tail wagging high up in the sky behind him.","Qin Yuanzheng frowned deeply and could not help but reach out, wanting to hold Qiao Lanshu's hand. However, Qiao Lanshu took a step forward and said to Guan Wenjun:","By the way, Director Guan, we have five special needs children in the orphanage who require care, and some of them also need to see a doctor for check-ups. It is rare to have such a generous and righteous good person like you visit today. These children are truly blessed. You will definitely sponsor their medical treatments, right?","Guan Wenjun did not sense anything wrong yet. He looked at Qiao Lanshu's sparkling eyes and listened to her soft, sweet words of flattery. Not to mention, this southern girl's voice was really pleasant to listen to.","It was not overly whiny, just light and soft, sounding incredibly gentle, making Guan Wenjun's ears tingle.","He nodded solemnly and said, Of course. Five children, right? Then take them to the hospital for a check-up. I will cover all the expenses.","Qiao Lanshu immediately burst into laughter. She gave Guan Wenjun a thumbs-up and said, Director Guan, you really are a great person! Truly, you are too kind! Since you are so kind, why not sponsor them with ten yuan every month, so they can afford to see the doctor and buy medicine every month? That way, it can be considered seeing a good deed through from beginning to end. What do you think?","With his hands in his pockets, Guan Wenjun looked at Qiao Lanshu's smiling face and nodded happily, saying, Yes, you are right. As the saying goes, if you are going to do a good deed, do it to the end. That makes perfect sense. Ten yuan a month, five children makes fifty yuan. That is absolutely no problem.","As he spoke, he turned to the subordinate behind him and said, You go and register the information of those five children. Take them to the hospital for a check-up this afternoon. When you get back, tell the personnel department that from now on, each of them will be sponsored ten yuan every month, to be deducted from my salary.","Subordinate: ...","The subordinate behind him was utterly astounded.","They looked at Qiao Lanshu with admiration.","Wondering what kind of magic this young girl possessed.","How did she manage to get Guan Wenjun to shell out fifty yuan every month to sponsor orphans with just a few words?","As for Guan Wenjun, how should one put it? His character was not exactly good, and he was particularly vindictive.","He had never done a single good deed in his daily life. Over his years of working in the Revolutionary Committee, he had never been soft-hearted.","Over the years, quite a few people had cursed him behind his back.","And now, not only had he come to visit the orphanage, but he had also decided to sponsor those five special needs children.","The subordinate rubbed his face, almost thinking he was dreaming.","Director Shen also thought she was dreaming.","Let alone five children, even for one child, a fixed monthly sponsorship of ten yuan was no small amount.","After all, the monthly salary of an official worker nowadays was only 35 yuan.","Director Shen, along with three other female workers, thanked Guan Wenjun profusely and pulled him inside to visit the five special needs children.","Under Qiao Lanshu's reverent gaze, Guan Wenjun straightened his clothes, smoothed his hair again, and with his hands in his pockets, followed Director Shen into the room with his head held high and his chest puffed out.","Watching him walk away, Qiao Lanshu turned around, covering her mouth to hide a giggle.","She took the initiative to link her arm through Qin Yuanzheng's and whispered, \"Brother Zheng, we are done with our business here. How about we head home?\"","At that very moment, she had yet to realize that her older man's expression had already turned incredibly dark."]},{"number":60,"title":"Chapter 60: How to Calm Brother Zheng When He's Angry","paragraphs":["Guan Wenjun was feeling immensely pleased after being praised by Qiao Lanshu. Not only did he sponsor those five special children, but he also told Director Shen to come to him if she faced any difficulties in the future, promising to provide some grain, eggs, and other supplies.","Director Shen was thrilled beyond words.","Today must be a lucky day!","How come not only Commander Qin came, but Director Guan also visited, and both promised they could be approached if there was any trouble?","Director Shen thought of Qiao Lanshu and immediately understood what was going on.","The reason these two men were acting like this was entirely due to Comrade Xiao Qiao!","Therefore, after coming out of the room, Director Shen immediately said to the female worker beside her, Go and ask Comrade Xiao Qiao and Commander Qin if they want to stay here for dinner this afternoon.","She really needed to thank them properly.","Guan Wenjun also came out, thinking smugly to himself that Comrade Xiao Qiao must have been captivated by him. Otherwise, why would she have spent so much time praising him just now?","She even stared at him with such admiring eyes!","Actually, right after Guan Wenjun was coaxed into sponsoring the five children, he faintly realized something was wrong.","But he firmly refused to admit that he had been sweet-talked into losing his bearings by just a few simple words from Comrade Xiao Qiao!","That was Qin Yuanzheng's wife, not his wife. What did it look like for him to be so obedient to her words?","He was not the kind of man without moral principles.","However, he was absolutely determined to steal Qin Yuanzheng's wife. Who told Qin Yuanzheng to steal his partner before?","Guan Wenjun walked into the courtyard but did not see Qin Yuanzheng or Comrade Xiao Qiao.","The female worker also walked over and said to Director Shen, Director, Commander Qin has already left with his family. They said they had other things to do today and would come back next time they are free.","Guan Wenjun was speechless.","Director Shen said with some regret, So that's how it is. That's really a pity. I was just about to ask them to stay for dinner.","As she spoke, she quickly turned to ask Guan Wenjun, Director Guan, would you...","Guan Wenjun kept a straight face. No need.","Guan Wenjun's previously radiant expression instantly clouded over.","Damn it, had he really been played?","Director Shen was startled by his expression.","To be honest, she had never seen a man change his face so quickly. It would be a shame if he didn't learn Sichuan face-changing opera.","Guan Wenjun said to Director Shen, I also have things to do, so I'll be leaving first.","However, he would not go back on the sponsorship he had promised, so he added, From now on, the fifty yuan a month will be remitted specifically to your reformatory's account. If there are any problems, just coordinate with him.","Saying that, he pointed to a subordinate behind him, then strode out of the reformatory.","He got into his car, angrily punched the seat, and cursed, Running away so fast, it was definitely on purpose!","He pondered in his heart. That Comrade Xiao Qiao looked so innocent, with a silly face that seemed very easy to deceive.","She definitely wouldn't have thought of coaxing him into sponsoring the children.","After all, fifty yuan a month was not a small amount.","It must be that bastard Qin Yuanzheng who taught a perfectly good young girl to be bad.","What kind of person was he? Truly shameless!","Guan Wenjun secretly put another black mark against Qin Yuanzheng in his heart.","Qin Yuanzheng's character was already precarious in his eyes.","...","Meanwhile, on the other side, Qin Yuanzheng, who was taking Qiao Lanshu home, also did not look too good.","Just now, Qiao Lanshu had praised Guan Wenjun for a long time, and he had been right there listening.","How should he put it? His little wife had said a basketful of good things to another man, but hadn't paid any attention to him.","In the past, when Comrade Xiao Qiao praised him, she only said a sentence or two. He had never seen her praise him like that.","Qin Yuanzheng felt a sour jealousy in his heart.","When this older man got jealous, it was quite fierce. He kept a straight face the whole way and didn't say a word.","Qiao Lanshu carefully watched his expression and belatedly realized that her Brother Zheng seemed unhappy. Was it because she had just praised Guan Wenjun?","But she only wanted to trick Guan Wenjun into sponsoring those children.","Who told Guan Wenjun to be so annoying and always go against her Brother Zheng?","Looking at Qin Yuanzheng's face, Qiao Lanshu asked tentatively, Brother Zheng, are you angry?","Qin Yuanzheng continued driving and said, Hmm? I'm not.","His face was tense, and he drove seriously, claiming he wasn't angry.","But how could Qiao Lanshu not know whether he was angry or not?","She just sat there and stopped talking.","When Qin Yuanzheng drove the car into their residential compound and the car had just come to a steady stop, Qiao Lanshu leaned over, rubbed her head against his arm, then hugged his arm, looked up at him pitifully, and whispered, Husband, stop being angry with me, okay?","Qin Yuanzheng was speechless.","Qin Yuanzheng turned to look at Qiao Lanshu, his gaze dark and deep.","Looking at Qiao Lanshu's fair little face, he felt that this wife of his really needed to be taught a lesson.","She still dared to call him husband at a time like this?","He pushed Qiao Lanshu away expressionlessly and then said, It's cold outside, let's go home first.","Qiao Lanshu was speechless.","How strange. Her usually foolproof coquettishness wasn't working?","She had only praised Guan Wenjun a few times, and Brother Zheng was actually this angry?","How was she supposed to coax him now?","Qiao Lanshu silently opened the car door and followed behind Qin Yuanzheng as they walked toward the stairwell.","On the way home, Qin Yuanzheng didn't speak or smile.","This made Qiao Lanshu nervous too.","She peeked at Qin Yuanzheng's face from time to time, and seeing his expressionless, stiff face, she drooped her head, feeling a little regretful.","When Qin Yuanzheng opened his apartment door, it just so happened that Huang Erling, hearing the footsteps, also opened the door next door.","Huang Erling, who had long since finished making the thick mattresses and quilts, had failed to find an opportunity several times.","This time, she had finally found the right moment to come out and give them the bedding.","As a result, as soon as she pushed the door open, she came face-to-face with Qin Yuanzheng, who had just opened his door.","Huang Erling was shocked.","Seeing Qin Yuanzheng's dark expression, Huang Erling's heart skipped a beat, and she took half a step back in fright.","Qin Yuanzheng looked at her, knowing she was the family member of Battalion Commander Zhao Jiannong next door, and asked, Is there something you need?","Huang Erling was speechless.","How could Huang Erling dare to say she needed something?","She smiled awkwardly and quickly said, Nothing, nothing, I'm fine.","Saying that, she quickly closed the door.","Standing inside her home, Huang Erling clutched her pounding heart, screaming silently in her head for a long time.","Really, why did she never pick a good time to go out?","Wasn't this Commander Qin just newly married and supposed to be in a great mood?","Who had provoked this living Yama again? They were definitely in for it now."]},{"number":61,"title":"Chapter 61: Stuffed","paragraphs":["When Qiao Lanshu saw Huang Erling open the door, she guessed the other woman probably wanted to talk about the mattress.","But Qin Yuanzheng was angry. Qiao Lanshu thought she had better coax Brother Zheng first.","The mattress wasn't urgent anyway; there was still bedding spread out on the kang.","Qiao Lanshu followed Qin Yuanzheng into the house.","As Qin Yuanzheng took off his clothes, he looked at Qiao Lanshu without saying a word.","Observing his expression, Qiao Lanshu felt as if he was deliberately waiting for her to coax him.","He didn't seem truly angry.","But she wasn't entirely sure, so she tried to get a closer look at his face. As a result, Qin Yuanzheng turned his back, refusing to let her see.","Qiao Lanshu: \"...\"","Qiao Lanshu took off her thick padded jacket, her lightly padded coat, and her cotton-padded trousers. She also hung her hat and scarf on the hooks behind the door.","Then, she went back into the room to pour herself some water. As she drank, she stole glances at Qin Yuanzheng's face.","Qin Yuanzheng was now wearing nothing but an army-green tank top and a pair of black shorts. He then went to the kitchen to cook.","Qiao Lanshu was stunned.","Was Qin Yuanzheng really angry?","Usually, when they came home together, he would help Qiao Lanshu take off her coat and hug and kiss her a few times.","But right now, let alone kissing her, he hadn't even given her a single hug.","Qiao Lanshu held her enamel mug, took a sip of water, and followed behind Qin Yuanzheng. She deliberately softened her voice and said, \"Hubby, this water is so cold.\"","Qin Yuanzheng: \"...\"","Qin Yuanzheng could barely maintain his straight face.","He coughed, took Qiao Lanshu's mug, and grabbed the thermos to pour her half a cup of hot water. Then he said, \"Alright, go out and sit down. I'm going to cook.\"","Qiao Lanshu: \"...\"","Qiao Lanshu didn't leave. Clutching her mug, she paced around Qin Yuanzheng. One moment she tilted her head to look at him from his left: \"Brother Zheng, are you angry?\"","The next moment she pressed closely against his right side, reached out to shake his arm, and whispered, \"Hubby, don't be mad at me, okay? I know I was wrong. I won't ever dare do it again.\"","Qin Yuanzheng simply couldn't resist her acting so coquettishly.","He paused his movements, turned around, and reached out to lift her chin. Looking at her, he asked, \"Where did you go wrong?\"","Qiao Lanshu blinked her eyes and said infuriatingly, \"I don't know.\"","Qin Yuanzheng: \"...\"","Stifling his frustration, Qin Yuanzheng scolded her, \"You don't know, yet you're apologizing to me?\"","Qiao Lanshu replied obediently, \"Because if I don't apologize, you'll ignore me.\"","See? The moment she said she was wrong, Brother Zheng immediately paid attention to her.","Qin Yuanzheng was completely wrapped around her little finger; he was utterly helpless against her.","At once, he abandoned the cooking and stopped asking questions. He hoisted Qiao Lanshu over his shoulder and strode into the bedroom, saying fiercely, \"I think you're just asking for it...\"","********","Pinned down on the kang by Qin Yuanzheng, Qiao Lanshu was genuinely crying this time.","While keeping busy, Qin Yuanzheng asked her, \"Now do you know what you did wrong?\"","With red-rimmed eyes, Qiao Lanshu said aggrievedly, \"I know, I know. Brother Zheng, I really know I was wrong.\"","Qin Yuanzheng asked again, \"Then tell me, where did you go wrong?\"","Qiao Lanshu knew exactly what Qin Yuanzheng liked to hear. She had only been deliberately provoking him earlier, but now she regretted it immensely.","After all, she really couldn't handle the consequences of provoking Qin Yuanzheng.","Looking pitiful, she said, \"I shouldn't have praised Director Guan. I should praise you. You are my man.\"","Hearing her say this, Qin Yuanzheng finally felt satisfied.","However, hearing the little girl say 'You are my man' made him lose control all over again.","He immediately pressed his little wife down again, making her say a whole basketful of sweet words to praise him. Only when she had said enough to make him happy and satisfied, and he calculated in his mind that it was half a basketful more than the praises she gave Guan Wenjun, was Qin Yuanzheng finally content.","By the time he finally forgave Comrade Xiao Qiao, he checked the time and saw it was already eight o'clock in the evening.","This apology session had lasted for more than three hours.","It completely exhausted and stuffed Qiao Lanshu. This time, she had truly and profoundly realized her mistake and made a sincere self-reflection.","She guaranteed she would absolutely never make the same mistake again.","With that, Qin Yuanzheng went to cook for her, completely satisfied.","******","The next day, Qiao Lanshu had to go to work.","But she almost couldn't get out of bed.","She was fed too much last night, causing her to sleep poorly through the night.","Qin Yuanzheng even threatened her, saying that if she ever praised Guan Wenjun again, he would make her apologize one more time.","This scared her so much that she had nightmares. In her dreams, Qin Yuanzheng locked her up with iron chains, feeding her while asking why she didn't praise him, and whether the food he made wasn't delicious enough or hadn't filled her up.","Qiao Lanshu was terrified, continuously shouting in her dream, \"I was wrong, I was wrong, I really know I was wrong.\"","After waking up, Qiao Lanshu touched her stomach, wanting to cry but having no tears left.","Qin Yuanzheng came out of the kitchen. He had already prepared breakfast and was coming to call Qiao Lanshu to eat.","Seeing Qiao Lanshu rubbing her stomach with a resentful expression, he found it somewhat amusing.","He walked over and asked, \"Are you hungry? Breakfast is ready. There's sweet potato and millet porridge, and cornmeal buns. Hurry up and get up to eat.\"","Qiao Lanshu muttered, \"I'm already stuffed to death, how can I eat anything else.\"","As she spoke, she let out a hmph, hopped off the kang, and sluggishly went to wash up while rubbing her waist.","Qin Yuanzheng watched her, his eyes filled with a smile.","......","After eating, Qin Yuanzheng drove Qiao Lanshu to the food factory, and then headed to the mining area military base for work.","After all, having rested for several days, there was a lot of work in the mining area that required his supervision. He would have to get busy recently.","Qiao Lanshu arrived at the factory, put on her protective clothing and gloves, and happily sat down to chop radishes again.","Wang Xue arrived a little later. She hurriedly sat opposite Qiao Lanshu and lowered her voice to say:","\"Xiao Qiao, do you want to eat some bread? There's a problem with the recent batches of pillow bread produced by our factory. Two batches were ruined; the taste is off, so they are classified as defective products. Our quality inspection director said they can't be sold!","They can only be consumed internally. You don't need ration coupons, and you can buy them at half price! As soon as I heard the news, I went over and bought two. I tasted one; it's a bit sour and the texture is rock hard, but it's still edible. Do you want to buy a couple too?\"","Defective products with issues like this could not be sold to the public.","However, food was precious and couldn't be wasted.","Therefore, they were usually sold internally.","Sometimes, if they couldn't be sold out, they would be sent to the food factory's internal cafeteria to be served as lunch for the employees.","Pillow bread was usually sold at a very high price. Even the food factory employees were reluctant to buy it for themselves.","With defective products available this time, many people were willing to spend their money.","Hearing her say this, and since she happened to like eating bread, Qiao Lanshu immediately asked, \"Sister, where can I buy them? I'll go buy two as well.\"","Wang Xue immediately grabbed her arm and said, \"They are with the bakery team. Come on, I will take you there!\"","On the way, Wang Xue continued to gossip, \"The team leader of the bakery crew is in deep trouble this time, though. I cannot believe she made such a massive mistake. The director of the Quality Control department just chewed her out on the factory floor right in front of everyone.\""]},{"number":62,"title":"Chapter 62: We Dare Not Keep You in Our Bakery Workshop Anymore","paragraphs":["He Juhong, the shift leader of the bread team, was truly out of luck.","She just could not figure it out: how did perfectly good bread get ruined in the oven?","The food factory's bread production was mostly mechanized, but it still required manual labor to portion the dough, knead it, and place it on the conveyor belt.","Then, the conveyor belt would automatically transport the dough into the oven. After a full rotation, the bread would be baked and ready for the staff to package.","The work was actually quite simple. He Juhong had not figured out where the problem lay just yet.","The director of the Quality Control Department was a man surnamed Liao, named Liao Zhihong. He was in his fifties and had worked at the food factory for over a decade. Having spent time in almost every workshop, rising from a regular employee to shift leader, then to workshop supervisor, and finally to QC director, he knew every step of the process inside and out.","He did not come alone this time; he was followed by Workshop Director Wei Zhengye and two deputy directors.","Liao Zhihong could not tolerate any mistakes. He was here to hold someone accountable.","Staring at He Juhong, he asked sternly, There is a problem with this batch of bread. As the shift leader, did you not do a preliminary inspection? Do you still not know where the issue is?","Over fifty loaves of bread were ruined in this batch.","That was no small number. Flour was precious; how could they be allowed to waste it like this?","He Juhong flushed red with shame. Enduring the embarrassment, she said, Director Liao, it is probably because we have a few new workers who have not gotten the hang of it yet, which led to the mistake. I will go check...","Director Liao scoffed coldly and scolded, Check my foot! Have you tasted the ruined bread? It is sour! What else could it be? It is obviously a fermentation issue! Who is watching the fermentation room? Call them out here!","He Juhong quickly ran to the fermentation room and called out the two female comrades working inside.","Wei Zhengye, standing behind Director Liao, felt his heart skip a beat the moment he saw his daughter.","A bad premonition suddenly arose in his heart. So, before they even walked over, he said to Director Liao, Director Liao, these new employees have only been here for a day or two. It is normal that they have not gotten the hang of it yet. Do regular employees not get a week to adapt and learn? In my opinion, this is probably still the fault of the senior employee.","Director Liao kept a dark face and said nothing. He just watched with a grim expression as He Juhong brought the two female workers out of the fermentation room.","The two female workers were Wei Hongmei and Sister Wu, who was in her forties. Sister Wu had worked at the food factory for several years. Later, her arms suffered frostbite, and her joints would ache every winter, so she was given special care and reassigned to watch the fermentation room.","Director Liao recognized the older female worker. With a dark face, he looked at the two of them and asked, What exactly happened with the bread fermentation this time? How did you monitor the temperature?","Sister Wu glanced at Wei Hongmei, and Wei Hongmei quickly said, Why are you looking at me? We were watching it together. Now that there is a problem, you are going to blame me, right?","Sister Wu saw Wei Zhengye standing there as well, staring at her.","She swallowed the anger in her heart.","She did not want to offend Wei Zhengye. After all, he was the workshop director. If he decided to target her, she would be in trouble.","Her arms were not very mobile now, so she could not do heavy labor, intricate work, or tasks involving cold water.","She cherished her current job very much, so she said, Director Liao, it was my negligence this time. My arm was hurting too much, so I took a moment to apply some medicine and lost track of time. It was probably during that time that I was not paying attention...","As she spoke, she looked at Director Liao's face and did not dare say any more.","Director Liao's expression was terrible; he was extremely disappointed in her.","Sister Wu lowered her head, not daring to speak again.","She was an official employee, so she probably would not be fired, but she would likely be fined.","Sure enough, Liao Zhihong said sternly, Both of you will share the responsibility for this accident. Five dollars will be deducted from your wages this month! If you make another mistake next time, you are both fired!","Liao Zhihong angrily called the pastry workshop supervisor, Liu Weihong, and the workshop director, Wei Zhengye, to his office for a meeting.","It seemed that this time, Liu Weihong would also get a scolding.","Everyone on the bread team breathed a sigh of relief. He Juhong felt incredibly unlucky. She looked at Wei Hongmei and asked, Wei Hongmei, how do you do your job?","Wei Hongmei said defiantly, What does this have to do with me? Did Sister Wu not admit it was her mistake?","He Juhong sneered, Before you came, no one ever made a mistake. As soon as you arrive, the bread gets ruined, and you have the nerve to blame Sister Wu?","Wei Hongmei had hardly ever been scolded in her life. Her father had spoiled her since she was little, and her husband, Sun Mingyong, was completely obedient to her after they married.","But ever since she came to the food factory, she faced grievances everywhere. She was disliked in the pickle workshop, and after coming to the bread workshop, she was scolded every day.","With red eyes, she said angrily, I am a new employee. I have not gotten the hang of it and I am not familiar with the work. Why do you blame me for everything?","Previously, when she went to package the bread, she could not control her strength and left fingerprint dents on the loaf, which earned her a scolding from the senior employee training her.","She felt that the pillow bread was so big and soft, it was completely normal to accidentally leave two fingerprint dents while wrapping it in kraft paper.","But they insisted on scolding her.","Now that she was in the fermentation room, she was just tired from working every day recently and waking up too early, so she had dozed off for a bit. She did not crush the dough, did she?","The fermentation room was so leisurely. The bread would ferment on its own just sitting there; she did not even need to do anything. Now that the bread was not baked right, they were scolding her again.","Wei Hongmei wiped her tears, feeling wronged herself, and said, I have been working hard. Why are you scolding me for everything? Why is it not Sister Wu's fault? Sister Wu was in there too.","Sister Wu was about to cry from anger as well. She took two deep breaths and said to He Juhong, Shift Leader, I am requesting a transfer. Please move me somewhere else. I can do anything.","He Juhong: ...","He Juhong said with a dark face, Your arms are not well, so you should stay and watch the fermentation room. Wei Hongmei, go back to your pickle workshop. Our bread workshop does not dare keep you anymore. And do not feel wronged; I feel more wronged than you! I will personally go talk to the factory manager about this transfer.","Wei Hongmei: ...","He Juhong was just a shift leader. She only managed the bread team and did not have the authority to transfer employees.","Normally, she would have to go to Supervisor Liu Weihong to handle this kind of matter.","But she did not count on Liu Weihong anymore. After all, Liu Weihong had forced Wei Hongmei into the bread team just to give face to Wei Zhengye.","And now that something had gone wrong, when Director Liao was scolding them, Liu Weihong, as the supervisor, did not say a single word to defend them!","After He Juhong finished speaking, she turned around and headed straight to the factory manager's office.","Everyone looked at Wei Hongmei, their eyes full of disgust.","It was not that they were being mean, but rather that Wei Hongmei had the temper of a spoiled princess. In that case, she might as well stay home and be a princess. Why even come out to work?","Would it not be better to leave the job opportunity to someone who actually needed it?"]},{"number":63,"title":"Chapter 63: Can You Marry Such an Adorable Wife","paragraphs":["Qiao Lanshu was pulled along by Wang Xue. Outside the bakery workshop, they watched the commotion through the window for a while along with people from several other workshops.","Then, the two went to the quality control department next to the bakery. Many people were buying bread. The pillow loaves were eight taels each, costing 50 cents apiece.","Now they were half price, so 50 cents could buy two.","Regardless of whether the taste was right or not, such cheap bread was truly rare, and everyone was scrambling to buy it.","Wang Xue was tall. She dragged Qiao Lanshu and squeezed into the crowd, forcefully snagging two loaves from someone else's hands. \"Oh my, can you even finish that much? Let me have two, let me have two.\"","She grabbed the bread and shoved it right into Qiao Lanshu's arms.","The man whose bread had been snatched turned around, about to yell at her, but when he turned, he met Qiao Lanshu's somewhat embarrassed face.","Qiao Lanshu's face flushed with embarrassment. She said tentatively, \"How about, I, I give them back to you? I won't buy them.\"","Wang Xue hid behind her and poked her in the waist upon hearing this.","This girl really was too thin-skinned!","The man looked at Qiao Lanshu and froze for a moment. Hearing her say that, how could he possibly snatch the bread back?","He quickly said, \"No need, no need. You buy them and eat them, little girl. I have enough, I have enough.\"","Saying that, he carried his remaining four loaves, paid his one yuan, turned around, and left.","Qiao Lanshu also paid her 50 cents and came out holding the two pillow loaves.","The pillow loaves had a fixed weight. One weighed eight taels, so two weighed over a jin. They felt quite heavy in her hands.","Wang Xue linked arms with her and said, \"You really are something. I thought you were actually going to give the bread back just now. You young girls are just too thin-skinned. Let me tell you, being thin-skinned means you'll go hungry. You have to be thick-skinned to get by.\"","Qiao Lanshu: \"...\"","Holding the two loaves, Qiao Lanshu thought of what she had just heard in the bakery and actually felt a bit curious. She said, \"The bakery team leader just said she wants to transfer Wei Hongmei back to our pickle team. She won't come back and cut radishes with us, will she?\"","He Juhong refused to keep Wei Hongmei and said she wanted to transfer her back to the pickle team.","Qiao Lanshu was a bit worried that the other woman would come to steal her position again.","She felt her current job was quite good. Every day she just chopped radishes and chatted with Wang Xue. The work was easy, and the atmosphere was great.","Wang Xue sneered and said, \"Our supervisor might not even want her. Even if she does come back, just let her go wash radishes.\"","Wang Xue did not like Wei Hongmei; Wei Hongmei really wasn't cut out for hard work.","She was despised wherever she went.","He Juhong went to find the factory director, Yang Wenyan. As soon as Yang Wenyan heard the purpose of her visit, his face darkened, and he said, \"This person was transferred over by Liu Weihong, right? Have Liu Weihong come see me.\"","He Juhong then went to find Liu Weihong.","Liu Weihong had just come out of Director Liao's office, looking miserable after being scolded.","As a result, He Juhong found her and said, \"Supervisor Liu, the factory director is looking for you and wants you to go over.\"","Liu Weihong's expression was terrible. She complained, \"It's definitely about the bakery team again, isn't it? Team Leader He, I'm not trying to criticize you, but you should put more effort into your daily work. Knowing full well that the new employees' professional skills aren't up to par yet, how could you just let them work on their own? You need to keep an eye on them.\"","He Juhong's face was also very ugly. She spoke bluntly, \"Supervisor Liu, you know exactly what's going on with this Wei Hongmei. Anyway, our bakery team doesn't dare to use her anymore. As for where she should be transferred, you can go discuss that with the factory director.\"","Saying that, He Juhong walked away angrily.","Liu Weihong was only in her twenties and hadn't worked at the factory for many years. Several of the team leaders under her were already somewhat insubordinate.","Now that she had pulled this stunt, He Juhong had completely fallen out with her.","Liu Weihong kept a straight face, but in her heart, she began to feel a bit of regret.","She originally just thought about transferring away the eyesore Qiao Lanshu, but she never expected that this Wei Hongmei would be so utterly useless.","Liu Weihong arrived at the factory director's office. Yang Wenyan looked at her and asked directly, \"What exactly is going on with that temporary worker in the bakery team?\"","At this moment, Liu Weihong had no need to shoulder the blame herself, so she pushed the responsibility onto Wei Zhengye. \"It was Director Wei who came to me and asked me to arrange an easy job for Wei Hongmei. Director, Director Wei is a workshop director. I had no way to refuse him, don't you agree?\"","Yang Wenyan: \"...\"","Wei Zhengye was also an old employee and had worked in the director position for several years. However, he had one major flaw: he doted on his daughter way too much.","It was simply a mindless kind of spoiling.","When it came to work, using connections and asking for favors was nothing unusual.","But you couldn't just use connections to bring an idiot in, right?","This was a food factory, after all!","Yang Wenyan remained silent for a moment before saying, \"Transfer Wei Hongmei to the family service team!\"","The family service team was a service group set up by all major state-owned factories.","It was usually composed of the family members of factory workers, forming groups of five or ten. Their main job was to regularly visit the factory to provide mobile services for the workers.","For example, haircutting, mending clothes, repairing shoes, and so on. The work was not easy, and the wages were even lower than those of temporary workers.","But at least this kind of work didn't require much brainpower.","Wei Hongmei couldn't possibly be so bad that she couldn't even mend clothes, right?","If so, she might as well just be fired outright.","Since Yang Wenyan, as the factory director, had spoken, Liu Weihong immediately went back to inform Wei Hongmei.","At this very moment, Wei Hongmei was still sitting outside the bakery team throwing a temper tantrum, absolutely refusing to enter the fermentation room with Sister Wu.","She was still saying, \"I just won't go in. If something goes wrong again this time, it has nothing to do with me!\"","Everyone was practically speechless, but few people paid her any mind. They didn't want to offend her, much less get close to her.","When Liu Weihong came to inform her about going to the family service team, she was stunned. She immediately stood up and said loudly, \"I'm not going! Where's my dad? I'm going to ask my dad.\"","Saying that, Wei Hongmei ran off.","Liu Weihong couldn't be bothered to deal with her either. Let her be.","Whether she could stay or not would depend on how capable Director Wei was.","...","Qiao Lanshu had originally been worried that Wei Hongmei would come back to steal her radish-chopping job.","But after worrying all afternoon, Wei Hongmei was nowhere to be seen.","She immediately breathed a sigh of relief.","Today, their workload was already very light because the radishes were almost completely chopped up. After this, there would be no more fresh vegetables to pickle.","After the workers of the pickle team had toiled for two months, it was finally time to relax.","As soon as it was time to get off work, Wang Xue dragged Qiao Lanshu out the door.","They each carried two bags of bread as they walked out of the clothing factory.","Qiao Lanshu looked around at the gate but did not see Qin Yuanzheng's car.","When the young man in the guardhouse saw Qiao Lanshu, he immediately said to her, \"Are you Comrade Qiao Lanshu?\"","Qiao Lanshu nodded. \"I am.\"","At this moment, she finally noticed her name written on the blackboard at the door of the guardhouse.","She quickly walked over and asked, \"Is there a letter for me?\"","The person in the guardroom handed her a small package and said, \"A package from Yangcheng. Oh, by the way, your husband came by at noon and said he wouldn't be able to pick you up on time this afternoon. He asked you to find a colleague to walk home with.\"","Qiao Lanshu: \"...\"","Qiao Lanshu nodded, \"Okay, thank you.\"","Qin Yuanzheng had originally wanted to pick up his wife, but something unexpected came up at the mining site and tied him down. Now, he had no idea what time he would be able to head back.","He was incredibly eager to get home.","Standing at the mining site, he listened to several engineers arguing. As he stood to the side, he kept glancing in the direction of the food factory.","Staff Officer Lin watched him from the side and deliberately teased, \"Oh, Commander Qin, there's no need to rush. Judging by their argument, you'll be able to go home in two hours at most. Why don't you have a smoke and calm down first?\"","Qin Yuanzheng: \"...\"","Qin Yuanzheng said with a cold face, \"I'm not smoking. I've already quit.\"","Staff Officer Lin: \"...\"","Staff Officer Lin was utterly shocked. He said, \"No way? You just got married, and you even quit smoking for that?\"","Qin Yuanzheng fell silent for a moment. Heaven knows what came to his mind, but he let out a chuckle, looked at Staff Officer Lin, and said, \"'Just got married'? Listen to you. Could you ever marry such an adorable wife?\"","Staff Officer Lin: \"...\""]},{"number":64,"title":"Chapter 64: Cried until my eyes were swollen.","paragraphs":["Staff Officer Lin had been following Qin Yuanzheng for quite a while, but he had never seen this side of him before.","In the past, this man was a total old fogey, a living Yama whose boundless energy at work would leave his subordinates paralyzed with exhaustion.","Yet now, he started clocking out right on the dot every day. As soon as it was time to get off work, he would stare at his watch while gazing at the distant food factory, acting just like a statue waiting for its wife.","In truth, he had just gotten married, and it was a late marriage at that. This older man had fought and struggled in the military camp, experiencing every kind of storm, except for women.","Now that he was thirty, an age where his comrades' children were already old enough to run errands, he had finally married a young wife and tasted what it was like to be with a woman. Like an old house catching a fierce fire, it was completely understandable that he wanted to stay home and accompany his wife.","However, his superiors said that while they could understand, if he wanted a couple of extra days off, the answer was a flat no.","Qin Yuanzheng felt frustrated, but there was nothing he could do. He could only stay in the mining area and continue holding meetings with a bunch of engineers and designers.","As the engineering and construction corps, their main responsibility was, in fact, construction.","Managing construction projects meant being incredibly busy.","What was more, Qin Yuanzheng was in charge of not only the coal mining area but also the construction of two highways.","After all, the original dirt road made transporting coal out far too inconvenient.","Therefore, they had planned two new highways that were set to begin construction next month. They needed a massive number of workers; relying solely on the engineering corps was obviously not enough.","So, their unit had to coordinate with the city's personnel section and the labor bureau to take in a large number of educated youths and workers.","Seeing that this meeting was going to take another two hours, Qin Yuanzheng sat in his chair, propped his forehead with his hand, and sighed silently.","Beside him, Staff Officer Lin leaned in and asked, Commander, are you wanting to go pick up my sister-in-law from work? How about I go pick her up for you?","Qin Yuanzheng stared silently at Staff Officer Lin for a few moments, then asked, Have you still not given up?","Staff Officer Lin: ???","Before Staff Officer Lin could even react, Qin Yuanzheng pointed at him and said, Comrade Xiao Qiao is already my wife. You had better kill that thought right now.","Staff Officer Lin: ...","Staff Officer Lin was utterly speechless.","Who was it, exactly, that had been going around introducing potential partners to Comrade Xiao Qiao back then?","Almost all the unmarried young officers in their unit had met Comrade Xiao Qiao. Especially Xiao Yang, who had even courted Comrade Xiao Qiao for several days. Who did not know about that?","Now he was getting jealous? Where was he earlier?","For the first time ever, Staff Officer Lin really wanted to beat Commander Qin up.","But in the end, he held back because he could not win in a fight and could not commit insubordination.","...","Qiao Lanshu came out of the food factory, holding a parcel sent from Yangcheng in her arms. Wang Xue was wrapped in a scarf, breathing out visible puffs of air, hopping in place from the freezing cold.","Seeing Qiao Lanshu come out, she walked over and asked, What is it, did your family send you something?","Qiao Lanshu nodded. Looking at the writing on the parcel, she said, When I got married, I sent a telegram home. I guess Father Qiao sent this to me.","Father Qiao loved her very much. After all, she was the child of him and his first wife, as well as his very first child. Qiao Lanshu had grown up being held in his arms.","But later on, she lost her mother, and a stepmother entered the family. Then, the stepmother gave birth to a son.","She could no longer stay at home. If she did not get married, she would have to go down to the countryside.","Father Qiao trusted Sun Mingyong very much, feeling that he was a child he had watched grow up. Entrusting Qiao Lanshu to Sun Mingyong put his mind at ease.","But as it turned out, this whole incident happened.","Qiao Lanshu did not hide anything from her father; she directly told him everything about Sun Mingyong tricking her into marriage.","Father Qiao must have been furious, which was why he sent a parcel over so quickly.","Holding the parcel, Qiao Lanshu asked Wang Xue, Sister, where do you live? I am heading this way.","Wang Xue linked arms with her and said, I know, you live in the military compound. We are going the same way; I need to go to the supply and marketing cooperative to buy some things.","The two of them walked together until they reached the vicinity of the cooperative. Wang Xue asked Qiao Lanshu, Xiao Qiao, do you need to buy anything?","Qiao Lanshu, holding her small parcel and the two loaves of bread she had bought from the food factory, hesitated about whether to go buy something.","The walnut pastries Qin Yuanzheng bought for her last time were quite delicious, and they were out of biscuits at home. She thought for a moment and said, Maybe I will go tomorrow. I forgot to bring my non-staple food coupons. I wanted to buy some biscuits or walnut pastries.","When she came, Father Qiao had given her a lot of national food coupons. She had some non-staple food coupons too, though not many, so she was quite frugal with them.","Hearing her say this, Wang Xue lowered her voice and said, Oh my, did you not know there is a mobile market nearby? You do not need coupons to buy things there.","Qiao Lanshu genuinely did not know. She looked around and asked, Where is it?","Wang Xue pulled her along, saying, Let us go, I will take you.","That mobile market was in an alley right across from the cooperative. When Wang Xue led Qiao Lanshu into the alley, they indeed saw people coming out carrying things.","As they walked further in, they occasionally saw people wearing worn-out padded jackets, carrying baskets on their arms or holding sacks, constantly keeping a watchful eye on passersby. They were clearly selling goods.","In fact, many people knew about this kind of place; it just depended on whether the authorities wanted to manage it or if anyone reported it.","A tightly bundled-up woman saw Wang Xue and Qiao Lanshu enter and immediately walked over. She lifted a corner of the black cloth covering her basket and said with a smile, Girls, want to take a look at this?","When Wang Xue and Qiao Lanshu saw the small fried dough twists in her basket, they instantly stopped in their tracks.","Wang Xue was craving them so badly. She swallowed hard and asked in a low voice, How much is this for a catty?","The woman held out her hand and said, Fifty cents.","Fried dough twists nowadays were considered grain and oil products. They were deep-fried, rich in oil, and incredibly fragrant. The sweet ones even had added sugar, making them sweet, aromatic, and crispy, needless to say, they were absolutely delicious.","Ordinary families would only be willing to spend money on a couple of catties during the New Year to use as gifts when visiting relatives.","Or they would buy them for the children to eat, as a way to improve their diet.","However, the normal price at the supply and marketing cooperative was twenty cents a catty, but that required food coupons.","Here, no food coupons were needed, but the seller charged fifty cents a catty.","Wang Xue felt a bit of a pinch at the price, but she really wanted to eat the fried dough twists. Gritting her teeth, she said, Give me fifty cents worth.","The woman immediately took out a small scale, weighed out a catty for her, and then said, Here, shall I put them in your pocket?","Wang Xue: ...","Wang Xue was exasperated: Seriously, you do not even have a piece of newspaper?","The woman replied, I really do not. All the newspapers are used up.","Wang Xue had no choice but to pull down half of her scarf and say, Wrap them in here.","She was not afraid of the oil at all. Literally wrapping a catty of fried dough twists in her scarf, she turned and asked Qiao Lanshu, Comrade Xiao Qiao, are you buying any?","Qiao Lanshu actually wanted to eat fried dough twists too. Moreover, looking at these twists, why did they look exactly like the ones made by their frying team?","However, the food from the food factory had fixed sales channels. Anyway, it definitely wouldn't flow into the mobile market.","Maybe she was mistaken?","Qiao Lanshu pondered for a moment, then quickly said, \"I'll take a pound too. Here's fifty cents, please weigh it for me.\"","As she spoke, she took fifty cents out of her pocket and handed it to the woman.","Immediately after, she pulled out a folded newspaper from her pocket. She set down the parcel and bread she was holding and folded the newspaper into a square bowl.","Wang Xue was stunned. She asked, \"Comrade Xiao Qiao, why do you carry a newspaper with you when you go to work?\"","Qiao Lanshu smiled and said, \"I got this from the factory. I wanted to take it home to read since we don't have newspapers at home.\"","Wang Xue was speechless.","Wang Xue then said, \"Your Commander Qin must have plenty of them at the military base. You should just ask him to bring some back for you.\"","Qin Yuanzheng had actually brought quite a few newspapers home. He had also wanted to buy her some books to read, but there weren't many readable books in the library nowadays. She had already read the ones she could, and she didn't dare to read the ones she shouldn't.","So she just read newspapers or magazines. Sometimes, she also read books on planting, raising pigs, or raising ducks, strictly for entertainment.","While the two were chatting, the woman had already weighed a pound of fried dough twists and poured them into the newspaper bowl Qiao Lanshu had made.","Actually, Qiao Lanshu wanted to buy two pounds, but she was holding a lot of things right now. Plus, fried dough twists were light and bulky; two pounds would be quite a lot. She was afraid she wouldn't be able to carry them all back, and if she dropped a few on the way, her heart would ache to death.","Wang Xue was also holding bread and didn't have a free hand to help her carry them. So, she helped pile the twists onto the parcel, and then pressed the bread on top of the twists. After making sure nothing would fall, the two of them finally walked out of the alley with their arms full.","After coming out, Wang Xue still had to go to the supply and marketing cooperative. Qiao Lanshu really couldn't carry anything else, so she didn't go.","The two parted ways on the street opposite the cooperative. Then, Qiao Lanshu walked forward another dozen meters, turned a corner, and arrived at the military residential compound.","The people at the compound all recognized Qiao Lanshu, knowing she was the family member of the famous head of the 21st Regiment, so they quickly opened the gate for her.","A guard saw her carrying so many things and specifically came out to ask, \"Sister-in-law, do you need help?\"","Qiao Lanshu recognized that this was the same guard who had helped her and Huang Erling carry things last time.","She immediately smiled and said, \"No need, I can carry it myself.\"","Saying that, she walked toward their guardhouse. She had originally wanted to grab some fried dough twists for them to eat, but there were two pillow breads pressing down on top of the twists.","She tried to grab some but couldn't reach them, so she took a pillow bread instead and placed it on the windowsill of the guardhouse, telling them, \"This is discount bread from our food factory. You two can share it. The taste isn't great, so please don't mind.\"","The guard didn't dare to accept it. Holding the bread, he chased after her, \"No need, Sister-in-law. Our troops have discipline; we cannot accept your things.\"","He had said the same thing last time; he was genuinely afraid to accept her things.","She quickly replied, \"This is a token of gratitude. If you don't take it, I won't dare ask you for help carrying things next time.\"","She walked a few steps, then turned back and said, \"Just consider it a gift from Commander Qin. Take it to fill your stomachs.\"","The guard hesitated for a moment, wavered for a long while, and finally accepted the bread.","They were guards in the mining area regiment, and happened to be Qin Yuanzheng's subordinates. Qiao Lanshu was already familiar with them from her past life.","When Qiao Lanshu returned home, Qin Yuanzheng wasn't back yet, so she tidied up the house a bit.","She planned to slice the bread for dinner, cook some sweet potato millet porridge, stir-fry some sweet and sour cabbage, and stew some potato glass noodles.","She started cooking the porridge first and soaked the glass noodles in water.","Only then did she bring the parcel over and open it. Inside was a letter from home, written to her by Father Qiao.","Father Qiao expressed shock and extreme anger at Sun Mingyong's behavior.","Out of the three pages of the letter, a page and a half were dedicated to cursing Sun Mingyong as a beast.","Then, he carefully asked how Qiao Lanshu was doing, wondering how a perfectly good regimental-level cadre was still unmarried at thirty, and how she managed to get so lucky that he registered for marriage with her as soon as she arrived.","He tactfully asked if there was something wrong with this Commander Qin, or if he secretly had a wife in the countryside that he was hiding. He also asked if this Commander Qin was made up, wondering if she had deliberately fabricated a person to deceive her old father.","The letter made Qiao Lanshu both cry and laugh as she read it.","At the end of the letter, a hundred yuan worth of food stamps was attached. Father Qiao said he had remitted two hundred yuan to her bankbook, telling her that if she encountered any difficulties, she should immediately take a train back. He would find a way to buy her a job so she wouldn't have to go down to the countryside.","Father Qiao was actually regretful too. He had trusted Sun Mingyong too much; after all, he was a child he had watched grow up.","If he had known earlier that Sun Mingyong was unreliable, he would absolutely, positively never have let his daughter go to the distant north to seek her husband.","From south to north, over thousands of kilometers, if his daughter was sold by someone, he wouldn't even know where to look for her!","Qiao Lanshu put away the food stamps and the letter.","Inside the parcel, there was a packet of dried salted fish, a packet of cured pork, a packet of Chinese sausage, a packet of dried squid, and two packets of homemade sun-dried radish.","It was mostly meat. He was afraid Qiao Lanshu wouldn't have meat to eat here and would suffer from hunger and cold.","These things were probably sent to her secretly by Father Qiao as well. After all, her stepmother had had some complaints when he previously sent money to Sun Mingyong.","Now he was sending her money again, and so much of it.","Qiao Lanshu took the items to the kitchen to organize them. Just then, she heard the front door open, and Qin Yuanzheng returned, looking travel-worn.","Qin Yuanzheng's body carried the cold scent of the coal mines.","Qiao Lanshu quickly ran over. Looking at Qin Yuanzheng, she said, \"Brother Zheng, I haven't seen you all day. I missed you so much.\"","Qin Yuanzheng took off his overcoat and jacket, immediately picked Qiao Lanshu up, kissed her on the cheek, and said, \"I missed you to death too!\"","Not only did his heart miss her, but his body missed her too.","Every part of him longed for her, missing her so much that his whole body could barely take it. His chest swelled uncomfortably, and his body swelled uncomfortably too.","In short, not seeing his little wife for a day made him feel off everywhere.","He set Qiao Lanshu down and wanted to kiss her again. However, upon seeing her eyes, he suddenly frowned. He rubbed the corner of her eye with his rough thumb and asked in a low voice, \"Why were you crying? Did someone bully you again?\"","His little wife, whom he hadn't seen for just a day, actually had swollen eyes from crying.","Even when he bullied her on the heated brick bed before, she hadn't cried this hard."]},{"number":65,"title":"Chapter 65: My Arms Are Strong","paragraphs":["When Qin Yuanzheng asked this, Qiao Lanshu suddenly felt an even stronger urge to cry.","It was not that she was too weak or prone to crying. Rather, it was because ever since she was reborn and found herself on the train, she realized she had not seen her father for almost two years in her past life, spanning the time before and after Qin Yuanzheng's death.","In her previous life, she was locked in a cave dwelling as soon as she arrived in the North, becoming a missing person.","Half a year after her disappearance, her father, Qiao Bingzhang, specially traveled all the way to Longcheng City to look for her.","Naturally, he returned empty-handed.","However, it was exactly because Qiao Bingzhang came that he discovered Sun Mingyong had not gone to pick up Qiao Lanshu, leading to her disappearance. Since Sun Mingyong already had a wife and children of his own, Qiao Bingzhang went to the provincial Revolutionary Committee to report him.","He had sent Sun Mingyong so much money and food coupons, and he had all the evidence. But at the time, because Qiao Lanshu's whereabouts were unknown and Qiao Bingzhang was an outsider, no one helped him.","The two places were too far apart, making it difficult to gather evidence. Therefore, Sun Mingyong only lost his job and was not sent to a labor camp.","Fortunately, Qiao Bingzhang had visited the police station, the Revolutionary Committee, and the Women's Federation. So, when Qiao Lanshu finally escaped from the cave and sought help from the Women's Federation, everyone realized that what the man from the South had said back then was actually true.","His daughter had truly gone missing in Longcheng City and had been kidnapped.","With the help of the Women's Federation, Sun Mingyong was sent to a labor camp.","At that time, Qiao Lanshu was too weak and could only recuperate in Longcheng City. It happened to be winter, and heavy snow blocked the roads, making it impossible for her to return to Yangcheng. The Women's Federation found her a job at a food factory, which successfully helped her settle down.","Of course, the man who had locked her in the cave was also caught and executed by firing squad.","Later on, with a stable job at the food factory and an assigned apartment, she no longer thought about returning to Yangcheng.","For one, she felt she had no face to return. For another, her body was damaged; not only was she weak, but she was also left infertile. Even if she went back, she would not be able to marry, and finding a job would be difficult.","In this life, she had not yet encountered the man who locked her up in her previous life. That person was probably still wandering around the villages at this moment, right?","If he had not committed a crime yet in this life, she could not just have him arrested for no reason. She would have to wait until she found him and look for an opportunity.","Thinking of this, Qiao Lanshu's expression darkened a bit.","Leaning into Qin Yuanzheng's embrace, she whispered, No one bullied me. It is just... I miss my dad.","Qiao Lanshu added, My dad sent me some food and a letter. He still does not believe I married a regiment commander. He asked if I was lying to him. He is probably worried.","Hearing her say this, Qin Yuanzheng breathed a sigh of relief. So it is because of this? Then tomorrow when I go to the base, I will send a telegram from the unit to his workplace?","Qiao Lanshu immediately nodded and smiled, Okay, that way, my dad should be able to rest easy.","Qin Yuanzheng looked at her expression. After a moment of silence, he suddenly said, We are too busy this year, and I probably will not have time during the New Year. But next summer, I can apply for leave. When the time comes, I will accompany you back for a visit.","Qiao Lanshu immediately looked at him with joy. Really?","Qin Yuanzheng nodded. Of course it is true.","Yangcheng was too far away. Qin Yuanzheng had never imagined before that he would marry a wife from so far away.","They had been married for quite a few days now, and he really should take the initiative to contact his father-in-law.","Qin Yuanzheng hugged Qiao Lanshu tenderly, reluctant to put her down. Seeing her look so sad made his heart ache.","He simply lifted Qiao Lanshu up into his arms. Startled, she quickly reached out to wrap her arms around his neck and wrapped her legs around his waist. Qin Yuanzheng supported her with his hands and smiled, I hold you every day, why are you still so scared?","He whispered, Do not worry. Although there is nothing strapping you in this time, my arms are strong. I will not let you fall.","Hearing him say this, Qiao Lanshu's face instantly flushed red with shyness.","Resting against his shoulder, she said with a blushing face, Then you better hold me tight. If I fall, I will not let you hold me ever again.","Qin Yuanzheng deliberately leaned close to her ear and murmured, Do you not already know very well whether my arms are strong or not?","Qiao Lanshu felt herself being held securely. Looking at Qin Yuanzheng's arm muscles, which were thicker than her thighs, how could she not know his arms were strong?","She knew it all too well.","The Qin Yuanzheng of this time was much younger than the Qin Yuanzheng in her past life, and his health was much better. Naturally, he was also more energetic and stronger than his past-life self.","Qin Yuanzheng carried her to the kitchen. Qiao Lanshu leaned on his shoulder and told him, I bought some discounted pillow bread today. I got two for fifty cents. I gave one to the guard, and I am planning to have the other one for dinner. I have already started cooking the millet and sweet potato porridge. Do you want some steamed buns? I saw a few left on the windowsill; should I steam them for you?","Qin Yuanzheng walked into the kitchen and sure enough, he smelled the aroma of the millet and sweet potato porridge. He immediately said, My wife is so capable. You even know how to cook millet porridge now.","After all, people in Yangcheng did not seem to drink millet porridge; they only had white rice porridge.","Millet was the main crop produced here in Longcheng, so it was one of the primary staple foods for every household.","Qiao Lanshu was somewhat left speechless by his praise.","Who did not know how to cook porridge?","Qin Yuanzheng saw that the porridge was ready. The pillow bread was quite large, but it definitely would not be enough for him to eat. He said, Then I will steam some buns and stir-fry a couple of dishes.","Saying that, he reluctantly set Qiao Lanshu down on the ground, having her sit at the dining table by the kitchen door. Then, he washed his hands, brought in the remaining five cornmeal buns, and put them in the pot to steam.","He also brought over some Napa cabbage and potatoes, preparing to make potato stir-fried with cured meat and vinegar-glazed cabbage.","It was winter recently, and the supply and marketing cooperative did not have many fresh vegetables and fruits left. Even if they did, the prices were very high.","Most people here ate winter vegetables, such as Napa cabbage, potatoes, radishes, sweet potatoes, pumpkins, and scallions.","Qiao Lanshu had sprouted some beans in the house herself, but they would need another two days before they were ready to eat.","Although Qin Yuanzheng looked like a rough and tough guy, he was quite meticulous in his actions and was a good cook.","Qiao Lanshu sat nearby, watching his large, rough hands holding the cabbage and chopping it.","Qin Yuanzheng's hands were very large and rough. His palms were covered in hard calluses, his knuckles were prominent, and all five of his fingers were long.","Qiao Lanshu stretched out her own palms to look at them, and then looked at Qin Yuanzheng's hands.","She thought to herself, how could someone have such big hands? Those calluses must be really torturous.","She pondered internally whether she should take out her sheep oil hand cream and apply some to his hands.","After all, with them being so rough, it was uncomfortable for her too."]},{"number":66,"title":"Chapter 66: Tonight I'll Feed You","paragraphs":["After Qin Yuanzheng finished cooking, he brought all the dishes out. Qiao Lanshu's favorite was his stir-fried sweet and sour cabbage.","It tasted perfectly tart and had a crisp texture—it was incredibly delicious.","Thank goodness there was still Chinese cabbage to eat during the northern winters!","They ate at a small table in the living room. Qiao Lanshu was sitting on the sofa waiting for Qin Yuanzheng.","When Qin Yuanzheng came over, he insisted on holding Qiao Lanshu while they ate.","He assertively pulled Qiao Lanshu onto his lap and told her, Be good, I'll feed you dinner tonight.","Qiao Lanshu was speechless.","Qiao Lanshu's back pressed against his chest. The height difference between them was significant, so even though she was sitting on his lap, she wasn't too high up, and they could still look at each other at eye level.","Qiao Lanshu tried to get off his lap. Blushing, she said, There's no need, I can eat by myself.","Who knew what was going through Qin Yuanzheng's mind, but his large, rough hands immediately held down his little wife who was trying to escape.","He was strong; with just a light press, Qiao Lanshu couldn't run away.","Qin Yuanzheng held her and said gently, Weren't you in a bad mood today? Then let me serve you, isn't that nice?","Qiao Lanshu was speechless again.","She had indeed felt a bit upset after seeing her father's letter, which reminded her of things from her past life.","But she was actually fine now.","She just felt that being held and fed by Qin Yuanzheng was a bit weird.","Qin Yuanzheng held her, his rough hand gripping her waist, and picked up some sweet and sour cabbage for her.","Qiao Lanshu had no choice but to let him feed her.","The food Qin Yuanzheng cooked was delicious, and without realizing it, she ate quite a bit.","Seeing that she had stopped eating, Qin Yuanzheng asked, Why did you stop? Are you really eating this little?","It was like feeding a cat. No wonder she was so thin. With such a small appetite, she would burn it all off just by taking a few steps around the house, let alone doing exercises.","But Qiao Lanshu refused to eat any more; she really couldn't fit another bite.","Qin Yuanzheng reached out and rubbed her stomach, then suddenly chuckled and said, It's not even bulging.","He added, Didn't it bulge up last night?","Qiao Lanshu was speechless.","Qiao Lanshu really had to hand it to Qin Yuanzheng. This older man really had no filter. How could he say such things without changing his expression?","He dared to say it, but she didn't dare to listen.","It was one thing for him to talk endlessly during their usual exercises, but now he was starting up while they were just eating.","This man was so proper, serious, and unsmiling in front of others;","Yet at home, the words that came out of his mouth were naughtier than the meat dishes on the table.","Qiao Lanshu ran into the bedroom.","Qin Yuanzheng couldn't help but laugh. Since his wife was full, he started to eat. He polished off the steamed buns, the remaining half loaf of bread, a large bowl of porridge, and the two leftover plates of food on the table.","He didn't even leave the vegetable juices behind, using a steamed bun to wipe the plates completely clean.","That night, true to his word, he told Qiao Lanshu again that since she was in a bad mood, he had to serve her and make her happy.","At first, Qiao Lanshu wondered how exactly he was going to serve her and make her happy.","As it turned out, perhaps because he hadn't eaten enough at the dinner table, he had another meal.","Qiao Lanshu wanted to cry but had no tears left.","Since they got married, the two of them had been quite harmonious...","Qiao Lanshu asked hesitantly, Brother Zheng, we're okay doing it like this, right?","Seeing her caressing her stomach, Qin Yuanzheng replied, I have infertility, what could possibly happen? Don't worry, we don't need to use any protection.","This was the only benefit of his infertility: he could do whatever he wanted and indulge himself.","He could do it however he pleased. Since they wouldn't have children anyway, there was nothing to worry about.","If he were a normal man without infertility, he would probably have to use protection, or at least he wouldn't dare to be so indulgent.","After all, his little wife had just turned eighteen two days before their wedding. He was enjoying their current two-person world very much and didn't want children.","...","Ever since getting married, Qiao Lanshu was incredibly tired every morning.","She yawned constantly on her way to work every day.","Qin Yuanzheng was actually puzzled. He had clearly restrained himself a lot, and he felt that he still had abundant energy.","How come Comrade Xiao Qiao was so exhausted?","After arriving at work today, Qiao Lanshu finished chopping the last few dozen pounds of radishes.","With that done, their cutting and washing shift had nothing left to do.","They rested for the entire morning, and in the afternoon, they were given time off to go home and rest instead of working.","After all, they had been busy for quite a while, so this half-day was given to them as an extra break.","But tomorrow, they would probably have to go help out in other shifts at the pickle workshop.","However, since they were being transferred over to help, they would mostly be assigned lighter tasks.","Qiao Lanshu and Wang Xue came out of the workshop. Wang Xue was telling her, Did you eat the fried dough twists we bought yesterday? They taste really good, not much worse than the ones produced in our factory. I'm going to buy another two pounds today, do you want to come?","Hearing Wang Xue mention it, Qiao Lanshu suddenly remembered that she hadn't eaten the fried dough twists she bought yesterday.","How could she have had the time to eat them...","Thinking of her experience last night, she immediately lowered her head, blushing. She nodded and said, Are they really that delicious? As good as the ones made in our factory?","Wang Xue immediately replied, Absolutely! They taste exactly like the ones from our factory.","As Wang Xue spoke, she realized something sounded off and quickly added, Of course, they definitely weren't fried in our factory.","The food from the food factory had fixed sales channels. If it actually flowed into the mobile market, it would be a serious problem.","A very serious problem.","If things went wrong, the factory director could even be dismissed.","Saying this, Wang Xue exchanged a glance with Qiao Lanshu. Both of them silently kept their mouths shut, not daring to continue discussing this topic inside the factory.","Wang Xue remained silent for a moment before lowering her voice to ask, Are we still going to buy them?","Qiao Lanshu nodded and replied, We'll buy them!","The two of them changed out of their protective workwear, bundled up in their padded jackets and scarves, and walked out of the food factory arm in arm.","As soon as they walked out the door, they saw her cousin-in-law's brother, Deng Weijun, walking outside with two other men, a cigarette dangling from his mouth.","Qiao Lanshu immediately recognized that one of the men was another boiler worker from their factory, Zheng Daliu.","Last time, Deng Weijun had gone out with them, which led to someone reporting them for peeping at female comrades taking a bath, and they were subsequently arrested and taken to the police station.","That time, it was Qin Yuanzheng who had gone to bail Deng Weijun out.","Didn't Deng Weijun say he wasn't going to hang around with Zheng Daliu anymore?","How many days had it even been?","Why was he acting all chummy with him again?","Qiao Lanshu quickly called out to him, Weijun, Deng Weijun.","Hearing her voice, Deng Weijun immediately turned his head.","After all, Qiao Lanshu's southern accent was too distinct; it was practically one of a kind.","He walked over from Zheng Daliu's side, threw away his cigarette, and said with a smile, Sister-in-law, did you call me? What can I do for you?","Qiao Lanshu didn't know what to say.","Qiao Lanshu glanced at Zheng Daliu. Zheng Daliu was standing not far away, smoking a cigarette and frowning as he looked at her.","Qiao Lanshu thought it over for a moment before saying, \"Weijun, it's like this. I get off work early today and need to go to the supply and marketing cooperative to buy a few things. I'm worried I won't be able to carry it all, so I wanted to ask if you could help me carry my bags. Would that be too much trouble for you?\"","Deng Weijun scratched his head and said, \"It's not really a trouble...\"","It was just that he had already promised Zheng Daliu to go meet up with some friends to play cards."]},{"number":67,"title":"Chapter 67: Buying Pickles","paragraphs":["Deng Weijun was actually a bit embarrassed. After all, he had told Qin Yuanzheng last time that he would never hang out with Zheng Daliu and his crew again.","But he had known Zheng Daliu for a few years, and when Zheng Daliu invited him to play cards, he figured playing cards couldn't possibly cause any trouble, so he agreed.","Besides, he had nothing else to do and would just be idling away in his dorm room anyway.","Moreover, they had played cards together plenty of times before, always for tiny stakes of a penny or two, so losing didn't hurt.","Zheng Daliu had brought someone else along. They walked over together, glanced at Qiao Lanshu, and asked Deng Weijun, \"Weijun, aren't you leaving yet?\"","As Zheng Daliu spoke, his eyes fixed on Qiao Lanshu's face. Qiao Lanshu and Zheng Daliu were not in the same workshop, and since she was a newly arrived temporary worker, Zheng Daliu had hardly seen her before.","He stared at Qiao Lanshu for a few moments, his gaze making her quite uncomfortable.","Zheng Daliu turned back to Deng Weijun and asked, \"Who is she? Your girlfriend?\"","Deng Weijun was speechless.","Deng Weijun was practically scared to death by his words.","He hurriedly said, \"Daliu, don't spout nonsense! This is my sister-in-law! Girlfriend? Are you crazy for a girlfriend or something?\"","Zheng Daliu was speechless.","Zheng Daliu said impatiently, \"How would I know if you don't tell me? Damn it, are you still coming today or not?\"","Deng Weijun started to hesitate again.","Wang Xue couldn't stand it anymore. She reached out, gave Deng Weijun a heavy smack, and scolded him, \"Comrade Xiao Qiao has already asked for your help, how do you have the nerve to refuse? Sister-in-law? You still have the face to call her that?\"","Deng Weijun quickly said, \"I'll help, I'll help! I never said I wouldn't! Sister-in-law, I'll go with you.\"","He mainly felt that since he had already promised Zheng Daliu, backing out now might make Zheng Daliu hold a grudge against him in the future.","However, being resented by Zheng Daliu was still better than being resented by Qin Yuanzheng, right?","Besides, Qiao Lanshu had helped him before.","Seeing him like this, Zheng Daliu was indeed very displeased.","Deng Weijun said to him, \"Daliu, I won't go with you guys today. You go ahead. I have to help my sister-in-law carry things. It's so cold out, it's not easy for her, you know?\"","Zheng Daliu was silent.","Zheng Daliu tossed away the cigarette in his hand and said with a dark expression, \"Suit yourself.\"","With that, he turned and walked away.","Watching Zheng Daliu leave, Qiao Lanshu finally breathed a sigh of relief. She looked at Deng Weijun and said, \"Let's go then. We'll head to the supply and marketing cooperative to buy some things.\"","Deng Weijun immediately nodded. \"Alright, sister-in-law. Are you going to buy winter vegetables? They're probably almost sold out by now, right?\"","Qiao Lanshu thought for a moment. They actually still had quite a lot of winter vegetables at home. She and Qin Yuanzheng had bought some together last time; there were about six or seven heads of napa cabbage, and a whole basket each of potatoes and sweet potatoes.","After all, the couple only ate dinner at home, so the winter vegetables they currently had stored would probably last them quite a while.","But since she had already said it, she definitely had to buy something heavy for Deng Weijun to help carry. Otherwise, what if he ran off to play cards with that Zheng Daliu again?","Qiao Lanshu thought about it and said, \"Yes, I need to buy winter vegetables. I'm thinking of buying twenty catties of kohlrabi to take back and make pickled vegetables.\"","Qiao Lanshu didn't know how to make pickled vegetables before, but anyone working at a food factory was certainly no stranger to them.","Even if she really didn't know how, she could just go over to the pickle workshop, take one look, and figure it out.","She planned to make the simplest salted vegetables: wash the vegetables clean, let them air dry, then slice them and put them in a vat, alternating a layer of vegetables with a layer of coarse salt. She would press them down firmly with a stone, and then add water.","After soaking like this for about a month, the pickled vegetables would come out sour and crisp. Stir-fried with some pork lard and chili peppers, they would be incredibly appetizing!","Thinking of this, Qiao Lanshu immediately nodded and said to Deng Weijun, \"The vegetables are a bit heavy. Can you carry twenty catties? I also want to buy another pickling vat.\"","Deng Weijun immediately patted his chest and said, \"Sister-in-law, you're underestimating me too much. Not to mention twenty catties, I could carry two hundred catties!\"","Wang Xue laughed at him and said, \"Keep bragging! Look at your skinny, bamboo-pole-like figure. You don't even weigh two hundred catties yourself, and you want to carry two hundred catties?\"","Deng Weijun was speechless.","Wang Xue then asked, \"Xiao Qiao, you know how to make pickled vegetables? You're quite young, but you're really capable.\"","Qiao Lanshu smiled and said, \"I just learned it from others. I haven't actually practiced it myself yet.\"","The three of them walked together. When they arrived at the supply and marketing cooperative, Wang Xue bought some non-staple food coupons, and then the three of them went together to buy winter vegetables.","Wang Xue bought some potatoes, and Qiao Lanshu bought twenty catties of kohlrabi. The vegetables were packed in a bag woven from straw. Deng Weijun tied the bag tightly and hoisted it directly onto his shoulder.","Qiao Lanshu also went to buy a pickling vat and five catties of coarse salt.","After buying these things, Qiao Lanshu got ready to head back.","Actually, Wang Xue didn't have much to buy either. She just felt that with Deng Weijun here, she couldn't let Qiao Lanshu stay alone with him. The people around here were awful gossips, and who knows what rumors they might spread by tomorrow.","Wang Xue walked back with them to the gate of the military residential compound. Then, Wang Xue waited for Qiao Lanshu at the gate, as the two of them had agreed to go buy fried dough twists together.","Deng Weijun helped put the things at the door of Qiao Lanshu's house. He didn't dare to go inside and said, \"Sister-in-law, I'll be leaving then.\"","Qiao Lanshu checked the time. It was still early, only a little past three in the afternoon. With it being so early, what if Deng Weijun ran off to find Zheng Daliu again? Wouldn't her efforts this time have been in vain?","So she said, \"Wait a moment. Help me drop off some things to my cousin-in-law.\"","Speaking of which, when Qiao Lanshu and Qin Yuanzheng got married, her cousin Yang Wenyan had even gifted them a sofa. The sofa was of good quality, very soft to sit on, and certainly not cheap.","This cousin was quite a nice person.","Qiao Lanshu went back inside and picked up the catty of fried dough twists she had just bought yesterday. She first kept a bowl for herself, and then divided the rest into two portions, wrapping them in newspaper.","She then went to the kitchen, took a piece of cured meat and three cured sausages that her father had sent her, put them together, and brought them out. She handed them to Deng Weijun and said, \"It just so happens that my family sent me some cured meat and sausages. Please help me take these things to my cousin and cousin-in-law. It's been cold lately, so I won't go over there myself. Also, take these fried dough twists home for yourself to eat.\"","Deng Weijun didn't cook for himself, so Qiao Lanshu didn't give him any cured meat or sausages.","Mainly, her father hadn't sent much, not even enough to share among a few people.","Deng Weijun took the items and said, \"Alright, this works out perfectly. I won't need to go to the public canteen tonight; I'll just go straight to my brother-in-law's place to eat.\"","Watching him go down the stairs, Qiao Lanshu still felt a bit uneasy and added, \"Take it over there right now. Don't go running around and wasting time, do you hear me?\"","Deng Weijun quickly replied, \"Don't worry, sister-in-law. I guarantee I'll complete the mission!\"","Qiao Lanshu watched him jump down the stairs in a few bounds, disappearing in the blink of an eye, and she shook her head helplessly.","In truth, Deng Weijun wasn't very old, only about eighteen or nineteen. People at this age were the easiest to fool.","In her past life, Qiao Lanshu had never heard of Deng Weijun. Either he had resigned, or something had happened to him.","Qiao Lanshu felt that Deng Weijun was highly dedicated to the food factory and did not seem like the type of person who would just quit.","Therefore, the only explanation was that something must have happened to him later on..."]},{"number":68,"title":"Chapter 68: Director Guan, your zipper is undone.","paragraphs":["Today, Qiao Lanshu could only stall him to prevent him from going out with Zheng Daliu. She had to go to work tomorrow. She planned to meet her cousin-in-law, Deng Xiaozhen, tomorrow afternoon after work, to ask her to keep an eye on Deng Weijun.","Qiao Lanshu took a woven rattan basket, walked out of the house, and prepared to go to the mobile market with Wang Xue to buy fried dough twists.","Wang Xue had been thinking about those fried dough twists for a whole day and night. She previously thought they were too expensive and couldn't bear to buy too many. As a result, her family ate them all in less than a day.","She had two sons, both in elementary school and growing fast. They had big appetites. Usually, they only drank coarse grain porridge or ate potatoes, which lacked any fat or oil, so they were hungry every day.","Wang Xue sighed and said, \"Raising children is really not easy. It's so hard to find something to eat.\"","Hearing this, Qiao Lanshu just smiled and didn't say anything.","Anyway, she didn't have this worry. She wouldn't have children in the future, so she couldn't chime in on topics about kids.","The two of them arrived at the place they visited last time. Sure enough, the woman was still carrying her basket, covered with a black cloth, looking around for customers to buy her fried dough twists.","Wang Xue muttered, \"Where does this person get so much flour to fry dough twists? What kind of family background must she have?\"","Qiao Lanshu was also curious, which was why she followed along to buy fried dough twists again.","As soon as the woman saw Wang Xue and Qiao Lanshu, her eyes lit up. She immediately came over and said, \"You two comrades, are you looking for me?\"","Saying that, she lifted the black cloth covering the basket.","Wang Xue took a look and saw that there weren't many fried dough twists left in the basket. She immediately frowned and said, \"Oh my, you're almost out. I wanted to buy two catties today.\"","She had already prepared one yuan. Although fifty cents a catty was very expensive, she didn't have ration coupons, and she might not be able to buy them normally, so she gritted her teeth and decided to splurge a bit.","Qiao Lanshu also leaned over to take a look. Sure enough, the basket was almost empty, probably holding only a little over a catty in total.","She pondered for a moment and suddenly said, \"I was thinking of buying five catties today. Do you have any more here? Or...\"","She paused and lowered her voice, \"Should we go back to your house with you to get them?\"","The woman hesitated for a moment, thinking to herself that five catties meant two dollars and fifty cents, and seven catties would be three dollars and fifty cents. That was a large sum of money.","These two female comrades had bought from her before, so they were definitely trustworthy.","So, the woman only hesitated for a few seconds before immediately nodding. She said, \"Of course, that's no problem, sisters. Come with me, I still have more at home.\"","Saying that, she led Wang Xue and Qiao Lanshu deep into the alley.","After reaching the end, they came out of the alley and arrived at an area of single-story houses.","The woman stopped at a door, knocked, and said, \"Lin Lao'er, open the door quickly, I'm back.\"","Before long, the door of the single-story house opened. A thin, middle-aged man poked his head out, glanced at her, and said, \"Why are you back so early today?\"","As he spoke, he looked in the direction of Wang Xue and Qiao Lanshu. His face immediately darkened, and he said, \"Why did you bring people here?\"","With that, he hurriedly tried to close the door. Qiao Lanshu suddenly took a few steps forward and said, \"Brother, I'm here to buy fried dough twists. I want five catties.\"","As she spoke, she glanced inside the house. Inside was a courtyard with several large boxes.","Those boxes looked very familiar to her, because they were the exact same boxes used to pack fried dough twists at their food factory.","Qiao Lanshu only got one look before Lin Lao'er closed the door. He said, \"Wait outside!\"","The woman also went inside, telling the two of them to wait while she weighed the fried dough twists inside.","Qiao Lanshu lowered her voice and said to Wang Xue, \"Sister, did you see that just now?\"","Wang Xue hadn't reacted at all. She asked, puzzled, \"See what?\"","Qiao Lanshu: \"...\"","Qiao Lanshu hesitated for two seconds, feeling that if the situation was really what she thought it was, the problem was quite serious.","She shook her head and said, \"That man was so fierce just now.\"","Wang Xue said in a low voice, \"Oh, people like them who engage in speculation and profiteering are just very cautious. It's completely normal that they don't want people showing up at their door.\"","The two waited at the door for a while. The woman wrapped the fried dough twists in newspaper and placed them into Qiao Lanshu's and Wang Xue's baskets respectively, saying to them, \"Five catties, two catties, all weighed out. Don't worry, the weight is absolutely accurate!\"","Qiao Lanshu silently memorized the address, then she and Wang Xue paid the money. Carrying the fried dough twists, the two turned back into the alley and returned the way they came.","After coming out of the alley, Wang Xue and Qiao Lanshu parted ways and headed to their respective homes.","Qiao Lanshu carried the basket with five catties of fried dough twists. It was quite heavy, so she switched hands.","Then, the basket in her hand was snatched away.","Startled, Qiao Lanshu turned her head to look. She saw Guan Wenjun standing there, sporting slicked-back hair and sunglasses, wearing a cold expression. He said, \"Caught you, little girl. You've been hiding pretty well these past few days, haven't you?\"","Qiao Lanshu: \"...\"","Qiao Lanshu looked helplessly at the vegetable basket he had snatched and asked, somewhat puzzled, \"Director Guan, I haven't done anything wrong, right? Why are you catching me?\"","The last time at the orphanage, Guan Wenjun had been praised by her so much that he lost his bearings. In a moment of impulsiveness, he sponsored five special needs children.","Later, the more he thought about it, the more he felt something wasn't right.","He pointed at Qiao Lanshu and accused her, \"Scheming, you are too scheming! On the surface, you look like a good girl, but in reality, you have a black heart.\"","Qiao Lanshu: \"...\"","A black heart? Qiao Lanshu hadn't even called him a psychopath yet.","She reached out her hand and said, \"Give me back my basket, Director Guan. Are you planning to commit a robbery on the street?\"","Guan Wenjun sneered and said, \"Robbery? This is stolen goods! Tell me, have you been engaging in speculation and profiteering?\"","Qiao Lanshu hadn't sold anything; she had only spent money to buy things. Normally, buyers weren't investigated.","She felt that Guan Wenjun was deliberately looking for trouble with her.","So she asked, \"Director Guan, do you just find me very unpleasant to look at?\"","Guan Wenjun froze for a moment. He lowered his head and looked at Qiao Lanshu's fair face, her large, dark eyes, and her nose that was red from the cold wind.","He coughed guiltily and said, \"Unpleasant... well, no, not really.\"","But even if she was very pleasant to look at, he couldn't admit it, right?","Otherwise, it would make him look like he was eager to be trained like a dog by someone else. How humiliating would that be?","He said, \"It's because I find Qin Yuanzheng unpleasant! Of course, if you could divorce Qin Yuanzheng, then I would definitely find you pleasant...\"","Saying that, he added seriously, \"Actually, let me tell you the truth. Qin Yuanzheng is not a good person. He has gone on blind dates with quite a few girls before, and he even stole my fiancee. He definitely didn't tell you about this, did he? He also has infertility and can't have children. I'm different; my physique is excellent.\"","As for where exactly it was excellent, he didn't specify.","The Guan Wenjun that Qiao Lanshu knew in her previous life was already lame in one leg and had fled to the south to do business.","He wasn't this high-spirited back then, nor was he so punchable.","In her previous life, when Qin Yuanzheng was seriously ill, he had wanted to introduce her to Guan Wenjun, and Guan Wenjun had indeed rushed back.","But she had been devastated at the time, completely consumed by the grief of losing Qin Yuanzheng, and hadn't paid Guan Wenjun any attention whatsoever.","Could it be that Guan Wenjun actually had feelings for her?","At this thought, Qiao Lanshu eyed Guan Wenjun with a hint of suspicion.","Guan Wenjun was incredibly vain. Feeling her gaze on him, he immediately stood up straighter and raised his watch-clad arm to slick back his hair.","Qiao Lanshu looked at him and suddenly said, \"Director Guan, your zipper is down.\"","Guan Wenjun: \"???\"","Startled, Guan Wenjun hastily dropped his vegetable basket on the ground and grabbed at his waistband. \"It is? No way!\" he stammered in a panic.","After frantically checking his pants, he found that they were perfectly fine and his belt was securely fastened.","When he finally looked up, Qiao Lanshu was nowhere to be seen.","Basket in hand, she had already sprinted far off into the chilly wind.","Guan Wenjun: \"...\"","He let out a laugh of pure exasperation. Grinding his teeth, he muttered, \"For someone with such short legs, she sure runs fast.\"","Damn, Qin Yuanzheng must be the luckiest bastard alive to have her."]},{"number":69,"title":"Chapter 69: Killed by Someone","paragraphs":["Qiao Lanshu carried the basket. By the time she ran near the residential compound, she was panting heavily.","Having not run for a long time, her physical condition truly made her easily exhausted.","She looked back. Fortunately, Guan Wenjun had not caught up to her. It had really scared her to death.","This Guan Wenjun was completely different from the one in her previous life.","In her past life, Guan Wenjun only had a physical disability in his legs. In this life, however, his brain was just downright abnormal.","Qiao Lanshu thought to herself that she should just take a detour whenever she saw him in the future, lest he cause trouble for her.","Upon returning home, it was still early. Qiao Lanshu placed the fried dough twists on the table and picked up two to taste. To her surprise, they were incredibly crispy and flaky, filling her mouth with a fragrant aroma.","Deep-fried and coated with sugar, the sweet flavor was unbelievably delicious.","They tasted even better than biscuits.","After eating two, Qiao Lanshu picked up another one and took a bite. She felt a bit conflicted. The texture of this fried dough twist was actually quite similar to the ones fried by the factory's production line.","Moreover, she had indeed seen several boxes piled up in that person's room, and they definitely bore the logo of their food factory.","But she couldn't just rashly report it. What if the other party was merely reusing the food factory's boxes, but the fried dough twists were made by themselves?","That wasn't impossible. After all, boxes were a type of asset that needed to be reused.","When the food factory delivered fried dough twists to various supply and marketing cooperatives, department stores, military bases, canteens, and so on, those boxes were meant to be recycled and reused; they wouldn't just be thrown away.","Qiao Lanshu ate a few more, then had another thought. If these really were the factory's fried dough twists, who on earth could smuggle out so many?","And without being discovered by anyone in the factory?","Qiao Lanshu pondered for a while. Just then, a knock sounded at the door.","She quickly wiped her hands, walked to the door, and asked, \"Who is it?\"","Huang Erling's voice came from outside. \"Sister, it's me, Huang Erling.\"","Qiao Lanshu hurried to open the door. Ever since she got married, she hadn't seen Huang Erling for quite some time. She smiled and said, \"Sister Ling, have you been really busy lately? I haven't seen you in ages.\"","Huang Erling was speechless.","Huang Erling thought to herself, she didn't even have a job, what could she possibly be busy with?","She had actually come over and knocked on the door several times, but the timing was never right.","But she was too embarrassed to say that.","She just covered her mouth and chuckled, teasing Qiao Lanshu, \"Oh my, you two just got married. I didn't want to drop by rashly, for fear of interrupting you.\"","Qiao Lanshu blushed slightly and whispered, \"It's fine, really. You're not interrupting.\"","Huang Erling laughed and said, \"I was mainly afraid of bothering Commander Qin. On the very first day of your marriage, the bed collapsed. When an older man gets fired up, it's truly something else. How could I dare to come in?\"","Over the past few days, whenever Huang Erling went out for groceries and chatted with the other military wives in the courtyard, everyone without exception would bring up the newlywed Commander Qin.","The most talked-about topic, of course, was how Qin Yuanzheng had carried out the broken bed on the second day of his marriage and hired someone to build a heated brick bed, known as a kang.","Everyone was experienced in marriage; what was there not to understand?","It was obvious that the wooden bed wasn't sturdy enough and had collapsed under the pressure. So he built a solid kang to go all out without holding back.","The poor little wife, could she even handle it?","Huang Erling lived right next door to them. Everyday when she chatted with the others, since there was rarely any fresh gossip in the compound, they would all swarm around her to pry for details.","How could Huang Erling dare to gossip about Commander Qin's private affairs?","She just claimed she didn't know or wasn't sure. She only mentioned seeing the two of them always together, and that Commander Qin was extremely protective of his little wife.","Teased by Huang Erling, Qiao Lanshu's face instantly turned bright red.","She stepped aside to let her in and said, \"Sister Ling, please stop teasing me. My Brother Zheng isn't back yet, so hurry up and come in to sit down.\"","Looking at Qiao Lanshu's blushing face, Huang Erling thought to herself that this young girl was just too thin-skinned and couldn't handle teasing.","Seeing her flushed and shy appearance, what man wouldn't feel his heart melt for her?","She replied, \"I won't come in for now. I just came to tell you that the thick mattress, the large quilt, and the two padded jackets you asked me to make are finished. Come over and take a look. You can try the clothes on while you're at it, and if they don't fit well, I can still alter them for you.\"","Hearing this, Qiao Lanshu's eyes lit up immediately. She happily said, \"Really? I'll come over and take a look then.\"","She and Qin Yuanzheng had been married for about ten days, and they were still sleeping on the bedding issued to him by the military.","But those were single-person beddings. It was a bit too small for two people to share, so lately, they had been laying out two mattresses on the kang.","Then, Qiao Lanshu and Qin Yuanzheng would each use their own quilt.","However, Qin Yuanzheng didn't like this arrangement. He would always push his own quilt aside and forcefully squeeze into Qiao Lanshu's quilt.","Thinking of this, Qiao Lanshu couldn't help but blush again.","She followed Huang Erling next door.","Huang Erling was also home alone.","Her children had all gone to school, and it wasn't time for them to be dismissed yet.","In a corner of the living room, there was a sewing machine. On the small sofa next to it, the neatly folded quilt and mattress were placed.","The quilt was sewn from red floral fabric, looking very festive.","The mattress, on the other hand, was made of black and gray patchwork fabric. Once taken back, it would still need a separate cover put over it.","Because the kang in Qiao Lanshu's house was quite large—2.4 meters long and 2 meters wide.","Therefore, the mattress Huang Erling made for her was two meters by two meters. With both length and width at two meters, it formed a perfect square when spread out.","She originally wanted to make the mattress according to the exact dimensions of the kang, but there wasn't enough cotton.","It was supposed to be a thick mattress, but as she made it, it ended up not being quite as thick. She said to Qiao Lanshu, \"I used over eight catties of cotton for this mattress. Look, once compressed, it's about an inch and a half thick. It's thick enough for the kang and will definitely be warm! Your Commander Qin is tall, so he needs a mattress this long, otherwise it wouldn't be enough.\"","As she spoke, she also brought out the quilt and spread it out for Qiao Lanshu to see. \"This quilt is also two meters by two meters. I purposely made it much thicker, using thirteen catties of cotton. Look, it's absolutely more than enough!\"","The central heating here only ran for a little over four months. The month or two before the heating started and after it stopped were always extremely cold.","Such thick cotton would definitely be warm enough.","This time, Qin Yuanzheng had found someone to exchange a lot of cotton ration coupons. Combined with what Qiao Lanshu had brought herself, and the various specially approved coupons they received for their marriage.","They had finally managed to save up twenty-five catties of cotton. After making the quilt and the mattress, Huang Erling used the remaining few catties to make a padded cotton jacket and a pair of padded trousers for Qiao Lanshu. With the last half catty, she even made a lightly padded thin coat for her to wear during spring and autumn.","Huang Erling's craftsmanship was truly excellent. Qiao Lanshu looked at the quilt and mattress, then at the padded jacket, and absolutely loved them. She said, \"Sister Ling, your hands are so skilled! I'm so lucky to be your neighbor. Otherwise, I wouldn't even know who to ask for help making these.\"","\"That is for sure,\" Huang Erling said with a hint of pride. \"Before I followed the army, I worked in the garment factory in our county. Later, I resigned because I had a baby and needed to take care of the child.\"","Speaking of this, Huang Erling felt a bit of regret about her job.","However, the military base was too far away, and she could only feel at ease if she took care of her two children herself.","Work could always be found later; it was better to raise the children first.","Huang Erling helped move the quilt to the next room and asked Qiao Lanshu, \"How many quilts do you have at home now?\"","Qiao Lanshu replied, \"This is the only newly made one, but there are two single quilts, the kind issued by the military.\"","Huang Erling understood, after all, her Zhao Jiannong also had this kind of quilt.","She said, \"Bring the military-issued quilts and mattresses from your house to mine. I will take them apart and sew them into a new double one for you. I will make it thinner and larger, perfect for spring and autumn.\"","Qiao Lanshu thanked and praised her repeatedly, making Huang Erling extremely happy.","Huang Erling loved making clothes. Having the clothes and quilts she made recognized and praised gave her a deep sense of satisfaction.","Qiao Lanshu took out ten yuan to give her as a tailoring fee.","She politely declined at first, only accepting five yuan, saying, \"Five yuan is enough. You girl, you do not know how expensive daily necessities are. Even if you have money, you should spend it sparingly. We are so familiar with each other, there is no need to be so polite.\"","Qiao Lanshu had no choice but to take back the five yuan and gave her half a catty of fried dough twists to take back and eat.","This time Huang Erling did not refuse, as her children loved eating them too. So she went home with the five yuan and the half catty of fried dough twists.","Qiao Lanshu carried the two single quilts and mattresses next door and asked Huang Erling to help make a spring and autumn quilt.","When she returned, she laid out the newly made mattress and quilt. Needless to say, the newly made mattress was soft and the quilt was thick, looking very warm.","After making the bed, Qiao Lanshu folded the newly made padded jacket and put it in the wardrobe.","Only then did she come out of the room to cook.","However, they had run out of steamed buns at home, and she did not know how to make them, but Qin Yuanzheng loved eating them.","She pondered whether she should go to the supply and marketing cooperative to see if they sold steamed buns.","It just so happened that they still had food coupons at home.","Anyway, it was still early, she thought, and started putting on her coat, hat, and scarf, ready to go out.","When she went out, it was a little after five in the afternoon. It was still light, but the sun was about to set, and the howling cold wind made it even colder.","Outside the main gate, a car slowly drove in.","She took a look and found the car looked familiar, so she stood aside and stared at the car.","Sure enough, when the car reached her, it stopped immediately.","The car window rolled down, revealing Qin Yuanzheng's face.","Qin Yuanzheng was still wearing his military overcoat and cap, his expression somewhat serious.","Obviously, he had just returned from the mining area military unit, and the two happened to run into each other.","As soon as Qiao Lanshu saw Qin Yuanzheng, her eyes lit up instantly, and she walked over happily, \"Brother Zheng, why did you get off work so early today?\"","It was not even six o'clock yet. He usually got off work at six, and the earliest he would get home was six-thirty. Sometimes, when he had to work overtime for meetings or something, it would be seven or eight o'clock.","However, working overtime until seven or eight did not happen often.","After all, Qin Yuanzheng did not want to work overtime; he just wanted to go home and accompany his little wife.","Qin Yuanzheng was also somewhat surprised to see Qiao Lanshu.","His originally stern expression softened a bit, and he asked gently, \"It is already this time, what are you doing going out? Where are you going?\"","Qiao Lanshu walked over and leaned on the car window to look at him, a constant smile on her face, her two dimples very prominent.","She whispered, \"Isn't it still early? The sun has not set yet. I want to go to the supply and marketing cooperative across the street to buy some steamed buns. We have run out of steamed buns at home.\"","Qiao Lanshu did not even like eating steamed buns, so she was definitely buying them for him.","Thinking of this, Qin Yuanzheng's heart softened a bit.","He could not help reaching out to rub her head and said, \"We will not eat at home today. Let's go to my cousin's house to eat. Come on, get in the car first.\"","Qiao Lanshu thought that Deng Weijun must have brought over the sausages and cured meat, which was why her cousin invited them for dinner.","As a result, as soon as she got in the car, she heard Qin Yuanzheng say, \"My cousin just came to find me, saying he wants to invite us to the state-run restaurant for dinner today, mainly to thank you.\"","Qiao Lanshu was speechless.","Qiao Lanshu blinked blankly and said, \"Thank me? State-run restaurant?\"","The food at the state-run restaurant was very expensive, especially the meat dishes, which were so expensive that ordinary people would not bear to eat them.","Qiao Lanshu did not know what Yang Wenyan meant by this. She said, \"Out of nowhere, what is he thanking me for?\"","Qin Yuanzheng shook his head and said, \"He did not explain in detail. Let's go over there first.\"","It was a good opportunity to take his little wife to a restaurant and order some meat dishes for her to eat. Looking at how thin his wife was, her arms were as thin as chicken claws.","The couple arrived at the state-run restaurant.","Yang Wenyan, Deng Xiaozhen, and Deng Weijun were already waiting there.","Deng Weijun's face was a bit pale, and he looked completely distracted.","Seeing Qin Yuanzheng and Qiao Lanshu come in, he stood up and greeted them, his smile looking worse than a crying face.","For some unknown reason, Deng Xiaozhen suddenly slapped Deng Weijun hard on the back and said angrily, \"Now you know to be scared? Huh? What did I tell you before? I told you not to mix with them, but you would not listen! Now you know to be afraid?\"","Qiao Lanshu remained silent.","Qiao Lanshu had roughly guessed what was going on.","She glanced at Deng Weijun, who looked at her awkwardly and said, \"Sister-in-law, please sit down quickly.\"","Saying that, he eagerly ran over and pulled out a chair for Qiao Lanshu, and Qiao Lanshu sat down silently.","On the other side, Qin Yuanzheng's hand had just rested on the back of a chair. Seeing this scene, he glanced at Deng Weijun, then pulled out the chair and sat down himself.","Yang Wenyan sat there with a complex expression, while Deng Xiaozhen had already quickly stood up.","She walked up to Qiao Lanshu with red eyes and said, \"Xiao Qiao, this time, we really owe it to you. If it were not for you, my brother would probably be gone.\"","Qiao Lanshu was startled. Was the situation even more serious than she had imagined?","She quickly asked, \"Cousin-in-law, sit down first. What... what exactly happened?\"","Deng Xiaozhen sat down, reached out to wipe the corner of her eye, and said, \"That Zheng Daliu took two people out today... and one of them was hacked to death...\""]},{"number":70,"title":"Chapter 70: Poor Appetite","paragraphs":["When Deng Xiaozhen said this, it gave Qiao Lanshu a fright. Her heart rate suddenly sped up, and she immediately turned her head to look at Deng Weijun.","Deng Weijun's face was full of dismay; his pale complexion carried a lingering fear.","He even looked a bit distracted, as if he had suffered a tremendous shock.","Even Qin Yuanzheng frowned tightly and his face instantly turned serious when he heard someone was hacked to death.","This area belonged to the military district, with many troops stationed here.","For a murder to happen here showed just how serious the matter was.","He looked solemnly at Yang Wenyan and asked in a deep voice, \"Cousin, did this happen at the factory? Did someone really die?\"","Yang Wenyan's face was grave. He first sighed, nodded, and then shook his head, saying:","\"Actually, it's not exactly a factory matter, but the factory workers caused trouble. The workers in the pickle workshop were given a half-day off today. Zheng Daliu took two colleagues out to play cards with someone. In the end, his old habits died hard. On the surface, he said they were playing cards, but in reality, he was stealing things from someone's house...\"","Zheng Daliu used to be an idle street punk. He only managed to get a job at the factory because he stumbled upon a good opportunity.","But recently he was tight on money and didn't have enough to spend, so he targeted his friend.","He lied to his colleagues, saying they were going to play cards, and claiming he was afraid of being reported, he asked a colleague to keep watch at the door and call out if anyone came.","Then, he took another colleague into his friend's house. Taking advantage of the fact that his friend had gone to work and hadn't returned, he took several hundred yuan and some grain and food coupons from the house.","Originally, if he had just run away with the money, it might not have resulted in a fatality.","But as he was coming out, he saw his friend's wife busy in the kitchen. Lust took over, and he ran into the kitchen to harass her.","She was a young woman, married for less than a year, with no children yet.","She was terrified at the time, and since she happened to be in the kitchen, she grabbed a kitchen knife during the struggle and slashed wildly. Zheng Daliu was slashed twice and ran out covered in blood. The guy who went in to steal money with him could have run away, but Zheng Daliu pulled him in front to block the knife. He was slashed in a vital spot... Anyway, he's dead.","The one keeping watch at the door only escaped after being chased out and slashed once by the frantic woman.","The lookout suffered the lightest injuries.","Zheng Daliu had knife wounds on his arms and body, and he ran to the hospital himself to get his wounds bandaged.","Yang Wenyan stared at Deng Weijun, his face gloomy, and said:","\"That Zheng Daliu came looking for Weijun in the afternoon, saying he wanted to take him to play cards. He had agreed and was originally going to go together. Moreover, he went out with Zheng Daliu once before and acted as the lookout. This time it was someone else's turn to keep watch. If Weijun had gone, he would have had to go inside the house. When that happened, even if he wasn't hacked to death and made it out alive, he would still be executed by firing squad.\"","The laws are very strict nowadays.","Theft is already heavily punished, let alone theft combined with attempted rape.","Zheng Daliu has already been caught and will definitely be executed.","The lookout was also caught and kept saying he knew nothing and was tricked by Zheng Daliu.","As for how he will be sentenced, it is currently unknown.","But the other one was hacked to death. By the time the comrades from the public security bureau got there, the body was already cold.","Hearing this, Qiao Lanshu's face also turned pale, a wave of lingering fear washing over her heart.","These people nowadays were really too bold!","Greedy for money and lustful, they really would do anything.","The reason she didn't let Deng Weijun go with Zheng Daliu at the time was just a subconscious feeling that something wasn't right. She felt she couldn't let Deng Weijun go out with Zheng Daliu's group, because in her previous life, she had never heard of Deng Weijun, nor had she heard of Zheng Daliu.","This was very strange. After all, a job at the food factory was very good. So many people racked their brains trying to squeeze in but couldn't.","Deng Weijun's brother-in-law was the director of the food factory, and he was proud of his job there.","How could he easily leave the food factory?","So, something must have happened in the middle of it all, but she never imagined it would be something this massive!","The matter was unexpectedly serious, and Qiao Lanshu fell silent.","Deng Xiaozhen's eyes were red, and she cried, \"Xiao Qiao, it's all thanks to you this time. You saved Weijun's life. I really don't know how to thank you enough.\"","Saying this, Deng Xiaozhen cried while pointing at Deng Weijun, scolding, \"You bastard! I told you long ago to behave yourself, not to cause trouble, and not to mix with those unreliable people. You just wouldn't listen! Is that Zheng Daliu any good? Ah? He's always been shady. I heard he likes to harass female workers in the factory from time to time. Don't you know how bad his reputation is? And you still went to play cards with him! I think you're just asking for a beating!\"","As she spoke, Deng Xiaozhen suddenly took off a shoe and started smacking it against Deng Weijun's forehead.","Deng Weijun hugged his head and squatted on the ground, crying and howling, \"Sister, just beat me to death! You might as well just beat me to death!\"","Deng Weijun also felt he deserved to be beaten. Rather than being beaten to death by someone else, he might as well be beaten to death by his own sister.","He was truly terrified today, so he kept crying.","Qiao Lanshu: \"...\"","Qiao Lanshu was stunned by this scene.","She had heard Deng Weijun say before that his sister would hit him.","She thought Deng Weijun was exaggerating, but she didn't expect it to be an actual beating!","And hitting him with a shoe, no less. Qiao Lanshu had never seen such a fierce way of hitting before.","She stood up nervously and quickly said, \"Cousin-in-law, you, you need to calm down. Don't beat him broken... Anyway, the matter has passed. It's good that Weijun is fine. Just be more careful in the future...\"","Deng Xiaozhen cried as she hit him. Actually, she couldn't bear to use her full strength. After all, he was the only younger brother in her maiden family, and she had protected him as he grew up. How could her heart not ache?","She was just too angry, both angry and afraid.","If she didn't give Deng Weijun a beating, she really couldn't vent this frustration.","Panting, Deng Xiaozhen put her shoe back on and ruthlessly kicked Deng Weijun twice, kicking him until he sprawled on the ground, still crying.","Deng Xiaozhen scolded him fiercely, \"If I didn't beat you up today, I don't think you would have learned your lesson. If you don't behave yourself in the future, I'll break your legs and see how you hop around then!\"","Qiao Lanshu: \"...\"","After beating her brother, Deng Xiaozhen walked over, held Qiao Lanshu's hands, and sobbed, \"Xiao Qiao, you are the savior of our Weijun. In the future, this rascal will work like a horse and toil like an ox for you. If you need anything, just order him to do it. If he dares to refuse, I'll beat him to death!\"","Qiao Lanshu: \"...\"","Qiao Lanshu didn't quite know what to say. She reached out and comfortingly patted Deng Xiaozhen's shoulder, saying softly, \"Alright, Cousin-in-law, this matter has passed, and fortunately Weijun is fine, which is the best outcome. Don't be angry anymore, lest you ruin your health from anger.\"","Actually, Deng Weijun's personality was quite good.","He had no intention of doing anything bad, let alone anything illegal. He had neither the desire nor the guts for it.","He was just young, at an age where he liked to gather friends and play around, which was why he was roped into playing cards by Zheng Daliu and the others.","Now that Zheng Daliu and his gang were in trouble, Deng Weijun was scared half to death. He would probably need a long time to recover from this.","Seeing that Qiao Lanshu was a bit tense, Qin Yuanzheng reached out, pulled her to his side, and asked in a low voice, \"Were you scared too?\"","Qiao Lanshu shook her head, then nodded.","Because she thought of how, in her past life, Deng Weijun had very likely already...","Yang Wenyan watched this farce and let out a long sigh, saying, \"This incident in the factory has a bad influence. We'll have to hold a few general meetings over the next few days. I hope this serves as a warning.\"","Yang Wenyan was truly helpless. He had been busy for a long time last time because of Sun Mingyong's matter, and now here was another one.","Were all these young people lately tired of living?","Deng Xiaozhen wiped the corners of her eyes. Having just vented her feelings, she had calmed down a bit. She wiped her eyes again and quickly said, \"Forget it, let's eat first. The food is getting cold.\"","Deng Xiaozhen had specifically invited them to eat at the state-run restaurant to thank Qiao Lanshu.","Although the food at the state-run restaurant was expensive, so be it. Wasn't her brother's life worth the cost of a meal?","The dishes she ordered were all meat dishes: half a roast duck, two bamboo steamers of lamb shaomai, a bowl of fine hand-rolled white noodles for each person, a large pot of Northeastern braised stew, a large plate of stir-fried Liuhe vegetables, and a portion of Peking shredded pork with sweet bean sauce.","She pointed at the plate of Peking shredded pork and said to Qiao Lanshu, \"Xiao Qiao, this shredded pork tastes great. It's stir-fried with sauce and is very fragrant. Use this pancake, roll it up with some green onions, and try it to see if you like it.\"","Deng Xiaozhen took a pancake, rolled up a thick shredded pork wrap, and handed it to Qiao Lanshu to eat.","Unable to refuse such hospitality, Qiao Lanshu quickly took it and said, \"Thank you, cousin-in-law.\"","As she spoke, she glanced at Deng Weijun, who was squatting in the corner, wondering if she should call him over to eat together.","After all, this table of food was full of substantial dishes. It was very expensive and not something they could eat normally.","Deng Xiaozhen didn't even look at her brother. She said, \"Ignore him. Let him cool off in the corner. He almost lost his life, and he still wants to eat? Let him have a good reflection!\"","Qiao Lanshu: \"...\"","Not to mention, Deng Weijun was truly afraid of this sister of his.","After Deng Xiaozhen scolded him a bit, he didn't dare to make a sound, only daring to squat in the corner and question his life choices alone.","Qiao Lanshu had no choice but to sit down and eat the wrap.","Deng Xiaozhen kept putting food into Qiao Lanshu's bowl. \"You definitely haven't had this lamb shaomai before, have you? It's our local specialty. And this Liuhe vegetable dish, made with bean sprouts, glass noodles, eggs, wood ear mushrooms, and so on, stir-fried with vinegar. It's incredibly fragrant and goes great with rice. We use it to wrap in pancakes with the roast duck. This is a dish we are even reluctant to eat during the New Year.\"","Saying that, she rolled another thick pancake for Qiao Lanshu and placed it in her bowl.","Deng Xiaozhen then brought her a bowl of sour soup noodles and said, \"Drinking this in winter, paired with lamb shaomai, warms the stomach and helps you gain weight. You are too thin; you need to eat more.\"","Qiao Lanshu: \"...\"","Although this table was indeed very abundant, a delicacy they might not even get to eat during the New Year.","But Qiao Lanshu had a small appetite. After eating one wrap, her stomach was already a bit full, and she couldn't eat anything else.","Qin Yuanzheng sat next to her, silently polishing off all of her leftovers.","After dinner, the sky had already turned dark.","Deng Weijun went home with Yang Wenyan and the others, because he was also badly frightened and wanted to stay at his sister's house for the night.","Even if he was beaten by his sister, he still had to cling to her.","Qiao Lanshu and Qin Yuanzheng went home together.","While in the car, Qiao Lanshu was a bit silent.","Ever since she got together with Qin Yuanzheng, she had been immersed in their sweet newlywed life and rarely thought about her past life.","Due to trauma, she had actually forgotten almost everything about the two years she was locked in the cave dwelling.","But regarding Qin Yuanzheng, she remembered very clearly.","After Qin Yuanzheng got together with her, he rarely talked about his past. However, because of his poor health, Qiao Lanshu pestered him about it several times.","He finally said that he was injured by an explosion caused by the enemy during a mission to capture a spy.","At that time, his entire back was blown to pieces, and he fainted on the spot. If it weren't for his strong constitution, he would have definitely sacrificed his life.","Thinking of this, Qiao Lanshu silently calculated in her heart. The mission was approximately in this year, but she didn't know the exact time.","Seeing her so silent, Qin Yuanzheng thought she was terrified, and coaxed her in a low voice the whole way:","\"Alright, don't be afraid anymore. Isn't Deng Weijun fine? If I can't come to pick you up from work in the future, I'll let Staff Officer Lin... no, let Xiao Yang... forget it, I'll come myself. I will definitely come to pick you up on time. I won't let you be alone, don't be scared.\"","Qiao Lanshu didn't hear the internal conflict in his words.","Her mind was entirely focused on Qin Yuanzheng's mission.","She turned her head to ask him, \"Brother Zheng, do you have any special missions recently?\"","Qin Yuanzheng shook his head, \"No, what's wrong?\"","Pausing for a moment, he added, \"I just got married, and things in the mining area are very busy. Even if there is a mission, they probably wouldn't let me go.\"","Of course, if he hadn't gotten married, they would definitely let him go if there was a mission.","Because at his level, many people had family members and children. Unlike them, he used to be all by himself, making it convenient for him to go anywhere.","Hearing him say this, Qiao Lanshu was still worried. She said softly, \"Brother Zheng, if you have any mission to carry out, remember you must tell me. Don't leave quietly by yourself, okay?\"","Feeling his little wife's care for him, Qin Yuanzheng's heart felt very warm. He nodded, \"Rest assured, if anything comes up, I'll definitely tell you right away.\"","Hearing him say this, Qiao Lanshu immediately felt relieved.","Qin Yuanzheng said with some heartache, \"Were you scared? You ate very little tonight. When we get back, should I cook you some noodles?\"","Qiao Lanshu's appetite hadn't been very good lately, and she ate very little.","Qin Yuanzheng was incredibly heartbroken over it.","He originally thought that eating out at a restaurant today would allow his wife to eat a bit better.","In the end, Qiao Lanshu's appetite was too small, and she didn't even take many bites.","Instead, it was him who ate two people's worth of food.","Having eaten too much lamb shaomai, his internal heat was burning strongly right now."]},{"number":71,"title":"Chapter 71: Becoming a Warehouse Keeper","paragraphs":["Qiao Lanshu had been feeling restless these past two days, frequently having dreams again.","In her dreams, Qin Yuanzheng always appeared pale and emaciated, lying on a hospital bed.","In the middle of the night, Qin Yuanzheng was startled awake by Qiao Lanshu's crying. He snapped his eyes open and looked down at Qiao Lanshu in his arms.","He saw that her eyes were closed, her face was covered in tears, and she kept calling out, \"Brother Zheng, Brother Zheng.\"","Qin Yuanzheng's heart ached terribly. He didn't know what his wife was dreaming about to make her suffer like this.","He didn't wake her up. Instead, he grabbed his undershirt to wipe her face, pulled her tighter into his embrace, and gently rubbed her hair, whispering, \"I'm here, don't be afraid.\"","Holding Qiao Lanshu, Qin Yuanzheng let out a soft sigh.","Having lost his sleepiness, he turned on his side to let Qiao Lanshu sleep more comfortably. Seeing that she gradually stopped crying, he finally breathed a sigh of relief.","...","The next day, when Qiao Lanshu woke up, she felt her eyes were a bit swollen. While washing up, she looked in the mirror and saw that the corners of her eyes were red and indeed a bit puffy.","She hesitated for a moment, thinking to herself that when Brother Zheng was bullying her last night, she had indeed cried and begged for mercy, but she didn't think she had cried that hard. How did her eyes get so swollen?","After washing up, she braided her long hair into two thick braids. Hair was prone to static electricity in the winter, so tying it into braids was neater.","Her straight bangs had also grown a bit long. Finding them a bit in the way, she found a long, thin black hairpin and pinned her bangs to the side, revealing her smooth, full forehead.","With her bangs pinned up, her face seemed a bit longer. She looked at herself in the mirror and thought that exposing her forehead looked quite nice. She decided not to keep bangs anymore; after all, she wasn't a student now.","Qiao Lanshu finished combing her hair, returned to the bedroom, put on a camisole, and then put on a warm, close-fitting cashmere sweater.","She came out of the room and saw Qin Yuanzheng cooking porridge in the kitchen.","Qin Yuanzheng was truly good at taking care of people. He made breakfast for her every day, deeply afraid she wouldn't have enough to eat.","Qiao Lanshu walked over and called him, \"Brother Zheng.\"","Qin Yuanzheng immediately turned his head: \"You're awake?\"","He glanced at Qiao Lanshu, paused for a moment, and then walked over. He cupped her face in his hands, examining it from left to right for a long while. Suddenly, he leaned in and planted a loud, firm kiss on her forehead. \"Your hair has grown long? Do you want to cut it?\"","Qiao Lanshu shook her head and said, \"I'm not cutting it. I'll just tie it up when it gets longer.\"","Today, Qin Yuanzheng kept checking Qiao Lanshu's expression from time to time, afraid she might be unhappy again.","But seeing that her mood was quite stable, it seemed yesterday's nightmare hadn't affected her much.","After eating, Qin Yuanzheng escorted Qiao Lanshu to the food factory and then headed to the mining area military base himself.","The workload in the pickle workshop had significantly decreased.","Especially in the washing and cutting section, because there were no more fresh local vegetables after the onset of winter, they naturally had no work to do.","They had half a day off yesterday. After arriving at work today, the workers in the pickle section were gathered together. Tang Wenxia, the supervisor of the pickle workshop, held a meeting and told everyone:","\"Winter is setting in, and there isn't much work left in our pickle section. According to the factory director's instructions, we are to go help out in other workshops. Of course, we've worked hard before, so this time we'll be assigned lighter tasks.\"","Except for the pickling section, the fermentation room, and a few boiler workers, most of the female workers were to be loaned out to help in other workshops.","This kind of temporary transfer happened often in previous years, not to mention that the tasks had increased this year, while the manpower hadn't increased much.","Tang Wenxia knew that Qiao Lanshu was introduced by the factory director, so she arranged the easiest job for her. She said, \"Comrade Qiao Lanshu, you will be in charge of watching the warehouse.\"","Wang Xue immediately looked at Qiao Lanshu with envy. She whispered, \"Comrade Xiao Qiao, this is a great job. Besides the timekeeper, the job I envy the most is watching the warehouse.\"","Timekeepers all had strong connections. It was a strict one-person-per-post situation, with not a single vacancy in over a decade.","Wang Xue wouldn't even dare dream of becoming a timekeeper.","She just wanted to watch the warehouse.","You just pull up a small stool, sit down, snack on sunflower seeds, drink some water, and the day is over.","Qiao Lanshu was also a bit surprised. Was Tang Wenxia looking out for her?","Otherwise, how could such a good job be assigned to a temporary worker like her?","After the work was distributed, Wang Xue went to the cake section to help with packaging, which was also a light task, so Wang Xue was quite satisfied.","The over twenty female workers were assigned their tasks and began heading to their respective posts to help.","Qiao Lanshu had thought that after joining the pickle section, she could just idle away the winter without working.","As it turned out, she was being too optimistic.","She arrived at the food factory's large warehouse.","The person originally in charge of the warehouse had taken a leave of absence to go home and have a baby.","So now, it was Qiao Lanshu's job to watch it.","She was only responsible for watching it until after the New Year, a period of about three months. Once the pregnant woman had her baby and returned, Qiao Lanshu would just go back to the pickle workshop.","After picking up the warehouse keys from the personnel office, Qiao Lanshu went to sit in the warehouse.","The warehouse was very large and its doors were usually kept closed. Outside the warehouse, there was a small room with a table, chairs, and a wooden bed that could be used for midday naps.","Qiao Lanshu fetched a thermos of hot water and returned. Sitting in the room, she diligently took a rag and wiped everything down.","After wiping it clean, she sat in the chair, lost in thought. She pondered that starting tomorrow, she could bring her books over to review.","She had attended high school, so when the college entrance examinations were reinstated, she was definitely going to take them.","It was currently the end of 1975, and 1976 was just around the corner. The time left for her to review was already running out.","Thinking this, Qiao Lanshu rummaged through the drawers. Inside, there was an abacus, two fountain pens, a bottle of ink, a ruler, an eraser, pencils, a rag, and so on.","In another drawer lay a stack of five or six notebooks.","She took the notebooks out to look and found that they contained the records of goods entering and leaving the warehouse.","The notebooks had dates and the quantities of outgoing goods scribbled on them.","However, they did not specify the year or the exact time, let alone have the signatures of the inventory clerks or receivers.","Isn't this job a bit too simple?","Just as Qiao Lanshu was thinking this, someone knocked on the window.","She quickly opened the window. Outside stood several male workers pulling a cart. The man leading them said, \"Comrade, I'm here to pick up goods. Please open the warehouse door.\"","As he spoke, the man handed Qiao Lanshu a pickup slip.","Qiao Lanshu reached out, took it, and glanced at it. But before she could even see it clearly, the man suddenly snatched the slip back. He said impatiently, \"I say, you're new here, aren't you? Why don't you know how to do things? We're in a hurry to deliver grain to the cafeteria. Can you stop dawdling?\"","Qiao Lanshu did not open the door. She took out the registration notebook and wrote down the year, month, day, and time on it, accurate to the exact minute and second.","Then, she asked, \"Which workshop are you from? What goods are you picking up, how much, and where are they being delivered? Which supervisor signed off on your paperwork?\"","The man outside: \"...\""]},{"number":72,"title":"Chapter 72: Three Hundred Jin of Fried Dough Twists","paragraphs":["The previous warehouse manager was a pregnant woman who usually stayed in the small cabin and never stepped out the door.","Whenever someone came to pick up goods, she would just casually glance at the slip without looking closely, and then open the door.","As for whether she actually registered the items, these deliverymen had no idea.","Anyway, it was quite easy for them to pick up goods, and they had never been questioned before.","Now that Qiao Lanshu was here and asking them so many questions, they felt quite annoyed.","The man leading the group said, Oh, you little girl, why do you have so much to say? Is this how you waste people's time?","Qiao Lanshu's expression instantly turned serious. Standing behind the window, she stared at the man and said, Since you don't want to waste time, then hand over the slip in your hand so I can take a careful look. You want to take goods from me without even showing me the pickup slip? Who knows if your slip is forged? If something goes wrong later, who will take responsibility, me or you?","The man immediately got angry. He said, Listen to what you're saying! This slip of mine was signed and approved by Director Wei. Could it be wrong?","Qiao Lanshu reached her hand out. Give me the slip.","The man was a bit irritated, but he was just a driver responsible for delivering goods. If he really delayed things, he could not bear the responsibility either.","Therefore, he reluctantly handed the slip to Qiao Lanshu.","Qiao Lanshu took a look at the pickup slip.","The slip clearly stated the year, month, and day, as well as the receiving unit. At the bottom corner under the approving supervisor, Wei Zhengye's name was signed.","Qiao Lanshu collected the slip, registered it in her own notebook, and said to Du Erniu, One hundred catties of fried dough twists, right? I'll open the door for you.","Du Erniu looked at Qiao Lanshu impatiently and scolded her, You really are too much trouble. Wouldn't it have been better if you just opened the door earlier? You wasted ten minutes of my time.","Qiao Lanshu did not bother to argue with him.","She took the keys and opened the warehouse door, and Du Erniu led the two men inside.","Suddenly thinking of something, Qiao Lanshu came over with a fountain pen and said to Du Erniu, Wait a moment, Brother Du. It's better if we check things clearly. Look, this box is 10 kilograms, which means 20 catties per box.","Holding the pen, she drew a circle around the 10 kg mark on the cardboard box.","Du Erniu said impatiently, I've been delivering goods for years, do I need you to tell me?","Qiao Lanshu was not angry. She drew a circle over the 10 mark on all five boxes of fried dough twists. Alright, five boxes in total. Brother Du, please count them.","It was just five boxes of fried dough twists, what was there to count?","Du Erniu cursed dirty words in his heart but was too lazy to speak up. He led his men to carry the five boxes of fried dough twists and left.","Qiao Lanshu followed behind them and locked the warehouse door again.","Qiao Lanshu said again, Brother Du, wait a moment.","Du Erniu: ...","Du Erniu had completely lost his temper by now. He said, If you have any other bullshit, spit it out quickly.","Qiao Lanshu handed over the pickup slip he had just brought, pointed to the deliveryman's column, and said to Du Erniu, Here, you need to sign to prove that you are the one delivering the goods. It will be easier to find the right person when checking in the future.","Du Erniu: ...","Du Erniu had never signed anything before. Of course, the warehouse manager had never even collected this kind of pickup slip before either.","After Du Erniu finished delivering the goods, he would just throw the slip away directly.","Since when did he need to sign?","If the warehouse manager were a man, he really would have gotten into a huge argument with him.","But the warehouse manager was a short and thin little girl who spoke gently and did things methodically.","No matter how angry he was, he could not vent his anger on a female comrade, right?","Arguing with a woman, wouldn't he lose his face?","Du Erniu walked over, took the pen, and crookedly wrote down the three characters of Du Erniu.","He hadn't studied for many years and didn't know how to write many words, but fortunately, he still knew how to write his own name.","Seeing him sign, Qiao Lanshu smiled and said, Thank you, Brother Du. By the way, if you come to pick up goods in the future, this pickup slip must also be given to me for my records. If you need a copy for yourself, ask the business department to make a carbon copy for you. Hand over the slip, take the goods.","Du Erniu was completely out of temper.","He said, Got it, got it. Anything else? If not, I'm going to deliver the goods.","Qiao Lanshu shook her head, Nothing else. The weather is cold and the roads are slippery, Brother Du, drive slowly on the road. Have a smooth trip.","Du Erniu: ...","Du Erniu felt that this new warehouse manager was really a bit weird.","If you said she was easy to talk to, she had a bunch of messy requirements, holding him up and not letting him go.","If you said she wasn't easy to talk to, she had a very sweet mouth and even told him to drive slowly.","He really had to hand it to her.","After Du Erniu left, Qiao Lanshu immediately tore off a piece of paper and wrote large characters on it: [Hand over the slip, take the goods]","Fortunately, those who came to the warehouse to pick up goods generally had pickup slips signed and approved by the workshop supervisors.","So throughout the day, Qiao Lanshu's work went quite smoothly.","As soon as it was time to get off work, Qiao Lanshu locked all her work receipts in the drawer and then locked the door of the warehouse manager's duty cabin.","Immediately after, she hurriedly put on her padded cotton jacket and came out of the factory.","When Wang Xue saw her, she chased after her and called out, Xiao Qiao, Xiao Qiao! What are you running for? Is there an emergency?","Seeing it was Wang Xue, Qiao Lanshu panted and whispered, Sister, I still have to go buy fried dough twists today. Are, are you going?","Today, one hundred catties of fried dough twists flowed out of the warehouse. Qiao Lanshu saw the receiving unit; it was received by the state-run restaurant.","But Qiao Lanshu just felt something was not quite right. Because in the previous warehouse manager's notebook, it was registered twice, a total of one hundred kilograms of fried dough twists had been taken away. Plus this time, it was a total of three hundred catties.","Why was it always picked up one hundred catties at a time?","Could there be some problem in this?","Qiao Lanshu felt something was wrong, which was why she took the pen and drew circles on the boxes of fried dough twists.","She was anxious to go buy fried dough twists now just to go over and confirm it.","In case her guess was right...","Wang Xue sighed and said, Fried dough twists are too expensive, fifty cents a catty. I can't bear to buy them. I'll buy them after a while.","Qiao Lanshu then said, My Brother Zheng likes to eat them. I want to buy a few more catties to bring to him to eat at the military base.","Wang Xue knew that military officers had money, and spending a few bucks on fried dough twists wouldn't hurt.","So she said, I have nothing to do anyway, I'll accompany you.","The two walked out of the factory arm in arm, and Qiao Lanshu did not see Qin Yuanzheng's car.","He was probably held up by a meeting again.","Qiao Lanshu didn't wait either, and hurriedly rushed to the mobile market with Wang Xue.","On the way, Wang Xue even said to her, Oh, Xiao Qiao, you don't need to be in such a hurry. The fried dough twists definitely won't be sold out.","Qiao Lanshu of course knew the fried dough twists wouldn't be sold out.","Wasn't she just worried that people would switch the boxes?"]},{"number":73,"title":"Chapter 73: Thinking She Wanted to Have an Affair with Him","paragraphs":["Qiao Lanshu was anxious to buy fried dough twists, so she and Wang Xue went back to the place where they had bought them before.","Sure enough, the woman was still there.","It seemed she had been selling for quite a while.","She even recognized Qiao Lanshu and Wang Xue. Upon seeing them, she greeted them very enthusiastically, \"Oh, it's you two again! Are you here to buy more fried dough twists?\"","Qiao Lanshu nodded. \"Yes, I want to buy more today.\"","The woman said with a hint of pride, \"Well, my fried dough twists are delicious, aren't they? Let me tell you, the taste of our fried dough twists is absolutely impeccable. They're practically the same as the ones produced by the food factory.\"","Neither Wang Xue nor Qiao Lanshu refuted her claim.","Because they really were almost identical to the food factory's products.","Qiao Lanshu asked her, \"Sister, how much more do you have? I want to buy a lot. Do you have enough?\"","The woman replied, \"Of course I do. I have as much as you need. How many catties do you want?\"","Qiao Lanshu said, \"I want five catties.\"","The woman's basket naturally didn't hold five catties, so just like last time, she took Qiao Lanshu and Wang Xue directly to her house to get the goods.","Compared to the previous time, the woman was much less vigilant this time.","After knocking on the door, she carried her basket inside. The door was left ajar, not fully closed.","Qiao Lanshu stepped forward and peeked inside. A middle-aged man inside suddenly yelled fiercely, \"What are you looking at? Get out of here!\"","With that, he immediately slammed the door shut.","Inside, the woman scolded him while weighing the fried dough twists. \"Lin Lao'er, why are you being so fierce? She's a regular customer who's bought from us several times. What if you scare her away?\"","Because the weather was too cold, Qiao Lanshu always wrapped half of her face in a scarf.","Wearing a hat as well, only her eyes were exposed. She looked quite young and docile.","But since Lin Lao'er was engaging in speculative and profiteering activities, he was terrified, so everyone looked like someone who was going to report him.","He said gruffly, \"I don't care who she is, we have to be careful. If we get reported, both of us are doomed.\"","Hearing this, the woman laughed and said, \"Oh, come on. A little girl like her, report us? She probably doesn't have the guts.\"","Saying so, she weighed out five catties of fried dough twists, brought them outside, and handed them to Qiao Lanshu. The two exchanged money and goods simultaneously.","Qiao Lanshu took the fried dough twists and immediately pulled Wang Xue away.","Wang Xue even teased her, saying, \"You were in a rush coming here, and now you're in a rush leaving. Your man probably hasn't even gotten off work yet. Rushing won't help you see him any sooner.\"","At this moment, Qiao Lanshu was in no mood to joke with Wang Xue.","Because she had just seen clearly that the several boxes stacked inside were the exact ones sent out from the food factory warehouse that afternoon!","She clearly saw the circles drawn with a black fountain pen on the boxes.","Previously, she had been a bit suspicious, worried that she might be wrongly accusing these people. After all, when goods were sent out from the food factory, people would often reuse the factory's boxes.","But now, she could say with absolute certainty that ninety-nine percent of the fried dough twists inside had been taken from their food factory.","Because the previous warehouse keeper hadn't kept detailed records, and the factory lacked a comprehensive registration process for these procedures.","As long as there was an order written by the business department and signed by a leader at or above the level of a workshop supervisor, goods could be picked up from the warehouse.","It seemed the food factory itself had some major issues.","Thinking of this, Qiao Lanshu figured she probably couldn't handle this alone. She decided it would be better to inform the factory manager.","When they reached the vicinity of the supply and marketing cooperative, Wang Xue bid farewell to Qiao Lanshu.","Carrying the fried dough twists, Qiao Lanshu planned to tell Qin Yuanzheng about this as soon as he returned, and then go find her cousin with him.","This matter had to be dealt with quickly, lest the other party sell out of the fried dough twists and the stolen goods disappear without a trace.","Carrying a basket of fried dough twists, Qiao Lanshu walked to the entrance of the military residential compound. Then, as luck would have it, she saw Guan Wenjun again.","Qiao Lanshu: \"...\"","Why was this Guan Wenjun so free?","Her Brother Zheng was clearly busy to death, yet here he was, loitering around the area every day, all just to get back at her?","Guan Wenjun was deliberately staking out the place.","He was staking out Qiao Lanshu.","As the dignified director of the provincial revolutionary committee, his presence outside struck fear into people's hearts. Who wasn't afraid of him?","Yet, he had been played for a fool by this little girl.","How could he swallow this insult?","He was truly at odds with Qiao Lanshu now. He refused to believe he couldn't handle a little girl.","As soon as Guan Wenjun saw Qiao Lanshu appear, he instinctively looked down to check his belt and zipper.","Confirming everything was fine, he rolled up his sleeves, pointed at Qiao Lanshu, and said, \"You little short legs, let's see how you run away this time!\"","He stared at Qiao Lanshu warily and strode forward, terrified that this little short legs would run off again.","To his surprise, when Qiao Lanshu saw him, not only was she unafraid, but she also didn't run.","Her eyes lit up, and she happily went up to him. Blinking her dark, jade-like eyes at him, she said excitedly, \"Director Guan! It's so great that you're here!\"","Guan Wenjun: \"...\"","Seeing her smiling eyes curving like crescents and her excited demeanor as if she had just seen her savior, Guan Wenjun paused in his tracks.","His protective instincts suddenly overflowed.","Guan Wenjun put one hand in his pocket, smoothed his hair with the other, and stood there in a rather handsome pose.","The cold wind was howling, and everyone had wrapped themselves up tightly in their clothes.","He, on the other hand, for the sake of looking good, hadn't even buttoned his black trench coat. He just left it open, letting the hem flutter in the wind.","He snorted coldly and said in a very aloof manner, \"Now you know to beg for mercy? Let me tell you, it's too late!\"","Qiao Lanshu didn't even notice him trying to act cool. In her eyes, no matter how handsome these men were, none could compare to her Brother Zheng.","She walked right up to Guan Wenjun and looked left and right, appearing a bit sneaky.","Guan Wenjun almost thought she wanted to have an affair with him.","Then, Qiao Lanshu lowered her voice and said, \"Director Guan, I want to make a report! For the sake of profit, someone took advantage of the management loopholes in our food factory and stole at least three hundred catties of fried dough twists! They are selling them in the mobile market. Look, these are the stolen goods. I bought them for fifty cents a catty.\"","Guan Wenjun: \"...\"","Guan Wenjun stared at her face. Whether out of disappointment or something else, he said somewhat speechlessly, \"You got this close just to tell me this?\"","Qiao Lanshu looked at Guan Wenjun and said with a serious expression, \"Director Guan, this is a very serious matter. If you don't have the ability to handle it, then I'll go to the police station.\"","Qiao Lanshu had pretty much figured out Guan Wenjun's personality.","Every word she spoke poked right at his sore spots.","Guan Wenjun instantly flared up. He said, \"What do you mean I don't have the ability to handle it? There is nothing in Longcheng that I can't handle!\"","He took off his sunglasses, stuffed them into his pocket, and asked with a serious face, \"Where is the address? I'll go take a look right now.\""]},{"number":74,"title":"Chapter 74: Let's eat on the kang.","paragraphs":["Qiao Lanshu had been to that place twice, so naturally she knew where it was.","Thus, she gave Guan Wenjun the address and told him, \"That house is in an alley, with alleys both in front and behind it. It's a residential area. When you go over there, make absolutely sure not to alert the snake in the grass. Otherwise, if they run away, they'll be hard to catch.\"","Guan Wenjun looked at Qiao Lanshu, let out a cold snort, and said, \"Just you wait and see. My capabilities speak for themselves.\"","With that, he turned to leave. However, after taking two steps, he suddenly doubled back. He sized Qiao Lanshu up with a suspicious look and asked her, \"You're not messing with me, are you? Is there really someone bold enough to steal fried dough twists from the food factory?\"","Qiao Lanshu immediately handed her basket to him and said, \"I'm really not lying to you, Director Guan. If you don't believe me, look at these fried dough twists yourself. I've bought them three times in a row now.\"","Saying that, she raised her hand and said with a solemn expression, \"I swear, if I'm lying to you, may you be struck by lightning!\"","Guan Wenjun hurriedly pressed her hand down and said, \"Alright, alright, alright. You little brat, why are you making such a vicious oath for no reason? If Qin Yuanzheng finds out, wouldn't he shoot me? Fine, I'll go take a look right now.\"","With that, he turned and left.","However, as he walked, he felt something wasn't quite right.","Was there something wrong with the vicious oath that little girl just made?","Guan Wenjun hurriedly called four people from the Revolutionary Committee, and the five of them ran toward the alley together.","Qiao Lanshu cherished her life very much. Although she was the one who reported it, she had no intention of going with them.","She stood at the entrance of the military compound for a while and soon saw Qin Yuanzheng driving back.","She immediately went up to greet him happily.","Qin Yuanzheng got out of the car looking a bit gloomy. When Qiao Lanshu ran over, he quickly took the basket from her hand without saying a word.","Qiao Lanshu looked at him in confusion and asked, \"Brother Zheng, are you in a bad mood today?\"","Qin Yuanzheng turned to look at her and asked quietly, \"What were you and Guan Wenjun just talking about?\"","From far away, he had seen Guan Wenjun and Qiao Lanshu pulling and tugging at each other. Qiao Lanshu raised her hand, and Guan Wenjun pressed it down.","Then he kept coaxing her?","It looked just like they were flirting.","Qin Yuanzheng, this older man, had finally managed to marry his beloved little wife, and he cherished her more than anything.","Normally, he even kept his guard up against Staff Officer Lin and Xiao Yang, preventing them from meeting Qiao Lanshu.","As a result, Guan Wenjun, the person he should be guarding against the most, had come knocking.","How could he tolerate this?","Qin Yuanzheng felt very uncomfortable in his heart.","It was as if a jar of vinegar had been overturned, but he could not show it too obviously, lest he appear too petty in front of his wife.","Hearing him ask this, Qiao Lanshu immediately said, \"It's like this, Brother Zheng. I found out that someone stole fried dough twists from our food factory and is selling them at the mobile market.\"","Qiao Lanshu told Qin Yuanzheng everything she had discovered.","After listening to her explanation, Qin Yuanzheng's expression also turned somewhat serious. \"Since the receiving unit is listed as the state-run restaurant, there must be someone at the state-run restaurant working as their inside connection. Otherwise, Du Erniu is a suspect.\"","Qin Yuanzheng was in the military, and the military and the Revolutionary Committee were two different systems. Since this matter had already been handed over to the Revolutionary Committee, he would not interfere.","After all, this was not within the military's jurisdiction.","He breathed a sigh of relief, pinched Qiao Lanshu's cheek, and said, \"Next time there's such a risky matter, tell me first, and I'll find someone to handle it. Don't go by yourself, it's too dangerous.\"","Qiao Lanshu nodded. \"Don't worry, Brother Zheng. I know.\"","She had originally intended to wait for Qin Yuanzheng to come back and tell him.","It was just that Guan Wenjun appeared first, so it happened to be handed over to their Revolutionary Committee to handle.","After returning home, Qin Yuanzheng, as usual, held Qiao Lanshu and kissed her for a long time.","Not seeing her for a day, he missed her terribly.","Not to mention he had just been provoked, making him want to hold his little wife and be intimate even more.","Qiao Lanshu was already used to his dominance and demands, and at this moment, she softly collapsed into his arms, letting him have his way with her.","Qin Yuanzheng said in a low voice, \"From now on, stay away from that Guan Wenjun. He is not a good person.\"","Qiao Lanshu's lips were numb. She felt that Brother Zheng was a bit rough today, as if he was afraid of something.","She whispered, \"Okay, I know.\"","Qin Yuanzheng looked at her, reached out his hand, and wiped his rough finger across her lips.","He asked in a low voice, \"You married far from home. Will you regret it in the future? Will you leave me behind and run back to Yangcheng?\"","As he spoke, he started to worry again. People said that as long as a woman had a child, she would naturally be tied down by the child and wouldn't run away easily.","But he suffered from infertility. What could he do?","He was afraid that Qiao Lanshu would despise him in the future and run off with another man. What would he do then?","Thinking like this, he grew somewhat frustrated again, pressing Qiao Lanshu down and kneading her like dough.","He brought tears to Qiao Lanshu's eyes. As she begged for mercy, she said, \"Brother Zheng, we haven't eaten yet...\"","Qin Yuanzheng said in a muffled voice, \"We'll eat on the kang bed. I will definitely feed you until you're full.\"","With that, he picked Qiao Lanshu up in his arms, and the two walked into the room.","Qin Yuanzheng absolutely loved the kang in his house.","It was also due to his foresight; when they first got married, he knew he had to build a kang.","If he had bought a wooden bed frame back then, it definitely wouldn't have been sturdy enough.","With his brute strength like a wild bull, a wooden bed frame would probably fall apart after just a few thrusts.","Just as the atmosphere between the two grew heavier.","When Qin Yuanzheng was ready to begin, a knock came from the door.","The couple's movements paused, both feeling left hanging in mid-air.","Qin Yuanzheng was so irritated. He was already an arrow on the bowstring, ready to fire, and yet someone came knocking.","He endured it until his head was covered in sweat, his entire upper body drenched.","He took a deep breath, covered Qiao Lanshu with the quilt, and whispered, \"I'll go out and see who it is. Wait for me here.\"","Saying that, he got off the kang, put on loose pants and a tank top, walked outside, and asked, \"Who is it?\"","From outside the door came Guan Wenjun's exasperated voice. He said, \"It's me! Qin Yuanzheng, open the door quickly!\"","Qin Yuanzheng: \"...\"","Thinking of how Guan Wenjun had just gone to catch the culprits, Qin Yuanzheng let him in, albeit very reluctantly.","Qiao Lanshu also heard Guan Wenjun's voice. She hurriedly got up, put on her clothes and pants, threw on her padded cotton jacket, tidied her hair, and quickly came out as well.","Guan Wenjun walked in from outside, with his four subordinates still standing outdoors.","He stood in the room, his clothes dirty and his face full of gloom, saying, \"Where is your wife? Tell her to come out! What exactly is going on this time? Didn't she report that someone was stealing and selling fried dough twists, three hundred catties of them? When I went over there, the yard was empty! I didn't see a single fried dough twist!\"","Qiao Lanshu hid behind Qin Yuanzheng and said in disbelief, \"That's impossible. Did you go to the wrong house?\"","Guan Wenjun: Didn't you say it was the third house on the south side of Makou Alley off Guanxi Street, the one with the pomegranate tree by the door? The one with the middle-aged couple where the man is named Lin Lao'er and the woman wears a headscarf?","Qiao Lanshu nodded, a doubtful look on her face: Yes, that is the right house. Did you really not see any fried dough twists?","It was not that Guan Wenjun did not believe Qiao Lanshu, but his luck this time had just been absolutely rotten. He said: No, I even went inside the house to search. Not only did I not find any fried dough twists, but I was chased for two streets by that woman wielding a broom dipped in a cesspit. Fuck!"]},{"number":75,"title":"Chapter 75: Take a break tonight","paragraphs":["Qiao Lanshu and Guan Wenjun double-checked.","They found that Guan Wenjun indeed hadn't gone to the wrong place, but the other party probably had lookouts set up, so they had transferred all the goods in advance.","Qin Yuanzheng and Qiao Lanshu sat on the sofa. Guan Wenjun sat opposite them, familiarly taking a teacup and pouring himself some tea without treating himself as an outsider.","He even rummaged through the drawer, found a packet of tea leaves, and put a pinch into his cup.","Qin Yuanzheng was only tolerating him this much for the sake of his little wife. After all, he was afraid that if a fight broke out, it would scare Qiao Lanshu.","In his eyes, his wife was delicate, lovely, weak, and kind-hearted, unable to withstand the slightest fright.","Guan Wenjun brewed tea for himself and took a few sips. Qiao Lanshu said, somewhat worriedly, \"What should we do now? Are we just going to let this go?\"","Such a big matter couldn't just be ignored.","Qin Yuanzheng had already heard the whole story and now said,","\"They probably have quite a few lookouts. After all, people who do this kind of thing are definitely very cautious. However, being able to transfer all the goods in such a short time not only requires multiple people to help but also a very close transfer site. They probably moved the fried dough twists somewhere nearby, we just aren't sure where. If we go over and investigate the area, we might find some clues.\"","Guan Wenjun sighed and said, \"We just made a scene, and now we've wasted time here. Even if there were any traces, they would have been wiped clean. Going back won't yield anything.\"","Qin Yuanzheng looked at Guan Wenjun faintly and said, \"If you don't have the ability, then don't stick your neck out blindly. Leave things to those who are more capable, can't you?\"","Guan Wenjun: \"...\"","He had already heard the words \"no ability\" twice from this couple today. He said angrily, \"Who says I have no ability? It's the other party who is too cunning. Even you might not have a solution.\"","Seeing that they were about to argue again, Qiao Lanshu hurriedly said, \"Brother Zheng, Director Guan, why don't we discuss this matter with Factory Manager Yang? He is the factory manager. It would definitely be more convenient for him to investigate this.\"","As Qiao Lanshu spoke, she lowered her voice and added, \"Besides, I have a suspect in mind. It might have something to do with him...\"","...","This was no small matter, so it needed to be dealt with promptly. The longer it dragged on, the harder it would be to trace.","Therefore, Qin Yuanzheng could only take Qiao Lanshu and Guan Wenjun to find Yang Wenyan.","The few of them discussed it carefully and decided to lure the snake out of its hole.","Of course, Qin Yuanzheng didn't participate, as he didn't have the time anyway.","In the end, this task still fell on Guan Wenjun's shoulders.","After the matter was discussed, Yang Wenyan said to Qiao Lanshu gratefully, \"Sister-in-law, thank you so much for this time. If you hadn't told me in advance, I would still be kept in the dark. If it was found out later...\"","Then he, as the factory manager, would not be able to shirk the blame and would definitely be disciplined.","The previous Sun Mingyong marriage fraud incident, as well as the incident where Zheng Daliu was hacked a few days ago, actually had nothing to do with the factory's management and efficiency.","As the factory manager, all he had to do was hold a meeting and give everyone a warning.","But this fried dough twist incident involved theft and embezzlement, severely damaging the interests of the food factory and the workers. As the factory manager, although he was just caught in the crossfire, he would still be held accountable.","He was so grateful that he didn't know what to say, only stating, \"You saved Weijun last time, and now you've saved me. Comrade Xiao Qiao, you are the savior of our family!\"","Qiao Lanshu was so young, beautiful, and healthy. She didn't despise Qin Yuanzheng and married him as his wife. Yang Wenyan, as the older cousin, actually thought Qiao Lanshu was pretty great and kept urging Qin Yuanzheng to treat his wife better.","When he wrote to Qin Yuanzheng's parents, he also praised Qiao Lanshu for a long time.","He was even planning to make Qiao Lanshu a regular employee when the factory got the quota in the spring after the New Year.","But now, Qiao Lanshu had helped them twice again.","Qiao Lanshu was simply their family's lucky star!","Yang Wenyan said to Qiao Lanshu, \"After this matter is over, I must thank you properly!\"","Qiao Lanshu quickly said, \"We are all family, Cousin, you don't need to be so polite. Besides, no matter who sees such a thing that damages the food factory's interests, they can't just sit by and do nothing.\"","Qin Yuanzheng was anxious to go home.","How much time had been delayed already?","He checked the time; it was already past nine in the evening. Usually, at this time, he would have already taken Qiao Lanshu to the bed and had meal after meal.","A man who had just tasted the forbidden fruit was very impatient.","Anyway, he felt himself getting more and more restless. As soon as it got dark, he only wanted to pull his wife onto the bed and leave everything else until dawn.","Qin Yuanzheng pulled Qiao Lanshu out of the room and said to Yang Wenyan, \"Then Cousin, it's getting late, we'll head back first.\"","Yang Wenyan nodded: \"Alright, hurry back and rest.\"","Yang Wenyan's complexion wasn't looking too good, carrying anger, disappointment, and some disbelief. He stood at the door, thinking that at least three hundred catties of the factory's fried dough twists had been stolen. What audacity!","Guan Wenjun looked at Yang Wenyan and said with a smile, \"Factory Manager Yang, don't worry, I will definitely investigate this thoroughly for you.\"","Yang Wenyan: \"...\"","Yang Wenyan gave Guan Wenjun a somewhat wary look, smiled awkwardly, and said, \"Then I'll have to trouble Director Guan.\"","In Yang Wenyan's heart, this Guan Wenjun was no good person.","Could he really be so kind-hearted as to come and help him investigate the case?","Yang Wenyan rather believed he wanted to come and raid his house.","So, after Yang Wenyan politely saw Guan Wenjun out, he quickly closed the door.","Guan Wenjun: \"...\"","Coming out of Yang Wenyan's house, Guan Wenjun thought of Qiao Lanshu saying he had no ability. What a joke, he hated it the most when others questioned him.","Therefore, he didn't even go to sleep.","He hurried to gather his subordinates to stake out and investigate the case.","He didn't believe it. Could those three hundred catties of fried dough twists just vanish into thin air?","...","By the time Qin Yuanzheng brought Qiao Lanshu back home, it was almost ten o'clock.","Ten o'clock was already very late. Qin Yuanzheng sighed; their wonderful intimate time had all been wasted.","When he went out, he was full of energy, but now that he was back, he looked down at himself, all wilted.","He was really feeling wronged.","Qiao Lanshu knew he was uncomfortable. Looking at his face, she also found it funny and said, \"Brother Zheng, stop looking, it's time to sleep.\"","Qin Yuanzheng: \"...\"","Qin Yuanzheng looked at her, suddenly took a large stride forward, picked Qiao Lanshu up in his arms, and walked towards the inner room. He said, \"No matter how late it is, we have to do it once. Don't even think about running away.\"","Qiao Lanshu hurriedly said, \"Wait a minute, Brother Zheng, how about we take a day off tonight?\"","Ever since they got married, she hadn't had a single day of rest. Who could stand working overtime every single day?"]},{"number":76,"title":"Chapter 76: Stealing grain will get you shot.","paragraphs":["Qiao Lanshu was pressed onto the kang by Qin Yuanzheng, helplessly working overtime all night.","The next day, she went to work yawning the whole way.","Fortunately, she was now a warehouse keeper. As long as no one came to pick up goods, she had plenty of free time.","Previously, this position was always assigned to pregnant women or employees with mobility issues.","Qiao Lanshu suspected that the supervisor of the pickle workshop had assigned her here out of respect for Factory Director Yang Wenyan.","Today, Qiao Lanshu brought along a few high school textbooks to work. She placed them in the warehouse keeper's small booth, sitting down to read and review whenever she had nothing else to do.","Not long after her shift started, the delivery driver, Du Erniu, suddenly came knocking on the door.","Qiao Lanshu opened the window. Seeing it was him, she assumed he was there to pick up goods and smiled, Good morning, Brother Du. Do you have an order form?","Du Erniu: ...","Faced with Qiao Lanshu's smiling face, Du Erniu's originally cold and gloomy expression softened a bit. He said, Comrade Xiao Qiao, I am here to get yesterday's form. Didn't I pick up a hundred catties of fried dough twists yesterday? I need to take that pickup form back.","Hearing this, the smile on Qiao Lanshu's face faded slightly. She replied, I am sorry, Brother Niu. I need to keep yesterday's pickup form on file. When we reconcile the accounts every month, it has to be handed over to finance and the cashier, so I cannot give it to you.","Du Erniu frowned, looking somewhat displeased. The previous warehouse keepers never collected the forms. Why is it that now that you are here, you need them?","Qiao Lanshu continued to speak in a mild and pleasant tone:","Brother Du, the past is the past, and now is now. I am currently just a temporary worker. Our supervisor said I will only be here until the spring after the New Year, which is just about three months in total. When I return to the pickle team, I will have to hand over the work.","At that time, I will have to verify every single account clearly. Tell me, if there are no forms kept on file, and what if a few hundred catties of grain go missing? As a temporary worker, I cannot bear that responsibility. Do you not think that makes sense?","Du Erniu felt that Qiao Lanshu was simply paranoid. He said, In a food factory as big as ours, every bit of grain is accounted for. How could it get lost? Stealing grain is an offense punishable by the firing squad. Who would dare to steal?","Qiao Lanshu thought to herself, who knows? I bet there are people bold enough to steal.","Observing Du Erniu's impatient expression, Qiao Lanshu probed, Brother Du, didn't you say yesterday that you didn't need the form? Why are you looking for it today? Who is asking you for it?","Du Erniu replied, Our supervisor, of course. He never asked for the forms before either. I do not know what is going on this time, asking me for the form. Forget it, I will go talk to him and let him come ask you for it himself.","Qiao Lanshu: ...","Du Erniu was a delivery driver responsible for transporting goods. His department was the business department, also known as the sales department, which was in charge of contacting and coordinating with various clients.","Previously, Sun Mingyong worked as a staff member in the business department. This position was leisurely and paid well.","It was Wei Zhengye who had pulled strings to get Sun Mingyong the job.","Whenever there was a client request, the people in the business department would issue a shipping order, have the leadership sign it, and arrange for a driver to deliver the goods.","They definitely kept a carbon copy of the order. After all, being responsible for client coordination, they also had their own set of accounting procedures.","Now, suddenly sending Du Erniu to retrieve the form, Qiao Lanshu guessed that it was probably because Guan Wenjun and the others had shown up yesterday. After urgently transferring the stolen goods, they knew they would be investigated today, so they were rushing to destroy the evidence.","But what was there to destroy about a delivery order that followed normal procedures?","Unless the person who stole the goods had signed the form and was afraid of being investigated?","Qiao Lanshu took out her keys, unlocked the drawer, took the form out, folded it neatly, and placed it in her inner pocket.","Then, she locked the drawer back up.","...","Meanwhile, in the factory director's office, after finishing the morning meeting, Factory Director Yang Wenyan dismissed the various workshop supervisors.","During the meeting, he had been restraining himself. He was afraid that if he could not hold back, he would have kept the pastry workshop supervisor, the business department head, and workshop director Wei Zhengye behind to thoroughly interrogate them.","But Qin Yuanzheng had said that this matter required luring the snake out of its hole; he had to pretend he did not know anything.","Factory Director Yang Wenyan had not slept at all last night, so he was not in good spirits when he got up today. Sitting at his desk, looking at the meeting directives passed down from his superiors, he could not help but feel that he was perhaps unsuited to be the factory director.","He felt he had let down the Party and the people, and failed all the employees of the food factory.","At this moment, Wei Zhengye, who had already left after the meeting, suddenly returned.","Factory Director Yang Wenyan glanced at him and said expressionlessly, If this is about your daughter again, do not even bring it up. Letting her join the family dependents service team was already doing you a favor. Otherwise, with the mistakes she made, she would have been fired long ago. Who else would dare to employ her?","Wei Zhengye quickly said, Director, I am indeed here about my daughter's work. However, I do not want her to stay; I want her to quit.","Factory Director Yang Wenyan was somewhat surprised by this. He asked:","Why the sudden decision to quit? Does she think the family dependents service team is too hard? Director Wei, if that is the case, I have to criticize you. Labor is the most glorious thing. Being able to serve the factory's workers is also a type of collective honor!","Did you not see last year when the garment factory's dependents service team was awarded the Five Good medal for their outstanding performance? As long as one is willing to endure hardship and is not afraid of suffering, they can achieve results wherever they work.","Wei Zhengye disagreed in his heart. If one had the ability, who would willingly let their child suffer?","Factory Director Yang Wenyan only talked a good game. Was not his own cousin's wife assigned to the warehouse to be a warehouse keeper?","Though Wei Zhengye thought this, he did not show it. He sighed and said, Director, Hongmei has been spoiled by me since she was little. Now she cannot bear even the slightest hardship. I really have no other choice. It is better to just let her go home and take care of the kids. Anyway, I can still work. Supporting her for another dozen years will not be a problem.","Hearing Wei Zhengye say this, Factory Director Yang Wenyan decided to drop the matter. Suit yourself. If she wants to quit, let her quit. But in the future, our food factory will not dare to hire your daughter again. Someone so unwilling to endure hardship should not come back. I cannot afford to employ her.","Factory Director Yang Wenyan's words were harsh, but they were the truth.","Having worked at the food factory for so many years himself, Wei Zhengye naturally knew that this entire matter had been his daughter's fault from start to finish.","But there was nothing he could do.","Wei Hongmei had always had this kind of personality. Otherwise, why would she have taken a liking to Sun Mingyong back then, whose family was wealthy but did not live locally?","Wei Zhengye continued, Director, I would like to request a half-day of leave to help my daughter and grandchildren move. As you know, because of Sun Mingyong's incident, their original housing was taken back by the factory. They are currently staying temporarily at my house...","\"I had originally planned to wait until Hongmei's job was stable before applying for a dorm room. But now, I have no choice. I need to go help her and the two kids move all their belongings to my place. Otherwise, the HR department is going to keep breathing down my neck, asking why the room hasn't been vacated yet while other workers are still waiting in line.\"","Yang Wenyan's heart skipped a beat at those words. He looked up, frowning as he studied Wei Zhengye, and asked, \"You're asking for time off?\""]},{"number":77,"title":"Chapter 77: Yin Yang Order Form","paragraphs":["Last night, Qin Yuanzheng had told Yang Wenyan, \"The other party hastily and urgently transferred the stolen goods. I reckon they couldn't hide them well, so tomorrow, he will definitely show up and handle this matter personally. After all, he might not trust an outsider.\"","Qin Yuanzheng: \"The person is definitely a worker inside the food factory. So, he will probably ask you for leave, Cousin. When the time comes, let him take it. Once he leaves the factory, Guan Wenjun can just send someone to keep an eye on him.\"","When Qin Yuanzheng said this, Yang Wenyan was still wondering in his heart if that person could be Du Erniu, who was in charge of deliveries.","After all, food was scarce nowadays, and most people didn't have enough to eat.","Incidents of deliverymen stealing food were not unheard of in the past.","However, they usually only dared to steal a few ounces, never too much, as it would be too obvious.","But this time, a clear one hundred catties had been stolen, and another two hundred catties were suspected to be stolen, pending evidence.","If it wasn't the delivery driver Du Erniu, then it must be the supervisor of the business department. After all, the pick-up slips were issued by the business department supervisor, and he was the one interfacing with the clients. It would be much more convenient for him to steal grain than anyone else.","When Qiao Lanshu told him back then that Director Wei Zhengye was also a suspect, Yang Wenyan remained skeptical.","Because Wei Zhengye had worked at the food factory for a long time. He was considered Yang Wenyan's right-hand man, helping him manage the workshop, and his working ability was outstanding.","Besides, he had a daughter and a grandson to support. Would he dare?","Thinking about this, Yang Wenyan didn't speak for a long while.","Wei Zhengye thought Yang Wenyan disagreed with his leave request, so he said, \"Factory Manager, if not, I can get off work early, even an hour early is fine. It's freezing outside right now, and it gets dark early. If I get off work early to move the things over, it'll save me from walking in the dark.\"","Yang Wenyan lowered his head and glanced at the desk calendar. Then, he said, \"Alright, alright, don't I know your family's situation? If you need to take leave, take it. Go back early, move your things, and hurry back to work.\"","A smile appeared on Wei Zhengye's face as he laughed, \"Alright, Factory Manager. Don't worry, I'll be back to work in two hours at most.\"","Saying that, Wei Zhengye turned and walked out the door.","As soon as Wei Zhengye stepped out of the food factory, he was spotted by the people from the management committee.","Guan Wenjun had instructed that if anyone came out of the factory during working hours, no matter how many, they had to be secretly tailed.","Therefore, someone immediately went to tail Wei Zhengye.","...","When she got off work in the afternoon, Qiao Lanshu came out of the food factory, the pick-up slip still in her pocket.","Qin Yuanzheng came to pick her up early this time. After all, Guan Wenjun and Qiao Lanshu had been close recently, and Qin Yuanzheng was afraid Guan Wenjun would come to harass his wife again.","As soon as Qiao Lanshu got in the car, she said to him, \"Brother Zheng, I want to make a trip to the state-run restaurant.\"","Qin Yuanzheng reached out to straighten her scarf and asked, \"Want to go to the restaurant for a meal?\"","Qiao Lanshu shook her head. She took out the receipt and said, \"I want to go to the state-run restaurant and ask around, see if I can fish out any information.\"","Qiao Lanshu whispered, \"This morning, the delivery driver came to ask me for the slip, but I didn't give it to him. I figured the reason they never kept the slips before was probably because the pick-up slip and the delivery receipt are different. So, the copy kept by the sales department to hand over to finance for verification is likely the state-run restaurant's receipt.\"","Qin Yuanzheng understood. It meant there was one slip for picking up the goods and another for receiving them.","Qiao Lanshu guessed that the other party might have genuinely delivered goods to the state-run restaurant, but the state-run restaurant probably didn't request that much. For example, they picked up a hundred catties of goods, but the state-run restaurant only received fifty catties, and the remaining fifty catties might have been embezzled.","Qin Yuanzheng was silent for a moment before saying, \"They should have a dedicated person handling this. If you go over as an unfamiliar face, they might not fall for it.\"","Qiao Lanshu said softly, \"Let's just give it a try. I know what I'm doing.\"","She was still wearing the garment factory's work uniform. She deliberately hadn't changed out of it, just for the sake of probing.","Nothing bad would happen inside a state-run restaurant. Qin Yuanzheng thought about it and still took Qiao Lanshu over.","He whispered, \"I'll wait for you at the door. If anything seems wrong, come out immediately.\"","Qiao Lanshu nodded. She got out of the car, took the receipt to the counter of the state-run restaurant, and smiled, \"Hello, comrade. I'd like to find your purchaser to verify an order. I'm from the food factory.\"","As she spoke, she even showed her work badge to the receptionist.","The receptionist took one look and immediately said, \"Don't you guys only come at the end of the month? It's only the middle of the month.\"","Qiao Lanshu: \"The situation is a bit special this time...\"","Then, she revealed a hesitant expression, as if she wanted to say more but stopped.","The receptionist didn't ask further and just said, \"Go straight to the office. Purchaser Liu hasn't gotten off work yet.\"","Qiao Lanshu hadn't even said anything, but the receptionist directly mentioned Purchaser Liu.","It seemed the person interfacing with the food factory was Purchaser Liu?","Qiao Lanshu calmly followed the receptionist's directions and arrived at the office of the state-run restaurant.","In the office, several people were sitting at their respective workstations working. The state-run restaurant was very large, specifically used to host leaders from various departments, so it was usually very busy, and the requirements for ingredients were also very high.","When Qiao Lanshu walked in, everyone in the room looked up at her.","She stood there poisefully and asked with a natural expression, \"Sorry to bother you, comrades, but may I ask which one of you is Purchaser Liu?\"","At this moment, a middle-aged man wearing blue overalls stood up by the window. He said, \"That's me. Little comrade, are you... from the food factory?\"","Qiao Lanshu smiled and nodded. She walked over to Purchaser Liu and deliberately lowered her voice, \"Purchaser Liu, it's like this. There was an order yesterday...\"","She paused intentionally, staring at Purchaser Liu's expression, and said in an even lower voice, \"Director Wei told me to come to you to get the delivery receipt. He said the matter is a bit urgent and told me I must get it from you in person.\"","When Purchaser Liu saw Qiao Lanshu, he noticed she was an unfamiliar young girl.","Truthfully, he was a bit hesitant.","However, Qiao Lanshu's expression, her tone, and the fact that she mentioned Director Wei...","Of course Purchaser Liu knew about yesterday's order. Could it be that they had been found out?","Purchaser Liu's face turned slightly solemn. He looked at Qiao Lanshu, narrowed his eyes, sized her up, and asked, \"Which department are you from? How come I haven't seen you before?\"","Qiao Lanshu pretended to be nervous and stammered, \"I-I'm a temp worker. I haven't been working here for long.\"","Looking at her naive appearance, Purchaser Liu thought he was probably overthinking it.","Every time the food factory delivered goods, they never kept a copy of the delivery slip.","What the finance department verified was the receipt of goods.","Even if he handed the receipt over to Factory Manager Yang Wenyan right now, there wouldn't be any flaws.","After all, his receipts were all processed according to the standard procedures of the state-run restaurant. In the past, a regular staff member from the sales department would come to collect the receipts every month.","However, he heard that the staff member had been arrested and sent to a labor camp for marriage fraud.","That was why a young girl had been sent to pick up the receipts instead.","Purchaser Liu did not think it was a big deal, so he dug out yesterday's receipt for the fried dough twists and handed it to Qiao Lanshu, saying, \"Are you only taking this one? Do you need to take back the ones from the first half of the month too?\"","He still had over a dozen receipts here, all from the food factory, for things like pickles, bread, pastries, soy sauce, vinegar, and so on—a messy stack of them.","Of course, Qiao Lanshu did not want them. After all, taking those receipts back would be useless; this was the only useful one.","She took the receipt and glanced over it roughly, only to see that the weight of the fried dough twists written on the receipt was actually just twenty kilograms.","That was forty jin!","Out of one hundred jin of fried dough twists, the state-run restaurant had only received forty jin. So where did the remaining sixty jin go?","The receipt bore the official seal of the state-run restaurant, and the receiving clerk's signature had the surname Liu, which was presumably Purchaser Liu.","Qiao Lanshu tucked the receipt into her pocket and looked at Purchaser Liu with gratitude. \"Purchaser Liu, thank you so much. Director Wei is in a hurry for this receipt, so I won't take the others for now. I'll go back and ask Director Wei, and if he needs them, I'll come back to get them from you tomorrow.\"","With that, she turned to head out the door. Before leaving, she politely bid her farewells, \"Thank you, Purchaser Liu. I won't disturb your work anymore. Wishing you smooth work and may you have wealth and prosperity.\"","Purchaser Liu: \"...\"","Everyone else: \"...\"","Purchaser Liu muttered, \"It's not even the New Year, what is she wishing me prosperity for?\""]},{"number":78,"title":"Chapter 78: He Upgraded His Skills a Bit","paragraphs":["After getting the receipts, Qiao Lanshu hurried out of the restaurant. Qin Yuanzheng had been waiting for her in the car.","Seeing her come out and reading her expression, he knew she had succeeded. He asked, \"Did you really get the receipts?\"","Qiao Lanshu nodded, her heart still pounding wildly in her chest.","She said, \"Brother Zheng, hurry, let's go to the Revolutionary Committee. I have the evidence!\"","Guan Wenjuan hadn't found the fried dough twists earlier, so he was holding in his frustration and investigating everywhere.","His men were currently tailing Wei Zhengye, but there were no results yet.","That was until Qin Yuanzheng and Qiao Lanshu arrived at his office, and Qiao Lanshu handed him the two receipts to look at.","After she explained the situation to him, what else was there for Guan Wenjuan not to understand?","Guan Wenjuan immediately slammed his hand on the desk and stood up, sneering, \"Men! Come with me to make some arrests.\"","With these receipts, arresting them would be easy.","Guan Wenjuan split his men into three groups and arrested Purchaser Liu from the state-run restaurant, the supervisor of the food factory's business department, the driver Du Erniu, and Director Wei Zhengye, who had taken leave to go home.","Anyone who had signed the receiving and picking receipts was brought to the Public Security Bureau for interrogation.","Guan Wenjuan was not a police officer, but as the director of the Revolutionary Committee, he had the authority to handle such matters upon receiving a report.","However, the final verdict and whether they would be sent to labor reform required the signature and approval of the military court.","In just under an hour or two, all these individuals were apprehended and brought back.","However, the three hundred catties of fried dough twists were still nowhere to be found, and it was unknown where they had been transferred.","That would depend on whether they could get the answers out during the interrogation.","This incident involved quite a few people; even the financial cashiers of the food factory were brought in and asked to cooperate with the investigation.","Because Yang Wenyan had been prepared and secretly reported the matter in advance, he was fine.","But for Wei Zhengye, a workshop director, to commit such an offense was something many people couldn't understand.","Yang Wenyan couldn't understand it either.","Guan Wenjuan stayed at the Public Security Bureau to keep an eye on things. Deputy Director Li led his men to lock the suspects up separately to prevent them from colluding on their stories.","But these people were tough to interrogate, and even late into the night, there were no results.","They had no choice but to stay up all night and try to wear them down.","...","It was past eight in the evening when Qin Yuanzheng finally brought Qiao Lanshu back from the Public Security Bureau.","Qiao Lanshu was hungry and tired, her mind still preoccupied with the matter. She asked, \"Brother Zheng, who do you think is the mastermind behind all this?\"","Was it Wei Zhengye, the business department supervisor, or perhaps Purchaser Liu?","Although they had all been arrested, they were still just suspects.","Qin Yuanzheng thought for a moment and said, \"Wei Zhengye is a workshop director and has worked for many years. Logically, he had no reason to do this, as his family isn't short on food.\"","A director earns a grade 6 salary, making over sixty yuan a month, plus the food factory provides non-staple food and grain coupons as subsidies.","Logically, as long as Wei Zhengye worked well, he wouldn't have to worry about food. Why would he pull a stunt like this?","But what about the others? There was no need for them either, right? Unless their families were facing some difficulties that forced them to take such a risk.","Qin Yuanzheng couldn't be bothered to guess anymore. Seeing that Qiao Lanshu looked a bit exhausted, he said, \"We'll know once the interrogation results are out. Are you hungry? What do you want to eat?\"","Qiao Lanshu thought about it and said, \"Let's have some millet porridge. I'm feeling a bit dry.\"","When Qin Yuanzheng was alone with Qiao Lanshu, he was like a completely different person, speaking without a filter. He lowered his voice and said, \"What, aren't you afraid of wetting the bed this time? Didn't you last time...\"","Qiao Lanshu frantically covered his mouth. \"Don't say it!\"","Qiao Lanshu stared at him, her face flushed red. If they weren't in the car, she would have run away.","Listening to his words was simply dying of embarrassment.","Qin Yuanzheng dared to say it, but she didn't even dare to listen!","Qiao Lanshu realized that the young Qin Yuanzheng was much more wicked than the forty-year-old Qin Yuanzheng.","Last time, because she had drunk two bowls of millet porridge and then a large glass of water after the meal, it led to... that moment on the heated brick bed where she couldn't hold it in.","Qin Yuanzheng kept bullying her, and she begged for mercy for a long time, calling him brother and husband over and over until he finally showed mercy and carried her to the washroom.","If she had really soiled the bed back then, her heart would have ached to death. After all, the mattress was newly made.","And the cotton quilt was new too; she cherished them very much.","Qin Yuanzheng just loved to bully her.","As Qiao Lanshu covered his mouth, Qin Yuanzheng turned to look at her, his eyes smiling, and mumbled, \"What's wrong? Feeling shy?\"","Qiao Lanshu swatted him lightly and said, \"Just focus on driving and stop talking nonsense.\"","Qin Yuanzheng had only been married to Qiao Lanshu for about a month. It hadn't been long, so they were still in their honeymoon phase.","The older man loved teasing his little wife. Whenever she glared at him with a blushing face, he would get aroused.","Qin Yuanzheng slowly drove the car into the military residential compound and whispered, \"I've been studying a bit lately. Let's put it into practice when we get back.\"","While Qiao Lanshu's mind was full of the food factory's fried dough twist case, Qin Yuanzheng's mind was completely occupied with how he was going to devour Comrade Xiao Qiao on the bed once they got back.","Hearing him say this, Qiao Lanshu was stunned. \"Studying? Brother Zheng, what have you been studying?\"","It couldn't be what she was thinking, right?","But where would one even go to study such a thing?","Qin Yuanzheng coughed. To be fair, there wasn't exactly a formal channel to study this stuff.","It was just that there were too many robust, vigorous men in the military. In their free time in the dorms, they loved chatting about these things.","Like how to please their partners, what female comrades liked, and how they needed to be more considerate of the female comrade's feelings when doing the deed.","Especially for some of the young men with no experience.","Doing that kind of exercise as if it were regular training, treating the female comrades like enemies...","Wasn't that just absurd?","It wasn't actual training, so they couldn't just act like brute bulls, only knowing how to blindly charge forward.","Anyway, Qin Yuanzheng had caught a few snippets of conversation here and there and thought it made a lot of sense.","He simply lacked experience, and a few times he had heard Qiao Lanshu say she was uncomfortable.","So he pondered it over, reflected on himself, and decided he needed to serve her first and satisfy her.","Qiao Lanshu was dumbfounded hearing this. With a flushed face, she said, \"Brother Zheng, why are you always researching this? Aren't you embarrassed?\"","Qin Yuanzheng got out of the car, pulled her into his arms, and looked down at her bright red ears. He said, \"We're husband and wife now, what's there to be taboo about? You, on the other hand, how are you still so shy even now?\"","As he spoke, he reached out to pinch Qiao Lanshu's chin, turning her face toward him. As they entered the stairwell, he lowered his head and planted a loud kiss on her lips.","He felt absolutely delighted inside; his little wife was truly adorable.","Qiao Lanshu blushed and didn't dare make a sound. After all, they were already in the stairwell, and if she spoke, the neighbors might hear.","Looking at Qiao Lanshu's flushed face, Qin Yuanzheng whispered, \"I'll get some hot water ready for you as soon as we get home so you can take a bath first.\"","Qin Yuanzheng had custom-ordered a wooden soaking tub to replace the water vat, but it hadn't arrived yet.","Qin Yuanzheng was already imagining the wonderful life ahead when the two of them could take baths together."]},{"number":79,"title":"Chapter 79: Don't Get Dizzy Every Time","paragraphs":["Qiao Lanshu thought Qin Yuanzheng was just teasing her on purpose.","As it turned out, Qin Yuanzheng genuinely intended to put his words into practice!","After eating and taking a bath, the two got onto the kang bed, and Qin Yuanzheng immediately pinned Qiao Lanshu against it.","He leaned close to her ear and whispered, \"Just lie down, I will serve you.\"","Qiao Lanshu: \"...\"","********","The older man was truly relentless when it came to tossing her around. After this experience, Qiao Lanshu was not only afraid when she saw Qin Yuanzheng's rough fingers, but she was even scared when she looked at his mouth.","The next morning, while Qin Yuanzheng was eating porridge, he slurped down half a bowl in one go, making Qiao Lanshu's heart palpitate with fear as she watched.","No wonder last night he was so...","Qin Yuanzheng finished the bowl of porridge in two gulps, picked up a soft cornmeal bun, and took a vigorous bite. He looked up to see Qiao Lanshu staring at him with lingering fear, her face flushed red.","He raised an eyebrow, walked over, sat beside her, and asked, \"What's wrong? Has the swelling not gone down yet?\"","Qiao Lanshu: \"...\"","Qiao Lanshu looked at his mouth. His lips were thin, surrounded by stiff stubble, and there was a tiny black mole near his mouth.","Thinking of something, she reached out and touched his chin. The stubble was very prickly, making the palm of her hand tingle. Blushing, she withdrew her hand, not daring to recall last night's experience.","Qin Yuanzheng knew she was just being shy.","He loved seeing his little wife blushing and shy; this look of hers truly made him love her to death.","The more he looked at his wife, the more he liked her, and the more he loved her.","He felt that she was fragrant and soft everywhere, just like the soft bun in his hand, making him constantly want to take a bite out of her.","Sitting beside her, his tall and sturdy body squeezed his little wife right into the corner of the sofa.","He smiled and asked, \"How did it feel last night? Did you like it?\"","Qiao Lanshu glared at him with a red face. Her gaze could not help but fall on his mouth and that prickly stubble again. She quickly lowered her head and said, \"I didn't like it. You are not allowed to do that again.\"","It truly tortured her to death; she simply could not handle it.","Qin Yuanzheng stuffed the remaining half of the bun into his mouth in one bite. He chewed while recalling the events before saying, \"That's not right. Weren't you quite excited last night? I saw you finish several times.\"","Qiao Lanshu: \"...\"","Although there was nothing wrong with a married couple communicating about these things afterward—after all, as husband and wife, they could certainly discuss such intimate matters.","However, even though Qiao Lanshu considered herself quite open-minded, when it came to Qin Yuanzheng, she was still scared into fleeing in panic.","She put down the porridge in her hands and said somewhat angrily, \"Brother Zheng, how do you have the nerve to bring this up! You, you... why did you even spank me.\"","Qiao Lanshu had been completely stunned at the time, and her tears had just fallen.","Qin Yuanzheng even said something about wanting to make her happy.","She was crying, so how did that have anything to do with being happy?","Didn't he know that his hands were full of calluses and his bones were very hard?","Qiao Lanshu was truly a little angry this time, but even when she was angry, her words were not fierce and sounded soft and gentle. Qin Yuanzheng genuinely hadn't known she was angry at the time.","Moreover, her reactions really showed that she liked it.","Qin Yuanzheng scratched his head and softly coaxed her, \"Alright, I know I was wrong. I'll pay more attention next time.\"","He would control his strength and also comfort her a bit.","Then, he touched his stubble again and said to Qiao Lanshu, \"Should I also shave my beard?\"","Qiao Lanshu: \"...\"","Qin Yuanzheng smiled as he looked at her. \"Wife, what do you say? Do you think I should shave it clean, or keep it? What kind do you like? I'll listen to you.\"","Qiao Lanshu swatted him again and said, \"It's up to you, don't ask me.\"","Saying that, she stood up, angrily preparing to leave.","Qin Yuanzheng smiled and reached out, pulling his petite little wife into his arms in one smooth motion.","He planted a loud kiss on her cheek and then said, \"Alright, on a serious note, do you want me to apply some medicine for you?\"","Qiao Lanshu reached out to push his face away. His beard was too prickly, causing a numb and painful sensation that was very uncomfortable.","Blushing, she whispered, \"There's no need. A whole night has passed, it's already healed.\"","Qin Yuanzheng was somewhat surprised. Looking at her, he asked in a low voice, \"Is it really healed?\"","He muttered under his breath, \"So magical, it healed on its own?\"","As he spoke, he placed Qiao Lanshu back onto the sofa and started to pull at her clothes, saying, \"Are you being shy again and too embarrassed to tell me? Let me see. I'll only be at ease if I inspect it myself.\"","After all, he had to exercise every day, and he still needed to continue his exercise today.","If Qiao Lanshu didn't heal quickly, how could he start? He couldn't just be expected to hold it in.","The older man simply couldn't endure it at all.","Qiao Lanshu had no choice but to let him examine her.","After Qin Yuanzheng finished his inspection, he suddenly felt thirsty again and wanted to drink water.","Fortunately, both of them still had to go to work; today was not a day off.","Looking somewhat unsatisfied, Qin Yuanzheng helped Qiao Lanshu put her clothes back on, and then took her out the door.","As they were leaving, Qin Yuanzheng was still whispering in Qiao Lanshu's ear, \"It really is healed, truly magical. Then next time I can...\"","He could last a bit longer, or perhaps he wouldn't need to hold back so much.","Yesterday was his first time, and he had been afraid of hurting his little wife, but looking at it now, she was perfectly fine.","He had still been too conservative.","Qiao Lanshu blushed and said, \"I told you, there won't be a next time.\"","Qin Yuanzheng always did what he promised, so this time, he chose to play deaf and pretend he didn't hear what she said.","Qiao Lanshu knew he would dare to do it again next time and felt utterly helpless.","The two got into the car, and Qin Yuanzheng dropped her off at the main gate of the food factory as usual.","Qin Yuanzheng looked at Qiao Lanshu tenderly and said to her with reluctance to part, \"At noon today, I'll come find you so we can eat together.\"","Qiao Lanshu looked a little surprised. \"Brother Zheng, aren't you eating at the military base?\"","Qin Yuanzheng reached out to stroke her cheek, looking as though he couldn't bear to let her go. He said, \"I heard the cafeteria is having extra dishes today, including mutton stew. I'll bring some over for you to taste.\"","In this day and age, food was scarce, and meat was in even shorter supply. The food in the military cafeteria was considered decent, but the food in the factory cafeteria was very ordinary.","The monthly grain rations for the factory workers were fixed, and meat was generally unavailable, only supplied a little during the New Year and holidays.","Qin Yuanzheng would usually figure out ways to buy some mutton to bring back to nourish his wife's body.","Hearing that there was mutton soup in the military cafeteria today, he decided to bring his portion over for his wife to eat.","He whispered to Qiao Lanshu, \"Eat your fill and gain some weight. Your stamina needs to keep up; don't faint every single time.\"","Qiao Lanshu: \"...\""]},{"number":80,"title":"Chapter 80: Case Closed","paragraphs":["When Qiao Lanshu went to work and had just arrived at the warehouse, Deng Weijun quietly ran over from the pickles workshop.","He leaned against the window and said to Qiao Lanshu inside, Sister-in-law, have you eaten breakfast yet?","After the previous incident, Deng Weijun had been depressed for several days and looked listless at work.","Qiao Lanshu hadn't seen him for two days.","Seeing him today, she noticed his mental state was much better, and he had returned to his usual chatty self.","Qiao Lanshu was also somewhat glad.","She put down the book in her hand, opened the window, and leaned out to chat with him, Oh, it's Weijun. What brings you here? Do you need something from me?","Deng Weijun scratched his head and smiled, Nothing much. It's just a bit slow right now, and I heard you became the warehouse keeper, so I came over to take a look.","The boiler workers in the pickles workshop hadn't been seconded to help out, so Deng Weijun was still working there.","He pulled a fist-sized, rock-hard, pitch-black object from his pocket, placed it on the windowsill, and said, Sister-in-law, this is a frozen pear I made. Give it a try.","Then he added, By the way, does your thermos have hot water? I'll go fetch some for you.","Deng Weijun probably wanted to thank Qiao Lanshu for saving his life, which was why he was being so attentive.","However, he also kept his distance, not daring to get within two steps of her. He spoke from a meter away, afraid that someone might misunderstand and word would reach Qin Yuanzheng's ears.","With Qin Yuanzheng's massive build, wouldn't one punch send him flying?","Qiao Lanshu understood his thoughts and didn't refuse. She smiled and handed over her thermos, saying, I just got here and haven't fetched water yet. I'll have to trouble you then.","Deng Weijun quickly took the thermos and said, No trouble at all! Sister-in-law, if you ever need anything, big or small, just call me. I've got plenty of free time anyway.","With that, he grabbed the thermos and sprinted toward the pantry.","It was just the start of the morning shift, so everyone's thermos was empty. Some people had brought cold steamed buns or flatbreads and needed hot water to soak them in before eating.","Because of this, the pantry was quite crowded, and Qiao Lanshu usually waited until later to go.","But since Deng Weijun was so eager to help her out, she let him fetch the water.","Qiao Lanshu looked at the frozen pear on the windowsill and picked it up to examine it.","The frozen pear was rock-hard and pitch-black, looking just like a lump of coal.","She had seen frozen pears in her past life but had never eaten one.","She tapped the frozen pear against the desk, making a loud bang bang sound.","Qiao Lanshu: ...","She put the frozen pear on the desk and placed her book in the drawer.","She wasn't actually in the mood to read, as she kept thinking about the fried dough twist incident. She wondered if the police station had managed to interrogate anything out of them last night.","A short while later, Deng Weijun returned with the thermos. He placed it on the windowsill and lowered his voice, saying to Qiao Lanshu, Sister-in-law, did you hear? Our workshop director was arrested, along with the delivery driver and the business department supervisor! None of them came to work today, and the finance accountants were all taken away by the Revolutionary Committee for questioning!","Deng Weijun said with a solemn face, What exactly did they do? It even alarmed the provincial Revolutionary Committee! Are they going to be paraded through the streets too?","Previously, Sun Mingyong had been made an example of for pretending to be a military officer to trick someone into marriage.","That was already considered a huge incident.","And now, another major event had occurred.","Qiao Lanshu already knew about this, so she wasn't very shocked. Since the matter hadn't been fully investigated, she didn't dare spread it around and simply said, Otherwise, you could ask my cousin. He definitely knows.","Yang Wenyan had also gone to cooperate with the investigation, but it was unknown when everything would be cleared up.","...","At the police station, Deputy Director Li led his people in interrogating them all night, questioning them separately.","Deputy Director Li couldn't get anything out of them at first. Guan Wenjun waited outside until the middle of the night and simply couldn't wait any longer.","He brought his people in and interrogated them personally.","With the Revolutionary Committee members present, these people became scared. Wei Zhengye was the most terrified. He feared being sent to a labor camp. If that happened, what would become of his daughter and grandson?","They wouldn't survive without him providing for them.","But Guan Wenjun was not one to be swayed by personal feelings. If he were, he wouldn't be the director of the Revolutionary Committee.","Deputy Director Li didn't know how Guan Wenjun interrogated them, but by a little after ten in the morning, those people had all confessed.","Among them, apart from the food factory's finance staff and accountants, the delivery driver Du Erniu was the most innocent.","Du Erniu genuinely knew nothing; he didn't even know why he had been arrested.","At the police station, he spent the night reflecting on his actions and even confessed to stealing a neighbor's pear when he was a child.","Guan Wenjun listened for a long time and finally walked out looking speechless.","Deputy Director Li asked, Director Guan, did you get a confession? What exactly is going on?","Guan Wenjun showed him the record sheet in his hand and said, Wei Zhengye only admitted to pulling strings and stealing sixty catties of fried dough twists. He is old acquaintances with Miao Hongwei from the business department and Purchaser Liu from the state-run restaurant, so he gave them some kickbacks. They transported the sixty catties of fried dough twists to the mobile market, sold them at a high price, and then reimbursed the base cost to avoid detection by finance.","In other words, Wei Zhengye used his own money to secretly buy sixty catties of fried dough twists at the lowest price, then sold them at a high price to pocket the difference.","When the food factory's finance department checked the receipts, the income and expenses appeared fine, so naturally, Yang Wenyan, as the factory manager, had no idea.","Meanwhile, Purchaser Liu from the state-run restaurant only had to help him write a delivery receipt to earn a kickback of over ten yuan, so of course he was willing to do it.","After all, it had no negative impact on him.","However, Miao Hongwei, the supervisor of the business department, was in partnership with Wei Zhengye. When those sixty catties of fried dough twists were shipped out, it was Miao Hongwei's relatives who helped sell them.","Deputy Director Li said suspiciously, Did Wei Zhengye say one hundred catties? That can't be right. The warehouse's shipping records show that three hundred catties of fried dough twists were sent to the state-run restaurant in the last two months alone.","Could the remaining two hundred catties have nothing to do with Wei Zhengye?","Guan Wenjun sneered, Then we'll have to ask Wei Zhengye's good son-in-law, Sun Mingyong.","Deputy Director Li: Sun Mingyong? Wasn't he sent to reform through labor?","However, on second thought, Deputy Director Li remembered that before Sun Mingyong was sent to reform through labor, he was a clerk in the food factory's business department. He was the one responsible for liaising with the state-run restaurant and the supply and marketing cooperatives.","Thinking of this, Guan Wenjun immediately said, Let's go to Sun Mingyong's house!","After Sun Mingyong was arrested and sent to reform through labor, Wei Hongmei should have moved out of the house and returned it to the food factory's personnel department.","After all, housing was in short supply, and many workers were waiting in line for a house.","But Wei Hongmei delayed moving out.","Wei Zhengye could have helped her move long ago, but he deliberately dragged his feet and didn't move her things.","It wasn't until yesterday that he asked the factory manager for a leave of absence, claiming he needed to help his daughter move. And by this time, it had been almost two months since Sun Mingyong was sent to a labor camp.","With this clue, everything would be easy to investigate.","Guan Wenjun led his men to Sun Mingyong's house. It was only upon arriving that Guan Wenjun suddenly realized the food factory's dormitory was actually quite close to that mobile market.","Wei Hongmei should have moved back to her parents' home a long time ago, but surprisingly, she was at home today.","When Guan Wenjun knocked on the door, she refused to open it. She said, I haven't moved out yet. This is still my home, and you cannot come in!","Guan Wenjun sneered and said, If you do not open the door, I am going to smash it down.","Wei Hongmei yelled from inside the house, Smash it if you have the guts! If you dare to smash it, I will die...","Before she could even finish her harsh words, a loud bang came from the tightly shut door.","It scared Wei Hongmei so much that she screamed and backed away.","Guan Wenjun clutched his agonizingly painful leg, looked at the door that had not budged an inch, and said to the people behind him, What are you all staring at? Hurry up and find a way to open the door!","His subordinates were left speechless.","They had thought Director Guan was so tough that he could actually kick the door open with a single strike.","In the end, it was the officers from the Public Security Bureau who found a comrade from the food factory's personnel department to bring a spare key, finally getting the door open.","The dormitory allocated to them by the food factory had a two-bedroom and one-living-room layout. The two bedrooms were not large, but the front hall was relatively spacious, furnished with a sofa and a dining table.","Wei Hongmei blocked the front hall, preventing them from entering the inner rooms. She screamed, If you come any further, I will smash my head and die right here!","Keeping a stern face, Guan Wenjun directly pushed Wei Hongmei aside and entered the inner room.","As soon as he walked in, he saw several boxes of fried dough twists piled up on the floor. At a rough glance, he estimated there were about seventy or eighty catties.","Guan Wenjun's face darkened as he said, So they were transferred here. Well played, Wei Zhengye, you move quite fast!","If it had not been for the conclusive evidence, Guan Wenjun would never have thought to come here and investigate.","Only then did Wei Hongmei start to feel afraid. She hurriedly said, These fried dough twists have nothing to do with my dad. It was all Sun Mingyong's doing. If you want to arrest someone, go arrest Sun Mingyong.","Wei Hongmei finally knew fear.","She was afraid that if Wei Zhengye lost his job, no one would support her and her children in the future.","Since Sun Mingyong was already sent to a labor camp anyway, she figured she might as well push all the blame onto him.","Guan Wenjun looked at Wei Hongmei and deliberately asked her, Are all five hundred catties of fried dough twists here?","Wei Hongmei froze and subconsciously replied, Five hundred catties? Wasn't it three hundred? What exactly are you trying to do?","She paused, looked at the seventy or eighty catties of fried dough twists piled in the room, and finally realized she had misspoken.","Consequently, Wei Hongmei was also taken to the Public Security Bureau for questioning, which made Wei Zhengye extremely anxious.","Wei Zhengye treasured this daughter the most; he could not bear to drag her down with him.","Ultimately, he had no choice but to confess.","While Sun Mingyong was still working, he had used his position to secretly resell fried dough twists. Wei Zhengye knew about the situation at the time but pretended to be ignorant.","After all, the money Sun Mingyong made was spent on his daughter. His daughter spent money lavishly, and the family's expenses were indeed high.","When Sun Mingyong was caught and sent to the labor camp, he left behind a debt of over a thousand yuan, which fell onto Wei Zhengye's shoulders.","Having no other choice, Wei Zhengye figured that since Sun Mingyong had resold the factory's food for so long without any issues, he would surely be fine if he did it too.","But who could have known that he would be discovered right after he started...","By nightfall, the case was concluded.","Factory Manager Yang Wenyan came to the Public Security Bureau. Looking at Wei Zhengye, he said with deep sorrow, Old Wei, you are truly foolish! It was just a debt of over a thousand yuan. If you had just told me, would I have refused to help you? How could you come up with such a terrible idea?","Wei Zhengye smiled bitterly, shook his head, and said, Factory Manager, I really lost my mind back then, but I had no other way...","He sighed, deeply regretting taking Sun Mingyong as his son-in-law.","Sun Mingyong had resold the food factory's products, not just fried dough twists, but also bread and pickled vegetables. However, the quantities were small, and he had replenished the costs in time, so the finance department never noticed.","But as a director, Wei Zhengye had discovered it early on, and he had initially scolded Sun Mingyong.","However, the profits from this illicit business were too high, and Sun Mingyong could not stop. Moreover, Wei Hongmei, who was raising a child, had been spoiled. She could not work, had no income, and spent heavily.","Wei Hongmei even helped Sun Mingyong find buyers and sell the goods.","Under such circumstances, how could Wei Zhengye stay out of it?","Thinking of the goods hidden at home, Wei Zhengye lowered his head slightly, feeling thankful that the Revolutionary Committee had not discovered them. Otherwise, he would likely have been sent to a labor camp for real.","Wei Zhengye's incident was actually not considered too severe. Since he had compensated the factory for the money, it did not constitute a true crime of theft, nor was it embezzlement. Ultimately, he was sentenced for the crime of speculation and profiteering.","He was expelled from the Party and fired from the food factory, meaning he would never be hired by a state-owned factory again. He had to accept public criticism at a factory-wide assembly and undergo a month of ideological education at the Public Security Bureau.","Although he did not have to go to a labor camp, he had lost his iron rice bowl.","Purchaser Liu received the same sentence as him, while the business department supervisor, Miao Hongwei, was sent to a labor camp for three years.","Wei Hongmei went home crying. That very night, she moved out of the dormitory, taking all her belongings back to her parents' home, leaving the apartment completely empty.","The people in the courtyard all shook their heads, discussing in private, This Wei Hongmei will probably have to get a job now, right? If she doesn't work, is the whole family going to starve?","Someone else added, Wei Zhengye was a perfectly good director, but he ruined his own career just for his daughter. I don't know what he's going to do from now on.","Wei Zhengye stayed at the Public Security Bureau for a month to receive ideological education.","Meanwhile, Wei Hongmei lived at her parents' home with her child. She still did not work, yet she ate fine rice and good dishes every single day.","When the neighbors noticed this, they all shook their heads.","They said Wei Hongmei was heartless; even at a time like this, all she cared about was eating.","Time flew by, and soon, the factory welcomed a new workshop director and a new business department supervisor.","Because of her outstanding performance and her contribution in reporting the crime, Qiao Lanshu had saved the food factory from massive losses.","Therefore, Yang Wenyan directly submitted an application to make her a permanent employee.","She was now an official worker at the food factory, holding the position of warehouse keeper.","The previous warehouse keeper, who had gone home to have a baby, was reassigned due to her negligence at work. When she returned to work in the future, she would be sent to the pickled vegetable workshop.","The monthly salary for an official worker was 42 yuan, along with a 5 yuan non-staple food ticket subsidy provided by the factory.","Qiao Lanshu's job was quite relaxed, and she worked even harder.","One day, when she got off work and had just left the food factory, she sensed that someone was following her.","Her sixth sense had always been strong. She turned around and saw, far in the distance, a few men coming out of the back door of the supply and marketing cooperative. They were holding baskets and pulling a handcart, busy unloading goods.","Qiao Lanshu observed them but did not notice anything particularly wrong, though she felt a bit puzzled. It seemed like one of the men looked quite familiar?","But she couldn't quite remember."]},{"number":81,"title":"Chapter 81: Unloading Worker at the Supply and Marketing Cooperative","paragraphs":["Qiao Lanshu's feeling was indeed right. At the back door of the supply and marketing cooperative, one of the men unloading goods looked up and watched Qiao Lanshu in the distance.","Qiao Lanshu had already walked far away, but he still stood there, squinting his eyes and staring for a while.","One of the men carrying things bumped him with his shoulder and said, \"Liangzi, what are you looking at? Hurry up and unload the goods.\"","The man named Liangzi was tall and big, with an ordinary appearance and an inch-long knife scar on his forehead. He threw his finished cigarette butt on the ground, crushed it with his foot, smiled, and said, \"Nothing. The streets in the city are just different, quite clean.\"","Even the women in the city were different. They were thin and had fair skin, looking quite distinct.","He pondered this in his heart but didn't show it.","The colleague next to him heard this and said with a smile, \"Of course. The streets in the city have dedicated people to clean them, unlike the countryside. Otherwise, why would everyone want to come to the city?\"","It was a pity that everything was managed by the production brigade now, and people from the villages couldn't even come to work in the city.","Even if they came to the city, without transferring their household registration, they could only do temporary work, just like Liangzi.","Liangzi was a temporary worker at the supply and marketing cooperative. He was a porter in the team, and his usual job was to load and unload goods.","However, he always slacked off. Whenever the fleet drove out to transport or deliver goods, he would lazily hide in the cooperative's fleet office, refusing to go out.","Only when the goods arrived would he come out to put on a show and help move the goods a bit.","Even so, no one dared to criticize him. After all, Liangzi had quite a background. His second cousin was Chu Haiming, the director of the supply and marketing cooperative, and Chu Haiming's wife had a brother who was a division commander in the army.","Therefore, even though Liangzi himself was from the mountains and his household registration was still in the village, he was able to work in the supply and marketing cooperative, and others dared not offend him.","After Liangzi finished unloading the goods, seeing that there was nothing else to do, he came out of the cooperative and walked down the street. When he reached the intersection, he stopped.","It was a crossroads. He stood there, looking left and right, not knowing which way the girl from earlier had gone.","Seeing that it was getting dark, Liangzi gave up and turned around to go back to his dormitory.","...","After Qiao Lanshu returned home, she felt constantly restless.","But she could never remember, feeling as if she had forgotten many things.","Thinking too much made her head ache again. She felt dizzy and uncomfortable all over.","Qiao Lanshu took off her padded jacket, curled up on the sofa in her knit sweater, and closed her eyes to rest.","Although Qin Yuanzheng didn't manage to pick her up from work, he still came back as early as possible.","By the time he returned, it was already past seven in the evening. Qin Yuanzheng felt a bit guilty. He had promised to pick up his wife from work every day, but in the end, he still didn't make it.","As soon as he got home, he saw that the house was very dim. It was dark outside, but the lights were not turned on.","His heart sank, wondering if his little wife hadn't come back yet.","What time was it already?","Thinking this, Qin Yuanzheng casually turned on the light, and then he saw Qiao Lanshu curled up on the sofa, her face pale and her eyes closed.","Qin Yuanzheng: \"!!!\"","Without even having time to take off his hat and overcoat, Qin Yuanzheng walked over in a few strides, squatted in front of the sofa, took off his gloves, and gently touched Qiao Lanshu's forehead. She had no fever.","He called out softly, \"Wife, wake up. Why are you sleeping here? Are you feeling unwell?\"","Qin Yuanzheng wondered if he had overdone it last night, so Qiao Lanshu hadn't recovered even after a whole day.","He reflected on himself for two seconds and then felt that it wasn't likely. His wife must be sick.","Qiao Lanshu was dreaming. She dreamed of her past life again, fainting on the street and being picked up by a certain man.","When she opened her eyes, exhausted and hungry, she found herself locked in a dilapidated house.","The man's face was blurry. She only vaguely remembered that he had a scar on his face.","But perhaps due to the brain's protective mechanism, she had forgotten what the man looked like. Even in her dreams, he was blurry.","The man said to her, \"I picked you up, so from now on, you are my woman.\"","Qiao Lanshu had cried and begged him to let her go, saying she had money and could give it to him.","But the man didn't want it.","The man said he only wanted her to be his wife.","Qiao Lanshu jolted awake from the dream. Opening her eyes, she saw Qin Yuanzheng looking at her worriedly. She was being held in his arms, and they were both sitting on the sofa.","Qiao Lanshu's face was pale, her eyes were full of panic, and her forehead was covered in cold sweat.","Qin Yuanzheng reached out to stroke her long hair and asked softly, \"Had a nightmare again? Don't be afraid, I'm right here.\"","Qiao Lanshu's eyes reddened, and tears fell again. Nestled in Qin Yuanzheng's arms, she cried and said, \"Brother Zheng, where did you go? Why are you only showing up now?\"","Qin Yuanzheng: \"...\"","Qin Yuanzheng felt even worse. He said, \"We had a meeting at the mining area today, so it delayed me a bit. I'm sorry, I promised to pick you up every day.\"","Qiao Lanshu just silently shed tears, crying as she whispered, \"If only I could have met you earlier. If I could have met you earlier...\"","Then Qin Yuanzheng wouldn't have had to wait until he was forty to go on a blind date with her, and they wouldn't have only had five years together.","Qiao Lanshu was somewhat bewildered now. She didn't know if her past life experiences were a dream, or if this beautiful life in the present was the dream.","She couldn't really tell anymore.","Qin Yuanzheng hugged her with an aching heart. He gently patted her back with one hand and asked softly, \"What nightmare did you have? Tell me about it?\"","Qiao Lanshu nestled in his arms and cried silently for quite a while.","She didn't make much sound when she cried, just silently shedding tears, which made Qin Yuanzheng's heart ache to death for her.","Qiao Lanshu cried for a good while before she calmed down. She said, \"I dreamed that when I first came to Longcheng, I fainted by the roadside, and then I was picked up by a man and locked in a cave dwelling in the mountains.\"","Qin Yuanzheng's arms tightened slightly. He held Qiao Lanshu close and whispered, \"It's all fake. After you fainted, I was the one who took you to the hospital. There was no other man, and no cave dwelling.\"","Qiao Lanshu said quietly, \"That man locked me in the cave dwelling and told me to bear him a son.\"","Qin Yuanzheng: \"...\"","Although it was just a dream, just hearing these words made an unspeakable anger surge from the bottom of Qin Yuanzheng's heart.","He was angry, heartbroken, and felt a trace of sorrow mixed in.","These complex emotions were like a turbulent tide, drowning him.","His mood also sank, and he held Qiao Lanshu without speaking.","Qiao Lanshu whispered, \"I don't remember much about being locked in the cave dwelling. I only know that I was locked up for two years before I managed to escape.\"","But she also understood that one of the unloaders she saw in the afternoon was likely the man who had locked her in the cave dwelling in her previous life."]},{"number":82,"title":"Chapter 82: What a man full of vigor and vitality.","paragraphs":["That night was the first time since Qin Yuanzheng got married that he did not engage in intimacy.","The couple simply held the quilt and chatted.","Qiao Lanshu whispered, \"If I had been picked up by that man this time and locked in a cave dwelling, we wouldn't have met, let alone gotten married. Brother Zheng, would you have married another woman?\"","Qin Yuanzheng said with a firm tone, \"No.\"","If Qin Yuanzheng were the type of person willing to settle, he would have married long ago and definitely wouldn't have waited until now.","After all, with his qualifications, even if he suffered from infertility, there would still be girls willing to marry him.","But, how should one put it? When he went on blind dates and talked with those girls, he always felt they weren't quite right for him.","Perhaps it was because he hadn't found a girl who caught his eye.","He held Qiao Lanshu, kissed her on the cheek, and whispered, \"I just like you the way you are. If you hadn't come along, I would definitely have remained a bachelor for the rest of my life.\"","Qiao Lanshu thought back to when she had just been reborn and saw Qin Yuanzheng walking with Wang Huiping and her son, thinking he was already married with a child.","At that time, she was not only sad but even a little angry.","She had thought that the Qin Yuanzheng of her past life was lying to her when he said he was forty and had never been married.","The sense of helplessness and panic Qiao Lanshu felt after her nightmare was finally soothed by Qin Yuanzheng's gentle and comforting words.","Qin Yuanzheng was bare-chested, wearing only a pair of shorts, and his body was practically like a furnace.","Even though it was snowing outside the window, their heated brick bed was very warm.","Qiao Lanshu lay in Qin Yuanzheng's arms, feeling drowsy.","Seeing that she no longer seemed sad, Qin Yuanzheng silently breathed a sigh of relief. He held Qiao Lanshu and whispered, \"Go to sleep, wifey. I'll hold you while you sleep.\"","...","Early the next morning, the snow had stopped. Looking out the window, everything was a vast expanse of white.","Qin Yuanzheng brought out the cooked millet and pumpkin porridge. Looking at his little wife coming out of the room in a daze, his heart filled with immense fondness.","He couldn't help but step forward, suddenly pulling Qiao Lanshu into his arms and pressing her against the wall. He whispered, \"Are you awake? It snowed outside. It's your first time seeing snow, do you want to go out and play?\"","Bright and early, Qin Yuanzheng was full of vigor again. Pinned against the wall, Qiao Lanshu could feel his...","Blushing, she said, \"I still have to go to work, and the snow is too freezing, so I won't go play.\"","To Qiao Lanshu, snow was really not a novelty anymore.","Qin Yuanzheng hadn't had any intimacy last night. He had just hugged his fragrant, soft little wife under the covers and simply slept through the night.","Now he was feeling somewhat uncomfortably pent-up.","It was truly strange. When he was single and alone in the past, he never had these thoughts at all.","Why was it that after getting married and having a little wife, he started losing control of himself every day?","Unable to hold back, he pressed Qiao Lanshu down and kissed her for a long time, feeling his trousers becoming impossibly tight.","He whispered, \"It snowed today, and it will probably snow again tonight. Wait for me in the guard room at the entrance after work, and I will come pick you up, understand?\"","Qiao Lanshu was left speechless by him now, so she could only nod to show she understood.","Although Qin Yuanzheng was very fierce and cold in front of outsiders, only Qiao Lanshu knew that in private, he was incredibly clingy.","He was truly exceptionally clingy.","When they were outside, he would restrain himself a bit, but once the two of them were alone or back home.","He would start sticking to her body, and he often didn't like to wear clothes either.","Qiao Lanshu found it sweet, but sometimes, she also found it a bit overwhelming.","Qin Yuanzheng said to Qiao Lanshu, \"Go drink some porridge and eat some steamed buns. I need to go to the washroom.\"","Qiao Lanshu was just about to ask him why he wasn't eating with her.","As a result, she saw Qin Yuanzheng close the washroom door, and then, she heard certain noises.","Qiao Lanshu's face instantly turned red again.","What a vigorous and robust man.","When the two finally came out of the house, Battalion Commander Zhao Jiannong from next door happened to be coming out of his house as well.","Looking at Qin Yuanzheng, who had his arm around Qiao Lanshu and was even wrapping her in his own overcoat, Zhao Jiannong simply didn't know what to say.","He also absolutely never expected that after getting married, Qin Yuanzheng would dote on his wife as if she were his own life.","Seeing this clinginess, he suspected that if possible, Qin Yuanzheng would love to tie his little wife to his belt and take her to work with him every day.","Zhao Jiannong coughed and said, \"Morning, Regiment Commander Qin, morning, Comrade Xiao Qiao.\"","Qiao Lanshu quickly escaped from Qin Yuanzheng's embrace and responded somewhat awkwardly, \"Good morning, Battalion Commander Zhao.\"","Qin Yuanzheng's expression was not very pleasant; he cast a glance at Zhao Jiannong.","Zhao Jiannong hurriedly said, \"Ah, I'm in a rush, I'll be going first.\"","With that, he quickened his pace and ran out of the corridor.","Qin Yuanzheng hooked his arm and pulled Qiao Lanshu back into his embrace, saying, \"It's so cold, why did you run?\"","Qiao Lanshu: \"...\"","Qin Yuanzheng escorted Qiao Lanshu to the food factory and said to her reluctantly, \"Remember to wait for me in the guard room this afternoon. I'll come pick you up.\"","Qiao Lanshu nodded, \"Okay, I know.\"","Watching Qin Yuanzheng leave, Qiao Lanshu finally went to work.","Deng Weijun came over as usual to help her fetch water and brought her another dark, frozen pear.","Qiao Lanshu placed the two frozen pears side by side on the desk and then began organizing the warehouse's inbound and outbound records.","There were quite a few people coming to pick up goods in the morning. Du Erniu also came. This time, he politely handed the pick-up slip in his hand to Qiao Lanshu and said very cautiously, \"Storekeeper, this is the pick-up slip. Please sign here.\"","After the fried dough twist incident, the factory investigated and discovered that Sun Mingyong had previously relied on this method to resell quite a few things.","Therefore, the factory's inbound and outbound warehouse management began to become stricter.","What Du Erniu brought over was no longer called a pick-up slip, but a delivery slip.","The slip was in triplicate, bearing the signatures of the supervisor, the delivery person, the receiver, and, of course, the storekeeper.","Qiao Lanshu took the slip, opened the warehouse door to get the goods for him, then signed her name. She kept one copy of the slip for herself and returned the remaining two to Du Erniu.","Du Erniu took the slips and the goods, ready to leave.","However, before leaving, he brought down two cans of mandarin oranges from the truck and placed them on Qiao Lanshu's windowsill. He said somewhat shyly, \"I, uh, don't like eating these canned fruits. You can have them.\"","With that, he ran off in a hurry.","Qiao Lanshu: \"...\"","Du Erniu was also doing this to thank Qiao Lanshu. After all, last time, if Qiao Lanshu hadn't gone to the state-run restaurant and gotten the slip from Purchaser Liu.","The loss of those hundreds of catties of fried dough twists would probably have been blamed on him.","After all, he was the driver and the deliveryman. So many fried dough twists were sent out, but the state-run restaurant only received half. Where was the remaining half?","Where did it go?","As the delivery person, it certainly wouldn't have been so easy for him to clear his name.","Fortunately, Qiao Lanshu had exposed Purchaser Liu, and Purchaser Liu in turn confessed about Wei Zhengye and Sun Mingyong.","Anyway, the whole situation was quite complicated. Du Erniu firmly believed that Qiao Lanshu had helped him, so he kept thinking about getting her a little something in return.","He spent some money on two canned goods and brought them over.","Looking at the cans on the windowsill, Qiao Lanshu found it rather amusing.","Just then, a salesman from the food factory's business department walked over and said, \"Oh, what is our Comrade Warehouse Keeper smiling about? Did you run into some happy news?\"","Qiao Lanshu looked up, and the smile on her face instantly vanished.","She stared at the three men following behind the salesman, her face turning slightly pale.","The salesman said, \"Oh, they are from the supply and marketing cooperative's transport fleet. They are here to pick up some goods today.\""]},{"number":83,"title":"Chapter 83: The Man Who Was Connected to Her in a Past Life Has Appeared","paragraphs":["The food in the supply and marketing cooperative was mostly transported from the food factory.","Because the cooperative required such a large volume of goods, the factory workers sometimes couldn't deliver them or couldn't make it in time, so the cooperative's fleet would come to pick up the goods themselves.","Besides, it was close by, which was always faster than going to the village to haul cabbage like they used to.","After all, when they went to the village for vegetables, they sometimes had to help twist off cabbages and pull radishes, which was no easy work.","The salesman handed three pickup slips to Qiao Lanshu and said, We've all signed, now we just need your signature.","Qiao Lanshu took the slips, signed them, pulled out one copy of each for her records, and handed the rest back to the salesman.","The salesman took the slips, chatted with the cooperative's fleet crew for a moment, and waited for Qiao Lanshu to open the door.","Qiao Lanshu didn't dare look their way. Her face was a bit pale, and the hand holding the keys was trembling slightly.","She forced herself to stay calm. Perhaps the events of her past life were just a dream. Now she was standing right here, and the other party was merely a temporary worker at the cooperative. They didn't know each other.","She had to pretend not to care about him.","Moreover, she needed to figure out a countermeasure. Even if he hadn't done anything to her in this life, she still had to get her revenge.","Otherwise, she would never be able to swallow this resentment.","Qiao Lanshu aimed the key at the keyhole several times but failed to insert it.","Taking a deep breath, she calmed herself again. This time, the key finally slid in, and she opened the door.","On the other side, the cooperative's driver stood with the salesman. Sniffling and blowing out a puff of cold air, he asked the salesman, Where's that heavily pregnant woman from before? Did she go on maternity leave?","The salesman nodded. Yeah, she left a while ago. She probably won't be back until after the New Year.","The driver continued, Aren't warehouse keeper jobs usually assigned to pregnant women and the elderly? Why did they assign such a young girl this time, short and stout like a little water vat? She's quite pretty, though.","The salesman: ...","Sighing, the salesman lowered his voice and said, Haven't you heard about the huge incident that happened at our food factory?","The matter of Wei Zhengye and others reselling fried dough twists had already been criticized in a factory-wide notice.","It seemed the news hadn't spread outside yet.","The salesman told the driver about it and then summarized, So, our warehouse keeper position is now a key inspection post. We have to find someone young, smart, educated, and good at accounting. Otherwise, if they can't even figure out the incoming and outgoing inventory, how can they manage the warehouse? Don't you agree?","The driver nodded in deep agreement. It should have been like this long ago. Food is so scarce nowadays. The workers building roads over at the mining area are eating vegetable substitutes every day, suffering from cold and hunger. Yet these people stole from their own factory! They really deserve to die!","The coal mine planned to build two highways to transport coal out. It was a key project and had recruited many migrant workers.","Almost every family in the surrounding area had someone working on the road construction. Watching their family members go hungry while the food factory's grain was being stolen made everyone feel terrible.","Therefore, the driver stood there and cursed Wei Zhengye for quite a while.","While they were chatting, Qiao Lanshu had already opened the warehouse door. Holding her slips, she stood at the entrance, about to head back to her little booth.","Just then, a temporary worker from the cooperative walked over. Staring at Qiao Lanshu's face, he smiled and asked, Comrade, where are our goods?","Qiao Lanshu's face darkened slightly. She turned to look and saw the man in front of her staring intently at her face, speaking to her with a cheeky smile: Little comrade, what's your name? How long have you been working here? Are you a temp?","Qiao Lanshu saw the scar on his face. She shoved her hands into the pockets of her padded jacket, afraid he would see her trembling hands.","Her whole body tensed up. For a moment, she was terrified and flustered. She stood rooted to the spot, head bowed, unable to react.","Seeing that Qiao Lanshu ignored him, Liangzi's expression instantly turned a bit gloomy.","He stared at Qiao Lanshu's face. The warehouse keeper in front of him had fair skin and a small face. She looked young, but very beautiful.","He had indeed never seen this type before. Liangzi didn't know what was wrong with him; it was as if he were bewitched. He just felt he couldn't take his eyes off the warehouse keeper.","The driver, who had been chatting with the salesman, noticed this and walked over. He slapped the slips in his hand against Liangzi's chest and said loudly, Liangzi, wake up! Have you gone dumb staring at the girl? How long has it been since you saw a woman? Hahahaha.","Liangzi: ...","The driver added, Hurry up and load the goods. We've wasted a lot of time. If we get back late, the boss is going to nag again.","With that, the driver led them inside, and the salesman held the slips to tally the goods for them.","Liangzi didn't follow them in. He remained standing at the door, staring at Qiao Lanshu and asking, Comrade, my name is Chu Liangjun. What's your name?","Qiao Lanshu kept her head lowered in silence for a long time. Finally, she looked up, gave Liangzi a small smile, and said softly, I'm not telling you.","Saying that, she didn't wait for Liangzi to speak again. With a toss of her braids, she turned and walked away.","She quickly returned to the warehouse keeper's duty room on the side of the warehouse.","Closing the door of the small room, she slid the inner bolt shut with trembling hands.","Liangzi had just been dazzled by her smile. His expression shifted, and his heartbeat quickened a little.","He immediately followed her, leaning on the windowsill. Just as he was about to speak, with a bang, the window shutters were pulled shut right in front of his eyes.","Liangzi: ...","Qiao Lanshu turned her back to him, ignoring him.","Liangzi knocked on the window. Hey, little comrade, you still haven't told me your name. Open the door.","Liangzi knocked on the window for a long time. Seeing that Qiao Lanshu still ignored him, he stood there with a dark look in his eyes.","Just then, the driver carrying goods out of the warehouse saw him and called out to him again, Liangzi, stop flirting with the young lady. We have a lot of goods today, hurry over and help load them.","The driver was truly at his wit's end with this Liangzi.","If it weren't for the fact that Liangzi's cousin-uncle was the director of the cooperative, and that Liangzi himself had a bad temper and was basically a hooligan, the driver would have gotten rid of him long ago.","Dragging around a lazy hooligan all day meant the driver had to do much more work than usual.","Getting stuck with someone like him was truly terrible luck.","Liangzi didn't dare genuinely anger the driver. Anyway, the warehouse keeper worked here; she couldn't run away.","At worst, he could just come back another day.","So Liangzi went to the warehouse to help move the goods.","Another porter who had come with him helped move the goods and asked with a smile, What's up, Liangzi? Do you know that warehouse keeper?","Liangzi gave a crooked smile and said, We'll know each other after a little chat, won't we?","The porter added, If you ask me, you'd better give up early. Most female comrades who can work here are probably already married. Even if they aren't, their family conditions are definitely not bad. They certainly wouldn't look twice at guys like us. We all have rural registrations, and doing temporary manual labor—who would fancy us, right?","Hearing this, Liangzi's face darkened.","It was precisely because his family's financial situation was poor and he couldn't find a wife back home that he had come to the city, hoping to try his luck and find a bride.","So what if they looked down on him? Wouldn't everything be settled once the deed was done?"]},{"number":84,"title":"Chapter 84: Qiao Lanshu retched a few times and vomited.","paragraphs":["After the people from the supply and marketing cooperative finished moving the goods, the food factory's salesman completed the inventory and left.","The driver also got into the truck, ready to leave with the cargo.","At this time, Qiao Lanshu should have gone out to lock the door, but since Liangzi hadn't left, she didn't dare to go out.","Although she knew rationally that this was the food factory's warehouse and people passed by from time to time, so nothing would definitely happen.","But subconsciously, she was still very afraid and didn't dare to step outside.","Liangzi waited there for a while, seeing that Qiao Lanshu had no intention of coming out to lock the door at all.","The driver urged him again, Liangzi, get in the truck quickly! Damn it, what's so interesting about a woman? Hurry up and get in.","Liangzi replied loudly, I'll be right there.","Saying that, he walked over to the window again and said to Qiao Lanshu inside, Little comrade, we are leaving.","Qiao Lanshu pretended not to hear him, keeping her head down to organize her receipts.","Liangzi gritted his teeth, slapped the window hard, and then turned and left.","After getting in the truck, the driver looked at him while driving and said with a smile, Liangzi, if you really fancy that little girl, just have your uncle come over and ask about it when we get back. Your uncle is the director of the supply and marketing cooperative and has a wide network of contacts. Wouldn't it be easy for him to arrange a marriage for you?","Liangzi didn't know what he was thinking about. He said somewhat absentmindedly, It's just courting a girl, isn't it? I can handle it myself. I don't need my uncle.","What he actually didn't say was that the reason he came to the city to find a wife was because he could no longer find one in his village.","No one was willing to marry him because he had once harassed girls in the village and was almost arrested for hooliganism.","Fortunately, his uncle was the director of the supply and marketing cooperative, and his aunt's family had a brother who was a division commander in the army.","Although he was only an uncle, they were relatives after all. The villagers were mainly afraid of that division commander, so they didn't pursue the matter.","But his reputation in the village was indeed ruined.","If his uncle knew that he was harassing female workers here again, he might criticize him.","How could he possibly help him propose a marriage?","After Liangzi left, Qiao Lanshu finally came out of the room and locked the warehouse door.","Qiao Lanshu's face was a bit pale. She went back into the room and drank half a cup of hot water before feeling her numb, frozen hands ease up a little.","She began to calm down and think of a countermeasure.","Actually, when she first saw Chu Liangjun, she thought about telling Qin Yuanzheng immediately and waiting for him to help her deal with it.","Because she was truly too afraid. She was in such a panic at the time that she had no idea what to do.","However, when she calmed down and thought about it, Chu Liangjun hadn't actually done anything to her. He just said a few more words to her during work. Without any cause or reason, how could he be dealt with?","Besides, Chu Liangjun seemed to have a relative who was a division commander, a rank much higher than Qin Yuanzheng's. She didn't even know which military unit he was in. What if he targeted Qin Yuanzheng because of this?","Anything was possible, so Qiao Lanshu had to overthink it.","The Chu Liangjun of this lifetime hadn't committed a crime yet, so if she wanted to take revenge on him, she could only let him make a mistake.","After all, he was never a good person to begin with.","But how should she do it? Qiao Lanshu didn't know much about Chu Liangjun at present.","She could barely remember being locked up in the cave dwelling. As soon as she forced herself to think about it, she would feel dizzy, nauseous, and want to vomit.","Qiao Lanshu lay on the desk, trying hard to recall things about Chu Liangjun. Fragments of memories flashed through her mind, endless mountain ranges, a dark cave dwelling, a rough man...","Qiao Lanshu suddenly covered her mouth and retched a few times.","Then, she squatted by the trash can and threw up for a long time.","It was too disgusting. Just recalling it made her feel sick.","At this moment, she suddenly missed Qin Yuanzheng very much.","...","Meanwhile, Liangzi followed the truck back to the supply and marketing cooperative. He helped move goods for a while before refusing to move anymore, saying he was going out for a smoke.","But everyone knew he was just slacking off, and probably wouldn't come back to move goods again.","No one bothered with him, as they couldn't control him anyway.","Chu Liangjun went and bought a jar of canned yellow peaches, stuffed it in his pocket, and strolled back towards the food factory.","He squatted at the main gate of the food factory, smoking a cigarette while waiting for the factory workers to get off work.","The guard at the factory gate looked at Chu Liangjun vigilantly. Standing at the door of the guardroom, he asked loudly, Comrade, what are you doing? Why are you squatting here?","Chu Liangjun stood up, pulled out a Daqianmen cigarette, and handed it to the guard. He smiled and said, Comrade, I'm waiting for my friend to get off work. Could you make an exception and let me wait here for a bit?","The guard didn't take his cigarette, just shook his head and said, Sorry, comrade. It's not that I won't make an exception, but our factory has rules. Outsiders are not allowed in. Even if you are waiting for someone, you have to wait over there.","Saying that, the guard pointed to the other side of the gate. His side was the main passage of the gate, where female comrades would be coming and going after work. With a man like this squatting here, what if something happened?","Chu Liangjun's face darkened. He stared coldly at the guard, wanting to curse at him, but he quickly restrained himself.","He still had serious business to attend to, so he couldn't cause a conflict here.","Therefore, he had to take his cigarette back and walk towards the other side of the gate.","Before long, Chu Liangjun saw a military vehicle slowly stop at the main gate of the food factory.","Smoking his cigarette, he glanced at the military vehicle. He saw the door open and a tall, straight-backed soldier wearing a military cap and greatcoat step out of the car, carrying a thermal cotton bag.","The soldier was extremely sharp. Almost the moment Chu Liangjun looked at him, he immediately turned his head, his sharp gaze locking onto him.","Chu Liangjun shuddered all over, feeling a chill run through his body under that stare.","Just that one second of eye contact left him stunned.","Soon, the soldier withdrew his gaze and strode towards the food factory gate carrying his things. The guard, who had just been unfriendly to Chu Liangjun, now respectfully and politely opened the large iron gate to welcome the soldier in.","Chu Liangjun...","Holding his cigarette, Chu Liangjun spat fiercely, his face gloomy as he cursed, What a snob.","If this were in the village, he would have definitely thrown a punch. Daring to disrespect him, he must be tired of living.","It wasn't quitting time yet. The reason Qin Yuanzheng came over was to bring Qiao Lanshu some delicious food.","He arrived at the door of the warehouse where Qiao Lanshu worked, stood by the window, and reached out to knock on the glass.","Qiao Lanshu thought someone else had come to pick up goods. She looked up, and then her eyes lit up with excitement, Brother Zheng? Why are you here?","Heaven knew how excited she felt to see Qin Yuanzheng when she was in such a state of panic!","Qiao Lanshu immediately opened the door, ran out, and threw herself into his arms.","Qin Yuanzheng quickly hugged her, smiling as he said, Is Comrade Xiao Qiao this passionate?","Saying that, he whispered in her ear, Did you miss me just because we didn't do it last night?","He was feeling frustrated because they had not been intimate yesterday. Even though he had taken care of his needs in the washroom this morning, he still felt unsatisfied.","While at work, his mind was entirely occupied by his little wife.","It had not been long since he finished lunch, but he managed to find some free time and hurriedly rushed over to see her.","Qiao Lanshu no longer scolded him for having no filter.","Nestling in his arms, she whispered, \"Yes, I just missed you. I missed you so much.\"","When his little wife spoke such sweet words, it was incredibly captivating.","Qin Yuanzheng simply could not withstand her charm.","He whispered, \"I will come pick you up after work later.\"","He paused for a moment, then added, \"It is cold outside. Let us go inside to talk.\"","With that, he gently ushered Qiao Lanshu back into the room. Then, carrying a cotton bag inside, he said, \"Take a look. What delicious treats did I bring you?\"","Reaching into the bag, he pulled out a large, round orange and said, \"Look, what is this?\"","Qiao Lanshu was completely stunned. \"An orange? Brother Zheng, where did you manage to get this?\""]},{"number":85,"title":"Chapter 85: The Man Waiting Outside the Factory Gate","paragraphs":["Ever since Qin Yuanzheng married a Southern girl, he spent all day thinking about where to get some rice and where to find Southern food for her.","After all, his little wife didn't have a big appetite to begin with. Feeding her was like feeding a cat; she ate very little every day before getting full and couldn't eat a bite more.","Her appetite for food wasn't even as big as her appetite in bed.","Qin Yuanzheng's heart ached for his little wife.","In the past, he was all alone, coming and going by himself with nothing to tie him down.","Now that he had a little wife, things were different. He had to provide for her and figure out ways to make sure she ate well and lived comfortably.","So, he kept looking around to see where he could find fresh fruits and vegetables. It didn't matter if they were a bit expensive; he would save up his own money to buy them for her.","He had comrades in Shanghai and Nanchang. As soon as he got married, he wrote to them, asking them to help send rice and other things.","He remitted money to his comrades.","The one in Shanghai sent him ten catties of rice.","These oranges were sent from Nanchang.","Freshly picked from the tree, the oranges were wrapped in oil paper and sent to the military base on a northbound train.","Because the further north the train went, the colder the weather became, and the colder it was, the less likely the oranges were to spoil.","It took three or four days for them to reach Qin Yuanzheng's hands. When he took them out to look, all ten oranges were round and large, with the leaves still attached. They were incredibly fresh, and not a single one had gone bad.","As soon as he got the oranges, he couldn't help but grab two and bring them over for Qiao Lanshu to eat.","He left the remaining eight in the car to take home that night.","When Qiao Lanshu saw the oranges, she was both pleasantly surprised and moved.","She held the oranges, looked at them, and then hugged Qin Yuanzheng. Standing on her tiptoes, she planted a kiss on his cheek and said softly, \"Thank you, Hubby.\"","Qin Yuanzheng: \"...\"","See, his little wife was teasing him again.","She usually called him Brother Zheng. The moment she called him Hubby, Qin Yuanzheng knew she was deliberately flirting with him again.","He said helplessly, \"You're just taking advantage of the fact that you're at work and I can't do anything to you, right?\"","Qiao Lanshu smiled and said, \"That's right.\"","As she spoke, she looked up at him again, grinning foolishly.","Qin Yuanzheng really couldn't do anything about her. He could only reach out to rub her hair and ask, \"Do you want to eat an orange? I'll peel it for you.\"","Qiao Lanshu shook her head. She put the oranges back into the bag and said, \"Let's eat them when we get home. It wouldn't be good if someone saw.\"","Qin Yuanzheng didn't think there was anything wrong with it. These oranges came from a legitimate source; it wasn't like they were stolen. Who would dare criticize him?","He looked at Qiao Lanshu's complexion and asked in a low voice, \"I noticed you didn't look too well just now. What's wrong? Are you feeling unwell?\"","Qiao Lanshu hesitated for a moment and said conflictedly, \"Brother Zheng, there's something... I don't know how to say it.\"","Qin Yuanzheng leaned against the wall, let Qiao Lanshu sit on the chair, looked down at her, and said, \"What's there to be conflicted about when talking to your husband? Go ahead and tell me, I'm listening.\"","Qiao Lanshu smiled, looked up at him, and said, \"Remember when I had that nightmare about being taken away by a man and locked up in a cave dwelling? The man in my dream had a scar on his face. Well, today I saw someone who looks just like that man from my dream.\"","Such words sounded like pure fantasy.","A man from a nightmare actually appearing in real life—most people would think Qiao Lanshu was talking nonsense and tell her to stop letting her imagination run wild.","But how could Qin Yuanzheng bear to scold his wife?","He stayed silent for a moment, reached out to gently pinch Qiao Lanshu's cheek, and asked softly, \"They look very similar?\"","Qiao Lanshu nodded. \"Very similar. They both have a scar on their face.\"","As she spoke, she reached up and tapped a spot above her eyebrow, saying, \"Right here. He's a temporary worker at the supply and marketing cooperative. He came here to pick up goods today. When I saw him, it gave me a real fright.\"","Qin Yuanzheng frowned slightly and immediately pulled her into his arms, saying, \"Don't be afraid. From now on, I'll come pick you up from work. If I'm busy, I'll have Young Company Commander Yang come get you. Don't be scared.\"","Although Qin Yuanzheng hadn't wanted Young Company Commander Yang to pick up Qiao Lanshu before—after all, he had once arranged a blind date for the two of them.","And they had actually gotten along quite well.","But now that his little wife was so frightened, it simply wouldn't do for her not to be escorted.","However, Qin Yuanzheng still kept this coincidence in mind.","A temporary worker at the supply and marketing cooperative with a scar on his face—that would be quite easy to find. He planned to arrange for someone to look into the guy's background as soon as he got back.","Qin Yuanzheng still had to get back to work, so after staying with Qiao Lanshu for about half an hour, he left again.","Qiao Lanshu sat there, beginning to plot how she would get revenge on Chu Liangjun.","When it was time to get off work, Qiao Lanshu bundled herself up tightly and came out of the warehouse. From a distance, she saw Wang Xue standing at the door of the workshop, calling out to her, \"Xiao Qiao, let's go! Let's head to the supply and marketing cooperative to buy some meat. I heard they're selling sheep offal today, limited to half a catty per person. If we go late, it'll all be gone.\"","Wang Xue was the one who paid the most attention to food updates. Whenever there was anything to eat, she was guaranteed to be the first to know.","As soon as she saw Qiao Lanshu come out, she grabbed her arm and hurried toward the main gate.","Qiao Lanshu smiled and said, \"Sister, my Brother Zheng said he would come pick me up from work from now on. I don't know if he's arrived yet or not. If he's here, I won't be able to go with you.\"","Hearing this, Wang Xue immediately sounded a bit envious, \"Oh my, no wonder they all say that if you're going to marry, you should marry a military officer. Look at that, the men of our motherland really know how to dote on their wives.\"","Qiao Lanshu smiled shyly.","The two of them walked together to the main gate of the food factory. Qin Yuanzheng hadn't come; instead, it was Young Company Commander Yang who was there.","As soon as Young Company Commander Yang saw Qiao Lanshu, he greeted her enthusiastically, \"Sister-in-law, our regiment commander asked me to come pick you up from work.\"","He added with a bit of awkwardness, \"However, there's no car today. The leaders in our base all went to the headquarters for a meeting, so there are no cars left. I'll walk you back; it's not far anyway.\"","He had originally wanted to ride a bicycle over and give the regiment commander's family member a ride back.","But Staff Officer Lin had scolded him, saying, \"You're going to let the regiment commander's wife sit on the back seat of your bicycle, do you think that's appropriate?\"","He didn't think there was anything wrong with it, but Staff Officer Lin had said it wasn't quite right.","He couldn't really figure out exactly what was wrong about it either.","But Staff Officer Lin was smarter, so what he said was probably right.","Therefore, he didn't ride his bicycle over.","The regiment commander had said that he had to personally escort Qiao Lanshu home, all the way to the gate of the military residential compound, and watch her walk inside with his own eyes for the task to be complete. If anything were to happen, he wouldn't be able to bear the responsibility.","Wang Xue looked at Young Company Commander Yang, eyeing him up and down. She grabbed him very enthusiastically and said, \"Oh my, he's a company commander!\"","He scratched his head in embarrassment and said, \"Comrade, please don't grab me.\"","This older sister had reached out to pull at him right from the start, scaring the big young man into stepping back repeatedly.","Wang Xue smiled brightly and said, \"Comrade Company Commander, are you married? Do you want to find a partner? I have a few younger sisters back in my maiden home, do you want me to introduce you?\"","Young Company Commander Yang blushed deeply with embarrassment. He said, \"No, that's alright. I'm not looking to go on any blind dates right now.\"","With that, he moved closer to Qiao Lanshu's side, terrified that Wang Xue might try to grab hold of him again.","Truth be told, Yang used to be quite enthusiastic about matchmaking.","He had been eager to find a local wife, get married, and settle down.","But ever since his date with Comrade Xiao Qiao, those desires had entirely vanished.","After all, once you have met someone as stunning as Comrade Xiao Qiao, the thought of going on blind dates with anyone else just loses its appeal.","He figured he would need quite some time to recover.","Watching the two of them, Qiao Lanshu found the situation rather amusing.","However, when she turned her head and gazed into the distance, she unexpectedly spotted Chu Liangjun squatting outside the gates of the food factory. Her face instantly darkened, and the smile completely vanished from her lips."]},{"number":86,"title":"Chapter 86: Just Want Him Dead","paragraphs":["Chu Liangjun had been staking out outside the main gate of the food factory for half the afternoon.","Finally waiting until the factory's quitting time, he immediately stood up from the ground, folding his hands and hiding them inside the sleeves of his dusty gray padded jacket.","After staring at the female workers coming out of the factory for a long time, he finally saw Qiao Lanshu emerge.","His spirits lifted, and he immediately walked toward Qiao Lanshu.","When Qiao Lanshu saw Chu Liangjun, she felt a mix of panic and surprise.","It was strange. Logically, the current Chu Liangjun shouldn't even know her. They had only met once, so why was he so fixated on her?","Could it be that he just liked her type?","Qiao Lanshu couldn't figure it out, but judging from Chu Liangjun's behavior, he definitely did not have any memories of his past life.","Seeing Xiao Yang standing beside her, Qiao Lanshu instantly felt a bit more at ease.","With a soldier accompanying her, Chu Liangjun surely wouldn't dare to try anything reckless.","Indeed, when Chu Liangjun saw Young Company Commander Yang, his expression froze for a moment, and then his eyes turned somewhat sinister.","He saw a soldier walking beside Qiao Lanshu. They were an arm's length apart, but their expressions as they talked were very natural, clearly indicating they were quite familiar with each other.","Chu Liangjun guessed in his heart what their relationship could be. Were they dating?","It would be normal, after all, the girl was quite pretty, looked young, had a formal job, and her family conditions shouldn't be bad.","In contrast, if Chu Liangjun wanted to date that girl, it really would be a toad lusting after swan meat.","However, Chu Liangjun was simply unwilling to accept this.","The first time he saw that girl, he subconsciously felt that she belonged to him.","Whether she was a swan or even a celestial fairy, she should be his woman. He just had this feeling.","Chu Liangjun followed behind them for a whole block.","At first, because there were many workers getting off work from the food factory, everyone was walking onto the street, so Xiao Yang didn't notice anything unusual.","However, as they were about to reach the supply and marketing cooperative, the workers who had come out of the food factory had mostly dispersed. Xiao Yang sharply noticed that someone seemed to be following them.","He glanced back and saw a rather tall man wearing a gray padded jacket and a cotton hat, walking with his hands tucked into his sleeves about seven or eight meters away.","When the man saw Xiao Yang, he didn't avoid his gaze but instead looked toward the cooperative as if nothing was wrong.","Looking at his demeanor, it seemed as though he was just heading to the cooperative to buy something.","However, Xiao Yang didn't let his guard down, because this man had a knife scar on his face and looked quite fierce; in short, he didn't look like a good person.","Xiao Yang kept a secret watch on him while silently following beside Qiao Lanshu, listening as Wang Xue continued to pitch her younger sister to him: Young Company Commander Yang, Young Company Commander Yang? Are you listening?","Young Company Commander Yang quickly nodded: Comrade, I'm listening, please continue.","Wang Xue then continued: I'm telling the truth, my cousin is really beautiful. She went to middle school and is educated. She works as an accountant in the production team, helping to keep the books, and she calculates very accurately. It's only because her household registration is in the village that she can't get a job in the factory. But whether it's her looks or her abilities, she is top-notch. She's not old either, just 20 years old. Do you want me to have her come over and meet you?","Wang Xue was very enthusiastically recommending her sister.","There was no helping it; in this day and age, who wouldn't want to marry a military officer?","Marrying an officer meant never having to worry for the rest of one's life. Food, clothing, daily necessities, everything would be the absolute best.","Living in the military compound, eating in the military cafeteria, one could even go their whole life without working.","Wang Xue was usually very envious of Qiao Lanshu. After all, she was young but had married a regiment commander. Although Commander Qin was infertile, that wasn't a major problem. As long as she was blessed enough to enjoy the good life, that was enough, right?","Having said so much, Wang Xue noticed Xiao Yang occasionally glancing back without responding, so she asked: Oh, Company Commander Yang, why don't you tell me what type you like? I'll keep an eye out for you.","Company Commander Yang felt a bit embarrassed by her question. He subconsciously glanced at Qiao Lanshu before saying, I... I don't know either.","Wang Xue: ...","Even Qiao Lanshu laughed upon hearing this.","How could anyone not know their own preferred type?","It was obvious that Young Company Commander Yang didn't want to go on a blind date, so he was just using this to brush Wang Xue off.","Wang Xue spoke up again: Company Commander Yang, what do you keep looking back at? Is there something wrong behind us?","As she spoke, Wang Xue looked behind them.","Qiao Lanshu also followed her gaze and looked back.","Xiao Yang then said: There's a person...","His voice paused as he watched Chu Liangjun walk toward the three of them.","Then, Chu Liangjun took a can of mandarin oranges out of his pocket. He handed it to Qiao Lanshu, looked at her, and said: Comrade Warehouse Keeper, this is for you to eat.","Qiao Lanshu's expression changed, and she subconsciously took a half-step back. Young Company Commander Yang instantly stepped in front of her, glaring sternly at Chu Liangjun, and asked him: What are you doing?","Chu Liangjun looked at the young and handsome Comrade Xiao Yang, and said in a mocking tone: Comrade Liberation Army, don't be so bossy. Don't think that just because you're wearing that uniform, you can casually bully us ordinary folks. I just wanted to thank the Comrade Warehouse Keeper, that's all. Why are you being so fierce? If people didn't know better, they'd think she was your wife.","Comrade Xiao Yang's face immediately flushed red. He frowned and said: Stop talking nonsense, how am I bullying you? You...","Alright, alright, you're mighty, you're amazing. I'll just leave, okay?","Seeing that more and more people were gathering, and considering they were at the entrance of the cooperative, Chu Liangjun was afraid his second cousin would see him and scold him again. He decided it was best to head back and stay with the motorcade, as he had been away for quite a while.","Besides, with a soldier accompanying the warehouse keeper, it really wasn't a good time to make a move.","Chu Liangjun took a few more glances at Qiao Lanshu, then turned around and left with the canned fruit.","Young Company Commander Yang was a little angry as he said: What is wrong with this guy, acting crazy in broad daylight.","They were the Liberation Army, protecting the country and defending their homes; how could they possibly bully ordinary citizens?","He hadn't even said a single harsh word, yet the man was already speaking in such a sarcastic, passive-aggressive manner.","Comrade Xiao Yang said to Qiao Lanshu and Wang Xue: That man just now clearly wasn't a good person. You two sisters-in-law, if you see him in the future, remember to stay far away from him.","Wang Xue shook her head and said: Before, Zheng Daliu from our factory was executed by firing squad for committing rape. Ever since that incident, those street thugs have been much more well-behaved. I can't believe we ran into another one today; it seems there are still people who aren't afraid of death.","Hearing Wang Xue say this, Qiao Lanshu also remembered.","Zheng Daliu had brought people to sneak into a friend's house, stealing money and ration coupons. Just as they were about to leave, he saw his friend's wife in the kitchen, and blinded by lust, he got wicked ideas.","As a result, the friend's wife grabbed a kitchen knife, hacked one to death, injured another, and the third one ran away.","In the end, the injured Zheng Daliu was executed by firing squad.","The charges were theft coupled with rape.","In truth, Zheng Daliu had not actually succeeded in the assault. He had barely even started before he was slashed and wounded.","However, this gave Qiao Lanshu an idea.","If a crime like this could result in execution by firing squad, then perhaps she could arrange a little plan of her own...","Right now, the only thing she wanted was for Chu Liangjun to die."]},{"number":87,"title":"Chapter 87: Whoever Buys It for Me, I'll Be Nice to Them","paragraphs":["Wang Xue visited the supply and marketing cooperative every day to see if there was anything she could buy without ration coupons, or to pick up some meat or fruit to take home if they were in stock.","Although they had stored winter vegetables at home, they were just Chinese cabbage, potatoes, and radishes. Eating them every day made her want a change of taste, especially since those vegetables lacked any richness.","At the cooperative, there was occasionally sheep fat or sheep offal available, and sometimes even pork fat, though the supply was small and strictly limited.","Families with children always had to keep an eye out for this. After all, adults could go without, but growing children could not.","That man from earlier was just a minor interlude. Wang Xue didn't pay any attention to the man with the scar on his face.","She pulled Qiao Lanshu toward the meat counter. \"Let's hurry. If we go late, there won't be any left.\"","They hadn't arrived early. If it weren't for the purchase limit on sheep offal, they probably wouldn't have been able to buy any.","Wang Xue and Qiao Lanshu bought one pound each.","Qiao Lanshu didn't know how to make sheep offal soup, but Qin Yuanzheng probably did.","Since there were still yellow steamed buns and multigrain mantou at home, Qiao Lanshu felt there was nothing else she needed to buy.","However, she still had a one-yuan meat ration coupon, so she used it to buy sheep fat, planning to render it down and store the oil for cooking. It would add some richness to their meals and make them more filling.","People around here also loved drinking oil tea, made by frying flour with sheep fat and steeping it in boiling water. Qiao Lanshu didn't know how to fry it, nor did she like eating it. She figured she would ask Brother Zheng when she got back to see how he wanted to handle it. Qiao Lanshu wasn't skilled at making Northern-style food.","She pondered for a long time but still didn't know what to make, so she eventually gave up thinking about it.","She would just let Brother Zheng cook when she got home.","After they finished their shopping, Young Company Commander Yang accompanied them out, and Wang Xue parted ways with Qiao Lanshu.","Xiao Yang escorted Qiao Lanshu toward the military residential compound.","Not long after they started walking, Qiao Lanshu looked back and, sure enough, saw Chu Liangjun again.","Chu Liangjun was truly bold.","Even seeing an officer walking beside Qiao Lanshu, he still didn't hide, openly following them from behind.","Chu Liangjun had found a loophole. He followed from a distance of several dozen meters. Even the Emperor of Heaven couldn't do anything about him.","Naturally, Xiao Yang couldn't say anything. After all, this was a public street where anyone could walk. He couldn't exactly forbid Chu Liangjun from walking there.","Xiao Yang asked in a low voice, \"Sister-in-law, do you know him?\"","Qiao Lanshu nodded. \"He's a porter at the cooperative. I think he's from a village.\"","Xiao Yang's expression turned a bit serious. He said, \"He seems to be following you. Don't go out alone these next few days. Wait in the guard room every day after work. If the commander doesn't come, I'll come pick you up.\"","Qiao Lanshu nodded. \"Okay, thank you, Company Commander Yang.\"","Xiao Yang waved his hand and said, \"It's my duty. You don't need to be so polite, Sister-in-law.\"","After escorting Qiao Lanshu into the military compound and watching her walk through the gates with his own eyes, Xiao Yang finally turned and left.","Seeing Qiao Lanshu enter the military compound from afar, Chu Liangjun immediately turned around and left as well.","He was somewhat shocked because he hadn't expected Qiao Lanshu to live in the military compound.","He had assumed she merely came from a well-off family, but he hadn't expected her background to be this impressive.","That made things difficult.","Chu Liangjun began to hesitate.","Obviously, this young woman was not someone he could afford to provoke.","But no matter what, he still felt a bit unwilling to give up.","After heading back, Chu Liangjun wanted to ask around about Qiao Lanshu's situation, but since he had just arrived in the city, he didn't have any acquaintances.","His relationship with the people in the motorcade wasn't great either. Since he usually slacked off and shirked his duties at work, no one wanted to talk to him much.","He really had no one to ask at the moment.","So Chu Liangjun started wandering around the city again. Since he was idle anyway, he loved strolling through the city to see what entertainment it had to offer.","...","That evening, when Qin Yuanzheng returned, he asked Qiao Lanshu, \"I heard from Xiao Yang that someone followed you when you got off work?\"","After dropping Qiao Lanshu off, Xiao Yang had gone back to report to Qin Yuanzheng.","He had also mentioned the man following them to Qin Yuanzheng.","Qin Yuanzheng thought about how his wife was young, beautiful, and looked easy to bully. It was inevitable that some blind fools would try to approach her.","Qiao Lanshu sat opposite him, drinking a bowl of rice soup. Hearing this, she nodded. \"Yes, he followed us the whole way.\"","After her initial panic, Qiao Lanshu was now fairly calm when thinking about Chu Liangjun.","She said to Qin Yuanzheng, \"Brother Zheng, don't worry. With Xiao Yang escorting me, I'll be fine.\"","That Chu Liangjun was a natural-born scoundrel, but he was also afraid of death.","Seeing her accompanied by a soldier, he wouldn't dare approach.","However, since she was planning to scheme against him, she still needed some opportunities to cross paths with Chu Liangjun.","Qin Yuanzheng said with a dark expression, \"The Zheng Daliu incident just happened in this district, and now someone dares to stalk female comrades. It seems the propaganda from the various departments still isn't thorough enough.\"","Fortunately, he had escorted Qiao Lanshu to work in the morning and arranged for someone to pick her up in the afternoon. Qiao Lanshu would definitely be safe.","Qin Yuanzheng had already asked Xiao Yang to investigate the background of the man stalking female comrades.","He said, \"I'm having him investigated. If he has a criminal record, we'll send him straight to a labor camp.\"","Being sent to a labor camp would mean three years at most. What Qiao Lanshu wanted was for him to take a bullet.","She was silent for a moment before saying, \"Brother Zheng, maybe it's a misunderstanding? If he continues to stalk female comrades later, it won't be too late to investigate him then.\"","Qin Yuanzheng said disapprovingly, \"You're just too kind-hearted. Dealing with these hooligans, they should be dragged straight to a labor camp.\"","Even though he said that, Qin Yuanzheng couldn't just casually send someone to a labor camp for no reason.","The prerequisite for a labor camp was that the person had actually committed a crime and could be sentenced.","Qin Yuanzheng kept the matter in mind. The next morning, he watched Qiao Lanshu enter the gates of the food factory with his own eyes before finally leaving with peace of mind.","Just as Qiao Lanshu started work, she saw Liu Weihong, the supervisor of the pastry workshop, walking over.","Liu Weihong had a gray towel tied around her neck and was wearing an overcoat.","It looked nice, sure, but wearing an overcoat in this weather was actually quite cold.","Holding a requisition slip, Liu Weihong walked over, knocked on the window, and said, \"Hey, open up quickly. I need to pick up goods.\"","Qiao Lanshu opened the window, glanced at her, and reached out her hand. \"Supervisor Liu, let me see the pickup slip.\"","Liu Weihong frowned and said impatiently, \"It's you, isn't it? Changing the rules the moment you arrive. Now everyone has to bring a slip, you sure are something.\"","With that, she tossed the slip in her hand through the window.","Qiao Lanshu: \"...\"","Qiao Lanshu glanced at her expressionlessly. Liu Weihong glared back, What are you looking at? Hurry up, these things need to be sent to the director's office at the Industrial Bureau. If you keep dawdling and the leaders blame us, you won't be able to bear the consequences.","Qiao Lanshu picked up the forms scattered on the desk and signed them. Then, she pulled out one signed copy for her records and tossed the rest out the window.","One of them even hit Liu Weihong in the face.","Liu Weihong immediately cursed, What do you think you're doing? You're just a lowly warehouse keeper, yet you have no manners!","Qiao Lanshu couldn't even be bothered to respond to her.","Holding the keys, she opened the main door of the warehouse. Supervisor Liu, if you want to get the goods, do it quickly, or I'm locking the door.","Liu Weihong angrily picked up the forms. She walked to the warehouse door and looked at the bulky padded jacket Qiao Lanshu was wearing, as well as her dusty cotton shoes. She immediately said smugly,","What's the matter? Even after marrying a military officer, you're still living such a shabby life? Don't tell me he can't even bear to buy you a coat and leather shoes? So it turns out that some officers not only suffer from infertility, but they're also broke?","Hearing her say this, Qiao Lanshu finally noticed that Liu Weihong was wearing a pair of small high-heeled boots.","The boots had a red leather surface, pointed toes, and a ring of fine wool around the edges. The style looked quite nice.","However, while this kind of shoe was fine to wear in the autumn, wearing it in this bitter winter would leave one's legs freezing.","Even with thick cotton shoes on, Qiao Lanshu's toes felt numb after walking outside for a long time, let alone wearing those thin leather shoes.","Right, she finally realized what was unusual about Liu Weihong today.","Liu Weihong was wearing a new coat, a scarf, and leather boots today.","She had clearly been wearing a padded jacket before.","Seeing Qiao Lanshu constantly sizing her up, Liu Weihong grew even more smug. She sniffled, feeling that the cold wind today was a bit strong.","But she still said proudly, How about it? Qin Yuanzheng didn't buy you a coat, did he? See this? This is a cashmere coat, and these leather boots—he didn't buy those for you either, right? Don't think military officers are so amazing; they still just earn a fixed salary. How much can a regiment commander make? A little over a hundred at most. Look at my leather boots—a pair costs thirty to forty dollars! He definitely can't afford them!","As she spoke, she added, However, my partner is rich. Whatever I want, he can buy for me. Your man just doesn't cut it.","When it came down to it, she was still holding a grudge over Qiao Lanshu previously saying that her own husband was very capable.","The things Qiao Lanshu had said last time really did piss Liu Weihong off.","Being petty-minded by nature, she held onto that anger and swore to find a man better than Qin Yuanzheng.","And wouldn't you know, she actually found one.","Leather boots costing tens of dollars, a cashmere coat costing nearly a hundred—he bought them for her without a second thought.","Not to mention, this man was quite generous.","Qiao Lanshu admitted that her coat was indeed very nice, but she would pass on the leather boots. High heels in the dead of winter would just make your feet ache.","Qiao Lanshu couldn't help but ask her, It's over ten degrees below zero. Aren't you cold wearing that?","Liu Weihong was shivering from the cold, but she stubbornly retorted, What do you know? This kind of cashmere coat is the warmest! Wearing it is like wearing a whole suit of sheep's wool. Tell me, are sheep afraid of the cold? Let alone ten degrees below zero, even at a hundred degrees below zero, it wouldn't be cold!","Qiao Lanshu: ...","Qiao Lanshu felt that Liu Weihong's brain wasn't working very well.","She looked like a normal person, but when she spoke, she sounded like an idiot.","So Qiao Lanshu said, Hurry up and grab your things, I'm going to lock the door.","Maybe Liu Weihong wasn't afraid of the cold in her cashmere coat, but Qiao Lanshu felt cold even in her padded jacket. She wanted to quickly return to her heated little room, drink some hot water, and read a book.","She didn't want to stand out here blowing in the cold wind while listening to Liu Weihong brag.","Liu Weihong had shown off enough and was indeed freezing too much. She quickly walked into the warehouse, grabbed two boxes of biscuits and a large jar of canned yellow peaches, and came back out.","These items were to be given to the leaders of the Industrial Bureau. Usually, Liu Weihong would rush to take on these lucrative errands.","Otherwise, she wouldn't have been able to hook up with her current rich partner.","Qiao Lanshu locked the warehouse door and went back to her little room.","Holding the canned goods without gloves, Liu Weihong felt her hands turning numb from the cold.","She called out to Qiao Lanshu, Hey, you! Hurry up and help me carry these things to my workshop office.","Bang! The only answer she received was the sound of Qiao Lanshu shutting her door.","Liu Weihong was furious. You! What's so great about you? I'm the supervisor!","So what if she married a military officer? She thinks she's so amazing!","Once she and her partner got their marriage certificate, she wouldn't be afraid of Qin Yuanzheng!","Qiao Lanshu originally didn't want to pay any attention to Liu Weihong, but Chu Liangjun showed up again.","As expected, she knew Chu Liangjun would come back.","But what she didn't expect was that Liu Weihong would be there too, which made things difficult.","Chu Liangjun had come alone today. He used his identity as a delivery driver for the supply and marketing cooperative's fleet to enter the food factory once again.","But he was actually here to find Qiao Lanshu; he had absolutely no goods to pick up.","Seeing Chu Liangjun approaching, Qiao Lanshu immediately opened her window and said loudly to Liu Weihong, So what if he bought you a cashmere coat and leather shoes? If I wanted them, there would be men willing to buy them for me too. They aren't even worth that much money, what's there to show off?","Liu Weihong, already holding the biscuits and canned goods, was about to leave.","Hearing this, she immediately blew up. Turning around, she yelled, What kind of nonsense are you spouting? Not worth much? Do you know how much this outfit cost? One hundred and fifty dollars! Do you even have a hundred and fifty dollars? How dare you say that?","Qiao Lanshu glanced at Chu Liangjun, who was drawing near, and said, Even if I don't have it, there are definitely men willing to buy it for me. Whoever buys it for me, I'll get together with him. Isn't that easy? It's just a hundred and fifty dollars, someone can definitely afford it.","Liu Weihong was stunned by her words.","She stared dumbfounded at Qiao Lanshu and said, Whoever buys it for you, you'll get together with them? Do you even know what you're saying? If your...","Qiao Lanshu cut her off, Even if my Brother Zheng was here, I would say the exact same thing. Whoever buys it for me, I'll be with him. Who told you to show off in front of me? It made me unhappy, and I want it too, is that a problem?","Liu Weihong: ...","See? See? She knew that Qin Yuanzheng was no good!","Not only was he infertile, but he was also impotent!","If he were even a little bit useful, a little bit more of a man, Qiao Lanshu wouldn't be saying things like this, right?"]},{"number":88,"title":"Chapter 88: Don't think about sneaking back to Guangzhou, do you","paragraphs":["Chu Liangjun actually overheard the conversation between Qiao Lanshu and Liu Weihong. He thought to himself, women really do love money after all.","Back when he was in the village, he was looked down upon simply because his family was poor.","He had finally managed to get a matchmaker to introduce him to some girls for blind dates, but every single one of them despised his family's lack of money and thought he was too poor.","Chu Liangjun was indeed poor, and there was nothing he could do about it. Because of this helplessness, he felt even more resentful.","Now, relying on his cousin's connections, he had come to work in the city. However, the city girls were even more materialistic. As soon as they opened their mouths, they demanded cashmere coats and leather shoes.","A whole set like that would cost over a hundred yuan. What ordinary person could afford that?","Chu Liangjun thought of the soldier who accompanied Qiao Lanshu. He wondered to himself, could a soldier really afford it?","Liu Weihong was in a hurry to deliver the biscuits and canned goods. She stood there, looking at Qiao Lanshu mockingly, and said, \"What's wrong, regretting it now? Don't think those military officers are rich. Their salaries max out at a hundred yuan, and most only make a few dozen yuan a month. How could they afford these things? But it's too late for you to regret it now. From now on, you can just watch others wear them.\"","With that, Liu Weihong turned and left, walking briskly.","There was no helping it; Qiao Lanshu was staying in a small, heated room where the cold wind couldn't reach her, so of course she wasn't cold.","But Liu Weihong was already wearing very little, and she had deliberately strolled around in front of Qiao Lanshu a few times to show off. Her hands and feet were nearly numb from the cold.","No, she had to go back and have a good talk with her boyfriend, making him buy her a fur coat to keep warm.","But that stuff was expensive. The price was incomparable to a regular coat, and she didn't know if he would be willing to buy it for her.","Pondering this, Liu Weihong hurried away.","Chu Liangjun waited on the side for a while. As soon as Liu Weihong left, he walked over.","Qiao Lanshu had seen him long ago. She had already locked the door to the small room, and seeing him approach, she prepared to close the window.","Chu Liangjun reached out to stop her, pressing his hand against the window. He looked at her with a burning gaze and said, \"What's this? You close the window as soon as you see me? Am I really that unwelcome to you?\"","As he spoke, he took out a jar of canned fruit from his pocket and placed it on the windowsill. He said, \"I bought this especially for you. Do you like it?\"","Qiao Lanshu felt disgusted just looking at him.","Especially that scar on his face. She had forgotten most of her memories from the cave dwelling, but she remembered the scar on his face very clearly.","Qiao Lanshu simply decided not to close the window. She sat inside, picked up a book to read, and treated him as if he were invisible.","Chu Liangjun was smart; he knew how to act without getting into trouble. So, he deliberately asked, \"Our supply and marketing cooperative needs to pick up bread and pickles the day after tomorrow. Do you have enough inventory in the warehouse here? Have you prepared the goods for us in advance?\"","Qiao Lanshu replied, \"They are prepared. Do you need anything else?\"","Chu Liangjun looked at Qiao Lanshu and asked again, \"Do you like that coat and those leather shoes?\"","Hearing this, Qiao Lanshu glanced at him and sneered, \"I also like watches and radios. What, are you going to buy them for me? How much is your monthly salary anyway? You have a lot of nerve asking about these things.\"","With that, she closed the window.","Chu Liangjun was a man with strong pride. He couldn't stand Qiao Lanshu looking at him with such disdainful eyes, let alone tolerate her speaking in such a condescending tone.","However, Chu Liangjun couldn't bring himself to be angry at Qiao Lanshu's face.","Qiao Lanshu was destined to be his woman; he just had this strong premonition.","Once he got his hands on Qiao Lanshu, he would definitely have to teach this woman a good lesson.","He stared at Qiao Lanshu and said in a low voice, \"Since you like them, I'll buy them for you. Just you wait.\"","Saying that, he turned and left.","Seeing him leave, Qiao Lanshu immediately made sure the window was shut tight.","She sat nervously in her chair, her heart pounding, breaking out in a cold sweat.","Although she knew that right now she was in the food factory's warehouse, and Chu Liangjun wouldn't dare and couldn't do anything to her.","But she was still terrified of him. Seeing the scar on his face and hearing his voice made her feel frightened and disgusted.","Qiao Lanshu looked at the canned fruit left on the windowsill. She suddenly stood up, grabbed the can, and wanted to throw it into the trash bin.","However, at the crucial moment, she paused.","This canned fruit was produced in the food factory, and it was not cheap.","Ordinary people would only bear to buy a can or two during the New Year. It would be such a pity to throw it away.","She placed the can back on the table. Although she didn't want to eat it, she could give it to someone else.","Qiao Lanshu opened her notebook. Chu Liangjun's name was written in it, and next to his name, she had written the name of the director of the supply and marketing cooperative, as well as the director's wife, and the wife's brother.","She wrote down what she knew, pondering who Chu Liangjun might borrow money from.","Or perhaps, where would he go to steal money?","...","During lunch at the cafeteria, Qiao Lanshu gave the canned mandarin oranges that Chu Liangjun had brought her to Wang Xue.","Wang Xue had two children at home, so she could share it with them. Qiao Lanshu couldn't just throw the can away.","Wang Xue looked at the canned oranges handed to her and said, \"Oh my, this is produced right here in our factory. It's quite expensive. You should keep it for yourself, why give it to me?\"","Qiao Lanshu felt a bit embarrassed. She was always straightforward with Wang Xue, so she said directly, \"Sister, please don't be offended. Someone gave this to me, but I really dislike him and don't want to eat his things. Throwing it away would be a waste, so I thought of giving it away.\"","Wang Xue was initially hesitant to accept it, but upon hearing this, she immediately took the can and asked with a smile, \"So that's how it is? Then if there's anything else you don't want in the future, just give it to me. I won't mind at all.\"","Canned fruit was a good thing. Wang Xue said, \"You really have a backbone. If it were me, I'd eat it even if it was a gift from an enemy.\"","Qiao Lanshu: \"...\"","While eating, Wang Xue added, \"Little Qiao, could you accompany me somewhere later?\"","After lunch, there was still more than half an hour of the lunch break left.","Usually, Qiao Lanshu would go back to read or do something similar.","But since Wang Xue asked, she inquired, \"Where to?\"","Wang Xue quickly finished the remaining dough drop soup in her bowl in two gulps, then lowered her voice and said:","\"I have a younger female cousin who sells tickets at the train station. She's quite pretty. A while ago, a guy took the initiative to court her. He bought her food and drinks every day and was very generous. My cousin gradually developed feelings for him. But guess what? They had only been dating for a couple of days when someone ran up to my cousin and told her that the man already has a wife and kids back in the countryside! Today, I have to go to the textile factory next door and ask around to see what exactly is going on with that man!\"","Hearing this, Qiao Lanshu was instantly surprised. \"That man already has a wife and children in the countryside? Then why is he still giving things to your cousin?\"","Wang Xue sneered, \"Who knows, he's just being a scumbag!\"","Qiao Lanshu: \"...\"","Wang Xue's younger cousin had been working here for a few years now. Since the rest of their family wasn't around, they had asked Wang Xue to take good care of her.","Wang Xue had originally wanted to find her cousin a good match. Previously, she had kept pestering Young Company Commander Yang with questions, just to see if Young Company Commander Yang might take a fancy to her cousin.","But now, this mess had happened.","The worst part was that she had only just found out about it. Her cousin had felt too humiliated to even tell her before.","Qiao Lanshu followed Wang Xue out the back door of the food factory. Just two streets over was the textile factory.","Qiao Lanshu asked in a low voice, Why did your cousin suddenly tell you about this? Did something happen?","Wang Xue nodded. As soon as she came out, she looked around and grabbed a stick as thick as an arm. She said to Qiao Lanshu, My cousin doesn't want to date him anymore, but he refuses to accept it and keeps pestering her. It's even affecting my cousin's work. Jobs are hard to come by these days. If he ends up making my cousin lose her job, I'll beat him to death!","Qiao Lanshu looked at the stick in Wang Xue's hand with some shock and swallowed hard. Sister, what are you going to do with that stick?","Wang Xue replied, Don't worry. If he talks reasonably, I definitely won't hit him.","Qiao Lanshu was speechless.","Truth be told, Wang Xue was quite tall, slightly plump, and had a loud voice.","If it came to a fight, some men might not even be her match.","It was Qiao Lanshu's first time encountering such a situation, and she was a bit worried that Wang Xue would actually get into a fight.","The two of them arrived near the textile factory where Liu Jianguo worked. At this hour, there were quite a few people coming in and out of the factory's main gate.","Wang Xue marched straight to the guardhouse at the main gate and asked the older man inside, Comrade, I'm looking for Liu Jianguo.","Hearing this, the man in the guardhouse spoke through the window, Liu Jianguo asked for leave. He's not in the factory this afternoon.","Wang Xue's face darkened. He asked for leave? What did he take time off to do?","The man in the guardhouse replied, How would I know what he went to do? Most likely, he went to see his girlfriend. He just started dating someone, everyone knows about it.","Wang Xue was speechless.","She was absolutely furious. Turning on her heel, she said to Qiao Lanshu, That bastard probably went to find my cousin. I have to go to the train station to find him.","Qiao Lanshu knew where the train station was; it was diagonally across from the Construction Corps Headquarters building.","She quickly pulled Wang Xue back and said, Sister, don't be impulsive. The train station is quite far, and we won't make it in time by walking. Why don't we go back to our factory to ask for leave first, and then take the bus over?","Wang Xue had just been blinded by anger.","Hearing Qiao Lanshu's words, she quickly nodded. Right, right, right, I almost forgot. We have to go back to the factory first.","The two of them hurried back to the food factory.","Since Qiao Lanshu had agreed to accompany Wang Xue, she naturally asked for leave as well. The two spent two cents to take the bus, heading straight for the train station.","Coincidentally, Qin Yuanzheng had also driven to the headquarters for a meeting today.","Staff Officer Lin was standing outside the headquarters smoking a cigarette. When he looked up, he happened to see Qiao Lanshu and Wang Xue getting off a nearby bus, crossing the street, and entering the train station.","Staff Officer Lin was dumbfounded.","The cigarette fell from his mouth.","Wait, in broad daylight, what major event required going to the train station?","With this thought in mind, he immediately ran inside the headquarters building.","Qin Yuanzheng was in Commander Li's office, having a meeting with other military officers.","Staff Officer Lin paced back and forth outside the office, burning with anxiety.","Staff Officer Lin's footsteps were entirely too clear. Commander Li took a sip of water and roared impatiently, Which son of a bitch is out there? Get your ass in here!","The guard at the door quickly opened it and invited Staff Officer Lin inside.","Seeing Lin Yucheng, Qin Yuanzheng frowned and asked, Didn't I tell you to go back to the mining area to handle some business? Why are you back?","In front of Commander Li and a group of division and regimental commanders, Lin Yucheng said, Reporting to the Commander! I just saw your wife go to the train station across the street. In broad daylight, I was afraid she was secretly taking a train to run away, so I came specifically to inform you!","Qin Yuanzheng was speechless.","Everyone else was speechless.","Commander Li stroked his chin and said with a gloating tone, This southern girl ate ten catties of my rice and ten catties of my sweet potatoes, and now she wants to run away? But it makes sense. Her hometown is thousands of kilometers away. She isn't used to living or eating here, and her husband doesn't know how to dote on her, right? It'd be strange if she didn't run.","Qin Yuanzheng remained silent.","The other officers in the office began to chime in. Eh? Xiao Qin, I heard a long time ago that you got married. You didn't force this marriage, did you? We are the Liberation Army, we don't condone forced marriages.","Commander Li said slowly, I don't know if he forced it, but I do know he forcefully carried her back from the hospital.","Gasp! That actually happened? Commander Li, this is where you were wrong. Why didn't you stop him back then?","Commander Li smiled and said, With his massive size, he's like a brute bull. How could I possibly stop him?","Oh my, could that little girl have been coerced by Xiao Qin? She didn't dare resist normally, so she took advantage of him being tied up in a meeting today to hurriedly run to the train station and escape?","Commander Li nodded, looking profoundly wise. Hard to say, hard to say! After all, with Xiao Qin's rotten temper, a normal young girl wouldn't be able to stand it.","Listening to everyone's teasing and observing Qin Yuanzheng's expression, cold sweat poured down Staff Officer Lin's forehead.","Qin Yuanzheng stood up with a stern face. He glanced at Staff Officer Lin, then said to Commander Li, Chief, I have an urgent family matter to handle and need to leave for an hour. I request that Lin Yucheng attend the meeting in my place and convey the spirit of the meeting to me later!","Commander Li waved his hand and said earnestly, Go on, go on. Talk things out nicely. Be gentler to the young lady. If she wants to leave, don't stop her. Everything must be based on the girl's own wishes, understand?","Qin Yuanzheng was speechless.","His face was pitch black as he replied, Understood, Chief! I'll be going now.","Saying that, he immediately turned and strode out of the office.","As soon as he left, the several people in the office immediately burst into loud laughter.","Lin Yucheng was completely numb. These senior officers usually looked so stern, but when they joked with their own people, they were quite ruthless.","It was only because of their high ranks that Qin Yuanzheng didn't dare lash out.","If this had been in his own regiment, a bunch of people would have been beaten to the ground by him long ago.","Qin Yuanzheng hurried out of the headquarters building.","He took large strides across the road, heading in the direction of the train station.","Wasn't his wife supposed to be at work? Why did she suddenly go to the train station?","Could it be that she really couldn't stand him anymore and wanted to sneak back to Yangcheng?"]},{"number":89,"title":"Chapter 89: You Know I'll Teach You a Lesson","paragraphs":["Qiao Lanshu and Wang Xue hurried to the train station together.","Wang Xue's cousin, Wang Haitang, worked as a ticket seller at the station. Since she saw a lot of people every day, men would often ask her if she was looking for a boyfriend.","Some people thought she had a good job and was decent-looking, so they would ask if she was looking for a husband and offer to act as a matchmaker for her.","Wang Haitang had turned down quite a few people. After all, she didn't have much of a mind of her own and originally planned to wait for Wang Xue to introduce someone to her.","However, a while ago, she ended up dating Liu Jianguo.","A few days ago, things had been going fine between her and Liu Jianguo. He was a worker at the textile factory. Although he wasn't particularly good-looking, he had a stable job, was very attentive, and was willing to spend money on her.","Wang Haitang herself was never really valued in her own family. Her family heavily favored boys over girls, and her parents only paid attention to her brothers. Raised by her grandmother, she had been neglected since childhood, and rarely did anyone show her any care.","This led to her being extremely introverted. She rarely spoke and suffered from low self-esteem.","Liu Jianguo knew exactly that she lacked love and care, so he showed her the utmost consideration. He would occasionally bring her brown sugar, wait for her to get off work, and tell her to drink more hot water so she wouldn't catch a cold.","In short, he hadn't spent much money, but he had already moved Wang Haitang deeply.","They hadn't been dating for more than a couple of days when someone told Wang Haitang the truth. Otherwise, she probably would never have known in her entire life that Liu Jianguo already had a wife back in his home village.","The household registration system was very strictly controlled nowadays. People with rural registrations couldn't just come to work in the city.","If villagers wanted to travel and visit the city, they had to get a letter of introduction from the production team or the commune. Even with the letter, they couldn't stay long and had to return home quickly. If they needed to stay in a guesthouse, they would need further approval from the production team.","Therefore, some male workers, despite having wives and children in the countryside, knew that their wives would never be able to come and find them.","They could date someone in the city, and no one would ever know.","Liu Jianguo had banked on the fact that Wang Haitang would never find out, which was why he pursued her.","Wang Xue was furious. She said to Qiao Lanshu, These scumbags are truly despicable. Having one at home isn't enough; they have to come and deceive innocent, unmarried young girls. What a bastard! Watch me beat him to death later.","The two of them arrived at the train station's ticket office. There were two ticket windows, one of which was empty.","Wang Xue and Qiao Lanshu walked over. Standing at the window, she asked the other ticket seller, Miss, is Wang Haitang not working today?","The young woman replied, Oh, her? She went to fetch some water.","Wang Xue asked again, Which way is the pantry?","The young woman pointed and said, Go all the way to the end from here, and it's right around the corner.","Wang Xue immediately turned and headed in the direction of the pantry.","Due to the winter snow, trains had been suspended for the past two days, so there were barely any people in the station.","Clutching her wooden stick, Wang Xue hurried to the pantry and searched inside and out, but she didn't see anyone.","Frowning, Wang Xue turned back and said to Qiao Lanshu, I'll go check near the restrooms.","With that, she walked toward the restrooms.","The pantry wasn't far from the side door. Qiao Lanshu stood there, walked a little toward the side door, and through the glass panels, she saw a man and a woman grabbing and pulling at each other on the small path outside.","The girl had a round face, wore a gray padded cotton jacket, and had her hair in two braids. The man was pulling her sleeve, refusing to let her leave, and she was stomping her feet in anxiety.","Looking at the man, he appeared to be twenty-six or twenty-seven, tall and thin, and he kept harassing her.","Qiao Lanshu's heart skipped a beat as she wondered: Could this be Wang Xue's cousin, Wang Haitang?","She quickly ran back just as Wang Xue came out of the restroom. Wang Xue walked up to Qiao Lanshu and said, I couldn't find her. Where on earth did she go?","Qiao Lanshu pulled her over to the side door and whispered, Sister, look at that. Is that your cousin?","Wang Xue went to the side door and peered through the glass. Ha, wasn't that Liu Jianguo and her cousin Wang Haitang?","Wang Xue's face instantly darkened. She said, Oh, this bastard! He actually dared to come and harass my cousin again! Watch me beat him to death!","Wang Haitang's personality was too soft and introverted; she never really knew how to reject others in the first place.","Let alone when someone was relentlessly pestering her.","She had absolutely no idea what to do.","Liu Jianguo had taken advantage of her cowardly nature, knowing she wouldn't fight back. He also knew that even if she found out about his family later on, she wouldn't dare make a scene.","Some people were just like that, even when they were being bullied right to their faces, they wouldn't dare utter a word.","Wang Xue had her own job and children, so she was quite busy and couldn't visit her cousin often. After all, they were only cousins, not biological sisters. To be honest, since they hadn't grown up together, their relationship was quite ordinary.","Because she rarely visited, she didn't know much about Wang Haitang's situation. This time, Wang Haitang was genuinely terrified of Liu Jianguo. At a complete loss and afraid that he might make her lose her job, she had no choice but to seek out Wang Xue and tell her about it.","Given Wang Xue's fiery temper, she exploded the moment she heard it.","She rolled up her sleeves, gripped the wooden stick she had been holding against her chest, and said to Qiao Lanshu, Xiao Qiao, wait for me here. I'll be right back.","Seeing her with the stick made Qiao Lanshu nervous. She whispered, Sister, be careful!","Saying this, she grabbed Wang Xue's arm and cautioned, Whatever you do, don't hit him in the head!","If she accidentally killed him, it would be a huge problem.","Wang Xue said in a low voice, Don't worry, sister. I have two kids; I know my limits.","With that, she pushed the door open and charged out.","Over there, Liu Jianguo was still pulling at Wang Haitang. He said, Haitang, you didn't actually believe the nonsense Lame Chen sprouted, did you? I already told you I don't. How could I have a wife? I truly like you and want to spend my life with you. What's the deal with you always avoiding me?","Wang Haitang kept her head down, so anxious she was on the verge of tears.","She pushed away the approaching Liu Jianguo and said helplessly, Brother Liu, please stop talking to me. I already said we aren't suitable for each other.","Liu Jianguo stared at her and sneered, How are we not suitable? Didn't you say I was pretty great before?","Wang Haitang said conflictedly, I was ignorant before. Let's just forget about it. You have a good job; you won't have to worry about finding a wife.","Liu Jianguo still kept a tight grip on her arm, relentlessly saying, Wang Haitang, what do you take me for? Someone you can have when you want and throw away when you don't? Let me tell you, since we've already started dating, don't even think about dumping me. Our relationship isn't something you can just call off!","Wang Haitang's eyes grew red with panic, and she was almost crying. She said, Don't pull me. Let go of me first...","Liu Jianguo pulled even tighter. He stared at Wang Haitang and said, I won't let go, I just won't! Don't even think about running away...","Right then, he heard someone roar, I'll beat you to death, you son of a bitch! Get your filthy paws off her!","Liu Jianguo immediately looked up and saw a woman charging towards him with a stick, roaring. He was instantly stunned, unable to react. In a flash, the stick whistled through the air and landed with a loud \"thwack,\" striking hard on the arm he was using to pull Wang Haitang.","\"Ah!\"","Liu Jianguo let out a shriek of pain, clutching his arm, his face instantly turning pale.","He stumbled backward in a panic, accidentally falling to the ground, and stared at Wang Xue in terror, shouting, \"You... who are you? Are you trying to kill someone? Are you crazy?\"","As soon as Wang Haitang saw Wang Xue arrive, her eyes welled up with tears. She cried out, \"Sis!\"","Wang Xue pushed her aside and said, \"Get behind me. Just watch me beat this shameless scoundrel who's acting like a hooligan today.\"","With that, she picked up the stick again and chased after Liu Jianguo, hitting him several times in a row. \"It's you I'm beating!\"","Having recovered his senses, Liu Jianguo gritted his teeth against the pain and lunged forward to snatch the stick from Wang Xue. He wrestled for it while cursing, \"Have you lost your mind, woman? Why are you hitting people for no reason? I'm going to report you! I'll have the public security comrades arrest you!\"","Wang Xue held onto the stick for dear life, kicking and stomping, even reaching out to scratch Liu Jianguo's face, all while yelling at him, \"Bah! You shameless bastard! What, the thief crying 'stop thief,' huh? Harassing a female comrade, and you think you're in the right! Go ahead and report me if you dare. Let's see if the public security comrades arrest me or you!\"","As she spoke, Wang Xue kicked Liu Jianguo a few more times. Provoked beyond endurance, Liu Jianguo finally managed to wrench the stick from her and started chasing Wang Xue to hit her back.","Qiao Lanshu was frantic with worry. The stick was quite thick, and a man's strength was considerable. What if Wang Xue really got hit?","She quickly opened the door and rushed out, standing to the side and shouting, \"The patrol team is coming! The patrol team is coming! Put down that stick!\"","Hearing this, Liu Jianguo was indeed startled. He halted his steps and looked up towards Qiao Lanshu.","When he saw Qiao Lanshu, he was momentarily taken aback, wondering where this young woman had sprung from. She was quite pretty. Was she a staff member at the train station?","He hadn't seen her before.","Then, he snapped back to reality and sneered, \"Don't try to fool me. I can see you're all in cahoots. Even if I hit you today, it's justifiable self-defense!\"","With that, he suddenly aimed a kick at Wang Haitang, who hadn't had time to run away.","Wang Haitang had originally intended to break up the fight, which is why she hadn't run.","She let out a sharp scream as Liu Jianguo's kick sent her sprawling to the ground.","Wang Xue was furious. Having initially run away, she picked up another stick and came back to fight Liu Jianguo.","Qiao Lanshu was stamping her feet in anxiety. Letting this chaos continue was not good.","However, she wouldn't be like Wang Haitang, foolishly stepping forward to get hit.","She looked around and suddenly picked up a stone from the ground, preparing to throw it at Liu Jianguo.","Just as she was looking for an opportunity to hurl the stone, she heard someone call her name.","The voice was cold and hard, carrying a mix of urgency and anger, and it was very loud: \"Qiao Lanshu!\"","Qiao Lanshu jumped, startled out of her wits!","Clutching the stone, she immediately turned to look.","Then, she saw Qin Yuanzheng, his expression stern, striding quickly towards her.","Qin Yuanzheng, who was usually so physically fit, was actually somewhat out of breath.","Qiao Lanshu was both surprised and a little guilty. She offered an ingratiating smile and said, \"Brother Zheng, what brings you here?\"","Qin Yuanzheng's face was serious. He walked over swiftly, grabbed Qiao Lanshu's arm, snatched the stone from her hand, and casually tossed it to the ground.","Then, he pushed Qiao Lanshu behind him and strode towards the chaotic scene. With one hand, he pulled Wang Xue aside, then lifted his leg and delivered a powerful kick to Liu Jianguo!","While Wang Xue's stick strike had only made Liu Jianguo yelp, Qin Yuanzheng's kick now completely silenced him.","Liu Jianguo clutched his stomach, lying on the ground, his face pale. It took him several seconds to recover before he started howling in pain.","The sisters, Wang Xue and Wang Haitang, were startled by Qin Yuanzheng's sudden appearance. They retreated a few steps, watching him nervously.","After all, Qin Yuanzheng's expression at that moment was extremely grim, and his aura was quite intimidating.","Qin Yuanzheng turned to look at Qiao Lanshu and asked with a dark face, \"Weren't you supposed to be at work? What are you doing here, of all places?\"","Qiao Lanshu looked at Qin Yuanzheng with sparkling eyes, full of admiration, and said, \"Brother Zheng, you're amazing! That kick just now was so cool!\"","Qin Yuanzheng: \"...\"","Everyone else: \"...\"","Wang Xue truly admired Qiao Lanshu. Couldn't she see Commander Qin's face was as dark as Lord Guan's?","And here she was, complimenting him.","No wonder she could be the family member of a regiment commander.","At that moment, the train station patrol team really did arrive—three of them.","Qin Yuanzheng then grabbed Qiao Lanshu by the arm, turned, and walked away.","Wang Xue and Wang Haitang couldn't leave and had to explain the whole story to the patrol team.","Liu Jianguo was Wang Haitang's boyfriend, at least he had been, so him coming to find Wang Haitang couldn't really be considered harassing a female comrade.","As for whether he actually had a wife at home, that would require investigation, which wasn't the train station patrol team's responsibility but fell under the public security bureau's jurisdiction.","After asking a few questions and determining it was a relationship dispute, the patrol team members mediated briefly and then told them to leave the train station.","Wang Haitang no longer had the heart to work, so she asked for leave and went home with Wang Xue.","...","Qiao Lanshu was dragged by Qin Yuanzheng out of the train station. Qin Yuanzheng went to the entrance of the headquarters building, got into his car, and only then asked Qiao Lanshu, \"Alright, explain. What exactly happened today?\"","Knowing Qin Yuanzheng was angry, Qiao Lanshu obediently recounted the events to him.","After listening, Qin Yuanzheng said with a stern face, \"I don't mind you accompanying someone here. But what were you doing picking up that stone just now, hmm? With your slender arms and legs, did you also want to join the fray?\"","Qiao Lanshu: \"...\"","Qiao Lanshu glanced at his expression and said softly, \"I just... I was afraid things would get out of control, so I wanted to help.\"","Qin Yuanzheng was genuinely very angry this time.","When he came, he was terribly afraid Qiao Lanshu had really gone back to Yangcheng. In his panic, he had even forgotten the trains were suspended these past two days.","Then, as soon as he arrived at the station, he saw Qiao Lanshu holding a stone, ready to fight that man?","Qin Yuanzheng sighed. He looked at Qiao Lanshu, his expression cold and stern, his tone very serious, as if scolding a disobedient child. He admonished Qiao Lanshu, \"Don't let there be a next time. You know I will punish you if you do, right?\""]},{"number":90,"title":"Chapter 90: He's Just Pretending to Be Angry","paragraphs":["After being scolded by Qin Yuanzheng for a bit, Qiao Lanshu immediately became obedient.","Qin Yuanzheng was truly angry this time. Not only did he call her by her full name, but his tone was also fierce. Qiao Lanshu sat obediently in the car, her head bowed, not daring to utter another word.","Seeing her like this, Qin Yuanzheng's heart immediately began to ache for her.","He really felt that he was completely wrapped around her little finger.","Such a cute little wife—he couldn't bear to be fierce or scold her. After just a couple of words of criticism, before his wife even reacted, he was already feeling sorry for her.","Qin Yuanzheng looked at Qiao Lanshu helplessly. Still a bit frustrated, he reached out to pinch her chin, lifting her head to look at him, and asked, \"Comrade Xiao Qiao, so do you know what you did wrong?\"","Qiao Lanshu quickly nodded and said very obediently, \"Brother Zheng, I know I was wrong. I promise I won't dare do it again next time.\"","Qin Yuanzheng didn't quite believe her, so he asked again, \"What if next time, your colleagues or friends or whatever ask for your help again? Will you still go?\"","Qiao Lanshu: \"...\"","In her heart, Qiao Lanshu was thinking that of course she would go.","But facing Qin Yuanzheng, she didn't dare say it out loud.","So, she fell silent for a moment. After two seconds of not speaking, Qin Yuanzheng applied a little pressure, pinched her cheek, and said in a deep voice, \"I see you don't know you were wrong at all.\"","Qiao Lanshu: \"...\"","Qiao Lanshu quickly tried to salvage the situation, saying, \"Then I won't go, I won't go, okay?\"","Qin Yuanzheng didn't say anything. He just started the car and drove straight home.","It wasn't early anymore, with only about an hour left until quitting time. Qin Yuanzheng was currently in a fit of pique, so he didn't return to the military base.","He might as well go home and vent his frustration.","Looking at Qin Yuanzheng's expression, Qiao Lanshu felt incredibly nervous.","In her past life, she had been with Qin Yuanzheng for so long, and he had never gotten angry with her.","Why was the young Qin Yuanzheng so temperamental?","She asked cautiously, \"Brother Zheng, are you angry?\"","Qin Yuanzheng ignored her, just driving in silence.","Qiao Lanshu suddenly felt a little panicked.","What should she do? She suddenly had a bad premonition.","When the car pulled into the courtyard, Qin Yuanzheng parked, pulled out the keys, and said, \"Get out, we're going inside.\"","Qiao Lanshu: \"...\"","Qiao Lanshu didn't dare get out of the car. She quickly said, \"Brother Zheng, it's still early. Why don't we go to the supply and marketing cooperative to buy some groceries first?\"","Qin Yuanzheng walked around the car and reached out to open her door.","He bent down slightly, looking at Qiao Lanshu with a serious expression that didn't look like he was joking. \"Don't worry, you'll have something to eat tonight.\"","Qiao Lanshu: \"...\"","Qin Yuanzheng asked in a low voice, \"If you don't get out, do you want me to carry you out over my shoulder?\"","Hearing this, Qiao Lanshu was so frightened that she quickly got out of the car.","How could she dare let Qin Yuanzheng carry her?","There were people coming and going in the military family compound from time to time, and children running around. How bad would it look if someone saw them?","Seeing her get out, Qin Yuanzheng opened the back seat and took out a coil of hemp rope.","Qiao Lanshu's eyes widened in fright. She stuttered, \"Brother... Brother Zheng, what are you doing with that?\"","Qin Yuanzheng held the coil of rope in his hand and slammed the car door shut with a bang. He looked at Qiao Lanshu's nervous little face and said, \"Now you know to be afraid? It's too late. I'm going to interrogate you properly later.\"","Qiao Lanshu: \"...\"","No way, was he treating her like an enemy to exact revenge?","Was he going to tie her up and beat her like interrogating a prisoner? Was that really necessary?","Qiao Lanshu suspected that Qin Yuanzheng was pretending to be angry just to punish her on purpose.","She really had that feeling!","After all, this man Qin Yuanzheng usually looked perfectly respectable, but once he got into bed, he completely changed into a different person.","He had a high demand in that area, which Qiao Lanshu could understand. After all, he was full of energy.","A vigorous and robust military officer needed to vent his energy somehow.","However, Qiao Lanshu suspected he also had some special hobbies!","After returning home, Qin Yuanzheng placed the hemp rope on the utility shelf. Qiao Lanshu had been staring at it the whole time, and only breathed a sigh of relief when she saw he didn't intend to use it.","However, not long after, she saw Qin Yuanzheng come out holding a roll of cloth strips...","Qiao Lanshu: \"...\"","Qiao Lanshu got a spanking.","Qin Yuanzheng seemed to be lecturing a child, sternly asking her if she knew she was wrong and if she dared to be so reckless in the future.","Qiao Lanshu kept blushing and admitting her mistake, saying she would absolutely never make this kind of mistake again, even though she still didn't think she did anything wrong today.","But she still had to admit it verbally! After all, Qin Yuanzheng just wanted her to admit her mistake. Even if she didn't agree in her heart, she had to make it sound good on the surface.","But even though she admitted her mistake, Qin Yuanzheng wasn't satisfied.","...","In short, Qiao Lanshu received a spanking.","He didn't let her go until Qiao Lanshu was crying.","It wasn't until past ten o'clock at night that he went to the kitchen to cook porridge. He made millet porridge for Qiao Lanshu, wanting her to drink a bowl before going to sleep.","Qiao Lanshu was wrapped in the quilt, feeling angry. She just glanced at him, then turned away and said in a hoarse voice, \"I'm not eating.\"","Qin Yuanzheng now knew exactly how to handle her.","He sat on the edge of the bed and said slowly, \"If you don't eat, should I feed you myself?\"","Saying that, he brought the porridge to his lips and took a sip himself.","Qiao Lanshu: \"!!!\"","Qiao Lanshu quickly rolled over and said, \"Ah, I'll eat it, okay.\"","Now she wasn't just afraid of Qin Yuanzheng's hands; she was also afraid of his mouth.","She took the porridge bowl and, under Qin Yuanzheng's staring gaze, blushed and said, \"Brother Zheng, isn't it time you shaved your beard?\"","It prickled her terribly.","Qin Yuanzheng said meaningfully, \"What if you're disobedient? Then I won't shave it.\"","Qiao Lanshu: \"...\"","Having finished bullying her, Qin Yuanzheng now asked intimately, \"Are you uncomfortable? Do you want to take a bath?\"","As he spoke, he came over to hug Qiao Lanshu again, acting as if he had skin hunger. He couldn't keep his hands off his little wife; they couldn't be apart for even a few minutes without him needing to hold her.","Even while she drank porridge, he insisted on holding his wife on his lap, like conjoined twins.","Qiao Lanshu was used to it. She happened to be tired right now, so she leaned against Qin Yuanzheng's chest and slowly finished drinking the porridge.","After she finished the porridge, Qin Yuanzheng took the bowl to the kitchen to wash it, then went to heat some water, intending to take Qiao Lanshu for a bath shortly.","However, when he came back, he found that his wife had already fallen asleep on the bed.","It seemed today's amount of exercise had exceeded the limit; his precious wife was truly exhausted.","Qin Yuanzheng sat on the edge of the bed, looking at the sleeping Qiao Lanshu, and whispered, \"Wifey, are you asleep? Not taking a bath?\"","He leaned in close to Qiao Lanshu and deliberately teased her, \"If you don't answer me, I'm going to prick you with my stubble.\"","Qiao Lanshu was most afraid of him pricking her with his stubble. If she had heard him say that, she would definitely have jumped up in fright.","But there was no reaction at all, meaning she was truly asleep.","Qin Yuanzheng couldn't help but smile. He tucked the corners of the quilt around her and gently rubbed her stomach.","He thought to himself that it didn't really matter if she didn't wash up, since they didn't have to worry about getting pregnant anyway.","His wife was still too young."]},{"number":91,"title":"Chapter 91: I gave you a massage last night.","paragraphs":["Qiao Lanshu slept soundly until dawn. When she woke up the next day, she saw red marks on her wrists...","Although Commander Qin was very measured and knew how to use the cloth strips properly.","But her skin... her arms were indeed prone to leaving marks...","Qin Yuanzheng had already prepared breakfast. He was happy last night and was now full of energy. The look in his eyes as he gazed at Qiao Lanshu was filled with deep affection.","He was wearing military trousers and boots on his lower half, but his upper body was bare, having just wiped himself down with a towel.","He sat on the edge of the kang and pulled the newly awakened, still-groggy Qiao Lanshu into his arms. His broad hands grasped her wrists, rubbing them gently as he asked in a low voice, Do your wrists hurt? I massaged you last night, does it feel any better?","Qiao Lanshu was speechless.","No wonder she dreamed of a tiger cub jumping all over her while she was sleeping last night.","It jumped on her back, then on her stomach, occasionally taking a few bites at her arms.","She had been terribly annoyed at the time and reached out to toss the tiger cub away, but a moment later, the cub pounced on her again.","Qiao Lanshu yawned, feeling that her body was indeed not as sore anymore, so she said, My body doesn't feel sore now.","Qin Yuanzheng kissed the palm of her hand and said, Then when I come back tonight, I'll massage you again.","As he spoke, he skillfully and naturally picked up Qiao Lanshu's clothes and pulled them over her head.","He even considerately helped pull her hair out from under the collar.","He looked at Qiao Lanshu's shiny, smooth hair with absolute adoration. I wrote a letter earlier asking my comrade to send me some women's hair oil from Shanghai. I wonder if it has arrived yet. I'll go check today.","When Qiao Lanshu was in Yangcheng, she rarely ever used hair oil.","Because the air there was humid and her hair was naturally smooth, it was fine without hair oil.","However, the north was dry, causing her hair to become frizzy. After coming here, she braided her hair every day to prevent it from getting messy and full of static.","Hearing Qin Yuanzheng say this, she immediately leaned over happily, kissed him on the cheek, and smiled, Thank you, Brother Zheng. You really are my good husband.","Qin Yuanzheng paused.","Qin Yuanzheng almost stood at attention for her right then and there.","His Adam's apple bobbed as he said, We're about to go to work, don't tease me.","Qiao Lanshu was teasing him on purpose at this exact moment.","Who asked him to bully her so much last night?","Qiao Lanshu finished getting dressed, combed her hair, and braided it into two thick, black, and shiny braids before getting off the kang.","Then, she saw the black cloth strips lying on the table by the edge of the kang.","Her heart immediately skipped a beat.","Blushing, she asked, Brother Zheng, why haven't you thrown this away yet?","The cloth strip was soft, made of some kind of stretchy material.","She had no idea where Qin Yuanzheng got it from or what its original purpose was.","Anyway, all the suffering she endured yesterday... was all because of...","Qin Yuanzheng had clearly promised her he would throw this thing away, so why was he still keeping it?","Seeing her embarrassed and indignant expression, Qin Yuanzheng hurriedly said, I'll go dispose of it right now.","Saying that, he rolled the thing into a ball and stuffed it into his own bag.","Qiao Lanshu was speechless.","Qiao Lanshu didn't know what to say.","She only said, Anyway, you are not allowed to bring this kind of thing home ever again, or I'll get angry.","Qin Yuanzheng smiled and nodded, but didn't outright agree. Instead, he leaned in, hugged her, and asked, You didn't feel that uncomfortable, I thought you liked it?","Qiao Lanshu's face instantly turned red, and she said, I didn't like it anyway, you're not allowed to use it again.","Qin Yuanzheng fell silent.","Qin Yuanzheng said with some regret, Really no more? You almost...","Qiao Lanshu quickly covered his mouth. Alright, stop talking. Aren't we going to eat breakfast?","Qin Yuanzheng looked at her with a smile. Alright, I won't say it.","Qiao Lanshu was truly afraid of Qin Yuanzheng's mouth. Not only was what he said startling, but what he did with it was quite startling too.","Qin Yuanzheng brought the porridge over, sat opposite Qiao Lanshu, and said in all seriousness, I remember we still have some cloth ration coupons at home, right? I'll find some time to go to the supply and marketing cooperative to see if they have any waterproof cloth and buy a few feet of it...","Qiao Lanshu glared at him. Say one more word! Say one more word and I won't eat.","Qin Yuanzheng immediately made a zipping motion over his lips and buried his head to gulp down his porridge.","After breakfast, the couple went to work.","Qiao Lanshu sat in the small room next to the warehouse, occasionally pounding her lower back with her fist.","At this time, Deng Weijun and Wang Xue came over together to look for her.","As soon as Wang Xue arrived, she leaned against the window and said to Qiao Lanshu, Xiao Qiao, this younger brother of yours is not bad, he even comes over every day to fetch water for you?","Qiao Lanshu glanced at Deng Weijun. Deng Weijun skillfully picked up Qiao Lanshu's thermos and said to Wang Xue, What do you know? My sister-in-law is my lifesaver! My sister said I should work like a horse for my sister-in-law and let her order me around, this is what I ought to do.","Qiao Lanshu quickly said, Cousin-in-law is exaggerating. Actually, it's not necessary, I can fetch water myself. If you're busy with work, you don't need to come over. It makes me feel bad.","Deng Weijun's job was as a boiler worker. Although the work wasn't considered very busy, it was physically tying. He had to stay there to watch the boiler, add coal, check the temperature, and so on. He had to keep an eye on it at all times and couldn't leave easily.","Deng Weijun only had time to run over and fetch water for Qiao Lanshu when he first arrived in the morning. Normally, unless he was off work, he didn't dare run around.","He still cherished this job very much, terrified of making a mistake and being scolded by his brother-in-law, who was the factory director.","Deng Weijun said, Sister-in-law, don't be so polite with me. It's just fetching water, it doesn't take me much effort. Besides, I have to fetch water for myself anyway, so it's just doing it in passing.","Saying that, he pulled a lunchbox out of his pocket, placed it on Qiao Lanshu's desk, and said, Sister-in-law, this is the oil tea my sister roasted herself. She specifically told me to bring some for you to try. Please don't mind that it's just a little.","With that, he put the lunchbox down and trotted off with the thermos.","Wang Xue clicked her tongue and shook her head, lowering her voice to say, This Deng Weijun... if we didn't all know that you really saved his life, people would think he was trying to poach Regiment Commander Qin's wife.","Hearing this, Qiao Lanshu immediately laughed and said, An ordinary person wouldn't dare try to poach Regiment Commander Qin's wife, would they?","Although she had the rose-tinted glasses of a lover and thought everything about Qin Yuanzheng was great.","She was also well aware of the awe and fear outsiders had for Qin Yuanzheng.","She opened the door, pulled Wang Xue into the small room, and asked in a low voice, Sister, how is the matter between your younger sister and that Liu Jianguo being handled?"]},{"number":92,"title":"Chapter 92: Find a Reliable Man","paragraphs":["Wang Xue came to look for Qiao Lanshu early this morning to thank her and to casually ask if she had been criticized by Regiment Commander Qin after going back.","After all, back at the train station that day, Regiment Commander Qin's expression was extremely ugly.","Wang Xue rarely had the chance to meet officers like Qin Yuanzheng before.","However, here in Longcheng, because of the forestry centers and mining areas, as well as the planned highway construction, there were quite a few stationed troops, so it was common to see People's Liberation Army soldiers from a distance.","Wang Xue had a very good impression of these PLA soldiers because they were all strong, young men who were brave, ready to stand up for justice, and always willing to help others. They were all great guys.","But when they saw Qin Yuanzheng yesterday, Wang Xue and her sister Wang Haitang were nearly scared to death by him.","That Liu Jianguo was kicked by Qin Yuanzheng and ended up lying in the hospital that very day.","However, the doctor said it was nothing serious, so the police took Liu Jianguo away again.","Wang Xue pulled a large, bright red apple from the pocket of her padded cotton jacket. She placed it on Qiao Lanshu's desk and said, \"Xiao Qiao, thank you so much for going with me yesterday. I don't have anything fancy to offer, but my maiden family sent me a few apples a couple of days ago. I brought one for you today. It's really sweet, I'm sure you'll love it.\"","In these times, to ensure enough arable land for grain, fruit was rarely cultivated.","The weather in the north was cold, making it easy to grow apples, pears, persimmons, and hawthorns. They would grow easily just by planting a sapling and bore plenty of fruit. As long as they got enough sunshine, the fruits would grow large and red, with exceptionally sweet juice.","Many people couldn't bear to cut down their fruit trees, so they would plant one or two apple or hawthorn trees on their private plots in the village, just to give the children a sweet treat.","Qiao Lanshu knew this apple was hard to come by, so she felt too embarrassed to accept it.","She pushed the apple back and said to Wang Xue, \"Sister, don't be so polite with me. When I first arrived, you took good care of me. Now that you're in trouble, of course I should help you. Besides, I didn't actually do much to help yesterday.\"","In that situation yesterday, the person who truly helped Wang Xue was Qin Yuanzheng. If he hadn't come over and sent Liu Jianguo flying with a single kick, Qiao Lanshu and Wang Xue might not have been able to subdue Liu Jianguo at all.","Qiao Lanshu stuffed the apple back into Wang Xue's pocket, telling her, \"You should take this apple back for the kids to eat. They are growing, and it's not easy for them to get apples.\"","Wang Xue clicked her tongue and shoved the apple straight into Qiao Lanshu's pocket. \"You're right, we shouldn't be so polite with each other. Just take it when I tell you to. Don't worry, I still have more at home. If I only had one left, I wouldn't bear to part with it either.\"","Wang Xue had a straightforward and frank personality, and Qiao Lanshu liked dealing with people like her.","But she still felt bad accepting it. She quickly took the apple out again to stuff it into Wang Xue's pocket. \"Sister, really, there's no need. Take it back for the kids. I feel bad taking it.\"","Wang Xue pretended to be angry and said, \"Xiao Qiao, don't treat me like a stranger. It's just an apple. If you don't accept it, I won't dare ask you for help again!\"","Unable to win the argument against Wang Xue, Qiao Lanshu stopped declining and accepted the apple, placing it in her padded jacket pocket.","Seeing her accept it, Wang Xue said with satisfaction, \"That's more like it. We're close, after all. Don't be so polite in the future.\"","As she spoke, she leaned closer to Qiao Lanshu. The two were right next to each other as she lowered her voice to ask, \"By the way, Xiao Qiao, I saw that Regiment Commander Qin looked quite angry yesterday. Did he criticize you when you got back? Did he mistreat you?\"","Wang Xue was thinking that Qiao Lanshu was young, inexperienced, and had a soft temperament, making her look easy to bully.","If Regiment Commander Qin got fierce, Comrade Xiao Qiao might not be able to handle it and would likely suffer a bit.","Hearing this, Qiao Lanshu suddenly didn't know what to say.","He hadn't criticized her, but he had punished her.","Even now, she still felt a dull ache in certain places.","She unconsciously blushed, a rosy tint appearing on her fair face. Playing with her braids, she whispered, \"Regiment Commander Qin... he treats me very well. He wouldn't criticize me.\"","He just liked to punish her and bully her.","He wouldn't let her go even when she was stuffed full.","Thinking of this, Qiao Lanshu's face grew even redder, and she even began to feel a phantom ache in her lower back.","Wang Xue was an experienced woman. Seeing Qiao Lanshu's little expression, she instantly knew what was going on.","She gave a suggestive smile and teased, \"Oh my, you really are newlyweds, so affectionate! Look at your face. Whenever Regiment Commander Qin is mentioned, it turns even redder than that apple from just now.\"","Qiao Lanshu: \"...\"","Wang Xue even gossiped, asking her, \"I used to hear people say that Regiment Commander Qin wasn't capable in that department. But from what I see, he seems quite capable. It looks like rumors are just rumors, and they're all lies, right?\"","Qiao Lanshu felt embarrassed. She lowered her head and said, \"Sister, please stop asking...\"","How was she supposed to answer that?","Seeing her bashful appearance, Wang Xue covered her mouth and laughed. Newlywed girls just couldn't take a tease; a casual remark was enough to make her blush. Look how thin-skinned she was.","She smiled and said, \"Alright, alright, I won't say any more, and I won't tease you. But speaking of which, that Liu Jianguo has already been released from the police station.\"","At this point, Wang Xue's expression turned ugly. She muttered, \"That bastard. He better not let me catch sight of him again.\"","Qiao Lanshu also looked surprised and asked, \"What happened? He has a wife and child in the countryside, yet he's dating someone in the city. Isn't that considered a crime?\"","Wang Xue had come to chat with Qiao Lanshu precisely because she had no one else to talk to about this.","She was just that kind of person—she couldn't hold things in and always needed someone to vent to.","With a dark face, she said angrily, \"Xiao Qiao, you definitely can't imagine how disgusting those men can be. That Liu Jianguo and his wife in the countryside never even got a marriage certificate! The police specifically looked into it—Liu Jianguo has no marriage registration. He is still single! The woman and child in the countryside are registered under his older brother's name. On paper, they are his sister-in-law and nephew.\"","Hearing this, Qiao Lanshu said hesitantly, \"Could it be that we misunderstood? Maybe that really is his sister-in-law? What if Liu Jianguo actually has never been married?\"","Wang Xue shook her head and said, \"Who knows? We have no way of investigating these things! If they don't want us to know, where can we even go to ask? The people in the village all stick together. Even the police couldn't get anything out of them when they asked, let alone us.\"","\"But that Liu Jianguo's character is truly terrible. When he was fighting with me yesterday, he actually went and kicked Wang Haitang. Didn't he say he liked Wang Haitang? And he still kicked her! If they get married in the future, wouldn't his wife be beaten to death by him? It's really disgusting. If a man like him were in my family, he would be slapped in the face.\"","Wang Xue felt extremely frustrated and angry.","She originally thought Liu Jianguo would be arrested for inappropriate relations between men and women.","After that, Wang Haitang wouldn't have to live in fear anymore.","But as a result of the investigation, Liu Jianguo was released without charge.","Because neither side wanted to press charges regarding their fight that day, and because it was considered a quarrel between a couple, it was treated as a domestic dispute. The police officers just criticized Wang Xue and Liu Jianguo a bit before letting them go back to work.","However, Wang Xue still felt uneasy about it.","She said fiercely, \"After this incident, he probably won't dare to harass my sister anymore. Otherwise, I'll go over there with a kitchen knife.\"","Qiao Lanshu: \"...\"","Qiao Lanshu sighed. It really wasn't easy being a woman. It was fine if you could find a good man.","But if you ended up with a bad man, your whole life would truly be ruined.","Qiao Lanshu stayed silent for a moment before suddenly saying, \"Sister, why don't you quickly introduce a reliable man to Haitang and have her get married soon? She works at the ticket window at the train station and sees too many people every day. Even without Liu Jianguo, there might be other men coming to harass her.\"","Once she's married, not only will she have a man to escort her to and from work and protect her, but she will also be a married woman. If any man dares to harass a married woman, that's the crime of hooliganism.","When that time comes, a man won't be able to just casually brush it off by claiming they were on a blind date or dating.","Hearing this, Wang Xue immediately sighed and said with a bitter face, \"I want to, too, but I just can't find a suitable man. That Young Company Commander Yang from before was quite good, but he didn't fancy our Haitang. If our Haitang were as pretty as you, I wouldn't have to worry at all.\"","Wang Haitang's appearance was rather ordinary, and her personality was too introverted. Even if she were set up on a blind date with a male colleague, she wouldn't even dare to look up at him. She wouldn't say more than a few words the whole day. How could she possibly date like that?","Liu Jianguo had taken advantage of her personality, knowing that Wang Haitang couldn't make a scene at all, which was why he pestered her relentlessly.","Otherwise, why didn't he go and harass someone else?","Wang Xue started to worry just thinking about this.","She said, \"Haitang has a formal job, too, so I wanted to find her a partner who also has a formal job. I asked around before but couldn't find anyone suitable, and I was just worrying about it. If worse comes to worst, I'll have her take a leave of absence for now. Anyway, the trains have been suspended recently, and there aren't many people buying tickets. We'll wait a few days and see.\"","Qiao Lanshu then asked, \"Did Haitang go back to work today?\"","Wang Xue: \"She did. After all, she took half a day off yesterday because of this incident, so she has to go back to work today. As for whether she should ask for leave later, I'll have to go back and ask her.\"","Actually, as long as Liu Jianguo didn't go harass her anymore, she generally wouldn't need to take time off. After all, taking leave meant having money deducted; if she didn't work, she wouldn't get paid.","At this moment, Deng Weijun, who had gone to fetch water for Qiao Lanshu, returned.","Deng Weijun was carrying a thermos in each hand.","One was his own, and the other was Qiao Lanshu's.","He placed Qiao Lanshu's thermos on the windowsill and said with a smile, \"Sister-in-law, I'm going to work now. Call me if you need anything.\"","Saying that, Deng Weijun also smiled at Wang Xue, turned around, and strode away.","Wang Xue: \"...\"","Wang Xue stared at Deng Weijun's back and said thoughtfully, \"Hiss, this Deng Weijun... although he's a bit foolish, he doesn't look bad at all.\"","Deng Weijun's brother-in-law was the director of the food factory, and his sister was a female worker at the textile factory.","Although his brother-in-law's family had quite good conditions, Deng Weijun's own family was from the countryside and held rural household registrations.","His household registration issue was actually resolved with the help of his brother-in-law, Yang Wenyan.","But at least he now had an urban household registration and a proper job. These conditions were already very good.","After all, in this day and age, as long as you had a formal job, it meant you could be allocated housing.","After getting married, they wouldn't have to worry about food, clothing, or housing. They could live a stable life and raise children.","Seeing Wang Xue staring thoughtfully at Deng Weijun, how could Qiao Lanshu not know what she was thinking?","Deng Weijun and Wang Xue had known each other for a long time. They had always been colleagues at the food factory, but they didn't work in the same workshop and rarely saw each other. It was only after Qiao Lanshu arrived that Wang Xue started exchanging a few words with Deng Weijun.","They hadn't really chatted much before.","It wasn't until Deng Weijun was completely out of sight that Wang Xue sneakily leaned over and asked in a low voice, \"Xiao Qiao, what do you think of Deng Weijun?\"","Qiao Lanshu: \"...\"","Qiao Lanshu thought about it seriously and said to Wang Xue, \"I think Comrade Weijun, although a bit careless, doesn't have a bad character. He used to be a bit playful and would often go out to play cards with friends, but...\"","She paused and lowered her voice, \"After the Zheng Daliu incident, he has settled down a lot. He hasn't gone out to play with colleagues recently. Every day after work, he just goes back to his dorm to stay. I think he's alright, but I just don't know what Haitang thinks and whether she would take a fancy to him.\"","Wang Xue clicked her tongue and said, \"That Liu Jianguo is a few years older than Deng Weijun, and he doesn't even look as good as him! Actually, as for this kid Weijun, I've known him for two or three years now. I know his character well. He has no bad intentions and is a solid, hardworking person. However, his sister keeps a very strict eye on him, and since she's a factory director's family member, she might not necessarily look favorably upon our Haitang. How about this, Xiao Qiao, could you go ask for me?\"","Wang Xue said this and quickly added, \"If this works out, how about I give you a matchmaker's red envelope?\"","The more Wang Xue spoke, the more she felt that Deng Weijun was a pretty good guy.","Her Wang Haitang was just cowardly by nature, lacked her own opinions, and had even less drive.","If she got together with Deng Weijun in the future, having a formidable sister and brother-in-law to help out and manage them a bit would actually be a good thing.","Although some people don't want to be controlled by their mother-in-law or sister-in-law, Wang Haitang was different!","She couldn't do without someone looking after her; otherwise, she would easily get bullied.","Thinking this way, Wang Xue slapped her thigh and said to Qiao Lanshu, \"Xiao Qiao, can you help me ask your cousin-in-law? Let's just have the two young people meet. If they are suitable, they can date; if not, we'll drop it. No matter what, let's create an opportunity for them first, what do you say?\"","Wang Xue suggested asking the cousin-in-law directly because she knew Deng Weijun listened to his sister.","Qiao Lanshu found it a bit amusing. She nodded and said, \"Alright, after I get off work, I'll go ask for you.\""]},{"number":93,"title":"Chapter 93: Here He Comes Again","paragraphs":["Wang Xue felt that Deng Weijun was a pretty good guy.","Qiao Lanshu agreed with this assessment, so she started making plans. She intended to discuss it with Qin Yuanzheng after work and find time to visit her cousin's house together. While there, she could ask her cousin-in-law, Deng Xiaozhen, about the situation to see if they should set up a blind date for Deng Weijun and Wang Haitang.","It was the dead of winter; the days were short, and night fell exceptionally quickly.","As it neared the end of the workday, fine snowflakes began to drift down from the sky.","Seeing this, Qiao Lanshu opened the window and reached out. After catching a few beautiful snowflakes, she blew some hot air onto her hands and hurried to finish processing the warehouse inventory receipts she was working on.","She then stepped outside and carefully double-checked that the warehouse door was securely locked.","Once she confirmed everything was in order, she swiftly slipped into her thick military-green padded jacket, pulled on a black woolen beanie, and snugly wrapped the red scarf Qin Yuanzheng had specially bought for her around her neck. She was ready to head home.","Today, Qin Yuanzheng was also, quite rarely, able to finish work on time.","He couldn't wait to pick up his cute, charming little wife and head home together!","The women's hair oil he had asked a comrade in Shanghai to buy for him had finally arrived. His friend had sent him five bottles in total, all osmanthus-scented. He tucked the five bottles into his overcoat pocket.","He thought to himself about his little wife's thick, dark hair. If she applied this hair oil, it would definitely be shiny, smooth, and incredibly beautiful.","At night, when he was in bed with his little wife, he really loved playing with her hair.","Of course, his wife was so sweet and beautiful, with fair skin and a great figure.","Every part of her was his absolute favorite.","He didn't just like playing with her hair; he loved exploring other places, too.","...","At that thought, Qin Yuanzheng suddenly realized that besides the hair oil, he should also buy some body lotion for his little wife.","Winters in the north were too dry, and his wife hadn't yet adapted to the arid climate.","She often complained about her skin being dry.","Although she still felt as smooth as her hair, if she applied some lotion...","Thinking of this, Qin Yuanzheng's heart began to burn with passion again.","Ah, having a wife was truly a wonderful thing.","He was finally experiencing the perks of marriage.","With his mind full of thoughts about his wife in bed, he walked outside.","Just then, Company Commander Xiao Yang returned from the mining area. As soon as he saw Qin Yuanzheng, he asked, \"Commander, it's snowing today. Do you need me to go pick up my sister-in-law?\"","Qin Yuanzheng glanced at Xiao Yang.","Xiao Yang was young, tall, and looked quite handsome in his military uniform. Young girls probably really liked his type.","Age-wise, Xiao Yang and Qiao Lanshu were much closer. When they were together, they probably had more in common to talk about, right?","If he hadn't been genuinely swamped with work before, Qin Yuanzheng would never have let Xiao Yang pick up his wife.","He pondered to himself that next time, he should just assign a guard to pick up his wife. Xiao Yang needed to spend less time hovering around her.","What if one day his wife got tired of him and ran off with Xiao Yang?","Although Qin Yuanzheng had these thoughts, his face remained completely expressionless.","He said, \"No need. I'll pick her up today.\"","Xiao Yang was a bit surprised. The Commander had been so busy lately; how could he actually finish work on time?","He nodded. \"Understood, Commander.\"","As he spoke, he suddenly stopped in his tracks. After hesitating for a brief moment, he quickly caught up with Qin Yuanzheng, leaned in close, and whispered, \"Oh, right, Commander, I almost forgot to tell you something important. A few days ago when I went to pick up my sister-in-law, I accidentally noticed a sneaky man who seemed to be tailing her.","Later, feeling that something wasn't right, I specifically went to investigate. I found out that the guy is actually a temporary worker at the supply and marketing cooperative! He just started working here in Longcheng over the last two months, and his permanent residency is still registered in a nearby village.\"","Hearing this, Qin Yuanzheng stopped dead in his tracks.","His previously relaxed expression instantly grew solemn.","Frowning deeply, he asked in a low, serious tone, \"Are you certain that guy was following Xiao Qiao?\"","Xiao Yang nodded in response. \"I'm about eighty or ninety percent sure!\"","Actually, after investigating for a while, Xiao Yang had already gathered a pretty good understanding of this man, Chu Liangjun. However, since he hadn't yet gone to the village for an on-site investigation, the information he currently had was limited to Chu Liangjun's workplace in the city, his residential address, and his working relationships with his colleagues.","Xiao Yang then continued his report to Qin Yuanzheng, \"Also, Commander, this Chu Liangjun has a bit of a background. I heard he's a distant relative of the director of the supply and marketing cooperative. He only got the job there because of the director's recommendation and backing. Fortunately, in the few months he's been here in Longcheng, he's behaved himself and hasn't caused any major trouble so far.\"","That was exactly why Xiao Yang was so puzzled.","Chu Liangjun and Qiao Lanshu were clearly two people whose paths should never cross.","Why would Chu Liangjun suddenly start tailing Qiao Lanshu?","Could there be something else going on that they didn't know about?","Qin Yuanzheng's face darkened. When it came to his wife, it was hard for him to maintain a calm expression.","He said in a deep voice, \"Arrange some men to keep a close eye on this Chu Liangjun. Let's see exactly what he's up to!\"","Xiao Yang nodded immediately. \"Understood, Commander. I'll make the arrangements right away.\"","Qin Yuanzheng walked to the door and looked out at the increasingly heavy snowfall. He thought to himself that it must be because his little wife was just too beautiful, making her a magnet for all sorts of unsavory characters.","It seemed he needed to keep a closer eye on things.","He was already getting older, and having married such a young, beautiful wife, he couldn't help but feel a bit anxious.","He was afraid he wouldn't be able to hold onto her.","With these thoughts in mind, Qin Yuanzheng dug into his pocket, pulled out a ten-yuan note, and drove to the supply and marketing cooperative. He browsed through both floors from top to bottom, buying a pound of raisins, half a pound of stone-baked biscuits, and a jar of honey.","He didn't really know the best way to dote on his little wife, but buying her food was definitely a safe bet.","Young girls all loved sweet things.","Oh, right. He had heard that Shanghai had a great variety of candies, like the White Rabbit creamy candies that were supposedly delicious. The cooperatives here didn't sell them, and he wasn't sure if they would have any in stock for the New Year. If not, he would just ask his comrades to mail some over.","Unfortunately, he didn't have any comrades stationed in Yangcheng; otherwise, buying things would be even more convenient.","Qin Yuanzheng placed his purchases on the back seat of his car. Just as he was about to leave, he paused in silence for a moment, got back out of the car, and walked inside the cooperative once more.","He approached the fabric counter. Seeing a military officer approach, the sales clerk's expression immediately grew more serious.","The clerk hurriedly asked, \"Chief, what kind of fabric would you like to buy? Or are you looking for yarn and cotton?\"","Qin Yuanzheng was dressed in his military overcoat and cap. His face was stern, and his gaze was unwavering.","Standing upright at the counter with an aura of righteousness, he asked in a deep voice, \"Do you sell waterproof fabric here?\"","The saleswoman looked at his serious and stern face, thinking that this military officer was going to use the waterproof fabric for some great patriotic deed.","She immediately turned serious as well, nodding and saying, \"Chief, we don't have waterproof cloth, but there is a type of leather made of sheepskin with a flannel backing that is waterproof. Would you like to take a look and see if it works?\"","Saying so, she brought out a thick fabric catalog, opened it to a certain page, and pointed to a piece of leather for Qin Yuanzheng to see.","Qin Yuanzheng reached out to touch it. The surface was sheepskin, smooth and shiny, just a bit cool to the touch. The back was lined with fine flannel, feeling soft and warm, and quite comfortable.","Qin Yuanzheng immediately felt this leather was a good choice.","In winter, they could use the fleece side, and in summer, they could use the smooth leather side.","It was clearly waterproof. When sleeping normally, it could be laid directly over the mattress.","It wouldn't require much organizing either.","In the future, when he and his little wife were on the kang together, with this cloth, he wouldn't have to worry so much.","To be honest, before this, he had been restraining himself.","He hadn't unleashed his full strength.","It was all to consider Qiao Lanshu's feelings.","Every time he saw she was about to lose control, he had to hold back a bit.","Otherwise, if the mattress and quilt got wet, his wife would definitely get mad at him.","At this thought, Qin Yuanzheng coughed. He was very satisfied with this leather, even feeling a faint sense of impatience.","He admitted his hobby was a bit eccentric; he just liked to bully his little wife and watch her gush.","Qin Yuanzheng coughed twice and said with a straight face, \"This will do. Two point four meters long and two meters wide. Please cut it to this size for me.\"","The saleswoman looked a bit troubled. \"I'm sorry, Chief, we don't have it that wide. How about I cut two pieces that are one point two meters wide and two point four meters long, and you can find someone to sew them together?\"","Qin Yuanzheng fell silent for a moment. Although not entirely satisfied, there was nothing else he could do.","After all, his kang was indeed quite large. Finding the exact right size wasn't that easy.","In the end, carrying two rolls of waterproof sheepskin fabric, he got into his car and drove to the food factory to pick up his little wife.","...","Qiao Lanshu walked out of the factory with the other food factory workers.","She didn't see Qin Yuanzheng's car at the gate, nor did she see Xiao Yang or any other military comrades.","She knew the person coming to pick her up hadn't arrived yet.","She went to wait at the door of the guardhouse, occasionally looking out toward the main gate.","Just then, Wang Xue also came out of the factory. Seeing her, Wang Xue stopped to talk. \"Xiao Qiao, why are you standing here? Are you waiting for your family to pick you up?\"","Qiao Lanshu had her face wrapped up tightly, revealing only a pair of big, bright black eyes. She smiled and nodded. \"Yes, he told me to wait for him in the guardhouse. He was probably delayed by something, but he should be here soon.\"","Because of the matter with Chu Liangjun, Qiao Lanshu didn't dare to be alone. As long as no one was accompanying her, she didn't dare to walk home by herself.","Wang Xue was going to pick up Wang Haitang from work today. After all, she was also afraid that Liu Jianguo would go and pester Wang Haitang.","So she wasn't going to the supply and marketing cooperative to buy groceries, which naturally meant she wasn't going the same way as Qiao Lanshu.","Wang Xue walked up to Qiao Lanshu and chatted with her for a bit. \"Then you wait here for a while. I have to go pick up my sister. I don't know how her shift went today. After that incident with Liu Jianguo, people at the train station have been gossiping about her. It's such bad luck for things to turn out this way. She even said she wants to quit. How could I let her quit over this? If anyone is going to lose their job, it should be Liu Jianguo.\"","Qiao Lanshu quickly said, \"Sister, a person like Liu Jianguo might not let it go so easily. Hurry and go pick up Haitang. The snow is getting heavier, so be careful on the road.\"","Wang Xue agreed as she briskly walked away.","The uncle in the guardhouse saw Qiao Lanshu standing there, stamping her feet from the cold, and opened the door. He said, \"Little girl, come inside and warm up. It must be cold out there, right?\"","The guardhouse at the gate was different from the inside of the food factory; there was no central heating here.","But because the gatekeeper uncle had to work night shifts here, the kang in the inner room was heated.","The charcoal fire in the stove made both the inner and outer rooms toasty warm.","Qiao Lanshu walked in and closed the door.","She stood near the doorway, and feeling that her feet were no longer as numb, she smiled and said, \"Thank you, Uncle.\"","As she spoke, she took a frozen pear out of her pocket. Deng Weijun had given it to her earlier; she had two of them.","She took one out, placed it on the table, and said, \"Uncle, try this frozen pear. They say it's very sweet.\"","The uncle knew Qiao Lanshu and knew she was a military officer's family member, which was why he took special care of her.","He didn't expect her to be so thoughtful and generous enough to give him a frozen pear.","When the uncle looked at Qiao Lanshu now, his smile was completely genuine.","He took the frozen pear, tapped it on the table, and smiled, \"It's frozen nicely, all dark and shiny. You have to put this on the heater. Wait until it thaws, and then suck the juice out. It's wonderfully sweet, even better than soda.\"","With that, he unceremoniously took the frozen pear and placed it on the stove.","Qiao Lanshu smiled and said, \"I thought you were supposed to just hold it and bite into it.\"","Uncle: \"...\"","Uncle: \"Do you think you have teeth of steel? It's like a block of ice, you can't bite into it easily.\"","Saying so, he brought over a small stool for Qiao Lanshu. \"Have a seat. It's tiring to stand. Sit here, so you don't block the door. People will be coming in to pick up their mail in a bit.\"","There was a blackboard hanging by the door of the guardhouse. Whenever someone's letters or packages arrived, the uncle would write their name on it.","When people got off work and saw their names, they would come in to get them.","Qiao Lanshu sat in the corner and waited.","The uncle stood by the window, looking out toward the main gate, and frowned. \"Why is that guy here again? How does he have so much free time every day?\"","Curious, Qiao Lanshu stood up, looked outside as well, and asked, \"Uncle, who are you talking about?\"","As she spoke, she saw Chu Liangjun standing by the wall outside the food factory's main gate.","The uncle pointed with his chin and said, \"That one, the guy standing over there in the gray padded jacket. He's been here before, saying he was looking for someone. Now he's back today. I remember he's an employee at the supply and marketing cooperative. I think he came to pick up goods before.\"","Qiao Lanshu: \"...\"","Qiao Lanshu silently sat back down on the small stool.","Why was Chu Liangjun here again?","Even coming in the snow. Fortunately, Qiao Lanshu hadn't gone outside."]},{"number":94,"title":"Chapter 94: Want to Pursue Her","paragraphs":["After Chu Liangjun found out that Qiao Lanshu was a woman who despised the poor and loved the rich, he actually considered whether he should just give up on her altogether.","At first glance, it was obvious that this woman came from a good family background.","She was beautiful, young, had a formal job, and lived in the military compound. When she got off work, she even had soldiers escorting her. She probably wouldn't have to worry about finding a good family to marry into.","But Chu Liangjun had high standards. He looked down on the women who actually took a fancy to him.","Furthermore, now that he had met a woman like Qiao Lanshu, he couldn't even look at anyone else.","So, after returning, he pondered whether he should borrow some money from his uncle first. After all, his uncle, Chu Haiming, was the director of the supply and marketing cooperative. He was well-off and surely had a lot of money.","However, how to bring it up with his uncle was indeed a problem.","After going back, Chu Liangjun tossed and turned until the middle of the night, his mind completely filled with Qiao Lanshu.","Perhaps he had thought about her too much during the day, because after finally falling asleep in the middle of the night, he suddenly dreamt of Qiao Lanshu.","The Qiao Lanshu in his dream wasn't like the one he had seen at the food factory during the day—aloof and looking down her nose at people.","In the dream, Chu Liangjun was on his way home from a night shift when he found Qiao Lanshu on the road.","At first, when he saw an unconscious woman on the road, he wasn't going to get involved.","But he just casually glanced down, and upon seeing the young woman's fair, beautiful little face, he instantly couldn't take another step.","At that moment, the road happened to be deserted. The biting wind of late autumn was howling, and the weather was so cold that there were hardly any pedestrians.","The unconscious girl on the ground was dressed thinly, her face completely pale.","Chu Liangjun suspected that the only reason she had fainted was that she had frozen to the point of passing out.","He looked around and, seeing no one nearby, took off his old padded jacket, wrapped it around the unconscious girl, hoisted her onto his back, and walked away.","Afraid that the girl's family might come looking for her, he deliberately stuck to the small alleys.","He even intentionally took a few detours.","However, halfway there, he suddenly remembered that he had only recently arrived in the city and had nowhere to go at the moment.","After all, he couldn't return to the supply and marketing cooperative's dormitory.","If he went back, he would be discovered immediately.","But it was dark now, and he couldn't return to his village either, since he still had to wait for the cooperative staff to issue him an introduction letter.","After some hesitation, he simply carried Qiao Lanshu on his back and went to find his uncle.","His uncle was the director of the cooperative; his house was large and had spare rooms.","Chu Liangjun brought Qiao Lanshu over and lied to his uncle, saying she was a younger sister from his village who had fallen ill, and that he needed to take her back to the village the next day.","His uncle believed him.","Qiao Lanshu slept in the room for the night. When she woke up the next day, she saw Chu Liangjun sitting by the bed, staring at her.","In the dream, Qiao Lanshu was very nervous and terrified. She kept asking who he was and if he could take her to some farm to find her fiance.","Afraid that his prize would slip through his fingers, Chu Liangjun lied to Qiao Lanshu that very day, saying he would take her to the farm. Then, before dawn, through a mix of deception and threats, he took Qiao Lanshu back to his village.","...","When Chu Liangjun jolted awake from the dream, he was still thinking about how incredibly real it felt, as if it had actually happened.","Even after waking up, it felt as though his hand was still grasping Qiao Lanshu's pale, slender, and slightly cool hand.","Chu Liangjun felt like he was completely obsessed, thinking about Qiao Lanshu all day long.","He imagined taking Qiao Lanshu back to his village, living in his family's cave dwelling, heating the brick bed for her, and cooking wild vegetable dough drop soup for her.","If she wanted to run away, he wouldn't go anywhere; he would stay in the house and watch her every day.","If he needed to go out and worried his wife might escape, he would use two heavy locks to secure the main door, ensuring she could never get out.","In his dream, Qiao Lanshu was his wife.","But in reality, Qiao Lanshu was so high and mighty that she even found looking at him to be beneath her.","Chu Liangjun couldn't quite take it, so he arrived early to stake out the main gate of the food factory.","He didn't plan on doing anything right now.","He just wanted to catch a glimpse of Qiao Lanshu.","But he waited around for half the day, and Qiao Lanshu never appeared.","The workers at the food factory gradually all left, until only a sparse few remained, yet he still hadn't seen Qiao Lanshu.","Unable to hold back any longer, he walked up to the guardhouse and knocked on the window.","Qiao Lanshu was actually secretly watching him from the window.","The moment she saw him coming, she was so frightened she immediately ran to hide inside the room.","The older man in the guardhouse, holding a steaming cup of tea, cast a glance at Qiao Lanshu.","Hiding inside, Qiao Lanshu gave him a somewhat awkward smile.","The guard silently withdrew his gaze. Then, he cracked the window open slightly and asked impatiently, What is it? What do you want? Spit it out if you have business!","The guard's tone was not very nice, and Chu Liangjun hated nothing more than people looking down on him and speaking to him in such a manner.","But he endured it and asked, Sir, let me ask you something. Isn't there a warehouse keeper surnamed Qiao in your factory? Why hasn't she gotten off work yet?","The guard finally understood why Qiao Lanshu had suddenly run inside to hide.","It turned out she was dealing with a man harassing her.","The guard stayed silent for two seconds before saying, She got off work a long time ago. She left past three o'clock. You should go back.","With that, the guard moved to shut the window.","Chu Liangjun quickly reached out, pressing his hand against the window frame, and asked with a frown, She got off at three? Why so early? Isn't quitting time at five-thirty?","In the dead of winter, it got dark early. Considering that the snowy roads were difficult to navigate and the weather was freezing, the various work units had set the off-work time at five-thirty.","This way, everyone could get off work a bit early and go home to cook for their children.","Qiao Lanshu had left past three—how could she leave so early?","She was a warehouse keeper; she had to watch the warehouse. If she left, who would watch it for her?","Just as Chu Liangjun was thinking this, he heard the older man say, You're asking me? How should I know? You don't expect me to be so nosy as to question every single person in this factory who leaves work early, do you? Do I look like I have that much free time?","The guard impatiently slammed the window shut.","He completely ignored Chu Liangjun after that.","Chu Liangjun stood by the main gate, feeling rather agitated.","Having failed to see Qiao Lanshu again today, he felt uneasy and frustrated.","However, he couldn't go stake out the military compound for her. After all, it was a military residential area filled with military officers, and there were plenty of guards patrolling the grounds.","If he went over there, he might end up getting arrested.","With these thoughts in mind, Chu Liangjun left the food factory.","He walked along the street for about forty minutes until he finally arrived at the residential quarters of the supply and marketing cooperative.","Chu Haiming from the cooperative lived here.","Chu Haiming was in his forties this year. He had three daughters, all in elementary school. His wife, Niu Weifen, didn't have a job and stayed home to take care of the children.","When Chu Liangjun first came to the city to work, he had no place to stay, so he lived at Chu Haiming's house for a few days.","His wife, Niu Weifen, did not like Chu Liangjun very much.","Because she felt that with the scar on Chu Liangjun's face and his constant gloomy expression, he clearly wasn't a good person.","So, as soon as Chu Liangjun started working at the supply and marketing cooperative, Niu Weifen hurriedly made him move out.","Chu Liangjun knew that Niu Weifen didn't like him. He had previously thought that he would never go back to bother them. He hated being looked down upon and living at the mercy of others' moods.","But this time, he swallowed his pride and came back anyway.","He stood at the gate of Chu Haiming's house and knocked. Niu Weifen, wearing an apron and holding a spatula, heard the knocking and shouted, \"Chu Haiming! Go get the door!\"","Chu Haiming, who was reading a newspaper in the living room, put it down and asked, \"Who is it?\"","\"Uncle, it's me, Liangjun,\" Chu Liangjun replied.","Niu Weifen was cooking in the kitchen and didn't hear Chu Liangjun's voice clearly. As she stir-fried, she asked her husband, \"Who's outside? Coming at this hour, is something wrong?\"","Generally, very few people would come visiting during dinnertime.","First, food was precious. Every household barely had enough for themselves, so they certainly couldn't bear to share it with others.","Second, everyone living in this area had jobs and families to take care of. Who would have the free time to drop by for a chat right at mealtime?","Walking to the door, Chu Haiming said, \"Oh, it's Liangjun. Coming over this late, he probably needs something. I'll go open the door.\"","Niu Weifen was speechless.","Hearing this, her face instantly fell. She tossed the spatula aside, turned to the kitchen door, and looked at Chu Haiming. Displeased, she asked in a low voice, \"Why is he here again?\"","Chu Liangjun was Chu Haiming's cousin's son. They were relatives after all, and since he had come to them for help, they naturally couldn't just ignore him.","But Chu Liangjun had a fierce-looking face and a difficult temper. Moreover, he was a man in his twenties; Niu Weifen felt uncomfortable having him drop by the house from time to time.","Knowing that Niu Weifen disliked Chu Liangjun, Chu Haiming whispered, \"He's my nephew, after all. He's been working for two months, and I don't even know how he's doing. Now that he's looking for me late at night, he must have run into some trouble. Fix your attitude and don't be so petty.\"","Niu Weifen was speechless again.","Looking unhappy, she pulled a long face and turned back into the kitchen to continue cooking.","Chu Haiming opened the door and saw Chu Liangjun standing there. He asked with concern, \"Liangjun, why did you come over at this hour? Did something happen?\"","Bringing the cold air in with him from outside, Chu Liangjun rubbed his hands together and said, \"Uncle, nothing's wrong. I just haven't seen you in a long time. I happened to have some business nearby today, so I dropped by to see you on my way.\"","Hearing this, Chu Haiming instantly smiled. Having no sons of his own, he had once considered adopting Chu Liangjun.","However, the idea was never carried out because Niu Weifen disagreed.","Now, hearing that Chu Liangjun had come to see him, he felt quite pleased. \"It's very thoughtful of you. Come in and sit for a while. It's too cold outside. Is it snowing?\"","Chu Liangjun nodded. \"Yes, the snow isn't heavy, but the wind is strong.\"","It blew so hard it made one's cheeks hurt.","Chu Haiming's three daughters were all in their rooms reading, leaving just the two of them in the living room.","Chu Haiming poured him a cup of hot tea and asked, \"Liangjun, how has work been lately? Are you getting used to it?\"","Although Chu Haiming was the director of the supply and marketing cooperative, he truly didn't know how Chu Liangjun was doing in the transport fleet.","After all, if he didn't actively ask, his subordinates wouldn't come gossiping to him.","Knowing this, Chu Liangjun said, \"I'm quite used to it. Thank you, Uncle, for finding me such a good job. When I get paid this month, I'll buy some supplements and come visit you again.\"","Chu Haiming smiled and said, \"Your salary is only a dozen yuan or so; what kind of supplements can you afford? You should keep it for yourself. When there's a chance in the future, I'll help you transfer your household registration to the city. Then, I'll introduce you to a nice girl for marriage.\"","Chu Liangjun looked at the mechanical watch on Chu Haiming's wrist, then at the radio, the desk clock, and the sewing machine in the room.","Chu Haiming's salary was decent, and Niu Weifen's family was wealthy, so they really had quite a few valuable things in their house.","Since he was a child, Chu Liangjun had done his fair share of petty theft, so he could roughly guess where Niu Weifen kept the money and ration coupons.","However, knowing was one thing; he didn't plan on making a move just yet.","He had come to borrow money from Chu Haiming.","Since Chu Haiming brought up the topic of marriage, he got straight to the point. \"Uncle, actually, I came to see you this time because I want to borrow some money.\"","In the kitchen, Niu Weifen was slowly preparing the food while keeping her ears pricked to listen to the commotion outside.","The moment she heard Chu Liangjun wanted to borrow money, her face darkened.","After marrying Chu Haiming, the thing she hated most was that he had too many poor relatives.","Look at this—helping him find a job wasn't enough; now they had to lend him money?","Chu Haiming's expression didn't change much. He looked at Chu Liangjun with concern and asked, \"Why do you suddenly need to borrow money? Are you short on cash?\"","But it made sense. Chu Liangjun had moved from the village to the city and worked for two months. Last month, he was paid at most 10 yuan.","This month's salary hadn't been issued yet, and living expenses in the city were much higher than in the village.","Chu Liangjun probably didn't have much money. After all, over these two months, Chu Haiming hadn't given him any money or coupons. Thinking about it this way, he felt he had been inconsiderate.","Chu Haiming immediately searched his pockets, pulled out two 5-yuan notes, and handed them directly to Chu Liangjun. \"If you're short on money, just tell me. I'm your uncle, don't treat me like a stranger.\"","Chu Liangjun didn't take the 10 yuan. He looked at Chu Haiming and, truly not treating him like a stranger, said, \"Uncle, 10 yuan isn't enough. I want to borrow 50 yuan. Don't worry, I'll work hard to pay you back.\"","Niu Weifen simply couldn't hold back any longer in the kitchen.","She marched out, glared at Chu Liangjun, and demanded:","\"You get room and board at the cooperative, and they pay you over a dozen yuan a month! How can you be so short on money? Fifty yuan! Do you know how much fifty yuan is? Your uncle's monthly salary is only a little over eighty!\"","Looking at Niu Weifen, Chu Liangjun's face instantly turned gloomy.","Chu Haiming also asked, \"Liangjun, did something happen? Why do you suddenly need fifty yuan?\"","Chu Liangjun replied in a deep voice, \"Uncle, I've taken a fancy to a girl. I want to court her and buy her a coat.\""]},{"number":95,"title":"Chapter 95: Should We Find a Matchmaker","paragraphs":["When Chu Liangjun said this, Niu Weifen and Chu Haiming were left completely speechless.","Niu Weifen was silent for a moment before she sneered, \"What kind of family is this girl from, asking for a coat worth dozens of yuan right off the bat? If you ask me, you're probably being scammed.\"","Chu Haiming glanced at Niu Weifen, then turned to Chu Liangjun and asked, \"What does the girl think? How about I find a matchmaker to go ask her for you?\"","Chu Liangjun immediately shook his head. He didn't even need to ask to know that Qiao Lanshu definitely wouldn't be interested in him; after all, he had no money.","Of course, he didn't expect Qiao Lanshu to follow him willingly either.","He just figured he would pursue her for a while, and once they were familiar with each other, he would find an opportunity...","Chu Liangjun said with a dark expression, \"Uncle, I want to talk to her myself. I don't need a matchmaker.\"","As he spoke, he felt a wave of impatience and added, \"Uncle, I promise to work hard and pay you back as soon as possible.\"","Fifty yuan wasn't a small amount, but it wasn't exactly a fortune either.","It wasn't that Chu Haiming was reluctant to lend him the money; he was just worried that his nephew was being conned.","After all, in this day and age, there was no shortage of women who used blind dates as an excuse to scam free meals and drinks.","Nevertheless, Chu Haiming took out fifty yuan and handed it to Chu Liangjun. \"Get along well with the girl,\" he advised. \"If you really like her, bring her back to show your uncle. If you need a matchmaker, come find me anytime, and I'll arrange it for you.\"","Chu Liangjun took the money and nodded. \"Okay, thank you, Uncle. I'll be leaving now.\"","Niu Weifen couldn't wait for Chu Liangjun to leave. Seeing that Chu Haiming still wanted to invite him to stay for dinner, she immediately opened the door and said to Chu Liangjun, \"It's getting late. You'd better head back now, or it will be hard to travel in the dark.\"","Chu Haiming: \"...\"","Chu Liangjun glanced at Niu Weifen, feeling a deep sense of disgust towards her. However, since he still needed Chu Haiming's help, he swallowed his anger, put on his hat, and left with the money.","After he left, Chu Haiming scolded Niu Weifen, \"Look at you, why didn't you ask Liangjun to stay for dinner?\"","Niu Weifen scoffed coldly and said, \"Do you really think he borrowed that money to pursue some girl? For all we know, he's taking it to gamble. Are there a shortage of people playing cards and gambling at the factory lately? Let me warn you, this is the last time you lend him money. If he comes back asking for more, you are not allowed to give him a single cent, or I won't let you hear the end of it!\"","Chu Haiming replied, \"It's not like that, it's really not. Liangjun is quite sensible; he's not that kind of person.\"","Niu Weifen sneered, \"He's no good, and you're the only one who takes him seriously.\"","With that, she turned and went to the kitchen to cook.","Chu Haiming shook his head, still muttering, \"You're just prejudiced against him. The young man is really quite decent.\"","As he spoke, he was secretly planning to ask around the supply and marketing cooperative's motor pool when he went to work the next day. He wanted to see if any of the workers who worked alongside Chu Liangjun knew anything about this girl.","He wanted to know exactly which girl had caught Chu Liangjun's eye. If she was a temporary worker at the cooperative, it would be easy to handle; he could just get a matchmaker to talk to her, and it might just work out.","But if she was a formal employee, it would be a bit difficult. After all, Chu Liangjun's own qualifications were quite poor.","A typical city girl wouldn't even give him a second glance.","...","Meanwhile, Qiao Lanshu stayed inside the guardhouse, only daring to come out after Chu Liangjun had left.","The older guard looked at her and chuckled, \"Look at how timid you are. What are you so afraid of him for? Don't worry, the next time he comes around, I'll chase him off for you.\"","Qiao Lanshu said gratefully, \"Thank you, Uncle!\"","Just then, Qin Yuanzheng drove up. When Qiao Lanshu saw him, her eyes lit up. Without even having time to say goodbye to the guard, she immediately ran out of the guardhouse.","Before Qin Yuanzheng could even get out of the car, he saw his little wife running up to him, opening the door, and hopping inside.","Seeing her hurried state, Qin Yuanzheng smiled and said, \"Did you wait long? I'm sorry, I went to buy you some food just now.\"","With that, he brought over the raisins, stone-baked flatbreads, and honey he had just bought, placing them on Qiao Lanshu's lap. \"The raisins are supposedly from Xinjiang. I tried a few, and they taste pretty good. They're very sweet; you'll definitely love them.\"","Qiao Lanshu stared at the jar of raisins, looking a bit shocked. \"Brother Zheng, why did you buy this? This must have been expensive, right?\"","Qin Yuanzheng replied while driving, \"It wasn't too bad, just fifty cents a catty. If you like eating them, I'll buy them for you. Isn't the whole point of me earning money so you can spend it?\"","Anyway, he didn't need to spend money himself.","His food, clothing, housing, and transportation were all practically provided by the military base; he had nowhere to spend his money.","Now that he had a wife, he naturally wanted to give her the best of everything. Besides, supporting a wife wouldn't cost that much anyway.","Qiao Lanshu was somewhat moved. She pinched a few raisins and popped them into her mouth. They were sweet and truly delicious.","After a while, Qin Yuanzheng suddenly asked, \"By the way, I heard from Xiao Yang that a temporary worker from the supply and marketing cooperative has been following you lately. Is that true?\"","Since he asked, Qiao Lanshu nodded. \"Yeah, I just saw him at the gate of the food factory. Luckily, I hid quickly.\"","Qin Yuanzheng frowned deeply, his face darkening as he said, \"You don't need to be afraid. I've already got someone keeping an eye on him.\"","If he dared to do anything to Qiao Lanshu, Qin Yuanzheng would absolutely not let him off the hook.","After the car arrived at the gate of the military family compound, Qiao Lanshu grabbed the food, opened the door, and stepped out.","Then, she saw Qin Yuanzheng holding two rolls of fabric. She asked curiously, \"Brother Zheng, why did you buy more fabric? We aren't short of fabric at home, are we?\"","When they first got married, she had already made a lot of clothes, and they had all the quilts and mattresses they needed. Why was Qin Yuanzheng buying fabric again?","Qin Yuanzheng looked at her, suddenly leaned in, and lowered his voice near her ear. \"This is made of sheepskin. It's waterproof fabric.\"","Qiao Lanshu: \"...\"","She didn't understand at first, but seeing the teasing look in Qin Yuanzheng's eyes, how could she not get it?","She looked at the fabric in his hands and blushed, saying, \"Brother Zheng, could this be for...\"","Qin Yuanzheng nodded. \"Yes, it's for laying over the mattress. Look, it's single-sided fleece, very warm, and also waterproof. We'll try it out tonight.\"","Qiao Lanshu: \"...\"","When he said try it out, could he possibly mean...","Qiao Lanshu instantly flushed red and remained silent.","As soon as the two returned home, Qin Yuanzheng laid the sheepskin fleece out on the heated brick bed.","Although it had been cut into two pieces, when laid flat, it was very smooth. The pieces sat tightly side by side, making the gap in the middle virtually negligible.","Bare-chested, Qin Yuanzheng inspected it from every angle for a long time before saying to Qiao Lanshu, \"Wifey, come over here and try it out. This fabric was a really great buy.\""]},{"number":96,"title":"Chapter 96: The Matchmaker","paragraphs":["Qiao Lanshu walked over to take a look, curiously touching the sheepskin fleece.","It was winter, so they laid out the fleece-lined side. It felt soft and fluffy to the touch, ensuring they wouldn't be cold sleeping on it during the winter.","However, as soon as Qiao Lanshu heard it was waterproof, she felt a little embarrassed.","She shot Qin Yuanzheng a glance and said, \"People usually only use this kind of waterproof fabric when they have kids at home. Why did you buy it?\"","Besides, this kind of fabric was quite expensive. Buying such a large piece must have cost a lot of money.","Qin Yuanzheng came over and hugged her, his body temperature so hot it was almost scalding.","He nipped at Qiao Lanshu's ear and whispered, \"Even if we don't have kids, newlyweds still need to use it, don't they?\"","Who could blame him when his wife was made of water?","Qiao Lanshu blushed, truly not knowing what to say at this moment.","That night, Qin Yuanzheng deliberately cooked a lot of millet porridge for Qiao Lanshu, making her drink two bowls of it.","Before bed, he mixed a large cup of goat milk powder for his little wife, claiming that goat milk was nutritious and that Qiao Lanshu was too thin and small, so she needed to drink more to nourish herself.","Having been married to him for a while now, how could Qiao Lanshu not know what he was plotting?","But since she liked Qin Yuanzheng, she was willing to cooperate with him, so she obediently drank all the goat milk.","As for Qin Yuanzheng, in the eyes of outsiders, he was usually serious and cold.","But only Qiao Lanshu knew that he had some strange hobbies in certain aspects, which made her feel very embarrassed every time.","Like this waterproof cloth he had bought himself.","And how, every night, he always liked to make all kinds of soups and drinks for her to consume.","He felt this made things more exciting, giving his heart a tremendous sense of satisfaction.","The more uncomfortable Qiao Lanshu felt, the more impulsive he became...","That very night, the two of them tested out the newly bought waterproof cloth.","After testing it for over an hour, Qin Yuanzheng said to Qiao Lanshu with a straight face, \"Wife, even though this cloth was a bit expensive, the waterproof effect is quite good. It was money well spent.\"","At this moment, Qiao Lanshu's face was as red as a tomato. She turned her head away and ignored him.","Qin Yuanzheng brought a pillow over and asked Qiao Lanshu in a low voice, \"Does your waist hurt? Would it feel a little better if I propped it up with a pillow?\"","As he spoke, he placed the pillow in his hands under Qiao Lanshu's waist.","......","Qiao Lanshu: \"......\"","Qiao Lanshu had just sighed in appreciation of Qin Yuanzheng's good intentions, but the very next moment, she realized his sinister motives.","......","In short, Qin Yuanzheng spent another colorful and fulfilling night.","The next morning, it was snowing heavily outside. The sky was just barely getting light when Qin Yuanzheng got up.","First, he washed the wet waterproof cloth clean, and then hung it up to dry on the balcony of the guest bedroom.","After all, in winter, the house was very dry with the heating on.","The freshly washed cloth would dry quickly.","After washing the waterproof cloth, he went to cook breakfast.","Last night, Qiao Lanshu had declared that she never wanted to eat millet porridge again!","Therefore, Qin Yuanzheng didn't cook porridge this morning. Instead, he took two sweet potatoes, washed, peeled, and chopped them into chunks, and put them in a pot. He added some water and pumpkin chunks to boil together. Once cooked, he added some brown sugar to the pot.","Afterwards, he used white flour, eggs, and shredded potatoes to pan-fry seven or eight potato pancakes.","Sweet potato soup paired with potato pancakes—this was today's breakfast.","His little wife liked sweet things, so the sweet potato soup was specially cooked for her.","He himself loved wheat-based foods, so he mainly ate the potato pancakes.","After making breakfast, he went to check on Qiao Lanshu.","Qiao Lanshu had already gotten off the heated brick bed. She was wearing a snug camisole and only panties on her legs. She was currently looking for her long johns to pull over her legs.","Then, sensing something, she glanced toward the door.","She saw Qin Yuanzheng standing there with his arms crossed, watching her with a smile.","Qiao Lanshu: \"...\"","Qiao Lanshu immediately pulled a long face, turned around, and put on her clothes with her back to him.","Qin Yuanzheng walked over, brought her thermal top and sweater, and said, \"Wife, let me help you put them on. Look how tired you are.\"","The current relationship between Qin Yuanzheng and Qiao Lanshu could truly be described as sweet as honey.","He never knew he could like someone this much.","Liking her so much that he even wanted to kiss her feet when he saw them.","Qiao Lanshu let him help her put on her clothes. Then, she hesitated for a moment, looked at Qin Yuanzheng, and said with a blush, \"I need to use the bathroom.\"","Qin Yuanzheng looked at her and whispered, \"Go if you want to. Isn't the bathroom right there?\"","Qiao Lanshu: \"...\"","Qiao Lanshu's face instantly turned beet red!","Wasn't she just used to asking?","She had subconsciously gotten used to it. Great, now Qin Yuanzheng was laughing at her again.","Blushing, Qiao Lanshu hurriedly ran inside and fiercely slammed the bathroom door shut.","Leaving Qin Yuanzheng standing there, laughing heartily.","During breakfast, Qiao Lanshu saw the sweet potato soup and, sure enough, happily ate an extra bowl.","Qin Yuanzheng silently watched her eat, thinking to himself that he would have to buy more brown sugar. The remaining amount wouldn't be enough for many more meals.","After finishing the sweet soup in her bowl, Qiao Lanshu said to Qin Yuanzheng, \"By the way, Brother Zheng, do you remember that girl you helped at the train station the day before yesterday? Her sister is my coworker, and yesterday she asked me to inquire about Deng Weijun.\"","Qin Yuanzheng ate eight potato pancakes, then gathered the clean-swept bowls and chopsticks, preparing to take them to the sink to wash.","Hearing this, he asked, \"What? Have they taken a liking to Deng Weijun?\"","Qiao Lanshu: \"My coworker thinks Weijun is quite nice and wanted to ask what type of girls he likes. If possible, she wants to arrange for them to meet.\"","Qin Yuanzheng listened to Qiao Lanshu calling him 'Weijun' with every breath, sounding quite intimate.","He wondered if they often saw each other since they worked in the same food factory.","Qin Yuanzheng pondered; Deng Weijun was in his twenties now, so it really was about time for him to get married, wasn't it?","His wife was only 18, a few years younger than that Deng Weijun. Two young people seeing each other every day...","Qin Yuanzheng immediately nodded and said, \"Sure, I'll find some time today to go to my cousin's house and ask. It really is time for Deng Weijun to get married.\"","Since Qin Yuanzheng said he would help ask, Qiao Lanshu washed her hands of the matter.","After all, as a married woman, it wouldn't be appropriate for her to proactively ask Deng Weijun about such things.","She thought it would take at least until tomorrow to get an answer.","As a result, at noon, her cousin-in-law Deng Xiaozhen, who originally worked at the textile factory, came looking for her.","Deng Xiaozhen had heard about the matter and came specifically to find Qiao Lanshu, the 'matchmaker.'","She had long wanted to find a wife for Deng Weijun, but she just hadn't asked anyone to look into it yet.","Now that there was a suitable candidate, wasn't it just perfect timing?"]},{"number":97,"title":"Chapter 97: Someone Sent Her a Coat","paragraphs":["Deng Xiaozhen came to the food factory to look for Qiao Lanshu, hurrying over during her free time in the morning.","She wore an army-green padded jacket over the blue uniform of the textile factory. Bits of cotton fluff from the factory workshop still clung to her clothes and hair.","Her collar was wrapped tightly, and a checkered scarf was wound around her face, revealing only half of it.","Because she had hurried all the way, fine beads of sweat dotted her forehead.","At the end of the year, the textile factory was rushing to fulfill winter clothing orders, and the entire workshop was running around the clock, keeping everyone constantly on their feet. As the monitor of the spinning workshop, she had to keep an eye on every process, from feeding materials and watching the spindles to checking for defective products. Attendance, production volume, and team discipline all weighed heavily on her shoulders. During the day, she even had to time her trips to the pantry. She could only squeeze out this gap of time to make this trip after finishing a busy spell in the morning.","Not daring to delay at the factory gate, she asked the security guard for directions and quickly walked around to the warehouse area at the back of the factory.","From a distance, she spotted the independent adobe hut next to the huge storage warehouse. Its walls were neatly painted; it was a dedicated room for the warehouse keeper, newly built by the factory in the past two years.","Deng Xiaozhen hurried to the window in a few quick strides. A thin layer of condensation covered the glass. She rubbed away a small patch with her hand and immediately saw the figure inside.","Qiao Lanshu was burying her head in organizing the warehouse management forms. A stack of ledgers printed with product names lay beside her hand. With her head bowed, she wore an earnest expression.","Deng Xiaozhen quickly curled her knuckles and knocked lightly but urgently on the window pane, tap-tap-tap.","Hearing the sound, Qiao Lanshu jerked her eyes up, her pen pausing on the paper. She looked up and saw Deng Xiaozhen leaning against the windowsill, her brows and eyes showing anxiety as she waved at her continuously.","She was taken aback at first, then quickly put down her pencil and reached out to push open the wooden-framed glass window. A blast of cold air instantly slipped in. Her tone was full of surprise, Cousin-in-law? Why are you here at this hour? Isn't the textile factory incredibly busy at the end of the year?","Afraid she hadn't made herself clear, Qiao Lanshu quickly added, lifting her chin toward the sauce and pickle workshop outside, Are you here to look for Weijun? He's boiling the boiler over there. He even came over specifically this morning to fetch hot water for me. If you had arrived ten minutes earlier, you would have run right into him.","Hearing this, Deng Xiaozhen shook her head rapidly, the corners of her mouth turning down. Her tone was wrapped in uncontrollable anger, That bastard, why would I want to see him? I can't even get angry enough at him! Xiao Qiao, I came here specifically for you today.","Ever since the vicious incident involving Zheng Daliu broke out, Deng Xiaozhen hadn't had a single peaceful night's sleep.","As soon as she closed her eyes, the person hacked to the ground in her dreams turned into her younger brother, Deng Weijun.","Then, every time, she would wake up in a cold sweat, wrapping herself in the blanket and tossing and turning.","Her usual neat and capable appearance had visibly haggard. Whenever she saw her dawdling brother, that anger and lingering fear would twist together, blocking her chest and refusing to dissipate.","Seeing her pale face and that she was standing in the wind, Qiao Lanshu quickly turned to open the wooden door of the hut, leaning out and waving, Cousin-in-law, the wind is harsh and it's freezing outside. Come inside to talk, don't catch a cold.","Deng Xiaozhen responded and stepped through the door, and a warm, comforting heat immediately enveloped her entire body.","This small room was connected to the factory's heating pipes. The sheet metal radiator felt warm to the touch, and as soon as one entered, their whole body felt comfortably warm.","In the early days, the warehouse keepers at the food factory didn't have a separate room at all. They would just move an old wooden desk and a chair with peeling paint, sitting directly in the large warehouse to work. The main doors of the warehouse were kept open year-round for ventilation, and when the cold winter wind blew in, a person's hands and feet would go numb from sitting there for half a day.","Moreover, the daily tasks of a warehouse keeper weren't too complicated, and those on duty were mostly elderly employees. Sitting for long periods made it easy to doze off, and upon waking up, missing or incorrect goods couldn't be traced. Instances of lost goods and unrecorded items occurred frequently.","After weighing the options for a long time, the factory finally built this dedicated hut next to the warehouse's main entrance and set a rule: the warehouse must normally be locked, and the warehouse keeper would keep watch from inside the room. This not only ensured the safety of the goods but also allowed the person on duty to suffer less hardship.","The room wasn't small, and its layout was neat.","By the window sat a sturdy solid wood desk paired with a backed chair, which was exactly where Qiao Lanshu had been doing the accounts just now. One side of the wall had a five-tier pine shelf nailed to it, stacked with ledgers, ink, pencils, as well as sundries like enamel mugs and coarse cloth towels.","The opposite wall had a row of iron nails, hanging a padded coat, a woolen hat, and a red scarf.","At the innermost side was a wooden plank bed, covered with a washed-out, grayish old mattress.","This was left by the previous warehouse keeper, specifically for resting temporarily during night shifts and inventory checks. Fortunately, goods weren't shipped out at night during the winter right now, so aside from the once-a-year major inventory check, night shifts were basically unneeded.","Deng Xiaozhen looked around and was somewhat satisfied with the working conditions here. She asked, Xiao Qiao, is this warehouse keeper job going smoothly for you? It's not too busy or tiring, is it?","Not long after joining the factory, Qiao Lanshu was able to secure such a position. Having an independent small room as an office meant she didn't have to face the wind and sun, nor did she have to stand all day doing repetitive mechanical work like the workshop workers. She could sit whenever she wanted and lean back when she was tired. It was comfortable and respectable. In the eyes of others, it was truly an excellent job.","Of course, this job was mostly the handiwork of Yang Wenyan.","Qiao Lanshu smiled faintly and nodded, It's not too busy. After winter sets in, all the units get off work early. Generally, after four in the afternoon, no one comes to collect materials or pick up goods. Once I finish my tasks, sometimes I can even leave a little early.","Deng Xiaozhen smiled along and naturally chimed in, It's good to have some free time. The winter days are freezing, so we shouldn't touch those physically exhausting and draining jobs. Just stay relaxed and idle, keep your body warm and cozy, and later when you give birth...","As soon as the words left her mouth, she snapped her mouth shut, mentally kicking herself hard, wishing she could slap herself across the face right then and there.","In her early years during the winter, she had damaged her constitution from the cold. Then, running into the famine, she had lived meal to meal, and her body had become extremely weak very early on.","She had seen a doctor, who said she had a cold constitution and weak Qi, lacking in Qi and blood, making conception inherently difficult.","Over the past two years, as life gradually became more comfortable, she had devoted herself to nursing her health, hoping to conceive a son or daughter. Whenever she chatted with close friends, she could hardly go three sentences without mentioning health regimens and preparing for pregnancy. Today, anxious to discuss matters, it had just slipped out of her mouth.","But saying this to Qiao Lanshu was quite inappropriate.","After all, everyone was well aware of Qin Yuanzheng's physical condition.","Deng Xiaozhen hastily stopped herself, a trace of awkwardness flashing across her face. She immediately changed the subject, lowering her voice, By the way, I heard from Yuanzheng that you have a girl here who is asking people to find her a husband, and her age is about the same as our Weijun? Is this true?","Qiao Lanshu's eyes widened slightly, full of surprise, Cousin-in-law, your news is way too fast! I only just mentioned it to Brother Zheng this morning. It's been two hours at most, and you've already come looking for me.","She was truly amazed by Qin Yuanzheng's efficiency.","Deng Xiaozhen covered her mouth and chuckled softly, her voice growing gentler and filled with a sister's endless worry. I definitely had to hurry over and ask about the girl you've been so kind to look out for. You know my Weijun; his temper hasn't settled down yet. After work, he just wanders around all day like a street loafer. I'm really afraid that without any discipline, he'll run into a second person like Zheng Daliu...","When that time comes, he'll just cause trouble for me again. Rather than living in fear every day, it's better to find him a grounded wife early on and start a little family. Once a man has something to care about and something to look forward to coming home to, he can finally settle down and live a proper life. Otherwise, he's always like a wild horse and will get into trouble sooner or later.","She paused, then sighed and added a sentence that reflected her true thoughts, Besides, what man doesn't want to marry a virtuous wife and live a peaceful, stable life once he reaches a certain age?","Actually, what she didn't say aloud was to just look at Qin Yuanzheng. He used to be a workaholic, only knowing work, work, work every single day.","Yang Wenyan had invited him over for a meal time and time again, but eight times out of ten, he would decline.","He would just say he was too busy with work and couldn't get away.","But look at him now. After getting a wife, Qin Yuanzheng went home early every day to pick her up.","From morning till night, he just wanted to be close to his wife.","In the past, when he lived in the dorms, if the chairs or tables broke, he would fix them if he could, and if not, he just threw them away.","The place was completely empty.","But now? Never mind tables, chairs, and furniture; he even knew to buy groceries and non-staple foods. He also knew to ask his comrades from all over the country to buy things for him.","This was the change in a man after marriage!","Qiao Lanshu looked at Deng Xiaozhen's expectant gaze and said in a low voice, Well, she is the younger sister of a colleague of mine. She currently works as a ticket seller at the train station. It's an official job, but her family is from the countryside, and she has brothers... Cousin-in-law, if you have time, how about I ask her older sister to come over and talk with you first?","Deng Xiaozhen quickly nodded. Oh my, that sounds great, Xiao Qiao. The girl already has an official job; I'm just afraid she might look down on my brother. Hurry and take me to see her sister so I can talk to her.","Actually, Deng Weijun also had an official job, and with a brother-in-law who was a factory manager, his conditions were definitely better than Wang Haitang's.","After all, Wang Haitang's family was all in the village, and her job transfer had been arranged by Wang Xue, who spent money to get it done.","To put it bluntly, Wang Haitang's family was just counting on her to work in the city, marry a city man, and then rely on their city son-in-law to improve their lives in the future.","However, Deng Xiaozhen herself was from a village. She had seen and fought with enough unreasonable relatives, so she wasn't afraid of these country relatives coming to sponge off them.","She felt that when marrying a wife, the most important thing was the wife's own personality and character.","So, Qiao Lanshu went to call Wang Xue over.","The three of them chatted in the small room for over half an hour.","Wang Xue and Deng Xiaozhen hit it off right away, and their conversation grew more and more agreeable.","In the end, before the two young people, Deng Weijun and Wang Haitang, had even met, their marriage was practically settled by their two older sisters.","Both of them still had to work, especially Deng Xiaozhen. The work at the textile factory was too busy, and she had to leave quickly; she had barely squeezed out the time to come out this time.","She walked out with Wang Xue and said, Then it's settled. When we have our days off in a couple of days, let's have the two of them meet!","Wang Xue also said readily, Alright, then when the time comes, bring him to my house. I'll write down my address for you.","As she spoke, Wang Xue asked Qiao Lanshu for a pen and paper, wrote down the address, and handed it to Deng Xiaozhen.","Deng Xiaozhen left happily with the slip of paper.","Wang Xue and Qiao Lanshu saw Deng Xiaozhen off together, and then Wang Xue said to Qiao Lanshu, This cousin-in-law of yours is truly a straightforward person. With my Haitang's cowardly temperament, having a sister-in-law like her to help look after her will finally put my mind at ease.","Qiao Lanshu nodded. Yes, Cousin-in-law is very capable. Weijun is extremely afraid of his sister.","It was probably because he had taken quite a few beatings from his sister when he was little, so he was still afraid of her even after growing up.","Wang Xue then secretly lowered her voice and said to Qiao Lanshu, Haitang is just too foolish. Her parents don't dote on her much, and they'll probably cling to her in the future. With her personality being the way it is... Forget it, I won't say anymore. I'll go back to work first. When my shift is over, I'll go pick Haitang up from work and tell her about this along the way.","Saying this, Wang Xue also hurried away.","The small room finally quieted down. Qiao Lanshu sat in her chair and continued working.","She didn't know if it was because she and Qin Yuanzheng lacked restraint at night recently, but she felt a bit tired.","She was exhausted every day. Sometimes, when she sat there reading a book, she would doze off as she read, falling asleep the moment she rested her head on the desk.","At this moment, Qiao Lanshu yawned again and tidied up the sorted inventory forms, putting them away properly.","Then she took out an orange and carefully peeled it.","This orange was specially sent over by one of Qin Yuanzheng's comrades at his request. There were only a few in total, and Qin Yuanzheng couldn't bear to eat them himself, saying they were all for Qiao Lanshu to eat.","Qiao Lanshu also couldn't bear to eat too many, but she was afraid the oranges would spoil.","These past two days, she ate one a day, and then kept the peeled orange skins, planning to make a honey orange peel drink following a honey pomelo recipe.","Just then, the security guard uncle walked over and knocked on the window.","Qiao Lanshu quickly opened the window a crack and asked with a smile, Uncle, what do you need me for?","The security guard replied, A salesperson from the department store is looking for you. They said the coat you ordered has arrived and asked you to go to the gate to pick it up. They require you to sign for it in person.","Normally, mailed parcels were left in the guardhouse for the staff to pick up after work.","But the people from the department store were different; they were delivering merchandise, not parcels. It had to be handed directly to the customer, and the customer had to sign for it. Otherwise, if the item was lost, those salespeople wouldn't be able to afford the compensation.","Qiao Lanshu hesitated and said, A salesperson from the department store? A coat? I didn't buy one...","As she spoke, she took down her padded cotton jacket hanging on the wall. After putting it on, she slipped the half-peeled orange into her pocket.","She went out the door, locked the small room, and followed the security guard outside.","The security guard had his hands tucked into his sleeves, wearing a crooked Lei Feng hat and a cigarette dangling from his mouth. As he walked, he said, Don't you have a military officer husband? Maybe he bought it for you? Although a coat is expensive, for a military officer, it's just a casual expense.","Qiao Lanshu was speechless.","Qiao Lanshu thought about it in her heart and felt that her Brother Zheng would definitely be willing to buy her a coat, but he would probably deliver it himself.","Rather than having a salesperson deliver it, right?","Forget it, since it was already delivered, she should just go and sign for it first. She would ask Brother Zheng about it when she went home in the afternoon."]},{"number":98,"title":"Chapter 98: Received a Coat","paragraphs":["A heavy snow had just fallen, leaving the world a vast expanse of white. A thick layer of snow had accumulated in the courtyard of the food factory, crunching underfoot.","The cold wind blew tiny snow particles against the face, bringing a chilly sensation. Several cleaners and the security guard uncle were holding shovels and brooms, working together to clear the snow in the courtyard. The shovels hit the frozen ground, making dull thuds.","Qiao Lanshu wrapped her old padded jacket tightly around herself and walked all the way through the snow to the main gate of the food factory.","From a distance, she indeed saw a figure standing by the door. The person was wearing a neat department store clerk uniform, the blue-gray fabric crisp and clean. He was holding a square kraft paper bag, looking exactly like someone who had just come from a city department store.","The clerk had sharp eyes and immediately noticed Qiao Lanshu walking towards him. Before she could get close, he took the initiative to greet her, his tone polite and proper: Hello, excuse me, are you Comrade Qiao Lanshu?","Qiao Lanshu nodded gently: That is me.","The clerk's face grew a bit more cautious as he spoke again: Please show me your work badge so I can verify.","Qiao Lanshu understood in her heart. A pure cashmere handmade coat cost a full forty yuan, while the monthly salary of an ordinary worker like them was only around thirty yuan. If he gave it to the wrong person and lost it, the clerk simply could not afford to pay for it.","She did not say much, reached into her jacket pocket, took out her work badge, and handed it over for the clerk to see.","Confirming there was no mistake, the clerk immediately revealed a smile.","He took out a neatly folded receipt from his pocket and handed it over with both hands: Comrade Qiao Lanshu, this is the cashmere coat your friend commissioned our department store to custom-make for you. Here is the sales receipt, please sign it.","Qiao Lanshu took the receipt, her eyes sweeping over the price on it, and her heart stirred slightly.","In this era, she really could not think of a second person besides Qin Yuanzheng who would be willing to spend such a large amount of money to buy her something.","She picked up the pen, signed her name in the designated spot, kept one copy of the receipt, and returned the remaining two copies to the clerk.","The clerk took the receipts and put them away, then handed the kraft paper bag to her: Please take the coat. If there are any minor issues after you go back, you can bring it to the store for repairs anytime. If there is nothing else, I will head back first.","Qiao Lanshu nodded and thanked him.","After the clerk turned and walked away, she gently opened a corner of the bag and took a peek inside.","Inside lay a gray-black women's cashmere coat. The material was thick and soft, with a delicate luster. At a glance, it was clearly a high-quality item, and the craftsmanship was very exquisite.","She put the receipt into the bag as well, tied the opening, carried the coat, and turned back to the small duty room outside the warehouse.","After entering the room, she carefully placed the coat on the wooden rack inside. She did not immediately examine it again, planning to ask Qin Yuanzheng face-to-face when she got home that evening.","If he really gave it to her, she would accept it.","If not, she would definitely return the coat untouched.","For the whole morning, there was nothing urgent in the factory, so Qiao Lanshu quietly read a book in the small room all morning. The room was peaceful, with only the occasional sound of shoveling snow coming from outside the window.","When it was time for lunch, the cafeteria was steaming hot and full of noisy voices.","Just as Qiao Lanshu found a seat and sat down with her rice bowl, Wang Xue came over with her food tray, looking mysterious. As soon as she sat down, she lowered her voice and said to her: Xiao Qiao, come with me for a moment.","Qiao Lanshu was puzzled. She also lowered her voice, picking up her food tray while asking: Sister Xue, what is going on that is so mysterious?","Wang Xue leaned close to her ear, her voice so soft it was almost inaudible: I had someone test Deng Weijun's character. If his character is no good, the two of them will not need to meet tomorrow.","Qiao Lanshu was stunned for a moment. Test his character?","It was the first time she had heard of such a thing, and she could not help but be curious: How do you test it?","Just as her voice faded, a crisp clatter suddenly came from the other side of the cafeteria. The sound of a lunchbox falling to the ground was particularly piercing.","The two of them subconsciously turned their heads to look at the same time.","They saw Deng Weijun, who had just gotten his food, being bumped unexpectedly. His body swayed, and the food tray in his hand almost slipped.","The person who bumped into him was a female worker wearing a cleaner's uniform. The lunchbox in her hand fell to the ground, spilling soup all over the floor. Fortunately, the bowl only contained soup and no rice.","The hot soup splashed all over the ground, and quite a bit spilled onto Deng Weijun's shoes and pant legs.","The female worker turned pale with fright. She hurriedly picked up the bowl, stood up, and kept bowing and apologizing: I am sorry, I am sorry, comrade. I lost my balance just now, it was really careless...","Deng Weijun's first reaction was to quickly and steadily place his own food tray on the table, afraid of spilling his hard-earned meal.","In these times, food in the factory was rationed. If a meal was spilled, one would have to go hungry for that meal. No one dared to be careless.","After safely putting down his food, he looked down and shook off the soup stains on his pant legs. He then looked up at the cleaner lady, his tone peaceful: Sister, I am fine, do not panic.","The lady held the empty lunchbox in one hand and supported her waist with the other. Her brows were slightly furrowed, and she breathed a sigh of relief: As long as you are fine. I was really scared just now.","Seeing her holding her waist, Deng Weijun guessed she had probably sprained it just now and could not help asking: Did you twist your waist? Why don't you sit down and rest for a while.","The lady shook her head: I cannot. I have to hurry and get my food, or there will not be any dishes left if I am late.","Seeing that she was walking uncomfortably, Deng Weijun sighed and offered: You sit here first, I will go get the food for you.","After saying that, he carefully helped the lady sit down on a nearby stool, picked up her empty lunchbox, and turned to walk towards the food serving window.","The cleaner lady gathered her bowls and chopsticks, watching Deng Weijun's back for a moment.","Then, she imperceptibly glanced towards Wang Xue. The corners of her mouth curled up quietly, and she nodded slightly. Anyone with a discerning eye could understand the meaning in her gaze.","Qiao Lanshu saw this entire scene completely, and she was entirely stunned.","She quickly turned her head, leaned close to Wang Xue's ear, and whispered in a soft and shocked voice: Sister, is... is this the test you arranged?","Wang Xue held her bowl and slowly took a bite of her coarse grain steamed bread, a knowing and satisfied smile appearing on her face. She replied in a hushed voice: Now I can rest assured. This young man Deng Weijun does not have a bad heart. He is a kind and honest comrade.","Qiao Lanshu took a bite of her steamed bun and nodded sincerely: Yes, he is indeed warm-hearted and simple. He did not mind at all just now and even took the initiative to help get food.","Hearing this, Wang Xue sighed softly, her chopsticks pausing on the edge of the bowl, her tone carrying a bit of helplessness and heartache:","I have no other choice either. Haitang's personality is too cowardly and soft; she just goes along with whatever others say. As her older cousin, I have to pick someone with a good heart for her. Otherwise, with her silent temper, if she really suffers grievances and gets bullied in the future, I am afraid she would not even dare to cry out loud.","This was the most she could do.","Helping to evaluate him and quietly testing the waters was the limit; as an ordinary female worker, she was powerless to do anything more.","After lunch, Wang Xue, being a woman of action who hated delays, wanted to go straight to the train station to find Wang Haitang and tell her the good news about Deng Weijun's reliable character.","Qiao Lanshu happened to have no urgent matters that afternoon, so Wang Xue grabbed her and pulled her along to the station.","As they were nearing the entrance of the train station, Qiao Lanshu suddenly stopped in her tracks and reached out to pull back the hurrying Wang Xue.","Wang Xue stumbled from the pull and turned around, asking in confusion, What is wrong?","Qiao Lanshu put a finger to her lips, making a shushing gesture, and then gently pointed to an inconspicuous narrow alley next to the train station.","The two quietly crept up to the mouth of the alley and peeked inside, their hearts instantly leaping into their throats.","They saw Liu Jianguo leaning casually against the wall, whispering something to a man carrying bamboo baskets on a shoulder pole, a man who clearly looked like a black market speculator. Neither of the men noticed them at the alley entrance.","They heard Liu Jianguo's vicious tone as he cursed, Damn her! I spent so much time and effort, and now she thinks she can just dump me with a few words? No way!","The man opposite him advised, Oh man, this thing has already gone to the police station. Why do not you just let it go? There are plenty of fish in the sea, can you not just chase someone else?","Liu Jianguo gave a cold sneer, his voice full of malice. Am I supposed to just watch a cooked duck fly away? I have to get my hands on her! When she gets off her night shift, I will naturally have a way to deal with her.","The other man laughed and said, Now that you mention it, with your girl's temperament, it will be pretty easy to get her. But, are you going to marry her?","Hearing this, Liu Jianguo immediately laughed and said, Marry her? Like you said, this has already gone to the police. How could I possibly marry her? Once I get my hands on her and the deed is done, will she not be entirely at my mercy?","The man nodded and added, I heard that in your textile factory, there are women who sleep with men in secret. When they get pregnant, they do not dare say a word and can only secretly go to back-alley clinics for abortions. Let me tell you, these women with formal jobs are even more afraid of exposure than you are. They are terrified of losing their jobs and losing face. As long as you get them into bed, they will be at our mercy from then on.","Liu Jianguo thought the same way. He fell silent for a moment, then said, When she gets off her night shift, I will naturally find a chance to do her.","...","Wang Xue and Qiao Lanshu heard every single word of this.","Wang Xue was so angry she could almost spit blood. She had never seen such a shameless man!","Her blood boiling, she was ready to charge into the alley right then and there, wishing she could rush up and beat Liu Jianguo to a pulp.","Fortunately, Qiao Lanshu reacted quickly. She grabbed her tightly, half-pulling and half-dragging her to a distant street corner, preventing them from being discovered.","Hiding in a safe place, Wang Xue's chest heaved violently with anger. Her face was flushed red, and her voice trembled. That bastard Liu Jianguo! He actually has not given up! Xiao Qiao, you heard him just now. He is actually planning to wait until Haitang gets off her night shift...","Before she could finish her sentence, Wang Xue angrily rolled up her sleeves, her eyes turning red. No! I have to go teach him a good lesson!","Qiao Lanshu hurriedly held her down and said anxiously, Sister, whatever you do, do not be impulsive! If you go over there now, you have no proof and no backup. You are no match for them at all. It is too risky and will only alert the snake in the grass.","The two of them had already fought last time, and it had escalated to the police station.","The police comrades had already warned them that if another such brawl occurred, it would not be resolved with a simple verbal reprimand.","Wang Xue was such a good person; she could not lose her job over a piece of scum like him.","Wang Xue also knew that she would not gain any advantage by confronting him head-on, but the thought of her sister being targeted and schemed against like this made the fire in her heart impossible to suppress.","Anxious and angry, her eyes a little red, she grabbed Qiao Lanshu's hand and asked, Then what should we do? Are we just going to let him run wild and ignore Haitang?","Qiao Lanshu steadied her nerves, thought quickly for a moment, and calmly analyzed the situation in a low voice:","We cannot fight him head-on. With this kind of person, we cannot step forward ourselves. Let us go to the police station right now and tell the comrades exactly what we just heard, word for word. We will ask them to arrange a militia patrol group to focus on this area and strengthen patrols along Haitang's route home from work. Having the authorities step in will be much more effective and much safer than us going up there ourselves.","Reasoning or fighting with a rogue like Liu Jianguo was useless. Only by having the police and militia step forward could he truly be suppressed.","Being pointed out like this by her, Wang Xue's mind cleared up a bit, knowing this was the safest method. She gritted her teeth fiercely and immediately nodded. You are right! Let us go. We are going to the police station right now!","It was truly fortunate for Wang Xue that she listened to Qiao Lanshu's advice from start to finish. She did not go to clash head-on with Liu Jianguo but went straight to the police station and explained the matter in full detail.","In these times, the police station was very short-handed. The entire city police station only had a total of four or five people, including the old man who guarded the gate. There were very few who could actually run field operations.","Fortunately, most of these police officers were veterans transferred from the military. They had a strong sense of responsibility, were agile, and were not the type to do things half-heartedly.","After hearing Wang Xue say that someone was persistently harassing and even threatening to attack a female worker, the comrades immediately took it seriously. They arranged for an officer on the spot to specifically stand guard in secret near the train station.","It was called standing guard, but on the surface, it was just a normal patrol. In secret, however, it was keeping an eye on Wang Haitang's route home from work to ensure her safety.","Before a report was filed, this matter could have been glossed over. But since the masses had come to their door to report a danger, they could not pretend they had not heard.","Coming out of the police station, the wind on the street still carried a chill. Qiao Lanshu pulled Wang Xue back a bit and cautioned her in a low voice, Sister, do not go pick up Haitang tonight. You already went once yesterday. If Liu Jianguo is really watching from the shadows, he will definitely recognize you. The moment you appear, he might just shrink back and not dare to show his face.","As things stood now, to deal with Liu Jianguo, they had to do it in one vigorous effort and pin him down once and for all. Otherwise, the longer it dragged on, the more complications would arise, making it even more troublesome. Dealing with a lingering ghost like him was the same principle as dealing with Chu Liangjun previously;","They could not just chase him away by force; they could only lure him into making a move himself and catch him red-handed.","Thinking of this, Qiao Lanshu suddenly thought of that overcoat in her heart. That overcoat, could it be..."]},{"number":99,"title":"Chapter 99: Deliberately Making Soup for Her Again","paragraphs":["Qiao Lanshu suddenly recalled the words she had deliberately let slip for Chu Liangjun to hear. Connecting them to that cashmere coat of unknown origin, her heart sank bit by bit.","Could it be that the coat was a gift from Chu Liangjun?","A pure cashmere coat cost forty yuan. How could an ordinary worker like him afford that?","Did he actually steal it?","The more she thought about it, the more amiss it felt. Qiao Lanshu secretly made up her mind to keep quiet about it and observe for a few more days.","Beside her, Wang Xue also figured out what Qiao Lanshu meant.","Arguing or kicking up a fuss with Liu Jianguo was useless. As long as he had not actually made a physical move, she could do nothing to him. Making a big scene would only easily ruin Haitang's reputation.","But once Liu Jianguo dared to lay a hand on Haitang, the nature of the matter would completely change. When he was arrested then, no one would be able to gossip.","Wang Xue's eyes lit up, and she nodded repeatedly. Xiao Qiao, you are right. We will do just that.","Saying so, she clenched her fists, her tone firm. Tonight, I will have my husband hide near the train station and keep watch in the dark. With only one police comrade, I am afraid they might not be able to subdue him and let that bastard escape.","Qiao Lanshu breathed a sigh of relief. Yes, you are being thorough.","The two discussed the details, and without delaying a moment, Wang Xue hurried home to make arrangements with her husband.","Qiao Lanshu turned and went back to the food factory. There was nothing urgent at the factory today, so she planned to get off work early.","Walking to the door of the duty room, she was about to lock up when her gaze inadvertently fell on the wooden rack inside.","The grayish-black cashmere coat lay there quietly.","She paused her steps, falling silent for a moment.","The thought that this item was very likely from Chu Liangjun made her stomach churn, filling her with deep-seated disgust.","But on second thought, if it really was from Chu Liangjun, it just proved that he completely believed her previous act of being vain and greedy for nice things.","He truly thought that as long as he was willing to spend money and give her expensive gifts, he could move her and make her look at him differently.","Thinking about it this way, it actually proved that her previous calculations were correct.","Qiao Lanshu stood there hesitating for a while, then turned back and reached out to take the cashmere coat off the rack.","Since this coat was not a gift from Qin Yuanzheng, she absolutely could not take it home.","Qin Yuanzheng was terrifyingly jealous and highly possessive.","If he found out that another man had given her such an expensive cashmere coat, who knew what kind of scene he would make.","At that time, he might really get so angry and anxious that he would tie her up and ruthlessly teach her a lesson.","At this thought, Qiao Lanshu's cheeks grew slightly hot. She hurriedly took the cashmere coat out of the bag, found a thick piece of kraft paper to wrap it carefully, and stuffed it securely into the drawer.","After doing all this, she neatly folded her own plain-colored scarf, put it into the kraft paper bag that originally held the cashmere coat, picked it up casually, and quietly left the small room.","Today she still waited for Qin Yuanzheng to pick her up at the main gate of the food factory, but she did not go into the warm guard room. Instead, she leaned against the most inconspicuous corner by the gate, holding the kraft paper bag in her hand, her gaze seemingly casually sweeping around.","With this glance, she saw Chu Liangjun standing across the road.","Qiao Lanshu frowned inwardly. This man was really strange. He came here every day. Did he not need to work? Why was he so free?","She pretended not to see anything and stood expressionless, treating him like thin air.","Across the street, Chu Liangjun's eyes remained glued to her. He first stared at her face for a moment, then his gaze fell on the familiar kraft paper bag in her hand, and his eyes immediately brightened.","He gathered the sleeves of his padded jacket and immediately strode toward her from across the street, wearing a smile that suggested he thought victory was within his grasp.","Only then did Qiao Lanshu faintly raise her eyes to glance at him, her gaze harboring undisguised disgust. Without waiting for him to get close, she turned directly and walked back into the food factory, showing no intention of acknowledging him.","Chu Liangjun paused, the smile freezing on his face.","He had clearly seen Qiao Lanshu holding the bag that contained the coat, and was certain she liked the clothes he gave her, perhaps even bringing it out deliberately to show off.","But just as he wanted to step forward to talk to her, she turned and walked away. Her attitude clearly showed she found him an eyesore.","Chu Liangjun sneered inwardly.","Who was she pretending for?","She accepted the gift and even carried the bag to the factory gate, eager for all the off-duty workers to see it. Was that not just vanity?","Wait until she knew that this expensive cashmere coat was from him; he would see if she could still put on this aloof facade.","However, since she was willing to accept the gift, everything would be easy to handle.","He would give her more expensive things in the future, and when she got used to accepting them, he would reveal the truth.","By then, having taken his gifts, she would not be able to turn against him even if she wanted to.","If she really dared to turn her back on him, he would go straight to the Revolutionary Committee to report her, saying she was greedy for pleasure and acted like a capitalist miss, getting her publicly criticized, making her lose her job, and having everyone point fingers at her.","When that time came, as a helpless woman with no one to rely on, what other path would she have besides relying on him?","In his eyes, Qiao Lanshu was just a young, naive, and vain woman who would eventually fall into his clutches.","Chu Liangjun stared gloomily at Qiao Lanshu's disappearing back for quite a while. It was not until she was completely out of sight that he spat unwillingly and turned to leave.","Qiao Lanshu returned to the small warehouse room and suppressed the hatred in her heart.","Her goal had been achieved;","Which was to make Chu Liangjun mistakenly believe that she had accepted the coat and liked it very much.","She placed the empty bag in her hand on the table, took out a towel to wrap around her neck, confirmed the door was locked, and then hurried back to the main gate.","Before long, Qin Yuanzheng drove over to pick her up.","Qiao Lanshu pulled open the car door and sat inside. Thinking of the coat she had just hidden, she felt a bit guilty, as if she had done something bad behind his back.","Seeing her sit obediently, Qin Yuanzheng reached out to adjust her scarf and asked naturally, What do you want to eat tonight?","Qiao Lanshu said softly, I can eat anything.","In this era of food shortages, being able to fill one's stomach was already good enough; how could anyone dare to be picky?","Qin Yuanzheng looked at her slightly reddened earlobes and chuckled softly. Then I will cook dough drop soup for you tonight.","Qiao Lanshu was speechless.","Her face instantly turned redder, and she muttered softly, Why is it soup again...","Qin Yuanzheng kept a straight face, his tone sounding exceptionally sincere. It is cold and dry, so you need to drink more soup and fluids. Do you not dislike millet porridge? Then have dough drop soup. I will make it, and I guarantee it will be delicious.","Qiao Lanshu pursed her lips and said nothing.","No matter how delicious it was, it was still soup.","She seriously suspected that Qin Yuanzheng had tasted the sweetness of drinking soup last night and was deliberately making soup for her again today!"]},{"number":100,"title":"Chapter 100: Treat Your Wife Like a Child to Dote On","paragraphs":["When the couple returned home, Qiao Lanshu hung their cotton-padded jackets and other coats on the hooks.","She actually felt a bit guilty because of the matter concerning Chu Liangjun.","Qin Yuanzheng knew about Chu Liangjun, but he could only arrange for people to keep an eye on him; he couldn't actually do anything to him.","This was because Chu Liangjun hadn't done anything out of line.","But Qiao Lanshu couldn't hold back anymore. Right now, she just wanted Chu Liangjun dead, which meant she had to lure him into a trap.","Her only fear was that if Qin Yuanzheng found out, he would think she was malicious and ruthlessly trying to harm an ordinary man who hadn't done anything wrong.","She couldn't let Brother Zheng know about this.","As she was thinking this, a large hand reached over, lifted her chin, and stared into her face. \"What are you thinking about? I was just talking to you, why didn't you answer me?\"","Qin Yuanzheng was quite clingy; when he didn't get a response after just two sentences, he immediately came over to ask her.","Qiao Lanshu quickly concealed her thoughts. Looking at Qin Yuanzheng with bright eyes, she smiled and said, \"I didn't hear you just now. What did you say?\"","Qin Yuanzheng looked down at her and said, \"I said, the waterproof cloth I washed this morning is dry now, and I've already laid it out.\"","Qiao Lanshu: \"...\"","Qiao Lanshu gave him a speechless look.","He might as well have said nothing.","Looking at her expression, Qin Yuanzheng found it amusing.","He said, \"I'm going to cook.\"","Ever since they got married, they ate at the cafeteria at noon, and when they came back in the evening, Qin Yuanzheng was the one in charge of cooking.","It wasn't that Qiao Lanshu was unwilling to cook, but rather that Qin Yuanzheng absolutely refused to let her enter the kitchen or hold a kitchen knife.","He worried that his little wife's hands would get cut by the knife, and it would be too ugly if it left a scar.","He felt his wife was well-nourished in every way; her hands were fair and translucent, slender like water scallions.","Such beautiful hands were not meant for manual labor. She was born to enjoy a life of blessing.","Qin Yuanzheng scooped out a bowl of flour and took two eggs, preparing to make dough drop soup.","Since the beginning of winter, they had been eating Chinese cabbage and potatoes every day.","But there was nothing they could do; in this day and age, there were no other fresh vegetables to eat.","They could only cook the cabbage in different ways: cabbage stewed with vermicelli, cabbage dumplings, stir-fried cabbage with cured meat, cabbage and potato osmanthus soup, sweet and sour cabbage...","Qiao Lanshu's favorite was still Qin Yuanzheng's sweet and sour cabbage.","It was sour, crisp, and exceptionally refreshing and delicious.","Qin Yuanzheng stir-fried another sweet and sour cabbage tonight.","He cooked a large pot of dough drop soup, steamed six multi-grain steamed buns, and steamed two potatoes, mashing them up and mixing in some pickled cabbage to make pickled cabbage mashed potatoes.","The simple meal was ready.","Qiao Lanshu looked at the large pot of dough drop soup, her expression turning serious.","After all, last night's experience was far too intense, leaving her with lingering fear.","Looking at her expression, Qin Yuanzheng immediately found it funny.","Just how scared was his little wife?","It seemed that one time last night had traumatized her.","He said, \"Tonight, I have to go back to the mining area for a meeting. You rest well at home by yourself. I will try my best to come back early.\"","Qiao Lanshu was stunned. She looked at Qin Yuanzheng with a somewhat disappointed expression. \"Ah? You still have to go out and work tonight?\"","Since they got married, the two of them had been together every single night.","They had never been apart even once.","Now that they were suddenly going to be apart, she wasn't quite used to it.","Qiao Lanshu immediately walked over holding her bowl, pulled up a small stool, and sat down closely next to Qin Yuanzheng.","She leaned against Qin Yuanzheng's sturdy arm and whispered, \"Then you must come back early. If you don't come back, I won't be able to sleep.\"","Seeing Qiao Lanshu acting so clingy, Qin Yuanzheng's heart softened. His wife was truly too well-behaved, and he actually couldn't bear to leave her either.","On a cold winter night, one should be holding their wife on a warm kang.","But he couldn't skip tonight's meeting.","He heard it was about enemy spies, a very serious matter, and they had to arrange for people to go provide support.","Qin Yuanzheng had just gotten married, so he figured they probably wouldn't send him.","But as for who would be sent, it was still unclear.","Qiao Lanshu rubbed against Qin Yuanzheng's arm. \"Then I'll wait for you to come back.\"","After eating, Qin Yuanzheng washed the bowls, put on his coat and hat, and prepared to head out.","Qiao Lanshu walked him to the door. He kissed her on the cheek, ruffled her hair, and whispered, \"It's cold in the hallway, hurry back inside.\"","Saying that, Qin Yuanzheng helped her close the door. Before closing it, he reminded her, \"Lock the door well, and then go to sleep. I have a key, so I'll open the door myself when I come back. Rest well.\"","With that, he closed the door and turned into the hallway.","Through the door, Qiao Lanshu listened to his footsteps slowly fading away.","She returned to the room, looking at the empty house, feeling a bit down.","With Qin Yuanzheng not by her side, she simply couldn't sleep.","In the middle of the night, she got up, washed the clothes, and hung them up to dry. Then she swept, mopped the floor, and wiped the tables.","She cleaned the house spotlessly until there was truly nothing left to do. When she checked the time, it was only eleven o'clock at night.","Qin Yuanzheng still hadn't returned.","Only then did Qiao Lanshu go back to the kang. She placed a small oil lamp at the head of the bed, covered herself with the quilt, and took out a middle school textbook to review.","Gradually, not knowing how long she had been reading, she fell asleep.","Qin Yuanzheng still had not returned.","The next morning, at past seven o'clock, someone knocked on her door.","Qiao Lanshu didn't know when she had fallen asleep last night.","She had even forgotten to blow out the oil lamp, and it burned for the entire night.","Her heart ached for the wasted lamp oil. She quickly blew out the oil lamp and got off the kang.","She looked at the small desk clock on the outer cabinet and only then realized that it was already seven-thirty in the morning!","She was startled. What was going on? A whole night had passed, why hadn't Brother Zheng come back yet?","At this moment, the knocking sound outside rang again.","Qiao Lanshu's eyes lit up, thinking it was Qin Yuanzheng returning!","She quickly ran to the door and asked, \"Who is it?\"","Outside the door came the voice of her neighbor Huang Erling: \"Sister, it's me, your neighbor!\"","Qiao Lanshu quickly opened the door. Sure enough, Huang Erling was holding a vegetable basket, which contained fried dough sticks and fresh goat's milk.","She handed two fried dough sticks and a packet of goat's milk to Qiao Lanshu, asking with a smile, \"Just woke up?\"","Qiao Lanshu had slept too late last night and almost overslept. She subconsciously took the breakfast handed over by Huang Erling and asked hesitantly, \"Sister Ling, what is this for?\"","Huang Erling smiled and said, \"In the middle of the night yesterday, my Lao Zhao came back and asked me to pass a message to you. Commander Qin couldn't come back last night and is still busy today. He told you not to worry, and especially reminded me to buy breakfast for you. He said it was Commander Qin's instructions, steamed buns or fried dough sticks are fine, but I definitely had to buy goat's milk because it's nutritious. Take it back and eat. I have to go back and make breakfast for the kids; they still have to go to school.\"","As she spoke, she took out her keys to open the door and said, \"Oh my, the snow outside has melted today, and the roads are completely covered in ice. It's freezing out there. Make sure you bundle up when you go out later, and watch your step so you don't slip and fall.\"","Qiao Lanshu, looking as if she hadn't fully woken up yet, nodded and said, \"Okay, I'll keep that in mind. Thank you, Sister Ling.\"","Huang Erling smiled as she opened the door to the house and said, \"Your Regiment Commander Qin really dotes on you, buying you goat's milk to drink every single day.\"","Around here, people only bought goat's milk for pregnant women and children; ordinary adults were usually too frugal to drink it themselves.","Cow's milk and milk powder required milk ration coupons, but in some places, goat's milk didn't.","Because there were many sheep and goat farmers in the area and pastures right on the outskirts of the city, goat's milk was relatively easy to buy, though it certainly wasn't cheap.","To think that Qin Yuanzheng insisted on buying goat's milk for his wife every day—he was truly pampering her as if she were a child, treating her like an absolute treasure."]}]);
